libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:3:KDL parser for `.loop` and `.vertex` files. Pure grammar — no runtime types, no execution. Start at Level 0. Only escalate when you hit a trigger.
libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:15:Only external dependency: `ckdl` (KDL parser). No cross-lib imports — lang is portable.
libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:103:**Don't reach for yet**: Population management, KDL text manipulation.
libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:126:**Storage modes**: `"file"` (external `.list` file), `"inline"` (KDL `with` rows), `"both"`.
libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:134:Population management also includes KDL text manipulation — `kdl_insert_with_row()`, `kdl_remove_with_row()`, `export_to_file()`, `import_from_file()`. These edit the `.vertex` file text directly to add/remove parameter rows. The CLI (`loops ls/add/rm`) uses these.
libs/lang/CLAUDE.md:145:- KDL is the surface syntax. `ckdl` handles lexing. Lang maps to domain AST.
