   323	
   324	    States: ``code`` / ``plain_string`` / ``line_comment``. Everything the
   325	    machine cannot prove is refused AT its first occurrence, so the
   326	    tracking is never trusted past an unprovable construct:
   327	
   328	    - non-LF newline characters (``\\r \\f U+0085 U+2028 U+2029``),
   329	      anywhere — checked up front (R6-01);
   330	    - in code state: ``/*`` (block comment — a quote inside ``/* " */``
   331	      would poison flat quote tracking, R6-02) and ``/-`` (slashdash);
   332	      ``//`` enters line_comment, where quotes are inert;
   333	    - in code state, at an opening quote: ``\"\"\"`` (multi-line string),
   334	      ``r`` immediately before it (zero-hash raw opener — trivially
   335	      position-aware here: a closing quote after the letter r is
   336	      plain_string state, so ``"system-monitor"`` stays allowed) and ``#``
   337	      immediately before it (hashed raw opener);
   338	    - in code state, ``#`` immediately after a closing quote (``"#``,
   339	      hashed raw closer);
   340	    - inside plain_string: a literal newline (R5), with ``\\\\`` and
   341	      ``\\\"`` escape-aware;
