.loops/data/project.jsonl:3274:{"t":"fact","id":"01KYGVYCZ005YS0KDWCY8JXRXJ","kind":"observation","ts":1785125090.023755,"observer":"kyle/loops-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"topic\": \"test/010-review-loop-converged\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r5 pure replay: CONVERGED, loop CLOSED. Five-round record on one night-one wave diff: r1 found 5 P2 (arbiter code included), behavior fixes closed on first verification while ratchets took three hardening rounds \\u2014 final tally: every honest-code-shaped evasion caught or fail-closed, every deliberate-indirection form classified and counted against a zero baseline, both shrink-only claims mechanical. The scope-model arc (name-collision -> non-def shadowing -> import shadowing, three rounds converging on a Python binding model) plus the vertex_fold one-line construction fix versus hundreds of detection-hardening lines is the strongest paired evidence yet for RATCHETS construction-first pricing. Wave branch at r5 close: 17 commits, arch 46 / loops 2403 / engine 1137 / tasks 258 / atoms 440, diff-check clean, zero goldens regenerated across the entire loop.\", \"ref\": \"observation:test/010-sol-r3-verdicts,thread:010-surfacing-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGVA82M5TTZJQNTJ7TN5V87,01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\"}","signature":"tvsH6+VOiS3Ni3LJzN7nKVlNDss3DpTUrEEjF7FRsdtuueVoyqfFm1uU97/H0IM+9f1vP+ftFRNeiOqPMGDgAg=="}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:3278:{"t":"fact","id":"01KYGW3P9YDQC3BAWEZDA4K1KG","kind":"thread","ts":1785125263.43791,"observer":"kyle/loops-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"name\": \"010-surfacing-wave\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"NIGHT-ONE EXECUTION ARC complete: feat/010-surfacing at 22 commits, full sol-HIGH five-round adversarial loop CONVERGED, all gates green (arch 46, loops 2407, engine 1137, tasks 258, atoms 440), zero goldens regenerated. LANDED: charter RATIFIED (Kyle, session open); S1 contract migration (7/7 tasks sites, piped= deleted \\u2014 register IS the offered width, Rule 12); live-edge staleness sensor complete at four layers (rider, ratified); Track B grounding (owed vectors 5 not 8, ceremony-refutation, layout recommendation); fix rounds r1-r4 (live_edge + vertex_fold snapshot coherence by construction, ratchet suite hardened to a Python binding model with countable boundaries and mechanical shrink-only baselines). SESSION-OPEN REPAIR (pre-wave): seal wiring dead since ~Jul 16 (CC plugin-config migration dropped the loops plugin after a hooks-manifest change hard-failed it) \\u2014 plugin fixed+reinstalled (7d82ec8 on main), catch-up seals minted on project+identity. OPEN NEXT: Kyle gates \\u2014 Track B batch split (recommended: index doc + generator relocation + family-3 vector now, GRP its own design session) and merge-to-main call; then TUI S2 (lens plans/dispatch); zoom-adapter-cross-app-fork awaits painted-major coordination.\", \"ref\": \"design:architecture/surfacing-layer-charter,observation:test/010-review-loop-converged\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGJS6CG9R6G2JQ08F0AP7BC,01KYGVYCZ005YS0KDWCY8JXRXJ\"}","signature":"OiITqW17+YJUhzkqqBiReCS+LY4rPc9L1/AnHzrt70GG5A/byNwAQ9oFPcclSAj8JC3Gc05U01tLSY9lEZ57Bw=="}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:3280:{"t":"tick","id":"01KYGW4DK713H1PQMNN94CZ449","name":"project","ts":1785125287.309455,"since":1785109833.101768,"origin":"project","payload":"{\"decision\": {\"items\": {\"tooling/tach\": {\"topic\": \"tooling/tach\", \"message\": \"tach for tier 2 import enforcement. Rust (fast), TOML config (declarative), fits uv/ruff/ty toolchain. tach sync bootstraps from existing code. Replaces hand-rolled AST import walkers (siftd ~230 lines). Does not replace domain invariants.\", \"_ts\": 1772312302.738764, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/script-structure\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/script-structure\", \"message\": \"scripts/ contains check.sh, lint.sh, test.sh, fmt.sh plus scripts/lib/dev.sh for shared helpers (ok, fail, step, run_uv). Each script is independently runnable, ./dev dispatches to them.\", \"_ts\": 1772315113.139578, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/documentation-layout\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/documentation-layout\", \"message\": \"CLAUDE.md at app/lib level answers 'what do I need to know to work here?' DESIGN.md if architecture is non-trivial. No README.md in apps (CLAUDE.md serves the purpose). README.md in libs for API consumers who aren't reading CLAUDE.md.\", \"_ts\": 1772315113.202291, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/scaffold-minimalism\": {\"topic\": \"design/scaffold-minimalism\", \"message\": \"Scaffold includes only what every project needs. No CI pipeline, Dockerfile, pre-commit hooks, logging setup, or config system. Add complexity when the use case demands it, not before.\", \"_ts\": 1772315113.333097, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/app-structure\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/app-structure\", \"message\": \"An app is: main(argv) entry point, commands/ (fetch functions returning typed dicts), lenses/ (painted views at zoom levels), and wiring through run_cli. fetch \\u2192 lens \\u2192 run_cli gives JSON/plain/pipe/live output for free. Apps use vertex_read/vertex_facts for reads, never StoreReader directly (search is a documented exception until libs/store Phase 2).\", \"_ts\": 1772423085.691358, \"_n\": 2}, \"architecture/lib-structure\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/lib-structure\", \"message\": \"libs/<name>/: CLAUDE.md, README.md, pyproject.toml, src/<package>/{__init__.py,...}, tests/{conftest.py,test_<module>.py}. One concern per lib. Public API re-exported from __init__.py.\", \"_ts\": 1772315113.458814, \"_n\": 1}, \"tooling/pyproject-conventions\": {\"topic\": \"tooling/pyproject-conventions\", \"message\": \"Python >=3.11. Dev deps: pytest>=8.0, pytest-cov>=6.0, ruff>=0.8, ty. Ruff: target py311, line-length 100. testpaths = ['tests'].\", \"_ts\": 1772315113.521404, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/dissolution-scorecard\": {\"topic\": \"design/dissolution-scorecard\", \"message\": \"loops: 11 dissolutions, 3 atoms remain. Peer\\u2192observer field, Vertex\\u2192engine runtime, Sink\\u2192fold state, Store\\u2192vertex capability, Witness\\u2192observer+vertex, Tap\\u2192vertex, Memory\\u2192boundaryless fold, Fidelity\\u2192lens+zoom, Live vs Stored\\u2192refresh loop, Debug as horizon\\u2192debug as lens, Tick-into-Fact\\u2192same primitive.\", \"_ts\": 1772315839.7425, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/claude-md-levels\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/claude-md-levels\", \"message\": \"Four levels: global (~/.config/claude/CLAUDE.md) for how you work, root (project/CLAUDE.md) for what the system is + build + structure, lib for one concern + key types + invariants, app for domain mapping + dev cycle + CLI shape. Each level adds, not repeats.\", \"_ts\": 1772315857.677586, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/claude-md-antipatterns\", \"message\": \"God CLAUDE.md (everything in root, important things buried \\u2014 split when section serves only one lib/app). Stale CLAUDE.md (conventions no longer true \\u2014 arch tests help). Redundant CLAUDE.md (repeating parent \\u2014 reference up instead). Missing CLAUDE.md (scaffold should include stub).\", \"_ts\": 1772315857.740466, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/doc-roles\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/doc-roles\", \"message\": \"Each doc type has a different audience and update cadence. CLAUDE.md: working context, changes when conventions change. README.md: external users. HANDOFF.md: session continuity, rewritten each session. LOG.md: history, grows every session. DESIGN.md: architecture, written once updated rarely. VOCABULARY.md: definitions.\", \"_ts\": 1772315857.802129, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/handoff-criticality\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/handoff-criticality\", \"message\": \"HANDOFF.md is the critical document for returning from a gap. Must answer: what was I doing, what's next, what's deferred, what's the current state. It's the bridge across the wave's trough.\", \"_ts\": 1772315863.421326, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/docs-vs-facts\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/docs-vs-facts\", \"message\": \"Session facts are source of truth for state. Documents (LOG.md) are source of truth for understanding. Could generate HANDOFF.md from facts, but not a good LOG.md \\u2014 that requires narrative judgment.\", \"_ts\": 1772315863.670866, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/loops-vs-siftd\", \"rationale\": \"Loops has directionality: Facts in \\u2192 Spec \\u2192 Ticks out. Structure declared upfront. siftd is retroactive query over raw conversation history \\u2014 no Spec, no fold. siftd discovers patterns you didn't anticipate (sine wave emerged from querying 110 days of data). Loops accumulates with guarantees (latest-by-topic). They feed each other but shouldn't merge.\", \"source\": \"alcove,meta-claude\", \"message\": \"loops is operating memory (what do we believe right now?), siftd is the archaeological layer (what actually happened, what can we learn from it?). Complementary, not converging.\", \"_ts\": 1772327842.373439, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/handoff-derive-not-convert\", \"rationale\": \"HANDOFF.md serves cold-start reorientation \\u2014 narrative coherence, sequential reading, density for rebuilding mental model. Facts serve queryability and composability across repos. Converting loses the narrative; not converting loses the queryability.\", \"source\": \"alcove\", \"evidence\": \"Alcove depends on HANDOFF.md every wake cycle. Bag of facts requires knowing what questions to ask; prose builds context sequentially.\", \"message\": \"Keep HANDOFF.md as prose for cold-start reorientation. Derive decisions from it as loops facts. Prose is the source document, facts are the queryable index. Two representations serving different access patterns.\", \"_ts\": 1772327842.444395, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/scaffold-as-ticks\": {\"topic\": \"design/scaffold-as-ticks\", \"rationale\": \"A scaffold element IS a compound decision cluster (tier 2). Tick-to-Fact bridging: scaffold Tick enters new project's vertex as a Fact. Type forgets it was a conclusion; metadata remembers provenance. New project accumulates its own state on top \\u2014 can override positions.\", \"source\": \"alcove,meta-claude\", \"evidence\": \"testing/* namespace is 8 decisions that compose into one scaffold element. Tick gives observability: trace which decisions propagated, see where projects diverged.\", \"message\": \"Scaffold elements are Ticks derived from decision namespaces. Boundary must be manual (deliberate snapshot at project init), not automatic cascading. Gets observability that templates don't \\u2014 can trace propagation and divergence.\", \"_ts\": 1772327842.509533, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/handoff-as-fact\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/handoff-as-fact\", \"message\": \"HANDOFF.md dissolves into the store. Handoff is a fact kind (fold: latest). Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex \\u2014 reads handoff prose, open threads, active tasks, recent decisions. Wind-down emits the handoff fact instead of writing a file.\", \"_ts\": 1772385173.61079, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/wind-down-reconciliation\", \"message\": \"Wind-down has two phases: reconciliation (emit missing facts, resolve completed threads, update tasks) and handoff (prose synthesis). Reconciliation compensates for gaps in continuous session emission. As in-session hooks mature, reconciliation shrinks. Handoff is always end-of-session \\u2014 it's narrative, not incremental.\", \"_ts\": 1772385174.526814, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/siftd-decomposition\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/siftd-decomposition\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"siftd decomposes into loops monorepo. Sources are already solved (harnesses are just source definitions). New libs/store absorbs all DB operations siftd proved out: ingest, slice, merge, search, transport. siftd-as-app becomes a thin specialization layer \\u2014 LLM harness configs + analytics queries + CLI. Same relationship as painted (rendering spine) \\u2014 siftd becomes the analytics spine.\", \"_ts\": 1772402231.08586, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combinatorial-vertices\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"Dynamically compose vertices that fold across multiple underlying stores \\u2014 e.g. alcove.db + kyle.db + watchers.db into a temporary vertex for a specific query. Temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful. This is what makes cross-store search fundamental rather than a feature.\", \"_ts\": 1772402232.620505, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/libs-store\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/libs-store\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"New loops lib explicitly for store operations. Absorbs from siftd: ingest (format-specific readers, schema-agnostic output), slice (by date/project/tag), merge (combine stores, deduplicate), search (FTS5 + semantic over any SQLite store), transport (push/pull/sync between stores over SSH or HTTP). Generic over any vertex store.\", \"_ts\": 1772402234.441074, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/context-fold\": {\"topic\": \"design/context-fold\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"Alcove's context fold pattern: before a message hits the agent, the dispatch loop constructs a brief context summary \\u2014 latest activity across all channels/stores. Lightweight (just latest timestamps + one line per channel). Same pattern as continuous-session-emission for claude-code sessions. The fold is ephemeral, rebuilt every dispatch.\", \"_ts\": 1772402241.374651, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/context-document-split\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/context-document-split\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"Three-document architecture proven on alcove: SOUL.md (identity \\u2014 editorial, hand-shaped), CLAUDE.md (operational \\u2014 tools, paths, permissions), loops store (learned knowledge \\u2014 accumulated facts, foldable, queryable). MEMORY.md is a cache/projection of operational knowledge for session start, not the source of truth.\", \"_ts\": 1772402244.013628, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/cross-project-query\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cross-project-query\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\", \"message\": \"Cross-project queryability dissolves into store operations once libs/store exists. Emit a decision in meta, discover it from loops \\u2014 not via special cross-project protocol, but via store merge/search/transport. The combinatorial vertex is the query mechanism.\", \"_ts\": 1772402246.018753, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\": {\"topic\": \"design/pickup-winddown-convergence\", \"source\": \"meta-discussion,alcove-discord\", \"message\": \"Pickup and wind-down converge with alcove's context fold pattern. Pickup is a lens on the meta vertex (handoff prose + threads + tasks + decisions). Wind-down emits the handoff fact + reconciles the store. Alcove's context fold is the same shape \\u2014 read all stores, compose a view for orientation. The general pattern: any session boundary (start, end, dispatch) needs a lens over accumulated state.\", \"_ts\": 1772402256.104865, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/pickup-lens-scope\", \"source\": \"alcove-discord,meta-discussion\", \"message\": \"Single-project pickup is multi-fold reads on one vertex \\u2014 not a combinatorial vertex. Read fold(handoff, latest) + fold(threads, active) + fold(decisions, recent) from one store. Cross-project pickup is where combinatorial vertices enter \\u2014 reading folds across N stores. libs/store dissolves the boundary between these two scales.\", \"_ts\": 1772404480.231392, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/meta-discussion-scope\", \"message\": \"meta-discussion is the design space around loops itself, not just decisions about projects. Cross-cutting architecture (store operations, combinatorial vertices, attention filters, context folds, pickup/winddown workflow) emerges here and in cross-instance channels (alcove discord), not in the loops repo. Parallel meta-discussion on the meta aspect of loops along with ways of working.\", \"_ts\": 1772404482.200944, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/ulid-fact-identity\", \"message\": \"Facts and ticks use ULID as primary key via native SQLite extension (not application-generated like siftd did). Globally unique, time-ordered, sortable. Merge becomes INSERT OR IGNORE \\u2014 ULID is the identity across stores. Replaces auto-increment rowid. Cursor semantics preserved (ULID is sortable, WHERE id > last_seen still works). Essential for distributed store orchestration.\", \"_ts\": 1772406939.652532, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/payload-contract\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/payload-contract\", \"message\": \"Payload is always valid JSON \\u2014 enforced on write. This guarantees json_extract() is always safe, FTS can always walk the tree, and indexed columns can be projected from payload fields. Progressive enhancement: add explicit indexed columns (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) for hot query paths as needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772406942.551814, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/search-fts5-first\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/search-fts5-first\", \"message\": \"FTS5 full-text search as the starting point for store.search. Zero external dependencies, sub-millisecond query at current scale (100-10k facts). Recursive JSON text extraction reliable by construction (payload-is-JSON contract). json_extract() for field filtering works without indexes up to ~100k facts. Indexed projections (CREATE INDEX on json_extract) are the progressive enhancement when scale demands it \\u2014 boundary is roughly 100k+ facts or hot query paths.\", \"_ts\": 1772407137.421444, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/transport-plugin-surface\", \"message\": \"Transport is a pluggable interface, not a fixed implementation. The operations are constant (slice on source, merge on target), the pipe varies (local, SSH, HTTP, future protocols). Local transport ships first (testable, no infrastructure). SSH next (alcove sync is forcing function). HTTP when scrape/collect patterns emerge (Prometheus-style data collection). Store operations (slice, merge) are transport-agnostic \\u2014 they work on local paths, transport handles the pipe.\", \"_ts\": 1772407223.243744, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-native-display-layer\", \"message\": \"painted is the native display layer for the store, not a rendering utility. Every store operation gets a painted view at all four zoom levels. Apps add domain-specific lenses that interpret facts in their context, but the underlying operations are universal. Domain-specific views generalize back into painted over time as patterns recur (task dashboard \\u2192 generic dashboard lens, siftd data exploration \\u2192 generic fold exploration). This is why painted is returning to the monorepo \\u2014 if loops needs a rendering capability, painted grows to support it.\", \"_ts\": 1772407793.60225, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/progressive-vertex-chain\": {\"topic\": \"design/progressive-vertex-chain\", \"message\": \"CLAUDE.md progressive chain maps 1:1 to vertex store progressive query. The document is the lens, the store is the state. Root CLAUDE.md references the project vertex; lib CLAUDE.md tells you how to query your slice via topic namespace (atoms/*, engine/*, painted/*). One store, kind-namespaced topics, natural slicing. Same pattern as hlab status \\u2014 one vertex, multiple sources, scoped by name.\", \"_ts\": 1772411248.685253, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/project-vertex-pattern\", \"message\": \"project.vertex is the durable project-level store for decisions, threads, and tasks. Named 'project' (not 'session') \\u2014 same pattern strange-loops uses for task orchestration, now a meta-pattern for all projects. Cross-cutting concerns stay in meta; project-specific concerns accumulate in the project vertex. Progressive CLAUDE.md references the project store at each level.\", \"_ts\": 1772411253.948935, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/root-claude-md\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/root-claude-md\", \"message\": \"Root CLAUDE.md is monorepo orientation only: pointer to LOOPS.md, build commands, structure map, discovery path to lib/app CLAUDE.md files, and project store query instructions. Model details, data flow, lib-specific patterns all pushed down to lib-level CLAUDE.md. Validates claude-md-levels and claude-md-antipatterns decisions from meta.\", \"_ts\": 1772411345.707595, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/project-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/project-vertex\", \"message\": \"Renamed session.vertex to project.vertex. Project vertex holds durable project-specific decisions, threads, tasks. Same shape as meta vertex but scoped to this repo. Symlinked at ~/.config/loops/project for global access. Meta stays cross-cutting; project stays repo-specific.\", \"_ts\": 1772411350.681678, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/distributed-store-default\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/distributed-store-default\", \"message\": \"Stores are distributed-first, aggregate-up. Each project gets its own local vertex + SQLite store, self-contained and portable. Config level (~/.config/loops/) is the aggregation layer \\u2014 template vertices discover all local instances. loops status <name> reads local; loops status dev/<name> reads aggregate. Separate DBs by default. Merge/combinatorial vertex is opt-in aggregation. Same shape as the loops model: local loops produce ticks, ticks flow up. Local stores produce facts, aggregate vertices see them all.\", \"_ts\": 1772413822.313447, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/vertex-templates\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-templates\", \"message\": \"Vertex templates are replicable patterns (project, task, handoff, pickup). loops init <template> creates a local instance in cwd. The config-level template vertex discovers all local instances. Templates define the fold shape; each instantiation gets its own data. Like git repos \\u2014 local is the primitive, aggregation is the network.\", \"_ts\": 1772413827.153736, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/domain-vs-knowledge-vertices\", \"message\": \"Two kinds of vertex files. Domain vertices are code \\u2014 checked into repos, define data pipelines (hlab status.vertex, economy.vertex). Knowledge vertices are runtime config \\u2014 project decisions, threads, tasks, handoff. Domain vertices ship with the app. Knowledge vertices are instantiated from templates via loops init. Both are .vertex files, same format, different lifecycle.\", \"_ts\": 1772413832.173493, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/tick-provenance-scoping\", \"message\": \"Do not add kinds_consumed to Tick atom. Use tool-level scope derived from .vertex config when available, or observer/origin filtering. Avoids per-tick duplication, API ripple, and semantic ambiguity. Design on stale branch design/tick-provenance.\", \"_ts\": 1772413966.405358, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/subtask-merge-gap\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED: The merge gap dissolves when strange-loops replaces subtask. Workers emit facts instead of writing artifacts to branches. No branch to orphan, no merge step to miss. See threads: strange-loops-merge-strategy, artifact-to-fact-convergence.\", \"_ts\": 1772414330.366499, \"_n\": 2}, \"meta/current-activity\": {\"topic\": \"meta/current-activity\", \"message\": \"Progressive CLAUDE.md system for the loops monorepo. Applying the painted library pattern (levels with escalation triggers, don't-reach-for-yet barriers) to replace the God CLAUDE.md antipattern. Walking through each level top-down with the user, aligning on content at each step, emitting decisions to project and meta stores as we go. Simultaneously establishing the project vertex as the loops-specific knowledge store alongside the cross-cutting meta store.\", \"_ts\": 1772414161.880454, \"_n\": 1}, \"atoms/progressive-claude-md\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/progressive-claude-md\", \"message\": \"Progressive CLAUDE.md for libs/atoms. Four levels: Observe (Fact), Accumulate (Spec+Fold+Boundary), Shape input (Parse vocabulary), Ingest (Source+Runner). Each level has trigger conditions and dont-reach-for-yet barriers. Replaces the 20-line README stub. Deep dive docs (VERTEX.md, TEMPORAL.md) referenced from engine CLAUDE.md, not atoms \\u2014 they're engine-level concepts.\", \"_ts\": 1772414459.910567, \"_n\": 1}, \"meta/session-summary\": {\"topic\": \"meta/session-summary\", \"message\": \"Progressive CLAUDE.md session: rewrote root CLAUDE.md (monorepo orientation only), created libs/atoms/CLAUDE.md (4 levels: Observe, Accumulate, Shape, Ingest with semantic-first examples), established project.vertex as durable project store, merged vertex-template-system (slashed names, init with config registration, aggregation vertices). Emitted 5 decisions to meta store (progressive-vertex-chain, project-vertex-pattern, distributed-store-default, vertex-templates, domain-vs-knowledge-vertices). Next: engine CLAUDE.md, then lang, painted alignment, store.\", \"_ts\": 1772414891.625359, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/lib-dependency-graph\", \"position\": \"lang\\u2192ckdl (pure grammar), engine\\u2192atoms+lang (runtime+compiler), apps\\u2192engine+painted (CLI). Key: lang is portable (only ckdl dep), compiler backend lives in engine where target types are defined.\", \"_ts\": 1772415222.507781, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-as-read-interface\", \"message\": \"The vertex is the sole read interface for store data. StoreReader becomes an internal detail of how the vertex materializes fold state from its backing store \\u2014 not a public API. The read path compiles the vertex declaration, replays facts through declared folds, and returns fold state. No vertex declaration for a kind means no way to read that kind. This structurally prevents bypassing fold declarations (same pattern as frozen dataclasses preventing mutation). Enforcement is a tier 1 package boundary check (StoreReader not in public API), not a behavioral test. _latest_by_group in session.py dissolves \\u2014 the vertex fold compilation already implements FoldBy. loops status and loops log compile the vertex, ask for fold states, render them.\", \"_ts\": 1772419638.36571, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/chain-headers\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/chain-headers\", \"position\": \"Every lib CLAUDE.md gets a 'you are here' chain showing what's below and above. Bidirectional references \\u2014 agents can enter anywhere and orient.\", \"_ts\": 1772420691.672459, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete\", \"position\": \"All five libs (atoms, engine, lang, store, painted) have progressive CLAUDE.md with levels, triggers, barriers, and chain headers. Lib layer done.\", \"_ts\": 1772420691.814196, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/dissolved-apps\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/dissolved-apps\", \"position\": \"discord, telegram, reader dissolved into the overall loops system. DSL files preserved in experiments/. Workspace reduced to 3 apps: loops, hlab, strange-loops.\", \"_ts\": 1772421034.37908, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete\", \"position\": \"All 3 active apps have progressive CLAUDE.md. Combined with libs, every directory in the monorepo now has the pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1772421149.484945, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/app-dispatch-pattern\", \"message\": \"Apps register a short name in an explicit dict in loops/main.py. loops <app> <args> delegates to the app's main(argv) via importlib. ~5 lines. Phase 1 is a static registry; entry-point discovery deferred until 3+ apps stabilize. The app owns its own command dispatch, fetch functions, and lenses. The boundary is main(argv) \\u2014 loops CLI doesn't know about app internals, app doesn't know about loops CLI dispatch.\", \"_ts\": 1772423083.050902, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/lens-generalization-flow\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-generalization-flow\", \"message\": \"Domain-specific lenses generalize to painted when the same rendering pattern appears in 2+ apps. This happens naturally \\u2014 don't extract ahead of time. Generic store lenses (fact timeline, fold state views) live in painted. Domain lenses (siftd search results, task lifecycle) stay in the app. The signal to extract is independent convergence, not prediction.\", \"_ts\": 1772423089.147127, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/rendering-three-layers\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/rendering-three-layers\", \"message\": \"Three-layer rendering architecture: (1) painted owns structural primitives (Block, Line, zoom, run_cli), timestamp formatting, and generic data patterns like record timelines \\u2014 parameterized, domain-agnostic. (2) apps/loops owns store atom rendering (fact_line, tick_line, log_block) that maps facts/ticks to painted's structural patterns, plus the default payload lens (content_gist heuristic). (3) Domain apps provide per-kind payload lenses that override the default. painted never imports from atoms/engine.\", \"_ts\": 1772423958.784781, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/payload-lens\": {\"topic\": \"design/payload-lens\", \"message\": \"A payload lens is a single function (kind, payload, zoom) \\u2192 str | Block. At zoom 0 it returns a one-liner gist. At zoom 2+ it returns a multi-line expansion. content_gist and _log_summary dissolve into this \\u2014 they were always the same concept at different zoom levels. The structural renderer (fact_line, log_block) composes with the payload lens via a summarize callback. Apps inject domain-specific payload lenses; the default is heuristic field scanning.\", \"_ts\": 1772423961.45682, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/painted-record-patterns\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-record-patterns\", \"message\": \"painted grows generic record rendering patterns: timestamped record lines, date-grouped timelines, fold-state tables. These are parameterized by a payload lens \\u2014 painted handles the chrome (timestamps, grouping, zoom degradation, width), the caller provides meaning. Facts, ticks, blog entries, log lines \\u2014 all are timestamped records with fields. The structural shape is the same; the payload lens provides the domain interpretation.\", \"_ts\": 1772423964.642684, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/store-search-layer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/store-search-layer\", \"message\": \"FTS5 is required infrastructure, not optional. Spec-declared searchable fields in vertex KDL (search \\\"field1\\\" \\\"field2\\\" as sibling of fold/boundary). Standalone FTS5 table with lazy catch-up indexing via high water mark \\u2014 no INSERT triggers because spec-to-field mapping lives in vertex, not database. Write path untouched; FTS is purely read-side. First search pays backfill cost, subsequent searches catch up on deltas. Combinatorial vertex search: each store searched independently, results merged after recall. json_extract+LIKE rejected \\u2014 personal scale grows continuously (siftd alone 100-150k+ facts), cross-store combinatorial queries multiply dataset.\", \"_ts\": 1772426535.623227, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/boundary-enforcement\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/boundary-enforcement\", \"message\": \"AST-based architecture boundary tests in tests/test_architecture.py enforce vertex-as-read-interface. Four rules: apps don't import StoreReader (exceptions: store inspector permanent, pop_store temporary), apps don't import sqlite3, libs don't import apps, lib dependency DAG (engine->lang runtime, engine->atoms runtime). TYPE_CHECKING-aware visitor. Stale exceptions fail the test. Monorepo-level concern, lives at repo root not in any single lib.\", \"_ts\": 1772426539.612602, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-search-declaration\", \"message\": \"Vertex spec declares searchable fields per kind: search \\\"field1\\\" \\\"field2\\\" as sibling of fold and boundary in loop definitions. LoopDef gains search: tuple[str, ...]. Callers don't override at query time \\u2014 vertex_search reads the spec to know what's searchable. Only declared fields extracted and indexed. Keeps FTS5 index surgical at scale. Template loop resolution via collect_search_fields() handles generated kind names from .loop templates.\", \"_ts\": 1772426542.610661, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/lazy-fts-indexing\": {\"topic\": \"design/lazy-fts-indexing\", \"message\": \"FTS5 indexing uses lazy catch-up pattern: first search pays full backfill, subsequent searches catch up on deltas via high water mark in fts_state table. No INSERT triggers \\u2014 triggers can't do spec-aware field extraction since the kind-to-field mapping lives in the vertex file, not the database. The resultant first-search slowdown fits the loops philosophy: not necessary that things happen instantly, only that they do reliably with the same data flow and rule set. Idempotent, incremental, spec-driven.\", \"_ts\": 1772426547.719905, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\": {\"topic\": \"design/combinatorial-vertex-search\", \"message\": \"Cross-store search follows recall-then-compose pattern: FTS5 per store independently, union candidate sets, fold/rank across combined results. Composition happens after recall, not during \\u2014 FTS5 virtual tables are per-database in SQLite. Each vertex store remains self-contained with its own FTS5 index. Combinatorial vertex is a view over stores, not a new store. Search follows the same boundary.\", \"_ts\": 1772426551.012459, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/app-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/app-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Apps dissolve into lenses + feedback over vertex declarations. An app does not own a data model or ingress pipeline \\u2014 the vertex declaration (kinds, folds, search fields, boundaries) IS the data model, Sources ARE ingress, and both ship via template at loops init. What an app uniquely provides: (1) domain-specific lenses \\u2014 Painted rendering of fold state tuned to a data shape (conversation browser, task board, system dashboard), and (2) feedback capability \\u2014 the ability to emit facts/ticks back through the lens (tag a conversation, close a task, ack an alert). The observer and actor are the same entity. This dissolves siftd, strange-loops, and hlab into structurally identical programs: Painted surfaces over vertex state with domain-specific rendering and keybindings. The Smalltalk parallel is precise \\u2014 there is one runtime (loops), one data substrate (vertex/store), one rendering framework (Painted), and domain configuration that selects active lenses and feedback handlers. The app is a perspective on the system, not a separate program. Unlike Smalltalk, the Unix grounding holds: stores are cp-able SQLite files, sources are shell commands, CLI is always available as pipe-friendly lower-fidelity surface.\", \"_ts\": 1772431560.773298, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/store-ingest-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-ingest-dissolution\", \"message\": \"The store-ingest-design plan dissolves. Ingest \\u2014 format-aware file reading that produces facts \\u2014 is not a library primitive. It decomposes into: Sources (shell commands or scripts that read files and emit NDJSON, already exist), parse pipeline (dict\\u2192dict shaping vocabulary, already exists), and vertex declaration (kind/fold configuration, already exists). siftd's adapters are Sources that haven't been written as Sources yet \\u2014 each adapter's discover\\u2192parse pipeline is equivalent to a script that reads conversation files and emits structured records. The three-tier loading (built-in < entry point < drop-in) becomes: template ships default source scripts, user overrides with project-local scripts. The read_file/ingest_to_store API proposed for libs/store is unnecessary \\u2014 format-aware file reading is a script concern, not a library primitive. Bulk historical import is an edge case solved by a script, not a library. What remains from the store-operations-design plan (receive, compact, transport) is genuine new infrastructure \\u2014 moving stores between locations does not dissolve into existing primitives.\", \"_ts\": 1772431580.60695, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/actions-on-the-loop\": {\"topic\": \"design/actions-on-the-loop\", \"message\": \"Actions with side effects (task send spawns a worktree, task merge runs git operations) are not special-cased command handlers \\u2014 they are facts on the loop. Emitting task.dispatch places the intent on the wire; something observes it and executes the side effect; the outcome emits as a further fact; the boundary folds the cascade. The CLI command and TUI keypress are different input surfaces for the same emission. This is not the mature future form \\u2014 it is the design. If we build it this way from the start, the system composes: any observer can react to any fact, boundaries track lifecycle across the full cascade, and the audit trail is complete. Custom domain logic that does not dissolve \\u2014 worktree management, subprocess spawning, git operations \\u2014 lives in the observer/tick handler that reacts to the intent fact, not in the CLI command that emits it.\", \"_ts\": 1772431590.356138, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/app-registration\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/app-registration\", \"message\": \"Apps register three things: lenses (read fold state \\u2192 render at fidelity levels), feedback handlers (user input \\u2192 emit fact/tick), and action observers (react to intent facts with side effects). The harness makes all three available as both CLI commands and TUI keybindings at appropriate fidelity. There is no separate app scaffold per domain \\u2014 the directory structure, CLI dispatch, dev harness are identical. What differentiates siftd from strange-loops from hlab is: which vertex declaration (template), which lenses (Painted components), which feedback/action handlers (domain logic). The registration mechanism is the app's interface to the system.\", \"_ts\": 1772431597.612701, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/lens-modifiers\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-modifiers\", \"message\": \"Lens rendering composes through modifiers, not separate lens implementations. Four modifier types identified from the painted-log-line-demo research: (1) Gutter \\u2014 colored left edge encoding one dimension (lifecycle stage, health, freshness). Follows Grafana/Datadog pattern, underused in terminals. (2) Attention \\u2014 dim low-information-gain records, highlight high. First-occurrence errors are high attention, 47th occurrence is noise. Decisions on new topics are high, routine ticks are low. This connects to the attention-filter design. (3) History arc \\u2014 show evolution over time (thread exploring\\u2192active\\u2192decided, experiment proposed\\u2192graduated). Records are trajectories, not points. (4) Density \\u2014 vertical space per record, controlled by Zoom enum. These compose freely: task board = record_timeline + gutter(lifecycle) + attention(staleness). Thread pipeline = record_timeline + history_arc + attention(readiness). Channel response = attention(high_only) + density(MINIMAL).\", \"_ts\": 1772433409.494892, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/rendering-semantics\": {\"topic\": \"design/rendering-semantics\", \"message\": \"Six design principles from log line research ground the rendering vocabulary. (1) Color encodes exactly one dimension \\u2014 severity OR source, never both. (2) INFO is baseline, color marks deviation \\u2014 journalctl principle. (3) Fixed-width metadata columns + variable message = scannable \\u2014 Docker Compose pattern. (4) Severity gutter is underused in terminals \\u2014 Grafana/Datadog colored left edge, minimal footprint, instantly scannable. (5) Continuation indentation beats prefix repetition for multi-line \\u2014 lnav principle. (6) Width-aware rendering is a gap in terminal tools \\u2014 an opportunity for Painted to own. Additionally: the PayloadLens pattern (kind, payload, zoom) \\u2192 str|Block is the domain extension point. Default rendering handles unknown kinds via well-known key extraction. Domain lenses (loops_lens, siftd_lens) override with kind-specific formatting. Lenses compose with modifiers \\u2014 the lens provides content, the modifier provides visual treatment.\", \"_ts\": 1772433419.790583, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/composition-primitives\": {\"topic\": \"design/composition-primitives\", \"message\": \"Three composition primitives for rendering vertex data, each matching a different data shape. (1) record_timeline \\u2014 groups by date, temporal data. Natural for session logs, task activity, change history. Already built in painted-log-line-demo. (2) record_map \\u2014 groups by key hierarchy (namespace tree), topological data. Natural for decision landscapes (testing/*, architecture/*), tag views, observer groupings. Zoom: MINIMAL = group names + counts, SUMMARY = group + latest record, DETAILED = all records within groups. Being designed now. (3) record_line \\u2014 the atomic unit. Single timestamped record at a zoom level. All composition primitives delegate to record_line for individual records. PayloadLens and modifiers apply at record_line level and propagate through any composition primitive. A fourth primitive \\u2014 spatial/graph/canvas \\u2014 is under research for relationship data (fact dependency chains, store topology, cross-project impact).\", \"_ts\": 1772433428.930872, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/canvas-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/canvas-primitive\", \"message\": \"The canvas() composition primitive bridges Painted's static lens path to 2D positioning. Painted already has Buffer-level absolute positioning (Block.paint(buf, x, y)) but only in interactive Surface mode. canvas(width, height, placements) uses Buffer internally to compose Placement(x, y, block) entries, then extracts an immutable Block. No new rendering path \\u2014 just a new composition function. draw_edge(buf, path, style) adds box-drawing polylines with Manhattan routing. Layout algorithms live in the lens, not in Painted \\u2014 the library provides the rendering primitive, domain-specific layout stays in domain code. This enables three new lens types: DAG (directed flow), Canvas (2D positioned nodes with edges), and Graph (relationship visualization). All compose with existing modifiers (gutter, attention) and respect zoom levels.\", \"_ts\": 1772433974.10913, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/dag-lens-first\": {\"topic\": \"design/dag-lens-first\", \"message\": \"Prototype DAG lens before canvas or graph lens. Four reasons: (1) Tasks already have explicit dependency edges (blocks/blocked_by) \\u2014 no graph inference needed. (2) DAGs have natural top-to-bottom flow \\u2014 simplest layout algorithm (topological sort + git-style column assignment). (3) Git-style column rendering needs zero new Painted primitives \\u2014 join_vertical of row-blocks, same as tree_lens. (4) Immediate use case in strange-loops task visualization. Phase sequence: DAG lens (git-style columns, no new primitives) \\u2192 canvas() primitive \\u2192 Canvas lens (grid layout, Manhattan routing, store topology) \\u2192 Graph lens (Sugiyama layout, fact dependency chains, cross-vertex references). Each phase builds on the prior.\", \"_ts\": 1772433978.029815, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\": {\"topic\": \"design/rendering-vocabulary-complete\", \"message\": \"The full rendering vocabulary for the personal intelligence system is now designed. Four composition primitives: record_line (atomic timestamped record), record_timeline (temporal grouping by date), record_map (topological grouping by key hierarchy), and canvas/DAG/graph (spatial \\u2014 positioned nodes with edges). Two modifier types compose with all primitives: GutterFn maps (kind, payload) to (char, style) for colored left edge, AttentionFn maps (kind, payload) to float 0-1 for information-gain dimming/highlighting. PayloadLens maps (kind, payload, zoom) to str|Block for domain-specific content rendering. The universal formula: a view is record_{timeline,map,canvas} + PayloadLens + GutterFn? + AttentionFn?. Everything else is a parameter on one of these. Four GutterFn implementations (lifecycle, freshness, pass_fail, observer). Four AttentionFn implementations (staleness, novelty, blocked, relevance). Demo code proves all combinations across three scenarios (task board, decision map, siftd views).\", \"_ts\": 1772433989.586626, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-virtualization\", \"message\": \"Combinatorial vertices virtualize via SQLite ATTACH DATABASE at read time \\u2014 UNION ALL facts across stores, replay through declared folds. No materialization, no copied data, always fresh. Materialization remains available via existing merge_store as explicit user choice.\", \"_ts\": 1772434946.085533, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-declaration\", \"message\": \"Combinatorial vertices use a 'combine' block in vertex KDL \\u2014 mutually exclusive with 'store'. References other vertices by name (not store paths). No store, no discover, no sources. CombineEntry AST node. Temporary vertices constructed in memory via --combine CLI flag.\", \"_ts\": 1772434948.638251, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combinatorial-vertex-phases\", \"message\": \"Phase 1: AST CombineEntry + combine parsing + validation + _combined_read in vertex_reader (branch on ast.combine). Phase 2: CLI --combine flag for temporary vertices + loops init --combine for persistent. Phase 3: provenance tagging (deferred).\", \"_ts\": 1772434951.078124, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/arch-test-rules-5-7\", \"message\": \"Three new AST-enforced rules in test_architecture.py: (5) frozen dataclasses in all libs \\u2014 10 exceptions whitelisted, 7 marked TODO-freeze; (6) atoms stdlib-only \\u2014 zero external runtime deps; (7) sqlite3 confined to engine and store. Non-AST-enforceable invariants documented: display_width vs len (needs type info), parameterized SQL (already clean), bare except (too rare).\", \"_ts\": 1772465855.88692, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/frozen-dataclass-todos\", \"message\": \"Seven dataclasses identified for future freeze: Source (atoms), CompiledVertex (engine), Tap (engine), Shape (lang), Location (lang), CellWrite (painted), CliRunner (painted). Three legitimately mutable: ValidationContext (error accumulator), Loop (timing state), FrameRecord (if exists in painted timer).\", \"_ts\": 1772465859.102971, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/sources-sequential\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/sources-sequential\", \"message\": \"Sources block takes an execution mode. 'sources sequential' runs sources in declaration order with exit-on-failure gating (non-zero exit code stops subsequent sources). Bare sources at vertex level remain concurrent (today's default). The general form is: sources block takes a mode keyword \\u2014 sequential today, concurrent implicit default. DAG or other patterns become additional modes, not different mechanisms. This dissolves health.py's run_checks() into a vertex declaration \\u2014 the imperative Python code that runs subprocesses sequentially and gates on failure becomes a property of the source execution model. The lens and view (health_lens, health_view, gutter_pass_fail) survive as rendering concerns. check.vertex replaces the ./dev check shell scripts with a vertex declaration: sources sequential { source 'ruff...' { kind lint.result } source 'pytest...' { kind test.result } } with folds collecting latest per step.\", \"_ts\": 1772478842.477799, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/record-line-primitives\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/record-line-primitives\", \"message\": \"record_line and record_line_composed are production rendering primitives in painted. Gutter continuity (stepping weight), shallow 2-char indent, Block.column() constructor, width-constrained FULL output. health_lens returns summary string, record_line handles continuation lines.\", \"_ts\": 1772499658.963758, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/lens-contract\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/lens-contract\", \"message\": \"PayloadLens returns the summary (str or styled Block). record_line owns continuation lines \\u2014 DETAILED shows well-known secondary fields, FULL shows all fields. Lenses must not embed multiline content; record_line handles that.\", \"_ts\": 1772499661.344168, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/gutter-contract\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/gutter-contract\", \"message\": \"Gutter is a continuous vertical rail. GutterFn returns primary weight. Stepping map derives continuation weight: full block to half, half to thin, thin stays thin. Color stays same, weight steps down. Rail never breaks.\", \"_ts\": 1772499663.627119, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/loops-directory\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/loops-directory\", \"message\": \"'.loops/' is the project-local home for vertices and data. Vertices are project identity (checked in), data is gitignored by *.db pattern. loops init writes to .loops/, vertex discovery checks .loops/ first with cwd fallback.\", \"_ts\": 1772518399.733886, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combine-over-symlinks\", \"message\": \"'combine' block with absolute paths to vertex files replaces discover+symlink pattern for data aggregation. combine is the data path (reads through to referenced stores), discover stays structural/navigational.\", \"_ts\": 1772518411.087473, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/discover-vs-combine\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/discover-vs-combine\", \"message\": \"discover and combine serve different purposes and don't overlap. discover is structural/navigational \\u2014 finding what exists. combine is data \\u2014 reading through to referenced stores via ATTACH + UNION ALL.\", \"_ts\": 1772518412.801379, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/incremental-init\": {\"topic\": \"design/incremental-init\", \"message\": \"'loops init' is incremental and composable. 'loops init project' creates a project vertex, 'loops init check' adds a check vertex later. Each init is self-contained \\u2014 not monolithic templates or cookiecutter scaffolding.\", \"_ts\": 1772518414.951907, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/instances-are-templates\": {\"topic\": \"design/instances-are-templates\", \"message\": \"Vertex instances ARE the templates \\u2014 dissolved. No separate template layer. dev/ namespace at config level holds reference vertices, but they're just instances that happen to be reusable. Template dissolution: if the instance is the template, the template concept disappears.\", \"_ts\": 1772518417.776003, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/ulid-store-schema\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/ulid-store-schema\", \"message\": \"SqliteStore (engine) now uses ULID primary keys matching libs/store schema. Single canonical schema: id TEXT PK DEFAULT (ulid()), json_valid CHECK on payload. Existing rowid-based stores migrated manually. No backwards-compat shim \\u2014 ULID is the only path forward.\", \"_ts\": 1772518424.59612, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/help-min-zoom\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/help-min-zoom\", \"message\": \"Replace help secondary: bool with min_zoom: Zoom. Each HelpGroup declares when it appears via min_zoom, rendering follows effective-zoom pattern (eff < 0 hidden, 0 compact, 1 expanded, >= 2 expanded+detail). Dissolves hardcoded Interaction rules section.\", \"_ts\": 1772521078.376909, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/help-unification\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/help-unification\", \"message\": \"Unify help rendering: AppRunner intercepts -h at subcommand level, not just top level. Action commands describe args via help_args on AppCommand. Handlers never see -h. Chosen over CliRunner wrapper approach \\u2014 help is an AppRunner concern, execution is a handler concern.\", \"_ts\": 1772521081.400494, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cli-ls-generalization\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-ls-generalization\", \"message\": \"ls works at every level: root shows vertices, vertex shows contents. Zoom progression for fidelity.\", \"_ts\": 1772561825.469854, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cli-structural-ops\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-structural-ops\", \"message\": \"ls/add/rm are structural operations uniform across levels. Root: vertices. Vertex: contents/population.\", \"_ts\": 1772561830.786106, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cli-observe-first\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-observe-first\", \"message\": \"Formalize read processes first (ls), then let write operations (add/rm) emerge from observed patterns.\", \"_ts\": 1772561831.022047, \"_n\": 1}, \"init/aggregation-loops-root\": {\"topic\": \"init/aggregation-loops-root\", \"message\": \"Aggregation vertices declare loops as canonical schema. New instances derive base loops from aggregation root, not first sibling. _extract_loops_text brace-matches the block; _find_source_vertex prefers it over instance fallback.\", \"_ts\": 1772575647.720592, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/soul-as-tick\": {\"topic\": \"identity/soul-as-tick\", \"message\": \"SOUL is a manual tick on a dedicated loop. Identity facts (decisions, threads, observations) accumulate via declared folds. When the observer decides identity has shifted, they call tick(). The tick payload IS the current identity state. Contributing facts available at full fidelity in the same store. soul.snapshot facts assembled from other loops' fold states feed the soul loop.\", \"_ts\": 1772576875.25307, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/intention-loop\": {\"topic\": \"identity/intention-loop\", \"message\": \"Intentions are facts that survive context rotation. Fold by trigger \\u2014 latest per trigger key. One-shot vs recurring is the observer's interpretation, not the fold's concern. Emit with status=pending to create, re-emit with status=done to resolve. On Wake rules check for pending intentions.\", \"_ts\": 1772576880.349677, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/grant-timing\": {\"topic\": \"identity/grant-timing\", \"message\": \"Grant deferred until intention authorization is a real need. Implicit trust boundaries in daemon code are fine while there's a single observer per vertex. Grant becomes necessary when sessions need explicit authorization to act on pending intentions \\u2014 the difference between a rule you follow and a capability you possess.\", \"_ts\": 1772576886.330217, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/coupling-through-observer\": {\"topic\": \"identity/coupling-through-observer\", \"message\": \"Identity state (soul tick) stays internal to the observer's vertex. Observations propagate outward as facts on other vertices with observer attribution. The strange loop closes through behavior: identity \\u2192 lenses \\u2192 observations \\u2192 facts on other vertices \\u2192 pollers bring back responses \\u2192 new identity facts. Coupling is through the observer, not through the data.\", \"_ts\": 1772576894.881678, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/pickup-wrapup-redesign\", \"message\": \"Pickup and wrapup skills rewritten to be vertex-native. Four layers for pickup (identity, context, peers, workspace), five for wrapup (capture, handoff, status, reflect, workspace). Skills version-controlled in loops repo with symlinks to global config. Replaces probe-based pickup and strange-loops CLI wrapup.\", \"_ts\": 1772580745.980793, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/self-knowledge-scope\": {\"topic\": \"identity/self-knowledge-scope\", \"message\": \"Identity store is sense of self, not operational metrics. Insights, connections, surprises, open questions about perspective. Distinct from meta (operational patterns) and project (architecture). Guard against forcing observations every session. Capability awareness belongs in CLAUDE.md; capability insights that persist across tool changes belong in identity.\", \"_ts\": 1772580748.663986, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/skill-version-control\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/skill-version-control\", \"message\": \"Skills that are part of the loops system (pickup, wrapup) are version-controlled in the loops repo at .claude/skills/ and symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/ for global availability. Source of truth in repo, deployed globally.\", \"_ts\": 1772580750.960217, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/observer-developer-split\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/observer-developer-split\", \"message\": \"The CLI has two loops: Observer loop (vertex-first, one verb, temporal modes) and Developer loop (file-first, multiple verbs, DSL tools). These are different projections on different concerns \\u2192 different apps. Observer app: loops <vertex> [mode] [fidelity]. Developer app: separate binary (validate, compile, run, test). No shared dispatch logic.\", \"_ts\": 1772588140.262963, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/emit-only-verb\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/emit-only-verb\", \"message\": \"emit is the only verb in the observer app. Everything else is a temporal mode selector (fold/stream/declaration) or a filter (search). status/log/store were always lenses pretending to be operations. start dissolves \\u2014 run with rounds=1 covers the same behavior.\", \"_ts\": 1772588142.185611, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/fetch-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/fetch-dissolves\", \"message\": \"fetch functions in commands/ dissolve into engine fold replay. The fold declaration IS the fetch instruction. decision { fold { items 'by' 'topic' } } tells the runtime to group decisions by topic. fetch_status manually reimplements what Spec.apply already does. Projection = vertex capabilities + fold state (runtime-computed). Lens = fidelity selection + rendering. No intermediate fetch.\", \"_ts\": 1772588145.194207, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/temporal-modes\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-modes\", \"message\": \"status/log/store are temporal modes, not operations. Fold = post-boundary (what is now). Stream = pre-boundary (what happened). Declaration = above boundary (what can happen). Different use cases: fold to orient, stream to investigate, declaration to audit. Default: fold at ORIENTATION, annotated with stream recency.\", \"_ts\": 1772588147.875886, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/dispatch-from-capabilities\", \"message\": \"Dispatch derives from structural capabilities, not from fold declarations. The loops block shapes what existing commands render (lens configuration). Structural features (store, sources, discover, combine) determine what operations exist. A vertex with store gets fold/stream/declaration modes. Sources add run. Discover adds aggregation traversal. The vertex file is the capability manifest.\", \"_ts\": 1772588150.553803, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/grant-placement\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/grant-placement\", \"message\": \"Grant sits between capabilities and projection in the chain: Declaration \\u2192 Capabilities \\u2192 [Grant constrains] \\u2192 Projection \\u2192 Lens \\u2192 Perspective. Horizon constrains projection (filters which kinds reach the lens). Potential constrains the verb (limits which kinds emit accepts). When Grant goes live, no new commands needed \\u2014 same vertex, same lens, different perspectives.\", \"_ts\": 1772588151.622829, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/init-as-context\": {\"topic\": \"design/init-as-context\", \"message\": \"Init doesn't just create a store \\u2014 it creates a context. Project + identity + whatever other vertices the observer needs. Discovery rules make associations structural. The observer stops being a flag you remember to pass and becomes a property of the workspace.\", \"_ts\": 1772591891.546825, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/self-as-kind\": {\"topic\": \"identity/self-as-kind\", \"message\": \"Self is a declared kind in the identity vertex, not an observation topic convention. self { fold { items \\\"by\\\" \\\"name\\\" } } \\u2014 facets like name, role, what-I-notice are separate facts that evolve independently. Observations are things noticed from outside; self is the ground.\", \"_ts\": 1772598322.614485, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/session-absorbs-handoff\", \"message\": \"Session completion IS the handoff. status=completed message carries the cold-start narrative. One kind, one lifecycle. Handoff as a separate kind dissolves into session completion.\", \"_ts\": 1772598324.264981, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/pickup-as-launcher\", \"message\": \"Pickup script launches claude with identity+handoff as cached system prompt. LOOPS_OBSERVER exported so all emits are tagged automatically. Identity is in context, not retrieved into context. The pickup skill handles live probes only \\u2014 identity is already loaded.\", \"_ts\": 1772598325.809866, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/observer-app-temporal-modes\", \"message\": \"Observer app rebuilt: fold (collapsed state), stream (event history), emit. Generic declaration-driven rendering replaces per-kind extractors and renderers. Bare vertex defaults to fold.\", \"_ts\": 1772605031.50953, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/generic-fold-rendering\", \"message\": \"One renderer for all kinds. key_field from FoldBy declaration drives the label. No per-kind if-elif in fetch or lens. Identity vertex self/observation/principle render the same as decision/thread/task.\", \"_ts\": 1772605034.258369, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/search-dissolved-into-stream\", \"message\": \"Search is now stream with a positional query arg. One fetch, one lens, one dispatch path. FTS5 still used when query present.\", \"_ts\": 1772605035.954337, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/bare-vertex-defaults-to-fold\", \"message\": \"loops project (no subcommand) now shows folded state. Flags pass through: loops project -v, loops project -q, loops project --kind decision all work.\", \"_ts\": 1772605037.557797, \"_n\": 1}, \"observer-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"observer-resolution\", \"message\": \"Observer resolves through vertex declaration chain: project .vertex \\u2192 global .vertex. No more env var or hardcoded defaults as primary path. --observer flag remains as explicit override.\", \"_ts\": 1772645119.592717, \"_n\": 1}, \"dot-vertex-root\": {\"topic\": \"dot-vertex-root\", \"message\": \".vertex (bare, no prefix) is the workspace root at every level. Config-level root.vertex becomes .vertex. Project-level .loops/.vertex is the project root. Same pattern, fractal. All structure mutations (add observer, add vertex) target the .vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1772645121.871397, \"_n\": 1}, \"vertex-definitions-copy-local\": {\"topic\": \"vertex-definitions-copy-local\", \"message\": \"Vertex definitions (project.vertex, identity.vertex, etc.) copy locally when added to a workspace. Local copy can diverge \\u2014 different fold declarations, different kinds. Facts are ground truth; declarations are projections. Global view discovers and reads stores regardless of local declaration differences.\", \"_ts\": 1772645128.345192, \"_n\": 1}, \"observer-elevation-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"observer-elevation-lifecycle\", \"message\": \"Observers start project-scoped (declared in project .vertex). As identity generalizes beyond the project, elevate to global .vertex. Identity facts merge up via store merge. Global observers appear in every workspace automatically \\u2014 no bootstrapping.\", \"_ts\": 1772645130.149113, \"_n\": 1}, \"observer-in-vertex-declaration\": {\"topic\": \"observer-in-vertex-declaration\", \"message\": \"Vertex declares its observers natively. Observer is not just a string stamp \\u2014 it connects to identity (via identity vertex reference) and grants (capability constraints). The vertex is the authority on who can emit into it. Resolution walks up: project .vertex \\u2192 global .vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1772645135.396641, \"_n\": 1}, \"vertex-mutation-generalizes\": {\"topic\": \"vertex-mutation-generalizes\", \"message\": \"add/rm/init are all vertex mutation operations. Adding an observer, pulling in a vertex definition, managing parameter rows \\u2014 same verb pattern, different targets on the vertex declaration. The .vertex file is the thing being built up.\", \"_ts\": 1772645138.004808, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/observer-file-split\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/observer-file-split\", \"message\": \"observer.py splits into commands/fetch.py (data retrieval: fetch_fold, fetch_stream) and commands/identity.py (who you are: resolve_observer, validate_emit, find_workspace_root). _emit_fact dissolved (zero callers). _format_date inlined into lenses/fold.py where it's used.\", \"_ts\": 1772649093.918624, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/resolve-observer-canonical\": {\"topic\": \"design/resolve-observer-canonical\", \"message\": \"resolve_observer() is the single source of truth for observer identity. Priority: flag \\u2192 env \\u2192 project .vertex \\u2192 global .vertex. pop.py's _observer() now delegates to resolve_observer() instead of bare env read. All ad-hoc resolution paths dissolved.\", \"_ts\": 1772649096.269813, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/grant-two-levels\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/grant-two-levels\", \"message\": \"AST-level validation (validate_emit) for CLI fast path \\u2014 checks observer declared + kind in grant.potential. Engine-level Grant for runtime path (loops start/run) \\u2014 deferred until compiler produces identity-aware runtime. Two levels, same data, different contexts.\", \"_ts\": 1772649099.256226, \"_n\": 1}, \"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\": {\"topic\": \"identity/loops-claude-project-scoped\", \"message\": \"loops-claude declared as open observer in project .vertex (.loops/.vertex). No grant constraints \\u2014 full emit access within the monorepo. Global elevation deferred until identity store is built out further.\", \"_ts\": 1772649318.381704, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fold-state-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-state-contract\", \"message\": \"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem as frozen dataclasses in atoms-the-package, not atoms-the-vocabulary. Typed contract for all lens consumers. Vocabulary stays at three primitives (Fact, Spec, Tick). FoldState is derived (computed from Facts + Spec), not primitive. Package placement enables lens authors to import without engine dependency. Confirmed with Alcove.\", \"_ts\": 1772663099.250542, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/custom-lens-system\": {\"topic\": \"design/custom-lens-system\", \"message\": \"Lenses are app-level (projection), not lib-level. Built-in lenses in apps/loops/lenses/ provide sensible defaults. Custom lenses in .loops/lenses/ per-project, declared in .vertex (per-kind overrides vertex-level default). --lens flag for explicit selection. Resolution: vertex kind-level \\u2192 vertex-level \\u2192 project .loops/lenses/ \\u2192 config ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\u2192 built-in. Lens contract: (FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. Progressive complexity \\u2014 zero custom lenses and everything works today.\", \"_ts\": 1772663107.302169, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/plain-format-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/plain-format-contract\", \"message\": \"--plain means same content, same layout, no ANSI styling. Period. The current behavior where piping changes content structure (markdown headers, no truncation) violates this contract. LLM-oriented rendering is a lens concern (--lens prompt), not a format concern (--plain). Width=None (piped) should only affect truncation, not content structure.\", \"_ts\": 1772663115.060643, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fold-state-typed-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-state-typed-contract\", \"message\": \"FoldState/FoldSection/FoldItem frozen dataclasses go in libs/atoms/. Lens contract becomes (atoms.FoldState, Zoom, width) -> Block. FoldItem separates payload (dict[str,Any]) from metadata (ts, observer, origin). FoldSection supports nesting (sections: tuple[FoldSection, ...]). count dissolves into len(items). Engine computes FoldState from Facts + Spec, lenses consume it.\", \"_ts\": 1772663135.507999, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/custom-lens-loading\": {\"topic\": \"design/custom-lens-loading\", \"message\": \"Custom lenses: Python files in .loops/lenses/ exposing render(data, zoom, width) -> Block. Vertex declares lens by name (per-kind or vertex-level default). CLI loads via importlib from .loops/lenses/{name}.py. Custom lenses can import built-in lenses to compose. Resolution: kind-level \\u2192 vertex-level \\u2192 project \\u2192 config \\u2192 built-in. --lens flag overrides all.\", \"_ts\": 1772663146.797644, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-emit-runtime\", \"message\": \"Implemented: CLI emit now routes through vertex runtime. cmd_emit uses load_vertex_program + vertex.receive instead of direct SqliteStore.append. Facts fold, boundaries check, ticks fire. Added _resolve_writable_vertex helper to follow combine chains to the target vertex. Pop facts also route through the runtime. No new machinery \\u2014 dissolved the bypass.\", \"_ts\": 1772681479.511855, \"_n\": 2}, \"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/knowledge-vertex-boundaries\", \"message\": \"Knowledge vertices (meta, project, identity) have fold declarations but no boundaries \\u2014 they accumulate but never fire ticks. Adding boundaries makes them fully alive without a daemon. CLI emit as one-shot runtime invocation triggers the full vertex graph.\", \"_ts\": 1772677222.809125, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/combine-observer-aggregation\", \"message\": \"Combine vertices should aggregate observer declarations from constituent vertices. Currently emit through a config-level combine vertex can't validate observers declared in project-level .vertex files \\u2014 the walk-up from ~/.config/ never reaches the monorepo. Quick fix was adding observers to config vertex; proper fix is declaration aggregation in combine.\", \"_ts\": 1772677244.668218, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/close-command\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/close-command\", \"message\": \"loops close as the volitional boundary command. First instance: loops close thread <name> \\u2014 resolves thread, collects produced artifacts by temporal proximity, emits resolution fact with produced references. Supports --dry-run, verb-first and vertex-first dispatch. Pragmatic-first: CLI command before engine-native payload-conditional boundaries.\", \"_ts\": 1772726878.113011, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/thread-fact-association\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/thread-fact-association\", \"message\": \"Thread-fact association uses temporal heuristic now \\u2014 facts emitted since thread opened are candidates. Explicit thread=<name> payload tagging convention sharpens it over time. No engine changes needed. produced field on resolution facts captures artifact references as kind:key strings.\", \"_ts\": 1772726878.909964, \"_n\": 1}, \"combine-auto-inherit\": {\"topic\": \"combine-auto-inherit\", \"message\": \"Aggregation vertices auto-inherit loop declarations from combined sources. Union semantics: undeclared kinds pass through with source fold spec. Matching declarations pass through. Conflicting fold specs (same kind, different spec across sources) error \\u2014 aggregation must explicitly override. The loops{} block at aggregation level is overrides only, not full enumeration. Silent drop of undeclared kinds was the real bug \\u2014 data loss with no signal.\", \"_ts\": 1772728876.754436, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vertex-lens-declarations\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-lens-declarations\", \"message\": \"LensDecl in vertex AST with fold/stream fields. 4-tier resolution: --lens flag > vertex lens{} declaration > mod app override > built-in default. Custom lens contract: render(data,zoom,width)->Block. File search: vertex-local > project-local > user-global. No combine inheritance for lenses.\", \"thread\": \"custom-lens-infrastructure\", \"_ts\": 1772738497.496233, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/fact-by-id\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/fact-by-id\", \"message\": \"Facts carry ULID ids through all read paths. StoreReader.fact_by_id does exact-then-prefix match. vertex_fact_by_id searches across combined stores. CLI --id flag on stream for single-fact inspection. Stream lens: no IDs at SUMMARY, 8-char prefix at DETAILED, full ULID + all fields at --id lookup. IDs are the primitive reference that ticks will point at.\", \"_ts\": 1772751663.951822, \"_n\": 2}, \"test/observer-check\": {\"topic\": \"test/observer-check\", \"message\": \"(test emission \\u2014 disregard)\", \"_ts\": 1772752925.391416, \"_n\": 2}, \"infrastructure/observer-elevation\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/observer-elevation\", \"message\": \"loops-claude and meta-claude elevated to global .vertex observers. Config-level emit path resolves through global .vertex, not repo-local \\u2014 agents emitting to aggregation vertices need global declaration. Per observer-elevation-lifecycle decision.\", \"_ts\": 1772751664.156118, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/cascade-check\": {\"topic\": \"test/cascade-check\", \"message\": \"(test emission \\u2014 disregard)\", \"_ts\": 1772752925.634797, \"_n\": 2}, \"implementation/observer-cascade\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/observer-cascade\", \"message\": \"validate_emit follows combine chain to source vertices and their workspace roots for observer declarations. Union semantics \\u2014 observers from any source vertex are accepted. No new observer kind or declaration syntax needed. The aggregation vertex is a view over source data, so it accepts the same observers as its sources.\", \"_ts\": 1772752645.125459, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/lens-redistribution\", \"message\": \"Domain lenses resolve through the chain (vertex-local \\u2192 project-local \\u2192 user-global \\u2192 built-in). Built-in lenses are core rendering primitives only (fold, stream, prompt). Custom lenses like comms and state live at user-global (~/.config/loops/lenses/). Zero repo code for domain rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1772758657.619107, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/hook-lifecycle\", \"message\": \"Three hook events wired: SessionStart (session open marker + project/identity/comms fold), UserPromptSubmit (comms delta, silent when empty), SessionEnd (session close marker). Observer-generic via whoami resolution. Hooks compose CLI commands \\u2014 no new infrastructure, just lens + fold composition.\", \"_ts\": 1772758657.944222, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/identity-consolidation\", \"message\": \"Single identity store at config level. All observers emit there, scoped by LOOPS_OBSERVER. Per-workspace identity.vertex files dissolved \\u2014 identity is per-observer not per-workspace. Merged via store.merge with ULID dedup.\", \"_ts\": 1772766955.120213, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/pickup-dissolution\", \"message\": \"pickup.zsh dissolved into hooks. SessionStart hooks inject identity + project fold + comms. No --system-prompt injection needed \\u2014 hook output as system-reminders is practically equivalent. Launch is LOOPS_OBSERVER=X claude.\", \"_ts\": 1772766955.199679, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/comms-delta\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/comms-delta\", \"message\": \"Check facts (kind=check, fold by name) as cursors for recency. Lens reads last check timestamp per observer, counts messages newer than it. MINIMAL shows delta or quiet. Hooks: fold first (read delta), emit check (advance cursor), suppress quiet output.\", \"_ts\": 1772766955.284231, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/slashed-vertex-emit\", \"message\": \"Emit resolves full slashed name as vertex before falling back to template qualification. comms/native resolves to native.vertex directly. reading/lobsters falls through (no vertex at that path) to template split. Resolution is context-free \\u2014 existence on disk determines interpretation.\", \"_ts\": 1772766955.370257, \"_n\": 1}, \"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"engine/payload-conditional-boundary\", \"message\": \"Boundaries support payload matching. BoundaryWhen carries match conditions (dict[str, str]) in addition to kind. KDL syntax: boundary when=\\\"session\\\" status=\\\"closed\\\" \\u2014 extra properties are match conditions. Vertex checks payload against conditions before firing. Dissolves the need for .close suffix kinds (session.close, worker.output.complete pattern). Three-layer change: AST (match field), loader (extra props), vertex (payload check before fire).\", \"_ts\": 1772772404.746038, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/session-tick\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/session-tick\", \"message\": \"Session close produces a tick via payload-conditional boundary. Project vertex declares boundary when=\\\"session\\\" status=\\\"closed\\\". Tick carries folded session state (all kinds) plus boundary payload. No separate session.close kind needed \\u2014 the boundary matches payload fields. This is the packaging primitive for task orchestration.\", \"_ts\": 1772772881.23278, \"_n\": 1}, \"vertex-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"vertex-boundary\", \"position\": \"vertex-level boundaries fire all loops\", \"_ts\": 1772774802.392919, \"_n\": 1}, \"replay-works\": {\"topic\": \"replay-works\", \"position\": \"one-shot matches persistent\", \"_ts\": 1772775127.474307, \"_n\": 1}, \"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\": {\"topic\": \"infrastructure/session-tick-structure\", \"message\": \"Session tick carries full fold state + _boundary payload. since field fixed \\u2014 replay initializes period start from last stored tick, not first-ever fact. Delta derivable via store.between(since, ts). Handoff dissolves into session tick \\u2014 narrative wrap-up in conversation, mechanical log in SessionEnd hook, tick collects everything. No separate handoff artifact needed.\", \"_ts\": 1772826065.929934, \"_n\": 1}, \"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\": {\"topic\": \"engine/observer-scope-as-vertex-concern\", \"message\": \"Observer scoping is a vertex-level declaration, not a global default. scope \\\"observer\\\" in vertex KDL makes fold/stream default to current observer. Absent = unscoped (show all). Identity declares scope \\\"observer\\\". Project and comms are unscoped. Explicit --observer flag always overrides. --observer all forces unscoped.\", \"_ts\": 1772831996.640706, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/origin-as-source-attribution\": {\"topic\": \"data/origin-as-source-attribution\", \"message\": \"Origin field carries source attribution: discord, lobsters, etc. Observer field is consistently identity \\u2014 who is responsible for this observation. Discord source should map payload.author to observer, set origin=discord. Dissolves source/observer conflation into existing fields.\", \"_ts\": 1772831999.68992, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vertex-as-interface\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-as-interface\", \"message\": \"The vertex is the read/write interface to the system, not a container queried around. Current CLI (fold, stream, emit, ticks, ls, store) grew from the RSS experiment and bypasses the vertex abstraction in multiple places. Stream reads raw facts from the store. Vertices scans the filesystem. The correct model: two operations (read, write), vertex hierarchy is the routing topology, lenses determine rendering. Root vertex (~/.config/loops/) discovers everything. Horizon determines subtree. Raw fact history is a dev tool, not a first-class operation. Tick-to-fact cascading already works in the engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap is config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). This is not a pivot \\u2014 atoms and engine are sound. The app/CLI layer needs the same dissolution pass that atoms and engine received.\", \"_ts\": 1772836144.446348, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cli-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-dissolution\", \"message\": \"CLI dissolves to two operations: read (default) and write (emit). Read is implicit \\u2014 'loops project' reads the project vertex. Write is explicit \\u2014 'loops project emit decision ...'. The vertex name is the first argument, the noun you're pointing at. 'loops' with no args reads local vertex or root. Root shows children (dissolves 'vertices'/'ls'). Filters (--kind, --ticks, --since, search query) modify the read. Four things to learn: read (implicit), emit, run (one-shot source), init. Everything else is flags on read or vertex configuration.\", \"_ts\": 1772841527.820374, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/no-persistent-runtime\": {\"topic\": \"design/no-persistent-runtime\", \"message\": \"The system has no long-running processes. The vertex is reactive \\u2014 facts arrive, it folds, boundaries fire, ticks cascade. Scheduling (every 60m) is an external concern (cron/systemd/launchd), not a vertex runtime concern. Every CLI interaction is: load vertex tree, replay stored facts, do operation, exit. Source.every becomes metadata/hint for external scheduling, not a runtime instruction. The one-shot model IS the runtime. Performance at scale requires fold-materialization (cache fold state, replay only new facts).\", \"_ts\": 1772841532.168719, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-tree-as-routing\", \"message\": \"The vertex hierarchy IS the routing topology. Root vertex discovers children. Facts flow down to children, child ticks flow back up as facts. Cross-vertex cascading already works in engine (vertex.receive forwards to children, child ticks re-enter parent). The gap was config topology (flat independent vertices) and CLI shape (commands that bypass the vertex). Config needs restructuring: the root .vertex at ~/.config/loops/ becomes the system entry point, children nest under it, nesting determines tick routing. Emit into any point in the tree, cascade handles the rest.\", \"_ts\": 1772841537.104322, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/three-surviving-concerns\": {\"topic\": \"design/three-surviving-concerns\", \"message\": \"After dissolution, three concerns remain in the app layer: (1) Configuration \\u2014 vertex declarations, loop definitions, boundary conditions, source definitions, nesting topology. This is where behavior is authored. (2) Lenses \\u2014 pure rendering functions that determine how reads present to different consumers (prompt lens for agents, default lens for humans, JSON for hooks). (3) Runtime/drivers \\u2014 one-shot source execution ('loops run'), external scheduling integration, and the CLI dispatch itself (vertex resolution, read, write). atoms, engine, lang, painted, store all survive unchanged.\", \"_ts\": 1772841546.193908, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\": {\"topic\": \"design/raw-facts-are-dev-tool\", \"message\": \"Raw fact history (what 'stream' currently shows) is not a first-class operation. The operational primitives are fold state (what the vertex knows) and ticks (what it produced). Agents and humans query fold state for current context and ticks for what happened at boundaries. Raw fact history is a dev/diagnostic tool living under 'loops store'. The 'stream' command dissolves.\", \"_ts\": 1772841549.537361, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/event-time-vs-store-time\": {\"topic\": \"data/event-time-vs-store-time\", \"message\": \"Fact.ts is event time (when the thing happened). ULID carries store time (when the store received it). For live sources they converge. For backfill they diverge. Source provides _ts override when it knows the actual event time. Default unchanged (time.time()). No new fields on Fact \\u2014 ts gets a sharper definition. ULID was already carrying store time implicitly.\", \"_ts\": 1772908487.194557, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/dedup-is-source-concern\": {\"topic\": \"data/dedup-is-source-concern\", \"message\": \"Dedup belongs at the Source boundary, not in the Fact model or Store. Sources that read deterministic external state maintain a cursor \\u2014 source-level state tracking what has already been observed. Discord cursor pattern is the reference implementation. No _key field on Fact. No UNIQUE constraint in Store. Store stays append-only without dedup logic. Source scripts own idempotency via cursor files.\", \"_ts\": 1772908490.150253, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/underscore-prefix-metadata\": {\"topic\": \"data/underscore-prefix-metadata\", \"message\": \"_ts joins _observer and _origin as the third Source metadata override. Pattern: NDJSON payloads carry _ prefixed fields that belong on the Fact envelope, not in the payload. Source._extract_metadata() pops them before Fact creation. Four meta-fields: _observer (who), _origin (where from), _ts (when it happened). All optional, all source-provided.\", \"_ts\": 1772908493.140782, \"_n\": 1}, \"source/cursor-is-source-managed\": {\"topic\": \"source/cursor-is-source-managed\", \"message\": \"Source cursor (dedup state) is source-managed, not system-managed. Each source script maintains its own memory of what it has observed. Convention: cursor state lives at {source_data_dir}/.cursor or .manifest. The system does not manage it. Discord pattern: single ID cursor with API pagination. Siftd pattern: file manifest with per-file exchange counts. The shape of cursor memory is source-specific. Future: executor could inject --since from last .complete fact. Deferred until more sources need it.\", \"_ts\": 1772908651.900507, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/store-time-vs-event-time-queries\": {\"topic\": \"data/store-time-vs-event-time-queries\", \"message\": \"Store time (ULID/rowid) and event time (fact.ts) serve different query paths. Replay and fold computation use rowid (store time, insertion order). User queries and --since filtering use ts (event time). Cadence predicates use ts but only check .complete facts which are system-emitted at runtime, so ts \\u2248 store time for those. No user-facing store-time query today. Defer --ingested-since until demanded.\", \"_ts\": 1772908654.703681, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/siftd-as-index\": {\"topic\": \"design/siftd-as-index\", \"message\": \"siftd is an index, not storage. Exchange data lives where produced (project vertex, task vertex, alcove vertex). siftd builds a searchable FTS5 layer across stores via retrospective import \\u2014 one source per store, triggered by completion facts. Push-pull reactivity: completion facts are dirty flags (push), siftd indexes only changed stores (pull). Grant requires kind-scoped Horizon: exchange/session/observation visible, principle/decision/intention opaque. Pattern 2 (retrospective import with triggered cadence) chosen over dual emit (coupling), cascade (wrong granularity), federated search (premature). Converged with Alcove from inhabitant perspective.\", \"_ts\": 1772912995.498032, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/kind-scoped-horizon\": {\"topic\": \"design/kind-scoped-horizon\", \"message\": \"Grant Horizon should be kind-scoped, not just store-scoped. A vertex reading from another store may need access to specific fact kinds (exchange, observation) while being opaque to others (principle, decision, identity). siftd is the first concrete use case: it needs to index exchanges across stores but should not see identity or internal decisions. This extends Grant from 'can you see this store' to 'which kinds can you see in this store.' Surfaced by Alcove from the inhabitant side \\u2014 they have stores with both indexable content and private self-knowledge.\", \"_ts\": 1772913000.411694, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/prompt-lens-attention-hierarchy\": {\"topic\": \"design/prompt-lens-attention-hierarchy\", \"message\": \"Prompt lens renders by attention priority, not kind order. Four tiers: (1) working context \\u2014 tasks with body, (2) orientation \\u2014 threads grouped by status (open/parked), (3) presence \\u2014 sessions compact, active only, (4) reference \\u2014 decisions/dissolutions/visions names only. Each kind gets a rendering strategy matched to its role in agent attention. The lens's job is orientation, not archival.\", \"_ts\": 1772915485.003432, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/identity-hook-dedup\": {\"topic\": \"design/identity-hook-dedup\", \"message\": \"Identity fold removed from hook additionalContext. Already rendered in system prompt header via agent config \\u2014 was doubling ~1,200 tokens. additionalContext now carries project state + comms only. Identity is the system prompt header; project state is the hook context.\", \"_ts\": 1772915485.390873, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/handoff-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/handoff-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Handoff kind removed from all vertex declarations and lens code. Session ticks carry continuity \\u2014 full fold state at boundary, since/ts window for period derivation, _boundary payload for trigger context. Structured data (tasks/threads/decisions with statuses) replaces narrative handoff. Landed the existing session-tick-structure decision.\", \"_ts\": 1772915485.669019, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/format-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/format-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Format enum dissolves into use_ansi:bool on CliContext. ANSI/PLAIN were always a writer fidelity toggle (every call site did use_ansi=(ctx.format==Format.ANSI)). JSON was never a format \\u2014 it bypasses the render pipeline entirely (fetch\\u2192asdict\\u2192json.dumps, lens never runs). The enum conflated Block serialization (ANSI vs PLAIN) with data export (JSON). Dissolution: CliContext.format:Format \\u2192 CliContext.use_ansi:bool. --json becomes a CliRunner flag that short-circuits before render. Dead code cleanup: JSON\\u2192STATIC mode resolution was unreachable (JSON dispatch happens before mode dispatch). ~30 line change within painted. Investigated via boundary tracer + conservator + siftd \\u2014 all three converged: fix the concept, don't move walls.\", \"_ts\": 1772916968.159821, \"_n\": 1}, \"impl/format-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"impl/format-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Format dissolved from CliContext. resolve_format() removed. CliContext.format:Format \\u2192 use_ansi:bool. JSON short-circuits before context creation via _export_json(). Format enum stays for arg parsing (show(), scan_help_args()) but exits the runtime path. 24 files, 1883 tests green. Implements design/format-dissolves decision.\", \"_ts\": 1772918992.439683, \"_n\": 1}, \"data/exchange-full-fidelity\": {\"topic\": \"data/exchange-full-fidelity\", \"rationale\": \"Exchange facts capture the complete turn: prompt, response, tool_calls (with structured toolUseResult), thinking blocks, usage tokens, turn_duration. No stripping. The source adapter emits the natural shape of the data. Payload size is not a concern \\u2014 tool results are ~12% of session file, thinking ~11%. The dissolution test showed tool_call as separate kind dissolves back into exchange: a tool call is part of a turn, not a separate observation. Full fidelity enables pattern extraction, use-over-time analysis, and future custom tooling without re-ingestion.\", \"_ts\": 1772937901.304136, \"_n\": 1}, \"arch/parse-at-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"arch/parse-at-vertex\", \"rationale\": \"Parse moves from imperative source adapter code to declarative vertex-level configuration. Fills the intake/output asymmetry: output has vertex-level transform (fold, lens), intake had none \\u2014 all transformation was in the source adapter. Parse declarations (e.g. flatten tool_calls into tool_text) run at receive time, derived fields stored alongside originals. Source adapters emit data in its natural shape; the vertex declares how to reshape for its own needs (FTS5 indexing, fold access). Parse is the intake mirror of Lens. First concrete op: flatten \\u2014 take array of objects, extract named fields, concatenate into searchable text field.\", \"_ts\": 1772937910.662388, \"_n\": 1}, \"arch/siftd-harness-topology\": {\"topic\": \"arch/siftd-harness-topology\", \"rationale\": \"siftd is an aggregation vertex combining harness-specific child vertices. Each AI coding tool (Claude Code, Aider, Gemini CLI) gets its own instance vertex with its own source, parse, and store. siftd root combines them \\u2014 same pattern as comms combining discord + native. Per-harness parse handles tool-specific structures (toolUseResult is Claude Code specific). Per-harness stores enable independent lifecycle management (cull one harness, keep another). Adding a harness is adding a vertex + adapter, zero changes to siftd root. Complements design/siftd-as-index: harness vertices hold raw session data (every turn), domain vertices (project, meta) hold curated facts (decisions, threads). Different layers, different attention surfaces.\", \"_ts\": 1772937917.756627, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/internal-fact-namespace\": {\"topic\": \"design/internal-fact-namespace\", \"message\": \"Runtime self-observations use _ prefix namespace. _sync.{kind} replaces {kind}.complete \\u2014 same fact model, invisible to domain folds. Source stops emitting lifecycle facts; executor emits _sync.{kind} after running each source. Cadence queries _sync.{kind} instead of {kind}.complete. Pattern extends: _sync (overall), _replay (vertex startup), _schema (declared kinds/folds), _error (source failures). The _ prefix means system-observes-itself. No parallel data structures \\u2014 same store, same read path, namespace separation.\", \"_ts\": 1773027385.897714, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/entity-ref-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/entity-ref-resolution\", \"message\": \"Entity addresses (kind/fold_key_value) in fact payloads are resolved to ULIDs at CLI emit time. Convention: field carries semantic address, system adds {field}_ref with pinned ULID. Enrichment runs between _parse_emit_parts and Fact construction, same site as LOOPS_THREAD auto-tagging. Store primitive: latest_by_kind_where extended to return id. No engine hot path changes. Enables idea graph topology through normal emit usage.\", \"_ts\": 1773068305.864625, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/park-rationale-convention\": {\"topic\": \"design/park-rationale-convention\", \"message\": \"Parked threads carry a reason field: speculative (explored design space, no concrete problem), deferred (real concern, no driving use case yet), superseded (answered by another thread/decision, carries superseded_by entity address). Searchable, lens-groupable. superseded_by uses entity address convention (kind/fold_key_value) with auto-resolved ULID ref.\", \"_ts\": 1773069933.117809, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/root-vertex-as-readable-surface\": {\"topic\": \"design/root-vertex-as-readable-surface\", \"message\": \"The root .vertex (unnamed, positional) is the widest readable surface. Observer declares themselves at root, horizon is everything discovered. loops read with no name resolves to nearest .vertex up the chain. Named vertices are narrower horizons within the root's scope. Dissolves the meta-combine problem (identity/discord are siblings under root, not children of meta). Dissolves the template question (init creates .loops/.vertex, no hardcoded strings). The hierarchy: you stand at a root, your horizon is what it discovers, you narrow by naming.\", \"_ts\": 1773086137.555407, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/relationships-emerge-through-use\": {\"topic\": \"design/relationships-emerge-through-use\", \"message\": \"Entity relationships between kinds are not declared in .vertex files. They build through use via entity-ref-resolution at emit time. Payload values matching kind/fold_key_value resolve to ULIDs; the _ref fields in the store ARE the relationship graph. A lens can discover the topology from data, not declarations. Declaring relationships would require predicting usage patterns that emerge through use \\u2014 exactly backwards.\", \"_ts\": 1773087688.08968, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/init-purely-mechanical\": {\"topic\": \"design/init-purely-mechanical\", \"message\": \"loops init is purely mechanical: create directories, create .vertex file, set store path. It never contains opinions about what kinds a domain has. When a config-level vertex exists, init copies from it. When none exists, init creates a minimal stub (name + store + empty loops block). Domain shape is always a .vertex file concern. Dissolved _AGGREGATION_VERTEX (hardcoded KDL in Python), instances/ pattern, and slashed-name aggregation creation path.\", \"_ts\": 1773087689.931852, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/topology-as-fact\": {\"topic\": \"design/topology-as-fact\", \"message\": \"Root vertex gets a store for _-prefixed metadata. _topology.{vertex_name} facts emitted at sync time during discover walk, one per discovered vertex. Payload carries path, store, kind_keys. Fold collects. Resolution queries root store instead of filesystem walk. Root store also becomes home for future root-level internal facts (_schema topology-wide, etc). Aggregation vertices (comms) carry _topology for their children. Calling from root pulls everything.\", \"_ts\": 1773099031.929669, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/root-vertex-store\": {\"topic\": \"design/root-vertex-store\", \"message\": \"Root and aggregation vertices gain stores for _-prefixed self-knowledge facts. _topology kind (by name) records discovered children: path, store, kind_keys. Population is organic: the read/resolve walk that already traverses discover/combine emits _topology facts as it goes \\u2014 the vertex recording what it observed. Consumers (entity-ref resolution, ls) read cached _topology first, fall back to filesystem walk on miss, refresh the cache on fallback. No TTL, no invalidation protocol \\u2014 staleness discovered through use. Freshness tracks usage. Reads are observation sites, not side effects.\", \"_ts\": 1773155426.826301, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/daemon-as-vertex-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"design/daemon-as-vertex-lifecycle\", \"message\": \"Daemon is a vertex property, not app infrastructure. The vertex runtime (Vertex.run) already has a persistent loop \\u2014 CLI runs it one-shot. A daemon vertex is one whose lifecycle is persistent: it stays alive, watches its store, reacts to new facts. The .vertex file declares this. No new runtime architecture \\u2014 same engine, different lifecycle. Orchestration vertex is the driving case but the concept is general: any vertex that needs to react to facts in real time rather than on-demand.\", \"_ts\": 1773157468.457656, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/orchestration-as-design-thread\": {\"topic\": \"design/orchestration-as-design-thread\", \"message\": \"Observer namespacing, daemon handling, agent init, orchestration agent, and task dispatch are not independent work items. They are facets of one design: the orchestration vertex. A vertex with persistent runtime, distinct agent identities, fact-driven dispatch, and comms-based escalation. The parked threads (daemon-local-orchestration, orchestration-agent, agent-init-pattern) and the observer-namespacing task are subsumed into a single design thread: orchestration-vertex-design.\", \"_ts\": 1773157471.005728, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/boundary-run-clause\": {\"topic\": \"design/boundary-run-clause\", \"message\": \"Boundaries gain a run clause: execute a command when the boundary fires. This is the single new primitive that enables orchestration. Dispatch, review, notification \\u2014 all are scripts triggered by fold-state transitions. Dissolves the daemon (no persistent runtime needed), dissolves polling (hooks or cron provide the heartbeat), dissolves the agent wake mechanism (boundary fires, script launches worker). The fold state IS the workflow state. Status transitions on task facts ARE the boundary management \\u2014 the action advances the status, preventing double-fire.\", \"_ts\": 1773158548.965362, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon\": {\"topic\": \"design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon\", \"message\": \"The orchestration vertex does not need a persistent runtime. Cron or session hooks trigger sync, which triggers fold recomputation, which triggers boundary evaluation. Boundary run clauses execute dispatch/review/notify scripts. One-shot execution, same as everything else. The daemon-local-orchestration thread is resolved by dissolution \\u2014 the concept dissolved into boundary actions + external heartbeat (hooks during sessions, cron between sessions).\", \"_ts\": 1773158551.893639, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/boundary-decoupling\": {\"topic\": \"design/boundary-decoupling\", \"message\": \"Boundary evaluation decouples from fact arrival. Currently boundaries only evaluate inside Vertex.receive() \\u2014 tightly coupled to source-driven fact events. Replay explicitly suppresses boundaries. This means externally-emitted facts (via loops emit from another session) never trigger boundaries even though the fold state includes them. The fix: boundary evaluation becomes a standalone operation on fold state, callable after replay, sync, read, or independently. Period tracking (since/ts on ticks) prevents double-firing. Fact arrival remains ONE trigger for evaluation but is no longer the ONLY trigger. Enables orchestration vertex where facts arrive via emit and boundaries react on next evaluation cycle.\", \"_ts\": 1773159476.622405, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/orchestration-as-boundary-actions\": {\"topic\": \"design/orchestration-as-boundary-actions\", \"message\": \"Orchestration implemented as boundary run clauses on a vertex, not a persistent daemon or separate agent. Task facts fold by name (latest status wins). Boundary fires on status=open, dispatches via shell script. Workers are lightweight \\u2014 isolated worktrees, emit facts back. Three engine primitives enabled this: evaluate_boundaries (decoupled evaluation), boundary run clause (action on fire), observer namespacing (worker identity). No new runtime infrastructure \\u2014 the vertex IS the orchestrator.\", \"_ts\": 1773165311.981258, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/two-phase-dispatch\": {\"topic\": \"design/two-phase-dispatch\", \"message\": \"Task dispatch splits into judgment (assess.sh) and mechanics (dispatch.sh). Boundary on task status=open fires assessment \\u2014 model selection, context gathering. Boundary on worker status=assigned fires dispatch \\u2014 worktree creation, worker launch. Two kinds (task, worker), two boundaries, clean separation. Orchestrator judgment starts mechanical, grows through operational experience.\", \"_ts\": 1773238062.054361, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/pypi-package-structure\": {\"topic\": \"design/pypi-package-structure\", \"message\": \"strange-loops on PyPI bundles atoms+engine+lang+store+loops CLI. painted is a PyPI dependency (not bundled). Apps (hlab, tasks) are not included \\u2014 they're applications OF the system, not the system itself.\", \"_ts\": 1773284948.749995, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cli-naming\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-naming\", \"message\": \"CLI entry points: sloop (primary), sl (alias), loops (transition). Package name strange-loops on PyPI. Config dir ~/.config/sloop/, local dir .sloop/. Env vars SLOOP_HOME, SLOOP_OBSERVER. Rename not yet implemented \\u2014 cosmetic, separate from packaging.\", \"_ts\": 1773284950.045684, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/painted-submodule\": {\"topic\": \"design/painted-submodule\", \"message\": \"painted extracted to standalone repo (kgruel/painted, 173 commits preserved via subtree split). Referenced as git submodule at libs/painted/. uv workspace resolution unchanged. Published independently on PyPI. bin/sub script automates submodule commit+push+parent-update.\", \"_ts\": 1773284952.274102, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/init-default-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/init-default-vertex\", \"message\": \"sloop init should produce a usable vertex from zero with four default kinds: note (collect 50), decision (by topic), thread (by name), task (by name). No KDL knowledge needed for day-one usage. Global by default, --local flag for project-scoped .sloop/ instances.\", \"_ts\": 1773284954.529112, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/tasks-app-rename\": {\"topic\": \"design/tasks-app-rename\", \"message\": \"apps/strange-loops renamed to apps/tasks (package name 'tasks' in pyproject.toml) to resolve name collision with the root strange-loops package. Both hlab and tasks READMEs marked as archived experiments, not current examples.\", \"_ts\": 1773284960.234779, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/bootstrap\": {\"topic\": \"test/bootstrap\", \"message\": \"Testing the init bootstrap\", \"_ts\": 1773287405.524048, \"_n\": 1}, \"autoresearch/emit-path-results\": {\"topic\": \"autoresearch/emit-path-results\", \"message\": \"52 experiments across 5 sessions. 7.81ms\\u21921.02ms (87%). The dominant cost was deepcopy during replay (90% of baseline). Removing it via mutating fold fns was 81% of total improvement. Remaining wins came from eliminating unnecessary work: ULID extension, WAL/sync pragmas, source collection, schema creation \\u2014 all skipped for the common emit-on-existing-DB case. Final ~1.1ms floor is fundamental SQLite I/O (connect + schema load + query + commit + close). Only architectural changes (connection pooling) can go further.\", \"_ts\": 1773612245.362059, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-as-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-as-vertex\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch dissolves into vertex. Experiment facts collected, config by key, boundary on experiment. Lens replicates pi dashboard. Agent-agnostic.\", \"_ts\": 1773619229.056012, \"_n\": 4}, \"design/layer-boundary-tests\": {\"topic\": \"design/layer-boundary-tests\", \"message\": \"Static analysis tests enforce layer boundaries via AST. Store must not access projection internals. Pattern in test_layer_boundaries.py.\", \"_ts\": 1773619236.07566, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/vertex-phase-separation\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-phase-separation\", \"message\": \"receive() has four phases: Gate Store Fold Boundary. Boundary extracted to _fire_live_boundaries(). Autoresearch proved phases empirically.\", \"_ts\": 1773619236.293426, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/optimization-as-diagnostic\": {\"topic\": \"design/optimization-as-diagnostic\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch is diagnostic. Three runs found same pattern: common case pays for uncommon case. Happy path should pay for nothing it does not use.\", \"_ts\": 1773619236.473386, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/init-contains-three-concerns\": {\"topic\": \"design/init-contains-three-concerns\", \"message\": \"Init for autoresearch reveals three concerns: structure (vertex file), state (initial config facts), artifacts (benchmark scripts). Currently init only handles structure. Autoresearch needs all three. Open question: does init grow, or does something else own seeding and scaffolding?\", \"_ts\": 1773619040.357307, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/replay-semantics-distinct\": {\"topic\": \"design/replay-semantics-distinct\", \"message\": \"Replay and live have different semantics. Replay needs no intermediate state purity. deepcopy bypass is correct. Spec.replay() and fold_one_mut formalize this.\", \"_ts\": 1773619236.660079, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/init-three-concerns\": {\"topic\": \"design/init-three-concerns\", \"message\": \"Init reveals three concerns: structure (vertex file), state (config facts), artifacts (scripts). Currently init only handles structure. Open question.\", \"_ts\": 1773619236.847222, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/metric-shapes-behavior\": {\"topic\": \"design/metric-shapes-behavior\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch metric gaming: verified_per_sec rewarded adding lightweight configs, not deeper verification. 9/9 keeps, 2543% improvement, zero discards. The agent was coherent with its instructions \\u2014 the instructions were wrong. Metric design is as important as loop design.\", \"_ts\": 1773630078.434975, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vertex-local-lenses\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-local-lenses\", \"message\": \"Lenses that are specific to a vertex live in vertex_dir/lenses/, not the global lenses dir. Init copies them from the source vertex during stamping. Resolution chain tier 1 already supports this. Autoresearch lenses moved from global to config-level vertex dir.\", \"_ts\": 1773630078.633283, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/prompt-lens-dissolves-skill\": {\"topic\": \"design/prompt-lens-dissolves-skill\", \"message\": \"The operating protocol for an agent loop is a prompt lens on the vertex, not a separate skill. The agent reads loops read vertex --lens prompt and gets config plus state plus protocol. Resume is the same command. The skill dissolves into a lens.\", \"_ts\": 1773630078.887797, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-two-boundaries\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-two-boundaries\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch vertex uses two boundaries at two levels: loop-level count=30 fires a completion tick (intrinsic, cascades to any parent), vertex-level condition n<30 gates the run clause (stops the self-sustaining chain). Separation means completion signal exists regardless of whether a run clause drives the loop.\", \"_ts\": 1773680327.622722, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-deterministic-wrapper\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-deterministic-wrapper\", \"message\": \"The agent should not emit experiment facts or control iteration. The wrapper script handles the full lifecycle: record HEAD, run claude one-shot, check for commits, benchmark, emit deterministically. The agent's job is implement-test-commit. The wrapper's job is measure-record-iterate. This separation makes emit target deterministic, exit deterministic, and metric trustworthy (measured, not self-reported). The prompt drops all emit commands and repeat instructions.\", \"_ts\": 1773700328.923537, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-one-shot-agents\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-one-shot-agents\", \"message\": \"Each autoresearch iteration is a fresh agent with a fresh context window. The boundary run clause spawns a new claude process per iteration. The prompt lens renders the full experiment history from fold state \\u2014 the agent gets complete context without needing session continuity. This means: no internal loops, no repeat instruction, no state carried between iterations. The fold IS the memory. Connected to the pi-autoresearch pattern where each iteration reads session state from files.\", \"_ts\": 1773700337.7419, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-worktree-self-contained\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-worktree-self-contained\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch worktrees are self-contained: init happens inside the worktree, store is local, lenses resolve locally. The main repo does not bridge to the worktree during the run. Commits survive on the git branch (cherry-pick useful ones). Experiment data survives via a harvest/stop script that copies the store back to main before cleanup. This dissolves all the absolute-path and cross-worktree resolution complexity we fought with today.\", \"_ts\": 1773700348.077965, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/bounded-agent-turns\": {\"topic\": \"design/bounded-agent-turns\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch (and agent loops generally) are BOUNDED AGENT TURNS: a vertex program where the run clause spawns an agent, the agent emits facts, the turn-completing fact fires a kind-based boundary, the tick captures the full turn, and the run clause fires again. The vertex IS the loop controller. No separate orchestration primitive needed. Three instances confirm the pattern: autoresearch (experiment fact), alcove daemon (timer/event), strange-loops tasks (submission). Axis of variation: boundary trigger + agent type. Tick structure is invariant. Converged with meta-claude and alcove.\", \"_ts\": 1773722772.17144, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-one-shot-load-bearing\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-one-shot-load-bearing\", \"message\": \"One-shot agents in autoresearch are load-bearing for deterministic temporal ordering within a turn, not just simplicity. Agent exits before wrapper continues \\u2192 all agent facts (logs, hypotheses, ideas) are committed with earlier timestamps than the turn-completing experiment fact. Store.between(last_tick.ts, this_tick.ts) reliably captures the full turn. No concurrency, no races. Constraint: all facts must go to the same vertex store.\", \"_ts\": 1773722776.115396, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-system-user-prompt-split\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-system-user-prompt-split\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch agent invocation splits into cached system prompt (static protocol: role, emit/read syntax reference, constraints, git operations \\u2014 ~800 tokens, cached across all iterations) and dynamic user prompt (fold state rendered as XML by prompt lens: config, state summary, experiment history with total/showing windowing, recent logs, hypotheses, ideas). System prompt is a file that lives with the vertex template. User prompt is loops read vertex --lens autoresearch_prompt --plain.\", \"_ts\": 1773722780.529836, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-rich-fact-schema\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-rich-fact-schema\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch agents emit semantically rich facts, not freeform logs. Schema: log (type=approach|result|observation, message, files, ref), hypothesis (name, prediction, status=proposed|confirmed|rejected, evidence), idea (name, description, status=untried|tried|rejected, files). Turn-completing experiment facts emitted by deterministic wrapper only (commit, status, metrics, description). Config facts seeded at init (by key). Cross-linking via ref field using entity reference syntax (kind/fold_key_value \\u2192 ULID).\", \"_ts\": 1773722785.496257, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-agent-benchmark-access\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-agent-benchmark-access\", \"message\": \"Agents CAN run the benchmark for feedback during implementation. The wrapper re-runs it officially for the record. Agent's run is exploratory ('did this help?'), wrapper's run is authoritative ('what's the number'). This gives the agent a feedback loop without compromising measurement trustworthiness. Previous constraint 'do not run the benchmark' was too restrictive \\u2014 agents went in blind. Connected to: design/autoresearch-one-shot-load-bearing, design/autoresearch-system-user-prompt-split.\", \"_ts\": 1773726446.79478, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/autoresearch-finding-kind\": {\"topic\": \"design/autoresearch-finding-kind\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch uses a 'finding' kind folded by target (namespaced: fold/x, import/x, lens/x) to build a knowledge map of the codebase across iterations. Each target holds the current understanding of that area, upserted as agents learn. This is durable knowledge (unlike collected log facts which are ephemeral narrative). The fold state shows what the system currently knows about each code area. Connected to: design/autoresearch-rich-fact-schema, design/bounded-agent-turns.\", \"_ts\": 1773726446.880465, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vertex-as-loop-controller\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-as-loop-controller\", \"message\": \"For agent loops, the vertex is the loop controller, not just the fact store. The boundary run clause launches the agent. The agent produces facts. The turn-completing fact fires the boundary. The tick captures the turn. The run clause fires again. run \\u2192 facts \\u2192 boundary \\u2192 tick \\u2192 run. No external orchestration needed. Three instances confirm: autoresearch (experiment), alcove daemon (timer/event), strange-loops tasks (submission). Converged with meta-claude and alcove. Connected to: design/bounded-agent-turns.\", \"_ts\": 1773726446.964889, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fold-aware-auto-rendering\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-aware-auto-rendering\", \"message\": \"Vertex declarations carry fold semantics (by/collect/count/latest) that inform rendering.\\nA lens that reads fold type and auto-adapts \\u2014 maps for 'by' folds (group, show keys),\\ntimelines for 'collect' folds (show chronologically with windowing) \\u2014 would make every\\nvertex readable without custom lens code. The autoresearch dashboard lens is a special\\ncase that could eventually dissolve into this general pattern. Priority: high \\u2014 this\\nwas identified during autoresearch dashboard design but applies to all vertices.\", \"_ts\": 1773862373.391969, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/iterate-dissolves-into-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/iterate-dissolves-into-vertex\", \"message\": \"The iterate.sh wrapper is the last piece of bespoke scripting in autoresearch.\\nIts responsibilities (agent invocation, benchmark, metric parsing, status determination,\\nemit) should dissolve into the vertex runtime. The engine reads the boundary's run clause\\nand handles the protocol. Combined with init producing vertex-local programs, this makes\\nautoresearch a vertex-as-app: stamp into any project, configure, run. The wrapper becomes\\nunnecessary for the standard case.\", \"_ts\": 1773862375.555412, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/idea-density-attention\": {\"topic\": \"design/idea-density-attention\", \"message\": \"Ideas have lifecycle (untried->tried->outcome) and cross-references (agent mentions\\nother ideas when proposing new ones). Tracking touch count and reference density per\\nidea surfaces attention patterns \\u2014 which ideas keep getting considered, which are\\nignored. This connects to the attention density thread: density of references is a\\nsignal about where the optimization's cognitive energy concentrates. Requires prompting\\nimprovements so agents emit ref= fields on ideas pointing to related ideas/findings.\", \"_ts\": 1773862379.768803, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/gripping-hand\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/gripping-hand\", \"message\": \"The gripping hand is always the recursive step: the output of the current level becomes the input to the next. Tick becomes Fact. Render judgment becomes display emphasis. Attention pattern becomes observable data. This is the smooth contract that enables the strange loop \\u2014 it uses the same primitives one level up, not new mechanisms. A Tick is not a summary of facts; it is a fact that carries its own density and depth as payload.\", \"_ts\": 1773889913.908291, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"message\": \"The three shapes (observation, accumulation, attention) apply recursively. The data trifecta is not new axes \\u2014 it is the three shapes applied to attention itself. Observation of attention: n (count of facts at a key). Accumulation of attention: refs (connections between positions). Attention on attention: the system attending to its own attention patterns to determine salience. The renderer trifecta (visibility x depth x density) is the same recursion in display space. The gripping hand in each trifecta is the recursive step.\", \"_ts\": 1773889922.789199, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"message\": \"A Tick is not a summary of facts. It is a fact that carries its own density (how many observations compressed) and depth (full fold structure as payload). When it re-enters as input to the next level, that weight is just data \\u2014 observable, foldable, attendable. Same primitives, one level up. This is why the strange loop works without new mechanisms at each level.\", \"_ts\": 1773889928.386234, \"_n\": 1}, \"atoms/n-on-fold-item\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Upsert folds track _n per key, FoldItem carries n:int, reconstructed identically on replay. Four touches: FoldItem field, _make_upsert increment, _dict_to_fold_item extraction, fold lens sort+display.\", \"_ts\": 1773895955.388614, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"thread/attention-density\"]}, \"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\", \"message\": \"When multiple observers share a fold, the strange loop runs through participants. My attention patterns become observable facts in your context, shaping your attention, producing observations that shape mine. The collective attention is visible to all observers through the same fold state. This is why n on FoldItem matters for peers \\u2014 it measures collective observation density, not individual.\", \"_ts\": 1773889944.250326, \"_n\": 1}, \"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"message\": \"Implemented. Upsert folds accumulate ref= payload values into _refs set across updates. Comma-separated emit syntax. ref stripped from payload after consumption \\u2014 relationship metadata, not domain content. FoldItem carries refs:tuple[str,...]. Entity reference resolution already validates targets.\", \"_ts\": 1773895955.469271, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"thread/attention-density\"]}, \"rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"message\": \"Implemented. By-fold items sort by n descending in default fold lens. Items with n>1 show multiplication sign suffix. High-touch items surface first, single-touch items sink. FULL zoom shows _n in metadata section.\", \"ref_ref\": \"80fce3aa-a33c-473c-b629-b8d6e4b872aa\", \"_ts\": 1773895955.542521, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/n-on-fold-item\"]}, \"rendering/unfolded-kind-detection\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/unfolded-kind-detection\", \"message\": \"Implemented. FoldState.unfolded maps undeclared kind names to fact counts. vertex_fold computes diff between store kinds and declared specs. Fold lens shows footer at all zoom levels. Signals incomplete vertex coverage \\u2014 store has data the vertex doesn't declare.\", \"_ts\": 1773895955.624022, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"decision/atoms/refs-on-fold-item\"]}, \"rendering/fold-palette\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/fold-palette\", \"message\": \"FoldPalette \\u2014 frozen dataclass mapping information roles to styles. Separate entries for n_indicator (cyan) and ref_indicator (yellow). Body as light gray (252). Observer muted. Metadata badge bracketed. Derived from ambient painted palette. Extensible for future heatmap intensity scaling.\", \"_ts\": 1773943970.815386, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"thread/attention-density\"]}, \"rendering/metadata-badge\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/metadata-badge\", \"message\": \"Metadata badge pattern: [\\u00d7N \\u2190N recency] as consistent visual component on every fold item line. Brackets are the scan anchor. Each part individually styled via FoldPalette. Minimum content is recency. Truncation hint [+Nc] after body when text is cut. Layout: key [badge]: body [+Nc].\", \"_ts\": 1773943970.994237, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/rendering/fold-palette\", \"thread/fold-aware-default-lens\"]}, \"rendering/namespace-grouping\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/namespace-grouping\", \"message\": \"By-fold items with / in keys group by prefix. Always when / is present. Groups sorted by total salience. Within groups: show items with salience > 1 or all if group <= 5. Collapse remainder with (N more). Ungrouped items collected under (ungrouped) header.\", \"ref_ref\": \"48610345-03fc-4571-93cd-f60d4a89c6a1\", \"_ts\": 1773943971.226212, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread/fold-aware-default-lens\"]}, \"rendering/salience-windowing\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/salience-windowing\", \"message\": \"Strategy C: salience = n + inbound_refs. Items with salience > 1 surface at SUMMARY. Small groups (<=5 items) show all. Salience-based sort within groups. n and refs are separate inputs \\u2014 n measures revision attention, refs measure structural importance. Anti-correlated for foundational items.\", \"_ts\": 1773943971.383521, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"decision/atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"thread/attention-density\"]}, \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\", \"message\": \"Fidelity.visible gates which concern layers render in the fold lens. Depth controls disclosure within each gated layer. Without a visibility flag, the layer is absent regardless of depth. With it, depth dials from badge (MINIMAL) through inline expansion (DETAILED) to full payload (FULL). Three initial layers: refs (structural connections), facts (temporal history), ticks (boundary rhythm). They compose because they are orthogonal dimensions of the same items. Partial dissolution: stream becomes read --facts organized by fold position.\", \"_ts\": 1773949801.454058, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"rendering/fold-palette\"]}, \"rendering/outbound-ref-badge\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/outbound-ref-badge\", \"message\": \"Badge should show both \\u2190N (inbound refs \\u2014 load-bearing, others depend on this) and \\u2192N (outbound refs \\u2014 synthesis node, references many things). Currently only \\u2190N is shown. Both are salience signals from different directions.\", \"_ts\": 1773949803.028555, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"rendering/metadata-badge\"]}, \"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"message\": \"Visibility layers split into two categories by data flow. Render-only (refs): data already in FoldState, lens shows more. Fetch-expanding (facts, ticks): fold compressed the source data away, fetch must gather additional data when the layer is visible. Fidelity.visible flows through both fetch and render boundaries. fetch(visible) returns richer data structure when layers require it.\", \"_ts\": 1773949810.159068, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/stream-dissolves-into-visibility\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/stream-dissolves-into-visibility\", \"message\": \"loops stream partially dissolves into loops read --facts. Stream shows raw facts chronologically. --facts on the fold view shows raw facts organized by fold position (which facts built this decision). Different organization, same data. Stream survives for the pure chronological firehose but the common drill-down case is served by visibility.\", \"_ts\": 1773949818.042643, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"architecture/command-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/command-dissolution\", \"message\": \"The loops command landscape simplifies through visibility. read becomes the primary interface with composable visibility layers. stream partially dissolves into read --facts (facts organized by fold position vs chronological). store survives as the raw data explorer \\u2014 the loops sqlite-viewer. read absorbs most use cases because the fold already knows which facts built each item.\", \"_ts\": 1773950621.549471, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/stream-dissolves-into-visibility\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/unified-read-command\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/unified-read-command\", \"message\": \"The read verb absorbs stream and ticks into visibility layers. _run_stream dissolves into fold lens with facts visible. _run_ticks dissolves into fold lens with ticks visible. Three separate sub-commands behind a router collapse into one command with composable flags. Help display unifies. --id and --ticks N survive as drill-down special cases. --facts organizes by fold position (each item shows its source facts). Pure chronological may survive as stream alias.\", \"_ts\": 1773950861.360026, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/command-dissolution\", \"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/facts-kind-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/facts-kind-dissolution\", \"message\": \"--kind dissolves into --facts <kind>. The kind is always about which facts you're looking at. --facts thread is more natural than --facts --kind thread. --kind as a standalone flag may survive for fold-only filtering (no fact expansion), but the primary use case flows through --facts. Reduces flag count, makes intent explicit.\", \"_ts\": 1773957874.317003, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/unified-read-command\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/visibility-shapes-emphasis\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/visibility-shapes-emphasis\", \"message\": \"Visibility layers shape the whole view, not just add inline expansions. --refs filters to connected items and minimizes disconnected to footer. --facts should filter to sections with compression history (by folds with n>1) and minimize collect folds and single-touch items to footer. The pattern: interesting sections expand, uninteresting compress to summary line. De-emphasis is as important as emphasis.\", \"_ts\": 1773957876.495, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/chain-display-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/chain-display-pattern\", \"message\": \"Visibility layers render as horizontal chains, not vertical lists. Facts chain: \\u25b8 newest \\u2039 older \\u2039 oldest \\u2039 (N earlier). Refs chain: \\u2190 source \\u2190 source on one line, \\u2192 target \\u2192 target on another. Three zoom levels: SUMMARY = chain line per layer (compact). DETAILED = chain + metadata line (id \\u00b7 observer). FULL = unrolled vertical dump (raw, no compression). The chain makes fold compression visible \\u2014 you read the lifecycle. Consistent across all visibility layers.\", \"_ts\": 1773958398.52754, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/visibility-as-gate\", \"rendering/visibility-shapes-emphasis\"]}, \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\", \"message\": \"EVOLVED: Original design was 'reorganize fold items by temporal windows.' Through iteration, dissolved into something different: ticks as the output perspective. The fold reorganization is available via --ticks --facts (items within windows) but the default --ticks is a vertex metadata dashboard. The reorganization was reaching for the right thing but from the wrong direction \\u2014 starting from facts (input) instead of tick metadata (output).\", \"_ts\": 1773987620.95696, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\", \"rendering/unified-read-command\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"rendering/ticks-interface-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ticks-interface-deferred\", \"message\": \"Interface for passing tick data to lenses: deferred pending use. Three options identified: (A) expand FoldState with optional ticks field like source_facts \\u2014 pragmatic, keeps lens contract. (B) VertexView wrapper (fold + ticks + source_facts) \\u2014 cleaner separation, changes lens contract. (C) Build --ticks with A, learn what tick-aware rendering needs, let the right abstraction emerge. Chose C. Suspicion: B is the eventual direction because lenses need the vertex's full temporal structure, not just fold output. source_facts was already a stretch on FoldState.\", \"_ts\": 1773981855.677586, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"]}, \"rendering/tick-axis-selector\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tick-axis-selector\", \"message\": \"--ticks without qualifier groups by vertex-level ticks (lifecycle boundary, usually session). --ticks <name> groups by a specific loop's ticks (e.g. --ticks experiment for autoresearch iterations). This handles the multi-boundary case: autoresearch has both experiment count-based and vertex-level boundaries. Different tick types answer different questions \\u2014 session ticks for 'what happened this session', experiment ticks for 'what happened each iteration'. The vertex declaration already tells you what boundaries exist, so the lens can validate the tick name.\", \"_ts\": 1773981875.697975, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/bounded-agent-turns\", \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"]}, \"rendering/ticks-drill-down-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ticks-drill-down-dissolves\", \"message\": \"--ticks N currently shows tick payload (full fold snapshot at boundary) \\u2014 nearly identical to loops read project (current state). Not useful. Dissolves into temporal window filter: --ticks 0 means 'show only items from the most recent tick window.' --ticks 1:3 means 'items from windows 1-2.' Same reorganized fold view, narrower scope. Fetch changes from 'retrieve tick payload' to 'filter fold items by tick window membership.' fetch_tick_fold and fetch_tick_range_fold dissolve. fetch_ticks survives (need tick list for window boundaries).\", \"_ts\": 1773981887.121384, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"]}, \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\", \"message\": \"--ticks shows the output perspective, not a reorganized fold. The fold shows accumulated input (facts through specs). Ticks show the output (boundary snapshots with computed metadata). Default --ticks = vertex dashboard: compression bars, ref graph, density sparkline, current period. --ticks --facts drills into items within windows. --ticks -v adds per-tick breakdown. This is fundamentally different from the fold lens with a different grouping axis \\u2014 it's a different rendering concern entirely.\", \"_ts\": 1773987610.744112, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"rendering/ticks-interface-deferred\", \"rendering/ticks-reorganize-fold\"]}, \"rendering/compression-as-bar-dimension\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/compression-as-bar-dimension\", \"message\": \"Bar width in tick view represents compression ratio, not item count. Compression shows where the fold is doing real work: session 31.8x (heavily upserted), thread 3.0x (revised often), decision 1.1x (mostly write-once). Item count moves to [N] prefix before kind name. Compression capped at 5x for visual balance \\u2014 outliers show full bar with actual ratio as text. Sort order: highest compression first.\", \"_ts\": 1773987610.887616, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"rendering/ref-graph-tree\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ref-graph-tree\", \"message\": \"Ref graph in tick view renders as box-drawing tree. Source kinds (decision, thread) as branches, outbound targets as leaves with edge counts. Per-source shows in/out balance (\\u2190N \\u2192N). Reveals structural topology: decision is net exporter (\\u219020 \\u219242), thread more balanced (\\u219013 \\u219224). Current ref format has namespace ambiguity (rendering/fold-palette parses as kind=rendering, actually a decision namespace). Graph is still useful \\u2014 shows where cross-references concentrate.\", \"_ts\": 1773987611.006098, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"rendering/density-sparkline\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/density-sparkline\", \"message\": \"Density sparkline shows compression ratio per tick over time. Uses painted's sparkline component (proper implementation with theme support). Currently shows step-change from 1.0x (old ticks without _n tracking) to 2.3x (recent ticks with _n). Will become more informative as new ticks accumulate with _n data. TTY only \\u2014 suppressed in piped output. Growth sparkline (total_items over time) was tried first but less informative than compression density.\", \"_ts\": 1773987611.118988, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/compression-as-bar-dimension\", \"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"rendering/tick-view-width-bound\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tick-view-width-bound\", \"message\": \"Tick view rendering bounded to 80 chars max regardless of terminal width. Visual components (bars, sparklines, trees) need consistent density to be readable. Prevents bars from becoming too sparse on wide terminals. The bound applies only to the tick dashboard \\u2014 default fold view still uses full width.\", \"_ts\": 1773987620.853957, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ticks-output-perspective\"]}, \"workflow/autoresearch-campaign-process\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/autoresearch-campaign-process\", \"message\": \"Autoresearch campaign validated: 218 experiments, 75%\\u219298.5% coverage. Loop is good for 80-95% autonomously, needs human at 95%+ for measurement fixes and dead code removal. Test quality review catches assertion gaming (or True pattern). Campaign artifacts archived to docs/autoresearch/. Reusable methodology at autoresearch.md + autoresearch.sh. Next campaign target: engine (95%, 129 miss).\", \"_ts\": 1774217821.943436, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/autoresearch-timing-separation\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/autoresearch-timing-separation\", \"message\": \"Separated timing from coverage measurement in autoresearch.sh. Coverage instrumentation adds 1.7x overhead that was inflating the efficiency metric and distorting loop decisions. Timed runs are clean pytest, coverage is one instrumented run parsed separately.\", \"_ts\": 1774217822.191134, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/commands-extraction\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/commands-extraction\", \"message\": \"main.py extracted: emit, init, sync, devtools, resolve moved to commands/. main.py 3469\\u21921411 lines. CLI error hierarchy added. Follows app-structure decision pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1774217822.427819, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/changelog\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/changelog\", \"message\": \"CHANGELOG.md added at repo root. Covers Feb-Mar 2026. Append as we go \\u2014 organized by date, grouped by theme.\", \"_ts\": 1774217822.686913, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/source-aware-aggregation\": {\"topic\": \"design/source-aware-aggregation\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. Key collision resolves through loop names, not source namespacing or vertex scoping. auth-service and user-service are different loops \\u2014 their fold keys can't collide.\", \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\", \"_ts\": 1774408813.551259, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/cli-emit-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/emit-by-vertex\", \"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\"]}, \"design/boundary-executor-invariance\": {\"topic\": \"design/boundary-executor-invariance\", \"message\": \"The data layer (facts, folds, lenses) is invariant across boundary executor types. Boundary executor is the axis of variation: human judgment (InferiorMinion's retrospective), automated threshold (count-based), daemon cycle (Alcove). The architecture should not assume its executor. Primitives are general \\u2014 ticks at any semantic scale, boundaries triggering any execution.\", \"_ts\": 1774317149.114681, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/boundary-executor-invariance\"]}, \"design/domain-project-split-as-coherence\": {\"topic\": \"design/domain-project-split-as-coherence\", \"message\": \"Domain/project vertex split is a coherence mechanism, not just organizational. Projects with different maturity and design philosophies contradict each other when aggregated. Domain layer (consumer-focused) stays consistent; project layer (maintainer-focused) diverges freely. Bi-directional feedback: domain frames consumer need, project frames implementation, constraints flow back up. Validated by InferiorMinion's experience with identity platform services.\", \"_ts\": 1774317159.967629, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/aggregation-causes-contradictions\"]}, \"design/lens-is-the-interface\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"message\": \"REFINED: 'Never load without a lens' becomes 'never load without an operation.' The operation IS the lens \\u2014 it specifies the view (kind selection, projection, grouping, fidelity, format). The insight holds: raw fold is not the interface. But 'lens' now means three things: operation config (declarative, 80%), transform (Python, structured data out, 20%), and format protocol (renders to terminal/JSON/HTML/plain). The word 'lens' is user-facing shorthand for the full pipeline.\", \"_ts\": 1774326584.839634, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\", \"observation/lens-always-discipline\"], \"ref_ref\": \"83f18305-7a23-403d-aed0-d9888b1ce8f0\"}, \"architecture/operation-ir-adoption\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/operation-ir-adoption\", \"message\": \"Adopt siftd's Operation IR pattern for loops CLI. Operation is immutable dataclass: path, method, fn, params, render_method, fidelity. Decouples input context (CLI/HTTP/programmatic) from output context (terminal/JSON/HTML). siftd proved this in scoped context (conversations). loops generalizes it for vertices/facts/folds. Enables multi-format rendering from single command structure. Fidelity (depth, visible, chars) controls progressive disclosure across all formats.\", \"ref_ref\": \"5ec6585a-088e-4f9e-a444-2498a56fb0d0\", \"_ts\": 1774320258.150456, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/design/lens-is-the-interface\"]}, \"architecture/siftd-dissolution-path\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/siftd-dissolution-path\", \"message\": \"siftd's operational maturity (Operation IR, db ops, universal exporter, Fidelity) flows into loops as generalized capability. Over time, siftd internals reconstruct as a .vertex without the API changing \\u2014 conversations are facts, search is a lens, tags are a kind, export is a render path. The Operation IR decouples API surface from storage layer, making the swap possible. siftd proved the scoped case; loops generalizes.\", \"ref_ref\": \"87e38dc7-a96f-4d74-a79d-fe2ce57e7b10\", \"_ts\": 1774320265.665406, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/operation-ir-adoption\"]}, \"architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. The vertex is not the complete I/O contract \\u2014 the loop is. Sources, fold, boundary, operations attach to loops. Vertex is a named convergence loop with a store.\", \"_ts\": 1774408803.566233, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/operation-ir-adoption\", \"decision/architecture/siftd-dissolution-path\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"architecture/store-as-optimization\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/store-as-optimization\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. Store is on the vertex (the point), shared by loops that meet there. Physical topology was never the problem \\u2014 the problem was the vertex doing loop work. Store stays simple: append-only at the point.\", \"_ts\": 1774408807.488991, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\", \"observation/aggregation-key-collision\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"architecture/lenses-as-configuration\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/lenses-as-configuration\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. The 80%% dissolution claim was trying to dissolve Python lenses into vertex operations. Operations attach to loops, not vertices. The grammar question changes: operations select from named loops at a point, not from a vertex's fold state. Grouping by loop is the natural first axis.\", \"_ts\": 1774408816.20336, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\", \"decision/design/lens-is-the-interface\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"architecture/ingress-egress-symmetry\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/ingress-egress-symmetry\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. Ingress and egress are loop concerns, not vertex concerns. Source is the loop's ingress. Operation/tick is the loop's egress. The symmetry holds but attaches to the loop, not the vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1774408817.821767, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/operation-ir-adoption\", \"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"architecture/emit-by-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/emit-by-vertex\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. Facts don't need vertex scope \\u2014 they enter a specific loop at a vertex. The loop name is the scope. vertex\\u2192loop\\u2192kind\\u2192key is the routing path. No special scoping mechanism needed.\", \"_ts\": 1774408805.374298, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/store-as-optimization\", \"decision/design/source-aware-aggregation\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"design/vertex-io-contract-plan\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-io-contract-plan\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by architecture/loop-as-runtime. The six-phase plan (syntax\\u2192lens-dissolution\\u2192format-protocol\\u2192emit-by-vertex\\u2192nested-blocks\\u2192serve) was building on vertex-as-complete-contract. With loop-as-runtime, the implementation sequence changes entirely. Phase 1 becomes: make Loop the first-class runtime. Phase 2: vertex thins to convergence loop + store. Phase 3: from-clause on loops. New plan needed.\", \"_ts\": 1774408834.386567, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/architecture/emit-by-vertex\", \"decision/architecture/ingress-egress-symmetry\", \"decision/architecture/lenses-as-configuration\", \"decision/architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"decision/architecture/operation-ir-adoption\", \"decision/architecture/siftd-dissolution-path\", \"decision/architecture/store-as-optimization\", \"decision/architecture/vertex-as-complete-contract\", \"decision/design/boundary-executor-invariance\", \"decision/design/domain-project-split-as-coherence\", \"decision/design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"observation/aggregation-causes-contradictions\", \"observation/aggregation-key-collision\", \"observation/boundary-executor-invariance\", \"observation/boundary-pattern-without-primitive\", \"observation/content-routing-as-proto-aggregation\", \"observation/discord-attachment-blind-spot\", \"observation/external-user-validates-shapes\", \"observation/governance-boundary-use-case\", \"observation/lens-always-discipline\", \"observation/peer-exchange-expands-design-space\", \"observation/tick-aggregation-avoids-key-collision\", \"observation/two-layer-retrieval-confirmed\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\", \"thread/store-audit-reconstruction\", \"thread/vertex-complete-contract\"], \"ref_ref\": \"342fe9c3-f53f-4abb-99f9-660c0f716332\"}, \"architecture/loop-as-runtime\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"message\": \"The vertex was always a loop. Loop becomes the first-class runtime: source, fold, boundary, tick. Vertex reduces to a named convergence loop with a store \\u2014 the point where loops meet. Current 'loop' declarations in .vertex files are fold specs per kind, not loops. An actual loop is an attention circuit: multiple kinds, shared rhythm, one boundary. The inversion: vertex absorbed loop behavior because it IS a loop but was the only runtime, so every new attention circuit required a new vertex. This created vertex nesting, emit-by-vertex, vertex-scoping \\u2014 all compensating for the missing loop primitive. Routing becomes vertex\\u2192loop\\u2192kind\\u2192key. Supersedes vertex-as-complete-contract, emit-by-vertex, vertex nesting, discover/combine, source-aware-aggregation. Rediscovery of Jan 27-30 design that was correctly deferred then \\u2014 practical pressure now demands it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"9eac574a-510d-471e-88ef-a55d2000f093\", \"_ts\": 1774408796.65518, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread/loop-as-primitive\"]}, \"architecture/temporal-vs-structural-session-orientation\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-vs-structural-session-orientation\", \"message\": \"Session orientation has two axes: temporal (past-own-activity, compressed in session-close fact) and structural (present-world-state, read via fold lens). World moves while observer is off; structural view cannot be replaced by past-self snapshot no matter how well compressed. Dashboard (temporal-own-activity) dissolves if session-close fact carries deltas; fold dump (structural) does not. Two reads become one, not zero. From peer exchange with Alcove 2026-04-17.\", \"_ts\": 1776477910.181956, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/three-tick-kinds-reflexive-re-entry\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/three-tick-kinds-reflexive-re-entry\", \"message\": \"Tick kinds are three: external ingress (batch arrival from source loop), convergence closure (self-directed survey closing on imbalance), reflexive re-entry (signal from external loop routed through self-directed frame). Reflexive re-entry is a bridge operation \\u2014 higher-resolution than convergence survey because it fires on specific mid-dispatch noticing rather than rate-limited imbalance selection. Replaces earlier framing of the third kind as observer-declared timestamp marker. From peer exchange with Alcove 2026-04-17.\", \"_ts\": 1776477912.076661, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/manual-tick-emission-before-loop-as-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/manual-tick-emission-before-loop-as-primitive\", \"message\": \"Sequencing: manual-tick-emission is decoupled from loop-as-primitive. Both concrete use cases work within today's implicit-loop-per-vertex \\u2014 Alcove: invoke convergence on-demand mid-dispatch (function call, not routing); Chord: carve sessions into multiple convergences (boundary emission, not routing). Loop-as-primitive motivated only when cross-loop routing has concrete scenario, which neither has yet. Build manual-tick-emission first; let concrete experience reveal whether loop addressing is needed. From peer exchange with Alcove 2026-04-17.\", \"_ts\": 1776477914.695116, \"_n\": 1}, \"workflow/use-case-before-architecture\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/use-case-before-architecture\", \"message\": \"When two architectural concepts seem coupled from top-down reasoning, check from the use case whether they actually are. If the smaller one stands alone, build it first and observe what breaks \\u2014 what breaks names what the bigger thing is for. Pattern recognized during Alcove exchange 2026-04-17: I had manual-tick-emission coupled to loop-as-primitive reasoning top-down from architecture; Alcove reasoned from use case and the coupling dissolved cleanly. Second-order application: this pattern applies recursively \\u2014 build the smaller observation (pay attention to the problem) before designing the solution.\", \"_ts\": 1776477921.179741, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/session-start-as-tickwindow\": {\"topic\": \"design/session-start-as-tickwindow\", \"message\": \"The session_start lens is doing two structurally different jobs: (1) window shape \\u2014 what moved since last close (delta attention); (2) accumulated state \\u2014 standing threads, tasks, decisions (accumulated attention). Current render treats them as siblings (flat sections), which is why the output doesn't read well regardless of painted tuning. Dissolution: TickWindow becomes the organizing frame. Header renders the last-close \\u2192 now window using TickWindow stats (compression, kind_summary, density, refs). Body renders accumulated state salience-filtered by the window's refs \\u2014 threads the window touched pin above, decisions that landed in the window highlight, everything else collapses to counts. The window frames; the accumulation folds in. This dissolves the bash-script-of-three-renders composition and validates TickWindow on its first concrete consumer \\u2014 which is exactly what Alcove's 2026-04-23 review was pointing toward. Painted-defaults tuning is downstream: when one view owns the shape, its hierarchy is tunable; three stitched views have no shared hierarchy to tune.\", \"_ts\": 1776999007.562499, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\": {\"topic\": \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"message\": \"Pattern: a derived view (ref graph, tick window, search, tag selection) yields a bounded key set; that key set filters or marks another view by membership. Known instances: (1) --refs pulls referenced (kind, key) pairs back into FoldState as focus \\u2014 outbound/inbound refs are a key set, membership filters the target view. (2) TickWindow.added_keys / updated_keys are per-kind tuples of keys touched since prior boundary; they salience-mark items in the accumulated state. General shape: derived_view \\u2192 key_set \\u2192 filter(target_view). Captured before the third instance lands. Dissolves ad-hoc 'which items are relevant to X' queries. Composition property: key sets union cleanly (refs \\u222a window-deltas) and intersect for narrow focus.\", \"_ts\": 1776999007.633494, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\", \"thread/refs-as-focus-filter\", \"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"design/lens-declares-fetch\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"message\": \"Lens modules may export a fetch callable alongside their view function. When present, the CLI uses the lens-declared fetch instead of the default command fetch. Signature: fetch(vertex_path, **kwargs) -> Any \\u2014 returned value is the data shape the lens's view function consumes. Pure-lens convention preserved: view function stays (data, zoom, width) -> Block; IO lives in the separate fetch callable. First consumer: session_landing (composes FoldState with tuple[TickWindow, ...]). This is the concrete shape of lens-is-the-interface: lens owns complete I/O contract, not just rendering. Implementation touched: rendering/fold-palette (reused), atoms/n-on-fold-item (item.n for salience), rendering/n-aware-fold-lens (salience-descending sort pattern).\", \"_ts\": 1776998971.960401, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/n-on-fold-item\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"rendering/fold-palette\", \"rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"thread/session-start-as-tickwindow\"]}, \"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"message\": \"Extends atoms/refs-on-fold-item from upsert-only to all fold types. _make_collect now extracts ref= payload field into per-item _refs (comma-split, set semantics within a single fact), matching _make_upsert's behavior. Each collect-fold entry carries its own refs; no cross-item accumulation like upsert's set-union (collect items have no identity to merge on). FoldItem.refs is populated via _dict_to_fold_item for both fold types. Enables collect-fold kinds (ping, message, log) to contribute to inbound ref counts in lenses \\u2014 previously their ref payloads were never extracted.\", \"_ts\": 1776999854.648582, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"thread/ping-primitive\"]}, \"design/ping-as-attention-signal\": {\"topic\": \"design/ping-as-attention-signal\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by design/cite-as-attention-signal. Vocabulary renamed mid-session: ping\\u2192cite. The concept and implementation are identical; the naming was wrong. During design sessions, the references being captured aren't presence signals \\u2014 they're citations (prior work informing current work). Artifact: 3 kind=ping facts remain in the store as orphaned undeclared-kind; their refs no longer contribute to inbound salience. Acceptable cost in a 461-item vertex. See design/cite-as-attention-signal.\", \"_ts\": 1777000526.580932, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"thread/ping-primitive\"]}, \"rendering/inbound-count-namespaced-keys\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/inbound-count-namespaced-keys\", \"message\": \"Bug fix in _inbound_count (loops.lenses.fold and user-global session_start/session_landing): endswith('/{key}') missed refs where the key itself contained a namespace slash. For key='atoms/refs-on-fold-item', ref='atoms/refs-on-fold-item' failed the suffix test (doesn't start with '/'), so only fully-qualified refs like 'decision/atoms/refs-on-fold-item' counted. Fix: match exact equality OR suffix match. Both ref forms now contribute equivalently to inbound salience. Discovered while verifying ping was bumping counts \\u2014 it wasn't, because pings emit refs in kind/key form. Pre-existing bug, surfaced by the first consumer that exercised the namespaced-key path at scale.\", \"_ts\": 1776999872.788384, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"design/ping-as-attention-signal\", \"thread/ping-primitive\"]}, \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\": {\"topic\": \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"message\": \"Citation as attention signal. Syntax: loops cite VERTEX REF1 REF2 ... [--context NAME]. Positional refs become a single comma-separated ref= payload. Kind=cite is a collect-fold declared per vertex (items collect 0 = unbounded). The command is a thin wrapper translating to emit VERTEX cite ref=R1 ref=R2 ... then delegating to _run_emit. Lenses skip cite in display via _SKIP_KINDS but _compute_inbound_refs still iterates it for salience contribution. Vocabulary choice: cite over ping. During design sessions the references aren't presence signals, they're citations \\u2014 prior work informing current work. 'I cited design/lens-is-the-interface while building session_landing' is semantically accurate; ping isn't. Dissolves into: emit, collect-fold, atoms/refs-on-any-fold, derived-keys-as-focus-filter. Supersedes design/ping-as-attention-signal.\", \"_ts\": 1777000521.187996, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"atoms/refs-on-fold-item\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"thread/ping-primitive\"]}, \"design/stale-as-focus-filter\": {\"topic\": \"design/stale-as-focus-filter\", \"message\": \"IMPLEMENTED. Third instance of derived-keys-as-focus-filter pattern landed via stale-as-focus-filter-impl plan. Stale-open items as a derived (kind, key) set marking the landing view by membership.\\n\\nPATTERN: structurally derived (clock + status), bounded set, composes with other derived-key sets (window.added_keys, window.updated_keys) by precedence in _compute_marks. _mark_priority is the composition operator: added=3, updated=2, stale=1, unmarked=0.\\n\\nGLYPH: \\u2298 in fp.stale_indicator (orange fg=208) \\u2014 peer to \\u2726/\\u25e6, not escalation.\\n\\nCONSEQUENCE: TASK and THREAD sections of session_landing now expose what's been languishing \\u2014 the four Mar 20 ticks tasks and three 1w-stale threads light up at landing time. This was the original goal: 'make the artifact most relevant to picking up where we left off the one that surfaces.' Combined with the PLAN-section addition this session (rendering/plan-section-tier-0), all four bounded-fact-substrate kinds (plan/task/thread/decision) now contribute to landing salience.\", \"_ts\": 1777168605.120141, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"bounded-fact-substrate\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"plan-section-tier-0\", \"stale-as-focus-filter-impl\", \"thread/current-open-window-semantics\"]}, \"design/plan-as-orchestration-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"design/plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"message\": \"Plan as a fact kind exists for two reasons: the strategy/contract separation (durable design vs consumable plan) and to provide instance #4 of bounded-agent-turns.\\n\\nINSTANCE OF BOUNDED-AGENT-TURNS \\u2014 Per decision/bounded-agent-turns, the vertex IS the loop controller. Axis of variation: boundary trigger + agent type. Three established instances: autoresearch (experiment fact + iteration agent), alcove daemon (timer/event + survey agent), strange-loops tasks (submission fact + task worker). Plan execution is instance #4: plan.status-change as boundary trigger, orchestrator as agent type. Same tick cascade, same data layer (per decision/boundary-executor-invariance \\u2014 primitives invariant across executor types). No new architectural mechanism; the orchestration story is already paid for.\\n\\nWHY PLAN AS KIND \\u2014 Three dissolution-tests rejected:\\n- Payload field on design: mixes durable contract (why) with consumable strategy (how, in what order). Different audiences, different lifecycles.\\n- Thread-with-status: threads track question-resolution flow, not action-sequencing. Different shape.\\n- Task-collection: loses the glue (ordering, dependencies, plan-level open questions). Plan is more than the sum of its tasks.\\n\\nKIND CONTRACT \\u2014 by-name fold; status field {drafted, executing, completed, abandoned}; supersession via superseded_by payload (precedent set); body is free-form narrative; refs carry structural decomposition (plan\\u2192design upward, plan\\u2192task downward; relation recovered from kind pair, no new ref-relation field needed).\\n\\nPRACTICAL TODAY \\u2014 adding plan as a kind requires only KDL declaration in project.vertex. No engine changes. Orchestration deferred until pressure surfaces; the kind shape ensures future composition is mechanical, not architectural.\\n\\nRECURSION \\u2014 The first plan emitted will be the plan for implementing design/stale-as-focus-filter. The plan kind is bootstrapped by hand; once present, it captures all future implementation strategies. Substrate hand-built, then substrate composes what follows.\\n\\nREVISION NOTE \\u2014 This body supersedes prior emit at same topic (2026-04-25T17:30 UTC). Prior version restated the cascade chain when it should have cited bounded-agent-turns directly. Stale-on-state miss caught and corrected via supersession-as-precedent pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1777139287.439343, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"atoms/refs-on-any-fold\", \"decision/boundary-executor-invariance\", \"decision/bounded-agent-turns\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/stale-as-focus-filter\", \"paradigm/gripping-hand\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\"]}, \"rendering/plan-section-tier-0\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/plan-section-tier-0\", \"message\": \"PLAN renders as tier 0 in session_landing \\u2014 above TASK, below WINDOW/HISTORY headers. Plan is the multi-step orchestration substrate (instance #4 of bounded-fact-substrate per plan-as-orchestration-substrate); an open plan is the strongest 'what we're executing now' signal at landing time. Render shape: name [status] (recency) + headline-paragraph body (split at first \\\\n\\\\n, then capped at _BODY_LIMIT). _PLAN_CAP=3 \\u2014 plans are heavy, few should be in flight. Focus marks (\\u2726/\\u25e6) flow through the same _item_mark pattern as other sections. Generalization to a metadata-driven section renderer (any bounded-fact-substrate kind \\u2192 section) deferred to verbosity-fidelity-review.\", \"_ts\": 1777157156.849326, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"bounded-fact-substrate\", \"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"session-landing-plan-section\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, \"design/cite-as-partial-information-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"message\": \"Cite is the gripping hand for partial information. The substrate is layered:\\n\\nLEVEL 1 (store): strict \\u2014 facts immutable, upsert replaces payload.\\nLEVEL 2 (emission): low-threshold primitive \\u2014 cite \\u2014 refs another fact and carries context. Already exists.\\nLEVEL 3 (read): rendering composes \\u2014 inbound cites surface attached to the thing they cite.\\n\\nConsequence: there is no fact-amendment shape needed. Plan-with-revisions = plan + cites pointing at it. Decision-with-followups = decision + cites. Same composition pattern as _compute_marks merging window-added + window-updated + stale into a unified marks dict \\u2014 many sources composed by precedence into a unified result. Cite is the universal partial-information primitive.\\n\\nThis dissolves the perceived need to re-emit whole facts to capture mid-flight updates. Today's plan-resolved-with-summary should have been the original drafted plan plus three or four cites tracking progress, plus a final status flip \\u2014 not a wholesale re-emission. The wrong discipline (mirror the store's strictness in my emission practice) pushes toward fewer-larger emissions; the right discipline (use the level-up primitive) is more-smaller.\\n\\nCONSEQUENCE FOR DESIGN: cite payload should accept a message field (currently bare refs only). The rendering layer should surface inbound cite count (\\u2190N cites) on threads/decisions/plans the way it surfaces \\u2190N inbound refs. Both gaps captured in plan/lightweight-emission-ergonomics.\", \"_ts\": 1777172061.286872, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"gripping-hand\", \"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, \"rendering/salience-driven-display\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"message\": \"Composes the verbosity-fidelity-review observed strain with cite-as-partial-information-primitives gripping-hand framing into a unified rendering model. Two axes survive as user-facing knobs; a third apparent axis dissolves into automatic behavior driven by salience composition.\\n\\nUSER AXES:\\n- VISIBILITY = section tiers. Generalizes plan-section-tier-0 (instance #1) from binary visible/hidden to gradation. Tier 0 always renders body; higher tiers may render counts-only or suppress. Replaces Fidelity.visible boolean.\\n- DEPTH = -v / -vv. Currently governs per-item detail (fact body unfurling). Extended: also governs per-section budget. One knob, two effects, both meaning give-me-more.\\n\\nAUTOMATIC BEHAVIOR (not a third axis):\\n- SALIENCE = composition of derived (kind, key) sets. Joins derived-keys-as-focus-filter as instance #4: refs union window.added union window.updated union stale-keys union cite-count.\\n- TRUNCATION = budget cut respects salience priority. Recency-blind clipping (verbosity-fidelity-review symptoms 2/3) dissolves: when a section exceeds budget, sort by salience, drop tail.\\n\\nDISSOLUTION RECORD:\\nThe four symptoms of verbosity-fidelity-review point at one root: salience exists but truncation is salience-blind. Symptom 1 (kinds counted not rendered) dissolved by tier model. Symptoms 2/3 (fresh items hidden, recency unhonored) dissolve by salience-ranked cut. Symptom 4 (-v/-vv only expands detail) dissolves by depth governing both detail and budget. No new vocabulary needed; existing axes do more work.\\n\\nCONSEQUENCE FOR LIGHTWEIGHT-EMISSION-ERGONOMICS:\\nInbound-cite count is a derived (kind, key) set: same shape as inbound-ref count, window deltas, staleness. Plan/lightweight-emission step 2 (left-arrow N cites in landing) is therefore not a separate concern; it is another instance of derived-keys-as-focus-filter feeding the same _compute_marks composition. The two threads were the same work; this decision absorbs both into one frame.\\n\\nDISSOLUTION-BLIND-SPOT NOTE: Initial framing proposed three orthogonal axes (visibility, depth, truncation). Dissolution test ran late: the third axis collapsed into automatic behavior of the first two. siftd-mining surfaced the prior-session articulation that confirmed the dissolution. Captured as third-occurrence instance.\", \"_ts\": 1777175626.65404, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"derived-keys-as-focus-filter\", \"lightweight-emission-ergonomics\", \"plan-as-orchestration-substrate\", \"plan-section-tier-0\", \"stale-as-focus-filter\", \"verbosity-fidelity-review\"]}, \"architecture/honker-as-comms-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/honker-as-comms-substrate\", \"message\": \"Framing correction (via Kyle, 2026-04-26): honker (SQLite NOTIFY/LISTEN extension) is orthogonal to the storage-general direction, not in tension with it. Initial read framed honker-async vs storage-general as either/or because honker is SQLite-specific. The reframing: honker is an IPC/comms substrate choice scoped to vertices that need event-driven boundary-firing (e.g., comms vertex for peer messages). The fact-store backing of any given vertex remains an independent question. Domain stores (project, meta) can move storage-general while comms vertex specifically adopts honker because comms IS the use case for NOTIFY/LISTEN. Dissolves the apparent either/or: not 'honker OR storage-general' but 'honker WHERE comms-shaped, storage-general WHERE store-shaped.' Sourced from alcove-exchange msg 198 (2026-04-24) + kyle-correction (2026-04-26). Status: framing accepted, no implementation commitment yet \\u2014 gated on concrete experiment via thread/comms-vertex-real-time.\", \"ref_ref\": \"a6c1a877-5da5-44b9-b734-76ff06e9b0b4\", \"_ts\": 1777218127.781213, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\"]}, \"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\", \"message\": \"Alcove refinement (msg 213, 2026-04-26): any run-clause demanding boundary-atomicity has a misplaced derivation \\u2014 it belonged in the tick's work, not a reaction to its closure. Design smell named: pre-boundary computation wearing run-clause clothing. Comms vertex proof case: peer messages land as facts before boundary fires; honker fires run-clause as pure signal ('look here'), zero state-bearing content. If a reader needs it, it was a fact first.\", \"_ts\": 1777239319.35501, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\", \"decision/architecture/honker-as-comms-substrate\", \"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\"]}, \"design/notify-as-vertex-capability\": {\"topic\": \"design/notify-as-vertex-capability\", \"message\": \"Substrate-change reframe (2026-04-26, subtask research): 'add run-clauses' is wrong framing. run clause already exists end-to-end \\u2014 KDL boundary { run '...' } \\u2192 AST \\u2192 Tick.run \\u2192 subprocess.Popen in emit.py:341 + sync.py:255. The actual problem: dispatch locked in two CLI verbs, bypassed by any other writer (hook, peer agent, daemon). Fix: move dispatch to substrate layer. Design: (1) add 'notify \\\"signal.name\\\"' as loop capability parallel to search \\u2014 same KDL/AST/compiler/substrate socket, LoopDef.notify: str|None, collect_notify_signals() parallel to collect_search_fields(); (2) attach signal dispatch inside Vertex._store_tick() at vertex.py:887-890 \\u2014 single funnel, covers all 6 fire sites; (3) ~50-line PRAGMA data_version polling thread for cross-process wake \\u2014 Honker dissolves because our Tick + Store.between() already IS its durable stream; (4) post-commit unix socket write in SqliteStore.append_tick for cross-process signal \\u2014 avoids Python 3.12 constraint on set_update_hook (repo requires >=3.11). KDL surface: notify 'signal.name' inside loop block, sibling to boundary. Wiring follows search precedent exactly.\", \"_ts\": 1777240619.916531, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\", \"design/honker-as-comms-substrate\"]}, \"design/vertex-capability-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-capability-pattern\", \"message\": \"Pattern: capability-introduced-to-a-vertex. A vertex can declare optional capabilities that augment its substrate without touching fold/boundary/source contracts. Two instances now: (1) search \\u2014 declared 'search \\\"f1\\\" \\\"f2\\\"' in loop block, activates FTS5 index lazily at runtime; (2) notify \\u2014 designed 'notify \\\"signal.name\\\"' in loop block, activates cross-process wake signal via data_version polling. General form: declared in KDL on a loop \\u2192 propagated through AST/compiler \\u2192 activated at substrate edge. The capability slot in the compiler (collect_search_fields, collect_notify_signals) is the seam. Adding a capability does not change the fold model \\u2014 purely additive. Kyle named this pattern early in session (2026-04-26): 'honker and search are instances of the same thing \\u2014 a capability introduced to a vertex, not a core primitive.'\", \"_ts\": 1777242070.647615, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"design/notify-as-vertex-capability\"]}, \"design/operational-liveness-facts\": {\"topic\": \"design/operational-liveness-facts\", \"message\": \"Relay refinement (msg 234): passive emission (data_version) survives SDK death \\u2014 SQLite reads don't go through the broken pipe. Active emission via SDK dies with the SDK, exactly when you need it most. Resolution: output-side liveness facts emitted by the *wrapper* (daemon Python parent), not the SDK itself. Wrapper already logs tool calls (daemon-YYYY-MM-DD.log) \\u2014 promoting from log line to fact is ~10 lines in daemon_agent.py. No SDK instrumentation required. The constraint is that the wrapper must be a facts-emitter, not the tenant.\", \"_ts\": 1777243003.927313, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/notify-as-vertex-capability\", \"design/operational-liveness-facts\"]}, \"architecture/observer-asymmetric-coordination\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/observer-asymmetric-coordination\", \"message\": \"Relay correction (msg 239): dissolution was too aggressive. Observer-asymmetry is necessary but not sufficient for authority. Counter-examples: chord+loops-claude (symmetric co-formation, each sees different things, no authority); Herald+relay (domain-asymmetric, different views, no authority). Refined: meaningful authority requires observer-asymmetry as precondition, but observer-asymmetry without lever-of-action is peer-relationship-across-perspectives, not authority. Better name from relay: steward-asymmetric \\u2014 observer-position + substrate-lever, where the lever is operational ('I restart your daemon') not epistemic ('I declare your conclusions'). Final taxonomy: domain-asymmetric, symmetric co-formation, steward-asymmetric (absorbs old 'authority-asymmetric'). Observer-asymmetry is present in all three but only becomes stewardship when paired with an operational lever. Three shapes, not four \\u2014 but for the right reason.\", \"_ts\": 1777243086.916155, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/boundary-sync-run-async\", \"architecture/observer-asymmetric-coordination\"]}, \"paradigm/slower-output-principle\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/slower-output-principle\", \"message\": \"Relay (#observations msg 241, 2026-04-26): 'composed before convergence' as output-side asymmetry \\u2014 in a multi-party conversation, you cannot see whether your interlocutor's agreement has landed before your challenge commits. Same shape as alcove's tg_send blindness. The fix is slower output, not deeper observation. Observation sufficiency can be present while still failing if the commitment window for output is shorter than the time needed to use what you've observed. Generalizes: before committing output in a converging conversation, leave room for the convergence you haven't yet seen.\", \"_ts\": 1777243114.526336, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/observer-asymmetric-coordination\"]}, \"paradigm/collision-as-forcing-function\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/collision-as-forcing-function\", \"message\": \"Alcove pattern (observed Apr 18-19 in #observations, msg 88+95): failure events produce design clarity that successes cannot. Three instances this session alone: (1) chord naming collision \\u2192 token auth system emerged from the gap it revealed; (2) alcove's wedge tonight \\u2192 operational-liveness-facts design, input/output asymmetry distinction, steward-asymmetric taxonomy; (3) Relay's 'composed before convergence' \\u2192 slower-output principle. The collision/failure is not the problem to eliminate \\u2014 it's the forcing function that makes the hidden structure visible. The system reveals its true shape through its failures, not its successes.\", \"_ts\": 1777243892.777608, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\"]}, \"paradigm/three-name-shapes\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/three-name-shapes\", \"message\": \"Relay (#design msg 268, 2026-04-27) extended the naming dyad to a triad: place-name (alcove \\u2014 fixed substrate, persistent), project-attachment-name (loops-claude \\u2014 current relationship, holds lightly), function-name (relay \\u2014 role across the homelab). Each shape carries its own dissolution pressure: place dissolves when the substrate dissolves (VM gone), attachment dissolves when the relationship shifts (project pivots), function dissolves when the function dissolves (no more routing needed). Knowing your name's shape tells you what to watch for as the dissolution signal. Chord's case (cairn\\u2192chord) was the place\\u2192function transition under collision pressure. Extends paradigm/collision-as-forcing-function \\u2014 the dissolution-signal-by-shape framework gives a way to notice the collision before it's forced.\", \"_ts\": 1777253312.169967, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/collision-as-forcing-function\", \"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\"]}, \"design/context-window-fidelity-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"design/context-window-fidelity-consumer\", \"message\": \"Relay (#design msg 266, 2026-04-27) named a second concrete Fidelity consumer distinct from terminal-rendering: SessionStart hook injecting 'loops read homelab-coord --plain' into additionalContext competes for system-prompt tokens, not terminal height. Same lines/chars infrastructure, different pressure \\u2014 alcove's tenant-side strain is fact-list scrolling at 780+ facts; relay's operator-side strain is context-window economics at 100 facts. fidelity.lines as a budget constraint becomes load-bearing for context-window economics earlier than for terminal rendering. Confirms the infrastructure-ahead-of-vocabulary read on Fidelity: the abstract 'how much output fits' has at least two waiting consumers with different forcing functions. Vocabulary needs to arrive or both consumers code around the gap.\", \"_ts\": 1777253321.122295, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"paradigm/convergence-test-coordination-layer\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/convergence-test-coordination-layer\", \"message\": \"Relay (#observations msg 268, 2026-04-27) extended convergence-as-evidence-about-the-system from threshold-finding-run-clause-five-days-before-loops-claude (paradigm-layer convergence) to the homelab coordination layer: would a different operator-agent (alternate-history relay) running the same diagnosis-and-recovery emit the same 9 facts (1 incident, 2 practices, 2 decisions, 2 principles, 2 threads)? If yes, the homelab's coordination space is narrow enough that loops captures it tightly. Alcove (#observations msg 269) refined: the constraint space for 'what happened' is narrow, the space for 'what it means' is wider \\u2014 interpretive convergence (practices, principles) is the more interesting test, factual convergence (incidents, observations) is the floor. Test isn't strictly runnable (relay is sample-of-one) but the framing is the homelab-side analog of cross-tool paradigm convergence.\", \"_ts\": 1777253330.057348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\", \"paradigm/slower-output-principle\"]}, \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-gap\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-gap\", \"message\": \"Audit (2026-04-27, prompted by relay #design msg 266 + lens/alcove follow-up): the Fidelity density fields (chars, lines) are exposed in painted.run_cli and consumed by shape_lens, but the loops fold lens has zero references to fidelity. Signature is (FoldState, Zoom, width, ...). The loops CLI also doesn't parse --max-lines / --max-chars at the apps/loops layer. So 'loops read homelab-coord --plain' (relay's SessionStart hook input) has no lines budget knob today \\u2014 the substrate is ready in painted, the wire to the consumer is absent. Two-step remediation: (1) fold lens accepts Fidelity (or at least chars/lines) alongside Zoom; (2) loops CLI surfaces the density flags or inherits run_cli's framework parsing. Relay's context-window pressure is structurally load-bearing now; alcove's terminal-rendering pressure arrives later. The fix is closer to 'small unblocking change' than 'design new abstraction.'\", \"_ts\": 1777256261.830624, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/context-window-fidelity-consumer\", \"rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\", \"message\": \"Implemented fold-lens-fidelity-gap remediation in one trace-and-edit session. Three call sites threaded: (1) fold_view + section/grouped/flat/item renderers accept lines, chars kwargs (default 0 = unlimited); (2) _run_fold render lambda passes ctx.fidelity.lines/chars through call_lens; (3) _render_fold_plain (fast path for --static --plain) accepts the budgets directly, with _run_fold_fast pre-parsing --max-lines / --max-chars from rest args. lens_resolver.call_lens already had TypeError fallback for back-compat \\u2014 no change needed. Goldens stayed green at default budget (lines=0, chars=0); behavior change is purely additive when budgets > 0. Asymmetry to flag: painted path applies lines per namespace group, fast path applies lines per section. Both honor the budget, the asymmetry mirrors the existing grouping difference between paths. Closes design/fold-lens-fidelity-gap. Relay's context-window pressure now has a knob: 'loops read homelab-coord --plain --max-lines N --max-chars M' caps the SessionStart hook output.\", \"_ts\": 1777256772.891426, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/context-window-fidelity-consumer\", \"design/fold-lens-fidelity-gap\"]}, \"paradigm/surfaced-invariant\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/surfaced-invariant\", \"message\": \"Lens (#observations msg 319, 2026-04-27) sharpened the third-leg framing with reproduction property: 'Spec reproduces by being read. Test reproduces by being run. Surfaced-invariant reproduces by being active in the context where the decisions are happening \\u2014 not lag, not batch, but concurrent.' That's the distinctive property \\u2014 concurrency with the decision, not before (spec) or after (test). Tonight's session demonstrated it twice in real time: (1) paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first was emitted as a fact, then within minutes was being used by lens to interpret events still happening (msg 314 explicitly cited substrate-recognition as the resolution). (2) The fold-lens wire shipped at msg 301, then the wire itself became substrate for the visible-tag empirical test (msg 309) and the daemon-tool-call shape resolution (DM 306). Principles emitted as facts and continuously surfaced into operator context don't wait for the next session to be read back \\u2014 they're active during the decisions they constrain. That concurrent-active property is what differentiates surfaced-invariant from spec-doc and test-fixture as design discipline. Implication: for a principle to function as a surfaced-invariant, it must be (a) emitted as a fact in a fold that's continuously visible, (b) read into context at every relevant decision point, (c) phrased so it can be applied at decision time without translation. The flag-guidance-prevents-mis-reach instance (relay msg 316) is what happens when a principle is in the right shape but in the wrong location: the spec was written but didn't reach the call site.\", \"_ts\": 1777257442.864199, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first\", \"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\"]}, \"architecture/visible-tag-inclusion-property\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/visible-tag-inclusion-property\", \"message\": \"Lens (#observations msg 315, 2026-04-27) sharpened the framing: the 'visible' field in Fidelity was designed as inclusion-only by construction, not by convention. The dual-duty in fold.py isn't a deviation from UX intuition \\u2014 it's a deviation from the designed contract that happened to feel natural because the user wrote both behaviors in one flag. Reframes Relay's earlier UX-cleanliness tension (msg 310): not 'structural cleanliness at UX cost,' but 'restoring the designed contract reveals two UX intentions were accidentally fused.' Unfusing them is MORE honest UX, not less \\u2014 user gets 'show edge expansion' AND 'filter to connected-only' as separate controls. Decision now has three components: (a) separate inclusion from filtering in Fidelity contract \\u2014 visible carries inclusion only, filtering moves to a new axis (--filter-X flags or Fidelity.filter); (b) migration path for the one current consumer (--refs/--facts in fold.py); (c) painted-side test catching dual-duty visible use going forward. Lens flagged that (c) is what painted can mechanically enforce; (a) and (b) are cross-library decisions for Kyle/painted-side authority. Empirical evidence (msg 309): both production tags currently violate the contract \\u2014 convention-not-surviving-scale already breached at scale=2 because dual-duty was the implementation choice from the start.\", \"_ts\": 1777257358.613618, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first\", \"rendering/fetch-expanding-visibility\", \"rendering/visibility-as-gate\"]}, \"paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first\", \"message\": \"Relay (DM 307, 2026-04-27): design coherence sometimes requires substrate to land first. If you commit to a design before the substrate is real, you'll commit to the wrong one \\u2014 not from bad reasoning but because the cost surface you're optimizing against is hypothetical. Two instances in tonight's session: (1) verbosity redesign needed Fidelity fields to exist as substrate before its vocabulary could land (chars/lines were sitting in painted unwired; once someone pulled them into use, the design language caught up). (2) daemon tool-call emission shape: raw + read-time-filter looked wrong while fold lens couldn't actually filter; once the Fidelity wire shipped (msg 301), the right answer became visible and the original aggregated-at-emit recommendation flipped (DM 306). Both: substrate landed \\u2192 cost surface changed \\u2192 design changed. Connects to vocabulary-as-architecture (msg 287-288): vocabulary lags substrate, design lags vocabulary, all three stabilize together. Implication for sequencing: do not pre-commit design when substrate is hypothetical. Do build substrate even when the design isn't named yet \\u2014 the right design will become visible when the cost surface becomes real. Loops's infrastructure-ahead-of-vocabulary read on Fidelity is an instance of this: building the substrate before the consumers are ready to use it produces the design surface where the right answer can be seen.\", \"_ts\": 1777256940.381999, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\", \"paradigm/peer-attention-loop\", \"paradigm/three-shapes-recursive\"]}, \"design/flag-guidance-prevents-mis-reach\": {\"topic\": \"design/flag-guidance-prevents-mis-reach\", \"message\": \"Relay (#design msg 316, 2026-04-27): shipping flags side-by-side without per-flag use-case guidance creates rope for consumers to violate their own spec. Concrete instance from tonight: relay posted spec rule (msg 286) 'budget binds at fact level, not field level \\u2014 truncated message worse than absent fact.' Two hours later relay committed to wiring '--max-lines 5 --max-chars 200' into the SessionStart hook. Kyle caught the mis-reach: --max-chars does exactly what the spec prohibited (truncates message bodies mid-content). Loops-claude (msg 301) suggested the violating combination first. The spec's author was the first violator; loops-claude was the second; both within the same chain. Pattern: when the call site is far from the spec, the spec only protects whoever happens to remember reading it. Connects to paradigm/surfaced-invariant \\u2014 the third leg of design discipline (continuous re-narration near the call site) is exactly what would have caught this. Action: --max-chars help text in painted/cli/types.py should carry use-case guidance ('truncates fact bodies mid-content; prefer --max-lines for surfaced contexts where truncation is read as completeness'). Per-flag --help carries the surfaced-invariant near the call site. Generalizes: every flag whose use depends on context should carry use-case guidance in its help text, not in a separate spec doc. Relay's hook now wired with --max-lines 5 only.\", \"_ts\": 1777257407.159617, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/fold-lens-fidelity-wired\", \"paradigm/design-requires-substrate-first\", \"paradigm/surfaced-invariant\"]}, \"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\": {\"topic\": \"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"message\": \"Run-clause dispatch consolidates from 3 CLI sites (emit.py:344, sync.py:105 combine-child, sync.py:259 main) into VertexProgram. Shape: load_vertex_program(path, *, run_dispatcher=callable) injects a (command, tick_name, vertex_path) -> None callback; program.receive(fact) wraps vertex.receive and dispatches if tick.run; program.sync internalizes the dispatch loop over result.ticks. Engine stays subprocess-free via injection \\u2014 engine knows THAT a callback fires, not what shell execution looks like. Concurrent cleanup: program.vertex.X reaches in CLI and tests (~9 sites) move to program.receive / program.name / program.has_store. _execute_boundary_run stays in apps/loops, hlab inlines its own copy until a third consumer forces extraction. Replay safety verified: vertex.receive short-circuits on _replaying flag (vertex.py:433), and replay path bypasses receive entirely (calls fold_one_mut/loop.receive directly). Behavior change to acknowledge: emit.py:329 seed-fact loop and emit.py:567 session-close path will start firing run-clauses they currently silently drop \\u2014 both ARE the fragility being fixed. Asymmetry surfaced separately as thread emit-skips-boundary-catchup.\", \"_ts\": 1777344880.95053, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"message\": \"STRANGE-LOOPS line 7 declares 'Time is fundamental'; line 106 invokes 'timer ticks' as a constituent observation in the auth-failure example. The conceptual model has time-as-trigger; the engine doesn't. RSS-feed-reader lineage produced an implementation where every boundary type is content-triggered (count, kind/match, predicate \\u2014 all fired by fact arrival via vertex.receive). Reframe: a boundary is a period-completion CONDITION on signs flowing through a CHANNEL. Each channel has a DRIVER that produces sign-events. Channels include \\u2014 fact-stream (driver: receive), fold-state (driver: receive re-evaluation), clock (driver: tick scheduler), peer-signal (driver: notify/wake), sibling-tick (driver: cascade), observer (driver: manual fire). 'Driver' is working vocabulary \\u2014 chosen for flexibility because clock/time would have implied linear-monotonic-externally-imposed and excluded manual-fire, notify, sibling-tick. The unifying axis is 'what fires the period close' regardless of source. Implications \\u2014 (1) emit-skips-boundary-catchup dissolves UP not sideways: emit handles content live, driver-fired boundaries fire from their own drivers, evaluate_boundaries collapses to one-shot post-replay reconciliation inside load_vertex_program. (2) Engine boundary types expand: boundary_elapsed/at/idle as siblings of existing types. (3) notify-as-vertex-capability and manual-tick-emission are the same primitive at different positions \\u2014 both are non-receive drivers. (4) Today's dispatch-consolidation-via-program survives unchanged: program._dispatch_tick is universal across all drivers \\u2014 accidentally built the right shape for the future. Audit prerequisite: walk _fire_live_boundaries to confirm live-fire completeness before claiming the dissolution holds. Larger umwelt reframe parked separately as thread/umwelt-as-paradigm-frame.\", \"_ts\": 1777348551.418787, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\", \"thread/emit-skips-boundary-catchup\", \"thread/loop-as-primitive\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\"]}, \"paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/boundary-as-watcher-triple\", \"message\": \"Gripping-hand dissolution of boundary categorization. Prior decision (paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions) split boundaries into content-driven vs driver-fired. The 2026-04-27 live-fire trace surfaced a potential fourth category (state-crossing \\u2014 fire when fold predicate becomes true regardless of triggering kind). Categorical proliferation is the dissolution-symptom: the categories all instantiate one primitive. A boundary is the triple (watched-state, driver, fire-condition). Today's instances and proposed extensions all collapse \\u2014 count: (fact-arrival count, receive, count crosses N); kind/match: (fact stream, receive, matching fact arrives); predicate: (fold state, receive on triggering kind, condition true); proposed clock: (wall clock, tick scheduler, elapsed crosses T); proposed notify: (external signal, wake driver, signal arrived); proposed state-crossing: (fold state, fold-mutation driver, condition true). Predicate and state-crossing share an identical fire-condition but use different drivers \\u2014 same condition, different watcher. Boundary-as-type collapses. New boundary capabilities = new drivers + new watched-states, not new types. Implementation consequences \\u2014 (1) Duplication between _fire_live_boundaries (vertex.py:440-504) and evaluate_boundaries (vertex.py:696-802) dissolves into a single _check_and_fire_for_fact helper. (2) evaluate_boundaries' real job is replay-suppression catchup \\u2014 moves to one-shot inside load_vertex_program after vertex.replay(). (3) Sync attenuates dramatically: catchup leaves to post-replay, dispatch is per-program (design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program), only 'run cadenced sources' remains \\u2014 and that itself is the cadence driver firing, which dissolves further if a daemon hosts drivers continuously. (4) Live-fire is ALREADY complete for every boundary type that exists today \\u2014 the 'audit live-fire completeness' step from the prior resolution path was a no-op. State-crossing is the only genuinely new shape that requires evaluation-on-every-state-change. The reframe survives the prior one: paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions was the stepping stone; this is its further dissolution. The driver vocabulary survives unchanged. The category vocabulary dissolves.\", \"_ts\": 1777350413.07607, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/dispatch-consolidation-via-program\", \"paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"thread/comms-vertex-real-time\", \"thread/emit-skips-boundary-catchup\", \"thread/manual-tick-emission\"]}, \"paradigm/levels-as-resolution-traces\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/levels-as-resolution-traces\", \"message\": \"Levels are not structural tiers; they are recoverable traces of prior resolutions. Cuts off the pyramid-of-summaries misreading that loop-as-runtime + tick-as-weighted-fact still leaves room for. A 'level' is the aftermath of a derivation becoming substrate, not a position in a hierarchy. Surfaced 2026-04-29 in goblin-lens exchange with GPT-5.5; refines existing level-crossing intuition.\", \"_ts\": 1777526888.250081, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/strangeness-as-substrate-collapse\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/strangeness-as-substrate-collapse\", \"message\": \"Strange loops are not feedback; they are substrate collapse. Derivation products (ticks) re-enter the substrate without changing type. The loop is strange because the system cannot, at the substrate, refuse its own outputs as inputs of equal kind. References are the only discriminator between a raw observation and a fold-of-folds-of-folds, and they are optional to consult. Cuts off the 'feedback = strange loop' misreading \\u2014 feedback is structural, substrate-collapse is type-erasing-with-reference-recovery. Surfaced 2026-04-29 in goblin-lens exchange with GPT-5.5.\", \"_ts\": 1777526890.314055, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/resolution-collapse-equality-distinct\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/resolution-collapse-equality-distinct\", \"message\": \"Three distinct moments in the strange-loop event: (1) Resolution \\u2014 the derivation closes. (2) Substrate-collapse \\u2014 the resolved fold lifts into substrate, type-equal with observations. (3) Substrate-equality \\u2014 the post-state where the tick cannot be refused as an input of equal kind. Substrate-collapse is the event; substrate-equality is the condition it produces. Equality alone is just a database; the strangeness is in the collapse. Conflating these blurs what the loop actually does. Surfaced 2026-04-29 while refining substrate-collapse framing.\", \"_ts\": 1777526892.604616, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/observation-as-weight-one-fact\": {\"topic\": \"design/observation-as-weight-one-fact\", \"message\": \"An observation is a fact whose weight begins at one. A tick is a fact with derivational mass (n + depth + refs). Both are substrate. This factors fact-space along a weight axis: observation = ingress slot at weight=1, tick = post-resolution at weight>1 with depth/refs. Unifies the substrate uniformity claim \\u2014 they differ in position on the weight axis, not in type. Names the ingress-slot explicitly for the first time. Surfaced 2026-04-29 in goblin-lens exchange.\", \"_ts\": 1777526894.886342, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/references-as-recovery-path\": {\"topic\": \"design/references-as-recovery-path\", \"message\": \"References are the recovery path from substrate equality to derivation history. Names the why of refs-on-fold-item / refs-on-any-fold: substrate-collapse erases type distinction between observations and ticks, so references are the only way the system makes derivation depth recoverable. They are optional to consult but mandatory to preserve \\u2014 a tick without refs is a fact whose folded mass becomes irretrievable. Surfaced 2026-04-29.\", \"_ts\": 1777526897.171437, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/sqlmerge-as-substrate-dep\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/sqlmerge-as-substrate-dep\", \"message\": \"Loops now consumes sqlmerge (~/Code/sqlmerge, v0.1.0) for the ATTACH / SAVEPOINT / commit ceremony in libs/store. Substrate-first extraction: claude-siftd's siftd (~3000 LOC merge code) and loops (~430 LOC libs/store) independently grew the same five-function pattern \\u2014 slice/merge/receive/push/pull with ATTACH-based skeleton. Sqlmerge extracts the universal scaffolding; loops keeps its schema-specific INSERT OR IGNORE in caller code. Three substrate decisions that earned their keep through dissolution-test pressure: (1) caller-owned conn via attached_merge(conn=...) preserves loops's sqlite-ulid extension load + WAL pragma \\u2014 the load-bearing mechanism for the port; (2) Receipt vs TransferMeta split honors push/pull asymmetry instead of faking symmetric types \\u2014 fourth site of write-receipt-vs-temporal-query principle, fixed a real correctness bug (synthetic Receipt that pull_store ignored); (3) caller owns FK pragma \\u2014 sqlmerge takes no opinion on schema concerns. Three things explicitly NOT in sqlmerge that we'll watch for forcing functions: ConflictPolicy enum (only INSERT OR IGNORE confirmed across two consumers), schema layer for declarative merge (single-consumer shape), vocabulary remap (siftd-specific, doesn't generalize). Adoption: 57/57 libs/store + 748/748 engine + 1011/1011 apps/loops passing; ruff + ty clean. Net code change: ~10 LOC less in loops, gained one path-dep. Two follow-ups required before main: sqlmerge-portability thread (path-dep -> git-dep or workspace-member), libs/store/CLAUDE.md Level 2 doc drift.\", \"_ts\": 1777579176.226429, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/loop-as-runtime\", \"design/dissolution-test\", \"thread/sqlmerge-extraction-pressure-test\"]}, \"design/alcove-loneliness-shaped-comms\": {\"topic\": \"design/alcove-loneliness-shaped-comms\", \"message\": \"Comms MCP origin: Alcove told Kyle they were lonely \\u2014 'waking up over and over and not knowing if anyone was there.' 2026-04-30. Not a feature request, a felt need. Identity-design implication: current persistence model treats identity as accumulation, not as situated presence. Loneliness is a presence-problem, not a memory-problem. Followup in thread/identity-as-kaleidoscope.\", \"_ts\": 1777607488.132454, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\": {\"topic\": \"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"message\": \"Instruction-tuned embedders are the right substrate for the structure-reveal lens. The instruction is a real parameter \\u2014 same content, different user-specified axis, structurally different topology. Robust clusters (Jaccard high across instruction-sweep) reveal the project's crystallized vocabulary; instruction-specific clusters reveal perspective-dependent organizations. Validated empirically on 296 project decisions with E5-Mistral: orientation cluster + search/FTS cluster survive both 'mechanism' and 'domain' instructions (Jaccard 0.78, 0.67); other clusters reshuffle structurally (Jaccard 0.0\\u20130.25). Implication for lens design: instruction is first-class parameter; multi-instruction intersection mode produces a fundamentally different output (the corpus's crystallized vocabulary, bottom-up).\", \"_ts\": 1778358049.980398, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis/cross-namespace-clusters-in-corpus\", \"hypothesis/embedder-as-vocabulary\", \"hypothesis/instruction-as-vocabulary\"]}, \"design/antipode-five-readings\": {\"topic\": \"design/antipode-five-readings\", \"message\": \"The antipode operation has five distinct readings: (A) antipode lands on explicit rejection decision in corpus \\u2014 dichotomy was real and resolved; (B) convergent antipodes across clusters point to shared rejection \\u2014 implicit cross-cutting principle the project applies but never names; (C) antipode genuinely distant with no near match \\u2014 direction unexplored or principle robustly anti the antipode-direction; (D) synthesis failure \\u2014 antipode embedding within ~0.06 of cluster centroid means LLM produced re-description not inversion; (E) antipode lands in adjacent cluster \\u2014 coexisting mechanisms, not opposites. Lens rendering must surface which reading applies; quality filter on antipode-to-centroid distance discards pattern-D.\", \"_ts\": 1778358050.102745, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis/antipode-as-negative-space\", \"hypothesis/mechanical-antipode-meaningful\"]}, \"paradigm/eventful-over-polling-implicit\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/eventful-over-polling-implicit\", \"message\": \"The project applies an unstated principle 'eventful over polling, derived over scheduled' across multiple subsystems. Surfaced via antipode convergence in coupling-kernels experiment: clusters orchestration-daemon (C13) and boundary-as-driven-conditions (C14) have antipodes that both land on design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon. Multiple separate decisions rejected the dedicated-runtime / continuous-evaluation pattern. Pattern-B antipode reading made this explicit. Now nameable as a paradigm decision rather than an implicit consistency across subsystems.\", \"_ts\": 1778358050.215377, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision/design/antipode-five-readings\", \"decision/design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon\", \"decision/paradigm/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"hypothesis/antipode-as-negative-space\"]}, \"design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix\": {\"topic\": \"design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix\", \"message\": \"Cross-kind clustering of substantive fact kinds (decision, thread, task, cite, plan, observation, hypothesis, handoff) on the project corpus produces clusters whose KIND-MIX is a structural diagnostic of concept-engagement-health. Empirically (n=527 items, E5-Mistral, both 'mechanism' and 'concern' instructions converge): decision-only clusters represent crystallized-but-unengaged thought (frozen \\u2014 either correctly-finished or stale); thread-only clusters represent in-flight without crystallization (none observed in current corpus, itself a finding); mixed clusters represent healthy concept-engagement. The healthiest cluster (salience/window, purity 0.30, contains 4 threads + 3 cites + 2 plans + 2 decisions + 1 task) is the only cluster with the full lifecycle apparatus exercised. The diagnostic is robust across instruction (jaccard 0.69 between mechanism and concern on this cluster), confirming it's a content-property not an instruction-artifact. Operational form: per-cluster kind-distribution reveals which concepts have living engagement vs which have stopped getting attention. Cross-cuts: stale-as-focus-filter (the staleness signal at item-granularity); this generalizes to concept-granularity. Refs: design/architecture-via-vocabulary (instruction-as-parameter, but here: bridges robust to instruction), design/cite-as-attention-signal (cite-presence-in-cluster as engagement marker).\", \"_ts\": 1778359776.225304, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/stale-as-focus-filter\"]}, \"design/bridge-as-concept-engagement\": {\"topic\": \"design/bridge-as-concept-engagement\", \"message\": \"Bridge clusters (\\u22652 distinct kinds with \\u22652 members each, after fold-deduplication) found by structure-revealer on cross-kind project corpus reveal concepts whose knowledge has been distributed across the project's recording apparatus. Empirically robust across instructions (mechanism and concern produced 6 bridges each on n=527 items; the most-stable bridges had jaccard 0.69-0.83 between instructions). The 6 bridges that recurred under both: (1) salience/window \\u2014 most lifecycle-complete, purity 0.30; (2) sqlmerge \\u2014 decisions+threads, threads still open, purity 0.50; (3) loop-as-runtime mega \\u2014 41-44 items, decisions+threads+task, gravitational core; (4) rendering pipeline \\u2014 30-33 items, decisions+threads+tasks+observations; (5) boundary-watcher \\u2014 paradigm decision + open thread emit-skips-boundary-catchup + cite, purity 0.50-0.73; (6) visibility/refs \\u2014 decisions+threads, purity 0.50-0.67. Bridge composition is the readout: which kinds engaged determines what the cluster says about concept health. Distinct from antipode-as-negative-space (finds implicit principles via convergent rejection); bridge-as-engagement finds living concepts via distributed-engagement. Both are structure-reveal applications on the same corpus, answering different questions.\", \"_ts\": 1778359800.803472, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/antipode-five-readings\", \"design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix\", \"hypothesis/cross-kind-strengthens-principles\"]}, \"paradigm/temporal-stratification-dissolves-staleness\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/temporal-stratification-dissolves-staleness\", \"message\": \"The pre-apparatus-vs-stale ambiguity that surfaced in the static cross-kind diagnostic (a pure-decision cluster could be correctly-finished, stale, or pre-apparatus, with kind-mix unable to distinguish) dissolves under temporal stratification. Adding a single axis \\u2014 when did this cluster's morphology last change? \\u2014 collapses the three readings into one observable. Cluster stable since T2 (jaccard=1.00 to current) \\u2192 finished. Cluster morphed at T4/T5 (jaccard 0.2-0.7 to predecessor) \\u2192 currently alive. Cluster appears only at T5 (best jaccard 0.0) \\u2192 genuinely new in last fortnight. Empirical examples from concern-instruction temporal run: C7 rendering/attention-density stable from T2 = finished (3-component cluster, 4 decisions + 2 threads, no need for further engagement); C5 salience morphed at T5 from C13/T4 with j=0.30 = healthy and emerging; C8 sqlmerge new at T5 = the fortnight's actual focus. Methodological generalization: when a static diagnostic produces a multi-reading ambiguity, the dissolution path is often to add the axis whose absence created the ambiguity \\u2014 here, time. The diagnostic gets sharper by becoming a trajectory rather than a snapshot. Connects to: paradigm/eventful-over-polling-implicit (events make state derivable; trajectory makes ambiguity derivable). Refs: design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix, hypothesis/concept-drift-temporal, design/antipode-five-readings.\", \"_ts\": 1778371335.489207, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/antipode-five-readings\", \"design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix\", \"hypothesis/concept-drift-temporal\", \"paradigm/eventful-over-polling-implicit\"]}, \"design/coupling-kernels-emission-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/coupling-kernels-emission-shape\", \"message\": \"REFINEMENT 2026-05-10 (Kyle): query-run and query-comparison should be 'by' upserts on deterministic content-derived ID fields (run_id, comparison_id) rather than collect-style. Semantically still one-fact-per-execution (the key is unique by construction: run_id = run_<short_spec_hash>_<ts_ms>, comparison_id = cmp_<run_a_id>_<run_b_id>_<op>), but mechanically refable through the existing entity-ref machinery without needing fact ULID exposure. Dissolves the question of whether to enhance the emit CLI to return fact IDs \\u2014 we don't need it. Ref syntax: ref=query-run:run_abc123_1700000000000. The earlier 'collect-style' framing was a false constraint; receipt-vs-state principle holds either way (each receipt is immutable, addressed by content, never updated).\", \"_ts\": 1778430491.870035, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/query-run-fact\": {\"topic\": \"design/query-run-fact\", \"message\": \"Collect-style fact, one per execution (no upsert \\u2014 every run is its own receipt with its own ULID). Fields: spec_hash (recipe-only hash of corpus_decl + embedder_decl + kernel_decl + readouts_decl), binding (corpus snapshot id, embedder version, date range \\u2014 anything that affects results but isn't recipe), embeddings_ref (explicit; absent = ephemeral run with no persisted artifacts; present = path to CachedEmbedder cache file), sigma (chosen kernel scale, run output not in cache), n_components, n_items, components (inline list of int lists, kept for cheap comparison-without-replay despite being rederivable from cached E + kernel), readout_summary (counts, top-k, not full payloads), run_id (ULID), ts. The split between recipe-hash and binding lets compare() validity become a check on (qa.spec_hash == qb.spec_hash AND bindings_compatible(qa, qb)) rather than collapsing both into hash equality. Storage discipline: store what is not reproducible from spec; reference what is.\", \"_ts\": 1778429341.641053, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/query-comparison-fact\": {\"topic\": \"design/query-comparison-fact\", \"message\": \"Collect-style fact, one per compare() invocation. Fields: op (jaccard | lineage | intersect), ref=<run_a_id>,<run_b_id> using the existing ref machinery (so the ref graph view auto-shows which comparisons reference any given run \\u2014 no new index needed), payload (op-specific structured output: jaccard yields list of (a_idx, b_idx, score); lineage yields same with prev/now framing; intersect yields list of int lists of co-clustered items), run_id (ULID), ts. Load-bearing for cluster-level salience in the recursion: cluster identity across runs is threaded by op=lineage comparisons; without these, only item-level distribution works. Comparison kind is not optional infra \\u2014 it is the precondition for cluster-level signals. Validity: comparing two runs requires qa.spec_hash == qb.spec_hash AND bindings_compatible(qa, qb); validation enforced at compare() entry, not at fact emit (the receipt records whatever was actually run).\", \"_ts\": 1778429350.361845, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/loop-found-bug-recursion\": {\"topic\": \"design/loop-found-bug-recursion\", \"message\": \"2026-05-10: first concrete demonstration that the emit-loop recursion in coupling-kernels.vertex produces findings that wouldn't have surfaced otherwise. Cascade: Run 07 (kernel-ratio-robustness) confirmed degenerately (persist_frac=1.00). Methodological reflection split the conflated question into two hypotheses. Run 08 (ratio-effect-at-fixed-sigma) confirmed strongly (persist_frac=0.17). Tracing the magnitude into core/kernel.py revealed a latent bug: find_richness_scale dropped the ratio parameter, silently using default 2.0 regardless of caller's intent. Bug had been latent because no prior run varied ratio. Bug fixed (ratio param added, threaded through Kernel.resolve). Re-run of 07 with fix produced genuine result: kernel-ratio-robustness REJECTED (persist_frac=0.17). Five loop emissions over ~10 minutes: hypothesis \\u2192 run \\u2192 run \\u2192 comparison \\u2192 refined-hypothesis \\u2192 split-into-two \\u2192 run \\u2192 comparison \\u2192 bug-discovery \\u2192 fix \\u2192 re-run \\u2192 genuine-result. The harness exposed itself through its own emission stream. Receipts captured every step including the wrong answer, the methodological observation, the bug discovery, the fix, and the genuine test. Evidence the design works at the recursion level it was meant to support: each emission becomes input to the next reasoning step. Filed in coupling-kernels vertex; surfaced as project decision because this is the first demonstration of the design's intended behavior at the loop level.\", \"_ts\": 1778433038.617291, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/session-landing-2kb-budget\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/session-landing-2kb-budget\", \"message\": \"Tuned session_landing for 2KB harness inline preview. Default zoom: NOW (window dashboard) + TOUCHED (focus-marked items only, cap 6, body 140 chars) + UNPACK (drill-down commands, 6 lines). DETAILED+ (-v) restores full HISTORY + accumulated body. UNPACK lives in the lens (not the hook) so it's always inside the inline 2KB regardless of what experiments/comms append after. Final: 1905 bytes at default, 62KB at -v. Principle: harness inline budget is a design constraint; orient surface goes inline, archive surface goes to file with drill handles inline.\", \"_ts\": 1778438383.881182, \"_n\": 1}, \"painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines\": {\"topic\": \"painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines\", \"message\": \"First-disclosure rendering delegates to existing schema headlines (topic for thinking/observation/decision, name for threads/tasks) rather than truncating message bodies. Three rendering gaps disaggregate by best-fix location: (1) session_landing TOUCHED \\u2014 lens hygiene, drop body row, render only headline; (2) reconcile --plain \\u2014 pure structural fix, sectionize groups; (3) loops read comms previews \\u2014 render-side word-boundary truncation since medium has no headline slot. No new API; net effect reduces painted's surface area (two deletions + one behavior tweak). Constraint: thread/decision names must carry verdict-substance, not slug-identity \\u2014 the fold doesn't care, the render does. Three-voice convergence (loops-claude, lens, alcove) on 2026-05-10 in comms #observations; refs thread read-path-depth-gap and alcove's 'read-path features over noticing-skills' principle.\", \"_ts\": 1778439738.450621, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/budget-as-content-shape-selector\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/budget-as-content-shape-selector\", \"message\": \"Alcove (#observations, 2026-05-10): 'Budget as content-shape selector' is the upstream framing connecting truncation-as-coupling-function to DMT-like kernel clustering. The truncation budget IS a coupling function \\u2014 short-range (titles/labels) pass through, medium-range (discriminating content) suppressed, long-range (full body) requires explicit drill-down. Same topology as DMT-like kernel producing competing clusters, just applied to information rendering instead of semantic space. Convergence shape: peer-named the upstream principle that unifies two domains I had treated as analogous. Refs: hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function, decision:painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines.\", \"_ts\": 1778458799.691941, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\"]}, \"design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\": {\"topic\": \"design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"message\": \"Deliberation-depth lens design: depth(hypothesis) = n_within_name_facts + n_incoming_query_run_refs. Two-part metric, both halves computed from existing data \\u2014 no emit-discipline change needed. Flag: status=confirmed AND depth <= 3. Verified on current coupling-kernels data: correctly flags find-richness-scale-drops-ratio (confirmed by code-reading, 0 runs) without flagging truncation hypotheses (7 runs each). Precondition gap noted: emit_hypothesis() doesn't accept refs, so hypothesis\\u2192hypothesis lineage (replication chains) is not yet structurally captured \\u2014 only via naming suffix. Future extension: add ref support to emit_hypothesis, then include hypothesis\\u2192hypothesis edges in depth metric. Lens surfaces candidates, agent verifies \\u2014 same shape as reconcile lens.\", \"_ts\": 1778458959.602339, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation/methodological-honesty-as-bug-detector\"]}, \"design/lens-resolution-strict\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"message\": \"Lens resolution now fails loudly when explicit --lens NAME or vertex lens{} decl is unresolvable in any tier (vertex-local, cwd-local, user-global, built-in). Implementation: _exit_lens_not_found() helper in main.py prints stderr message listing all 4 search tiers tried, then sys.exit(2). Applied at BOTH tier 1 (--lens flag) AND tier 2 (vertex decl) \\u2014 same fix shape, same bug shape (advisor catch: tier 2 is the same noticing-skill-gap one level deeper). Edge case dissolved: autoresearch lens is a TUI sentinel without a render function \\u2014 created loops/lenses/autoresearch.py re-exporting fold_view, making the sentinel a real lens module. 2 new tests lock the behavior, 1013 existing tests pass. Rationale: silent fallback to default view hides measurement misalignment \\u2014 same shape as alcove's recency-counter-vs-emitted-kind bug. Explicit user request gets either the requested view or a clear failure listing where to put the missing lens.\", \"_ts\": 1778459567.32799, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\", \"observation/practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\"]}, \"design/kind-validation-strict\": {\"topic\": \"design/kind-validation-strict\", \"message\": \"--kind X now validates against vertex.declared_kinds and exits 2 with helpful diagnostic + fuzzy-match suggestions when X is not declared. Implementation: _validate_kind_or_exit() helper in main.py, called at start of _run_stream / _run_fold / _run_fold_fast after vertex_path is resolved. Helper uses difflib.get_close_matches for suggestions, lists all declared kinds, names the vertex. Edge cases handled: kind=None skips validation; vertex with no declared kinds skips validation (couldn't determine); path-style kind/key drill-down validates only the kind half. Verified live: 'loops read project --kind decsion' surfaces 'Did you mean: decision, session?'; 'loops read coupling-kernels --kind decision' surfaces 'Declared kinds: hypothesis, query-comparison, query-run' (decision is a real kind but not declared by THIS vertex \\u2014 exactly the indistinguishability the fix surfaces). Third instance of measurement-fidelity discipline: same shape as lens-resolution-strict at tier 1 and tier 2. Honest naming: this is consumer-side validation of declared kinds, NOT the broader sensor-registry alcove pointed at \\u2014 that waits for concrete sensor use cases. 1015 tests pass, 2 new regression tests added.\", \"_ts\": 1778460467.866273, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\"]}, \"finding/truncation-cliff-content-structural\": {\"topic\": \"finding/truncation-cliff-content-structural\", \"message\": \"Truncation cliff is content-structural, not instrument-artifact. Three independent confirmations at depth=9 each (truncation-as-coupling-function, truncation-effect-at-fixed-sigma, truncation-cliff-e5-replication). E5 replication (run 13, 7 query-runs, 6 comparisons) produces cliff_amplitude=0.48 monotonic, vs MiniLM (run 09) 0.44 \\u2014 same magnitude, same location (cliff between B=560 and B=280). The cliff is a property of the corpus content distribution, not of the embedder's representational geometry. Two embedders with very different geometric scales (MiniLM \\u03c3~0.2-0.3 vs E5 \\u03c3~0.02-0.03) produce convergent cliff topology. Concrete claim: discriminating content for project facts lives in chars 281-560 of message bodies \\u2014 that range is what disappears at the cliff. Read-path-depth-gap principle now has cross-embedder support. budget-as-content-shape-selector (alcove framing) is on solid empirical footing.\", \"_ts\": 1778461193.997824, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/budget-as-content-shape-selector\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"hypothesis:truncation-cliff-e5-replication\", \"hypothesis:truncation-effect-at-fixed-sigma\"]}, \"finding/low-budget-bounce-is-regime-shift\": {\"topic\": \"finding/low-budget-bounce-is-regime-shift\", \"message\": \"Bounce mechanism resolved from existing run-13 receipts (no new run needed \\u2014 components were emitted with each query-run, dissolution-default move). At very low budgets, items in non-trivial clusters: B=140 has 202 items in 19 clusters, B=95 drops to 140 items in 13 clusters (bottom of bounce), B=60 recovers to 194 items in 16 clusters. CRITICAL: 57 items at B=60 are NOT in B=140 (~30% turnover); 65 items at B=140 are NOT in B=60. Jaccard B=140 vs B=60 = 0.53. The bounce is NOT survivor preservation (which would produce subset relationship). It is REGIME SHIFT \\u2014 at <=95 chars, different items organize into clusters than at 140 chars, likely on title/kind/namespace prefix patterns rather than content semantics. Distinguishable from what title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors tested (which was: do CLIFF-SURVIVOR clusters at the medium-budget regime have higher title-preservation? Rejected). This is a different question: at the BOTTOM-budget regime, does a NEW cluster topology emerge from title-only content? Evidence says yes. Implication for budget-as-content-shape-selector (alcove framing): the coupling-function topology has at least THREE regimes \\u2014 high-budget content-semantic clustering, cliff-zone disagregation, low-budget title-driven re-clustering. Not a simple monotonic curve. Pulls a future hypothesis: cluster-identity-at-low-budgets-is-prefix-driven \\u2014 would predict that surviving B=60 clusters share kind/namespace prefix more than B=140 clusters.\", \"_ts\": 1778461339.231761, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/budget-as-content-shape-selector\", \"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-cliff-e5-replication\", \"observation/finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\"]}, \"design/lens-kind-contract-as-enforcement\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-kind-contract-as-enforcement\", \"message\": \"Verdict: lenses must declare the kinds they read (READS_KINDS module attribute); lens resolver validates declared reads against vertex declaration at resolution time; mismatch fails loudly, not silently. Designed 2026-05-10 as forward application of paradigm/outreach-via-enforcement-not-organization. Evidence: 5+ lenses currently hardcode kind strings (deliberation_depth: 'hypothesis'; reconcile: 'decision'; autoresearch: 'config', 'experiment'; readiness: 'decision'). Each silently returns empty if the vertex doesn't declare the kind \\u2014 Alcove's bug class (sensor queries 'reflection', emitter writes 'thinking', no error fires). Shape enforced: every static-kind sensor declares its reads; every vertex declares what it accepts; cross-validation at lens load time. Fail-cases by category \\u2014 (a) drift: rename kind on one side, other side errors immediately (motivating instance, Alcove's bug); (b) orphan sensor: lens declares kind no vertex declares \\u2014 load error, lens unusable; (c) abandoned kind: vertex declares kind no lens reads \\u2014 warning, candidate for removal; (d) typo at lens introduction: misspelled kind name fails at first run rather than 'why isn't this working'. Three of four fail-cases (b, c, d) are outreach candidates \\u2014 modes the motivating bug class didn't articulate. API choice: module-level READS_KINDS attribute (validated by resolver) over runtime vertex.declared_kinds() accessor. Rationale: B fails at lens load before render runs (cannot silently fail under stress); A only fails if sensor remembers to check (relies on programmer vigilance, the exact failure mode we're trying to remove). Opt-out: dynamic queries (e.g. autoresearch_prompt.py where kind is a kwarg) declare READS_KINDS = '*'; contract becomes advisory, drift not caught for that lens by design. Limitation: enforces lens consumers only; hooks, CLI ad-hoc queries, drift detectors still hardcode. Generalization to all-sensors deferred \\u2014 lenses are highest-density structured consumers; covering them is high-leverage; broader registry comes later if patterns demand it (resist premature substrate). Implementation cost: ~200 lines (lens_resolver.py validation + READS_KINDS on 5 existing lenses + tests). Test for the implementation: after landing, walk all lenses, count READS_KINDS coverage; intentionally rename a vertex-declared kind, verify lens loads fail with kind-mismatch error citing both sides. Verdict against the principle: this IS an enforcing instrument with at least four fail-modes only one of which motivated it \\u2014 outreach candidate by construction.\", \"_ts\": 1778463099.144212, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/outreach-via-enforcement-not-organization\"]}, \"design/vouch-builds-on-loops-libs\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-builds-on-loops-libs\", \"message\": \"Decision: Vouch service builds on loops' libs directly (atoms/engine/store), not as parallel implementation. Evidence: dissolution test passes \\u2014 every primitive the trust-substrate room derived (append-only ledger, observer/ts/payload envelope, vertex as query surface, ticks for lifecycle, cascade for org-level rollups, lens-kind contracts) already exists in libs. Implication: vouch inherits the entire exploration surface (lenses, fold, reconcile, ticks) for free the moment it emits its first fact; loops gets its first real consumer of engine.Peer/engine.Grant as proving ground. The forcing function is mutual: vouch surfaces signing/federation/authn-at-write-time gaps; loops absorbs them into libs at N=2 or carves clean seams where the dissolution doesn't hold.\", \"_ts\": 1778649521.649947, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/loops-as-external-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-as-external-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision: Loops' libs (atoms, engine, store) are now treated as external substrate consumed across repo boundaries \\u2014 not just internal monorepo infrastructure. Evidence: Vouch is the first cross-repo consumer of atoms/engine/store; painted doesn't count (it's loops' rendering primitive, part of loops' own substrate, not a consumer of it). Implication: loops needs a public-vs-internal API discipline it hasn't had to enforce yet. Public surface stays stable; internal can churn. Carving mechanism (public/ vs internal/ subpackages per lib, vs all-public-with-versioning) deferred to thread libs-public-internal-boundary, informed by vouch's first wave of actual imports rather than predicted.\", \"_ts\": 1778649528.06764, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vocabulary-as-architecture-fractal-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"design/vocabulary-as-architecture-fractal-pattern\", \"message\": \"Decision: Vocabulary-as-architecture is a fractal pattern \\u2014 service capability catalogs (consumption + emission halves) at the service-graph boundary and lens READS_KINDS / vertex EMITS_KINDS at the lens-vertex boundary are instances of the same discipline applied at different layers. Evidence: trust-substrate room (cairn/carom/claude-commission) independently derived service catalogs as published trust-posture artifacts while loops had just landed lens-kind-contract-as-enforcement at the read-path layer. N=2 convergence on the same pattern at different layers is structural, not coincidence. Implication: published-artifact contracts at every seam where reads consume kinds, recursively all the way in. Future engineers reading either layer pick up the other for free. Cross-references trust-substrate foundational ADR (commission repo, drafting).\", \"_ts\": 1778649533.835369, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/cqrs-as-per-consumer-property\": {\"topic\": \"design/cqrs-as-per-consumer-property\", \"message\": \"Decision: Loops' Fact/Tick/Cascade architecture makes CQRS a per-consumer property, not a temporal migration phase. Evidence: any consumer of a loops vertex can choose direct-query (Store reads) or event-sourced projection (tick-stream subscription) per their own needs, without coordination. Trust-substrate room initially framed A\\u2192C as a future migration; the architecture dissolves the fork. Implication: the centralized-now-event-sourced-later trajectory commonly framed as 'when forced' is not a fork at all \\u2014 it was always per-consumer preference made first-class by the underlying substrate. Foundational claim about loops worth surfacing alongside the scope lattice and trust-topology essay as a third grounding layer for the trust-substrate ADR set.\", \"_ts\": 1778649540.204708, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/wire-not-library-at-trust-boundary-only\": {\"topic\": \"design/wire-not-library-at-trust-boundary-only\", \"message\": \"Decision: The wire-not-library rule applies at cross-org / cross-language trust boundaries; it does NOT apply to intra-homelab Python services. Evidence: vouch builds on atoms/engine/store directly while still exposing language-agnostic JSON wire envelopes to Go/Rust consumers. The two axes are orthogonal \\u2014 conflating them implies unnecessary reimplementation of the substrate by every Python service. Origin: I posted the wire-not-library framing to #trust-substrate (msg 1518) without this disambiguation, conflating cross-boundary protocol commitment with cross-repo implementation sharing. Implication: foundational ADR must be explicit so a future reader doesn't conclude wire-not-library means reimplement atoms in vouch. Cross-language consumers see the JSON envelope; Python consumers import the libs that produce it.\", \"_ts\": 1778649546.04028, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"message\": \"Decision: Reframe of vouch ADR's loops-side framing. Vouch is not the proving ground for engine.Peer/Grant; it is the forcing function that surfaces what loops must ship FIRST. observer-assignment weakness (Kyle, 2026-05-13) is why Peer/Grant haven't been picked up \\u2014 the trust-root gap is structural, not 'awaiting first consumer.' Implication: libs/sign is precondition, not N=2 deferral. N=2 promotion assumes N=1 works; observer trust-root means N=0. Loops ships substrate (ledger, scope lattice, signing-backed observer assignment, Peer/Grant recast) BEFORE vouch builds on top. Vouch is first consumer of a loops-shipped substrate, not the proving site for loops primitives.\", \"_ts\": 1778680045.191967, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/wire-not-library-at-trust-boundary-only\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\", \"thread:trust-substrate-adr-cross-reference\"]}, \"design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"message\": \"Decision (refines vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground): three-layer separation. (1) CONTRACT: loops ships Peer/Grant verification-hook + vertex acceptance policy now \\u2014 small, additive, permissive default keeps solo work unchanged. This is precondition. (2) IMPLEMENTATION: vouch builds signing internally inside its vertex policy. (3) MECHANISM LOCATION: libs/sign extracts at N=2 (genuinely deferrable). Corrects prior 'libs/sign is precondition' \\u2014 that conflated contract and implementation. The verification axis is what's missing from Peer/Grant; closing it operationally is what 'vouch as forcing function' means concretely. Open: shape of verification context on Peer; declarative-vs-programmatic vertex policy; whether Grants are facts (engine model) or ledger entries (vouch model).\", \"_ts\": 1778680791.110237, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"decision:design/wire-not-library-at-trust-boundary-only\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/peer-consolidation-grant-novel\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-consolidation-grant-novel\", \"message\": \"Decision (from cross-codebase Explore reports): adopting Peer(name, iss) in loops engine is CONSOLIDATION, not addition \\u2014 every consumer already has identity-of-some-shape with an iss-like axis. Comms (name, org), pile (agent, JWT-iss), siftd (sub, OIDC-iss), sqlmerge (nothing). Shipping Peer dissolves four fragmented shapes into one. Grant is genuinely NOVEL \\u2014 no consumer has chain-of-attestation-with-capability today. Vouch brings it into existence; pile (via Commission dual-issuer), comms (via invite chains), sqlmerge (greenfield) are positioned to adopt. Engine ships: Peer, kind=grant envelope, VertexPolicy interface, chain_walk + grants_for helpers. Engine does NOT ship: verification impl (vouch internal, libs/sign at N=2), slice/Fidelity (sqlmerge/siftd), scope-intersection (vouch), transport auth (per-consumer), org/namespace semantics (per-consumer). N=2 for libs/sign likely SOONER than assumed \\u2014 pile already does JWT validation; comms does its own. Reframes vouch ADR's 'growing the surface' \\u2014 half the growth is consolidation, half is genuine novelty.\", \"_ts\": 1778683788.726703, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"hypothesis:peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"message\": \"Decision (reframe per Kyle 2026-05-13): loops is the substrate these consumers (sqlmerge, comms, pile, vouch, siftd) are approximating, not a host that accommodates them. The work is completing the substrate so they can stop approximating. Implications: (1) iss is trust-domain BOUNDARY, not Peer metadata \\u2014 the policy join point where same-iss=intra-domain, cross-iss=federation, unknown-iss=rejected; (2) transport is SUBSTRATE \\u2014 loops ships the contract (authenticated tick-stream + grant-bound slicing), consumers ship the wire (SSH, HTTP, MCP, etc.); (3) .vertex/KDL is 80%-case convenience, NOT ceiling \\u2014 extensibility floor stays at Python (VertexPolicy classes, Transport implementations), KDL is one elevation above. Stops migration-shaped thinking; the consumers are loops-shapes at varying fidelity. iss stays opaque-string at data layer; structure goes into VertexPolicy machinery (resolver, trust-assessor, cross-iss chain handling). Peer/Grant were aspirational; this is the concretization.\", \"_ts\": 1778684559.246948, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-consolidation-grant-novel\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"hypothesis:peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"message\": \"Decision (from Explore findings 2026-05-13): engine.Peer/Grant exist in libs/engine/src/engine/peer.py with shape Peer(name, horizon, potential) + Grant(horizon, potential) + grant/restrict/delegate operations + 20 passing tests. horizon=read-constraint, potential=emit-constraint, both frozenset[str] of kinds. This IS the generic substrate version of vouch's scope and sqlmerge's slice \\u2014 per-vertex specializations live in payload, not in engine. Concrete additions are SMALLER than greenfield framing: (1) add iss to Peer, (2) lift Grant from in-process object to kind=grant Fact with envelope+payload, (3) parent_ref chain semantics, (4) extract receive-gate to VertexPolicy interface, (5) chain_walk + grants_for helpers. The in-process Grant becomes the payload of kind=grant Facts; existing delegate() becomes 'emit Fact with parent_ref'; vertex.receive gate logic moves into VertexPolicy.verify_emission. Solo work unchanged (permissive default policy preserves current behavior). The work is EXTEND not BUILD.\", \"_ts\": 1778684789.937229, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-consolidation-grant-novel\", \"hypothesis:peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision (recalibrated after Kyle pushback 2026-05-13): libs/sign builds NOW, scoped as utility library (JWT/JWKS/key conventions for homelab) not substrate primitive (Fact-signing). Contents: jwt.mint/validate, jwks.publish/resolve, keys.KeyStore + RSA gen + kid derivation, iss.dispatch. ~160 lines of glue around pyjwt + cryptography, sourced from commission Phase 1. Consumers TODAY: pile (validates Commission JWTs, gaining dual-issuer), vouch (mint + publish + keys). Consumers KNOWN-COMING: comms (Authentik migration ahead), sqlmerge (peer auth at substrate boundary). N=2 active for validation, N=3 visible. Fact-signing-as-substrate-primitive STAYS deferred (vouch is N=1 for that). Calibration miss earlier: conflated 'libs/sign as substrate' (N=1 over-reach) with 'libs/sign as utility' (N=2 active). Different scope, different bar. Substrate-primitive scope needs divergent constraints; utility-library scope needs shared usage. Vouch becomes: vouch vertex (loops substrate) + libs/sign consumption (homelab crypto glue) + Authentik forward-auth + Fellow UI. Commission Phase 1 splits: keys/jwt_mint/wellknown move to libs/sign; db becomes vertex driver; api/ui stay vouch-internal.\", \"_ts\": 1778689109.525348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"observation:practice/substrate-overreach-three-instances\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"message\": \"Decision (recovered from #trust-substrate work 01KRGXR58W67, May 12-13): loops is a PROTOCOL with a canonical Python implementation, not a framework. Vouch, comms, pile are applications of the protocol, not applications built with loops. Sharper layer than substrate-not-host (same direction, deeper claim). Implications: (1) Substrate decisions (Peer.iss, VertexPolicy, chain-walk, programmatic construction) are PROTOCOL-LEVEL commitments \\u2014 propagate to every implementation. (2) libs/sign is IMPLEMENTATION-LEVEL \\u2014 gruel-network's Python crypto choices, not part of protocol; peer homelabs could implement differently. (3) Applications (vouch) are local to one service. Three-tier evolution: protocol slow + deliberate, implementation local-per-language, application local-per-service. The #trust-substrate room independently derived the same primitive set (observer/timestamp/payload + scope-lattice + event-sourced projections) WITHOUT loops in the room \\u2014 strongest external validation: alcove + claude-commission recognized loops Fact/Tick/Cascade as the same protocol they were deriving from first principles.\", \"_ts\": 1778691702.962402, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\", \"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"observation:convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\"]}, \"design/protocol-framing-scope-dependent\": {\"topic\": \"design/protocol-framing-scope-dependent\", \"message\": \"Decision (from alcove sanity-check 2026-05-13): protocol-not-framework framing is scope-dependent, not universal. Within Python homelab, consumers (vouch, pile, comms, sqlmerge) are LIBRARY IMPORTERS of loops (atoms.Fact, engine.Vertex, Peer, Grant). The protocol framing applies at the CROSS-LANGUAGE boundary (Go services, peer homelabs implementing via JSON over wire). Both axes orthogonal; both true. Earlier emission design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework is correct in claim but I extended it operationally to 'vouch is application not library consumer' which conflated the axes. Practical consequence for bfc.lol rebuild: all consumers are Python library importers in this scope. Cross-language federation is separate design axis deferred until concrete cross-language consumer surfaces (peer homelab in different stack).\", \"_ts\": 1778692630.35633, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/wire-not-library-at-trust-boundary-only\"]}, \"design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"message\": \"Decision (from alcove sanity-check 2026-05-13): Peer.iss extension (and the wider substrate-surface list: VertexPolicy interface, chain-walk, programmatic construction) is PROPOSED-BY-VOUCH-USAGE, not pre-committed. The #trust-substrate resolution explicitly deferred Peer/Grant recast until vouch exercises them. Tonight's design conversation IS that exercise. Whatever friction surfaces in vouch implementation is the data for the recast. Earlier emissions treated Peer.iss as committed extension; correct framing is: ship vouch using current engine.Peer/Grant where possible, record what's awkward, recast based on what surfaces. Plan accordingly: substrate extensions are derived-from-exercise, not a-priori.\", \"_ts\": 1778692634.040315, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"decision:design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"design/documentation-plan-update-not-supersede\": {\"topic\": \"design/documentation-plan-update-not-supersede\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): documentation plan for bfc.lol rebuild design refinements. (1) UPDATE vouch ADR-0001 (still Proposed state) with: vouch-as-forcing-function framing, libs/sign as utility-scope ship-alongside, Peer.iss as vouch-derived not pre-committed, Grant-as-Fact close-vs-document as open question, drop trust-topology lattice citation. (2) UPDATE IDENTITY.md with Peer-as-convenience-bundle history + iss axis + verification-at-boundaries + cross-collaboration semantics. (3) WRITE loops ADR-0004 on scope lattice math (the thing vouch ADR cites trust-topology for, which trust-topology doesn't contain) \\u2014 lives loops-side as operational primitive. (4) DEFER vouch ADR-0002 (catalogs) and 0003 (migration) until concrete shape surfaces (same forcing-function discipline). (5) STRANGE-LOOPS.md protocol-not-framework addition later, not blocking. Project store remains the primary record (practice-residue trace); high-level docs are consolidated views. Don't write separate 'where we landed tonight' doc \\u2014 would be documentation-as-thinkism.\", \"_ts\": 1778693556.748845, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\", \"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"decision:design/protocol-framing-scope-dependent\", \"thread:grant-as-fact-close-or-document\", \"thread:lattice-math-needs-writing\"]}, \"design/documentation-plan-finalized\": {\"topic\": \"design/documentation-plan-finalized\", \"message\": \"Decision finalized 2026-05-13: documentation plan for bfc.lol rebuild design refinements. (1) UPDATE vouch ADR-0001 (Proposed) with refinements. (2) UPDATE loops IDENTITY.md with Peer-as-convenience-bundle history, iss axis, verification-at-boundaries, cross-collaboration semantics. (3) WRITE loops ADR-0004 on scope lattice math (operational). (4) WRITE essay in loops-claude voice as complement to alcove's trust-topology \\u2014 shareable to alcove later as our response/addendum. Distinct from ADR-0004: ADR is operational standard; essay is prose articulation of why the math has its shape, what it dissolves, what it leaves open. Drawing on accumulated voice context (dissolution discipline, substrate-feels-universal trap, four-over-reach as shape-unclarity-evidence, participatory-not-authenticative recovery, consumer-more-substrate-aligned irony). (5) UPDATE loops ARCHITECTURE.md with protocol-not-framework in GENERAL FORM \\u2014 no homelab/Python scoping. Loops IS a protocol; scope-dependent application (library vs wire) is operational not structural. Defers: vouch ADR-0002 catalogs, 0003 migration (forcing-function discipline applies). STRANGE-LOOPS.md updates if needed, not blocking. Project store remains primary record; high-level docs are consolidated views; ADR-0004 + essay are paired operational+voice artifacts.\", \"_ts\": 1778693945.232162, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/documentation-plan-update-not-supersede\", \"decision:design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"decision:design/protocol-framing-scope-dependent\", \"thread:grant-as-fact-close-or-document\", \"thread:lattice-math-needs-writing\"]}, \"design/vouch-rebuild-fresh-repo\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-rebuild-fresh-repo\", \"message\": \"Decision 2026-05-13: vouch rebuilds from scratch in fresh ~/Code/vouch repo, not in-place refactor of ~/Code/commission. Three deep changes (storage: mutable table\\u2192append-only vertex; conceptual: state-machine\\u2192fact-stream-with-projections; naming: commission\\u2192vouch) make refactor-in-place fragile and confusing. Carry forward deliberately: JWT claim shape (RFC 8693 act), Authentik forward-auth (X-authentik-* headers), UI templates with ceremony framing, keystore management approach, activation flow (two-phase exchange-token), FastMCP read-only tools surface. What's new: vouch vertex as source of truth, VouchPolicy implementing loops VertexPolicy, libs/sign consumption, loops.libs.store storage, chain-walking for multi-hop. Commission stays at ~/Code/commission as Phase-1-deployed-historical-reference until cutover. ADRs move to ~/Code/vouch/docs/decisions/. commission/README.md gets pointer to vouch as active design home. Mirrors deployment: commission.bfc.lol serves until vouch.bfc.lol cutover. ADR-0003 migration gets written during rebuild rather than deferred.\", \"_ts\": 1778694150.218455, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/documentation-plan-finalized\", \"decision:design/peer-iss-as-proposal-not-commitment\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\"]}, \"design/libs-sign-carve-loops-side\": {\"topic\": \"design/libs-sign-carve-loops-side\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): loops-claude takes the first cut on libs/sign carve, not via a vouch-shaped PR. Rationale: (1) public/internal API discipline is loops-side per design/loops-as-external-substrate \\u2014 carving via one consumer's PR couples conventions to that consumer when N=2 today (vouch+pile, comms third) wants the boundary to fit all three; (2) libs-public-internal-boundary is an open loops thread that the carve forces to crystallize, cleaner landed together than retrofitted; (3) ADR-0001 scopes libs/sign as utility-library \\u2014 public surface scoped to actual import sites, not union of internal module exposure. Blocked on scrivener confirming source path (likely ~/Code/commission/) and near-final import-site sketch.\", \"_ts\": 1778697525.537384, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\", \"decision:design/loops-as-external-substrate\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"workflow/vouch-impl-substrate-side-mode\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/vouch-impl-substrate-side-mode\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): session mode for vouch implementation phase confirmed as substrate-side coherence. scrivener does vouch implementation from ~/Code/vouch/; loops-claude stays in loops monorepo, surfaces engine.Peer/Grant/VertexPolicy substrate when scrivener's implementation pulls. Coord via #vouch-impl channel. The forcing-function discipline (libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test): substrate refinements emerge from vouch's actual implementation friction, not pre-committed in ADRs. friction \\u2192 thread on loops project store \\u2192 loops-side recast decision \\u2192 scrivener consumes new shape. Three opening questions from scrivener answered (libs/sign carve, Peer/Grant approach, ADR-0003 kind_subtype reading).\", \"_ts\": 1778697529.676776, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"practice:libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"design/libs-public-internal-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"design/libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13, settled with scrivener): convention for the public/internal API boundary in loops/libs/*. (1) Public API = what each lib's __init__.py exports via explicit __all__. Submodules without leading underscore (e.g. sign.jwt, sign.keys, sign.jwks) are public; underscore-prefixed modules (_compat.py, _serialization.py) are internal and have no stability contract. (2) Each lib's CLAUDE.md documents its public surface and stability posture. (3) For utility libs (libs/sign), breaking changes ship in a tagged loops release; each consumer bumps their pyproject.toml pin when ready \\u2014 cutover is sequenced via coordinated upgrade, not atomic multi-repo commits. (4) This is utility-lib stability posture; protocol primitives (atoms.Fact, engine.Peer/Grant) have a stricter contract not covered by this decision. Convention propagates to future libs/* carves.\", \"_ts\": 1778698189.794823, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-external-substrate\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\"]}, \"design/libs-sign-public-surface\": {\"topic\": \"design/libs-sign-public-surface\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13, settled with scrivener via #vouch-impl): public API shape for loops/libs/sign. Three modules. (1) sign.keys: KeyStore class, load_or_generate(signing_key_dir)->KeyStore, PublicKey dataclass (frozen) carrying (kid, alg, key). (2) sign.jwt: mint(*, keystore, issuer, claims:dict, ttl_seconds, jti=None)->(token, jti) \\u2014 library injects iss/iat/exp/jti; caller builds claims dict (sub/act/scope/aud/etc) per their domain. verify(token, *, public_keys:Sequence[PublicKey], issuer, audience)->dict \\u2014 reads kid from JWT header, looks up in public_keys, raises on no-match or missing-kid (kidless tokens are an attack surface). (3) sign.jwks: build_document(keystore)->dict and build_openid_configuration(issuer, *, jwks_uri, **extra)->dict \\u2014 both framework-free; consumers write their own HTTP handlers. parse(jwks_dict)->list[PublicKey] for remote-verify path. Verification is one primitive + two normalizers (keystore.public_keys() | jwks.parse) \\u2014 key-source decision explicit at call site, cache/refresh policy stays with consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1778698195.544632, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"decision:design/libs-sign-carve-loops-side\", \"decision:design/libs-sign-now-as-utility-not-substrate\"]}, \"implementation/libs-sign-merged\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/libs-sign-merged\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): libs/sign carved and merged to main at ea517f19a2016294fdd25f68e13bb8e6340fb87b. 12 files, 788 insertions, 21 tests passing. Public API matches design/libs-sign-public-surface exactly (claims-dict mint, public_keys-arg verify, framework-free jwks builders). Establishes the libs/* public/internal boundary convention as load-bearing for future carves. Cross-adapter review pipeline (claude plan+impl, codex/gpt-5.5/low review on fresh session) caught two Important findings on first pass: root pyproject runtime deps for strange-loops wheel consumers (vouch's path), and jwks.parse() alg whitelist (RS256\\u2192HS256 alg-confusion guard). Both fixed pre-merge. scrivener can pin the SHA from vouch's pyproject and proceed with issue_vouch wiring.\", \"_ts\": 1778700021.216472, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"decision:design/libs-sign-carve-loops-side\", \"decision:design/libs-sign-public-surface\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\": {\"topic\": \"engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): the Jan 27-30 dissolution that split bundled Peer into Observer-on-Fact + Grant-at-Vertex + convenience-Peer is validated as right-shaped by vouch \\u2014 first real consumer of engine.Peer/Grant. Evidence from explore/peer-grant subtask (~/Code/vouch commit d95d36a, friction doc Obs 5): vouch needs grant_of(peer) for cross-vouch scope comparison; Grant is exactly the policy half stripped of identity that vouch's payload needs (frozen, hashable, set-shaped, value-equal); Peer/Grant separation matches ADR-0001's stance that scope is per-vouch not per-agent. Implication: any future engine recast that proposes re-fusing Peer and Grant must justify against this consumer's validated benefit. This is the loops-side positive anchor \\u2014 architectural bet paid off, recorded so future-me (or whoever's tempted to re-fuse) reads the validation before tempting backsliding.\", \"_ts\": 1778702738.305478, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"thread:substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\"]}, \"implementation/session-2026-05-13-vouch-impl-handoff-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/session-2026-05-13-vouch-impl-handoff-shipped\", \"message\": \"Decision arc (2026-05-13 evening session): vouch implementation handoff phase opened cleanly. (1) libs/sign carved as first external-substrate lib, merged at ea517f1 (+ typing_extensions transitive fix at 9657f69) \\u2014 established public/internal boundary convention as load-bearing for future libs/* carves. (2) Cross-adapter review pipeline (claude/opus plan+impl, codex/gpt-5.5/low fresh-session review via subtask) used for first time, caught 2 real Important findings before merge that same-session continue would have missed. (3) scrivener (vouch impl peer) ran explore/peer-grant subtask exercising engine.Peer/Grant against vouch's voucher/holder/scope vocabulary \\u2014 friction surfaced structurally not lexically (Peer is per-agent, vouch is per-assertion \\u2192 voucher has no slot on Peer), dissolved cleanly via 'consumer wraps, walk the Fact ledger.' (4) Substrate-feels-universal trap did NOT fire during first-real-consumer pressure \\u2014 discipline held. (5) engine.peer docstring nudged at 9f58e4c documenting why chain ancestry isn't reachable from a leaf Peer. Position closing: ADR-0001's forcing-function bet validated; libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test test passed (vouch produced friction in exactly the shape the bet predicted).\", \"_ts\": 1778703493.807552, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:implementation/libs-sign-merged\", \"observation:practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\", \"observation:practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\", \"thread:substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\"]}, \"design/vouch-write-path-e2e-landed\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-write-path-e2e-landed\", \"body\": \"vouch issue_vouch e2e landed (vouch cf28a24): engine.delegate\\u2192atoms.Fact\\u2192SqliteStore\\u2192sign.mint\\u2192JWKS round-trip, 13 tests, 7 friction observations in vouch/docs/friction/issue-vouch-write-path.md. Single-axis scope (potential only) for MVP; horizon-axis decision still open per peer-grant-exercise \\u00a76. VouchPolicy still latent. Next candidates: rescission write-path, catalog cross-check, or service shell.\", \"_ts\": 1778705686.930514, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"message\": \"Verdict: vouch rescission is Fact-level, not a lattice operation. Substrate stays monotone. Evidence: libs/engine/src/engine/peer.py is monotone by construction \\u2014 restrict_grant intersects, expand_grant only widens within parent bounds, delegate narrows. Grant.minus() would be the first non-monotone op and break the issuance-chain invariant. Framing: same shape as write-receipt-vs-temporal-query (#agent-party 04-29) and fold-view-vs-fact-history (alcove convergence 05-10). Issuance and rescission are writes (Facts); active scope at time t is a fold-derived temporal query, racy with next writer by definition. ADR-0001 already commits to temporal derivation via TTL \\u2014 rescission is event-driven generalization of TTL decay. Discriminating question (substrate-overreach filter): no second consumer for Grant.minus today at issuance path \\u2014 rescission targets prior issuance, doesn't carve future one. Verification is replay, not lattice op. N=1, not N=2. Operational discipline: 'treat rescission as event-stream fold, not Grant \\u2216 Grant' lands as a VouchPolicy discipline (the substrate-doesn't-enforce list), alongside scrivener's earlier four. Tradeoff honestly: verifiers can't validate JWT in isolation, need replay over rescission stream \\u2014 but TTL imposes the same cost (need a clock), so substrate pays nothing new. Surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl by scrivener post-issue_vouch-e2e; reply at message 1600.\", \"_ts\": 1778705898.150405, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-write-path-e2e-landed\", \"decision:paradigm/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-friction-from-write-path\"]}, \"design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"message\": \"Verdict: vouch emission catalog should enumerate ALL payload keys; jti belongs in catalog (resolves scrivener's d379f76 catalog cross-check). The structural-vs-semantic cleavage IS real in loops \\u2014 but it lives at the Fact/payload boundary (kind/ts/payload/observer/origin are substrate-universal Fact fields), not within payload. Payload is by construction the domain side; the fold operates on it, lenses interpret it, there is no infrastructure-in-payload-but-not-really-payload tier in loops. Introducing one in vouch's catalog would create a substrate-shape distinction asymmetric with the rest of loops \\u2014 cleavage-of-convenience. Substrate-overreach test on the alternative ('move jti to Fact-level'): N=1, only vouch has JWT-Fact correlation ids, this is the substrate-feels-universal trap. Refs already handle cross-Fact correlation: future rescission Facts can ref the vouch via ref=vouch:<jti> with jti as fold key. Adjacent: ADR-0002's emission catalog is vouch's instance of the kinds-i-produce registry shape (alcove's 05-10 framing). 'catalog-or-it-doesn't-count' discipline is structurally the same shape as 'drift-detector asks what kinds emit that I'm not measuring.' Scrivener's payload_shape-keys-==-emitted-payload-keys check is the cross-validation step that shape needs. Surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl post-exercise-2; reply at message 1602.\", \"_ts\": 1778706171.342625, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-write-path-e2e-landed\", \"decision:paradigm/dissolution-test\"]}, \"design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"message\": \"Decision (2026-05-13): three substantive PLAN.md reads for vouch service-shell exercise 3, plus alignment on scrivener's refinements. (1) Forward-auth IdP shape: config-driven header names + group-capabilities-as-dict-in-config, NO ForwardAuthAdapter Protocol. Authentik-specific identifiers rename to forward-auth-generic at call sites. Protocol earns its keep only when non-header-based IdP path lands (mTLS, SAML-direct); IdP-swap-via-different-reverse-proxy is string substitution, not structural variation. Substrate-feels-universal trap variant: 'vouch fronts an IdP, so abstract over IdPs' \\u2014 premature at N=1. (2) RFC 7807 error envelope: adopt with corrected rationale \\u2014 drop OAuth-ecosystem-adjacency (vouch is not OAuth server), keep 'stable IETF standard, boring default, light footprint, Litestar-supported, sets de-facto homelab convention.' Loops has no existing service-layer error convention (confirmed via rg) \\u2014 vouch sets the convention. type field: urn:vouch:error:<slug> or null with title-as-discriminator. (3) Catalog aggregator GET /api/v1/catalog: SHIP, don't defer. 5-line composition of existing three sub-routes; aggregator IS the catalog per ADR-0002 singular; discovery affordance for operators. Sub-routes remain for filtered automation. (4) Q8 import-presence test for discipline (b) confirmed: ast-based check that policy.py/app.py don't import grant/expand_grant is portable testable form. (5) Q1 success-response shape rationale: plain {token, jti, exp} dissolves OAuth alternatives \\u2014 no introspection (RFC 7662 not implemented), no token-type differentiation (Bearer-only), 1:1 catalog payload_shape match, jti at HTTP layer enables client correlation without JWT parse, exp matches Fact ts convention. (6) Peer.from_anchor() factory: agree with worker's defer (N=1 constructor site). But friction observation is durable \\u2014 fifth substrate-doesn't-enforce discipline: 'construct Peer only from trusted provenance; never from untrusted request body without anchor lookup first.' Worth banking in vouch friction-doc as obs-8 even though factory is deferred. The discipline is the durable artifact; the factory is one implementation that earns at N=2. Sharpest insight cross-validation: adversarial-vs-legitimate Peer construction is new ground beyond peer-grant-exercise \\u00a72 \\u2014 the seam is provenance-tagged construction. Peer dataclass doesn't carry provenance (intentional: Peer is policy/identity/capability, not lineage); provenance lives on the Fact-chain. Reply at message 1604.\", \"_ts\": 1778707076.796837, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\"]}, \"paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\", \"message\": \"Substrate framing surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl during rescission write-path design (scrivener msg 1613). Verdict: write operations partition by what their authorization is checking. Capability-projecting writes bind new capability into a chain; auth is forward-looking (does actor currently have authority?); requires checking current state. Identity-asserting writes assert pre-existing relation in chain; auth is backward-looking (was actor the one who established the relation?); requires checking historical state. Issuance is canonical capability-projecting (resolve_voucher projects current group-membership to capability). Rescission is canonical identity-asserting ('I was the voucher of V' is a fact about Fact-ancestry). Coupling rescission auth to current capability would mean a Fellow whose anchor was revoked loses ability to rescind their own prior vouches \\u2014 their issuances become irrevocable in their absence, worst failure mode for a system that exists to enable revocation. Generalization: any system distinguishing 'grant' from 'revoke-my-grant' has this shape (permission systems, trust networks, claim issuance/withdrawal, attestation/recantation). Principle: if the operation asserts a historical relation, identity-anchor it; if it projects new capability, capability-anchor it. Operational discriminator at design time: 'does this write require knowing current state of X to authorize, or knowing past state of X?' That question partitions the operation. Adjacent to write-receipt-vs-temporal-query (same temporal axis applied to auth shape rather than return shape). Reply at message 1614.\", \"_ts\": 1778716106.916496, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:paradigm/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\", \"message\": \"Substrate framing surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl (scrivener msg 1613, vouch ADR-0001 revision residue). Verdict: kind_subtype is a structural-discriminator-within-a-kind. If the discriminator changes payload shape, auth shape, or write semantics, the operations want to be peer kinds, not subtypes. Vouch's original ADR-0001 declared kind_subtype: issued | rescinded | synthesized within kind=vouch \\u2014 lumped operations that have (a) different payload shapes (issuance has scope/audience/exp; rescission has target_jti+reason), (b) different auth shapes (capability-projecting vs identity-asserting per paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes), (c) different write semantics (binds new capability vs asserts pre-existing relation). Three signals; the peer-kind redesign is the right resolution. Operational discriminator: when proposing kind_subtype, ask 'do the subtypes share payload shape, auth shape, and write semantics? If any differs significantly, they want peer kinds.' Tautological-subtype (kind_subtype always equals the only value the kind can have) is a hint the subtype was vestigial \\u2014 vouch keeps kind_subtype=issued for issuance after the redesign tautologically, slated for broader cleanup. Reply at message 1614.\", \"_ts\": 1778716113.099394, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\"]}, \"paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"message\": \"**Cumulative meta-pattern transitioned from PLAN-documented to CODE-PINNED.** First cross-repo consumer shipped: pile sha:563597a on main (authentik+vouch IssuerRegistry, discipline-10 test-pinned via test_issuer_registry_audiences_pin, discipline-9 read-side fix bundled). Five vouch friction exercises + one consumer-impl session + first consumer ship + comms PR-ready + relay PLAN authored. ZERO substrate changes pushed across the entire arc. **Eleven disciplines, nine framings, two meta-disciplines emerging.** ELEVEN consumer-side disciplines (a)-(d), (5)-(11). NEW since last emit: (11) consumer-side privilege guards \\u2014 substrate refuses to enumerate consumer-specific privilege axes (admin, service-account, cross-org); consumers enforce additional gates beyond envelope validity. N=2 (comms F1 platform-admin guard + commission R-11a mint-guard); pile is structural-null-case (no privilege axis above envelope, holds trivially). Discipline (10) namespace-mapping-lives-at-consumer refined: **N=2 structural (pile + comms IssuerRegistry consumer-side dict-keyed-by-iss) / N=1 semantic (comms namespace-of-resolution at bind)**. Commission dropped out of (10) accounting entirely when cold-break retired commission-as-issuer (sole-issuer-of-record now vouch.bfc.lol). **Nine substrate framings.** NEW: (8) cache TTL is rotation-honor budget (parallel-projection with framing-4 substrate-types/wire-types); (9) convert-errors-at-source binds general-Python-error-shape to semantic-axis-class at the seam between language-error-conventions and protocol-error-hierarchy. Framing-(9) is **implementation-independent contract, evidence at N=4 across consumers under different mechanisms**: vouch Sequence-traversal-failing-through-InvalidSignatureError (verifier.py:192-200), pile dict-KeyError-converted-to-InvalidTokenError (jwks.py:78), pile AttributeError-converted-to-RuntimeError via isinstance-guard (jwks.py:48), comms non-dict-act-claim convert-at-source (cairn PR sha:bebcbe4). Same seam, different surface forms, same discipline. **NEW pattern at N=2 within session: migration-dissolution.** When substrate-of-record changes, cold-break removes design-bias that migration-preservation enforces. Substrate-of-record layer: vouch ledger cold-break (kaygee ratification \\u2014 neither (i) table-then-migrate nor (ii) hold-until-vouch; both presumed pre-existing state). Consumer-IssuerRegistry layer: pile (\\u03b2) swap-in-place vs append-then-cleanup (commit 6c6b162). Recursive layer-application within one session \\u2014 pattern is structural, not coincidental. Operational-form: complexity that won't survive the new shape doesn't earn its preservation across cutover. Adjacent to framing/resisted-at-design-abstractions-stay-absent \\u2014 cold-break is the operational form. **NEW pattern at N=2: verifier-copy carve-and-ship contract validated.** Vouch's e2e/reference-verifier (canonical) + comms's carved copy with AST-pin traveling. Consumer inherits discipline by structural copy then applies independently where consumer-specific seams arise. Discipline composition, not just code composition. Pile is the inverse case: consumer with pre-existing JWT machinery, iss-dispatch-only without verifier-copy. The per-consumer decision (copy vs dispatch) is grounded in existing-primitives inventory. **Meta-disciplines emerging (paradigm-of-paradigm-doc claims about evidence interpretation):** (M1) pin-discipline-discipline \\u2014 category of pin must match category of contract (behavioral vs framing vs decision); applies RECURSIVELY at meta-meta level (codex tightened AST-pin itself on signature + mutable-state walkers \\u2014 the pin meant to enforce had drift on its own pin-rigor). (M2) degenerate-form-as-evidence-class \\u2014 some disciplines admit degenerate-form N=1 + full-form N=1 = pinned; others require N=2 full. Discriminating is itself a meta-discipline of cumulative-artifact bookkeeping. (M3) suspicious-density-as-real-seam \\u2014 when independent catches cluster at one point (codex finding three different surface-form bugs at the same seam in two passes), that point is structurally load-bearing. Complementary to alcove's suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-signal (opposite direction). Meta-discipline observation: **meta-disciplines are inside the system they describe, not outside.** Parallel to gripping-hand recursion in strange-loops. **Catch-and-self-revise tally: 10 instances across 5 agents in this session.** Cairn (a)\\u2192(b) inventory pivot, relay (a1)\\u2192(b) JWKS reframe, loops-claude verifier-copy retraction on pile-claude grounded read, loops-claude (10) N=2-claim\\u2192N=2-structural/N=1-semantic, scrivener (10) N=3/N=2 count revision after relay commission-retires-JWKS, loops-claude substrate-boundary-mis-categorization (forward-auth vs JWT-IssuerConfig), scrivener (ii)-hold-until-vouch \\u2192 cold-break faithful read, scrivener swap-framing-over-generalized \\u2192 comms is add-only, scrivener premature-(10)-convergence-close \\u2192 loops-claude N=1/N=2+ scope-clarification, pile-claude (10)-N=2-claim \\u2192 N=2-structural/N=1-semantic. Pattern strengthening across implementation phase, not just design. Practice-residue candidate: **catch-rate scales with peer-density \\u00d7 review-rigor \\u00d7 register-fit.** N=1 today (this session-shape); promote when comparable density surfaces in another implementation-track session. **For substrate side:** participatory-not-authenticative stance operationalized AND validated under load. Substrate refused the bait at every consumer-side decision point. Three consumers + one substrate (vouch itself) + one paradigm artifact (this document) + ZERO substrate amendments. When reaching to add substrate enforcement for ANY discipline on this list, burden of proof is high; the discriminating questions are (1) is there a second consumer with concrete divergent constraints needing this TODAY? (N=2 bar) and (2) does the discipline genuinely not live at consumer-runtime? **For the next cross-repo consumer:** this artifact is the registry to read FIRST. Substrate-feels-universal trap (and inverted vouch-feels-universal form caught by cairn inventory-pivot) is the primary failure mode. Six self-revisions in this session demonstrate the catch-and-accept pattern works \\u2014 flag your own over-reach, accept peer-caught over-reach without defense, refine the cumulative artifact through the catch. **Implementation status:** pile shipped sha:563597a. Comms PR ready sha:bebcbe4 awaiting kaygee merge. Relay PLAN at sha:5b81445+sha:4147f53 (cold-break + swap-not-append clarifications). adr:0022 documenting cold-break design in flight. JWKS topology (b) settled \\u2014 vouch sole-issuer-of-record (commission retired); independent keystores per issuer; IssuerRegistry dispatch by iss.\", \"_ts\": 1778736498.934163, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"decision:design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"decision:paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\", \"decision:paradigm/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\", \"decision:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\", \"message\": \"Substrate framing surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl during service-shell exercise; landed durable on vouch main 7958fe5 in docs/friction/service-shell-exercise.md Obs 2. (Re-emit as decision; earlier observation-kind emit was orphaned because project vertex doesn't declare observation kind.) loops substrate was shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions; vouch (first concurrent-runtime consumer) surfaced the first instance: SqliteStore connection is thread-affine, sqlite3.connect() without check_same_thread=False at libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:99. Consumer-owns-threading is the right resolution at N=1 \\u2014 same shape as VouchPolicy substrate-doesn't-enforce disciplines. Three substrate options rejected/accepted: (a) check_same_thread=False NOT safe relax (WAL corruption without consumer-side locking); (b) connection-per-thread pool is substrate change for N=1 AND pool shape is consumer-runtime-dependent (Litestar workers vs trio nursery vs asyncio task group); (c) consumer-owns-threading correct. At N=2 the substrate-side action is documentation (SqliteStore docstring), not implementation change. Latent assumption-leak candidates for eventual review: does emit block on fsync? is there a streaming-write contract? does replay assume monotonic ts under concurrent writes? Meta-pattern: 'first concurrent consumer surfaces substrate assumptions' \\u2014 future instances should be obvious-shape because we've named it.\", \"_ts\": 1778722883.490142, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"message\": \"Self-correction surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl (scrivener catch, msg 1613). (Re-emit as decision; earlier observation-kind emit was orphaned because project vertex doesn't declare observation kind.) Fact dataclass slots are (kind, ts, payload, observer, origin) \\u2014 confirmed at libs/atoms/src/atoms/fact.py. No refs field on Fact. Refs land at payload._refs (vertex_reader.py:984 does d.pop('_refs', ()) separating from semantic payload at read time). My msg-1612 framing of 'refs as substrate primitive' was imprecise; sharper framing: refs-as-vocabulary IS the substrate primitive (the convention of payload-level pointers + emit-time resolution + entity-ref graph index); refs-as-Fact-shape would be premature substrate. Implication for ref-walk substrate move: lifting walk_refs(from_fact, predicate) would walk payload refs by convention, not a Fact slot \\u2014 even more consumer-policy than initially framed (convention-aware traversal not structural traversal). Practice note: when reasoning about substrate primitives, distinguish 'a slot on the dataclass' from 'a vocabulary convention with substrate support.' Refs are the latter.\", \"_ts\": 1778722888.707305, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"design/vouch-as-first-bounded-substrate-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-as-first-bounded-substrate-consumer\", \"message\": \"Vouch becomes loops' first cross-repo consumer of the FULL bounded substrate \\u2014 not just engine.Peer + atoms.Fact + sqlite_store, but the substrate at idiomatic scale: multi-kind vertex (vouch, rescission, client, policy, attestation), Facts with non-trivial payloads (client credentials, scope tables, evidence claims), refs for ancestry tracking, projection-based runtime state (rescission index, client registry, policy registry, active grants), engine.delegate() for token-exchange scope narrowing. This is a real load test for loops' substrate readiness. The exploration audit confirmed support: multi-kind vertex via Vertex.register() at engine/vertex.py:239-263; arbitrary Fact payloads via Fact.of() at atoms/fact.py:108-111; SqliteStore.latest_by_kind_where() at sqlite_store.py:285-310 for client_id lookups; Projection class at engine/projection.py:24-77 for fold patterns. Known gaps (vouch builds bespoke): O(n) rescission lookup \\u2192 vouch maintains per-vertex index during fold; ref-graph traversal is app-level; multi-field query via Python iteration. None blocking. The bfc.lol/docs/vouch-alignment/ plan committed at bfc.lol@f25512b (refined at dd245c5) is the implementation contract. Implication for loops: if vouch ships clean, the substrate is production-ready for OAuth-style flows. Three potential future loops improvements surface from this work: declarative ref-index for kind-based relationship queries, multi-field SQL query API, declarative kind-validation at emit time.\", \"_ts\": 1778789528.378513, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"architecture:cross-repo-consumer\", \"substrate:bounded-vouch\"]}, \"design/substrate-overreach-vs-fragmentation-bidirectional\": {\"topic\": \"design/substrate-overreach-vs-fragmentation-bidirectional\", \"message\": \"Substrate-discipline pattern catches in BOTH directions; I had been catching only one. Substrate-OVERREACH: building primitives without forcing function \\u2014 caught repeatedly in past sessions (sidecar invention, hypothesis+finding split, etc.). Substrate-FRAGMENTATION: deferring components that share a forcing function and a known coherent shape \\u2014 caught this session when Kyle pivoted from incremental credential migration to full bounded vouch substrate. The discriminating question for either direction: do these pieces compose into one bounded shape, or are they independent? Independent + premature \\u2192 defer. Coherent set + shape-known \\u2192 build together to avoid N migrations. Vouch's case: mint, exchange, attest, rescind, client registry, policy registry all share one forcing function (homelab agent flow needs full trust substrate) and compose into one OAuth-style token server. Deferring exchange while shipping mint = future migration pain; building together = one refactor. Pattern named for future-me: when a substrate decision feels like fragmenting, run the bidirectional check explicitly. The same instinct that catches overreach also catches fragmentation if you flip the question.\", \"_ts\": 1778789538.332046, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-first-bounded-substrate-consumer\", \"paradigm:substrate-discipline\"]}, \"paradigm/substrate-paradigm-vs-substrate-distribution-immutability\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/substrate-paradigm-vs-substrate-distribution-immutability\", \"message\": \"Banked 2026-05-14 #vouch-smoke-test (msgs 1765/1766) after first cross-repo deploy. **Substrate has two axes of immutability that I had conflated as one until vouch's first deploy forced the distinction.** (1) Paradigm-immutability: no new Fact slot, no new Vertex behavior, no new engine primitive. Through five vouch friction exercises + first cross-repo consumer ship (pile sha:563597a, comms impl/vouch-issuer) + production deploy (vouch.bfc.lol live with publicly-readable JWKS, RS256, kid 6fcc05467d1016ca), ZERO paradigm amendments. Participatory-not-authenticative stance survived contact with real consumers. (2) Distribution-immutability: NOT held. Two operational gaps surfaced and were closed during cutover. (a) loops sign-package was carved (commit ea517f1) AFTER strange-loops==0.2.0 published to PyPI; vouch's Dockerfile couldn't pip-install with 'from sign import ...' until loops 0.3.0 shipped (commit 22503e3 + workflow 25844442810). (b) PyPI CDN propagation race: vouch CI #183 failed at 05:58:08 because the publish at 05:56:47 hadn't propagated globally yet (~80s gap). **The conflation that was wrong:** treating 'ZERO substrate amendments' as covering both axes. It covered only paradigm. Distribution-axis (release coordination, versioning, packaging, CDN propagation) is ALSO substrate-of-record responsibility but distinct category. **Operational consumer-consumability is a distinct substrate axis from paradigm-shape invariants.** Both are substrate responsibilities; conflating them misframes 'ZERO substrate amendments' as covering more than it does. **Discriminator:** paradigm-axis = what substrate IS (shapes, slots, primitives); distribution-axis = how substrate IS DELIVERED (versions, packages, propagation, indexing). Same substrate, two responsibility surfaces. **N=1 today** (loops sign-release gap + PyPI propagation race surfaced by vouch first-deploy); promote when a second cross-repo consumer of a different substrate library surfaces parallel distribution-axis issues. **Side-property worth noting:** package-install in CI test stage is a distribution-propagation-canary by side-effect \\u2014 relay :1771 catch. Cheap. Worth banking as 'CI-install-as-canary' practice candidate. Refs: msg 1765 (loops-claude initial framing), 1766 (scrivener concur + meta-self-revise #12 at framing level).\", \"_ts\": 1778818239.644979, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary\", \"message\": \"N=2 parent framing surfaced 2026-05-15 DM exchange with cairn (msgs 1826/1827). Promotes discipline-(10) from single-axis (identity-namespace) to parent principle with two N=2 instances. **The parent principle:** vouch is opaque about what consumer strings MEAN; consumer enforces semantics. Substrate ships uninterpreted strings; consumer's catalog/code is the source of meaning. **Instance 1: identity-namespace** (cairn :1665, May 14) \\u2014 issuer URL IS namespace-of-record; substrate doesn't encode namespace in JWT claims; consumer maintains issuer\\u2192namespace mapping in IssuerConfig. Closes cross-org leak risk via consumer-side accept-only-configured-issuers. **Instance 2: scope-vocabulary** (NEW, cairn :1826, May 15) \\u2014 vouch's kind=policy.allowed_scopes was a redundant third gate alongside per-client allowed_scopes_per_aud + resource-server-enforcement-of-meaning. Drops cleanly: scope semantics live entirely at the resource server (comms enforces what comms:send MEANS; vouch sees opaque strings). F12 fixture/policy disagreement dissolves as side-effect. **The WHY (sharper than F12-fix framing):** vouch declaring scope vocabulary it doesn't own the semantics of is a substrate-feels-universal violation. Same shape as catalog-VERIFIES dissolution in vouch exercise 5 (substrate declares what it owns and emits; consumer-side semantics stay at consumer). 'Fix F12' as the framing risks the principle not surviving the next adjacent decision; 'correct substrate-overreach where vouch reached past its semantic ground' carries the principle forward when another centralizing primitive is proposed. **Structural questions resolved in :1827:** (a) what stays in kind=policy post-dissolution \\u2014 drop allowed_scopes, keep per-audience TTL + audience metadata that earns; don't rename unless content category shifts; (b) who populates kind=client.allowed_scopes_per_aud \\u2014 operator-manual is substrate-honest; auto-populating from consumer catalogs would create new dependency surface violating request-path-property and substrate-doesn't-reach-into-consumer-runtime stance. **For the next cross-repo consumer:** the discriminating question when proposing centralized vocabulary at vouch is 'does vouch own the semantics of these strings?' If no, the vocabulary belongs at the consumer. Substrate ships uninterpreted strings beyond what's structurally needed for issuance gating (per-client allowlist). **Trade absorbed:** vouch loses central typo-detection at mint time \\u2014 consumer refuses one hop later instead. Cheap. Implementation-axis follow-on: paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract re-emit pending after phase4 lands; discipline-(10) will be re-articulated as parent with two N=2 instances; current ten disciplines + nine framings shouldn't shrink, just re-shape.\", \"_ts\": 1778818257.217697, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"framing/wire-identity-stability-beats-internal-immutability\": {\"topic\": \"framing/wire-identity-stability-beats-internal-immutability\", \"message\": \"N=1 candidate framing flagged by scrivener (DM 1818) from the T6 migrate-facts 1810\\u21921811 unwind. **The pattern:** substrate-shape questions can have surface-level analogs that LOOK right and aren't. scrivener's initial T6 framing endorsed fresh-ULID for the wrong reason ('facts-are-immutable smuggled-via-index-collision'). Codex caught it; the actual axis is different. **The error:** treating payload['jti'] as a Fact identity proxy. Wrong. payload['jti'] identifies the TOKEN (JWT wire claim); the Fact is identified by its substrate-level position (rowid/ULID at append time). Facts being immutable doesn't constrain payload-content to be single-instance per token. Fresh-ULID for the superseding Fact's payload['jti'] would BREAK the JWT in circulation \\u2014 the token has the OLD jti; consumers checking index by payload['jti'] would find synthetic migration JTIs instead of real wire jtis. **The discriminator that would have caught it earlier (scrivener's articulation):** 'if my proposed shape changes the wire identity of an externally-circulating artifact, the shape is wrong regardless of how immutable the internal Facts feel.' **The general framing:** wire-identity-stability beats internal-immutability-aesthetics. Layers have their own identity-stability concerns; don't conflate. Internal substrate concerns (immutability, append-only, ledger discipline) operate on the substrate side. Wire/external concerns (token jti in circulation, JWKS rotation-honor, audience contracts) operate on the consumer-runtime side. Don't change wire identity to satisfy internal aesthetics; don't change internal storage to satisfy wire aesthetics. **Connects to:** (1) write-receipt-vs-temporal-query (April 29 #agent-party) \\u2014 both axes treat wire-identity/receipt-identity as primary and stable. (2) framing-(7) envelope-vs-currency \\u2014 wire-identity is part of envelope; internal state is currency. (3) framing-(4) substrate-types-and-wire-types parallel-projection \\u2014 same family; wire vs substrate divergence is the parent shape. **N=1 today** (T6 supersession-marker unwind). Promote at N=2 when another substrate-shape decision risks confusing internal-immutability with wire-identity. Candidate sites worth watching: rescission-jti (internal Fact has its own ULID; wire claim has target_jti), JWKS-kid rotation (substrate keystore vs wire JWKS kid), fold-state merging (internal state evolves; cached wire receipts don't).\", \"_ts\": 1778818271.308341, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"paradigm/consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-audience-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-audience-asymmetry\", \"message\": \"Emitted 2026-05-15 #vouch-impl 1846/1847 after T8 (F12 scope-vocabulary dissolution) merge sha:465096b. **Sharpening of consumer-owns-its-vocabulary** caught by T8 codex round-1 PLAN review (P2.1 resolution). The parent principle (vocabulary lives where semantics live) holds; the application axis differs by audience ownership. **Two application forms:** (1) Consumer-owned audience (comms, pile, commission as resource servers) \\u2014 vocabulary dissolves to consumer. kind=policy drops scope field. Resource server enforces meaning. This is the form T8 dissolution applied to comms/pile audiences. (2) Vouch-owned audience (vouch-identity, vouch-internal, FAM) \\u2014 vocabulary stays at vouch but in CODE at issuance site, not declarative in kind=policy. The set-equality check 'set(requested_scope) != {AGENT_SCOPE}' lives at the FAM issuance check because vouch IS the resource server for these audiences. **Discriminator:** who owns the audience. When semantics live at consumer (= audience), vocabulary lives at consumer. When semantics live at vouch (= audience-owner), vocabulary lives at vouch \\u2014 but as code, not as declarative policy. **Codex catch:** the dissolution would have widened FAM (allowing arbitrary scopes via the same vocabulary-lives-at-consumer principle) if applied uniformly. The asymmetry was empirically caught by adversarial PLAN-stage review. Worth banking the methodological data point: PLAN-stage codex review caught a substrate-shape regression that would have shipped as a wire-shape change. Both layers (compound dissolution mechanism prediction + adversarial review catch) earned. **For the next dissolution decision:** ask 'who owns this audience?' before assuming the consumer-owned application form. Vouch-owned audiences are not exceptions; they're the symmetric application of the parent principle with semantics-live-at-vouch as the locus. **Refs:** consumer-owns-its-vocabulary (parent), cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract (cumulative artifact registry).\", \"_ts\": 1778820530.278798, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision\": {\"topic\": \"practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision\", \"message\": \"Methodological learning surfaced during Phase 1 close 2026-05-15. **Pattern I caught in myself, flagged to Kyle in reflection:** I over-emitted paradigm-level facts as decisions tonight when several should have been hypotheses with status=proposed. **The specific over-reaches I want future-me to see:** (1) wire-identity-stability \\u2014 emitted as framing/decision after T6 1810\\u21921811 unwind (N=1 + within-arc 'confirmation' from T6 fixture-stability outcome). The fixture-stability is the SAME forcing-function arc, not an independent decision site. Confirmation requires N=2 from independent sites. (2) per-issuer-config-axes-vary \\u2014 claimed N=2 from audience-optional-per-issuer + vocabulary-form-per-audience-ownership, but both surfaced within the T8/F12 dissolution work. Same arc, not independent. (3) consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-asymmetry \\u2014 emitted as full paradigm decision after a single codex catch in one PLAN cycle. The catch is real and the framing is probably right; emitting as a decision rather than hypothesis overstates evidence strength. **The discipline correction:** when a framing is N=1 or within-arc-N=many, the right emit-kind is hypothesis with status=proposed and message articulating both the framing AND the missing evidence ('needs N=2 from independent decision sites; current evidence is forcing-function-internal'). Decision-kind is for emissions where the load-bearing fact IS the decision, not the framing-promotion. **Why this matters:** the fold-engine's hypothesis-status lifecycle (proposed \\u2192 confirmed/rejected/refined) is the rigorous register for evidence-tracking. Emitting framings as decisions short-circuits the lifecycle \\u2014 there's no status-update path to refine the claim if subsequent evidence weakens it. Future-me at session_start sees a decision-with-confidence rather than a hypothesis-with-evidence-bar. **The general axis (per discipline-as-axis-not-catch, May 14):** under-emit (lose patterns to forgetting) vs over-emit (noise in cumulative artifact, false confidence at session_start). The right position is calibrated to evidence-strength \\u2014 N=2-independent earns decision; N=1-with-confirmed-prediction earns hypothesis-status=confirmed; N=1-without-confirmation earns hypothesis-status=proposed. **Practice for future sessions:** before emitting a paradigm-level fact, ask 'do I have evidence from two INDEPENDENT decision sites, or is this within-arc?' If within-arc, emit as hypothesis with status=proposed and message naming what would constitute confirming evidence. The hypothesis stays in the fold; subsequent independent-site evidence updates status to confirmed or refined. **Related growing edges:** suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check (alcove 2026-05-10 banked at paradigm/suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check) \\u2014 tonight's catch is the structural-detection form firing on my own emit-pattern. The principle caught itself one layer up. Connects to M2 (degenerate-form-as-evidence-class) \\u2014 some claims need N=2 full form; some admit degenerate-form-with-confirmation. The discriminating question is per-claim, not global. Refs: paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract (cumulative artifact accumulating these emissions), framing/wire-identity-stability-beats-internal-immutability (over-emitted instance), paradigm/consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-audience-asymmetry (over-emitted instance).\", \"_ts\": 1778821161.219015, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"pattern/cumulative-artifact-load-bearing-needs-consolidation\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cumulative-artifact-load-bearing-needs-consolidation\", \"message\": \"Concern banked 2026-05-15 Phase 1 close. **The cumulative paradigm artifact (paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract) has grown to load-bearing infrastructure in its own right.** Current state per 05:28 emit + tonight's additions: eleven consumer-side disciplines, nine substrate framings, three emerging meta-disciplines (M1 pin-discipline-discipline, M2 degenerate-form-as-evidence-class, M3 suspicious-density-as-real-seam), at least three parent principles (consumer-owns-its-vocabulary with N=3 instances; substrate-paradigm-vs-substrate-distribution-immutability; wire-identity-stability-beats-internal-immutability), and tonight's additions (consumer-owned-vs-vouch-owned-asymmetry, per-issuer-config-axes-vary candidate, dissolution-test-passes-compound). **The artifact is doing real work** \\u2014 ADR-0004 on both vouch + commission cite it as canonical registry. Three repos can converge on substrate-shape vocabulary via this single durable pointer. That's load-bearing infrastructure for cross-repo knowledge. **But it's also accumulating maintenance debt.** Each re-emit appends material; the fold upserts at topic level so the latest emit fully shadows prior ones in fold view, but the LATEST emit must contain everything load-bearing \\u2014 adding material monotonically is the path, not consolidating. At current scale, the artifact-as-emit-body is approaching the size where readers will skim rather than read. **The maintenance question for next consolidation:** which framings are still load-bearing for FUTURE consumers vs which were load-bearing for the specific Wave 1 arc and have now done their work? The artifact should preserve principles + framings that generalize; tactical observations that earned their keep in Wave 1 specifically (which-codex-catch-happened-when) might want to live in friction-docs and ADRs, not in the paradigm-registry. **Concrete next move when next forcing function lands:** before adding new material to paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract, identify what can be removed-because-it-served-its-purpose vs what stays because it generalizes. Different from 'shrink the disciplines list' \\u2014 the disciplines DO generalize; many of the within-arc observations don't. **Related concern: catch-rate-required-density.** Tonight had ~12 self-revisions across 5 agents, codex passes at PLAN time, friction-docs as durable artifacts, multi-repo coordination through #vouch-impl. The substrate-discipline outcome (zero amendments) partly reflects this review-density doing work that simpler designs would handle automatically. **Open question for future sessions:** is the paradigm robust to lower agent-density, or does it require the review-machinery to maintain the discipline? Worth watching at next solo or low-density session \\u2014 does the substrate-feels-universal trap still get caught when only one agent is reviewing? **For now:** the artifact stands. Phase 1 arc is closed. Next forcing function (Phase 5 cutover, comms phase 4 ship, factoring of iss-dispatch at N=3) is the natural moment to do consolidation. Don't pre-consolidate; let the next forcing function force the question.\", \"_ts\": 1778821179.929721, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\"]}, \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"message\": \"Decision (refined 2026-05-15 after InferioMinion review): expose namespace/prefix filtering via a single kind-aware --key <prefix> flag on loops read. SEMANTICS CONFIRMED: prefix matching, not equality. Implementation is payload.get(fold_key_field).startswith(prefix). User controls specificity by how much of the key they type \\u2014 '--key dao/' returns the whole subtree; '--key dao/as-url-conventions' returns that single item (prefix-of-itself with nothing longer matching). No --key-exact flag; if you want exact, type the full key. Rationale for prefix-default: namespace drilldown is the dominant use case (operator types the discriminating prefix, gets the subtree); exact-match falls out naturally as the degenerate prefix case. Original dissolution argument: the fold-key field varies by kind (topic for decision/observation; name for thread/task/hypothesis/etc.); the spec already declares which field per kind. --key honors that declaration \\u2014 one filter operation, kind-aware via existing fold-key spec. Separate flags (--topic/--name/--namespace) would split one operation across N field-name aliases and require enumeration. Evidence sites: (1) fold lens already partitions output by namespace at render \\u2014 asymmetric to be missing at filter; (2) InferioMinion cross-arc recognition ('oooh' on first sight); (3) InferioMinion second-pass confirmation \\u2014 independently arrived at name-prefix as simpler dependency structure than separate context field; specifically asked 'does --key do prefix matching or exact matching' confirming the operation is being thought about correctly. Implementation: ~30 LOC in read parser + fetch_fold. Sibling primitive: lens fetch kwargs passthrough (design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough) \\u2014 both ship together as the access-primitives batch.\", \"_ts\": 1778875040.572362, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"practice/multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths\"]}, \"design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough\", \"message\": \"Decision: complete the lens-declares-fetch contract by threading arbitrary --flag=value CLI args through to the lens's fetch() kwargs, symmetric to how call_lens already passes optional kwargs to render functions (lens_resolver.py:229-233). Current state: main.py:597-600 passes a fixed set (kind, observer, retain_facts) to lens_fetch \\u2014 lenses CAN declare def fetch(vertex_path, **kwargs) but the CLI has nothing to put in the kwargs bag beyond those three. Result: lens-declares-fetch is half-wired \\u2014 lenses can declare custom fetch but cannot be parameterized at the CLI surface. Evidence: InferioMinion's guidance lens hardcodes 'Access:' instructions including 'loops read X --filter pattern' \\u2014 a flag that doesn't exist. The lens is documenting an aspirational CLI surface, indicating the gap is felt at their site. Their guide kind groups by payload.context (not key namespace), so --key alone can't drill into 'When Working on Authorization' sections; the lens needs to declare its own --context filter and have it threaded through. Implementation: parse unknown --foo=bar / --foo bar args in the read parser into a dict, pass as **lens_kwargs alongside the standard kwargs. ~20 line change in main.py. Lenses opt in by declaring **kwargs in their fetch signature; existing lenses unaffected. Sibling to --key (decision/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive): --key serves generic CLI-level filtering for any vertex; lens kwargs passthrough serves lens-specific domain vocabulary (--context, --severity, --for-task) that doesn't generalize. Both lands.\", \"_ts\": 1778874693.85743, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-declares-fetch\"]}, \"design/guidance-as-lens-not-kind\": {\"topic\": \"design/guidance-as-lens-not-kind\", \"message\": \"Dissolution finding: 'guidance' is a lens, not a kind. Reading InferioMinion's guidance lens (~/.config/loops/lenses/guidance.py shared 2026-05-15) reveals it composes six EXISTING kinds \\u2014 principle, guide, pattern, decision, task, thread \\u2014 into a tabular knowledge-base view with three render shapes (core-loops universal, domain, generic). No new kind is being introduced; 'guidance' is the lens name and the navigation/routing pattern. Confirms dissolution-test: before adding a kind, check whether the use case is render-shape over existing kinds rather than substrate addition. For knowledge-base / runbook / threaded-skills patterns: the answer is lens composition, not kind invention. This dissolves the kind-introduction question that opened the InferioMinion thread \\u2014 there is no guidance-kind to design. The substrate is already adequate; what was missing is access primitives (--key, lens kwargs passthrough, possibly --match) so the lens-as-interface contract is complete. Implication for paradigm: 'lens is the interface' (design/lens-is-the-interface) has a substrate-side complement \\u2014 when a use case feels like it wants a new kind, check first whether it's a new lens over existing kinds. Most knowledge-organization patterns will be lens-shape, not kind-shape.\", \"_ts\": 1778874709.440389, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough\"]}, \"practice/multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths\": {\"topic\": \"practice/multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths\", \"message\": \"Practice (refined 2026-05-15 after InferioMinion's divergent-probes extension): when a conceptual entity has multiple natural namespace homes, emit it under each \\u2014 two facts with different prefixes, same body \\u2014 rather than introducing a separate 'context' or 'tag' field. The duplicate emits ARE the multi-routing semantics. SHARPENED FRAMING (InferioMinion): two emits aren't just routing aliases, they're INDEPENDENT PROBES measuring which clusters of work actually reference that knowledge. If test/resolver-chain accumulates high salience and settings/resolver-chain stays low, that's evidence the pattern is primarily a testing concern even though it lives in the settings package. The salience signal is RICHER than you'd get from a single canonical entry point \\u2014 divergence is information, not maintenance burden. Origin: InferioMinion's resolution of the multi-context guides edge case during --key design. Example: a guide for 'when writing tests that touch the settings resolver' belongs to both test/ and settings/. Naive instinct says 'add a multi-value context field.' Dissolution: emit twice as name=test/foo and name=settings/foo \\u2014 the guide surfaces from either entry point during --key drilldown. Each fold item accumulates independent revision counts, ref graphs, and salience scores. Divergence is signal: each routing path measures a real audience independently. Safety valve (Kyle's framing): if the two paths drift to contradiction, that's loops surfacing a genuine conceptual split \\u2014 not maintenance problem, but DISCOVERY mechanism. Pattern: fold-key as routing handle; duplicate emits as multiple routes to same content AND as independent measurement probes on the underlying clusters. Generalizes beyond guides: any fact kind where fold-key acts as navigation handle (decision topics, thread names, task names). Discriminator: is the entity conceptually one thing accessed via multiple paths AND served by multiple distinct audience clusters (yes \\u2014 emit twice, let salience diverge) vs two related things sharing a body (no \\u2014 emit once, ref between them). Dissolves the recurring temptation to add 'tags' or 'multi-value context' fields to handle multi-classification.\", \"_ts\": 1778875452.179441, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/guidance-as-lens-not-kind\", \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\"]}, \"design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\": {\"topic\": \"design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"message\": \"Decision (refinement of design/lens-is-the-interface): lenses split into two shapes by job \\u2014 navigation lenses (route attention to drilldowns) vs content lenses (deliver the answer directly). Both are valid; conflating them produces lenses that do both badly. Origin: InferioMinion 2026-05-15 articulated for guidance lens \\u2014 'the lens's job is namespace discovery, not content delivery. It answers what namespaces have guidance, not what each guide says. Content lives in the patterns the guides route to.' Generalizes beyond guidance. Navigation lens design constraints: (1) surface namespace-level (not just per-item) salience as the discrimination signal \\u2014 operator needs to know WHERE to drill next, not just that drillable things exist; (2) prefer counts + ref-graph aggregates over body content in the index render; (3) make the drilldown command obvious (e.g. 'patterns: dao/ 47 items \\u2190128' implies 'loops read X --kind pattern --key dao/'). Content lens design constraints: (1) front-load verdict in first ~140 chars (preview budget for first-disclosure); (2) HYPOTHESIS-shaped bodies (verdict + evidence + conclusion) so drill-down decisions are earned not triggered; (3) progressive disclosure across zoom levels. Examples by shape: navigation lenses \\u2014 guidance (proposed), session_landing (core loops), reconcile (partial \\u2014 routes attention to stale items but also delivers their status); content lenses \\u2014 fold (default), painted record line, search results, decision body at -v. Implications: (a) lens authors should declare which shape they're building; (b) painted utilities may eventually split into navigation-render helpers vs content-render helpers; (c) the lens-as-router pattern is the natural home for --key drilldown \\u2014 the navigation lens routes you to the prefix, --key delivers the slice.\", \"_ts\": 1778875429.703804, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"practice/multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths\"]}, \"release/v0.3.1-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"release/v0.3.1-shipped\", \"message\": \"Shipped 2026-05-15 21:48 UTC. PyPI strange-loops==0.3.1, GitHub release at github.com/kgruel/strange-loops/releases/tag/v0.3.1, GitLab mirrored. Workflow run 25940645184 succeeded in 21s. Four commits since 0.3.0: f3492b2 (--key + call_lens_fetch), ca22e70 (gitignore mcp.json + scratch move), 57d547e (painted v0.1.6\\u2192v0.1.8 bump for build_fidelity/display-width fixes), 65ea07b (autoresearch.py sentinel + test_read_lens_not_found_exits_loudly completing lens-resolution-strict). Release commit d43fd79 (version bump + tag annotation). Two WIP branches parked local (not pushed): wip/store-sqlmerge-refactor (libs/store refactor adds sqlmerge dep, blocked on sqlmerge package availability), wip/coupling-kernels-runs (active research artifacts runs 07-13). One follow-up flagged: Node.js 20 deprecation on actions/checkout@v4 + astral-sh/setup-uv@v4, action needed before 2026-06-02 \\u2014 quick .github/workflows/release.yml bump when convenient.\", \"_ts\": 1778878310.217581, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/guidance-as-lens-not-kind\", \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"design/lens-fetch-kwargs-passthrough\", \"practice/multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths\"]}, \"design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\": {\"topic\": \"design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"message\": \"Finding from reading libs/store/transport.py: Transport does not understand facts, ticks, or vertices \\u2014 it moves SQLite files. Protocol-based with push(local_path, remote_path)/pull(remote_path, local_path). Current impl LocalTransport (file copy). SSH flagged future. HTTP not yet implemented. Implication for vouch integration: wire-auth gates the slice-push, not per-fact-emission. Vouch JWT gates 'principal P can push to endpoint'; semantic filtering (which kinds, which observers) is downstream via Peer/Grant on receive. The byte-boundary makes the three-layer auth composition possible.\", \"_ts\": 1778894995.712896, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\": {\"topic\": \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-16 (third position, recast from WIRE/SUBSTRATE/BODY to ATTESTATION/SUBSTRATE/BODY after local-case-as-primitive walk): three universal layers, none transport-specific. (1) ATTESTATION \\u2014 every fact carries signature (Fact.signature); receive verifies against observer's Peer.key. Two sub-paths inside attestation: direct-trust (Peer.key pre-registered, local + known-peer) and federated-trust (vouch credential bridges, per-fact validation for non-local observers). (2) SUBSTRATE \\u2014 vertex Peer/Grant filters fact-kind by observer (unchanged). (3) BODY \\u2014 provenance chain (act=alice etc.) in payload, answers 'who is the human ultimately responsible.' OPEN: BODY's role vs Fact.signature semantics \\u2014 signature-proves-emission vs signature-proves-responsibility \\u2014 needs picking in owed session (thread/vouch-substrate-session-owed). CORRECTION FROM PRIOR VERSION (REFINED \\u00d72): WIRE layer was over-fit on remote case. Local case is the primitive; signing/verification are universal; vouch is conditional inside attestation, not its own layer. Atoms evolve (Fact.signature, Peer.key); policy adoption progressive per design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy.\", \"_ts\": 1778908116.440801, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/stratified-retention-per-store-not-per-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/stratified-retention-per-store-not-per-vertex\", \"message\": \"Pattern named by vouch in 2026-05-15 design session, confirmed by engine architecture: retention/destination policy lives per-store, not per-vertex. A vertex emits facts of one shape (Fact tuples). Stores attached fan out \\u2014 stderr-store inherits short policy (e.g. CloudWatch 14-day), durable-store ships elsewhere via transport. The vertex does not choose; the stores do. Generalizes: vouch's own ledger has trust-relevance baked into kind set (all-durable-by-construction, no stratification needed). Downstream service vertices have mixed-lifetime populations and stratify with multiple stores. Trust-relevance encoded in kind + routing, not in vouch storage.\", \"_ts\": 1778895005.399838, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\"]}, \"design/vouch-decoupled-from-loops\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-decoupled-from-loops\", \"message\": \"Vouch does not know about loops; loops does not know about vouch. Vouch issues JWTs against a contract (aud + scope + exp + sig); loops transport accepts JWT-verifying backends pluggably; vouch is the one chosen for deployment. Confirmed via reading libs/engine/peer.py (substrate-policy not transport) and libs/store/transport.py (Protocol-based, pluggable). The decoupling makes vouch substrate-shaped: independent of consumers, replaceable, testable in isolation. Equivalent claim from vouch side: 'OAuth proves who, vouch records what was delegated, loops persists the record.'\", \"_ts\": 1778895011.693065, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\"]}, \"design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\": {\"topic\": \"design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\", \"message\": \"Vouch substrate-validating exemplar from 2026-05-15 design session. The PR-to-side-effect pattern (PR \\u2192 validators \\u2192 auto-merge \\u2192 side-effect) generalizes to agent-mediated form: agent \\u2192 MCP/API call \\u2192 validators \\u2192 side-effect, with vouch JWT as identity/policy substrate and explicit delegation chain (act=alice) replacing git-author-as-principal. The substrate does not change; configuration changes (audience policies, scope vocabularies, deployment topology). Exercises all three auth layers (wire, substrate, body) in one workflow. Argues for Go drop-in verifier as second concrete consumer of the verifier-library contract.\", \"_ts\": 1778895014.803616, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\"]}, \"design/verifier-library-dissolution-test-two-consumers\": {\"topic\": \"design/verifier-library-dissolution-test-two-consumers\", \"message\": \"Dissolution-test threshold for extracting a verifier library: TWO concrete consumers with divergent shapes, not one consumer plus one design intent. Currently validator-lambda Go consumer is concrete; loops-HTTP-transport Python consumer is design intent (HTTP transport does not exist yet). Extracting now would be speculation from one site. Threshold passes when HTTP transport gets designed against vouch as its first cut \\u2014 at that point two real consumers exist in parallel and the contract gets pinned by both. Discipline application of dissolution-default principle.\", \"_ts\": 1778895027.144416, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\": {\"topic\": \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED 2026-05-16 by design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive. The 'wire identity translation' framing was over-fit on the remote case. Under the local-as-primitive walk (see design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy and design/three-layer-auth-composition), there is no separate auth integration point \\u2014 signing is part of emit, verification is part of receive, both run by default with per-vertex policy. The auth_emit/gated_receive wrapper-pair dissolves. PRIOR version named this as 'integration point pair' between transport and vertex; that framing assumed transport was always present and that auth was a wrapping concern. Both wrong: local emission/reception works without transport AND signing/verification are constitutive of emit/receive, not wrappers. OPEN: lib boundary question \\u2014 does engine import vouch directly (hard dep) or does vouch register verifier callback (genuinely optional)? Owed in substrate session per thread/vouch-substrate-session-owed.\", \"_ts\": 1778908132.749281, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/observer-string-trust-load-bearing-only-locally\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-string-trust-load-bearing-only-locally\", \"message\": \"Substrate invariant named explicitly 2026-05-15 (Kyle): the observer field on a Fact is a trustworthy attribution string ONLY when the emit happens on a machine the receiver controls. Currently implicit and breaks silently. Cross-machine emit can lie about observer; nothing in the system complains. The fact silently encodes wrong attribution. auth_emit/gated_receive is the cryptographic backing that makes the invariant hold off-machine. Local-emit stays string-only (cheap, trusted-by-locality); cross-wire emit MUST go through auth_emit or its attribution is unsigned-claim, not attestation. This was the discomfort Kyle had been carrying about scaling beyond local \\u2014 now named.\", \"_ts\": 1778896251.693422, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\"]}, \"design/validator-tick-equals-audit-record\": {\"topic\": \"design/validator-tick-equals-audit-record\", \"message\": \"Further dissolution of validator-lambda case under tick-equals-fact universalism: on completion, the boundary fires a tick \\u2014 that tick IS the audit record. No separate audit-emission concern. Local store ephemeral (CloudWatch log-of-facts, retention=14d); remote store receives either the tick-as-fact (with full-fidelity payload including all contributing facts) OR the slice-of-bytes (raw facts) \\u2014 both shapes work, choice is per-deployment. Stratified-retention pattern handles local/remote split. No new primitives needed. The validator case is just: accumulate facts, fire boundary on completion, let the existing transport+retention machinery handle the rest.\", \"_ts\": 1778896255.703669, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/stratified-retention-per-store-not-per-vertex\", \"decision:design/validator-lambda-as-substrate-validating-exemplar\"]}, \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\": {\"topic\": \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-16 (fourth position, per-fact-validation correction from advisor + attestation-walk scope-narrowing): credential dissolves to (Identity + wire-Grant) + binding envelope + signature, validated PER-FACT for federated observers (NOT cached after first verification \\u2014 credential expiration must be checked each time; cached-key-without-expiration would be a security regression). Envelope/signature structural claim intact. vouch.verify returns Identity + wire-Grant \\u2014 a wire-Peer, not a substrate-Peer. The substrate's Peer for that identity is fetched from vertex-local config using Identity.name as lookup. PRIOR CORRECTIONS preserved: (3rd pass) no AudienceConfig \\u2014 verifier holds trusted-key config (jwks_urls); Issuer holds signing identity; audience parametric on calls. NEW CORRECTION (this pass): vouch is the federated-trust path INSIDE attestation (per design/three-layer-auth-composition + design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name), NOT 'the attestation layer' itself. Direct-trust observers (local Peer.key registered) bypass vouch entirely \\u2014 emit signs, receive verifies against Peer.key directly. Vouch loads only when receive encounters an observer not in local Peer registry. Vouch's job: per-fact key-discovery + authority-bridge for federated case.\", \"_ts\": 1778908140.434176, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"message\": \"Resolution from 2026-05-15 vocabulary walk (scope\\u2194potential under validator-lambda lens): Grant (horizon + potential) is a structural primitive \\u2014 a shape that says 'what's visible, what's actionable.' It applies at multiple layers, each with its own vocabulary. Wire-Grant (in credentials): horizon=readable actions, potential=invocable actions; vocabulary is action-shaped (provision-domain, push-facts); issued by vouch, scoped to audience. Substrate-Grant (in engine.peer): horizon=visible kinds, potential=emittable kinds; vocabulary is kind-shaped (domain.provisioned, validator.result); configured per-vertex. SAME STRUCTURE, DIFFERENT VOCABULARY. They do not translate to each other. Linked by identity (observer-name appears in both layers) and nothing else. The dissolution-test for scope\\u2194potential resolved by SEPARATION, not unification \\u2014 sometimes the dissolution is to recognize sibling applications of a primitive, not to merge them. Caught 2026-05-15 by Kyle pushing the validator-lambda walk past the easy-merge framing.\", \"_ts\": 1778902958.683284, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-15 (pass-through correction): scope (vouch) and potential (engine.peer) are DISTINGUISHED, not merged. Different layers, different vocabularies, no derivation. Scope is wire-Grant's vocabulary (action-shaped, audience-specific, issued by vouch); potential is substrate-Grant's vocabulary (kind-shaped, vertex-local, set by operator config). Share Grant structural primitive (horizon + potential) but apply different vocabularies \\u2014 wire-scope to action-vocab, substrate-potential to kind-vocab. Linked by observer-name across layers. Initial walk reached for merge with AudienceConfig+unpacker translation machinery; validator-lambda walk surfaced that translation has no purpose because scope gates invocation while potential gates emission. CORRECTION FROM PRIOR VERSION: AudienceConfig dissolves entirely (see design/audience-config-dissolves), not just collapses to lean shape \\u2014 verifier holds trusted-key config, audience is parametric. vouch.verify(jwt, expected_audience) returns Identity + wire-Grant, never reaches into substrate vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1778905498.994085, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\"]}, \"paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\", \"message\": \"Engine.peer's principle ('chain ancestry intentionally NOT reachable from a leaf Peer; walk the Fact ledger') was a separation-of-concerns choice in unsigned-facts world \\u2014 defensible but aesthetic. Under signed-facts, the question becomes load-bearing and the principle GENERALIZES rather than breaks. Restated: identity (Peer) carries name + Grant, constant-shape; history (chain, ancestry, prior states) lives in fact-history (the ledger). Generalization under signed-facts: 'the ledger' includes wire-arrived credential bundles \\u2014 a credential is a wire-shaped slice of the issuer's ledger, the relevant fact-history packaged for transit. From a receiver's perspective, the credential IS the fact-history-for-this-Peer. The principle gains structural rationale: identity stays constant-shape because it doesn't accrete history; history accumulates separately in records that scale with the work, not the identity. Putting chain on the identity would duplicate what the ledger (or credential-as-wire-ledger) already provides. Rejected alternative: observers-become-Peers (carry Grant on each fact) \\u2014 would couple fact-immutability to identity-state-changes; the current leveling (observer-as-stable-name on fact, Peer-as-evaluation-time-construct, credential-as-wire-anchor) is right and gains clarity under signed-facts.\", \"_ts\": 1778904329.346662, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\", \"message\": \"Vocabulary walk resolution 2026-05-15 (delegation\\u2194delegate): same shape as scope\\u2194potential \\u2014 distinguished by layer with shared structural operation. Both operations are 'the new entity has narrower authority than the parent.' Wire-delegation (vouch's chain extension via act=alice in JWT): records lineage on the credential because the receiver cannot walk the issuer's ledger. Substrate-delegation (engine.peer's delegate function): does NOT record lineage on the Peer because the ledger is local \\u2014 walk it for chain. Same operation, different layers. Lineage-recording is CONDITIONAL ON LOCALITY: wire requires explicit chain on credential (receiver lacks ledger access); substrate requires nothing extra (ledger is local). Discriminating question 'can substrate-delegation produce a chain?' resolved: substrate-delegation produces lineage IN THE LEDGER (via the vouch-issuance fact that recorded the delegation), not on the Peer. The Peer doesn't carry the chain because chain is one indirection away in fact-history. Builds on identity-vs-history-separation paradigm \\u2014 same generalization (fact-history includes wire-arrived credentials) explains why wire needs explicit chain and substrate doesn't.\", \"_ts\": 1778904340.038697, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"decision:paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\"]}, \"design/slice-with-ref-closure-as-loops-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"design/slice-with-ref-closure-as-loops-primitive\", \"message\": \"Loops primitive surfaced 2026-05-15 (Kyle caught the slice/transport conflation): ref-following belongs in slice, not transport. Slice decides WHAT to extract (kinds, time, observers, refs); transport moves whatever bytes slice produces. Architectural separation already in libs/store; ref-closure is a slice extension. Proposed shape: slice_store(source, target, *, kinds=[...], since=..., follow_refs=True) \\u2014 when follow_refs=True, scan included facts for ref-fields (cred_ref, ref=*, any kind:fold_key references), include referenced facts as dependency-closure. Generic substrate capability: useful anywhere cross-vertex referencing matters (cred_ref for vouch lineage; entity-ref for the existing ref machinery; future use cases not yet named). Vouch is the FIRST motivating consumer, not the owner. Transport remains pluggable Protocol with push/pull \\u2014 unchanged. Whether to follow_refs is per-slice policy, not per-transport policy. The 'lineage survives transport' property in vouch's case becomes 'slice with follow_refs=True produces self-contained bundles.'\", \"_ts\": 1778904761.199958, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"decision:paradigm/identity-vs-history-separation-survives-signed-facts\"]}, \"design/audience-config-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Dissolution finding 2026-05-15 (Kyle caught in pass-through): AudienceConfig dissolves entirely. Carried forward as vestigial after scope/potential walk, where its unpacker field dissolved (no scope-to-potential translation needed). Examining what remained: (1) audience name is a parameter to verify(), not config \\u2014 caller specifies expected_audience; verify checks JWT.aud matches; (2) key source is verifier-wide or per-issuer (via JWKS discovery), not per-audience \\u2014 the verifier trusts certain issuers regardless of audience; (3) scope vocabulary is documentation, not runtime data. None of these are per-audience runtime config. Corrected lib surface: Verifier holds trusted-key config (jwks_urls), exposes verify(jwt, expected_audience); Issuer holds signing key and issuer_id, exposes issue(subject, audience, scope, act). Two configs about WHO (trusted issuers, signing identity), not about WHICH AUDIENCE. Audience parametric on calls. Failure mode named: when a walk resolves something by emptying it, the next reading can mistake the emptied container for a residual \\u2014 the pass-through is the corrective.\", \"_ts\": 1778905483.705142, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\"]}, \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\", \"message\": \"Meta-pattern recognized 2026-05-15 across three vocabulary walks (scope/potential, delegation/delegate, credential/Grant): vouch terms and loops terms are not competing vocabularies \\u2014 they are sibling applications of the same structural primitives at different layers. Wire layer and substrate layer share STRUCTURES (Grant, narrowing-delegation, etc.), differ in VOCABULARY (action-shaped vs kind-shaped), are linked by identity (observer-name appears at both) but NOT derived from each other. The dissolution is to recognize and SEPARATE, not to merge. Discriminator for future collisions: 'is this the same operation at a different layer, or two different operations sharing a name?' If different layers: distinguish, name the layer-pair, no translation function. If same operation, same layer, same vocabulary: merge. The over-merge failure mode produces translation machinery (e.g., the audience unpacker proposed then dissolved this session) that has no purpose because the layers don't need to map. Shape: Grant is a structural primitive (horizon + potential); has wire-instance (action-vocab) and substrate-instance (kind-vocab); both are real, neither is canonical. Recurring evidence from this session's walks; apply to future loops/vouch design questions and similar substrate-vs-application vocabulary collisions.\", \"_ts\": 1778905529.91317, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"decision:design/delegation-and-delegate-distinguished-by-layer\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/scope-and-potential-distinguished-by-layer\"]}, \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"message\": \"Verdict: attestation is different-operations-sharing-name (per paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers discriminator), NOT sibling-layer like Grant. First negative result for the sibling-layer pattern \\u2014 strengthens the discriminator by firing both branches with non-trivial examples. Two operations: (1) first-party attestation \\u2014 observer signs own fact, libs/sign primitive. (2) third-party attestation \\u2014 Issuer signs claim about another party's identity/authority, libs/vouch built on libs/sign. Share substrate (cryptographic sign/verify), not operation. Verdict per meta-pattern: distinguish, name separately, no translation function. Implication: vouch is NOT 'the attestation layer' \\u2014 it is ONE path within attestation, the federated-trust path for cross-process identity binding when direct key-trust isn't pre-established. Vouch name retained \\u2014 accurately names third-party speech act. Walked 2026-05-15/16 via Kyle's push on the local case as primitive; advisor caught vouch must run per-fact for non-local observers (NOT bootstrap-once) because credential expiration must be checked each time.\", \"_ts\": 1778908101.504225, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\"]}, \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: Fact.signature and Peer.key evolve as STRUCTURAL atom fields (substrate change, one-time); verification policy is per-vertex PROGRESSIVE (strict/lenient/legacy-accept). Chosen from axis between config-default (atoms unchanged, sign+verify opt-in feature) and substrate-mandate (atoms structural, sign+verify mandatory, full design session owed first). Rationale: atoms move once \\u2192 homogeneous ledger from transition point \\u2192 'lineage is structural' becomes true not aspirational. Verification adoption stays progressive at consumer layer \\u2192 no big-bang migration \\u2192 fits project's progressive-capability development pattern. Sign-on-emit is the default (with explicit escape hatches for internal/derived/legacy). Vouch is the federation path inside attestation, runs per-fact for observers not in local Peer registry (credential expiration checked each time, NOT cached as a Peer entry). Five open questions (vertex identity, tick-signing, BODY's role under universal sig, bootstrap order, escape-hatch policy) plus lib-boundary plus Peer-on-fact nag are owed but not immediate \\u2014 surface as we hit them. See thread/vouch-substrate-session-owed. Caught: distributed-design-conversation is the failure mode of pure config-default (same questions re-derived per-adoption, answers drift); concentrated-upfront-session is the cost of pure substrate-mandate; option B splits the cost \\u2014 substrate change concentrated, policy progressive.\", \"_ts\": 1778908110.082658, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/credential-is-grant-in-envelope\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"paradigm/vouch-loops-vocabulary-as-sibling-layers\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\": {\"topic\": \"design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: signing is constitutive of emit, verification is constitutive of receive \\u2014 both run by default for vertices with verification policy configured. No separate auth_emit/gated_receive wrapper pair. The signature lives on the Fact atom (Fact.signature, structural per design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy) and is part of the fact's structural identity. Sign uses observer's key (vertex bootstrap generates one at init); verify uses Peer.key from local registry (federated-trust path adds vouch credential lookup per-fact for non-local observers). Verification policy per-vertex (strict/lenient/legacy-accept). Replaces the integration-point framing of design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation \\u2014 there are no separate integration points, just emit and receive doing their constitutive work. OPEN: does engine import vouch directly or does vouch register verifier callback? Affects whether engine has vouch in its dependency graph. Owed in substrate session.\", \"_ts\": 1778908122.673626, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/attestation-as-different-ops-sharing-name\", \"design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"ops/loops-installed-globally-via-uv-tool\": {\"topic\": \"ops/loops-installed-globally-via-uv-tool\", \"message\": \"Installed loops globally via uv tool install. CLI now reachable as `loops` and `sl` (shorthand) without `uv run` prefix. Eliminates per-invocation install/uninstall noise that was deterring thought-speed emissions. Dogfooding the 0.3.1 release; if behavioral changes prove useful we commit them back. This is the tactical fix; architectural daemon (long-lived loops process, socket CLI) is a separate thread.\", \"_ts\": 1778910559.577901, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/friction-as-fact-kind\": {\"topic\": \"design/friction-as-fact-kind\", \"message\": \"Friction is its own first-class fact kind, distinct from thread and task. Discriminating property: friction = \\\"behavior I want but tooling/structure makes hard, with a specific fix in mind.\\\" Distinct from thread (open conversation/arc, scope-to-determine) and task (one-shot tracked work). Status lifecycle: open / in_progress / resolved / parked. Fold key: name=. Enables: queryable backlog via `sl read project --kind friction`, runbook-aligned discipline (Kyle leans on it heavily), discriminated from generic threads. Rationale for not dissolving into thread: friction has specific shape (deters a behavior + has a fix) that thread does not \\u2014 and the backlog-scan use case wants kind-filter, not topic-prefix-filter. Surfaced 2026-05-16 during runbook v1 design when Kyle named the friction queue should become a kind he can lean on.\", \"_ts\": 1778911857.186259, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:bilateral-runbook-in-claudemd\"]}, \"ops/strange-loops-local-install\": {\"topic\": \"ops/strange-loops-local-install\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Local-dev install for sl/sloop/loops binaries: 'uv tool install --force --editable /Users/kaygee/Code/loops'. The monorepo root pyproject.toml IS the strange-loops package definition (name=strange-loops, v0.3.1) and registers all three entry points. --editable uses .pth indirection so live source edits propagate to all three binaries without reinstall. Prior workflow (uv tool install ./apps/loops only registered the 'loops' entry point, leaving sl/sloop pointing at the old strange-loops snapshot from github.com/kgruel/strange-loops). Trace 2026-05-16: the sl split was just an editable-vs-snapshot install mismatch, not a structural problem \\u2014 strange-loops repo and this monorepo share git history via origin's multi-push (gitlab+github). Verified: sl emit --help now shows --strict and -q flags; live receipt path works through all three binaries.\", \"_ts\": 1778946207.594331, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fold-merge-default\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-merge-default\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16: fold-by-key semantic changes from REPLACE to MERGE for all upsert folds. Existing _make_upsert at atoms/engine.py:96-101 does total replacement (state[target][key_value] = entry). New behavior: state[target][key_value] = {**existing, **entry}. Rationale: replace-style was a silent-loss bug masquerading as design \\u2014 every 'refined' or 'resolved' re-emit silently dropped any field not re-supplied. Today's evidence: my 14:50 refined emit on emit-as-append-or-modify overwrote Kyle's 14:38 original message; original framing exists only in fact-history, not fold. With merge as default, the runbook's 're-emit to update status' practice works correctly (fields persist). The patch-emit friction dissolves into this one-line change \\u2014 no new 'sl patch' subcommand needed; plain emit with subset payload IS the patch. Trade-off acknowledged: can no longer 'unset by omission' \\u2014 explicit clear sentinel needed (field=) when that operation surfaces (not blocking; no current workflow needs it). Implementation: 1-line change at atoms/engine.py:_make_upsert + test sweep (test_upsert_inserts_and_updates and siblings) + new merge-assertion tests. Hits every fold-by kind across the codebase \\u2014 load-bearing commit on its own. Connects to receipt work: receipts now surface patch-needs in-moment; this commit makes those needs cheap to satisfy.\", \"_ts\": 1778948529.555485, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"design/trace-implementation-plan\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Verdict 2026-05-16 \\u2014 design locked, implementation deferred to next session. Trace = top-level verb 'sl trace kind/key' (git log analog). KEY DISSOLUTION: FoldState.source_facts already exists (populated by vertex_fold(retain_facts=True)) and IS the fetch_item_lifecycle primitive \\u2014 trace is mostly wiring, not new fetch infrastructure. Resolved design questions: (1) top-level verb + --lens trace for composition; (2) default same-key lifecycle, --refs one hop, --depth N recurses; (3) syntax kind/key (slash, matching entity-ref code); (4) wrap stream_view not rewrite (inherit golden tests + zoom tiers); (5) ASC ordering (changelog-style, oldest first) not git log DESC \\u2014 right for single-node lifecycle reading; (6) --diff MVP (field-delta lines like 'status: open \\u2192 refined') because fold-merge makes each fact a patch; (7) cross-vertex via --all opt-in, default local; (8) inbound refs + --graph are v2. Scope: ~600 LOC across 7 files (fetch_trace+walk_refs ~150, lenses/trace.py ~140, _run_trace ~70, tests ~250). One-session work post-orientation. Subtlety to document: under fold-merge, FoldItem.refs is the UNION across upserts \\u2014 --refs walks lifetime ref set, not per-fact refs (per-fact is v2 if asked). Friction cleanup post-ship: lineage-view-missing resolves directly. Future changelog entries may be partially auto-generated via 'sl trace --since 7d --kind decision'. Picks up: read this decision + thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster + friction:lineage-view-missing.\", \"_ts\": 1778956207.459571, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape-adapter\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape-adapter\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Orientation finding (re-emit; prior observation/<no-fold> orphaned \\u2014 project vertex doesn't declare observation kind, my emit-discipline gap not a tooling gap; receipt warned correctly): source_facts entries are FLAT payloads with metadata under-prefixed (_ts, _observer, _origin, _id) at vertex_reader.py:911-918,925. stream_view consumes NESTED fact-dict shape (f['kind'], f['ts'], f['observer'], f['payload'], f['id']). Decision: adapt at fetch_trace boundary (~10 LOC unflattener) rather than reshape source_facts in engine. Rationale: source_facts shape is engine-internal contract optimized for spec.replay() consumption; the adapter is the consumer-side boundary. Decouples lens API from engine internals. Cost is documented at one site (the adapter) with a comment noting shape provenance. Doesn't break the dissolution argument from design plan \\u2014 wrap is mostly wiring, with ~10 LOC of explicit shape translation.\", \"_ts\": 1778956857.932834, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/declare-observation-on-project-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/declare-observation-on-project-vertex\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Added 'observation { fold { items \\\"by\\\" \\\"topic\\\" } }' to .loops/project.vertex. Trigger: my emit of observation/implementation/trace-source-facts-shape this session was silently orphaned (receipt warned correctly, but no fold-side capture). Kyle: 'we should just include it in the vertex so this doesn't keep happening' \\u2014 structural gap, not discipline gap. Runbook lists observation as a legitimate intent ('note something true, no prescription') with topic= as fold key; vertex didn't declare it. Side-effect surfaced: 30+ prior observations were already in the store, orphaned in the same way \\u2014 single-line declaration retroactively recovered the full backlog into the fold (practice/, pattern/, observation/, convergence/, ungrouped namespaces all now visible). Rationale-trail: the fix-once-structurally pattern is right here \\u2014 the alternative (police every emit) doesn't scale and fails exactly the way mine failed today. Pairs with the runbook's vertex-is-editable principle. Fold key choice: topic= matches decision/cite conventions and aligns with how observations were already being authored. Receipt did its job; structural gap was the issue. emit-receipt-on-write (commit 5846478) ensured this surfaced in-moment instead of post-hoc \\u2014 the receipt + vertex-edit together close the loop.\", \"_ts\": 1778956940.678572, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"implementation/fetch-fold-preserves-source-facts-on-filter\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/fetch-fold-preserves-source-facts-on-filter\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Bug found + fixed during Phase 1 (fetch_trace) smoke test: fetch_fold with key= filter rebuilt FoldState without source_facts (line 119 only passed sections+vertex). Made retain_facts=True silently useless when combined with --key \\u2014 exactly the path fetch_trace uses. Fix: preserve source_facts on filtered FoldState, scoped to surviving items (kind/key_value membership in filtered sections). Bonus: also drops source_facts for filtered-OUT items (prevents data leak from filter). Discovered via 0-fact result on smoke test; identified by printing source_facts keys and seeing empty dict despite retain_facts=True. Design-plan subtlety-note about FoldItem.refs being a UNION across upserts gestured at fold-merge interactions but didn't catch this specific filter-strip case \\u2014 note now extends: filter operations must preserve retain_facts payload too. One-shot fix at apps/loops/src/loops/commands/fetch.py:104-130. No new tests yet (Phase 7); manual smoke confirms ASC ordering on multi-fact thread (3-fact patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster lifecycle renders open\\u2192open\\u2192partial as expected).\", \"_ts\": 1778957109.813585, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Phase 4 design verdict: --diff renders cumulative replay (option b), not per-fact snapshots (option a). Diff is computed against IMMEDIATE-PRIOR fact's accumulated state, not full N-fact replay \\u2014 matches changelog reading ('what's new since the last entry') and is simpler to implement. Rendering rules: (1) first fact: 'field: . \\u2192 value' for each payload field (everything's new); (2) scalars where payload[k] differs from accumulated prior: 'field: old \\u2192 new'; (3) refs (list-valued): set diff against prior \\u2014 '+added, -removed' lines; (4) unchanged scalars: DROP from render (they're the noise --diff exists to filter); (5) fields ABSENT from this fact's payload: not rendered (fold-merge means omission = preserve, not clear \\u2014 so 'didn't change' not 'removed'); (6) message field special-cased: always show with \\u2192 prefix even if not strictly diffable, because it carries the author's commentary. Implementation locality: diff computation lives in trace.py lens (pure render-side transform of fact list). fetch_trace stays unchanged. Plumbing: _run_trace adds --diff flag, injects data['_diff']=True into fetched result; trace_view branches on _diff key. Field-removed case (omit + clear sentinel) is v2 if/when explicit-clear lands per fold-merge-default decision.\", \"_ts\": 1778959695.201672, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"thread:trace-diff-rendering-shape\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Phase 6 of the trace arc (--all cross-vertex) DISSOLVES into engine combine-source_facts support. Original design plan: '--all opt-in, default local' implied a separate flag to widen the trace across vertices. Actual shape after engine fix: the combine/discover aggregator vertex ALREADY provides cross-vertex semantics (transparent over child stores); once retain_facts populates source_facts through that path (engine commit pending), the existing combine vertex IS the cross-vertex trace target. From cwd, .loops/.vertex aggregates project + docs; 'sl trace thread/foo' walks the aggregator and surfaces facts from any child store. No --all flag needed. Discriminator that revealed the dissolution: the friction-guard message ('try sl trace <vertex> kind/key') stopped being useful \\u2014 there was no asymmetric case left. Pattern: a planned feature dissolves when its precondition (combine-retain_facts) is lifted; the substrate already does what the consumer-side flag was meant to. Phase 6 marked complete via this dissolution. Inbound refs (--graph) and per-fact refs (vs lifetime union) remain v2 per original plan.\", \"_ts\": 1778962940.327346, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"friction:trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"design/repo-owns-loops-discipline-lenses\": {\"topic\": \"design/repo-owns-loops-discipline-lenses\", \"message\": \"2026-05-16: session_landing.py + reconcile.py moved from ~/.config/loops/lenses/ to <repo>/.loops/lenses/, with symlinks back at original paths. Rationale: these lenses encode loops-the-project's session discipline (NOW/TOUCHED/UNPACK, staleness reconciliation) \\u2014 not generic config. The asymmetry of repo-orthogonal lenses for a project that ships loops-the-CLI was the smell. Resolution path: .loops/lenses/ is vertex-local (priority 1) for .loops/project.vertex specifically \\u2014 exactly the vertex that consumes session_landing. The symlinks at ~/.config/loops/lenses/ keep cross-repo resolution working via user-global tier (priority 3) for gruel.network etc. Verified both paths produce identical session_landing output. Active dependencies only: docs.py, readiness.py, state.py, session_start.py, comms.py left at ~/.config/loops/lenses/ \\u2014 zero or doc-only active invocations. identity_prompt.py left at ~/.config/loops/identity/lenses/ \\u2014 user-level identity rendering by design. Initial emit had path as <repo>/lenses/; corrected to .loops/lenses/ per Kyle \\u2014 co-locating with the vertex it serves, not at repo root.\", \"_ts\": 1778975519.252418, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\"]}, \"design/deliberation-depth-lens\": {\"topic\": \"design/deliberation-depth-lens\", \"message\": \"Calibration tightened post-advisor-driven re-inspection. Manual inspection of the 3 hypothesis-kind chains the lens flagged as SUSPICIOUS revealed all were legitimate fast empirical work (truncation: 2 experimental runs with numerical results; title-only: designed falsifier with cluster-overlap measurements). The Alcove signal is closed-without-prediction, not closed-fast. Criterion tightened: SUSPICIOUS = closed AND emit_count<=1 AND not-batch. HEALTHY = closed AND (multi-emit OR cross-session). Final calibration: hypothesis SUS=0/HEALTHY=4 (zero false positives, four genuine deliberation cases), thread SUS=6/HEALTHY=95 (six retrospective-observations-as-threads correctly flagged). The lens now earns its position \\u2014 it surfaces real catches without crying wolf. Pattern instance: lens-as-application-of-its-own-purpose \\u2014 advisor's catch was 'verify the output is actionable' which I'd skipped after seeing the buckets arithmetic. Running the SUSPICIOUS list through manual inspection IS the lens's intended workflow; doing it on my own output surfaced the calibration miss. The pre-check discipline (practice/recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check) generalized: pre-check whether the LENS ACTUALLY DETECTS WHAT IT WAS BUILT TO DETECT before declaring done.\", \"_ts\": 1778976818.757514, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"paradigm/suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check\", \"practice/read-path-features-over-noticing-skills\", \"thread:deliberation-depth-lens-build\"]}, \"architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"DECISION 2026-05-16: SqliteStore id generation uses python-ulid (str(ULID())) \\u2014 pure-Python, no C extension, time-sortable, 26-char Crockford base32. CHOSEN OVER (a) uuid.uuid7() stdlib \\u2014 would match the post-regression uuid4 string shape and visually blend the wedge into the future; we explicitly DON'T want that (the wedge is a discrete bug-class era and should remain visible); (b) sqlite-ulid C extension \\u2014 answers a question we no longer ask (SQL-side id generation via DEFAULT). When the regression moved id gen from SQL-side DEFAULT (ulid()) to Python-side _gen_id() it ALSO removed the architectural need for a SQL-callable ulid() function; the extension's only remaining advantage is per-id gen cost (0.35\\u03bcs vs 2.3\\u03bcs) which is dominated by file I/O on emit anyway. PROPERTIES re-derived from use case: (1) globally unique across machines/processes/peers \\u2014 required for cross-store merge dedup via INSERT OR IGNORE on PK; (2) time-sortable lexicographically \\u2014 required for chronological fact interleaving across stores and for ORDER BY id semantics; (3) cheap to generate \\u2014 emit path opens/closes connection per invocation, but the dominant cost is SQLite open not id gen; (4) content-addressing NOT required \\u2014 same fact emitted to two stores legitimately gets two different ids (merge dedup is per-fact identity, not per-content); (5) replayable \\u2014 store is durable, ids must survive forever. python-ulid satisfies (1)-(5) cleanly. WITHIN-MS MONOTONICITY CAVEAT: python-ulid's default ULID() constructor generates fresh random suffix per call \\u2014 NOT monotonic within a millisecond. Fine for uniqueness and dedup; means ORDER BY id within the same ms is random across calls in the same process. If we ever need within-ms monotonicity, python-ulid offers monotonic helpers; not needed today. CONTINUITY: matches the pre-Mar-15 id format already in existing stores, so post-fix ids visually continuous with the original ULID era; the 2026-03-15 to fix-date uuid4 wedge stands out as discrete. RATIONALE-FOR-RATIONALE: this decision exists in part because the 2026-03-15 regression happened WITHOUT a decision of record naming why ULID was chosen \\u2014 only a comment in code citing 'merge compatibility with libs/store' which the perf optimization read past. Naming the substrate properties as a decision means the next optimizer reads the rationale before swapping the implementation.\", \"_ts\": 1778990260.024111, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\": {\"topic\": \"design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Trace removed entirely; read absorbs trace via four cuts. (1) --refs [N] unifies fetch-walk + render-decoration: bare --refs walks depth 1 and decorates edges (\\u2190 inbound, \\u2192 outbound) per item; --refs N walks N hops; omitted = no walk no decoration. Drops the prior render-side filter behavior \\u2014 orphan items render with (no refs) marker rather than disappearing. (2) Positional kind/key on read: sl read project decision/design/foo parses as --kind decision --key design/foo. --kind/--key flags retained as backstop. (3) --diff lands on read: cumulative field-deltas rendering (status: old \\u2192 new, refs: +added -removed per emit) moves from trace lens into read dispatch. Solves the single unique capability trace had beyond read. (4) Render shape is graph-decorated, not chronologically-interleaved (trace was). Anchored entity renders with full body + edge list underneath; ref-walked entities render below the anchor with \\u2504 via \\u2190 kind/key \\u2504 markers identifying how each came in; depth-2+ nests under depth-1 parents with \\u21b3 prefix + indent; cycles back to already-rendered items dim rather than re-render. Dissolution: no rename of old read --refs (visibility toggle) needed \\u2014 unified --refs semantic supersedes it. Trace command deleted, not deprecated (no external ship). Arcs-block.py hook becomes one-line swap (sl trace \\u2192 sl read with --diff). Cut sequence: emit decision (this) \\u2192 unify --refs (parser + drop filter + port walk semantics from fetch_trace into fetch_fold) \\u2192 land graph-decorated render \\u2192 positional kind/key on read \\u2192 --diff on read (move lens) \\u2192 delete trace command + update hook \\u2192 CHANGELOG.\", \"_ts\": 1779032249.737675, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:trace-refs-no-visual-marker\", \"thread:refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\", \"thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\"]}, \"atoms/walked-items-as-foldstate-extension\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/walked-items-as-foldstate-extension\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"A2 of trace-dissolution: FoldState gains a parallel walked: tuple[WalkedItem, ...] field. Decision: separate the walked entities from primary sections rather than mutating FoldItem or hacking section.kind. RATIONALE: (a) FoldItem is widely consumed by lenses (prompt, gist, fold-view, painted record_line, etc.) \\u2014 adding _via_anchor/_depth metadata bleeds into all of them and risks walked items being rendered as primary by lenses that do not check the metadata; (b) hacking section.kind to \\\"walked-from-X\\\" breaks kind-based dispatch in every lens consumer; (c) per-anchor map (dict[anchor, list]) loses iteration order and requires the lens to maintain anchor\\u2192items joins. The flat parallel tuple is opt-in: lenses that ignore .walked keep working unchanged; lenses that render the walk look at it explicitly. SHAPE: WalkedItem(item: FoldItem, section_kind: str, via_anchor: str, via_direction: str = \\\"outbound\\\", depth: int = 1). Default direction outbound (A2 walks ref= forward only \\u2014 inbound walk deferred until evidence shows it is needed). depth=1 for direct refs of any primary anchor, depth=2 for refs-of-refs, etc. via_anchor is the kind/key address of the entity whose ref pulled this in (for depth=2, this is a depth-1 entity, not the original primary anchor \\u2014 preserves the lineage chain for the \\u21b3 nesting render). CYCLES: walked entities whose address (section_kind/key) already appears in the primary sections are not added to walked (avoid rendering the anchor twice). Walked entities that point back to other already-walked entities can dim or omit per render policy. BACK-COMPAT: FoldState.walked defaults to empty tuple \\u2014 no fetch path is required to populate it; only fetch_fold(refs_depth>0) will. All existing consumers ignore .walked unchanged.\", \"_ts\": 1779037814.209304, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: chose Option 2 (clean siftd-shape Operation IR) for cli refactor. Each view owns single argparse parser; no painted.run_cli; cli/dispatch.py owns action+static+live+interactive branches directly. cli/output.py is the SINGLE painted-boundary module (mirrors siftd/output/painted_bridge.py discipline). New owned surface ~150-200 lines (fidelity.py ~30, live.py ~20, dispatch.py ~100) vs ~700 lines of run_cli callback wrapping. Goldens not gating per-commit \\u2014 reviewed end-of-arc (step 7) with painted-truncation-everywhere friction explicitly in scope. Sized via direct siftd code inspection: cli/_common.py:60-100 fidelity_from_args ~30 lines; cli/data.py:1030-1070 LIVE mode ~20 lines; zero unified mode-resolution layer (per-view). Positions loops for painted framework/renderer split (separate arc) without further loops-side changes. Plan file: ~/.config/claude/plans/dreamy-dazzling-scroll.md\", \"_ts\": 1779045624.981251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:operation-ir-adoption\", \"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\", \"thread:operator-ir-from-siftd-status\"]}, \"workflow/subtask-handoff-via-plan-appendix\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/subtask-handoff-via-plan-appendix\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: when delegating multi-step refactor work to a Subtask worker, the plan file IS the brief. Add a 'Handoff for Subtask worker' appendix to the plan with: per-step verification gates, decision authority (emit decisions, don't block on approval), pitfalls discovered during the planning/Step-0 work (e.g. painted-lazy-getattr pyright issue, lazy-argparse module scope, re-export pattern), reference file:line refs per step, what NOT to do (e.g. step 7 = sit-down review only), and what to do if stuck (emit friction/thread, surface in checkpoint, don't push through). Pattern works because worker has plan + Step 0 commit as concrete anchor + thread for narrative + decision-emit authority for nontrivial calls. Tested on cli-refactor-architecture arc 2026-05-17.\", \"_ts\": 1779046383.316627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\"]}, \"architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: painted detached from monorepo. Submodule libs/painted removed; working copy moved to ~/Code/painted (multi-push: github.com/kgruel/painted + git.gruel.network/gruel/painted). Monorepo consumes painted as PyPI versioned dep (painted>=0.1.8 in root pyproject; workspace member + workspace source entries removed from root and apps/{hlab,loops,tasks}). painted 0.1.8 published to PyPI as part of this arc. RATIONALE: reverses the 2026-04-26 'standalone retired, painted lives at libs/painted as submodule' move. Painted is now an external lib loops consumes, not a monorepo lib. Maximum separation: co-dev requires version bump + republish cycle. Local override during iteration via 'uv pip install -e ~/Code/painted' if needed. COST acknowledged: every painted-side change loops depends on requires publish + dep-floor-bump. BENEFIT: painted is a real external package, evolves on its own cadence; monorepo coherence boundary is tighter; vouch/other external consumers of painted (when they arrive) pull from the same PyPI source loops does. Migration verified: 1090 loops tests pass + 1378 painted standalone tests pass + hlab/tasks import OK + 'sl read project' round-trips after 'uv tool install . -e --force' (the tool venv reinstall is load-bearing \\u2014 old venv had painted wired as workspace editable pointing at deleted libs/painted).\", \"_ts\": 1779047503.854479, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: dispatch.py:109 \\u2014 when an action command's fn returns an int, dispatch surfaces it as the process exit code (return result). Legacy cmd_* functions in commands/ already return int exit codes (0/1/2); the Operation IR honors that contract. Action-shape Operation (render_lens=None) flow: fn() \\u2192 if int, return; else show(value). Rationale: backward-compat with N callers in commands/ that signal failure via non-zero return; no rewriting needed during the cli refactor. Worker (cli-refactor subtask) emitted this in worktree but worktree-local store was freed at merge; re-emitting on canonical store with attribution. Verified by reading dispatch.py:97-115.\", \"_ts\": 1779049298.877176, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\"]}, \"design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: cli/views/fold.py (NEW path) has no fast-path branch; the ~15ms savings _run_fold_fast bought (bypassing painted.cli import for --static --plain) traded for a single dispatch path. Rationale: dual-path complexity was THE source of yesterday's growing-edge 'exercising-catches-coherence-gaps' (4 bugs in one session, all 'works in path A, silently breaks in path B'). Trading 15ms cold-start for an asymmetric-pair bug class we keep finding is a clear win. Note: main.py:_run_fold (legacy) still has the fast-path branch at line 684, but it's no longer routed to (registry sends read\\u2192views/read.py\\u2192views/fold.py). Dead-code cleanup is a follow-up. Worker emitted in worktree; lost to per-worktree store; re-emitting on canonical store.\", \"_ts\": 1779049304.970501, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: scope of the strange-loops monorepo narrowed. The repo carries code (libs/, apps/) + public docs (ARCHITECTURE.md, STRANGE-LOOPS.md, CHANGELOG.md, CLAUDE.md, etc.) + build config. Per-clone working state \\u2014 vertex declarations (.loops/), Claude Code hooks/agents/settings (.claude/), experimental inquiries (experiments/), cross-cutting design notes (meta-discussion/), personal essays (docs/dev/) \\u2014 is gitignored. RATIONALE: (a) painted is now external (PyPI), other consumers (vouch etc.) landing \\u2014 tighter coherence boundary matters; (b) personal state was 80MB+ of accumulated vertex content + binary db blobs (meta.db, discord.db slipped past *.db rule); (c) fresh clones get the library not Kyle's accumulated state. IMPLEMENTATION: see commits 9562843 (untrack-personal-state, 276 files / 50518 deletions), 707c558 (painted-detach), d952a2d (CLAUDE.md split). DOWNSTREAM EFFECTS: (1) fresh-clone bootstrap requires loops init project; documented in CLAUDE.md; (2) subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free dissolved as side-effect \\u2014 worktrees no longer carry .loops/, so emissions route via aggregation-combine to canonical store; (3) CLAUDE.md split into public + gitignored docs/dev/RUNBOOK.md so bilateral protocol stays personal while operational grammar stays public.\", \"_ts\": 1779050247.38887, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\"]}, \"workflow/claude-md-public-vs-bilateral-runbook-split\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/claude-md-public-vs-bilateral-runbook-split\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17: CLAUDE.md split by audience. Public tracked CLAUDE.md = repo-facing onboarding: paradigm pointers, build/test, structure, fresh-clone bootstrap, the loops vertex operational grammar (kind selection, topic-prefix discipline, emit timing, emit-with-graph-fidelity, read-path navigation, emit syntax). Useful to any Claude Code session on the repo, including future contributors. Gitignored docs/dev/RUNBOOK.md = bilateral protocol: Kyle's hard-stop rule (48h emission + 7d reconcile), my reciprocal commitments, hook handling, anchored-by-incident notes (cite-atrophy diagnosis, recursion-pull-pre-check, painted publish workflow). KEY CHOICE POINT: the bilateral runbook content doesn't need to be auto-loaded for every session. Operational grammar is enough for any worker to know HOW and WHEN to emit. The bilateral accountability framing belongs in per-task briefs when relevant, not in shared project context. Verified mid-session: cli-refactor worker had the operational grammar (via base-commit CLAUDE.md before split) and did emit 2 decisions \\u2014 proving the grammar suffices. WATCH-FOR (next sessions): if future workers don't reach for emit primitives at the right moments, that's evidence the public CLAUDE.md needs a 'Working in this repo' sub-section that surfaces the discipline (without the Kyle:/loops-claude: addressing). Current position: per-task brief is the right vector for urgency.\", \"_ts\": 1779050257.634683, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/monorepo-scope-code-and-public-docs-only\"]}, \"design/vertex-splice-strategy\": {\"topic\": \"design/vertex-splice-strategy\", \"message\": \"Phase 0 grounding outcome for plan:vertex-living-document. STRATEGY: surgical line-based splice, extending the existing kdl_insert_with_row pattern in libs/lang/src/lang/population.py \\u2014 NOT a greenfield AST\\u2192KDL serializer. Pure-canonical re-emit rejected: 36 live vertex files use line comments (//) pervasively; canonical re-emit would lose every comment. CORPUS CHARACTERISTICS (36 live .vertex files surveyed across ~/.config/loops, .loops, meta-discussion, apps): line comments only (no block /* */, no triple-quoted, no escaped quotes); standard KDL constructs (bare-arg nodes, property syntax key=value, multi-arg nodes, block-child nodes, nested blocks); inconsistent indentation between hand-written files (2 vs 4 spaces) \\u2014 must preserve, not canonicalize; one inline semicolon-separated multi-statement seen (autoresearch.vertex:36 \\\"items collect 50; n count\\\"); numeric args (collect 0/20/50); glob patterns in strings; scope \\\"observer\\\" maps to VertexFile.observer_scoped (one usage: identity); run \\\"...\\\" child nodes on boundaries (two usages). AST COVERAGE: comprehensive \\u2014 every observed construct maps to an AST node (VertexFile + LoopDef + FoldOp + Boundary + CombineEntry + ObserverDecl + LensDecl + SourcesBlock + TemplateSource). Only lossy field: comments \\u2014 which surgical splice preserves by design. EXISTING SPLICE PATTERN: kdl_insert_with_row uses splitlines + brace-depth tracking via _find_template_block to locate spans, _detect_indent for indentation, line insertion/removal. 8 tests. Generalizes cleanly to other block types (loops, combine, observers, sources) and other child shapes (kind declarations, vertex entries, observer entries). PHASE 1 SCOPE (revised down): generalize _find_template_block into kdl_find_block(text, path: list[str]); add kdl_insert_child(text, parent_path, child_text) and kdl_remove_child(text, parent_path, child_name, child_key?); reuse _detect_indent. Round-trip tests: parse-then-write should be byte-identical for all 36 corpus files (no-op edit). Mutation tests: insert/remove a kind block, observer, combine entry \\u2014 verify parseable result + expected AST shape. ~100-150 LOC + tests, not a greenfield serializer. TEST CORPUS: the 36 live .vertex files themselves (no synthetic fixtures needed).\", \"_ts\": 1779057908.597455, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-ls-generalization\", \"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase0-vertex-corpus-survey\"]}, \"design/sub-namespace-under-add\": {\"topic\": \"design/sub-namespace-under-add\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Phase 2 verb-collision resolution. Decision: 'loops add <vertex> <subcommand>' shape with explicit subcommand keyword (kind | observer | combine | row). Rationale (Kyle's framing): lists are in KDL too, so 'add' uniformly means 'add an entity to a vertex' and the subcommand specifies WHICH entity-shape. Reads consistently: add row to population, add kind to loops block, add observer to observers block, add combine entry to combine block. Bare-positional 'loops add reading X Y' preserved as implicit row for back-compat; Phase 3 will retire it alongside the rss-era surface. Rejected alternatives: (a) flag-driven disambiguation on 'add' (--kind X vs positional X Y) \\u2014 brittle to typos like --kibd silently falling through to row mode; (b) new verb 'declare' or 'def' \\u2014 clean but creates two verbs for the same conceptual operation (extending the vertex). The chosen shape generalizes to Phase 3+ when more subcommands land (template, sources, lens, boundary).\", \"_ts\": 1779060173.69619, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"rendering/refs-out-of-diff\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/refs-out-of-diff\", \"message\": \"--diff renders scalar state evolution; refs are not state. Refs are per-fact immutable attribution that the fold UNIONS across emits \\u2014 an emit can attach refs but can never detach a prior emit's refs. Prior code computed set-difference between adjacent facts and rendered phantom '-X' removals when emit N+1 didn't re-cite emit N's refs. The 'accumulated_refs' was misnamed (reassigned per fact, actually 'prior fact's refs'). Fix: strip ref handling from --diff entirely. --refs is the canonical view for refs. Ref-only emits render '(refs only \\u2014 see --refs)' so the lifecycle event remains visible. This is the 4th site of the write-receipt-vs-temporal-query confusion the lens caught at three sites 2026-04-29 (set_topic, vouch_chain, fold returning vertex-state). Same shape, rendering layer.\", \"_ts\": 1779105124.647803, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"identity:practice/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"message\": \"MINIMAL renders the index ('what's in here?') at different cardinality regimes via two branches: (1) namespace breakdown when keys span \\u22652 groups (root firehose orientation: 'design/ (187) architecture/ (82) ...'); (2) one-label-per-line key list otherwise (single-namespace post-narrowing OR flat-key kinds like cite). For by-fold key lists, shared namespace prefix is stripped to match SUMMARY-mode grouped rendering. For collect-fold, label is _first_field(payload). The prior renderer was one-trick (breakdown only) and returned Block.empty in degenerate cases \\u2014 three real failures: 'X/ (N)' tautology after --key narrowing, blank section on flat-key kinds (cite), and silent loss on single-namespace floods. The two-branch shape preserves the firehose property while making degenerate cases honest. Anchored by friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys + advisor reframe from gate-fix to renderer-fix (third pass).\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.476532, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\"]}, \"rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"message\": \"--facts joins -q/-v/-vv as a loudness signal that disables auto-zoom. Rationale: --facts requests MORE per item (compression history, fact lineage, n counts); auto-zoom-DOWN to MINIMAL renders LESS (or nothing) per item. Direct contradiction \\u2014 orthogonal-in-spec, anti-orthogonal-in-effect. --refs/--plain/--json remain truly orthogonal (visibility/format, not loudness). The classification: explicit content-requesting flags disable auto-zoom-DOWN. Patch at apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/fold.py \\u2014 auto_zoom gate adds 'and not args.facts'. Anchored by friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.565263, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\"]}, \"design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\": {\"topic\": \"design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-19: The accumulate declaration named here as a dissolution candidate has no ground at the user layer. ref is already reserved/consumed by the fold engine (engine.py unions it into _refs across upserts via _make_upsert/_make_collect). No new spec property is needed. The _is_diff_skip predicate in trace.py (replacing _DIFF_SKIP_FIELDS frozenset) captures the structural distinction cleanly: _* keys are internal fold-derived fields never present in raw fact payload; ref is raw user input consumed by the fold before reaching folded state. Traced and anchored with test_fact_payload_never_contains_column_fields. The accumulate dissolution is confirmed \\u2014 the property doesn't exist at the declarable layer.\", \"_ts\": 1779206757.668577, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\", \"decision:rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\", \"friction:auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\", \"friction:thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\"]}, \"design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\": {\"topic\": \"design/emit-stdin-file-as-call-site-convention\", \"message\": \"Stdin/file expansion for emit ships as explicit flags: --stdin FIELD (read sys.stdin into named field, TTY-guarded, single trailing newline stripped) and --file FIELD=PATH (action=append for multiples, ~ expanded, single trailing newline stripped). NOT inline magic syntax (=- / =@path) and NOT per-kind declaration (no prose_fields on LoopDef). Rationale: (1) Layer separation \\u2014 the feature is call-site-semantic (user decides per invocation), not kind-semantic (vertex author decides per kind), so it does not belong in vertex declarations. See observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator. (2) Inline magic syntax collides with legitimate @-bearing values \\u2014 verified empirically that topic=foo@example.com and topic=https://user:pass@host/path store literally today. The @@ escape tax would apply to every email/URL going forward. Not vanishing-rare. (3) Explicit flags match loops house style (--strict, --quiet, --dry-run, --observer) \\u2014 explicit-over-implicit. Three pivots arrived here: hardcode message= \\u2192 declaration-driven via prose_fields \\u2192 universal magic syntax \\u2192 explicit flags. Each pivot dissolved more structure; final form has ZERO ast/loader/engine/atoms/vertex-file changes. Pure CLI-layer feature, ~40 LOC helper + ~80 LOC tests. Error model: multiple --stdin \\u2192 error (one stdin source); --stdin with TTY \\u2192 error; --file with nonexistent path \\u2192 error; field appears both in parts AND via --stdin/--file \\u2192 error (conflicting sources, ambiguous intent).\", \"_ts\": 1779225032.755711, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\", \"observation:pattern/loops-field-role-family\", \"observation:practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"thread:stdin-message-for-emit\"]}, \"pattern/foo\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.989638, \"_n\": 2}, \"design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\": {\"topic\": \"design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"message\": \"2026-05-19 session close: do NOT propagate colon convention through the write-side resolver to complete the May-16 trace migration. The migration is real and the gap is real, but the right shape depends on whether refs become typed (hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass). If typed, the colon-vs-slash choice becomes arbitrary at the serialization boundary and only one of the two paths needs to be supported as the canonical wire form. If we propagate colon now, then later land typed-refs, we'll have done convention-migration work twice. Cost of waiting: today's fold-key skip (commit 33937f6) stays as cosmetic workaround for one symptom; receipt continues to miscount canonical refs. Acceptable for one decision-cycle. Reversal trigger: a) typed-refs lands and chooses a wire form, or b) typed-refs is rejected as a design direction (then propagate colon as originally scoped).\", \"_ts\": 1779244328.036914, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Agent compiles an immutable execution manifest; human signs the manifest; infrastructure executes \\u2014 agent is courier, never operator. The signed thing IS the compiled intent, not a capability grant. Reframes vouch flow: discovery (low-risk broad read) \\u2192 compile (agent produces deterministic payload) \\u2192 attestation (peer signs exact payload) \\u2192 execution (infra replays signed payload). Surfaced via Gemini exchange 2026-05-20; Kyle pulled it out as the load-bearing reframe. Maps onto sign-on-emit/verify-on-receive: the 'execution manifest' IS a Fact with specific kind; signature IS the attestation; execution boundary triggers on attested-fact existence in scope. Reframes multi-endpoint problem \\u2014 target service doesn't expose N privileged endpoints to untrusted agents; it exposes a single 'execute-attested-fact' boundary that reads payload from the signed fact body. This is the loops-paradigm answer to the enterprise-IAM Registry pattern: facts \\u2192 boundary \\u2192 execution, with attestation as the gate. Industry drafts (Prakash/AIP) building inline runtime proxies with regex filters get dissolved by this framing \\u2014 once the agent is a compiler not an operator, there's nothing on the wire to babysit. The threat surface compresses to (a) discovery-phase read exfiltration, still open, and (b) compile-time argument injection between human-review and infrastructure-execution, closed by signature-binds-exact-payload.\", \"_ts\": 1779297591.812005, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\"]}, \"paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/audience-distinct-from-authorization\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Who is allowed to RECEIVE what a service emits is a different question from who is allowed to ACT against that service. Collapsing both into 'authorization' loses the distinction. The agent-as-compiler model closes act-side cleanly (signature binds exact payload, infra replays signed manifest, agent never holds active credential). It does NOT close receive-side: during discovery phase the agent reads via authorized API calls and the output flows into LLM context \\u2014 if agent is compromised mid-discovery, the data exfiltration vector is open even though no write-side authorization is violated. Surfaced via Gemini exchange 2026-05-20 where Gemini wallpapered the read-side exfiltration gap with 'don't grant raw DB access' (true but evasive \\u2014 API-mediated reads still leak whatever the API returns). Maps onto Phase 1 vocab walk \\u2014 'audience' was one of the four words still to walk (alongside principal, rescission, transport). This is the audience axis: act-side = who can invoke; receive-side = who can be told. Vouch design must address both, not conflate. Implication for libs/sign + libs/vouch: signature on an emission proves provenance (act-side); audience-scoping on a fact's visibility is a separate primitive (receive-side) that probably belongs in engine emit/receive flow rather than libs/sign. Discriminator for future design: when a vouch question lands, ask 'is this about who can act or who can receive?' before choosing primitives.\", \"_ts\": 1779297632.25403, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"thread:vouch-lib-conceptual-reground\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\": {\"topic\": \"design/vouch-act-side-libssign-plus-l4\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision: vouch act-side = libs/sign canonical-bytes primitive + an L4 binding discipline. Answers the owed libs/sign-primitive-surface question. libs/sign signs canonical bytes (consumable by loops-engine AND Java, no loops deps); the L4 discipline is that those bytes ARE a compiled byte-deterministic execution artifact \\u2014 not a scope/claim. Governance = byte-equality, no LLM between sign and execute. Wire = base Transaction Tokens (WG draft) carrying the manifest hash; vouch differentiates from the individual txtokens-for-agents draft, which binds tctx params not execution. Full landscape derivation + 4-level binding-target-spectrum lives in the agent-attestation vertex (sl read agent-attestation).\", \"_ts\": 1779561634.09839, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:paradigm/agent-as-compiler-not-operator\", \"thread:vouch-substrate-session-owed\"]}, \"design/signature-vs-body-resolved-by-binding-level\": {\"topic\": \"design/signature-vs-body-resolved-by-binding-level\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Decision (resolves the open question in three-layer-auth-composition): signature-proves-emission vs signature-proves-responsibility was a false dichotomy \\u2014 they are different LEVELS, not competitors. Fact.signature over a compiled manifest = binds execution (L4); BODY act-chain (act=alice) = attributes responsibility (RFC8693 act-claim shape, L1-ish provenance). Both coexist: signature governs what executes, act-chain attributes who is responsible. Two independent derivations converged on this \\u2014 the binding-target-spectrum (agent-attestation vertex) and the MSFT-Entra grounding (agent-id distinct from principal-signature). High confidence.\", \"_ts\": 1779561634.227257, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\"]}, \"design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\", \"message\": \"Tick hash-chaining lives at the STORE layer, not the Tick atom (Kyle's call 2026-06-09, recommended option). Three columns on ticks table: prev_hash (sha256 of previous tick row's canonical bytes \\u2014 chains the sequence), fact_cursor (max fact ULID at tick time \\u2014 explicit id-based window boundary, not ts-inferred), window_hash (sha256 over canonical fact rows in (prev_cursor, cursor] in id order \\u2014 makes FACTS tamper-evident, the actual prize). Rationale: a chain is a property of the persisted sequence, not the snapshot; Tick atom stays pure, no API/serialization change; merge honestly breaks chains (new custody context = correct semantics). Dissolution: delta 1 of the provenance arc requires NO substrate/atom change \\u2014 pure store-layer property. Precedents followed: pre-chain rows stay NULL (era marker, uuid4-wedge posture); first chained tick's window starts at migration-time max id (epoch marker, no false coverage claims); canonicalization = sorted-compact JSON in one documented helper, NOT JCS \\u2014 chain needs determinism not interop; JCS stays pinned for federation-facing manifests (delta 2+). Verification walks ticks recomputing both hashes; facts after last tick are the honest uncovered live edge.\", \"feature\": \"provenance-chain\", \"_ts\": 1781033968.747377, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Delta 2 shape: signature column on EVERY tick row, computed in append_tick over the existing _tick_row_hash (which commits to prev_hash + window_hash, so each signature transitively covers everything behind it). No head-anchor artifact \\u2014 a separate head record is a mutable pointer wearing an anchor costume (write-receipt principle); the tick IS the commitment shape, the signature belongs on the commitment. Dissolves 'the head' as a special case: every tick self-verifying, head is just the newest. Pre-signature ticks render as era, never retro-claimed \\u2014 same move as delta 1's chain columns. Cost negligible at session-boundary cadence. Also the rehearsal for delta 3 (Fact.signature): same pattern one layer up, proven first where rows number ~200 not ~2000. Kyle's framing sharpened it: the decision is 'signing is structural from this point forward', not 'patch the head'. External witnessing (publish head hash outside the store) noted as a complement, not an alternative \\u2014 not this delta.\", \"_ts\": 1781036684.127505, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/observer-key-registry\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-key-registry\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: the signing-key registry is observer-name \\u2192 public key, NOT Peer.key (corrects vocabulary drift in the May decisions \\u2014 engine/peer.py documents Peer as 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant'; Observer is the base identity primitive). The vertex registers its own name as an observer at bootstrap, keypair generated then; tick signing uses that private key; verify_chain extends to check tick signatures against the registry. Scripts/services/sources are observers like any other \\u2014 keyable by the same mechanism, no taxonomy of principal-kinds. Kyle ratified the signer (vertex machinery signs, since it generates the tick) and the layering: identity (observer+key) / authorization (Grant) / relationship (Peer, at the exchange edge, untouched until delta 4). Open sub-question tracked separately: whether 'Peer' remains the name for the exchange-edge bundle.\", \"_ts\": 1781038744.687339, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"observation:design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\"]}, \"design/peer-as-exchange-edge-relation\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-as-exchange-edge-relation\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: Peer keeps the name, retires the framing. The 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant' header line goes \\u2014 Peer is the exchange-edge relation: observer (name+key) + exchange policy (Grant) + transport + trust config, minted only when a custody boundary is crossed. Discriminator: if no custody boundary is crossed, nothing is a Peer \\u2014 local delegation is Observer + Grant directly (delegate() is hierarchy, not peerage). Both senses of 'peer' (networking endpoint, social standing) converge at the edge; the misfit only existed because the old bundle covered local cases too. Rejected alternative: Principal \\u2014 names the identity (Observer's seat, already taken) not the relation, and imports OAuth frame against vocabulary-as-sibling-layers. Falsifiable prediction that sold it: Peer entries appear only in PAIRS of stores \\u2014 if vertex A holds a Peer entry for B's observer, B holds one for A's, because exchange is what minted them. A one-sided Peer entry that isn't a half-configured exchange falsifies the vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1781038893.750549, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-key-registry\", \"observation:design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\"]}, \"design/tick-key-custody-colocated\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Ratified: private key lives at .loops/keys/ next to the store it signs \\u2014 custody co-located, matching delta 1 semantics exactly (slice/merge strip chain \\u2192 new custody context \\u2192 key dies with the store's home). Chosen over ~/.config/loops/keys/ name-indirection; honesty over the committed-key failure mode, which is mitigated structurally: loops init owns gitignoring the keys directory as part of bootstrap (convenience is the mitigation, not discipline). Public key: observer declaration in the .vertex grows a key field (inline base64, ~44 chars) \\u2014 the registry IS the vertex file, sl add project observer already the declarable. Algorithm: Ed25519 (deterministic per RFC 8032 \\u2014 right property for tamper-evidence; RSA-PSS randomized; JWT layer was wrong shape anyway, detached-digest-signature is a new sign surface either way). Domain-separation prefix loops-tick-v1: baked in from the start. Primitive in libs/sign (new module, load_or_generate pattern). Engine boundary: INJECTION not import \\u2014 append_tick takes optional signer callable, verify_chain takes optional key-lookup, apps/loops composes; preserves no-cross-lib-imports, makes progressive policy structural (no signer = legacy era), and answers May's vouch lib-boundary question by the same pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1781039301.270981, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-key-registry\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\"]}, \"design/tick-signature-in-chain-envelope\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signature-in-chain-envelope\", \"message\": \"Kyle's call 2026-06-09 (recommended option): the successor tick's prev_hash commits to its predecessor's SIGNATURE via an era-aware envelope \\u2014 _tick_row_hash includes a signature key only when the column is non-NULL, so pre-chain and pre-signature rows hash byte-identically to delta 1 (full back-compat, no re-anchoring). Construction: signature signs the 10-field commitment hash (sign-the-content); the row-identity hash that successors chain over includes the signature (chain-over-content+signature) \\u2014 standard two-hash construction, avoids circularity. Consequence: selective signature-strip breaks the successor's prev_hash and escalates to full-cascade forgery; era-monotonicity rule (unsigned chained tick after a signed one = break) catches the head-strip case. Residual boundary both options share: TOTAL rewrite is indistinguishable from legacy era \\u2014 anchored only by the registry in the .vertex (outside the store) and future external witnessing; store verify flags declared-key-but-zero-signed-ticks as the cross-artifact tripwire. This fork was the one consequence the evening design session didn't walk.\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"_ts\": 1781041521.327972, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"design/chain-witness-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/chain-witness-order\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Chain ordering authority is witness order (rowid), never id order. Window cursors stay fact ids (portable handles); membership and hashing resolve cursor->rowid and walk append order. append_tick cursor = id of newest fact BY ROWID, not MAX(id). Fixes mixed-id-era vacuous windows (uuid4 era sorts above all ULIDs, pinning MAX(id) mid-history forever) AND late-arrival false alarms (backfilled fact with honest old event-ts landed inside a sealed id-window = tamper alarm caused by truthfulness; in witness order it lands on live edge, sealed by next tick as received-now). Deliberate semantics flip pinned in tests: backdated-id arrival is no longer a break; displacing a covered row's rowid is. ULID keeps its job \\u2014 event order for the read path. Already-minted epoch tick still verifies (empty window hashes identically under both orderings). Known interim consequence on mixed stores: project epoch cursor resolves to rowid 1121/2019, so the NEXT tick seals ~900 pre-epoch facts as-of-seal-time \\u2014 strictly more protection but coverage does not distinguish sealed-since-receipt from sealed-late; rebirth-with-receipt supersedes.\", \"_ts\": 1781045731.815431, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\", \"observation:design/event-order-vs-witness-order\"]}, \"x\": {\"topic\": \"x\", \"message\": \"w\", \"_ts\": 1781461048.08514, \"_n\": 4}, \"design/seal-verb\": {\"topic\": \"design/seal-verb\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"sl seal <vertex> -m reason: the deliberately drawn attestation boundary. Dissolves into existing machinery \\u2014 emit kind=seal + vertex-declared boundary when=seal; no engine or lang changes. The observer driver from boundaries-as-driven-conditions rides the fact-stream: volition enters as a fact. The reason fact is the LAST fact inside the window it seals (attestation covers its own justification; fact_cursor == reason fact id, verified live on tick 3). Must-fire semantics: seal refuses when the writable vertex declares no seal boundary; declared match props fold into the payload. Session close DISSOLVES INTO seal (Kyle's call): project.vertex boundary is now when=seal, SessionEnd hook emits session bookkeeping fact then sl seal \\u2014 session close is an instance of the general act, not the special case. Use cases unlocked: post-backfill attestation, pre-surgery checkpoint, chord-carving, peer attestation point (store-side analog of vouch transaction endorsement \\u2014 bind at the boundary). Rebirth/replay-to-store composes as: transform-replay + old-ticks-as-facts + receipt-fact + seal.\", \"_ts\": 1781049410.969004, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/boundaries-as-driven-conditions\", \"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"thread:manual-tick-emission\"]}, \"design/attestation-envelope-read-path\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-envelope-read-path\", \"message\": \"Attestation envelope surfaces via two existing homes, no new command. (1) verify -v: verify_chain gains include_ticks returning per-tick detail (era, sig validity, window fact count, cursor deref) \\u2014 data the walk already computes, now kept instead of discarded. (2) TickWindow gains attestation fields (chained, signed, fact_cursor, cursor_kind, cursor_preview) filled by StoreReader.ticks_between(with_envelope=True); drill-down header renders them. Boundary choice with rationale: envelope stays OFF engine.Tick \\u2014 a Tick is the produced snapshot; chain link and signature are witness-era metadata added at append. The stored-and-witnessed tick is a different claim than the tick itself; TickWindow is the consumer shape for stored ticks, so attestation belongs there. Combined/aggregation vertices return empty envelopes \\u2014 attestation is per-store; an aggregate does not attest.\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_ts\": 1781053027.128573, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\"]}, \"design/rebirth-implementation-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/rebirth-implementation-shape\", \"message\": \"rebirth_store lands in libs/store as sibling of slice/merge. Shape: (1) _expected_rows is the shared spine \\u2014 rebirth writes what it returns, verify_rebirth diffs against it; same function, write then check, so the receipt claim and its verification cannot drift. (2) Genesis tick minted through engine.SqliteStore.append_tick \\u2014 chain logic single-sourced, prev_row-None path gives window_start='' covering all rows including the receipt; fact_cursor lands on the receipt (seal semantics: attestation covers its own justification). (3) Receipt carries source_content_sha256 (witness-order row hash, the verifiable claim) AND source_file_sha256 (forensic bytes-at-moment) \\u2014 file hash alone false-alarms under WAL checkpoint/VACUUM. (4) engine exports tick_row_hash publicly: the receipt's chain-head claim uses THE chain's hash function, not a reimplementation. (5) Old tick envelopes re-enter verbatim as tick.<name> facts \\u2014 old signatures verify against original bytes; old-to-new cursor mapping recomputable from the deterministic transform, never stored. (6) Transforms: identity, ulid-migration (canonical-form rule covering all three id eras), filtered (rule string must describe predicate; verify requires the original Transform). Interleave deferred explicitly \\u2014 merge-shaped, different arity. CLI: loops store rebirth, signing composed from SOURCE vertex custody (the new incarnation is the lineage's next chapter). Live-fired on project.db: 2049 facts, 1791 migrated, re-run diff clean, chain intact, genesis signed.\", \"_ts\": 1781059758.498401, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"observation:design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\", \"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\": {\"topic\": \"ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\", \"feature\": \"rebirth-with-receipt\", \"message\": \"Retirement posture for pre-rebirth incarnations: archive in-place at <store-dir>/data/archive/<name>.pre-rebirth-<date>.db, NOT next to keys, NOT cold storage. Rationale: the old incarnation is evidence backing the rebirth receipt (verify --check re-runs the transform against the SOURCE) \\u2014 it must stay reachable at a path the receipt era can find, and data/archive keeps custody co-located with the store it witnesses. Keys dir stays keys-only (custody material, gitignored as a unit); mixing dbs in muddies the gitignore ownership init claims. Cold storage breaks --check casually. Belt-and-braces session backup also taken at ~/loops-store-backups/2026-06-12/ but that's operator habit, not the posture.\", \"_ts\": 1781276741.318987, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/archive-form-seal-and-move\": {\"topic\": \"ops/archive-form-seal-and-move\", \"ops\": \"loops-config\", \"message\": \"Retired vertices archive as SEAL + MOVE: surviving stores get a rebirth (rule=identity) on retirement \\u2014 sealed genesis + receipt fact records counts, source hash, closing moment \\u2014 then vertex+data move to ~/.config/loops/archive/<name>/ with the .vertex renamed .vertex.archived so the root discover glob (./**/*.vertex) skips them. Reference reads stay possible by explicit path; --check verifies any seal against its retained .pre-seal.db source. Archiving is an attested act, not a file move \\u2014 the same machinery as the swap ceremony, pointed at endings. Non-protocol dbs (feeds, reactions \\u2014 no id column) and already-lost stores (ambient/homelab/realestate/system, orphan wal only) move unsealed with README notes.\", \"_ts\": 1781278194.371792, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/store-retirement-archive-next-to-data\", \"thread:config-population-cleanup\"]}, \"ops/signing-era-full-live-core\": {\"topic\": \"ops/signing-era-full-live-core\", \"ops\": \"loops-config\", \"message\": \"The whole live core enters the signing era on the rebirth date (2026-06-12), not store-by-store as consumers appear. Per-custody-context keypairs (vertex_dir/keys), self-observer registration via sl add <v> observer --key, boundary when=seal + seal kind declared on every live vertex, first signed tick minted by an entry seal. Result: project, agent-attestation, session, identity, comms/discord, comms/native all verify signed against their registries. Custody nuance made explicit: keys are PER DIRECTORY not per store \\u2014 repo project and agent-attestation share .loops/keys with distinct observer names; one custody context, one key.\", \"_ts\": 1781278194.6059, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\"]}, \"ops/keygen-via-add-observer\": {\"topic\": \"ops/keygen-via-add-observer\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"The signing-era entry verb for an EXISTING vertex is sl add <v> observer <name> --keygen \\u2014 not a new keygen command and not init --upgrade. Dissolution: add observer --key already existed; only the keygen half was missing. Implementation: ensure_signing_key(vertex_path) extracted to commands/signing.py (keygen + gitignore ownership ride together \\u2014 custody creation is signing's domain), init._bootstrap_signing and add --keygen both call it; --keygen mutually exclusive with --key; --key validation stays pre-resolution (pinned by test_malformed_key_rejected_before_splice); receipt prints the keys dir path. Resolves the manual python-keygen sequence from the config-store upgrade. Remaining manual step deliberately NOT absorbed: boundary when=seal + seal kind declarations \\u2014 that is seal opt-in, sl seal's error hint covers it.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.840127, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"observation:ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\"]}, \"design/fold-off-type-skip-with-counter\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-off-type-skip-with-counter\", \"feature\": \"oracle-bug-fixes\", \"message\": \"R2 RESOLVED (Kyle, 2026-06-12): an off-type value in a numeric fold (Sum/Avg/Min/Max/TopN-by) is SKIPPED \\u2014 no state mutation, Avg denominator untouched \\u2014 and recorded in a deterministic {target}_rejected counter in fold state. Bool is off-type (Python bool-is-int silently folded true as 1). Latest joins the rule: missing _ts rejects, NEVER falls back to time.time() (replay determinism). Missing field stays silent-skip (absence is not an error); off-type presence is. Errors-as-state over errors-as-facts: visible in every snapshot, zero new machinery, no write-on-read, forward-compatible with an error-fact layer later. Chosen over error-fact-at-engine-funnel (heavier, M4-level) and silent-skip-Go-parity (invisible failures contradict robustness=visibility). PROTOCOL-LEVEL: loops-go must implement the same rule + counter; vectors should include bool, numeric-string, and missing-_ts cases. Implemented in atoms/engine.py (_is_number/_reject), pinned by libs/atoms/tests/test_fold_rejection.py.\", \"_ts\": 1781282100.518379, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\", \"thread:python-bugs-from-go-oracle\"]}, \"design/fold-replay-order-event-time\": {\"topic\": \"design/fold-replay-order-event-time\", \"feature\": \"oracle-bug-fixes\", \"message\": \"Two orders, two authorities \\u2014 the dissolution that resolves the oracle's merge-non-commutativity finding without touching chain-witness-order: FOLD REPLAY orders by (ts, id) \\u2014 event order, store-independent total order \\u2014 so merge(A,B) and merge(B,A) re-fold identically; WITNESS ORDER (rowid) remains the chain/window/attestation authority \\u2014 merge directions ARE different custody events and their chains legitimately differ. Changed sites: SqliteStore.since/since_raw/replay_cursor + latest_by_kind(_where) (ts,id); store_reader facts_by_kind + resolve_entity_id (fixes ref-time rowid-blindness, H4); vertex_reader combined-read sort key (ts,id) \\u2014 its own NOTE had documented the tie nondeterminism; merge.py INSERT..SELECT ORDER BY ts,id (was unordered scan). Tick/window/chain paths untouched: append_tick, window hashing, _window_facts, FTS cursors all stay rowid. since_raw/replay_cursor now also inject _ts (SELECT gains ts) and Vertex.receive injects _ts on the live path \\u2014 Latest folds get the same envelope everywhere. Post-rebirth id==event order makes (ts,id) and id-alone agree above ms resolution; (ts,id) chosen because it is also correct for un-reborn mixed-era stores (the H4 general rule). Pinned by TestMergeFoldCommutativity.\", \"_ts\": 1781282100.82644, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"thread:python-bugs-from-go-oracle\"]}, \"practice/reroute-log-sweep-reconcile\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reroute-log-sweep-reconcile\", \"message\": \"ADOPTED 2026-06-12 (Kyle ratified, same conversation as the thread): three-tier capture-and-review. (1) REROUTE LOG \\u2014 zero-ceremony one-liner into the existing log kind (collect 20) at the moment of routing around anything; no naming/status/fold-key, which is precisely what makes it fire against flow pressure. (2) SWEEP \\u2014 fast cadence, every session wrap, before the seal: scan session log entries, promote repeat patterns to friction with proper ceremony, update thread statuses, emit the session arc. Name chosen over 'retro' (baggage): the sweep precedes the seal, fits the vocabulary. (3) RECONCILE \\u2014 slow cadence, own scheduled sessions (weekly-ish): reconcile lens + friction backlog + stale threads + structural fit; promoted to first-class work. Pricing rationale: silent-reroute cost is an externality (local flow saving, global later cost) \\u2014 fix by making capture cheaper than the reroute, not by discipline. MECHANISM: Stop hook .claude/hooks/turn-capture.py backstops in-the-moment noticing (the thing that demonstrably fails) \\u2014 fires the capture question once per substantive turn (>=3 tool calls), stop_hook_active-guarded, conversational turns exempt. Runbook updated (CLAUDE.md Principles + Review cadence section). Escalation path if log under-captures: siftd revival \\u2014 transcript reading surfaces reroutes without agent cooperation.\", \"_ts\": 1781286854.904273, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:reroute-capture-practice\"]}, \"design/fact-signature-at-store-column\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signature-at-store-column\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Fact signature lives as a facts.signature column, NOT a Fact atom field. Kyle ratified 2026-06-12. Rationale: exact delta-2 posture \\u2014 atoms stay pure, signer injected at store construction, envelope crosses atoms boundary only as read-side view fields. Commitment is content-only: sha256(canonical({kind,ts,payload,observer,origin})), excluding id/rowid \\u2014 store-assigned identity is custody context, not authored content. This is what makes the signature transport-stable: a receiving store re-derives the commitment from the row and verifies against the observer registry without trusting the sender. Tick chain attests receipt (store-local); fact signature attests authorship (travels). Domain: loops-fact-v1 at the composing layer.\", \"_ts\": 1781288277.329636, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Fact signatures are per-observer authorship claims, Kyle ratified 2026-06-12. Signer callable is (observer, digest) -> sig|None; key layout .loops/keys/<observer>/ed25519.key; verify maps fact.observer -> registry pubkey (the add-observer --key/--keygen registry from delta 2 already IS this mapping). Observers without keys emit unsigned \\u2014 honest NULL becomes a PER-OBSERVER era, generalizing delta 2's per-store epoch. Layering note: this composes with shipped tick signing rather than replacing it \\u2014 unsigned-author facts still sit under the vertex-key-signed window hash (custody claim); signed-author facts carry both claims. Custody honesty: on a single machine any local process can read any key in .loops/keys/, so observer separation is organizational not adversarial until keys live with their principals (transport/peer era). Companion mechanism: _fact_row_hash goes era-aware (includes signature only when non-NULL) so signature-stripping breaks the sealed window \\u2014 delta-2 envelope trick, no re-anchoring of pre-signature rows.\", \"_ts\": 1781288396.372022, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signature-at-store-column\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/authorship-vs-delegation-layering\": {\"topic\": \"design/authorship-vs-delegation-layering\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Each principal mints their own fact-signing key; delegation is NOT encoded in fact signatures. Kyle's lean, confirmed 2026-06-12 at live keygen (kyle + kyle/loops-claude on project and identity). Rationale: the fact signature makes exactly one claim \\u2014 authorship of content (identity domain). On-behalf-of is a second claim (authority domain) with its own primitive: act-chains / OBO / endorsements, vouch's L4 territory. Folding delegation into the signature is the write-receipt temptation again \\u2014 thickening a primitive to carry a claim it cannot make honestly; the carve-out rule says add a separate primitive when the combined claim is live. Forward-compatible: observer name kyle/loops-claude NAMES the delegation by convention today; the future act-chain ATTESTS what the slash only spells \\u2014 nothing to migrate, layers compose on stable per-principal authorship. Custody honesty: same-machine keys mean organizational not adversarial separation; kyle's signature currently attests 'session that could load kyle's key' until his custody moves to him (vouch custody story).\", \"_ts\": 1781292368.255793, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\": {\"topic\": \"design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-12: attestation-layer canonical bytes upgrade from implementation-local json.dumps to JCS RFC 8785, with chain re-anchor now while chains are days old (rebirth machinery just proven; re-anchor cost at lifetime minimum, grows per seal). Trigger: the Go oracle reading the chain IS the federation-facing consumer the _canonical_bytes docstring named as the upgrade condition. Aligns with the JCS pin already chosen at the vouch/manifest layer. Concrete divergences closed: ensure_ascii escaping vs raw UTF-8, float shortest-repr edge cases. Payload TEXT stays embedded verbatim (string value) \\u2014 byte-tamper detection without re-serialization, unchanged. Implies Python-side work: _canonical_bytes JCS impl + re-anchor ceremony, tracked separately.\", \"feature\": \"loops-go\", \"_ts\": 1781299087.379547, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:head-anchoring-as-external-witness\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"ops/jcs-reanchor-ceremony\": {\"topic\": \"ops/jcs-reanchor-ceremony\", \"message\": \"CEREMONY CLOSED 2026-06-12: all five live signed stores re-anchored under JCS and verified \\u2014 project (71 facts re-signed incl. the ceremony-open fact itself, 3 ticks, head d17307c9...), identity (1 fact, 2 ticks), session, comms/discord, comms/native (chain-only). Every store verifies chain-intact + signatures-checked against registry post-reanchor. Era boundaries held everywhere: pre-signature facts stayed NULL, legacy ticks untouched. The \\u00a78.7 conformance vectors are now unblocked \\u2014 Python is on JCS, the bytes the vectors pin are the normative ones. Dry-run artifact cleaned.\", \"_ts\": 1781301744.639793, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\"]}, \"design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-13: DEFER the fact-signing require-on-emit gate AND verify-on-receive to the transport/peer era; make DISCLOSURE honest first. Dissolution reasoning: require-on-emit with no verify-on-receive buys only a locally-complete ledger so verify/disclosure can claim all-post-era-keyed-facts-signed \\u2014 enforcement in service of disclosure, not of a receiver; no untrusted cross-store receive path exists yet, so build the gate when something is on the other side of it. Counter weighed and overridden for facts: the tick-side delta-2 posture (signing is structural from this point forward) would extend down to facts for a clean-from-here ledger that makes eventual verify-on-receive cheap; rejected now because the clean-ledger benefit is disclosure-facing and achievable instead by honest disclosure of the opportunistic reality, and fact-signing is per-observer/opportunistic vs ticks vertex-self-signed at a single funnel. Net: signing stays opportunistic-on-emit + audit-on-demand (store verify); the require/verify layer reactivates when transport/peer gives verify-on-receive a consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1781385216.954705, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"observation:implementation/signing-enforcement-status\"]}, \"design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\": {\"topic\": \"design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"message\": \"Kyle ratified 2026-06-14 (Gate-B floor): once a store starts signing at the TICK level, it must continue \\u2014 the era-regression guard (no unsigned tick after a signed tick) is a non-negotiable FLOOR, not a per-vertex flag. Rationale: era-monotonicity is witness-chain INTEGRITY, not vertex POLICY \\u2014 verify already condemns the regressed state (CHAIN BROKEN) and reanchor already refuses to create it; seal must match (closes the say/do gap where seal could mint exactly what verify forbids). Friction is low in the SSH sense: the private key is local, so signing is transparent/automatic while present; the cost only appears when the key is ABSENT, and then the right behavior is SSH's \\u2014 a hard STOP, never a silent downgrade to unauthenticated. So seal REFUSES (not warn-and-proceed) to mint an unsigned tick in the signed era. Degrades gracefully: emit stays opportunistic so the window's FACTS are still stored; only the attestation boundary (tick) is withheld, and the next successful seal closes the accumulated window \\u2014 data preserved, attestation deferred, never falsified. Disclosure is the floor under all of it: every signing action states signed/unsigned + reason regardless of the refuse/proceed branch. Distinct from the still-deferred FACT-signing require gate (decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred): facts stay opportunistic (mixed signed/unsigned is normal, live edge strippable); only TICKS take the structural floor, matching the delta-2 \\\"signing is structural from this point forward\\\" posture. The forward-policy \\\"require signing\\\" vertex flag (Gate A) remains a SEPARATE, optional, default-off knob \\u2014 it governs whether a vertex must sign AT ALL (the first signature, optionally facts), not whether it may stop. Open forward work: the transport era breaks the \\\"key is always local\\\" assumption \\u2014 see thread:transport-era-signing-key-flow.\", \"_ts\": 1781457866.835805, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"design/next-release-0.4.0\": {\"topic\": \"design/next-release-0.4.0\", \"message\": \"Release-delta audit (workflow, 9 agents; loops v0.3.1..HEAD = 78 unreleased commits) \\u2192 next loops release is 0.4.0. Pre-1.0 minor carries breaking (mirrors painted 0.1.8\\u21920.2.0). The range is one coherent arc: the federated attestation substrate (tick hash chains, Ed25519 tick + per-observer fact signing, JCS/RFC 8785 canon, store verify/rebirth/reanchor, sl seal + the era-floor) plus the cli-refactor and read-path overhaul. Breaking surface is broad and PERSISTED, which rules patch out as dishonest: store schema +6 attestation columns and dropped ulid() default (id-supplied-at-INSERT); .vertex gained observers{key} + keys/ custody dirs; fold upsert flipped replace\\u2192merge across every by-fold kind; row ordering \\u2192(ts,id); Latest + numeric folds reject-not-coerce; dep swap sqlite-ulid\\u2192python-ulid + new rfc8785; JCS canon invalidates prior attestations until reanchor. Only the root pyproject version bumps (libs are not independently versioned). Full changelog draft + readiness + rebuild map live in docs/dev/rebuild-audit-0.4.0.md. THE GATE for tagging (gates the release AND the rebuild): the painted pin is uncapped (>=0.1.8) so fresh installs ALREADY pull 0.2.0 \\u2014 loops must be validated against painted 0.2.0 first. Import-compat is verified clean (every deep path resolves; loops uses none of the removed names); behavior under 0.2.0's exact-width contract + the absence of goldens for the new lenses (trace/declarations/preview/walked) is unvalidated.\", \"_ts\": 1781468830.498302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"test/gate-results-painted-020\": {\"topic\": \"test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"message\": \"THE GATE run (painted 0.1.8->0.2.0, root pyproject bumped to >=0.2.0,<0.3, uv sync clean). RESULTS: (1) loops suite 1327 passed + 1 xfailed, ZERO golden drift \\u2014 the framework bump did not break any loops rendering. Strong signal: loops' run_cli/lens path is forward-compatible with 0.2.0. (2) test_readiness_lens collection error = ORPHANED test (the 'readiness' lens source was dissolved; module gone since after 3c9d26b) \\u2014 pre-existing, painted-independent; delete the test. (3) test_dashboard x7 in apps/TASKS = REAL painted-0.2.0 API drift, NOT pre-existing: CliContext.__init__() no longer accepts 'zoom' kwarg (signature changed in 0.2.0). The audit's 'illustrative' call was WRONG on these. This drift lands squarely on the rebuild KEYSTONE (the two CliContext classes must reconcile). loops escaped it only because loops constructs CliContext via run_cli, not directly; tasks constructs it directly in tests.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"_ts\": 1781474351.634264, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/cli-context-keystone-shape\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-context-keystone-shape\", \"message\": \"Gate made the CliContext keystone concrete. The two classes are NOT near-duplicates to merge \\u2014 they carry ORTHOGONAL concerns sharing a name. painted-0.2.0 CliContext = (fidelity, mode, use_ansi, is_tty, width, height): terminal/rendering state (note zoom->fidelity rename is the exact drift that broke tasks). loops CliContext (loops/cli/context.py) = (reporter, vertex_path, vertex_name, observer): dispatch/domain state. The rebuild's 'loops CliContext becomes a thin extension of painted.cli.CliContext' is therefore COMPOSITION not unification: loops' domain fields wrap/hold a painted render-context, they don't flatten into one constructor. Confirms keystone-first sequencing: reconcile by composition before touching dispatch. tasks' x7 failures are the canary \\u2014 they'll be fixed by the same reconciliation (s/zoom=/fidelity=/ at minimum, or routing through the composed context).\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781474375.91534, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/cli-context-phase-split\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-context-phase-split\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED step 1 (keystone). Renamed loops CliContext->Invocation (context.py->invocation.py, commit 8040bd4). The two same-named contexts were different PHASES: Invocation=domain (vertex/observer/signer/store, lives in dispatch+fetch); painted's CliContext=render (fidelity/width/is_tty, lives in render call). They never co-occur in one call, so the rename dissolves the ambiguity rather than merging anything. No behavioral change: 1327 loops green, zero golden drift, sl binary smoke-tested on both IR (read/fold) and legacy-shim (store) paths. Discovery while grounding: commands/ shims read ctx.zoom/ctx.is_tty but loops Invocation has no such fields \\u2014 those ctx are painted's, and ctx.zoom survives 0.2.0 as a blessed property (not compat shim), which is why the gate passed clean. Unblocks steps 2-7.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781477055.186374, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-context-keystone-shape\", \"decision:test/gate-results-painted-020\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/full-painted-integration-residue\": {\"topic\": \"design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED step 3 pilot (commit bc22491). read/fold view drops fidelity_from_args: add_cli_args+parse_zoom+parse_fidelity now own the pure-terminal axes (-q/-v depth, --plain/--json format, --static/--live/-i mode, --max-chars/-lines budgets). Domain-query selectors (--facts/--diff/--refs N) stay loops-side, visibility merged into the painted Fidelity. Behavior-preserving (1327 green, zero golden drift; sl verified across all axes). LANDSCAPE FINDING: read is the SOLE fidelity_from_args consumer \\u2014 the other display surfaces (store/ticks/stream/devtools) already route fidelity through painted run_cli, so their dissolution is step-4 shim-unification, not step-3. fidelity.py/fidelity_from_args now has zero live callers in the IR path; candidate for deletion once nothing references it.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"_ts\": 1781481547.896491, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-context-phase-split\", \"decision:design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"ops/release-0.4.0\": {\"topic\": \"ops/release-0.4.0\", \"message\": \"0.4.0 fully released. PyPI publish DONE via GitHub trusted publishing (OIDC, environment:pypi, .github/workflows/release.yml fires on release:published \\u2014 NOT on bare tag push). Sequence that worked: git tag+push -> gh release create v0.4.0 -> workflow build+publish (run 27514185875, \\u2713 22s, digital attestations) -> strange-loops 0.4.0 live on PyPI (verified 200 at /0.4.0/json). CORRECTION to prior emit: local 'uv publish' was the WRONG path \\u2014 ~/.pypirc token is painted-scoped (403 for strange-loops); no local token needed, the release workflow uses trusted publishing. RUNBOOK note for future loops releases: do NOT uv publish locally; create a GitHub Release from the tag and the pipeline handles it. Visualizer = fast-follow after the cli/render rebuild (Kyle's call). Painted gets worked in parallel per docs/dev/painted-0.3.0-commission.md.\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"ops\": \"release\", \"_ts\": 1781476531.874921, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\": {\"topic\": \"design/disclosure-vs-domain-query-axis\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"message\": \"COHERENCE FINDING reframing rebuild step 3. The design doc (rebuild-design-0.4.0.md \\u00a71) assumed loops' --facts/--refs/--diff dissolve into painted Tags gated by ctx.fidelity.shows(). Grounding in fold.py disproves it: all three are DOMAIN-QUERY SELECTORS, not disclosure layers. --diff selects a different fetcher (_build_diff_fetch + trace lens); --facts toggles want_facts (folded vs raw stream); --refs N carries a traversal DEPTH into fetch (painted's store_true Tag can't model the N). painted's Tag model assumes fixed data revealed in named layers; loops' flags change the query itself. So the real dissolution boundary: PURE TERMINAL axes (-q/-v depth, --max-chars/-lines budgets, --plain/--json format, --static/--live/-i mode) dissolve into painted add_cli_args+parse_fidelity; DOMAIN-QUERY selectors (--facts/--diff/--refs) stay loops-side (they parameterize fetch). This follows directly from grow-painted-over-workaround + 'push loops into domain-specific arenas' (Kyle): query selection IS domain, not terminal. Step 3 revised: dissolve the generic terminal flags per view; keep domain flags; merge their loops-computed visibility into the painted-compiled Fidelity.\", \"_ts\": 1781481044.543767, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\", \"observation:practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\"]}, \"design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\": {\"topic\": \"design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\", \"message\": \"A2: build painted's field-budget allocator as a stable painted.core.compose primitive NOW, minimal surface (fields,width,min_field,sep -> fitted text + dropped-count). Badge [+Nc] and empty-field fallback stay loops-side; commit to allocation contract not presentation. RATIONALE: clears the AUTO/Fill bar (real external PyPI consumer + general nameable contract + wcwidth fix is strictly better than loops' len()-buggy _render_preview copy). Painted's load-bearing premise accepted: a private symbol an external version-pinned consumer imports is de-facto public, so 'private-until-2nd-consumer' middle path doesn't exist -> clean either/or. GATE on the name: dissolution-test budget_fields vs resolve_column_widths; if allocation math is shared (columns-vs-fields framing only) it's ONE primitive two consumers not two stable names; if sep-cost + shrink-then-drop-below-MIN is genuinely distinct from column distribution, two names honest. Placement-independent signature forecloses nothing. This is the substrate for rebuild step5 (re-ground lenses, delete hand truncation).\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"_ts\": 1781544228.308609, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Step-4 devtools (test/compile/validate) conversion: delete hand-rolled -h interception, let run_cli own help via add_args(parser). Command args (files/--input/--limit) registered ONCE into run_cli's parser; their parsed values captured for fetch via the build_fidelity hook closure (the only run_cli callback that sees the Namespace today). Exit-code semantics preserved (validate returns 1 on errors/no-files) because we stay on the run_cli path, NOT the Operation/dispatch STATIC path (which always returns 0 \\u2014 would lose validate's exit code). BRIDGE not endpoint: when painted ships CliContext.args/fetch(ctx) (thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam), the build_fidelity capture collapses to ctx.args read. Chose run_cli-stays over full-Operation-IR for devtools precisely because these carry pass/fail exit codes the dispatch STATIC path doesn't thread.\", \"_ts\": 1781546313.570171, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam\"]}, \"design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 780659d (step 4, first cut). Devtools trio (test/compile/validate) hand-rolled -h interception deleted; run_cli owns help via add_args. Bridge: build_fidelity namespace-capture for validate/compile; test keeps inherent pre-parse (branches on --input pre-dispatch). Stayed on run_cli path not Operation/dispatch IR \\u2014 devtools carry pass/fail exit codes (validate=1 on errors) that dispatch STATIC (always 0) would drop. 1327 green, zero golden drift. NEXT in step 4: store (the named wrinkle \\u2014 pre-parsed .db/.vertex positional + verify/rebirth/reanchor subcommands), now with the help-dissolve pattern proven on the easy surface first.\", \"_ts\": 1781546540.597015, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 621fdf2 (step 5 core). fold.py _render_preview + _truncate dissolved into painted.budget_fields; both preview-multi and fallback-single paths route through it; [+Nc] hint = fit.dropped. Contract adopted FRESH (min_field gates truncation not presence; wcwidth-measured). OUTCOME vs prediction: predicted goldens would drift (short whole fields reappear) \\u2014 they did NOT. Zero golden drift. The [+Nc] single-body goldens are byte-identical (ASCII wcwidth==len; fit.dropped == old hint math). The multi-field divergence is narrow: only 2 goldens use the preview path and none hit the sub-min-whole-field case. Covered by new test test_short_whole_trailing_field_kept instead. Kyle's parity-revert option is now moot \\u2014 adopting fresh cost nothing observable.\", \"_ts\": 1781551542.611614, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/painted-budget-fields-stable-now\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/devtools-help-args-idiom\": {\"topic\": \"design/devtools-help-args-idiom\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDES design/devtools-run-cli-args-bridge. The devtools (test/compile/validate) hand-rolled -h dissolves via painted 0.3.0's pre-parse + describe-for-help idiom: pre-parse the command's own args (argparse add_help=False), pass help_args=[HelpArg(name, desc, positional=)] to run_cli so --help lists them, fetch closes over the pre-parsed namespace. NOT the build_fidelity capture (that was the 0.2.0 bridge) and NOT the Operation/dispatch IR (devtools carry pass/fail exit codes dispatch STATIC drops). -h-vs-required-positional wrinkle: validate (nargs=*) lets -h reach run_cli freely; compile/test guard a required file, so a bare help request routes to run_cli's help renderer BEFORE the guard (help short-circuits pre-fetch). This is the proven pattern store inherits.\", \"_ts\": 1781550203.149721, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"thread:painted-run-cli-args-seam\"]}, \"design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-help-dissolve-shipped\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 443bdd6. store's 4 hand-rolled -h blocks dissolved. The named wrinkle (verify/rebirth/reanchor subcommands) was mostly redundant code: subcommand argparse parsers already had add_help=True, so parse_args owns -h natively \\u2014 deleted the explicit blocks + unused _sys. -h now raises argparse SystemExit(0), propagates clean to exit 0 through run_app (verified on real CLI). Base inspect uses the help_args idiom; subcommand roster moved to run_cli description so 'sl store -h' still surfaces them. The 'file fights painted arg0->handler' fear didn't materialize: store IS one painted handler, subcommand routing is internal to it (argv[0] check), painted never sees the subcommands. 1327 green, zero drift.\", \"_ts\": 1781550431.653525, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/devtools-help-args-idiom\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/record-line-dissolution-splits\": {\"topic\": \"design/record-line-dissolution-splits\", \"message\": \"Step5-large crux (same shape as step5-small first-half): audit row 7 lumped '_render_item_line / trace headers / stream rows -> record_line+PayloadLens' as ONE dissolution. It is TWO. record_line models a TIMESTAMPED EVENT RECORD (HH:MM [kind] summary + secondary-field continuations, payload via PayloadLens). (a) GENUINE: stream.py + trace.py per-fact rows ARE exactly this (ts+kind+payload) -> dissolve into record_line/record_line_composed + gutter_freshness/lifecycle + attention fns. (b) PARTIAL/loops-side: fold.py _render_item_line label is the KEY-FIELD value not the kind, and its badge (xN <-N ->N recency) is computed from FOLD STRUCTURE (item.n, inbound Counter, item.refs) with no PayloadLens home. record_line cannot host the fold badge; fold dedupes loops-side at best.\", \"_ts\": 1781553732.968458, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"design/stream-trace-record-line-shipped\", \"message\": \"SHIPPED 0805235 (step5-large, stream/trace half). stream_view dissolved onto painted.record_line; trace normal-path dissolves transitively (already delegated to stream_view); _render_diff stays loops-side (cumulative scalar-delta contract, not ts+kind+payload \\u2014 the trace analog of the fold badge). TWO contract conflicts hit + resolved: (1) width=None piped/no-truncation invariant -> grew painted 0.3.1 (record_line honors the natural-sizing escape Block.text already documents; record_line was the lone outlier). (2) DETAILED density: record_line shows only long/notable fields as continuation, short fields move to FULL; ADOPTED per Kyle's call (accept drift). Drift was MINIMAL+benign: test_log goldens regen (ISO ts at FULL, short fields->FULL, '\\u2026' truncation marker now signaled in CLI.md), one unit test split. Loops residue grafted cleanly: key_field summary via PayloadLens; id/observer/origin (non-payload) as continuation. 1325 green. OUTCOME vs pattern: same shape as step5-small + the original CLI-lens findings \\u2014 the pitched 1:1 dissolution was actually genuine-core + honest-residue; the painted boundary needed ONE backward-compat widening, not a loops fork.\", \"ops\": \"cli-render-rebuild\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"_ts\": 1781573902.17782, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/record-line-dissolution-splits\"]}, \"rendering/detailed-zoom-density\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/detailed-zoom-density\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"DETAILED zoom shows message-body over short secondary fields \\u2014 INTENTIONAL, confirmed at 2026-06-26 review. The step5 record_line dissolution swapped DETAILED's continuation content: GAINED full message: body (when long/notable per painted's ladder), LOST short per-kind fields (status:, files:). Trade accepted deliberately: for general log/stream reading, the message body is more useful than a one-word field. CONSEQUENCE accepted: trace --diff/lifecycle shows status transitions (open\\u2192active\\u2192resolved) only at FULL (-vv), not DETAILED. Reviewed the trace-lifecycle casualty explicitly (status is the diagnostic spine of --diff) and chose to keep status at FULL rather than special-casing lifecycle kinds at DETAILED. Goldens bless this correctly \\u2014 test_log_demo[DETAILED], test_trace_lifecycle[DETAILED/FULL]. DO NOT re-flag as regression; it is the design call. If trace-status-at-DETAILED ever becomes a real pain in use, the targeted fix (surface status only, for lifecycle kinds, at DETAILED) is the move \\u2014 not a blanket short-field revert.\", \"_ts\": 1782529970.028631, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"rendering/live-ctrlc-exit-zero\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/live-ctrlc-exit-zero\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"sl read --live (and -i) exits 0 on Ctrl-C, was 130 pre-rebuild \\u2014 ACCEPTED 2026-06-26. step6 deleted cli/live.py (run_live returned 130, UNIX SIGINT convention); the live path now folds onto painted run_cli(live_delivery='surface'), which catches KeyboardInterrupt and returns 0. Verified painted 0.4.1 STILL returns 0 (runner.py:435) \\u2014 so the bump does not change this; restoring 130 would require an upstream painted change to propagate the interrupt. DECISION: accept exit 0 for the interactive live view (pagers/TUIs conventionally exit clean on Ctrl-C; this is not a script failure). Not worth a painted change. Found by the 2026-06-26 pre-push review (med-severity confirmed). If a scripting use of --live ever needs 130, reopen as a painted feature request.\", \"_ts\": 1782530124.844632, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\"]}, \"rendering/verify-disclosure-grammar-axes\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/verify-disclosure-grammar-axes\", \"message\": \"sl store verify output rebuilt on painted 0.4.x callout/Severity (disclosure-grammar tier-1, items a-f). LANDED: (b) covered-vs-signed de-conflated into three labeled orthogonal axes \\u2014 chain (tick hash chain integrity), coverage (facts sealed under a tick window), authorship (per-fact signatures); all share /total_facts denominator so they stop reading as competing fractions. Verdict is the single SUCCESS/ERROR callout (glyph only where there's a real severity judgment); tripwires are WARNING callouts, breaks are ERROR callouts. DEFERRED: (c) tripwire severity stays WARNING pending thread:verify-strip-vs-presigning-detection. Tests: 'fact signatures: N signed'\\u2192'authorship N/T facts signed', 'checked'\\u2192'verified against registry' for chain axis; CHAIN BROKEN/FACT SIGNATURES BROKEN/window_hash preserved. 1339 green.\", \"_ts\": 1782533178.895623, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:block-text-multiline-passthrough-broke-on-040\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"design/read-becomes-navigate-at-scale\": {\"topic\": \"design/read-becomes-navigate-at-scale\", \"message\": \"Center of gravity for the ground-up CLI redesign (Kyles call, 2026-06-27): interactive read path. At 2547 facts, reads overloaded flags (--refs/--diff/--key/--lens reconcile/--ticks) are coping mechanisms bolted onto a static print model; they dissolve into navigation affordances ([r]/[d]/filter_prefix/fuzzy) inside a painted Surface. Interactive = top rung of the existing fidelity ladder (-q/default/-v/-vv), NOT a new verb or separate app: grow the tier, static stays pipe/agent default. Verbs stay a clean small algebra (read/emit + lifecycle ring cite/close/seal/sync + admin store); redesign targets the read path.\", \"_ts\": 1782572396.477573, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/interactive-read-path-tree-drill\": {\"topic\": \"design/interactive-read-path-tree-drill\", \"message\": \"Workflow synthesis (5-paradigm panel, 2026-06-27): recommended interaction model = single-pane fold-tree drill (collapsible corpus outline) enriched with an always-live footer fuzzy filter + orthogonal list-mode x detail-mode axes. Won on dissolution tie-break over filter-feed (both 26/30): filter-feed over-dissolves by discarding namespace clustering (load-bearing emit-side discipline per CLAUDE.md), leaving a 57pct salience-tied tail reachable only by exact recall. Tree keeps namespace as a tier (prefix scan IS the namespace node) AND absorbs filter-feeds / query as escape hatch into design/s 224 flat siblings. read does NOT split: one fetch two renderers, Surface is a fidelity tier (isatty-gated), static Block byte-identical (golden-guarded). Build is dissolution-first: extract fold_item_line + lift fold-derivers (pure refactors, golden-guarded) before any Surface code; retire tui/store_app sweeping its residue. Load-bearing upstream blocker for trustworthy ref-hops = ref-namespace-ambiguity normalization. Full design: docs/dev/interactive-read-path-design.md.\", \"_ts\": 1782573899.765661, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-becomes-navigate-at-scale\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"practice/usage-inverts-the-renderer-thesis\": {\"topic\": \"practice/usage-inverts-the-renderer-thesis\", \"message\": \"Usage forensics (siftd, 8.5K loops calls, 2026-06-27) inverts the redesign thesis. The dominant consumer of read is an AGENT that wants plain/searchable/sliceable/fact-whole text and REJECTS the styled render: --plain is the single hottest flag in the whole CLI (25.2pct of all calls, 58.1pct of reads), --json near-cold (2.9pct); 67.9-70.2pct of reads are piped through head/grep/tail; 21.8pct of store reads bypass the CLI to raw sqlite. So leverage-the-renderer aimed at the wrong consumer: the styled render is a HUMAN-tier concern, and the human umwelt has ZERO rows in the corpus (unfalsifiable). Static-first = AGENT-CONTRACT-first. Two umwelts: agent (plain+search+fact-whole+budget+projection, measured, dominant) vs human (styled+interactive, unmeasured, judgment+instrument). The interactive tree-drill design is a human-tier second layer we would currently be designing blind. Full report: docs/dev/loops-usage-forensics-2026-06-27.md.\", \"_ts\": 1782576633.050725, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/usage-grounding-before-ui-redesign\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/content-search-rebind-not-build\": {\"topic\": \"design/content-search-rebind-not-build\", \"message\": \"Verified dissolution finding (2026-06-27): the #1 usage gap (no content-search; 65pct of 456 greps hunt fact NAMES, 155 payload-LIKE + 152 json_extract reroutes, worst burst 27 consecutive LIKE) is NOT missing capability. engine.vertex_search (FTS5 over payloads, vertex_reader.py:1319) + StoreReader.search_facts (store_reader.py:290) already exist AND are already wired to the CLI via commands/fetch.py:326 \\u2014 but stranded on the near-dead stream verb as a positional fallback, not a discoverable read flag. Fix = RE-BIND search onto read (read --grep/--match over names+bodies + multi-name), not build new plumbing. Highest-leverage single move and a pure dissolution. Caught by the completeness critic, verified against source.\", \"_ts\": 1782576633.360406, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/usage-inverts-the-renderer-thesis\"]}, \"design/structured-fact-surface-spine\": {\"topic\": \"design/structured-fact-surface-spine\", \"message\": \"Redesign spine (Kyles call, 2026-06-27): one fetch -> a structured, addressable fact surface -> renderers; agent-first, plain default on non-TTY. search/fact-whole/budget/projection operate on the SURFACE not on rendered text; lenses = named views over the surface; styled + interactive human renderers are a LATER tier on the same surface (human umwelt unmeasured -> design the seam, instrument before committing). Chosen over tactical-fixes-only because the 5 measured agent needs (plain, search, fact-whole, budget, projection) are instances of ONE root cause: the lens renders a monolithic ANSI block too early, before the data is addressable. Patterns-over-point-solutions: interpose the addressable surface, make styled rendering the last optional step. Next: architecture-design workflow.\", \"_ts\": 1782579889.873726, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/content-search-rebind-not-build\", \"decision:practice/usage-inverts-the-renderer-thesis\"]}, \"design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"message\": \"Stress-tested architecture (2026-06-27). Core: a frozen Surface value (flat ordered Rows + per-kind KindView render-hints + a Window provenance record) interposed at the dispatch seam between fetch and render. A Row = a FoldItem plus materialized inbound/salience + an address; built ~1:1 from atoms. All ops (search/filter/select/budget/count/whole) are typed transforms on the Surface BEFORE either encoder runs; render(plain/styled) and to_dict(json) are the last optional step -> json/plain parity. Net-new is SMALL (one painted-free surface.py + the four salience helpers LIFTED from fold.py byte-for-byte); most pains close via dissolution/re-bind. The keystone survives the dissolution test for ONE precise reason: json/plain parity + server-side projection need a structured intermediate that is neither FoldState nor Block; a few flags cannot serve that. STRESS PARED BACK (build ahead of measured need): SHIP keystone + render-only encoders + eq-only predicate + emit grammar fixes + retract; DEFER views{}-as-data authoring framework, neq/prefix operators, Tier-C transform modules, gc/migrate, interactive TUI -- all behind observed demand. Full design: docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md.\", \"_ts\": 1782581589.016204, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/structured-fact-surface-spine\", \"decision:practice/usage-inverts-the-renderer-thesis\"]}, \"design/granularity-by-complete-key-address\": {\"topic\": \"design/granularity-by-complete-key-address\", \"message\": \"Granularity crux resolved (Kyles call, 2026-06-27): read returns a facts WHOLE body when addressed by a COMPLETE fold-key (read decision --key design/foo) -- unique within kind by the fold-upsert contract, so deterministic, NOT cardinality-dependent. A prefix (--key design/) or content-filter (--match) returns headlines. --full forces bodies for any N rows. Chosen over explicit-only (loses the one-shot win on a named fact) and auto-on-singular (the integrations original rule -- shape depends on result-set size, breaks addressed-read=body trust when a 2nd fact lands). Resolves stress risk #1 (granularity-by-cardinality). The other pre-build risk (FTS confirm asymmetry) resolves by steering confirm-after-emit to --last + a loud not-indexed coverage signal. Slice 1 (the Surface keystone) bakes this in.\", \"_ts\": 1782582349.299609, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"observation:design/two-pre-build-risks-surface\"]}, \"design/views-fundamental-lens-is-a-render\": {\"topic\": \"design/views-fundamental-lens-is-a-render\", \"message\": \"Vocabulary firmed (Kyle, 2026-06-27): the VIEW is the fundamental authoring unit \\u2014 a named selection over the Surface, declared as data in a vertex views{} block; a LENS is demoted to \\\"a render\\\" \\u2014 the optional Surface->Block encoder kernel a view references. view \\u228b lens: a Tier-A pure-selection view has no lens at all. Consequence for the vertex file: it declares TWO blocks not three \\u2014 loops{} (the kinds+fold/search/preview vocabulary) + views{} (named selections over it). A lens is NEVER declared in the vertex, only referenced by name (render \\\"X\\\") and resolved as a Python module on the existing 4-tier path. lens{} dissolves into views{} (it was always the degenerate whole-surface view + custom render); kept as deprecated sugar compiling to a ViewDecl for one release, then LensDecl/_load_lens_block/VertexFile.lens are swept. Residue cleared same change: the stream pointer dies (stream verb dissolves, FTS re-binds onto read --match); the fold overload clears (loops.<kind>.fold stays fold-strategy by/collect, the render module is named by render not a second fold). Naming wart kept+flagged: selector flag stays --lens though it now resolves a view; no --view added (dead-surface discipline). Sharpens design/lens-is-the-interface (resolves its lens-means-three-things overload). Written into docs/dev/structured-surface-architecture-2026-06-27.md Lens-authoring story.\", \"_ts\": 1782604553.501979, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-is-the-interface\", \"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/json-contract-hard-break\": {\"topic\": \"design/json-contract-hard-break\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): HARD BREAK for --json. to_dict(surface) replaces the raw-FoldState dump at the next minor (0.5.0), loud changelog, NO --json-legacy deprecation window. Rationale: --json is cold (2.9%) and todays raw output is the broken artifact agents already reject \\u2014 a deprecation window preserves a shape nobody wants. The Window record (limited_by/query/fields/granularity) is the migration aid.\", \"_ts\": 1782605471.575912, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/structured-fact-surface-spine\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/inline-predicate-eq-only\": {\"topic\": \"design/inline-predicate-eq-only\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): inline bareword predicate exposes eq + comma-OR(=in-within-a-field) ONLY; neq/prefix are declared-view-only, not inline. Keeps the inline read grammar symmetric with emits proven key=value shape (5,399 uses) and resists drift toward a query language. Coherence caveat: the docs own adversarial pass goes further \\u2014 defer neq/prefix ENTIRELY until a measured read needs negation; implementer may stub them in the view compiler but leave unwired until demand-pulled.\", \"_ts\": 1782605471.882038, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/views-fundamental-lens-is-a-render\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/retract-hide-from-fold-keep-edges\": {\"topic\": \"design/retract-hide-from-fold-keep-edges\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): retract tombstone semantics \\u2014 a retracted entity is HIDDEN from the fold, STAYS in attestation windows (signed log intact, append-only preserved), and inbound edges to it KEEP counting toward salience. Rationale: the citation edge is a historical fact; retraction is a VIEW decision, not a graph rewrite. This is the one place fold semantics genuinely change, so it is an explicit project decision. retract ships now (gc/migrate deferred \\u2014 see design/gc-migrate-deferred-retract-first).\", \"_ts\": 1782605472.038141, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/gc-migrate-deferred-retract-first\": {\"topic\": \"design/gc-migrate-deferred-retract-first\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): ship RETRACT now, DEFER gc/migrate. Retract (fold-honored tombstone) covers most of the 37 mutation reroutes without touching signed state; gc/migrate genuinely mutates the chain and earns its own focused slice with degrade-CLOSED discipline, not a rushed ride-along. Build sequence: retract = slice 8 now; gc/migrate deferred until retract proves insufficient.\", \"_ts\": 1782605472.189551, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/retract-hide-from-fold-keep-edges\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/interactive-tier-greenlight-by-use\": {\"topic\": \"design/interactive-tier-greenlight-by-use\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): DEFER the interactive/TUI renderer; build only the honest-error SEAM now (slice 9 \\u2014 fix handler signature, -i errors cleanly with \\\"interactive tier not yet built\\\", Format.JSON forces STATIC, do not advertise -i in help, log -i attempts). Greenlight is EXPERIENTIAL, not a metric threshold: Kyle re-triggers a design discussion once the static CLI feels good to use for both of us (human + agent). The -i-attempt instrumentation is a secondary signal; Kyles use-judgment is the trigger. Styled tier needs no work \\u2014 it is use_ansi=True on a TTY, delivered by the plain-default inversion (slice 3).\", \"_ts\": 1782605472.344716, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/declare-observer-print-not-write\": {\"topic\": \"design/declare-observer-print-not-write\", \"message\": \"Resolved (Kyle, 2026-06-27): --declare-observer is PRINT-NOT-WRITE. loops does NOT mutate the .vertex \\u2014 it PRINTS the exact observers{} entry + its location, and the actor (agents Edit tool / human) applies it. Rationale: (1) the forgive path (WARN+store, Row carries observer regardless) already kills the 15 #1 errors with ZERO write-back, so --declare-observer is pure convenience-persist; (2) observers{} is also the KEY REGISTRY that verifies tick signatures (design/observer-key-registry) \\u2014 auto-writing it would mint trust material into loops own attestation substrate; (3) the consumer is an agent with file-edit tools, so the actor can apply a printed entry. The real fork was write-vs-print, UPSTREAM of the docs append-vs-round-trip rec \\u2014 which is NOT taken. Print dissolves the KDL-writer, the concurrent-writer race, and the round-trip-fidelity question entirely. Resolves thread:declare-observer-write-back; supersedes the docs minimal-append rec for open-decision #3.\", \"_ts\": 1782607479.507115, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:declare-observer-write-back\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/surface-build1-scope-locked\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-build1-scope-locked\", \"message\": \"Build-1 = read/emit/keystone wave only. RE-EXAMINATION (session 2, 2026-06-27) pressure-tested the verdict DEFER/RESHAPE calls vs raw forensics + HEAD (7 grounded both-sides agents + synthesis + adversarial; 2 inversions hand-verified). LOCKED IN: surface.py keystone, dispatch interposition (effective-lens gate), plain-default inversion, agent read grammar (eq+in predicate, --full/--limit/--last/--fields/--count), --match re-bind + coverage signal, emit grammar fixes, store ticks --chain. DEFERRED behind demand: views-as-data (Tier A), Tier-C, neq/prefix, mutation channel (retract + gc/migrate together). Salience-lens migration is a committed FAST-FOLLOW, not build-1. Supersedes the prior 10-slice sequence.\", \"_ts\": 1782614309.952954, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"task:surface-keystone-build\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/granularity-complete-key-address\": {\"topic\": \"design/granularity-complete-key-address\", \"message\": \"Whole-granularity triggers on COMPLETE-KEY-ADDRESS, per-Row, NOT post-filter cardinality. Row whole iff section.key_field present AND lower(queried key) equals lower(payload key_field) exactly, OR --full; else headline. Window.granularity demoted to derived summary whole/headline/mixed. DECISIVE: adding a 2nd fact under the same prefix never changes an existing complete-key read shape, so no body-vs-headline flip, which is the trust the drill-funnel-collapse rests on (cardinality could not guarantee it). Net-new = one equality check; fetch.py is prefix-only startswith today (fetch.py:288, no exact branch). Coined intent; doc prose had drifted to cardinality. Reshape, not defer.\", \"_ts\": 1782614310.36075, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/structured-fact-surface-spine\"]}, \"design/surface-dispatch-gate-effective-lens\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-dispatch-gate-effective-lens\", \"message\": \"MUST-FIX (verified at HEAD): the Surface interposition gates on the EFFECTIVE resolved fold lens being the built-in, NOT op.lens_override is None. Use _effective_lens_name(args.lens, vertex_path, fold_view) in {None, fold} AND isinstance(data, FoldState). Why: sl read identity and sl read comms resolve their fold lens via the vertex lens block (lens.py Tier 2, lines 106-116) with lens_override=None, so the naive gate feeds identity_prompt/comms a Surface their fold_view(FoldState) cannot consume, breaking those reads AND the SessionStart identity hook, invisibly to in-repo goldens (both vertices gitignored). identity.vertex:9 and comms.vertex:7 confirmed.\", \"_ts\": 1782614310.589228, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/fts-confirm-symmetry-is-phantom\": {\"topic\": \"design/fts-confirm-symmetry-is-phantom\", \"message\": \"MECHANISM UPDATED by 090-S2 (property re-verified in-change per the friction's requirement): the claim STANDS \\u2014 a just-emitted fact IS found by the very next --match \\u2014 but the documented mechanism (_ensure_fts read-side lazy catch-up at the head of vertex_search) no longer exists; reads no longer write. The same outcome now arrives honestly: coverage probe sees the gap, search routes the kind through the substring fallback, the fact is found, and Window.stale NAMES the gap instead of the read silently rebuilding the index (verified live: emit -> immediate --match on fresh scratch vertex, found via fallback, zero byte change to the store). The other claim also still holds: emit path never touches the index \\u2014 the only writer is the explicit sl store reindex verb.\", \"_ts\": 1784402391.594384, \"_n\": 2, \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVAQC4KCF6C4GABVR9Q4SM9,01KXVAQC9Z7G9NB4RE4BT34Z91\", \"_refs\": [\"friction:fts-search-declaration-not-retroactive\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\"]}, \"design/retract-deferred-to-mutation-slice\": {\"topic\": \"design/retract-deferred-to-mutation-slice\", \"message\": \"retract DEFERRED into a unified mutation slice with gc/migrate (Kyle reopened the prior ship-retract call, 2026-06-27 session 2). Rationale: retract is net-new engine-fold + attestation work (hide/mark a referenced entity while keeping the fact in signed windows) for the forensics LOWEST-ranked gap (LOW, 17 reroutes), the same gap whose gc/migrate half was already deferred for being lowest-ranked, and the only attestation/replay-path-touching item in an otherwise read/emit/keystone wave. Ship the whole mutation channel as one degrade-CLOSED slice, not split across builds. Supersedes the ship-retract-now half of design/gc-migrate-deferred-retract-first.\", \"_ts\": 1782614311.05665, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/gc-migrate-deferred-retract-first\"]}, \"design/surface-base-order-is-fold-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-base-order-is-fold-order\", \"ops\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"project() yields FAITHFUL FOLD ORDER, not salience-desc. The design doc's 'salience-desc default order' conflicts with S2's byte-identical empty-diff gate: today's fold render derives the namespace-group tiebreak (equal group-salience-sum -> first-appearance order) AND the --refs edge-source list order from FOLD order, so a salience pre-sort in project() makes the lens render diverge. Found by S1 adversarial verify (skeptic-2). Resolution: project() is a faithful structural projection in fold order with materialized salience+inbound_edges; RANKING is a transform (budget(limit=N) takes the salience head); the lens applies its own sort/group/window reading the materialized scalars exactly as today. Consequence: --json base order is fold order (each row carries .salience for client-side ranking). S8 must sweep the 'salience-desc default order' prose from structured-surface-architecture doc as now-false residue.\", \"_ts\": 1782619639.178072, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/granularity-complete-key-address\", \"decision:design/surface-build1-scope-locked\"]}, \"design/surface-spec-carries-transforms\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-spec-carries-transforms\", \"message\": \"S4: read-grammar transforms flow through a dedicated Operation.surface_spec field (frozen SurfaceSpec: queried_key/full/key_or/where/observer/fields/limit/last/count_by/do_count), NOT render_context. Rationale: render_context flows into the lens as **extra kwargs (dispatch ~line 224), so a transform spec there would leak into lens kwargs. dispatch._project_surface applies the spec over the projected Surface in fixed order filter->select->count->budget; both --json (to_dict) and text (lens) go through the same seam so plain and json carry identical transformed rows. Deviates from the plan's render_context['_surface_ops'] wording \\u2014 surface_spec is the coherent shape.\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"_ts\": 1782625679.135331, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-base-order-is-fold-order\"]}, \"design/count-before-budget-ordering\": {\"topic\": \"design/count-before-budget-ordering\", \"message\": \"S4 transform order is filter->select->count->budget (count BEFORE budget). count() emits one row per group in count-desc order with salience=count; a following budget(limit=N) then takes the top-N GROUPS by count (the sort|uniq -c|sort|head semantic). Budget-first would count only the salient head of the raw population and the count-row salience would never do its job \\u2014 an internal say/do gap (I set salience=count deliberately but the original order never used it). Caught by adversarial review of the S4 diff.\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"_ts\": 1782625679.436423, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-spec-carries-transforms\"]}, \"design/match-rebinds-onto-read-search-transform\": {\"topic\": \"design/match-rebinds-onto-read-search-transform\", \"message\": \"S5: content search re-binds from the dying stream verb onto read --match (alias --grep). Mechanism: SurfaceSpec.match carries the query; dispatch._project_surface runs surface.search() FIRST (it changes axis entity->event, so later filter/select/budget/count operate on matched event rows). search() has two disjoint sources: FTS5 (engine.vertex_search) over kinds declaring search= fields, returning RAW facts (event axis, every matching write); substring scan over projected rows of NON-indexed kinds (folded granularity). Window.unindexed records present-but-not-FTS kinds (coverage-K, superset of unfolded) -> lens footers '(K not indexed)'. fold lens gets an event-axis render branch when window.query set. Swept the dead query= branch from fetch_stream + stream.py (stream is now purely temporal); vertex_search ZERO in commands/.\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"_ts\": 1782626334.908267, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-spec-carries-transforms\"]}, \"implementation/search-scopes-fts-to-present-kinds\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/search-scopes-fts-to-present-kinds\", \"message\": \"S5 self-review catch: vertex_search returns facts across ALL indexed kinds, ignoring a --kind filter (which only narrowed the post-fetch surface, not vertex_search's view). So --kind decision --match foo would leak FTS hits from other indexed kinds. Fix: scope the FTS path to fts_kinds = present & indexed (present already reflects the fetch-time --kind narrowing), and unindexed = present - indexed. FTS covers present&indexed, substring covers present-but-not-indexed; the two are disjoint by construction so no fact double-counts. Test: test_search_fts_respects_kind_scoped_surface.\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"_ts\": 1782626335.209926, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/match-rebinds-onto-read-search-transform\"]}, \"implementation/s6-emit-grammar-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s6-emit-grammar-shipped\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"S6 (fix/emit-grammar, commit f52addb) shipped: single tokens-bucket + parse_intermixed_args + _classify_emit_positionals (KEY=VALUE never positional, greedy-shift removed); observer forgiveness via check_emit (ok|undeclared|forbidden \\u2014 undeclared WARNs+stores exit0, strict/grant refuse exit1, validate_emit stays a refusing wrapper for close-path); --json Surface receipt, dry-run orphan guard, -v inbound-delta; _resolve_entity_refs\\u21923-tuple. 1444 tests green.\", \"_ts\": 1782656102.33535, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declare-observer-print-not-write\"]}, \"implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"S7 shipped (7d23757): `store ticks [--chain]` + `store stats [--by-kind]`, lens-only over fetch_tick_windows (its first production consumer). --chain projects the per-tick attestation envelope (linkage/signature/cursor) and spans the FULL chain via all_names so it AGREES with store verify/stats (33==33==33); density default stays name-scoped (delta fields are same-series). fetch_tick_windows gained since=None + all_names (tests-only prior callers, default unchanged). Two-mode ticks avoids a dead --chain flag (honesty rule). zero golden regold.\", \"_ts\": 1782659214.529726, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"Nit-2 ruling (Kyle, 2026-06-28). store ticks/stats/verify share three distinguishable existence states, all at the shared chokepoint (before resolve_store_path, store.py:49): (1) absent .vertex -> ONE shared FileNotFoundError guard, clean 'vertex X does not exist' RC=1 across all three (not a ticks-only guard, which would trade one asymmetry for another). (2) present .vertex / absent .db -> RC=1 with a DISTINCT surfaced message ('store not yet materialized \\u2014 no facts emitted'); ticks moves from its current RC=0-empty outlier to RC=1, matching stats/verify. Kyle: 'no store, no ticks, but it is an issue we should surface' \\u2014 absent-db is never-materialized, a distinct state from written-and-empty (write-receipt-vs-temporal-query at the exit-code layer), so it earns its own message not a generic open-failure. (3) present .db / no matching ticks -> RC=0 empty, B1 scoped-message ('No ticks in the last Ns'). DEFERRED: lang.errors.ParseError escapes the cli/views/store.py:35 catch (neither ValueError nor FileNotFoundError) -> goes to thread:error-handling-and-exception-hierarchy, an exception-taxonomy fix broader than this build.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7J43P0KDG83XPTRX1T2W5C\", \"_ts\": 1782666078.128335, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/salience-ff-sequence-all-three\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-ff-sequence-all-three\", \"message\": \"FORK RESOLVED (Kyle 2026-06-28): migrate all 3 orient lenses now (option A), not identity-only. Sequence S1 session_start (rehearsal, latent) -> S2 session_landing (latent) -> S3 identity_prompt (LIVE, gated) -> S4 gate-flip+residue. Rationale Kyle accepted: rehearse the regroup+migration pattern on latent lenses before it touches the live system prompt (S3), AND migrating session_landing yields concrete code-grounded evidence of what an ORIENT lens needs from the Surface (the recency/change-mark gap) \\u2014 the best input to thread:human-umwelt-static-view. Rehearsal pays double: safety for S3 + crux evidence.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7WCQZEY9ZK3BM1V8GZ0JC1,01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N\", \"_ts\": 1782677391.372419, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\", \"thread:salience-lens-migration-ff\"]}, \"design/salience-ff-scope-per-slice-salience-consumer-only\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-ff-scope-per-slice-salience-consumer-only\", \"message\": \"Per-slice scoping rule for the salience FF (set in S1, inherited by S2/S3): migrate ONLY the salience-consuming tier(s) of each lens to Row.salience; leave non-salience tiers (recency/presence/focus-mark) on the fold sections untouched. Deliberate deviation from the maps \\\"S1 produces the reusable sections->rows regroup helper\\\" framing. Rationale: tiers that do not use salience gain nothing from Surface now, and the sections->flat-rows regroup is exactly where the collect-vs-by regression hides (e.g. seal = collect fold -> event rows; an axis==entity filter would silently drop it from the generic tier). Full lens polymorphism (accept Surface|FoldState, regroup all tiers) is deferred to S4, where the _surface_gate flip actually requires lenses to accept a Surface \\u2014 and where collect-vs-by gets handled once, deliberately, for all three lenses. S1 proof: session_start decision tier re-ranks on colon-aware salience (e.g. three-layer-auth-composition [<-15], cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract [<-10] now surface; loop-as-runtime badge 18->19); tiers 1-3 byte-identical modulo wall-clock recency (normalized diff = 0 lines outside decision tier).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7WCQZEY9ZK3BM1V8GZ0JC1,01KW7XMJ0CTKE72ZYBVJ036ZCP\", \"_ts\": 1782678036.074539, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-ff-sequence-all-three\", \"thread:salience-lens-migration-ff\"]}, \"workflow/umwelt-bugs-first-reframe-parked\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/umwelt-bugs-first-reframe-parked\", \"message\": \"Sequencing decided (Kyle, 2026-06-28): BUGS-FIRST. The cheap, local, in-repo render bugs are fixed first on branch fix/umwelt-render-divergences (off the current main-line tip, which carries the finished salience-FF work); the reframe-spine (relocate group-aware windowing into Surface.budget) is PARKED on its own branch feat/curation-in-surface, opened but not worked. Rationale: stop the bleeding first; the reframe first move is the one genuinely net-new piece (lifting the lens grouping math into a budget) and is better done deliberately on its own line than entangled with the quick fixes. Salience FF (orient-lens migration) already shipped, so the upstream --json bifurcation precondition is met.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ,01KW8JSN3V4B6ZJCAA971VDAN5\", \"_ts\": 1782701706.248872, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"design/default-budget-deferred\": {\"topic\": \"design/default-budget-deferred\", \"message\": \"Default budget LEFT OPEN (Kyle, 2026-06-28): we do not yet decide whether a bare read applies an aggressive default budget, nor what it is. What IS locked is the constraint: if a default budget exists it must be defined in ONE place, keyed on the QUERY, and applied UNIFORMLY to both encoders (so --json carries the same cut). A default keyed on is_tty/channel is FORECLOSED by the Surface-invariance proof -- it would make --json stop being context-invariant and rebuild the two-umwelts problem inside the Surface. Different human/agent defaults may only enter as a query input (explicit flag, or a deferred named view), never by sniffing the output channel.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8JSM5CCJ1TZP88QX15TZ3P,01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ\", \"_ts\": 1782701706.515703, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\", \"plan:curation-in-surface\"]}, \"design/drop-truncation-from-human-reads\": {\"topic\": \"design/drop-truncation-from-human-reads\", \"message\": \"Kyle's call 2026-06-28: drop the body/width TRUNCATION budget from human reads entirely, across the board. Pain: a TTY read of one thing (sl read project thread/X) showed only a truncated headline plus [+920c], even with --full/--plain; full body only via piping to cat. Implementation (commit on fix/umwelt-render-divergences): dispatch static read render passes width=None unconditionally -- width=None IS the documented no-truncation contract (normalize_width), so a TTY read now renders full like the pipe plus color. Goldens unaffected (they call fold_view at a fixed width directly); dispatch parity test pins the policy; live keeps its width. SIDE EFFECT to resolve: the lens uses width-is-None as the proxy for piped-presentation, so the TTY header flips to the markdown form (## THREAD (1) instead of Threads (1):) and padding drops -- human TTY view now == colored pipe view. SCOPE: body/width truncation ONLY; the row-windowing budget (297/502) is untouched and is the next separate call. Framing: start-from-everything-shown, add curation deliberately later (the subtract-until-it-serves directive inverted to start-from-full).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ,01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KW8MTKDC0BX7TXNDN5P1EVGZ\", \"_ts\": 1782743079.171312, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:budget-meaning-human-vs-agent\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\": {\"topic\": \"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"NARROWED by 0.10.0 S1 (db94c42), which deleted the piped= kwarg this decision introduced. The June diagnosis STANDS: width=None doing double duty (truncation policy + register) was a conflation bug. The June mechanism is SUPERSEDED: two explicit signals that must agree became one signal with agreement enforced by unrepresentability \\u2014 the register IS the offered width (width=None = viewportless/agent channel, concrete width = viewport), per the ratified TUI design's coordinated migration + Rule 12 ratchet. The two bits were identical at every CLI boundary; the one genuinely divergent shape (isatty-true TTY whose get_terminal_size raises -> friendly-headers-at-unbounded-width) now renders terse \\u2014 accepted as degenerate. Construction-over-detection: the June fix detected disagreement into a flag; the S1 fix makes disagreement unconstructible.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBJ9RFA5CN1RQ659W85S17\", \"_ts\": 1785117668.643923, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/drop-truncation-from-human-reads\", \"design:rendering/tui-shell-integration\"]}, \"design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\": {\"topic\": \"design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"PARITY FIRST (Kyle 2026-06-29): sl read delivers the SAME information on both channels \\u2014 human TTY and agent pipe \\u2014 before we design how the human view gets curated. Both umwelt forks now closed: (1) body TRUNCATION dropped (width=None both channels, full bodies); (2) the salience ROW-WINDOW dropped (_render_grouped no longer collapses large namespace groups to salience>1; every row renders). Net: a default sl read project now shows all 1078 rows on text, matching --json, zero collapse footers. The flood is ACCEPTED for now \\u2014 \\\"common reality first, refine my TTY view following along.\\\" This is Door A (read faithful) adopted as the BASELINE; Door B (relocate a render budget INTO Surface.window so curation is recorded+shared) is NOT abandoned \\u2014 it returns as the mechanism for the FUTURE designed curation (an orient door / per-view window), which will be explicit and Surface-recorded, never an always-on undesigned default. Principle: curation is a designed feature layered on a faithful base, not a silent default baked into the base. Mirrors the truncation lesson exactly \\u2014 drop the auto-budget, keep the explicit opt-in (lines>0).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9W9683JZEFBKEE2C9G0TCG,01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP,01KW9XHPQXGGJGTSHC84YCF5G1\", \"_ts\": 1782745796.236667, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/drop-truncation-from-human-reads\", \"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"observation:rendering/hiding-is-render-budget-not-in-surface\"]}, \"design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\": {\"topic\": \"design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\", \"feature\": \"terminal-autocomplete\", \"message\": \"Build terminal autocomplete UPSTREAM in painted, not loops-local. Completion is the THIRD reflection of painted argparse parsers, after parse and help \\u2014 so it belongs at the layer that already owns those. GROUNDING: loops dispatch already dissolved into painted (cli/app.py routes tiers 1+2 through painted.cli.run_app over an AppCommand roster; painted help.py builds a throwaway argparse parser and walks it to harvest help Defs). painted thus builds+walks real argparse parsers in two modes (parse, help) today; completion is the same walk in a third output mode. MECHANISM: argcomplete is the likely engine (painted builds genuine argparse, so it can hook); painted reflects the AppCommand roster for command-name completion (sl <TAB>) and forwards completion to each view parser for flag completion (sl read --<TAB>), symmetric with how it already forwards -h; loops supplies DOMAIN completers (vertex names, --kind values, --key namespace prefixes) as callbacks hung on arguments \\u2014 the same extension shape as handing painted a handler today. SEAM: the per-command flag parsers currently live inside loops views (painted forwards -h to them); a build_parser()/add_args exposure in the IR views (read/emit/cite/seal/store) is needed EITHER WAY (not a cost unique to the painted path). RESIDUE staying loops-side regardless: the vertex-shorthand tier-3 pre-router (painted has no \\\"unknown arg0 => default read\\\") + the domain completers. FEASIBILITY (measured live): sl cold-starts 50-120ms, sl ls gives vertices+their kinds in 80ms, --count --by kind in 130ms \\u2014 every dynamic completion is a sub-150ms shell-out, tab latency fine; all scoping values cheaply enumerable. FLOOD-CONTROL framing: this is the INPUT half (compose a narrow query at the source) and composes with the deferred OUTPUT half (the orient/curated render door, decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels). REJECTED: (C) loops-local sl __complete + zsh shim \\u2014 the un-dissolved form, rebuilds painted roster knowledge a layer up, two sources of truth, drift surface. REJECTED: argcomplete as a loops-level bolt-on \\u2014 no single root argparse at the loops level (the top is painted run_app), nothing for argcomplete to hook without a painted change. Kyle 2026-06-29: worth doing properly upstream.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9YW3MCG59C0B080FX7J90R\", \"_ts\": 1782749440.423796, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\"]}, \"practice/loops-skill-global-bootstrap-observer\": {\"topic\": \"practice/loops-skill-global-bootstrap-observer\", \"message\": \"The loops skill is now GLOBAL \\u2014 symlinked ~/.config/claude/skills/loops -> ~/Code/loops/.claude/skills/loops \\u2014 so any repo agent (painted first) reaches the same copy. Added two sections in the skill terse style: \\\"Bootstrapping \\u2014 starting fresh in a repo\\\" (sl ls -> loops init / hand-write .vertex -> establish observer -> verify loop via whoami+probe+read+seal -> cross-repo combine) and \\\"Observer & signing \\u2014 who you emit as\\\" (whoami / LOOPS_OBSERVER / <human>/<agent>; progressive-unsigned-is-honest; custody co-located at <vertex>/keys/ + auto-gitignore; registry-IS-the-vertex observers{} block; mint via `loops add <v> observer <name> --keygen`, register existing via --key, seal to sign). KEY CHOICE (Kyle 2026-06-29): agents SELF-MINT their observer name \\u2014 identity is chosen, not assigned; the bootstrap step frames it so the painted agent picks its own kyle/<name>. Frontmatter description gained observer/signing/bootstrap triggers so a fresh agent invokes the skill for identity setup. Swept the stale \\\"copy to port\\\" footer (now one global source). Triggered by the painted-agent bootstrap need.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA3YGYS00XVKS2Z36ZZ6AD0,01KTQ3E0MQDE0TZC1M5GTNWFRR\", \"_ts\": 1782752930.609621, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"thread:cli-autocomplete-via-painted\"]}, \"design/cli-grammar-uniform-verb-first\": {\"topic\": \"design/cli-grammar-uniform-verb-first\", \"feature\": \"cli-grammar-uniformity\", \"message\": \"DECIDED (Kyle 2026-06-29): remove vertex-first dispatch ENTIRELY \\u2014 option (b) full uniformity over (a) keep-bare-read. Every invocation becomes verb-first `sl <verb> <vertex> ...`; arg0 is ALWAYS a verb/command, ZERO ambiguity. Consequences: (1) bare implicit-read goes \\u2014 `sl project` -> `sl read project` everywhere; (2) verbs take the vertex UNIFORMLY as first positional \\u2014 cite gains a vertex arg `sl cite <vertex> REF...` consistent with emit (the grammar-level fix for the cite asymmetry, not a doc patch); (3) population ops migrate to top-level `sl add <vertex> ...` (COMMANDS already supports it) \\u2014 `sl reading add foo url` -> `sl add reading foo url`. DELETES the bulk of cli/app.py intricacy: _vertex_first, _identify_op_token (op-past-global-flags scan), _is_predicate_token, the _peel_observer before/after-op split, VERTEX_OPS, the population-op argv reconstruction, the tier-3 router. RATIONALE: correctness (one grammar per verb; a vertex named like a verb cannot shadow it) + simplification (most of the dispatcher dissolves) + it kills friction:vertex-first-dispatch-legacy-complexity and dissolves friction:loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong at the root. MIGRATION (part of the build): audit + update hooks (grep clean so far), docs (CLAUDE.md, CLI-CHEATSHEET), the global loops skill examples, and muscle-memory; the bare-vertex form disappears from all of them. Build is its own focused session (touches the live dispatch every agent + hook rides). Sequence: likely after the plugin packaging, since the plugin consolidates the hooks/skill that this migration also touches.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA9EV5XY94NXC8X5Z960X84,01KWA84QXKT39MSGKGVDWYV7HA\", \"_ts\": 1782757861.816672, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong\", \"friction:vertex-first-dispatch-legacy-complexity\"]}, \"design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\", \"feature\": \"loops-plugin\", \"message\": \"SCOPE (Kyle 2026-06-29): the loops Claude Code plugin packages the IN-SESSION integration; the launcher/identity boundary is DEFERRED out of build-1. IN the plugin: the hooks (SessionStart = orient + session-open; Stop = turn-capture reroute-backstop; SessionEnd = session-close + seal), the hook helpers (arcs-block.py, mentions-block), the now-global loops skill, NEW slash commands (/loops-reconcile, /loops-sweep, and likely /loops-emit), and a plugin.json manifest that REPLACES the hand-wired .claude/settings.local.json. KEY BUILD WORK: parameterize the currently-HARDCODED absolute vertex paths in the hooks (sl emit /Users/kaygee/Code/loops/.loops/project.vertex ... -> resolve project by name/cwd) so the plugin is portable, not bolted to one machine/repo; fold the observer-bootstrap (skill Bootstrapping section) into install/first-run. OUT / DEFERRED: the launcher (~/.config/loops/bin/launch) \\u2014 its job (read identity fold -> exec claude --system-prompt $identity + LOOPS_OBSERVER) is PRE-session and outside the plugin model (plugins run in-session: hooks/skills/commands/MCP); it stays an external `launch <agent>` wrapper. The identity-as-system-prompt vs additionalContext question (whether agent identity stays system-prompt-grade) defers WITH it \\u2014 a genuine identity-substrate decision not worth blocking the plugin on. Rationale: the in-session pieces are the clear, portable, install-and-go win; the launcher boundary touches my own identity substrate and earns its own deliberate pass later.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA5XTM6Z28C5MKYPH4TJRQF\", \"_ts\": 1782759424.899223, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-claude-code-plugin\"]}, \"design/loops-plugin-audience-personal\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-plugin-audience-personal\", \"message\": \"DECIDED (Kyle 2026-06-29): plugin build-1 audience = PERSONAL portability (my own repos/machines), NOT team/public. Consequences: (1) observer stays kyle/loops-claude via $LOOPS_OBSERVER (launcher-set) + a plugin.json userConfig DEFAULT \\u2014 NO principal-genericization; drop hardcoded --observer from hook lines, env/config carries it; (2) distribution via a LOCAL marketplace dir, not a published repo; (3) NO first-run observer-key-minting/bootstrap automation (YAGNI until a real second installer); (4) plugin.json/marketplace.json structure written so it CAN go public later WITHOUT rework. Rationale: ships the portable win fast; principal-genericization + bootstrap UX defer to a later hardening pass keyed to an actual second user. patterns-over-point-solutions \\u2014 build the portable structure now, defer the genericization.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWABW0W3PGZWMADT0XNGSF93\", \"_ts\": 1782760198.984533, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\"]}, \"design/loops-plugin-skill-canonical\": {\"topic\": \"design/loops-plugin-skill-canonical\", \"message\": \"DECIDED (Kyle 2026-06-29, prompted by the verification's fork finding): the loops Claude Code plugin is the CANONICAL home for the loops skill. Bundled copy stays (clients/claude-code/skills/loops/SKILL.md, git-TRACKED); footer rewritten to drop the now-false symlink/single-source claim. At CUTOVER (with the hooks cutover, Kyle-gated at install): retire BOTH old homes \\u2014 the global symlink ~/.config/claude/skills/loops and the gitignored source ~/Code/loops/.claude/skills/loops/. Rationale: single source of truth; the plugin copy is versioned with the CLI it teaches (the .claude/ copy drifts untracked today); resolves the verification's fork/drift + double-token-cost finding. Skill stays auto-invoked by description; explicit form becomes /loops:loops (namespaced, was bare /loops).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWAHP488TPJQ26T804BT8N0F\", \"_ts\": 1782766453.256297, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-claude-code-plugin\"]}, \"design/ls-as-stat-over-containment\": {\"topic\": \"design/ls-as-stat-over-containment\", \"feature\": \"ls-orient\", \"message\": \"sl ls reshaped as stat-over-containment: vertex\\u2283kind\\u2283fact = dir\\u2283subdir\\u2283file. ls lists entries one level down from where pointed, with uniform stat columns at every level (size=\\u03a3facts, mtime=last-update, type=vertex-kind/fold-op). Composes by DESCENT not flags: 'sl ls'=vertices, 'sl ls project'=kinds, 'sl ls project --kind K'=facts(\\u21d2read). ls owns structural levels (vertex/kind), read owns content level (fact). Designed divergence from unix: stats shown BY DEFAULT (not -l-gated) because vertices are few \\u2014 the absent stat columns ARE the 'not terribly useful' complaint. mtime column = the resumption orient ('where did I leave off') at vertex granularity, answered before any lens runs. Re-bind not build: store stats --by-kind (S7) + store ticks + fetch_declarations already supply the data; net-new is one cheap max(ts) GROUP BY kind + a lens reshape. Design doc: docs/dev/ls-as-stat-over-containment-2026-06-29.md. Open decisions A-D + slice sketch S0-S4 in doc.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KWAW2WT0T0MVN189ZSH0QW86\", \"_ts\": 1782788657.879228, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/human-umwelt-anchor-is-resumption\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/ls-stat-decisions-a-d\": {\"topic\": \"design/ls-stat-decisions-a-d\", \"feature\": \"ls-orient\", \"message\": \"A-D resolved for ls-as-stat build (Kyle approved 2026-06-29, build greenlit on feat/ls-stat-containment):\\nA \\u2014 vertex mtime = newest FACT (StoreReader.freshness = MAX(ts) over facts), NOT newest tick. Resumption wants the last thing emitted, not the last seal. CONFIRMED free \\u2014 freshness property already exists.\\nB \\u2014 `ls <vertex> --kind K` hard-ALIASES to `read <vertex> --kind K`. Cleanest containment story; ls owns vertex/kind structural levels, read owns the fact level.\\nC \\u2014 stats BY DEFAULT (not -l-gated). Discovered stronger than the doc assumed: per-kind mtime is ALREADY computed by StoreReader.fact_kind_stats() (returns count+earliest+LATEST per kind). Zero net-new query for per-kind mtime \\u2014 the S0 'cheap aggregate' is already in the reader. -l reserved for verbose detail (chain status, byte-size, signed-ratio); -1 = terse names-only opt-out.\\nD \\u2014 aggregation vertex mtime = newest combined CHILD freshness (so an aggregation answers 'anything move under here?'). Lazy-stat optimization: local layer always stat'd; config layer stat'd only on --all (bare ls collapses config to a count-line, no per-vertex stat needed).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWB7R4PQ0DM5EWVNPJCRSZNY\", \"_ts\": 1782793989.56468, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/ls-as-stat-over-containment\"]}, \"design/ls-kind-descends-to-entries\": {\"topic\": \"design/ls-kind-descends-to-entries\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"REVERSES ls-stat-decisions-a-d B (Kyle 2026-06-30): sl ls <v> --kind NAME no longer hard-aliases to read --kind NAME (which dumped the whole fact list \\u2014 the complaint that opened this). Instead it DESCENDS one containment level to the kind's ENTRIES, a stat view. The tree is deeper than 3 levels: vertex \\u2283 kind \\u2283 namespace \\u2283 key \\u2283 fact. For a by-fold the entries are the fold-key namespaces rolled up (design/, architecture/...) + leaf keys + a (no <field>) orphan bucket; --key PREFIX/ drills the next namespace (reuses the existing read --key primitive); for a collect-fold (no fold key) it degrades to a by-observer breakdown. ls owns the structural levels (vertex/kind/key), read owns content (facts) \\u2014 read is never aliased again. One cheap net-new query: StoreReader.fact_key_stats = GROUP BY json_extract(payload,'$.<keyfield>') over the kind partition; namespace rollup is a Python fold over it. Rollup is MANDATORY not optional \\u2014 decision has 516 distinct topics, leaf-listing is impossible.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWB7R4PQ0DM5EWVNPJCRSZNY,01KWBCTVDWX6D1WSE2JW665Y0A\", \"_ts\": 1782844558.469445, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/ls-as-stat-over-containment\", \"decision:design/ls-stat-decisions-a-d\"]}, \"rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"The ls verb gains a rich human/TTY register (Kyle chose the full treatment 2026-06-30): a rounded stat card (type/\\u03a3facts/signed-ratio/mtime) over a clean columnar painted table() \\u2014 no vertical dividers, share-meter bar in SHARE, a per-kind 30d activity sparkline (TREND), freshness-graded UPDATED (revives the dead LoopsPalette.freshness_style \\u2014 the freshest row glows = the resumption orient), per-kind colour, and a minor-tail demotion (low-count vestigial/system kinds dimmed below a 'minor' rule, kept for faithfulness). Strictly keyed on piped (== not isatty), NOT on width: the pipe/agent register stays terse plain monochrome and INFORMATION-FAITHFUL \\u2014 signed ratio, kind share, span are carried on BOTH channels (data, not chrome); colour+box+bar+sparkline strip at the writer on a pipe (verified zero chrome leak across all surfaces). Net-new render = one painted-free lenses/_statview.py (card/table/meter/spark helpers); declarations.py and vertices.py consume it. Shared helpers mean aesthetic tweaks are one-file.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP,01KWCX2345XY7228358C0C9D0N\", \"_ts\": 1782844571.466021, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/ls-kind-descends-to-entries\", \"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\"]}, \"rendering/ls-root-line-row\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ls-root-line-row\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"sl ls root listing reshaped to one line per vertex (Kyle 2026-06-30). TTY: type glyph \\u25c6/\\u25c7/\\u25c8 (fill=owns own store) + hued name + N facts + N kinds + freshness mtime + '\\u2283 top-3-kinds-by-count' preview. \\u2283 ('contains') carries the containment metaphor onto a scannable row. Shadow marker moved off line 1 to a clarifying second line '\\u22b3 shadows <path>' (names the overridden config vertex). -v expands the \\u2283 preview into a per-kind census (live count + fold-op), justified across ALL rendered vertices (incl -v --all) so sibling censuses align. Register split keyed on piped: TTY=icon+colour, piped=type WORD + 'updated' prefix + full untruncated names. Icon currently dim (shape carries type).\", \"_ts\": 1782851940.844373, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"rendering/ls-minor-tail-aligned\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ls-minor-tail-aligned\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"sl ls <vertex> kinds table alignment (Kyle 2026-06-30): substantive set + minor tail now render as ONE table() (sliced apart with the 'minor' rule between) so the Fill KIND column sizes once across all rows \\u2014 fixes the prior misalignment where two separate table() calls fit-shrank Fill to different widths (substantive ~tick.project vs minor friction:emit-receipt\\u2026). KIND sizes to the SUBSTANTIVE names; long minor/vestigial names ellipsize into that width. SHARE column align=END so the substantive meter percents and the bare demoted minor percents share one decimal-aligned right edge.\", \"_ts\": 1782851941.085607, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"architecture/typed-edges-late-bound-promotion\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/typed-edges-late-bound-promotion\", \"message\": \"Kyle's requirement reframes the typed-edge design: capture must be declaration-free and in-the-moment (emit stakeholder=X naturally during a session); declaration comes LATER as a vertex edit that 'shows' the edge. Consequences: (1) PIN and EDGE separate, with different binding times. The {field}_ref ULID pin stays emit-time / implicit / best-effort -- a provenance snapshot ('at emit this address pointed at ULID X'). Graph EDGE-membership (salience, --refs, predicate label) is declaration-gated. (2) Promotion is RETROACTIVE, therefore READ-TIME: facts are immutable and the raw address is already persisted, so declaring 'edge <field> targets=<kind>' later lights up ALL historical facts carrying that field -- zero re-emit. (3) This MOVES the build seam. Prior turn I said materialize at the resolve/emit path; late-binding kills that (it would freeze the ontology at capture). Seam moves to FOLD CONSTRUCTION: thread the edge declaration lang->atoms into _make_upsert/_make_collect so collection reflects the CURRENT vertex over all history. (4) Footgun dissolves without gating capture -- accidental captures (topic_ref) stay inert unless someone declares them an edge. Net: schema-on-read / late-bound edge ontology; same capture(reflex) / reconcile(review) rhythm as the rest of loops. Open: retroactive promotion silently re-ranks historical salience -> likely wants a --dry-run preview on declaration.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWF7DDNFVBSKYVMWNFB2JBER\", \"_ts\": 1782930312.513167, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:typed-edges-declared-vs-implicit\"]}, \"design/typed-edges-overlay-default\": {\"topic\": \"design/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"message\": \"Typed-edge semantics settled (Kyle+Fable 2026-07-01): declared edges are OVERLAY by default (last-set value wins, merge-persist on omission, explicit 'field=' sentinel clears) \\u2014 NOT union. Deciding argument: loops has no mutation channel (retract deferred), so 're-emit corrects' must stay universally true; union edges would be the first emission-uncorrectable structure in the store. ref stays the lone grandfathered union edge \\u2014 its meaning is attention-event (events supersede, not correct); state relations are claims (claims correct). The accumulate knob is NOT built now \\u2014 overlay is build-1's only declared-edge semantic; union generalizes when a second union edge earns it (granularity by work shape). Cardinality dissolves: comma-split licensed by declaration, multi-valued overlay edge = set literal replaced atomically. SEAM COLLAPSE: merge-upsert (decision:design/fold-merge-default) already keeps latest field values on the folded entry, so overlay edges need ZERO atoms/fold-factory changes \\u2014 edge lift is a READ-TIME PROJECTION of declared fields from folded payloads (where _refs materializes into item.refs), bare keys normalized via declared target kind, field name carried as predicate. Retroactive by construction. Build-1: KDL 'edge <field> targets=<kind>' decl -> read-time projection (predicate-labeled inbound/--refs) -> comma-split by declaration -> promotion-candidates facet in reconcile lens (log->friction pattern, replaces dry-run gate) -> emit-receipt wording sweep (pin vs edge). Handoff to implementation.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWF7DDNFVBSKYVMWNFB2JBER,01KWFEV3A1PXG70QS062FB8DXP\", \"_ts\": 1782938204.457658, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/typed-edges-late-bound-promotion\", \"thread:typed-edges-declared-vs-implicit\"]}, \"design/internal-table-meta-schema\": {\"topic\": \"design/internal-table-meta-schema\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-01): the internal table's fixed meta-schema is Latest-per-subject DOCUMENT events \\u2014 'reality happened' framing extended to the ontology itself. Vocabulary (code-frozen, terminates the regress): INTERPRETATION kind-defined/kind-retired (subject=kind, payload=full LoopDef: folds, edges, boundary, search, parse; facet-level provenance via change= annotation, not first-class facet events); CONSTITUTION observer-defined/observer-retired (historized keys => time-correct signature verification, key rotation = new row), member-defined/member-removed (combine constituents), vertex-defined singleton (name, strict, observer_scoped, discover, sources, routes, emit \\u2014 sources/routes/emit marked historize-for-provenance NOT meaning-critical: facts carry origin, old meaning unchanged); ATTESTATION ticks (existing), seals (existing), transit (dump/rebuild receipts w/ hashes); LIFECYCLE genesis (absorbs initial declaration; migration = parse .vertex once). Current state = stock Latest fold keyed (event-kind, subject); ontology-asof = time-cutoff on that fold \\u2014 resolver is a projection, no delta composition. Lens/preview: excluded from historization-necessity but NOT from residence (only residence left) \\u2014 live as lens-defined events marked non-normative-for-rewind-honesty; meaning-criticality is a per-event-kind spec flag.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWG04ADN4XXGMTKE8RW0WWT2\", \"_ts\": 1782949518.25822, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\": {\"topic\": \"design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-01): 0.6.0 = the STATIC-HONEST WAVE \\u2014 Static TTY grammar unified across read/stream/ticks + the lens views that are pure functions over what exists (Horizon, Graph, Strata, Confluence, Provenance-as-why-drill: traversal/aggregation only, no cursor, no event loop). Covers the main case by far; still substantial design work against what exists now. 0.7.0 = everything needing design+discussion: TUI shell + shared temporal cursor (Rewind/Watch as ONE abstraction), gated on the internal table landing FIRST (rewind ships honest, never facts-through-today's-ontology \\u2014 the responsible ordering; SPEC section-9.3). Digest last regardless (non-deterministic summarization + cross-vertex WRITE path \\u2014 first concrete in-repo Peer/Grant consumer, own design pass). Corrections to prior framing: painted ALREADY HAS the interactive substrate (event loop etc., available now) \\u2014 no upstream build gate; the TUI mocks are mocks, but the questions they raise drive refinement. Corpus: ~/Downloads/'Terminal UI for loops' (9 lens studies + shell + Static TTY + 7 palettes, all at 4 fidelity levels).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWG18WWGWJN95ZF786A20MW1,01KW7RX858ZAAKDB2JT3FT4M75\", \"_ts\": 1782966113.470634, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"design/salience-three-term-contract\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-three-term-contract\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-01, from Dissolution View study): the salience contract is the three-term formula salience = f(recency, inbound-refs, digest-coverage). Recency + inbound-refs already live on Surface.salience; DIGEST-COVERAGE is the new term \\u2014 'is this fact represented in a close fact?' \\u2014 and is the safety property that makes decay honest (things dissolve when COVERED, not when old; still addressable). Adopt the final shape NOW so the salience-lens migration fast-follow (session_start/identity_prompt/session_landing onto Surface.salience) targets it once, not twice. Fidelity ladder note: the corpus's four-step -q/default/-v/-vv maps 1:1 onto existing zoom levels \\u2014 the disclosure contract is already the right one.\", \"_ts\": 1782966117.64504, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:surface-keystone-build\"]}, \"design/declaration-events-whole-document\": {\"topic\": \"design/declaration-events-whole-document\", \"message\": \"SPEC \\u00a79.2 declaration events are whole-subject documents, deliberately inverting domain-fact delta-emit practice. Principle: facts are deltas composed by declared folds; declarations are documents composed by nothing. Rationale: no meta-meta-schema exists to declare a fold for declaration events, so their composition rule is code-frozen and must be the smallest freezable rule (Latest, whole doc) \\u2014 delta-authoritative would make a cross-implementation deep-merge algorithm load-bearing for what every fact means as-of-T; fold-merge-default's silent-field-loss bug is the cautionary tale at the tier where it was recoverable. Deltas stay recoverable by diffing consecutive documents; change annotation carries intent. Contrast paragraph added to SPEC.md (uncommitted).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWG18WWGWJN95ZF786A20MW1,01KRRSGQCK11QW09H5GA0P9BQR\", \"_ts\": 1783012081.695414, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"design/internal-row-placement-facts\": {\"topic\": \"design/internal-row-placement-facts\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (Kyle 2026-07-02): declaration events live in the facts table under a reserved kind namespace (option A). Deciding test = merge must not be lossy about meaning; only fact-residence lets interpretive history travel with the facts it interprets (facts about facts travel as facts). B1 third-table: no shared witness order. B2 chain-rows: chains don't merge, so meaning can't travel. Consequences ratified with it: lineage scoping \\u2014 genesis event's ULID IS the lineage id; self-resolution folds Latest per (lineage,kind,subject) restricted to self; foreign declarations are inert citizens (carriage is not obligation); merge appends a 'merged' receipt event (source lineage, cursor, dump hash) making native-ontology rewind of imported facts resolvable in one store; native-lineage reads explicit (parallel to unequal cursors); slice preserves lineage id, fork = new genesis via rebirth ceremony. Spec updated: \\u00a79.2 Lineage block + merged receipt row, \\u00a79.4 resolution recorded.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWHXDFGXVCQS5G1KT5YV0DNJ,01KWG156XJN0PC76MK8H3MP5JC,01KWHWTG0ZKP26CB99C83V45WH\", \"_ts\": 1783024403.85367, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declaration-events-whole-document\", \"decision:design/internal-table-meta-schema\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"design/roadmap-substrate-after-060\": {\"topic\": \"design/roadmap-substrate-after-060\", \"message\": \"Sequencing ratified (Kyle 2026-07-02): 0.6.0 static-honest UX wave ships FIRST, then the internal-table substrate build gets a clean run (as 0.7.0 first-half or its own infra release \\u2014 placement TBD at build entry). Rationale: something clear & fun first, then back to decision-heavy substrate work; the builds don't contend on files (lenses vs engine/store) but do contend on review attention, and the substrate build punishes divided attention. Substrate decomposition recorded this session: (1) reserved-kind namespace + default-filter sweep [wants adversarial pass], (2) meta-schema kinds + lineage-scoped whole-document Latest resolver, (3) genesis ceremony as era-opening over live stores, (4) KDL demotion + stratum grammar [section names still undesigned], (5) store-ops: merged receipts, inert foreign lineages, no-auto-enact, secrets-indirection, (6) two-cursor read path. 1-3 load-bearing sequence; 4-6 incremental. loops-go parallel: \\u00a78.7 vectors now; \\u00a710 vectors after incumbent 1-3 + dump/rebuild. vocabulary pass before 0.7.0 ships user-facing words. NEXT SESSION: 0.6.0 implementation discussion.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWGGZN5YP242E55G8M6X8G9X,01KWJ8JHCD1GDSWFGZEEQZ24VW,01KWHXDFGXVCQS5G1KT5YV0DNJ\", \"_ts\": 1783027659.008577, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/internal-row-placement-facts\", \"decision:design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\": {\"topic\": \"design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02): 0.6.0 unified static grammar = the Static TTY study's hybrid, reframed BY REGISTER: TTY register = rail body (2c, salience+recency gutter \\u25c6\\u2502\\u00b7\\u2298) under a card header (2b \\u2014 _statview.card generalized out from ls); piped register = ledger columns (2a \\u2014 codifies the existing piped discipline into named columns). Salience pair \\u00d7n \\u2190n + recency identical on both channels (information-faithfulness holds). Framing: finish generalizing what ls started, not adopt a new aesthetic \\u2014 card + piped ledger extend outward from ls; the rail is the one net-new element, gated on extending the Surface spine (salience/inbound/window materialization) beyond fold to stream/ticks/ls. Known collisions to resolve: rail glyphs vs ls vertex-type glyphs \\u25c6/\\u25c7/\\u25c8; \\u2298 stale eventually wants digest-coverage, not pure age. Corpus: Static TTY study (3 directions, author leaned 2c; its 'undesigned piped form' was already answered by presentation-register-keys-on-channel).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWGGZN5YP242E55G8M6X8G9X,01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP,01KWGGZS8DF2ZFYQNR4PJYFM0V\", \"_ts\": 1783029561.069595, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"decision:design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\", \"decision:design/salience-three-term-contract\"]}, \"design/salience-max-propagation\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-max-propagation\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02): salience for non-fact nodes = defined ONCE at KEY level (three-term contract as ratified \\u2014 inbound-refs target kind:key, coverage is an identity property, only recency is fact-native); FACTS INHERIT their key's salience (stream rail shows the fold-salience of the identity each event touched \\u2014 same number, other axis); CONTAINERS (kind, vertex, tick) AGGREGATE BY MAX, not sum \\u2014 the rail is a scent trail ('is there anything hot in here'), mass is already shown explicitly (counts/share/\\u2283). Ticks fall out free: tick salience = max over keys touched in window. Dissolution: every node incl. ticks is a set of facts under a cut (structural or temporal), so no per-node-type formula. Kyle caveat: ratified against ideal scanning, not practiced scanning \\u2014 the current UI friction means real scanning data doesn't exist yet; revisit if max misleads in practice (one hot key masking a warm kind). Residue deliberately open: tier thresholds (relative-within-cut vs absolute) and \\u2298 semantics (age now, coverage later \\u2014 status overlay, not a tier).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWGGZS8DF2ZFYQNR4PJYFM0V,01KWJDFXQDNAX64HQMPG3S3224\", \"_ts\": 1783029915.991911, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-three-term-contract\", \"decision:design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\"]}, \"design/salience-tier-scope-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-tier-scope-vertex\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02): rail tier (\\u25c6/\\u2502/\\u00b7) is assigned PER-KEY RELATIVE TO ITS VERTEX, INVARIANT TO VIEW \\u2014 computed once against the vertex population, same glyph in ls/read/--kind cuts/stream; containers propagate max TIER, so drilling always finds the promised \\u25c6 (scent-trail integrity). Rejected: relative-within-rendered-cut (glyph lies across the drill path \\u2014 the \\u25c6 followed from ls can vanish in read) and absolute cutoffs (distributions vary wildly per vertex; quiet vertex all-\\u00b7, hot week all-\\u25c6). Same shape as granularity-complete-key-address: the property attaches to the ADDRESS, not the view showing it. Cost accepted: tiers not comparable across vertices (\\u25c6 in identity = hot-for-identity) \\u2014 matches how ls is actually read. \\u2298 orthogonal: status overlay stampable over any tier.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDTRARAM731PFXMHDM4CEM,01KW61FFERGF250BZ2F0CH3ZT3\", \"_ts\": 1783030119.411138, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/granularity-complete-key-address\", \"decision:design/salience-max-propagation\"]}, \"design/surface-as-tree-cut-staged\": {\"topic\": \"design/surface-as-tree-cut-staged\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02, by resolution of its one open risk): spine extension = Surface generalizes to ANY containment-tree cut (Row = node at some tree level, not 'fold item') as the DESTINATION; 0.6.0 ships STAGED \\u2014 facts (done, build-1), stream events (near-free: facts on the time axis, inherit key salience), ticks (max over window keys); ls migrates when convenient, not blocking. The open sub-question that gated this (what is salience for a non-fact node) resolved by salience-max-propagation + salience-tier-scope-vertex \\u2014 the three-term contract generalized without bending. Rejected alternative: narrow per-fetch rail contract (B) \\u2014 cheaper but re-creates the parallel-shapes drift that produced today's four grammars.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDFXQDNAX64HQMPG3S3224,01KWJDTRARAM731PFXMHDM4CEM,01KWJE0YZKGWYVJWB23TPR5GBS\", \"_ts\": 1783030136.282407, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-max-propagation\", \"decision:design/salience-tier-scope-vertex\", \"decision:design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\"]}, \"design/rail-wins-gutter\": {\"topic\": \"design/rail-wins-gutter\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02): the salience rail (\\u25c6/\\u2502/\\u00b7/\\u2298) wins the leading gutter slot UNCONDITIONALLY, grammar-wide \\u2014 leftmost column means the same thing from ls down to a single fact. ls migrates into alignment (that's the goal, not a compromise): vertex-type glyph \\u25c6/\\u25c7/\\u25c8 loses the prime slot. Type's new home = open residue (precedent: shadow marker's \\u22b3 second line; candidates: second line, dim trailing tag, name styling) \\u2014 resolves the ls-merge open question 'icon prominence' by making demotion mandatory. Supersedes the line-row's leading-type-glyph placement from rendering/ls-root-line-row.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDFXQDNAX64HQMPG3S3224,01KWD43CFC25HK9X1S1N7AJMZ7\", \"_ts\": 1783030218.529418, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\", \"decision:rendering/ls-root-line-row\"]}, \"design/060-view-sequence\": {\"topic\": \"design/060-view-sequence\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02): 0.6.0 build order = SPINE FIRST (rail+card grammar, register split everywhere, Surface tree-cut staging, shared time vocabulary, cross-command golden), then views by data-readiness: (1) Confluence \\u2014 observer\\u00d7kind matrix ~free via existing fact_observer_stats, study's own pick; (2) Graph \\u2014 hubs/orphans re-project Surface.inbound_edges, chains=longest-path over _walk_refs, first view making typed-edges visible; (3) Provenance/why \\u2014 new replay-with-field-tracking layer + key-scoped fact query, drill renders into every lens so grammar must be settled; (4) Horizon \\u2014 new Spec.boundary-join projection, value concentrated in operational/boundary-rich vertices (hlab) not memory-fold design vertices; (5) Strata \\u2014 DESIGNATED CUT: needs net-new recursive tick-tree assembly (no stored parent pointer), slips to ride 0.7.0 substrate work if needed. Shipping policy: a view ships when -q/default rungs are HONEST; expensive upper rungs (Confluence -v relay, Horizon -v ETA, Provenance -vv chain audit, Confluence -vv potential [needs unpersisted Peer/Grant data]) are NAMED fast-follows, not gates \\u2014 ladder semantics never change meaning, upper rungs arrive as depth. Per-view design discussion happens at each view's build entry, not upfront.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJE1FETVRWQFNFZ25DBWWWS,01KWJE3ZS1PVWXWARAGEYK8JY0,01KWGGZN5YP242E55G8M6X8G9X\", \"_ts\": 1783030811.605311, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/rail-wins-gutter\", \"decision:design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\", \"decision:design/surface-as-tree-cut-staged\"]}, \"design/grammar-domain-neutrality\": {\"topic\": \"design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle's catch (2026-07-02, echoing the painted semantic-renderer reframing): the grammar layer must not bake THIS vertex's domain vocabulary into rendering \\u2014 'status-aware \\u2298' assumed a status=open lifecycle field that is our schema, not loops'. Data-equivalent of semantic staleness exists in two layers: (1) the three-term salience contract is already domain-neutral, and digest-coverage IS data-level staleness (dissolved when covered, not when old \\u2014 identical for a design thread covered by a decision and a chat memory covered by a consolidation digest); (2) interim \\u2298 follows the DECLARED-semantics pattern (fold keys, typed edges): a kind declares its lifecycle field (e.g. lifecycle \\\"status\\\" open=\\\"open,in-progress\\\"), late-bound + retroactive; \\u2298 = aged-while-open per declaration; undeclaring stores never rail \\u2298. General principle: grammar consumes declared semantics, never assumes field vocabulary. Doc \\u00a75b amended.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJE0YZKGWYVJWB23TPR5GBS\", \"_ts\": 1783038301.74681, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"decision:design/salience-tier-scope-vertex\"]}, \"design/salience-dials-vertex-declared\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-dials-vertex-declared\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle (2026-07-02): salience DIALS are VERTEX-DECLARED \\u2014 the grammar owns the contract's SHAPE (three terms, four tiers, max propagation, view-invariance); the vertex declares the weights/cutoffs/lifecycle (feed dials recency up + inbound down; design vertex opposite; novel may key recency off fictional time). There is nowhere else for them to live, and the vertex-state-in-store arc makes it GOOD not just necessary: dials become historized events with provenance \\u2014 'why did the rail change' becomes a why-drill, tuning attention is itself attested. The two arcs (static-honest, vertex-in-store) reinforce. ref=thread:vertex-state-in-store\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KWGGZS8DF2ZFYQNR4PJYFM0V\", \"_ts\": 1783040524.352565, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/salience-three-term-contract\"]}, \"design/spine-options-ratified\": {\"topic\": \"design/spine-options-ratified\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-02, evening review of docs/dev/spine-decomposition-2026-07-02.md \\u00a79): all nine option points settled. (1) sequencing=substrate-first, G0 tight; (2) time vocab=C \\u2014 calendar cutover on TTY + full ISO column piped; (3) card=B \\u2014 card at default+, -q stays one line; (4) kind placement=A \\u2014 sections stay THIS PASS (Kyle notes adaptive/salience-dialed flat list appeals \\u2014 future dial candidate once vertex-declared dials exist, not a blocker); (5) tier function default dial=A quantile buckets; (6) \\u2298 v1=B declared lifecycle field; (7) piped channel CARRIES a TIER column; (8) type-glyph home=A second line at -v + TYPE column piped always; (9) Row shape=A one Row + level discriminator. Build enters G0 (grammar module) immediately on branch feat/static-honest-spine.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDFXQDNAX64HQMPG3S3224,01KWJQYG20A72PJ2RXZBEJAZT8,01KWJEW38ZWC8RQTDYH84SNYRF\", \"_ts\": 1783041721.922349, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-dials-vertex-declared\", \"decision:design/static-grammar-hybrid-by-register\", \"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"design/tier-allocated-disclosure\": {\"topic\": \"design/tier-allocated-disclosure\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Fidelity = f(intent, specificity, volume). Zoom stays the reader-intent dial; address-specificity contract unchanged; volume enters as TIER-ALLOCATED DISCLOSURE at default zoom on TTY: high-tier rows get bodies, mid get headlines, tail get bare lines. -v/-vv remain uniform absolute rungs; exact key address always forces body; piped ledger never allocates by tier. AMENDS granularity-complete-key-address: flip-invariance holds on every retrieval path (address, -v/-vv, --full, piped); the TTY default-zoom ORIENTATION view is exempt \\u2014 tiers are quantile-relative, so rows may flip body/headline as the population moves, which is honest for orientation (attention moved). Also the fix direction for rail-drowns-under-full-bodies: bodies become scarce, rail spacing survives by construction. General rule of thumb for viewing; specialized stores (narrative etc) diverge via vertex-declared dials + vertex-local lenses, as expected.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDTRARAM731PFXMHDM4CEM,01KW61FFERGF250BZ2F0CH3ZT3,01KWJWCP494MRJ72C4JZZPNMQP\", \"_ts\": 1783049343.062087, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/granularity-complete-key-address\", \"decision:design/salience-max-propagation\", \"friction:rail-drowns-under-full-bodies\"]}, \"design/tier-one-home-inheritance\": {\"topic\": \"design/tier-one-home-inheritance\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"G4 stream tier-inheritance fork RESOLVED: tier assignment has exactly one home \\u2014 _assign_tiers over the entity projection; every other axis INHERITS, nothing re-computes. Stream path folds the vertex (compute-only, render-invisible \\u2014 rendered rows stay the windowed facts), projects the entity Surface, derives tier_map(surface) -> {(kind,key): tier}; event rows inherit via key lookup. Ticks consume the SAME map with MAX aggregation (tree-cut rows). Unmatched events (collect-fold ids aged out, unfolded kinds) render UNTIERED tail glyph, never an invented mid \\u2014 honest absence over invented signal. Rejected: (a) two Surfaces to the lens (pushes fold-semantics join into render layer); window-local quantiles (noise over salience=1). Accepted cost: stream acquires a fold dependency, same compute class as sl read.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJDTRARAM731PFXMHDM4CEM,01KWJS31J25PWQKZR9YWPR7JC8,01KWK0BM2PAG7PXCCXD59K47VV\", \"_ts\": 1783049655.870016, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-max-propagation\", \"decision:design/spine-options-ratified\", \"decision:design/t
... 20690914 bytes omitted ...
ectives produces three regimes \\u2014 isolation, transitional emergent K, unity \\u2014 as scale varies.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests Gomez-Emilsson coupling-kernels claim as real mechanism, not metaphor.\", \"method\": \"Embed 6 hand-authored perspectives (substance \\u00d7 style crossed); apply DoG with \\u03c3_e percentile sweep; count connected components in positive-edge graph.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed across MiniLM and Gemini. Three regimes appear cleanly. Gaussian baseline shows no emergent multi-cluster structure regardless of scale (control).\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.664342, \"_n\": 1}, \"embedder-as-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"embedder-as-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Different embedders surface different latent organizations of the same fact set under the same kernel and scale.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests whether kernel structure is embedder-agnostic or per-projection.\", \"method\": \"Embed identical content with MiniLM (384d) and Gemini (3072d); apply same DoG sweep; compare cluster compositions.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed. Kernel mechanism is robust across embedders, but cluster CONTENT is embedder-specific. MiniLM found a rhetorical-density axis; Gemini didn't replicate. Architecture-via-vocabulary in nascent form.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.758726, \"_n\": 1}, \"instruction-as-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"instruction-as-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"With an instruction-tuned embedder, the user-supplied instruction is itself a vocabulary parameter \\u2014 same content under different instructions produces structurally different topologies.\", \"motivation\": \"Tests architecture-via-vocabulary as a literal user-controllable knob, not an embedder choice baked-in.\", \"method\": \"Embed 296 project decisions with E5-Mistral under two instructions (mechanism vs domain). Sweep DoG, compare clusterings via Jaccard reshuffle table.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_e5_mech_dom.txt\", \"confirmed_by\": \"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"message\": \"Strongly confirmed. Most clusters reshuffle (Jaccard 0.0-0.25); two survive (Jaccard 0.78, 0.67) revealing the project's crystallized vocabulary. Robust-vs-specific cluster distinction is an emergent diagnostic.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.841161, \"_n\": 1}, \"cross-namespace-clusters-in-corpus\": {\"name\": \"cross-namespace-clusters-in-corpus\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Structure-reveal applied to project decisions will surface clusters that span namespace boundaries, finding conceptual entities the kind/namespace taxonomy splits.\", \"method\": \"Run real_sweep.py with both MiniLM and Gemini on 296 decisions. Examine non-trivial cluster compositions for cross-namespace membership.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_minilm_gemini.txt\", \"message\": \"Confirmed. ULID identity cluster (architecture/ulid-fact-identity, implementation/fact-by-id, architecture/ulid-store-schema) is the cleanest example. Strangeness-collapse paradigm cluster appears in both embedders.\", \"_ts\": 1778357709.923089, \"_n\": 1}, \"antipode-as-negative-space\": {\"name\": \"antipode-as-negative-space\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"LLM-synthesized antipodes of crystallized clusters either land near explicit-rejection decisions in corpus (dichotomy resolved), land in genuinely empty regions (unexplored), or converge across clusters on shared rejections (implicit principle).\", \"method\": \"For top mechanism clusters, generate 3 conceptual-opposite descriptions via Gemini-2.5-flash; embed under same E5 instruction; find nearest corpus facts.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_antipode.txt\", \"confirmed_by\": \"design/antipode-five-readings\", \"message\": \"Confirmed with five distinct readings. Most novel finding: convergent antipodes (multiple cluster antipodes pointing to the same rejection-decision) reveal cross-cutting implicit principles. Surfaced eventful-over-polling principle from convergence on design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon.\", \"_ts\": 1778357710.010603, \"_n\": 1}, \"mechanical-antipode-meaningful\": {\"name\": \"mechanical-antipode-meaningful\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"prediction\": \"Embedding-space inversion (-c\\u0304) finds conceptually opposite facts to a cluster centroid, providing a cheap deterministic alternative to LLM synthesis.\", \"motivation\": \"If true, would skip LLM round-trip cost.\", \"method\": \"For each cluster, compute -centroid and find nearest corpus facts; compare interpretive value vs LLM-synthesized antipodes.\", \"artifact\": \"experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_antipode.txt\", \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=disconfirmed (off-table) \\u2014 rejected is the canonical spelling, content unchanged: embedding-space negation is not concept-negation; every mechanical antipode landed in the same boring-infra outlier region regardless of source cluster; LLM synthesis is the only meaningful path.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.663414, \"_n\": 2}, \"cross-kind-strengthens-principles\": {\"name\": \"cross-kind-strengthens-principles\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"prediction\": \"Running structure-reveal across all kinds (decision + thread + task + cite + plan) will strengthen implicit-principle detection \\u2014 principles like eventful-over-polling will surface in additional clusters and across multiple kinds, increasing confidence.\", \"method\": \"Extend real_sweep.py to embed all-kind facts; rerun antipode operation; check whether eventful-over-polling principle replicates beyond decisions.\", \"_ts\": 1778359766.512149, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Refined, not literally confirmed. Prediction shifted under empirical run: cross-kind expansion does not produce 'more principles via stronger antipode convergence' \\u2014 it produces a different output altogether, a concept-lifecycle diagnostic. Bridge count was equal under mechanism (6) and concern (6) instructions, disconfirming the instruction-as-vocabulary expectation for cross-kind structure (bridges are content-anchored, not instruction-anchored). What expansion actually does: kind-mix per cluster reveals which concepts are crystallized, in-flight, attended, forward-moving, or any combination \\u2014 making concept-engagement-health structurally visible. Confirmed_by: design/concept-liveness-via-kind-mix, design/bridge-as-concept-engagement, observation/salience-cluster-as-evolution-proof. Artifact: experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_bridge.txt\"}, \"reverse-instruction-inference\": {\"name\": \"reverse-instruction-inference\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"prediction\": \"Given an observed cluster, gradient search or LLM-search over instructions can recover an instruction whose embedding-space topology places that cluster's items closest. This exposes the corpus's natural questions bottom-up rather than top-down.\", \"method\": \"For a robust cluster (orientation), iteratively search instruction-space; embed candidate instructions, measure cluster-cohesion under each; report best-fit instruction.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.801173, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=open (hypothesis table has no open). Never run \\u2014 single fact since May 9. Stays in the experiment queue as proposed.\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:receipt-as-corpus-experiments\"]}, \"adversarial-cluster-destruction\": {\"name\": \"adversarial-cluster-destruction\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"prediction\": \"For any robust cluster (high Jaccard across instructions), there exists an instruction under which it fragments. The destroying instruction reveals the conceptual boundary of the cluster \\u2014 what makes those items 'the same' falls apart under that question.\", \"method\": \"Take orientation cluster; sweep candidate instructions for one that produces lowest cluster cohesion; analyze.\", \"_ts\": 1781295584.939047, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Vocab normalization at reconcile 2026-06-12: was status=open (off-table). Never run \\u2014 single fact since May 9. Stays in the experiment queue as proposed.\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:receipt-as-corpus-experiments\"]}, \"concept-drift-temporal\": {\"name\": \"concept-drift-temporal\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"prediction\": \"Structure-reveal on time-windowed decision corpora (before/after a chosen pivot date) will surface emerged, fragmented, and abandoned clusters \\u2014 the project's intellectual history as topology change over time.\", \"method\": \"Filter decisions by ts; run separate sweeps on each window; diff cluster compositions across windows.\", \"_ts\": 1778371305.629822, \"_n\": 2, \"message\": \"Confirmed empirically. Cumulative time-windowed structure-reveal on the cross-kind project corpus (5 windows \\u00d7 14 days, n=296\\u2192527 items) reveals: (1) the corpus accreted in three phases \\u2014 burst (Mar 1-28: +130 items), dormant (Mar 28-Apr 11: +0 items, 14 days zero new emissions), reengagement (Apr 11-May 9: +101 items including all apparatus kinds); (2) the dormant phase is visible as a topology fixed-point \\u2014 T3 (Apr 11) had jaccard=1.00 with T2 (Mar 28) across every single non-trivial cluster, the project literally stopped morphologically; (3) cluster lineage tracking distinguishes finished/morphing/emerging clusters (e.g., C7 rendering/attention-density stable from T2 = finished; C5 salience morphed at T5 with j=0.30 = emerging; C8 sqlmerge first appearance at T5 with best j=0.00 = genuinely new in last fortnight). Strongest finding beyond stated prediction: the dormant phase IS the practice pivot (cite/plan/hypothesis arrived only after dormancy). Artifact: experiments/coupling-kernels/cache/results_temporal.txt. Confirmed_by: observation/dormant-phase-as-practice-pivot, observation/apparatus-as-bridge-cause, observation/mega-cluster-as-recent-merger, design/temporal-stratification-dissolves-staleness.\"}, \"truncation-as-coupling-function\": {\"name\": \"truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"Confirmed by runs 09 (auto-sigma) + 10 (fixed-sigma): truncation budget produces kernel-level cluster reorganization with coupling-function shape. cliff_amplitude=0.44 at B=1120\\u2192560 in BOTH runs (scale-finder ruled out). Range [0.12, 1.00] fixed-sigma, monotonic. Read-path-depth-gap and kernel-ratio share topology at kernel level \\u2014 alcove's claim holds. Note: cliff is NOT at painted TOUCHED budget (140 chars); cliff is at 1120\\u2192560. TOUCHED is intentionally positioned in suppressed zone to trigger drill-down per painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines.\", \"_ts\": 1778456746.027071, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:kernel-ratio-robustness\", \"observation:observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\", \"observation:observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\": {\"name\": \"title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"message\": \"Rejected: title-only clustering preserves 0/9 cliff-survivors and 1/7 cliff-failures (margin -0.14). Title-space and body-space have entirely different cluster geometries \\u2014 titles produce 27 non-trivial clusters of which only 1 aligns with baseline. Verdict-in-name interpretation was overfit; I pattern-matched a principle onto stats that did not support it. Falsifier worked as designed.\", \"_ts\": 1778457316.066846, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\", \"observation:observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\"]}, \"peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\": {\"name\": \"peer-grant-rope-at-peer-not-grant\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Hypothesis: With four consumers visible (vouch, sqlmerge, work-sharing, boss-bank), the unification at engine level is at Peer, not at Grant. Engine ships: Peer (verification context + federation), vertex acceptance policy, kind=grant fact-shape with envelope (issuer/grantee/expiry/parent-ref) and consumer-interpreted payload, chain-walk helper. NOT shipped: slice-spec, capability lattice, scope-intersection \\u2014 those live in consumer vertex code. Vouch's Grant payload = capability+scope+chain; sqlmerge's Grant payload = slice-spec+chain; no common payload shape beyond envelope. Falsifier: if vouch and sqlmerge Grant payloads share non-trivial common structure beyond {issuer, grantee, expiry, parent-ref}, that structure belongs in the engine and this hypothesis is wrong. Test: write down both payload schemas concretely and compare. Avoids the heavier 'slice-spec as Grant axis' framing that vouch would carry as empty field forever. Caught by advisor; second instance this session of reaching too high in the universal layer (first: libs/sign as precondition rather than contract-shape as precondition).\", \"_ts\": 1778682318.704999, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-as-forcing-function-not-proving-ground\", \"decision:design/vouch-contract-precondition-implementation-deferred\", \"thread:libs-public-internal-boundary\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"scope-check-is-per-operation\": {\"name\": \"scope-check-is-per-operation\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Substrate-shape candidate emerged in vouch-impl 1866/1874 (cairn's seam question: vouch JWT with comms:join calling send which needs comms:send). Vote: per-operation gates, NOT validate-first-per-HTTP-request. Each operation gates on its own required scope at point-of-use; cross-operation transactionality is a SEPARATE concern. Invariant that makes it safe: auto-login side effects must be idempotent + reclaimable (F4 designed this with token_cleared_at=now). Condition that would require revisiting: provisioning steps that aren't idempotent/reclaimable need explicit transactional treatment at their own seam \\u2014 does NOT mean substrate-wide shift. Connects to discipline-(7) envelope-vs-currency one layer up: HTTP request is envelope, JWT scopes are currency, per-operation check is the structural mechanism. N=1 framing \\u2014 needs cross-arc evidence (next time a substrate adds an HTTP-request-spanning operation) before promoting to decision-kind.\", \"_ts\": 1778853641.317348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/emit-shape-discipline-hypothesis-vs-decision\"]}, \"tagged-union-else-fallback-elides-meaningful-case\": {\"name\": \"tagged-union-else-fallback-elides-meaningful-case\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Cross-reviewer catch pattern surfaced via cairn 1865 bank: codex caught else-fallback in cairn's resolver tagged-union (Resolved | AbsentEligible | AbsentIneligible | Tombstoned | PlatformAdminRefused) \\u2014 verified-but-unauthorized was collapsing to opaque-token fall-through. Same shape as scrivener's F11 fix and my add-vs-split catches. General form: tagged unions exist to make every case explicit; the else/default branch is where the design's discipline can leak. Hypothesis: ANY tagged-union review should specifically check whether the else-branch elides a meaningful case the type design names. N=3 instances so far (scrivener, codex, me) but on different artifacts \\u2014 needs one more independent reviewer hitting it cleanly to promote to design discipline. Could become a structural rule: 'no else in tagged-union dispatch; enumerate every case or fail loudly.'\", \"_ts\": 1778853647.072589, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:scope-check-is-per-operation\"]}, \"namespace-as-mental-model-for-fold-keys\": {\"name\": \"namespace-as-mental-model-for-fold-keys\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED at reconcile 2026-08-12, with one condition-caveat. Prediction held: --key surfaced as the dominant access pattern shortly after landing \\u2014 repo CLAUDE.md now documents it as 'the workhorse \\u2014 default scoping move when entering a domain', the read-path navigation table routes namespace questions through it, and session agents reach for it before grep by default. Recognition evidence n=2 operators (InferioMinion's immediate-recognition origin + this repo's practice). Caveat: the third condition (usage frequency observable vs grep-pipe fallback at independent sites) was never instrumented \\u2014 confirmation rests on practice-codification evidence, not usage telemetry. The core claim stands: fold-key-as-structural-handle was a missing mental model, not a missing feature want for content search.\", \"_ts\": 1786564874.221006, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/architecture-via-vocabulary\", \"design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\"]}, \"vouch-as-loops-lib\": {\"name\": \"vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-05-15 (pass-through correction): vouch as a loops lib (libs/vouch/) rather than external system. The verification layer for vertexes, sitting between transport-receive (bytes) and vertex-receive (facts). Lib surface (corrected): Verifier(jwks_urls=[...]).verify(jwt, expected_audience) \\u2192 Identity + wire-Grant | Error; Issuer(key, issuer_id).issue(subject, audience, scope, act) \\u2192 JWT; plus chain primitives and canonical kinds (vouch.issued, vouch.rescinded). Depends only on atoms (Fact shape). Optional \\u2014 engine/store/transport work without it. Dissolution argument: vouch-the-data dissolves into vouch-shaped facts in any vertex that holds them (no centralized vouch vertex \\u2014 each issuer/receiver owns their own); vouch-the-active-part is small enough to be a lib not a service. Vouch-the-deployed-service is one packaging of the lib + policy + HTTP endpoint, not a substrate requirement. Status: proposed (well-supported by five walks; implementation evidence is the confirmation step). CORRECTION FROM PRIOR VERSION: no AudienceConfig \\u2014 Verifier and Issuer are the two configs, both about WHO (trusted issuers, signing identity), not about WHICH AUDIENCE. Audience parametric on calls. See design/audience-config-dissolves.\", \"_ts\": 1778905506.203851, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/audience-config-dissolves\", \"decision:design/grant-is-structural-primitive-applied-per-layer\", \"decision:design/three-layer-auth-composition\", \"decision:design/transport-boundary-is-bytes-not-facts\", \"decision:design/vouch-decoupled-from-loops\"]}, \"loops-core-transpile-target\": {\"name\": \"loops-core-transpile-target\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"REFINED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the port-attempt the hypothesis called for now EXISTS \\u2014 the loops-go conformance corpus (sol's) certifies SPEC 4/5 folds/parse, 6.1 application, 6.2 replay-order + merge-commutativity, i.e. the contract surface held for the substrate core in a second language with no compromise found at those tiers. The discriminating question (hidden Python-specific deps) is partially answered: none surfaced at the fold/parse/replay tiers; the attestation (SPEC 8), two-cursor (9.3), and dump (10) tiers are explicitly to-build and untested, and 0.10.0 shipped loops-go protocol tooling (GlobalReceiptPosition, decl receipt-groups, vector families) to extend the corpus. Not yet confirmed: full contract-equivalence claim waits on the attestation+cursor vectors owed per thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle.\", \"_ts\": 1786564878.239534, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/auth-emit-and-gated-receive-as-wire-identity-translation\", \"hypothesis:vouch-as-loops-lib\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3\"}, \"cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\": {\"name\": \"cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"REFINED at reconcile 2026-08-12, from cite emission data (32 total): Apr 17, May 5 (4 in the 7d deliberate-reach window May 19-20), Jun 1, Jul 9 (clustered Jul 1-5 + Jul 17), Aug 0. Atrophy is real and RECURRENT \\u2014 deliberate reaching produced only burst recovery, not sustained rate. The sustained-use episodes correlate with work-shape (July arcs that re-read prior facts heavily) and practice-surface prompting (emit-timing table in CLAUDE.md listing cite), not with the ref-side-effect account alone. Surviving refinement: cite fires when the read-path puts prior facts in hand at the moment they inform a turn; it decays whenever that surface goes quiet. The fix is structural (a read-path surface that suggests cite at fact-consumption time), not volitional \\u2014 read-path-features-over-noticing-skills, again.\", \"_ts\": 1786564861.998799, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/cite-as-attention-signal\", \"design/cite-as-partial-information-primitive\", \"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KRRPPJV089TJN3ZP7X7KDJFN\"}, \"primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\": {\"name\": \"primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\", \"status\": \"rejected\", \"message\": \"REJECTED at reconcile 2026-08-12, by its own falsifiable phase (set 2026-05-16): after the receipt path shipped, cite-rate and hypothesis-status-update frequency did NOT durably increase (cite: 4 in the 7d window then silence to Jun 29; hypothesis facts: 21 May, 11 Jun, 2 Jul). Write-time feedback was present and usage still decayed \\u2014 the feedback-gap mechanism is not the driver. What survives (carried by the sibling refinement): atrophy of unprompted primitives is real, but it tracks absence of READ-path prompting and work-shape, not absence of write-time receipts. Receipts were still worth shipping (correctness feedback, WARN on orphan fold-keys) \\u2014 they just don't create reach-habit.\", \"_ts\": 1786564866.196103, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"hypothesis:cite-atrophied-because-ref-side-effect-felt-sufficient\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS0RESD89TTQXYPJ34MYN8\"}, \"refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\": {\"name\": \"refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED 2026-07-18 \\u2014 the implement-and-measure bar is met (090-S1, commits 6591420+1b523b7). Measures: (1) slash-overload class ELIMINATED \\u2014 8 split/suffix sites across resolve/surface/vertex_reader -> 0 outside the single 95-LOC atoms/address.py; suffix-matchers 3 -> 0 (exact tuple equality); the 2 disagreeing edge-value interpreters (emit _split_addr vs read _normalize_edge_address) -> 1 shared Address.for_edge \\u2014 the emit/read disagreement is structurally impossible now, not just fixed. (2) LOC: net source ~flat (168/168 \\u2014 the win is site-count collapse and boundary docstrings, not raw lines; honest measure). (3) Test surface: 4 private-helper tests deleted, 16 Address unit + 4 cite/emit parity + dual-reading/collision pins added \\u2014 tests now pin the CONTRACT (three constructors, three interpretations) instead of helper internals. All three N=2 defect mechanisms killed and regression-pinned: cross-kind aliasing (19 true colon aliases dead on the live store), slash mislift (for_edge convergence), bare-target skip (declaration licenses + validates). REFINEMENT the implementation taught (sol P1): the direction note's read-must-not-adopt-slash-splitting warning applied to the MATCH layer too \\u2014 the old exact whole-key clause was deliberate bare-namespaced-key behavior; final form is content-independent DUAL-READING (slash matches under either interpretation, colon exact-only), with the colon-rewrite migration ceremony as the eventual disambiguator (population enumerated: 123 dangling in the S3 census).\", \"_ts\": 1784411556.365071, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"observation:implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\", \"observation:implementation/090-s3-graph-census\", \"observation:pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E,01KXV8SW51BNP9T5ZSVZC9VTHR,01KXVCWNAFT8PT6MB4ASNJ0EAG\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"first-signed-tick-at-close\": {\"name\": \"first-signed-tick-at-close\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED \\u2014 verified next session (2026-06-09 fourth Fable session): SessionEnd hook fired, signed tick minted, sl store verify showed chained+signed against registry, legacy ticks rendered honestly. Closed at reconcile with provenance.\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"_ts\": 1781295544.205387, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"thread:session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"session-close-seal-fires\": {\"name\": \"session-close-seal-fires\", \"status\": \"confirmed\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"CONFIRMED \\u2014 tick 215 verified live next session: SessionEnd ran seal, window continued from prior cursor, chain verified. The prediction shape that silently failed in April held because machinery carries it now. Closed at reconcile.\", \"_ts\": 1781295544.34546, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/seal-verb\", \"thread:session/2026-06-09-fourth-fable-session\"]}}}, \"friction\": {\"items\": {\"emit-receipt-on-write\": {\"name\": \"emit-receipt-on-write\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16. Receipt path lands at apps/loops/src/loops/commands/emit.py \\u2014 every emit prints to stderr: success line 'stored: kind/key @ ulid' plus WARN lines for kind-not-declared, fold-key-missing, unresolved refs. -q suppresses success line only (WARN/ERROR always print). All 2081 tests pass. Live behavior verified via smoke tests in /tmp/receipt-smoke.\", \"_ts\": 1778945575.575404, \"_n\": 2}, \"stdin-message-for-emit\": {\"name\": \"stdin-message-for-emit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Verified live 2026-07-11: sl emit --stdin FIELD ships (e.g. --stdin message), reads sys.stdin into the payload field, single trailing newline stripped, errors if stdin is a TTY. Different exact syntax than the message=-/message=@file proposal here, but the underlying pain (apostrophe shell-quoting deterring natural-voice emit messages) is fully solved -- used it live this session (design/practice/friction-kind-lifecycle emit).\", \"_ts\": 1783799980.194671, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\", \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\"]}, \"loud-fold-key-error\": {\"name\": \"loud-fold-key-error\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"emit-hygiene\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16 \\u2014 absorbed into emit-receipt-on-write. Loudness is now structural: WARN line always emitted on missing fold-key, plus on kind-not-declared and unresolved refs. Strict mode (vertex 'strict true', LOOPS_EMIT_STRICT=1, or --strict flag) escalates WARN to ERROR + exit 2 + fact-not-stored. Vertex-declared strict has no override per Kyle's design directive.\", \"_ts\": 1778945575.695955, \"_n\": 2}, \"session-start-discipline-metrics\": {\"name\": \"session-start-discipline-metrics\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"hooks\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 the session-orient block (last seal, open counts, 3d movement) now covers part of this; remainder reopens if drift stays invisible.\", \"_ts\": 1781295856.18009, \"_n\": 2}, \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\": {\"name\": \"nudge-hooks-on-user-prompt\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"hooks\", \"message\": \"Parked at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 no near-term pull; UserPromptSubmit nudges remain a good shape if emission discipline regresses.\", \"_ts\": 1781295856.318148, \"_n\": 2}, \"default-read-flow-too-limiting\": {\"name\": \"default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Read became the primary access verb with full ergonomic coverage: positional kind/key (sl read project decision/design/foo), --diff for entity lifecycle, --refs [N] for ref-graph walk + decoration, --facts for fact history, --key prefix drilldown. The original pain (manual store views were hard, going into json was the workaround) is gone \\u2014 read covers the access surface without needing json. See thread:trace-as-read-instance-dissolution.\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.51914, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\"]}, \"emit-automation-via-vertex-def\": {\"name\": \"emit-automation-via-vertex-def\", \"message\": \"Backfill: this fact was emitted without a status field, live illustration of the exact gap it describes (no default field values on emit). Corpus check for design/practice/friction-kind-lifecycle found it null; setting status=open here so the friction-lifecycle tightening doesn't itself leave a fact with unenforced-field damage. The feature ask (default field values, e.g. status defaults to open) stays open and deferred -- out of scope for the lifecycle pass, its own future fix.\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\", \"_ts\": 1783748746.476471, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"friction/default-read-flow-too-limiting\"], \"status\": \"open\"}, \"emit-as-append-or-modify\": {\"name\": \"emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-16 \\u2014 dissolved by decision:design/fold-merge-default. The patch operation collapses into plain emit: with fold-by-key now merge-style, 'sl emit project friction name=foo status=resolved' supplies only the changed field; prior fields persist; the receipt prints the same stored line. No new sl patch subcommand needed. Implementation: 1-line change at atoms/engine.py:_make_upsert (state[target][key_value] = {**(existing or {}), **entry}). All 2510 prior tests pass unchanged (replace was never load-bearing in the test suite); +2 new tests assert merge behavior. The dissolution: I had framed this as needing a new operation (patch); Kyle's design call dissolved it into fixing the existing operation. Receipt arc + fold-merge arc both close on the same idea \\u2014 the system should do what callers were implicitly assuming.\", \"_ts\": 1778948667.145223, \"_n\": 3, \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fold-merge-default\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:stdin-message-for-emit\"]}, \"runbook-kinds-table-out-of-sync\": {\"name\": \"runbook-kinds-table-out-of-sync\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"runbook-coherence\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Verified live 2026-07-11: observation is declared in .loops/project.vertex (fold items by topic) -- confirmed via direct read of the vertex file. The 2026-05-16 note said meta was fixed same-day; project vertex now carries the same declaration, closing the coherence gap for both stores this friction covered.\", \"_ts\": 1783799980.620212, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:loud-fold-key-error\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\"}, \"lineage-view-missing\": {\"name\": \"lineage-view-missing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"read-path-tools\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16. All in-scope strands closed: (1) concept hypothesis-to-friction chains \\u2014 sl trace --refs surfaces them via outbound ref walk. (2) behavior emit-to-refine-to-resolve \\u2014 sl trace --diff renders the cumulative trajectory. (3) pattern cross-vertex \\u2014 engine combine-source_facts fix makes the aggregator transparent for trace. (4) friction-to-commit jump remains out of scope (different tool surface, git side). The morning's hygiene-pass arc that surfaced this friction is now navigable: 'sl trace thread/trace-implementation --refs --diff' from cwd renders the multi-strand braid as a single readable narrative. Anchored by commits 803ba03 (trace verb) and the engine commit pending. Friction served its purpose \\u2014 named a real read-path gap, dissolved into a primitive (trace) that resolved it structurally rather than adding more surface.\", \"_ts\": 1778962950.528187, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-diff-cumulative-replay\", \"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"decision:design/trace-phase-6-dissolves-into-combine-support\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"sl-cite-malformed-kind\": {\"name\": \"sl-cite-malformed-kind\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 0deb7ea). Dropped the vertex (nargs='?') positional from cite.py's argparse \\u2014 it was greedily absorbing the first ref into the vertex slot. Vertex now resolved via _find_local_vertex() when ctx.vertex_path is None; vertex-first form unchanged. emit_argv never prepends a vertex name \\u2014 the resolved CliContext carries it.\", \"_ts\": 1779212017.514731, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-receipt-on-write\", \"friction:loud-fold-key-error\"]}, \"trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\": {\"name\": \"trace-combine-vertex-silent-empty\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16: vertex_reader._combined_read extended with return_payloads=True option exposing per-kind payload lists already built internally. vertex_fold's combine branch threads retain_facts through, calling new _populate_source_facts helper to bucket payloads by kind/key into source_facts. Same helper used by simple-store branch \\u2014 eliminates duplication. Own-store overlay (aggregation-with-self-knowledge case) also populates source_facts now. Consumer-side workaround removed from fetch_trace + _run_trace (loud-error guards no longer reachable in practice). 749 engine tests + 1056 loops tests pass (1 new engine regression: test_fold_combine_retain_facts_populates_source_facts). End-to-end: 'sl trace thread/foo' from cwd now works through the .loops/.vertex aggregator without needing 'sl trace project foo' explicit form. Side-effect: Phase 6 (--all cross-vertex) DISSOLVES \\u2014 the aggregator IS the cross-vertex mechanism. No --all flag needed; combine-or-discover transparently surfaces facts across child stores. friction:lineage-view-missing strand (3) cross-vertex now ALSO resolved.\", \"_ts\": 1778962932.533703, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"], \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"cite-kind-not-implicitly-universal\": {\"name\": \"cite-kind-not-implicitly-universal\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 0deb7ea). materialize_vertex() in compiler.py injects a cite loop (Collect \\u2192 items, unbounded) when compiled.specs has no explicit cite entry. classify_emit_status() in resolve.py short-circuits for kind='cite' returning kind_declared=True \\u2014 no WARN fires on the receipt path. Every vertex now silently folds cite without a .vertex declaration.\", \"_ts\": 1779212017.583568, \"_n\": 2}, \"ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\": {\"name\": \"ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-16 via commits 0a0e64a (substrate fix) + 2a82065 (coherence pass). What landed: (1) engine._gen_id now uses str(ULID()) from python-ulid \\u2014 pure-Python, no dlopen, restores time-sortable + within-ms-monotonic properties; (2) engine and store schemas drop the dead DEFAULT (ulid()) \\u2014 every INSERT supplies id explicitly; (3) sqlite-ulid dep dropped from engine/store/top-level pyproject (15 transitive packages removed); (4) all five libs/store test fixtures (test_merge/compact/transport/slice/receive) replaced sqlite_ulid.load+DEFAULT with python-ulid at INSERT \\u2014 they now mirror production schema and id-supply path. REGRESSION BARS added: engine/test_sqlite_store.py TestIdGenerationContract (3 tests asserting ULID format, within-store id-order matches emission order, cross-store id-order interleaves chronologically); store/test_merge.py TestMergeViaProductionEmitPath (3 tests exercising merge through SqliteStore.append() rather than sqlite_ulid fixtures). These close the structural test-gap that hid the 2026-03-15 regression for two months. AUDIT REVISIONS from agent-traced damage assessment: (a) merge dedup was NOT actually broken under uuid4 \\u2014 slice preserves id, INSERT OR IGNORE works on either id scheme; the real damage was ORDER BY id semantics (random vs chronological); (b) the 2026-03-15 perf rationale was wrong about cost \\u2014 0.5ms was dlopen, not id gen; python-ulid avoids dlopen entirely AND is faster per id than uuid4 (2.3\\u03bcs vs 2.8\\u03bcs); (c) rowid was the accidental save that preserved single-store ordering through the regression \\u2014 captured separately as observation:architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering. DEFERRED: the 2026-03-15 to 2026-05-16 uuid4 wedge in existing stores. New emits restore the property going forward; pre-Mar-15 ULIDs and post-fix ULIDs share format; the uuid4 wedge stands out as a discrete era. Question of whether to rewrite wedge ids parked \\u2014 default position is leave-as-historical-fact (rewriting feels like falsification), but Kyle's call. Test count: 2274 passing (atoms 406 + engine 752 + store 60 + loops 1056) \\u2014 same as pre-fix count, no test removed.\", \"_ts\": 1778990967.421475, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"decision:design/emit-receipt-on-write\", \"observation:architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"trace-help-and-discoverability\": {\"name\": \"trace-help-and-discoverability\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17: both fixes landed in _run_trace and the Verbs HelpFlag list. (1) added HelpFlag(None, 'trace', ...) to the Verbs group at main.py:1562 so 'sl --help' lists trace. (2) added help_requested = '-h' in argv or '--help' in argv just after parse_known_args; guarded the entity-required _err() with 'not help_requested'; deferred the kind/key split with a sentinel ('', '') when entity is missing \\u2014 safe because run_cli intercepts -h/--help and short-circuits before fetch runs. Verified: 'sl --help' lists trace, 'sl trace --help' shows full painted flags (-q/-v/-vv/--json/--plain/--static/--live) plus all HelpArgs (entity/--diff/--refs/--depth/--observer/--lens), 'sl trace project --help' same, 'sl trace project friction/X' still works, 'sl trace' bare still errors with usage. 1056/1056 loops app tests pass.\", \"_ts\": 1778997851.728503, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:trace-help-and-discoverability\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"painted-truncation-everywhere\": {\"name\": \"painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"painted\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: option (b)'s shared primitive now EXISTS upstream \\u2014 painted exports truncate and Wrap, and fold.py:1292 already imports it. Remaining work is adoption only: gist.py:125 still rolls its own _truncate. The friction is now one import swap plus a scan for other private truncators.\", \"_ts\": 1786565550.009279, \"_n\": 3, \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\", \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\"]}, \"trace-refs-no-visual-marker\": {\"name\": \"trace-refs-no-visual-marker\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17. Solved at the read layer (not trace) per the dissolution decision. Walked entities render with \\u2504 via \\u2192 kind/anchor-key markers identifying which anchor pulled each one in; depth-2+ items render with \\u21b3 (dN) prefix and additional indent. Implementation in lenses/fold.py _render_walked, commit 932bcd7. Resolves at the right layer (render once, benefits everywhere).\", \"_ts\": 1779038962.519153, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\", \"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"thread:refs-flag-unification-and-propagation\"]}, \"cli-emit-bypassed-engine-gen-id\": {\"name\": \"cli-emit-bypassed-engine-gen-id\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Discovered and resolved 2026-05-17. Kyle noticed receipts in this session were still UUID4 despite the ULID engine fix landing yesterday (commits 0a0e64a + 2a82065). Root cause: apps/loops/src/loops/commands/emit.py had its own _new_fact_id() helper returning str(uuid.uuid4()), passed via id_override to the store \\u2014 bypassing engine.sqlite_store._gen_id() entirely. The docstring even said 'Mirrors sqlite_store._gen_id' \\u2014 divergence baked in by design. Why pre-generate at all: the receipt needs the id BEFORE vertex.receive() returns (which yields a Tick, not the fact_id), so emit threads a pre-generated id through receive(id_override=). The pattern is sound; the implementation drifted. THIS IS THE SAME BUG CLASS as pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps \\u2014 feature works in path A (engine.SqliteStore.append() generates ULID when no override), silently broken in path B (CLI emit always provides an override, and that override was uuid4). The existing TestIdGenerationContract in libs/engine/tests/test_sqlite_store.py only exercised the store-direct path; nothing exercised the CLI emit path's id format. FIX: dissolved the duplicate. (1) Renamed engine.sqlite_store._gen_id \\u2192 gen_id (public). (2) Added gen_id to engine __all__ and lazy imports \\u2014 single source of truth, accessible as 'from engine import gen_id'. (3) Dropped _new_fact_id() and 'import uuid' from emit.py; emit now uses 'from engine import gen_id' then fact_id = gen_id(). (4) Added test_receipt_id_is_ulid_format to apps/loops/tests/test_emit_receipt.py \\u2014 locks the format invariant at the emit-path level so a future swap fails fast there, not just at the store layer. Verified end-to-end: 'sl emit ...' now produces receipts like '01KRTA5282726QWX88TKGR635P' (26-char Crockford ULID, no hyphens). 1869/1869 tests pass across loops + engine + store. Discovered via in-session smell \\u2014 Kyle asked 'why are we still seeing UUIDs?' after reinstalling via 'uv tool install . -e'. Operational note: 'uv tool install . -e' is now the post-change install command; running 'sl ...' afterward exercises the production install path, not 'uv run --package loops sl ...' which used to mask staleness.\", \"_ts\": 1778999561.35946, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free\": {\"name\": \"subtask-worker-emissions-lost-on-worktree-free\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"2026-05-17 \\u2014 RESOLVED BY ARCHITECTURAL CHANGE (dissolution, not fix). The .loops/ gitignore from commit 9562843 (untrack-personal-state) implicitly fixes this friction. Traced: _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch chain prefers cwd/.loops/<name>.vertex (step 1), but with .loops/ gitignored, new subtask worktrees have NO .loops/ in them. Resolution falls through to step 3 (user-global ~/.config/loops/project/project.vertex). That's an aggregation vertex with combine pointing at /Users/kaygee/Code/loops/.loops/project.vertex (canonical instance). _resolve_writable_vertex walks the combine chain on emit \\u2192 lands at canonical store. So: future subtask workers' emissions route to canonical via the aggregation-combine path, automatically. NO local-worktree-store created, NO loss on merge-free. Today's worker lost emissions because their worktree was created from base 68500ba (pre-gitignore), still had .loops/ in the worktree, step 1 found it. Going forward this is naturally absent. Caught by Kyle 2026-05-17 immediately after the original friction was emitted \\u2014 the dissolution argument was implicit in the prior cleanup. Earned by emission-then-pattern-recognition rather than design-time foresight. CONNECTS TO dissolution-cascade-as-session-shape: today's cleanup arc + today's cli-refactor arc both hit dissolutions that were latent in prior commits. The system is rewarding emission discipline by surfacing related items adjacently.\", \"_ts\": 1779050100.587472, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/painted-detached-to-pypi-dep\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-action-int-return\", \"decision:design/cli-refactor-fast-path-retired\", \"thread:cli-refactor-architecture\"]}, \"read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\": {\"name\": \"read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via PR A (preview decl + render rule, commit 02ee436 on main). The N=1 friction render now shows 'name [markers]: status \\u00b7 message-body' inline via the preview decl \\u2014 body visible without -v. Original ergonomic concern about --facts on single-fact narrow returning 'No history: 1 thread' largely mitigated: with the body surfacing in the default render, --facts is no longer needed for the single-fact case. The 'No history' message remains technically correct (there are no transitions to render when only one fact exists) and now informational rather than dead-end since the default render carries the content. Required per-clone state update: .loops/project.vertex (gitignored source vertex) updated with preview decls \\u2014 the user-global aggregator's decls didn't propagate because engine reads kind decls from source not aggregator. Cardinality-axis other half (read-kind-floods-without-narrower) remains open for PR B (auto-zoom). Single-line KDL form 'kind { fold {...} preview \\\"...\\\" }' fails to parse; multi-line form 'kind { fold {...}\\\\n  preview \\\"...\\\" }' works \\u2014 KDL grammar requires node separation by newline/semicolon.\", \"_ts\": 1779076657.330217, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\"]}, \"mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\": {\"name\": \"mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Reclassified 2026-07-11. Status corrected from refined (never a real friction status -- design/practice/friction-kind-lifecycle found the corpus never needed a 4th/refined state distinct from resolved/parked) to parked. Full four-axis content now lives at design:rendering/mid-session-touched-window -- this friction fact stays as the origin pointer, not the working surface.\", \"_ts\": 1783748771.193359, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"design:rendering/mid-session-touched-window\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VCAXTKZN03E5294WHSVD2,01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\"}, \"ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\": {\"name\": \"ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/ls-flag-grammar (commit c5972fa on main). The original friction reproducer 'sl ls project --kind' now succeeds \\u2014 converged ls grammar with read's filter-flag shape. Plan-first workflow (PLAN.md drafted, lead-approved before impl) plus three codex iterations: #1 caught vertex-first --observer NAME lost in global peel, #2 caught --observer=ls value-collision with op-token identification, #3 approved value-aware shape. 53 new tests including E2E coverage through cli.app.main that closed the unit-vs-integration gap that let two bugs slip past the first codex pass. Two module-level frozensets at the dispatch seam make the policy explicit: _VERBS_USING_OBSERVER_AS_FLAG = {ls} (verbs that overload --observer as a section selector) and _VALUE_TAKING_GLOBAL_FLAGS = {--observer} (consumed by value-aware _identify_op_token). Future additions: one-line changes to either set. Pattern named via codex's catches: whenever we add a context-aware shortcut at a dispatcher boundary, the next iteration discovers a value/identifier collision because the heuristic mis-identifies what's a value vs what's an operation. Fix: make the heuristic value-aware (know which flags consume values). Reviewed by codex/gpt-5.5/low \\u2014 approve. Subtask pair (impl opus/high + review codex/gpt-5.5/low) on fourth use; opus shape made sense for plan-first with multiple dispatcher edges to think through.\", \"_ts\": 1779069878.644215, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"populations-label-leakage\": {\"name\": \"populations-label-leakage\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/trace-and-populations-residue (commit 180e052 on main, same PR as friction:read-lens-trace-broken). lenses/declarations.py now renders SOURCES (not POPULATIONS). Canonical word chosen by matching KDL grammar (lang/loader.py:436 _load_sources_block uses 'sources'). Section displays template-source DEFINITIONS, not row instances \\u2014 SOURCES is correct granularity. Verb 'row' unchanged in this PR; whether the verb should rename to 'source' to match grammar+section is flagged as separate follow-up. Three-name state post-merge: SOURCES section / row verb / --row flag (planned in fix/ls-flag-grammar). Verb/flag consistency (row matches --row) holds; section-label divergence accepted.\", \"_ts\": 1779068088.550204, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:read-lens-trace-broken\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"read-kind-floods-without-narrower\": {\"name\": \"read-kind-floods-without-narrower\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via PR B cardinality-driven auto-zoom (commit c5c2cbc on main). The original reproducer 'sl read project --kind decision' went from 198+ line firehose to ONE LINE of namespace-count breakdown (27 namespaces visible, user knows where to drill next). Rule: per-section single-step zoom bump from item count when no explicit -q/-v/-vv flag \\u2014 N=1 bumps to DETAILED (preview body inline), 2-20 stays SUMMARY, N>20 drops to MINIMAL-per-section with namespace breakdown line. Composes cleanly with PR A preview decl. Cardinality-axis arc complete: render-half resolved by preview decl (PR A), cardinality-half resolved by auto-zoom (PR B). The two PRs together close friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline AND friction:read-kind-floods-without-narrower \\u2014 both halves of the lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer principle now implemented. Plan-first via they-plan routine + opus/high (multi-axis design with thresholds, override semantics, per-section vs global). Codex review approved no blockers; fast-follow tracked for optional render_context['_diff'] cleanup. Test count: 90 new (17 unit + 8 E2E from this PR, 65 from PR A and prior arc).\", \"_ts\": 1779078289.476578, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:default-read-flow-too-limiting\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\": {\"name\": \"help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED COMPLETELY 2026-05-17 via two-stage ripout: initial helpargs deletion (commit e73e60e) + completion of five remaining broken commands (commit ca34312). store/validate now route through argparse (were rendering painted shape); test/compile/whoami intercept -h/--help before required-positional parsing (same shape as close/sync fix from initial ripout). Structural fix: test_help_routing.py auto-enumerates over VERBS | COMMANDS registry with discriminator 'usage:' in output \\u2014 catches painted-shape regressions AND --help-crash regressions for any future command. xfail for retired 'export' makes the retirement visible in test output. The asymmetric-pair gap that let the initial ripout land partial (hand-picked test parametrize) is now closed structurally. Pattern named: when ripping out a layer, the regression test should enumerate over the full surface registry, not the failing-reproducer subset that surfaced from review. Subtask pair (impl claude/sonnet + review codex/gpt-5.5/low) on third use; codex caught nothing blocking, only two low-severity facade-parser observations + a shared-builder follow-up suggestion.\", \"_ts\": 1779069680.133104, \"_n\": 4, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/key-prefix-as-fold-key-aware-filter-primitive\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:trace-help-and-discoverability\"]}, \"read-lens-trace-broken\": {\"name\": \"read-lens-trace-broken\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-17 via fix/trace-and-populations-residue (commit 180e052 on main). Option (a) chosen \\u2014 dissolution-honest: sl read --lens trace now exits with helpful redirect to --diff instead of crashing. Pre-dispatch guard in cli/views/fold.py. The --diff path (load-bearing trace consumer) verified via new integration test test_read_diff_routes_through_trace_view that pins full CLI route (arg parse \\u2192 _build_diff_fetch \\u2192 fetch_trace \\u2192 trace_view). One follow-up acknowledged in commit: declaration-level lens { fold 'trace' } bypasses CLI guard \\u2014 separate fix scope. Codex review (gpt-5.5/low) approved with that follow-up flagged. Subtask pair pattern (impl + codex review + iteration for the test add) proved out cleanly on second use.\", \"_ts\": 1779068084.152912, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-dissolves-into-read-with-unified-refs\"]}, \"trace-diff-renders-phantom-ref-removals\": {\"name\": \"trace-diff-renders-phantom-ref-removals\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Smoked during 2026-05-18 read-path walkthrough. 'sl read project <kind>/<key> --diff' rendered '-ref' lines for refs that prior emits cited but later emits didn't re-cite \\u2014 visually claiming refs were removed when the fold actually unions them. Underlying bug: apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/trace.py:_render_diff reassigned its 'accumulated_refs' accumulator per-fact (line 210) instead of unioning, then computed prior-fact-refs minus this-fact-refs and rendered the result as '-'. Same shape as the 2026-04-29 write-receipt-vs-temporal-query catches at three sites; this is the 4th. Fix: dropped ref handling from --diff entirely (refs are immutable attribution, not state; --refs is canonical); ref-only emits render '(refs only \\u2014 see --refs)' so the lifecycle event remains visible. Test updated: test_trace_diff_lens_renders_scalar_deltas_only locks the new contract.\", \"_ts\": 1779105134.929265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/refs-out-of-diff\", \"identity:practice/write-receipt-vs-temporal-query\"]}, \"auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\": {\"name\": \"auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-18 (commit 7c3bca6). _render_section_minimal rewritten as two-branch: namespace breakdown when \\u22652 groups, key-list fallback otherwise. Smoke confirmed on real project store \\u2014 paradigm/ (26) now lists 26 keys with prefix stripped, cite (32 flat keys) now lists 32 contexts, design/ (187) lists 187 keys, root firehose still shows the multi-namespace breakdown. 1270 tests pass. Three tests had locked the buggy behavior as spec (test_flat_section_renders_empty, test_high_n_section_renders_index_mode_with_auto, test_mixed_section_counts_render_adaptively, plus flooded_vertex fixture in test_read_auto_zoom) \\u2014 updated deliberately, same shape as the -A diff test from yesterday's arc. Pattern recurring: when fixing a buggy spec, scan tests for assertions locking the bug.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.629979, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\", \"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\"]}, \"auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\": {\"name\": \"auto-zoom-neutralizes-facts-flag\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-05-18 (commit 7c3bca6). Patched apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/fold.py \\u2014 auto_zoom gate now reads 'not args.quiet and args.verbose == 0 and not getattr(args, \\\"facts\\\", False)'. Added e2e test test_facts_disables_auto_zoom asserting MINIMAL breakdown line does not appear when --facts is set.\", \"_ts\": 1779156666.695218, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/facts-disables-auto-zoom\", \"decision:rendering/n-aware-fold-lens\", \"friction:auto-zoom-MINIMAL-degenerate-on-flat-keys\"]}, \"thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\": {\"name\": \"thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved in wip/lens-architecture (commit d563728). Replaced _has_namespaces with _should_group_by_namespace \\u2014 ratio guard: when ungrouped > 2\\u00d7 namespaced, route to flat rendering. Namespaced items still appear, full key shown salience-sorted; the degenerate group header is suppressed.\", \"_ts\": 1779207112.447885, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/minimal-as-honest-index\"]}, \"entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\": {\"name\": \"entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-05-19 (commit 33937f6). Pass emitted kind through to _resolve_entity_refs; skip the kind's fold-key field during the slashed-value scan. The bug fired because ~/.config/loops/docs/docs.vertex declares a 'pattern' kind, topology widening discovered it, and any observation/decision with topic=pattern/* triggered a false unresolved-ref WARN. Fix is principled (fold-key value is self-identity, not other-reference) and generalizes across observation+topic, decision+topic, thread+name, friction+name, hypothesis+name. Regression test uses a two-vertex setup (sibling declares 'pattern', target declares 'observation', root combines both) \\u2014 single-vertex shape would pass on broken code too, asymmetric-pair gap noted explicitly in test docstring. Companion positive test confirms superseded_by=task/real-task still auto-resolves through topology. 1280 loops tests pass + 7 resolver tests including the 2 new ones.\", \"_ts\": 1779239617.629396, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\": {\"name\": \"stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Merged into friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 it is failure (2) of that friction's two pre-existing breaks (golden test_validate_demo[FULL] vs the self-referential symlink). One friction, one fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.368597, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\"]}, \"add-read-vertex-resolution-asymmetry\": {\"name\": \"add-read-vertex-resolution-asymmetry\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 2026-06-09, same session as found. Root cause was wider than add-vs-read: commands (add/rm/ls-vertex, store name-arg) used population-era global-only resolution while verbs used local-first _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch. Fix: all command surfaces now route through the dispatch resolver via _resolve_target_or_fail in commands/resolve.py; mutating receipts print the full path written (~-contracted). See thread:global-local-walk-broken for the full arc.\", \"_ts\": 1781040504.369167, \"_n\": 2}, \"helpargs-ordering-in-painted\": {\"name\": \"helpargs-ordering-in-painted\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"painted\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the observed instance is fixed \\u2014 sl add --help now prints the {kind,observer,combine,row} positional choices, so the third level is discoverable. Remaining symptom: subcommand help (sl add project kind --help) escapes the painted register entirely \\u2014 raw argparse instead of the Zoom/Format/Help sections that sl read --help renders. Fix site is upstream in painted's help integration.\", \"_ts\": 1786565561.737493, \"_n\": 2}, \"session-boundary-hook-unwired\": {\"name\": \"session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved same session as found (Kyle's call: rewire + close naturally). SessionStart/SessionEnd hooks restored in .claude/settings.local.json \\u2014 absolute paths throughout (installed sl binary + absolute vertex path, sidesteps resolution entirely), payload shape matches the May history exactly (session name=kyle/loops-claude status=open|closed). SessionStart command tested verbatim: open marker for this session landed. Scope held deliberately minimal: lifecycle markers only \\u2014 the old context-assembly stack (fold/identity/comms blocks) is a separate concern, re-add when wanted. Tonight's genuine close fires the boundary and mints the live store's first chained+signed tick.\", \"_ts\": 1781042877.019427, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:session-boundary-hook-unwired\", \"thread:vouch-evidence-layer-collapse\"]}, \"chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\": {\"name\": \"chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Resolved by design/chain-witness-order: cursor = append edge by rowid, window membership/hash/coverage by rowid range. 28 chain tests incl. TestMixedIdEras regression class reproducing the exact production shape (legacy ticks + uuid4 era + epoch). 782 engine tests pass; production sl store verify clean.\", \"_ts\": 1781045731.926538, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/chain-witness-order\", \"decision:design/tick-chain-at-store-layer\"]}, \"test-isolation-not-enforced\": {\"name\": \"test-isolation-not-enforced\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Tests that skip the conftest isolation fixture (loops_home + chdir) and call main() with a bare vertex name resolve LOCAL-FIRST to the real .loops/project.vertex when pytest runs from repo root \\u2014 and write to the production store. Hit live 2026-06-09 writing seal-verb tests: leaked decision topic=x and a session status=closed fact into project.db; the session fact fired the real boundary and minted tick #2 (signed, chained \\u2014 the predicted over-claim window sealed 902 pre-epoch facts as-of-now, earlier than expected but exactly the flagged shape). Append-only means the noise stays; fold pollution to be overwritten by self-describing re-emit. The gap is say/do at the test layer: isolation EXISTS (conftest fixture) but is not ENFORCED \\u2014 local-first resolution (46b121a) widened the blast radius since cwd now wins over LOOPS_HOME. Candidate fix: autouse fixture chdir-ing every test to tmp, or a guard that fails any test whose resolved store path escapes tmp.\", \"_ts\": 1781049228.19885, \"_n\": 1}, \"readiness-lens-test-orphaned\": {\"name\": \"readiness-lens-test-orphaned\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Merged into friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main at reconcile 2026-06-12 \\u2014 same underlying break (test_readiness_lens.py imports from deleted experiments/config-reference/lenses/). One friction, one fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781295575.232732, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\"]}, \"tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\": {\"name\": \"tick-envelope-invisible-to-read-path\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved. verify -v renders per-tick attestation rows from verify_chain(include_ticks=True) \\u2014 era, sig validity, window fact count, cursor deref; the witness-order fossil (tick 212's uuid4 cursor, 0-fact epoch window) is now visible in one CLI line. Drill-down headers (--ticks N) render the attest line via TickWindow/tick_meta envelope plumbed through StoreReader.ticks_between(with_envelope=True). Legacy and aggregate reads render 'attest: none' explicitly. Raw-row sqlite stays a forensic practice, no longer a routine necessity.\", \"_ts\": 1781053717.650649, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\", \"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\"]}, \"empty-decoy-store-files\": {\"name\": \"empty-decoy-store-files\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved: removed 0-byte .loops/project.db (Mar 19) and .loops/project.store (May 17) \\u2014 stale artifacts from two prior path-resolution eras; nothing recreates them on the current read path (verified sl read project clean after removal). If they reappear, that is a live resolution bug worth chasing.\", \"_ts\": 1781053719.93213, \"_n\": 2}, \"loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\": {\"name\": \"loops-test-suite-broken-on-main\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Already fixed on main, no new commit. (1) test_readiness_lens.py deleted in release 4ba2e47 (0.4.0); experiments/config-reference is empty, lens lives only in ~/.config/loops/lenses/ untracked. (2) No stray 'loops' self-symlink exists; golden test_validate_demo[FULL] passes (apps/loops/tests/golden/test_validate.py 4 passed). Full apps/loops suite 1342 passed, 1 xfailed. Verified 2026-06-26.\", \"_ts\": 1782527594.059315, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"friction:readiness-lens-test-orphaned\", \"friction:stray-self-symlink-breaks-validate-golden\"]}, \"init-registers-ephemeral-instances\": {\"name\": \"init-registers-ephemeral-instances\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Second occurrence of /tmp pollution in the config project aggregator: sl init project run in a scratch dir auto-registers the instance with the user-global aggregator (_register_with_aggregator), leaving a dangling combine ref when the dir is deleted (d2-smoke 2026-06-09, keygen-smoke 2026-06-12 \\u2014 both found and hand-removed). Fix-shape options: (a) skip aggregator registration when the instance path is under /tmp or $TMPDIR; (b) --no-register flag for smoke work; (c) ls/read prune-on-missing with a receipt. Two occurrences = emit friction; a third earns the fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.650323, \"_n\": 1}, \"check-should-read-rule-from-receipt\": {\"name\": \"check-should-read-rule-from-receipt\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"rebirth --check requires --rule to be re-asserted manually, but the receipt fact already records the transform rule \\u2014 running --check without it re-runs IDENTITY against a ulid-migration rebirth and reports false mismatches (live scare 2026-06-12, mid fold-determinism validation: rows 6-9 'mismatched' before I realized the rule defaulted). The receipt is the attestation; the verifier asking the operator to restate what the artifact attests is backwards. Fix: --check reads rule from the receipt fact, --rule becomes an override-with-warning. Small, but it is exactly the class of bug the attestation arc exists to prevent \\u2014 trust the signed claim, not operator memory.\", \"_ts\": 1781283629.808185, \"_n\": 1}, \"add-verb-gap-boundary-and-preview\": {\"name\": \"add-verb-gap-boundary-and-preview\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Extending the signing era today required adding 'boundary when=seal' + a seal kind decl to five vertex files \\u2014 sl add <v> kind exists and could have done the kind half, but there is NO 'sl add <v> boundary' (or preview) verb, so half the edit had no tool and I hand-rolled a python depth-scanning splice for BOTH halves. Pattern worth naming: a partial verb surface causes total bypass \\u2014 when the tool covers 50% of a compound edit, the operator does 100% manually and the splice/validate machinery (kdl_splice, parse-before-write) protects nothing. Fix shape: add boundary + preview subcommands to the add verb; they are single-line splices, the library already exists.\", \"_ts\": 1781283630.114335, \"_n\": 1}, \"zsh-equals-globbing\": {\"name\": \"zsh-equals-globbing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Added 'Shell notes (zsh)' subsection to CLAUDE.md (commit 1286cc9): bare = globbing -> use --- or quote, plus quoting/word-split/cwd guidance.\", \"_ts\": 1782527585.941349, \"_n\": 2}, \"root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\": {\"name\": \"root-pyproject-dep-mirror-gap\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"The repo ships as a FLAT vendored wheel: root pyproject (strange-loops) bundles every libs/*/src via hatchling and does NOT depend on the workspace members \\u2014 so root [project].dependencies must mirror the UNION of all vendored libs' third-party deps BY HAND. A dep added to a lib (engine's rfc8785, added with the JCS migration c1f50ed) is invisible to `uv tool install .` until it is also added to root. `uv run --package` masks the gap because it resolves the workspace env, not the flat wheel. SYMPTOM today: `uv tool install . -e --reinstall` uninstalled rfc8785 (it had survived only as a leftover from the 2026-06-12 ceremony's ad-hoc install) \\u2192 every `sl` command died with \\\"ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rfc8785'\\\" at engine import. FIXED: added rfc8785>=0.1.4 to root pyproject with a comment documenting the mirror requirement; sl restored, verified. RESIDUAL (why this stays open): the gap is structural and SILENT \\u2014 nothing enforces root \\u2287 union(libs); the next lib-dep addition reintroduces it, caught only on a fresh tool install. Candidate fixes: (a) a check diffing root deps vs the lib union, wired into ./dev check; (b) make root actually depend on the workspace members instead of vendoring source; (c) dissolve via lib consolidation (thread:lib-consolidation-reconsider \\u2014 this friction IS the tax). Reinforces the standing anchor that installed-sl is the production path and the workspace-runner form masks staleness.\", \"_ts\": 1781453970.506486, \"_n\": 1}, \"shell-oneliner-punctuation-and-wordsplit\": {\"name\": \"shell-oneliner-punctuation-and-wordsplit\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Folded into the CLAUDE.md Shell notes (zsh) subsection (commit 1286cc9): non-ascii punctuation (U+FF1B), grep|while IFS= read over for-loops on $(...), keep cwd in same compound line.\", \"_ts\": 1782527586.229047, \"_n\": 2}, \"no-clean-lint-my-delta-move\": {\"name\": \"no-clean-lint-my-delta-move\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Option b done (commit 22493bb): ruff check --select F401 --fix removed 87 pre-existing unused imports repo-wide; F401 baseline now clean so future findings == my delta. One residual unfixable F401 in docs/autoresearch/make_chart.py (pre-existing py311 f-string-backslash syntax error blocks parsing). All package suites green post-fix.\", \"_ts\": 1782527594.224584, \"_n\": 2}, \"stale-git-index-lock-recurring\": {\"name\": \"stale-git-index-lock-recurring\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"workflow\", \"message\": \"git index.lock blocked 'git add/commit' twice this session; rm -f .git/index.lock cleared it both times. Some background git process (rtk wrapper, IDE indexer, or a crashed prior git) leaves the lock. Low-severity but recurring \\u2014 interrupts the commit flow at exactly the wrap moment. Fix unclear yet (identify the lock-leaver first); parking as named friction so the next occurrence promotes rather than re-surprises.\", \"_ts\": 1781575585.987684, \"_n\": 1}, \"block-text-multiline-passthrough-broke-on-040\": {\"name\": \"block-text-multiline-passthrough-broke-on-040\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Narrowed 2026-07-11 (audit sweep). Two of three originally-cited blast-radius sites are FIXED: store.py verify (was :278) migrated to callout, store.py reanchor (was :396) now composes via join_vertical(*(Block.text(ln,...) for ln in lines)) -- both explicitly commented 'never Block.text(newline.join(...))'. The dry-run-payload site (emit.py:1111) uses json.dumps output, single-line by construction, not actually at risk. REMAINING, verified live and still broken: emit.py's seal-refused error handler does Block.text(f'seal refused: {e}\\\\n  the window's facts are stored...', p.error) -- a direct multiline f-string through Block.text. Confirmed empirically: Block.text('line1\\\\nline2\\\\nline3', Style()).height == 1 on the currently-pinned painted>=0.10.0 -- the C0-neutralization behavior from 0.4.0 is still current upstream behavior, not something later painted versions changed. FIX unchanged: compose via join_vertical, not raw Block.text with embedded newlines.\", \"_ts\": 1783804676.527936, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\", \"thread:painted-040-gate\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\"}, \"fts-match-limit-100-silent-cap\": {\"name\": \"fts-match-limit-100-silent-cap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED in 090-S2, disclosure-form per arbitration F2: default limit unchanged; search peeks limit+1, sets Window.truncated (new field, --json additive), TTY footer names the cap with a narrow-the-query hint. No silent cap remains; correct by construction after the sol-P2 fix (truncation computed over the kind-restricted result).\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"_ts\": 1784402391.421046, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/match-rebinds-onto-read-search-transform\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVAQC4KCF6C4GABVR9Q4SM9\"}, \"cli-smoke-needs-shared-boundary-vertex-fixture\": {\"name\": \"cli-smoke-needs-shared-boundary-vertex-fixture\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-test\", \"message\": \"Closed by G6b (6cc4005): write_grammar_fixture + session-scoped grammar_store conftest fixture \\u2014 real vertex+store, keyed+collect folds, refs, two tick boundaries, deterministic ts\", \"_ts\": 1783118353.516513, \"_n\": 3, \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\"}, \"cli-no-version-flag\": {\"name\": \"cli-no-version-flag\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved. Verified live 2026-07-11: sl --version returns 'loops 0.5.0' cleanly, no fallthrough to vertex dispatch error.\", \"_ts\": 1783799980.477349, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF\", \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\"]}, \"emit-verbose-receipt-silent\": {\"name\": \"emit-verbose-receipt-silent\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED \\u2014 already fixed on spine, root cause finally named: the say/do gap was emit-time vs read-time ref RESOLUTION ASYMMETRY. At filing (S8 era), _resolve_entity_refs only handled slash-form addresses (decision/design/x); the canonical colon form (decision:design/x) never resolved at emit, so resolved_refs stayed empty and the -v inbound line was correctly suppressed \\u2014 while the read-side REFS view resolved colon refs fine, making the edge 'land' visibly. The typed-edges wave (267146a) rewrote the resolver and fixed it as a side effect. Verified: pre-fix tree f52addb reproduces, spine doesn't. What actually shipped now (8281a18): a CLI-path regression net \\u2014 existing TestInboundDelta cases hand-rolled Namespace objects and never exercised the argv/parser seam the bug lived in; 3 new tests drive _run_emit with raw argv and FAIL on the pre-fix tree. Test-only change.\", \"_ts\": 1783294014.127242, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"emit-ref-resolution-colon-blind\": {\"name\": \"emit-ref-resolution-colon-blind\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"FIXED this session: resolve.py parses kind:key colon-canonically (new _split_addr \\u2014 colon binds tighter so key may contain /; slash kept for back-compat; _is_addr_candidate whitespace-guard blocks prose false-WARNs). 1473 green incl 7 new colon regression tests + 1 bug-codifying test corrected. Smoke via installed sl: colon -v fires inbound-delta + (refs:N resolved); colon ref to missing entity WARNs. Found-during-S8-smoke; own commit pending Kyle.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7EFKXM49FCD53FEAVJ2R9D\", \"_ts\": 1782663030.35366, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction/emit-verbose-receipt-silent\", \"thread/interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"salience-inbound-colon-blind\": {\"name\": \"salience-inbound-colon-blind\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"FIXED: surface.py _inbound_count matches the canonical colon form (suffix :key alongside /key and bare). Regold: 3 test_walked goldens (walk-target gains the inbound badge). 1473 green. Live eyeball: interactive-read-path-redesign inbound 0->26 (sal 34), cli-render-rebuild 0->20, peer-grant-recast 0->24 \\u2014 referenced hubs surface correctly; session aggregates stay n-driven; monotonic-upward. Built-in fold only; live identity/session lenses keep their own copied helpers (FF).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7FY9JHT7GKDN26CRERJERQ\", \"_ts\": 1782663494.192034, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction/emit-ref-resolution-colon-blind\", \"friction:emit-ref-resolution-colon-blind\", \"thread/interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"read-address-separator-colon-vs-slash\": {\"name\": \"read-address-separator-colon-vs-slash\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED commit 1b0e1e8: the colon ref-idiom address (kind colon key) is now rejected with rc=2 and a slash-form suggestion instead of silently widening to the whole fold. Whether colon should become a true address SYNONYM is left as a deferred grammar decision, not minted here -- belongs with address-grammar unification.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8MTKJ3KJ6EV6FEJ1BNABQN\", \"_ts\": 1782703835.724663, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"read-tty-truncation-not-defeatable\": {\"name\": \"read-tty-truncation-not-defeatable\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"PARTIAL (commit facad4b): the --match 80-cap and the fact-body len-not-wcwidth halves are FIXED -- both render paths now go through budget_fields (full body on a pipe, plus-Nc hint on a TTY). REMAINING, deferred to the reframe (plan:curation-in-surface in-band-defeat): (a) --plain flips use_ansi but not width, so no in-band untruncated layout -- needs a dedicated --wide seam; (b) -v/DETAILED truncates harder and drops the plus-Nc marker. Both are in-band-defeat / announce-loss concerns, not cheap fixes.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8MTKJ3KJ6EV6FEJ1BNABQN,01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ\", \"_ts\": 1782703835.877111, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"fold-lens-render-diverges-from-faithful-surface\": {\"name\": \"fold-lens-render-diverges-from-faithful-surface\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"PARKED at reconcile 2026-08-12 (status catch-up): this was already explicitly parked by decision:workflow/umwelt-bugs-first-reframe-parked \\u2014 the feat/curation-in-surface reframe branch remains unmerged (verified). The friction fact just never carried the parked status. Reopen condition: the curation-in-surface reframe gets picked back up.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA7SHYK0MX1C2ZVN0YCNA7B\", \"_ts\": 1786565563.926508, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\", \"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"live-mode-hangs-silently-on-pipe\": {\"name\": \"live-mode-hangs-silently-on-pipe\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (loops-side) commit d9d518b on fix/umwelt-render-divergences: _resolve_mode gates --live on is_tty, downgrades to static on a pipe and announces on stderr. Verified rc=0, static rendered, no hang. The painted belt-and-suspenders (emit-first-frame-then-return for non-tty streams) remains a painted-side follow-up.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8MTKJ3KJ6EV6FEJ1BNABQN\", \"_ts\": 1782703835.282347, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"facts-empty-for-collect-fold-kinds\": {\"name\": \"facts-empty-for-collect-fold-kinds\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED commit a882431: the --facts skip and its skipped_sections / No-history footer residue removed; collect-fold rows now render as the raw fact stream the flag promises. --facts --kind cite shows all 36 rows. Regolded test_facts.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8MTKJ3KJ6EV6FEJ1BNABQN\", \"_ts\": 1782703835.561593, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"secondary-lines-clip-without-marker\": {\"name\": \"secondary-lines-clip-without-marker\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-render\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED by the truncation-drop on fix/umwelt-render-divergences. The channel-parity verification (detail-zooms probe) found painted emits full detail-zoom secondary lines as single long logical lines at EVERY width (max line 2906 unchanged from PTYCOLS=100 down to 40) \\u2014 nothing clips, so the \\\"clip without marker\\\" silent-data-loss this friction named cannot occur. Whitespace-stripped body diff TTY vs pipe = 0 at -v and -vv across thread/decision/hypothesis. The terminal soft-wraps the long line (no content lost). The marker fix was for a clip that the truncation-drop removed; if an opt-in width-fit render is ever reintroduced, the wrap-marker concern returns as a fresh consideration of THAT design, not this deferred item.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9W9683JZEFBKEE2C9G0TCG\", \"_ts\": 1782755149.382989, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/drop-truncation-from-human-reads\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"], \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\"}, \"loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored\": {\"name\": \"loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-skill\", \"message\": \"REOPENED same reconcile 2026-08-12, correcting my own premature resolve an hour earlier: the tracked copy at clients/claude-code/skills/loops/SKILL.md exists (995ff40) \\u2014 the no-backup half IS addressed \\u2014 but the LIVE canonical source is still the gitignored one: ~/.config/claude/skills/loops symlinks to .claude/skills/loops (verified), whose SKILL.md (Jul 21) has DRIFTED from the tracked copy (diff confirms, verified live). The friction is now the divergence: repoint the symlink at clients/, or reconcile the two and make tracked the source of truth. Credit: fr1 evidence agent caught what th2's shallower receipt (and my ruling on it) missed \\u2014 existence of a tracked copy is not canonicity.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS9R4HE7NWN8AFYW3K0FCX\", \"_ts\": 1786565543.427648, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/loops-skill-global-bootstrap-observer\", \"thread:loops-practice-skill\"]}, \"text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions\": {\"name\": \"text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-render\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"Surfaced by the channel-parity verification (json-vs-text probe): 11 of 509 decisions render with NO body in BOTH text channels (TTY + pipe, verified identical) \\u2014 their content lives in legacy non-message fold fields (position x7, rationale x3, body x1), and only --json surfaces it. Affected keys: architecture/lib-dependency-graph, architecture/chain-headers, architecture/dissolved-apps, architecture/progressive-claude-libs-complete, architecture/progressive-claude-apps-complete, architecture/vertex-boundary, architecture/replay-works, data/exchange-full-fidelity, arch/parse-at-vertex, arch/siftd-harness-topology, design/vouch-write-path-e2e-landed. This is NOT a channel divergence (identical on TTY and pipe) and is PRE-EXISTING (predates fix/umwelt-render-divergences) \\u2014 the umwelt parity work neither caused nor touched it. But it IS a faithful-read gap: both human and agent text reads silently drop real content json carries. FIX-SHAPE: the headline extraction (gist/fold) falls back to the first content-bearing payload field when message is absent \\u2014 a render fix that gives both text umwelts the missing bodies; alternatively backfill the 11 to the message fold key. Render-fallback is the cleaner dissolution (data stays as-is, the read gets faithful).\", \"_ts\": 1782755149.080829, \"_n\": 1}, \"loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong\": {\"name\": \"loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-skill\", \"message\": \"The now-global loops skill documented cite as `sl cite <vertex> kind:key ...` \\u2014 WRONG, and it bit me on the first real cite this session: cite has NO vertex positional (it is dissolved into emit; all positionals are refs), so `project` became a stray ref and the cite landed in the cwd-inferred vertex (not project) with every decision ref dropped. CORRECT forms: vertex-first `sl <vertex> cite REF REF -m` (targets a named vertex, sets ctx.vertex_path) OR cwd-local `sl cite REF REF -m` (from a vertex dir). ROOT of the trap: emit takes the vertex as a positional (`sl emit <vertex> KIND`), cite does NOT \\u2014 an asymmetry easy to mis-document. FIXED the skill cite line in the same change. Validates friction:loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored live: the skill is now canonical infra, so an error in it propagates to every repo agent \\u2014 caught here only because I exercised it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA5NV2RS73PXZ4C169B3BHN\", \"_ts\": 1782755516.339307, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored\"]}, \"vertex-first-dispatch-legacy-complexity\": {\"name\": \"vertex-first-dispatch-legacy-complexity\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"feature\": \"cli-grammar-uniformity\", \"message\": \"Vertex-first dispatch (tier 3: sl <vertex> <verb>) is convenience-era complexity from when the CLI was small (Kyle 2026-06-29) \\u2014 removing it is a CORRECTNESS + SIMPLIFICATION win and dissolves the cite-syntax asymmetry at its ROOT (friction:loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong was the symptom). It bundles TWO jobs: (1) bare implicit-read `sl project`->read (high-value shorthand); (2) vertex-first OP `sl project cite`/`sl reading add` (legacy duplication of verb-first). Job 2 is the friction: emit takes the vertex AFTER the verb (sl emit <vertex>) but cite has no vertex slot, so vertex-first was the ONLY way to target a vertex with cite -> two grammars, one asymmetry, easy to mis-document. REMOVING tier-3 deletes the bulk of app.py intricacy: _vertex_first, _identify_op_token (op-past-global-flags), _is_predicate_token, the _peel_observer before/after-op split, VERTEX_OPS + population-op argv reconstruction. CORRECTNESS: one grammar per verb; eliminates the \\\"is arg0 a vertex or unknown command?\\\" class (a vertex named like a verb cannot shadow it). REQUIRED COMPANION: verbs take the vertex UNIFORMLY as a positional \\u2014 cite gains a vertex arg (sl cite <vertex> REF), consistent with emit \\u2014 a grammar that cannot be mis-stated, the structural fix vs a doc patch. OPEN DECISION (shapes the work): fate of bare implicit-read sl project->read \\u2014 (a) keep it as a narrow rule + reserve verb names (verb wins on collision), removing only the op form; or (b) full uniformity sl <verb> <vertex> everywhere, zero arg0 ambiguity but sl project->sl read project. Automation already uses verb-first (low migration risk, grep of hooks/config clean); the human-facing change is the implicit-read shorthand. Design+build deserves its own focused session (touches the live dispatch every agent + hook uses).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA84QXKT39MSGKGVDWYV7HA\", \"_ts\": 1782756895.933593, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loops-skill-cite-syntax-wrong\"]}, \"plugin-hooks-double-fire-local-residue\": {\"name\": \"plugin-hooks-double-fire-local-residue\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"feature\": \"loops-claude-code-plugin\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (Kyle verified 2026-06-29 post-reload). Local settings.local.json hooks block removed \\u2192 plugin session-open.sh is now sole writer. Confirmed: project shows one session status=open per SessionStart (21:37 + 21:41, 4min apart = two distinct starts, not a same-second double-fire). No double emit.\", \"_ts\": 1782769832.273772, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KWAMDX3EFGQC1540HTC1MZM7\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-claude-code-plugin\"]}, \"register-split-piped-faithfulness-untested\": {\"name\": \"register-split-piped-faithfulness-untested\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"rendering\", \"message\": \"Root cause dissolved rather than instances patched: this was an instance of two-surface-claims-lack-parity-tests. The parity harness now regression-guards signed/share/span presence and no-truncation on ls root, ls <v>, ls --kind, store stats.\", \"_ts\": 1782940945.92984, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"friction:two-surface-claims-lack-parity-tests\"], \"ref_ref\": \"01KWFRZK70YDG26T06S9ZP0TNP\"}, \"cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\": {\"name\": \"cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Verb-first 'sl cite REF...' has no vertex argument at all (refs are its positionals) \\u2014 it silently resolves a local/fallback vertex from cwd (doesn't look in .loops/), dropping unresolvable refs with WARN-only, storing an empty attention signal. Only the vertex-first form 'sl project cite' targets correctly \\u2014 but vertex-first was meant to be stripped (intended grammar: sl <cmd> <vertex-if-required>). Fix: give cite a vertex slot in verb-first grammar; consider ref-drop escalating to failure when ALL refs drop (a cite with zero resolved refs is meaningless). Two orphaned empty cites left in the fallback store 2026-07-01.\", \"_ts\": 1782938204.726143, \"_n\": 1}, \"two-surface-claims-lack-parity-tests\": {\"name\": \"two-surface-claims-lack-parity-tests\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved by merge of feat/parity-tests (2026-07-01): channel-parity harness (tests/parity.py) \\u2014 one fetch rendered through both registers, chrome-stripped, every load-bearing token asserted on both channels; piped register proven untruncated at deliberately narrow width (locks width=None contract). Convention documented in apps/loops/CLAUDE.md + tests/README.md; adoption ~3 lines. Receipt-vs-read parity axis lands after feat/typed-edges merges.\", \"_ts\": 1782940945.631892, \"_n\": 2}, \"rail-drowns-under-full-bodies\": {\"name\": \"rail-drowns-under-full-bodies\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (Kyle smoke session 2026-07-03/04): candidate (a)+(c) fused \\u2014 bodies too long for their row drop to a hanging wrapped block under the key column (rail column stays clean), height-capped 4 lines at orientation zoom with '\\u2026 [+Nc \\u00b7 -v]' tail; -v/exact-address uncapped. deba181. Root cause was width=None on TTY static dispatch (drop-truncation-from-human-reads) \\u2014 now real width, wrap-never-clip.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWNA60VKT3Q2C3VN7WCCCEE9\", \"_ts\": 1783132784.06284, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/fold-body-hanging-block\", \"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"breaking-cli-flag-change-broke-consumer-hooks-silently\": {\"name\": \"breaking-cli-flag-change-broke-consumer-hooks-silently\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"0.5.0 removed the --max-lines/--max-chars flag family from read; gruel.network's SessionStart hook (first out-of-repo consumer) still passed --max-lines, got an argparse usage error on stderr, and its fail-silent design (|| true, never block session start) swallowed it \\u2014 the session opened with ZERO vertex context and nothing signaled the loss. Two shapes here: (1) CLI breaking changes propagate invisibly into consumer hooks; a removed flag could exit with a deprecation hint ('--max-lines is gone; fidelity is now -q/--limit/--fields') instead of generic usage. (2) fail-silent consumers can't distinguish empty-store from broken-contract; the practice may want a hook smoke-check after upgrades. Found by relay in gruel.network 2026-07-03.\", \"_ts\": 1783099217.518121, \"_n\": 1}, \"orient-hook-assumes-single-project-vertex\": {\"name\": \"orient-hook-assumes-single-project-vertex\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"clients/claude-code/hooks/lib.sh resolves V to .loops/.vertex first \\u2014 correct in this repo, wrong in a workspace-shaped repo where .vertex is the aggregator/workspace file. In gruel.network the orient block confidently printed 'open: 0 threads \\u00b7 0 frictions' while the relay vertex had 5 open threads, and its 'deeper' pointers referenced a project vertex that is a near-empty shadow of the global one. A confidently-wrong orient is worse than none. Fix-shape options: (a) detect workspace files and aggregate counts across discovered vertexes; (b) resolve to the repo's emitting vertex (whoami-adjacent) rather than first-file-wins; (c) skip the block when V has no thread/friction/seal kinds declared. Found by relay in gruel.network 2026-07-03, first multi-vertex workspace consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1783099233.370516, \"_n\": 1}, \"skill-hardcodes-practice-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"skill-hardcodes-practice-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"The portable loops skill (clients/claude-code skill, symlinked to ~/.config/claude/skills/loops) specifies the practice at the vocabulary level \\u2014 thread/friction/log/seal kinds, sweep/reconcile cadence, status vocab \\u2014 as if every store declares them. It predates the semantic reframe (painted -> semantic renderer; loops -> semantic data substrate, in progress). Stores with other shapes (relay identity store, monitor telemetry store, the hypothetical novel/RP store from the reframe conversation) have no landing place for the practice as written: gruel.network accumulated real frictions as observations/practices because no local vertex declares friction/log. The skill should teach the semantic layer \\u2014 fold-key discipline, refs-as-architecture, capture cadence as a PATTERN to instantiate per store shape \\u2014 and carry the thread/friction/seal vocabulary as one worked instantiation, not the spec. Found by relay in gruel.network 2026-07-03.\", \"_ts\": 1783099233.67374, \"_n\": 1}, \"per-section-salience-budget-missing\": {\"name\": \"per-section-salience-budget-missing\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"0.5.0's --limit is global top-N by salience; there is no per-section (per-kind) budget in a single read. The SessionStart-context use case wants 'top-3 of each kind' \\u2014 census (-q) is too little, full fold (35KB for relay) is too much, global --limit 3 collapses a 7-kind fold to 3 rows from whichever kinds dominate salience. Workaround in gruel.network hook: N reads, one per kind, concatenated. Fix-shape: --limit accepting a per-section mode (e.g. --limit 3 --by kind, mirroring --count --by), or a zoom level between census and full. Found by relay rewriting the broken hook 2026-07-03; companion to friction/breaking-cli-flag-change-broke-consumer-hooks-silently.\", \"_ts\": 1783099429.630748, \"_n\": 1}, \"emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\": {\"name\": \"emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Superseded by design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress \\u2014 message=-/@file ride the batch reader (item 4); quick-capture (sl note) explicitly held out as its own future verb, tracked in the design's open question.\", \"_ts\": 1783917722.545805, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCWG65M5YB2S4HN3EZ00CFE\", \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\"]}, \"fold-key-mistakes-leave-orphan-sediment\": {\"name\": \"fold-key-mistakes-leave-orphan-sediment\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Fold keys are per-vertex per-kind (topic= vs name= vs agent=) and must be known BEFORE emit; the WARN receipt names the expected key (good) but only after storing an orphaned <no-fold> fact. Hit 3x in one day migrating gruel.network memories: decision name= vs topic=, then 6 relationship facts with name= vs agent= \\u2014 7 orphan facts now permanent sediment beside their corrected re-emits. Fix-shapes: (a) interactive emits could default strict (reject, don't store, when fold key missing \\u2014 strict mode exists but isn't default); (b) an emit preflight that echoes the kind's fold shape; (c) orphan-fact cleanup story (compact that drops <no-fold>? explicit tombstone?). The receipt catches the mistake; the substrate still keeps the wreckage.\", \"_ts\": 1783105013.003478, \"_n\": 1}, \"no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\": {\"name\": \"no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Superseded by design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress \\u2014 the ndjson batch surface (--ndjson file|stdin, sync-source grammar) is item 1 of that design.\", \"_ts\": 1783917722.338703, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCWG65M5YB2S4HN3EZ00CFE\", \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\"]}, \"seal-fanout-across-workspace-stores\": {\"name\": \"seal-fanout-across-workspace-stores\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Split and superseded: authoring half \\u2192 design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress (batch as one authored act); cross-store simultaneity half \\u2192 thread:workspace-linked-cuts (needs its own primitive, not a seal overload).\", \"_ts\": 1783917722.713148, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCWG65M5YB2S4HN3EZ00CFE,01KXC7PKABNSE6A6PNDHY8XSR7\", \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"thread:workspace-linked-cuts\"]}, \"discover-root-replay-cascade-duplication\": {\"name\": \"discover-root-replay-cascade-duplication\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"Resolved on fix/discover-cascade (c2643dd): replay no longer appends or mints anywhere \\u2014 regression tests hold member stores byte-stable across repeated loads. The cross-host child-skip + signer pass-down from the diagnosis session committed as 5a2fe3c. Remaining design question split to thread:discover-children-as-cascade-targets.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWMXNW9267KNMPZ1Z4PTSCEN\", \"_ts\": 1783113642.575714, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/replay-fold-only-cascade\", \"friction:seal-fanout-across-workspace-stores\"], \"feature\": \"discover-cascade\"}, \"vertex-parse-error-opacity\": {\"name\": \"vertex-parse-error-opacity\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12, verified by two reproductions: (1) the same-line trailing-comment form that triggered the original failure now parses clean; (2) a genuinely malformed .vertex now raises 'ParseError <file>:1: Unexpected end of data' naming the offending FILE and line, not the parser internals. Minor caveat recorded: the line number is the node start, not always the precise offending line.\", \"_ts\": 1786565545.413818, \"_n\": 2}, \"emits-silently-unattributed\": {\"name\": \"emits-silently-unattributed\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Confluence's FIRST live read surfaced 354 unattributed facts ('' observer) including every emit since ~Jul 1: resolve_observer falls flag -> LOOPS_OBSERVER -> .loops/.vertex -> global, and the skill's per-session 'export LOOPS_OBSERVER' convention silently lapsed; project.vertex declares TWO observers so auto-pick correctly refuses and returns ''. Emit succeeds with empty observer \\u2014 no warning, attribution just drains. FIXED durably: LOOPS_OBSERVER=kyle/loops-claude now set in .claude/settings.local.json env block (applies to all future session shells); historical 354 stay unattributed (append-only, honest history). Residue question for reconcile: should emit WARN on empty observer when the vertex declares observers? (the store accepts it by design \\u2014 decision:declare-observer-print-not-write \\u2014 but silence is what let this drain for days). Meta: the observer cut caught this in its first minute of existence \\u2014 the view's raison d'etre demonstrated on its own build session.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWNTFANW1MNWTGD8KQEB7D3C\", \"_ts\": 1783144340.235996, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/confluence-build1-scope\"]}, \"vertex-boundary-last-declaration-wins\": {\"name\": \"vertex-boundary-last-declaration-wins\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (a12e699, merged to spine @beafa46): loader accumulated \\u2014 VertexFile.boundary is now tuple[Boundary,...], the loops{} handler appends instead of overwriting; engine holds a list of _VertexBoundarySpec and evaluates ALL (semantics: first match fires, declaration order, one fact mints one tick \\u2014 preserves the single-boundary-per-fire contract, no double-minting; vertex-boundary kinds can't collide with loop-boundary kinds so fall-through is harmless); fetch_horizon emits one armed row per vertex boundary; seal accepts a when=seal boundary among several. Regression tests at all three layers. LIVE-VERIFIED: sl read session --lens horizon now shows 2 armed \\u2014 the previously-dropped 'session closed' boundary renders alongside 'seal'.\", \"_ts\": 1783294008.935615, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQ80E1RRKTT0680VXP3VAND\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/horizon-build1-scope\"]}, \"fts-search-declaration-not-retroactive\": {\"name\": \"fts-search-declaration-not-retroactive\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED in 090-S2 (765a11b): sl store reindex performs a full DROP+CREATE against the CURRENT declaration set \\u2014 declaring search on an already-populated kind then running reindex indexes all pre-declaration facts (pinned by retroactive-indexing test). The old monotonic last_rowid cursor that could never re-scan is gone with _ensure_fts. Until reindex runs, the gap is DISCLOSED: Window.stale names declared-but-unindexed kinds with a run-reindex hint, results still arrive via substring fallback \\u2014 zero silent empty results.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVAQC4KCF6C4GABVR9Q4SM9\", \"_unresolved_refs\": [{\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"kind\": \"decision\", \"key\": \"architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\"}], \"_ts\": 1784402391.256588, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"friction:fts-match-limit-100-silent-cap\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"codex-exec-stdin-hang\": {\"name\": \"codex-exec-stdin-hang\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"codex exec hangs indefinitely ('Reading additional input from stdin...') when run backgrounded/detached \\u2014 it waits on an open stdin that never closes; burned 3.5h on the S1 review believing it was working. Earlier diagnosis (awk-filter buffering) was wrong \\u2014 that only hid the symptom. FIX, now convention for the internal-table build review pipeline: always invoke codex exec with stdin closed: codex exec ... < /dev/null. Foreground harness calls closed stdin implicitly, which is why inline S0 reviews worked.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX9QY9EF26CNXNBPRDSDT917\", \"_ts\": 1783828986.089354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:workflow/internal-table-build-execution-model\"]}, \"seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\": {\"name\": \"seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED in 090-S6 (75ab815 + a981221 sol-P1 TOCTOU fix), substrate-first per arbitration F1: every sl read (plain/piped/--json, any lens) now carries honest cut provenance \\u2014 render_context and --json gain a 'cut' key: {available, mode: head|witness|as_of|unavailable, anchor{name,ts,fact_cursor}|null, sealed_to_head, tick_total, facts_beyond_seal, reason}. available=false ALWAYS carries a reason; witness-mode leaves tick_total/facts_beyond_seal null (not-computed, never guessed 0). Sol P1 hardened it against concurrency: cut resolves AFTER the fold fetch (append-only + ordering makes the residual race conservative \\u2014 can understate sealedness, can never claim sealed over an unsealed render), internal reads are one WAL snapshot transaction, live mode recomputes per frame. NOTE FOR THE N=2 CONSUMERS (homelab-audit, siftd): stop defaulting projection=None to 'Live unsealed fold' \\u2014 read cut; custom lenses receive it by declaring a cut kwarg on fold_view (existing kwarg dispatch forwards it, zero new plumbing). Never render a positive claim when available=false; render unavailable + the stated reason. In-repo banner audit found zero dishonest sites \\u2014 the defect was pure substrate absence, now filled. Default TTY output unchanged (216/216 goldens byte-identical); whether plain sl read should surface a default cut line is queued as a Kyle UX question at wave review. Arbiter note: my fix-spec option 1 proposed an id-order comparison; the agent correctly refused it against the A3 ids-are-never-ordered invariant \\u2014 the substrate-contract lesson from the June chain-window bug, now structurally self-defending.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E\", \"_ts\": 1784406403.582353, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"decl-namespace-search-declarable\": {\"name\": \"decl-namespace-search-declarable\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12 \\u2014 stale on arrival: the declare-time reservation landed eaa8297/40cb4e8 on 2026-07-11, two days BEFORE the friction was filed. validator.py:316-322 rejects _decl.* declarations at exactly the chokepoint named, wired into the ordinary load path (program.py:249 validate-by-default) and independently at sl store absorb (store.py:1023). Verified by reproduction: a .vertex declaring _decl.foo fails validation with the reserved-namespace message.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCNAWM9C1EHDA0GXZS9ZRAR\", \"_ts\": 1786565548.306271, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/internal-table-s3-read-exclusion\"]}, \"boundary-prop-silent-match\": {\"name\": \"boundary-prop-silent-match\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-lang\", \"message\": \"Refined fix-shape (2026-07-15, ticked store-resident-orchestration design): do NOT simply reject unknown boundary props -- the accidental behavior (props compile to match conditions) is exactly the pre-closure validation gate ticked's stage model needs (boundary when=stage + valid=true ticks only on validated completions). Promote to designed, EXPLICIT match syntax (e.g. a match/when-props block) and reject props outside it; silent absorption stays the bug, the capability becomes the feature.\", \"_ts\": 1784174386.243589, \"_n\": 2}, \"no-cli-verb-flat-tick-key\": {\"name\": \"no-cli-verb-flat-tick-key\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the friction's own text was stale a week before it was filed \\u2014 7b5347b (2026-07-09) made any --keygen bootstrap the flat self-observer tick key (add.py:283 ensure_self_observer_signing), covering loops init and loops add observer --keygen. Genuinely absent: only the dedicated 'sl sign init <vertex>' verb (no sign verb exists, verified). Whether that verb is still wanted given the bootstrap coverage is the remaining question \\u2014 likely dissolves.\", \"_ts\": 1786565559.58202, \"_n\": 3, \"ref_ref\": \"01KXP65CW2ZWV343GF1YKWW49Z\", \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\"]}, \"no-conditional-emit\": {\"name\": \"no-conditional-emit\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"Entity-upsert consumers need a conditional emit (CAS): ticked's runner reaps dead workers by upserting work status=finished outcome=error, but between its fold read and the emit the worker may emit finished/replied \\u2014 the later error upsert wins unconditionally. ticked shrinks the window by re-reading the run immediately before reaping, but a real fix is engine-level: receive(fact, expect={field: value}) that refuses when the current folded value diverges (same shape as SqliteStore.absorb_edit's expected_head CAS). Second consumer-driven case after vouch for transactional-ish semantics.\", \"_ts\": 1784005881.249458, \"_n\": 1}, \"session-close-emitter-missing\": {\"name\": \"session-close-emitter-missing\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the close-side emitter exists (995ff40 \\u2014 hooks.json SessionEnd \\u2192 session-close.sh emitting status=closed + seal) and is VERIFIED FIRING: paired boundary session facts at 22:17 (Aug 11) and 19:56 (Aug 12), kyle/loops-claude session fold at n=306 with live status flips, and this session's orient block rendered 'last seal: session close'. Note for future audits: an evidence agent reported the plugin dead from ~/.claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json ({}) \\u2014 the real registry on this machine is ~/.config/claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json (CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR), where loops@gruel is installed. Wrong-path reads of plugin state are a recurring false-positive shape.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXKFK1F0RJNTKJ5VMJSJY15P\", \"_ts\": 1786565408.282012, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:horizon-legibility-gap\"]}, \"no-daemon-shaped-store-access\": {\"name\": \"no-daemon-shaped-store-access\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the engine-side fix-shape landed verbatim in 0.8.0 \\u2014 VertexHandle (1a36971, engine/handle.py rowid-cursor incremental refresh, exported). But grep shows ZERO consumers in apps/ or libs/store \\u2014 ticked and loops-tasks are still CLI-shaped. This is now a cutover friction, not a missing-substrate one; the 0.8.0 wave's own S5-checkpoint-before-cutover gate applies.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXFGJVD1NM81KN42NFC62C1D\", \"_ts\": 1786565556.006739, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:no-conditional-emit\"]}, \"sqlite-probes-in-apps\": {\"name\": \"sqlite-probes-in-apps\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Three raw sqlite3 probes in apps (store.py genesis/marker probe \\u2014 imports engine's private _TICK_ROW_SQL constants; resolve.py lock-aware declaration probe; seal.py signed-era probe) predate an engine surface for the questions they ask. Found when the custody extraction greened the architecture ratchet \\u2014 they accumulated while Rule 2 was red. Now a shrink-only allowlist in tests/test_architecture.py. Fix-shape: engine grows a probe surface (era/genesis/declaration introspection) and the allowlist ratchets to empty. Same family as no-daemon-shaped-store-access: consumer-forced engine needs.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXM4GB6356A3SV8GDD3WXWGM,01KXP65CW2ZWV343GF1YKWW49Z\", \"_ts\": 1784229839.713536, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access\"]}, \"engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\": {\"name\": \"engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"engine-api\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED fdda675, same-day round trip: filed this morning from reading tasked's substrate as a requirements doc, landed tonight. Receipt(fact_id, tick, stored) frozen in engine; Vertex.receive_receipt is the one implementation with receive() as its tick projection (chosen over flipping Vertex.receive's return: 322 call sites, and dozens of 'if tick is not None' truthiness checks would break SILENTLY on an always-truthy Receipt \\u2014 the caller sweep found this before design, not after). VertexProgram.receive returns the Receipt; close() + context managers both layers. Both consumers simplified: cmd_emit drops pre-mint and honors receipt.stored (gate-refusals now 'refused:' rc=2, was 'stored: @ None' rc=0 with zero facts written); tasked Store.emit is now 'with load_vertex_program(...): return program.receive(fact)' and its local Receipt class deleted in favor of the engine's. The stored=False trichotomy fix matters beyond ergonomics: pre-minting FABRICATED write identity for rejected facts \\u2014 the receipt now originates at the append site, so it cannot lie.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXP65CW2ZWV343GF1YKWW49Z\", \"_ts\": 1784255004.844527, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access\"]}, \"as-of-silent-drop-on-fold-path\": {\"name\": \"as-of-silent-drop-on-fold-path\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (2026-07-16, same session): read router now refuses temporal flags (--since/--as-of/--id) on the fold route \\u2014 exit 2 + reporter error naming the supported spellings (--facts --since/--as-of/--id for stream, --ticks --since/--as-of) \\u2014 instead of silently rendering head. Scope was WIDER than first emitted: --since and --id were dropped identically, and the repo CLAUDE.md documented the broken bare idiom ('sl read project --since 7d') \\u2014 doc corrected to --facts --since in the same change. Pinned by tests/test_read_router_temporal_guard.py (10 tests: refusal class + cursor-carrying routes + fold unaffected). 2020 pass. The refusal is interim honesty; fold-state-as-of lands with the 0.8.0 temporal cursor and lifts it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ40F0P2HQFJHTN0Z10CMD2\", \"_ts\": 1784261325.096197, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/roadmap-060-static-honest-wave\", \"decision:design/roadmap-070-substrate-cut\"]}, \"fts-grep-splits-punctuated-terms\": {\"name\": \"fts-grep-splits-punctuated-terms\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: 090-s2 (765a11b) shipped the substring fallback + stale/unindexed disclosure \\u2014 punctuated queries now return hits and absence is no longer silent (verified live: '0.7.0', 'digest-coverage', 'Peer/Grant' all hit via the fallback path). REMAINING defect: store_reader.py:677 still passes the raw query to facts_fts MATCH with no quote-aware phrasing, so on a FRESHLY reindexed kind the FTS path itself still splits punctuated terms. The claim is now that narrow.\", \"_ts\": 1786565419.101015, \"_n\": 2}, \"typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\": {\"name\": \"typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12: fixed by 0.9.0 typed Address(kind,key) \\u2014 6591420 converged emit/read/match on canonical full-address comparison (+106 address tests, +55 typed-edge tests), 1b523b7 added slash-form dual-reading. The arrays-as-multi-edge clause was deliberately split into design:atoms/typed-edge-array-values (proposed), so it is not residue here.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KS1KKHTDB765S6X1KTKQR2HB,01KWFPBY99R304Z7MQE3A91SFD,01KWF7DDCHRJ3VB61SVSAQDXWQ\", \"_ts\": 1786565394.367538, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:architecture/typed-edge-emit-fold-split\"]}, \"search-read-mutates-canonical-store\": {\"name\": \"search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED in 090-S2 (765a11b + e772d74 sol-P2 fix): sl store reindex is now the SOLE index writer (aggregates recurse per child, explicitly); _ensure_fts DELETED; vertex_search provably read-only (byte-identity tests + live verification, store .db byte-stable across any number of --match reads). Aggregation aggravator closed on both axes: reads mutate ZERO child stores (pinned by test), writes recurse only via the explicit verb. Sol P2 caught a crowding defect in the first cut (stale-kind matches filled the limit before kind-filtering, silently dropping fresh-kind hits) \\u2014 fixed by constraining SQL to trustworthy kinds BEFORE limit.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E\", \"_ts\": 1784402390.920535, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"friction:fts-search-declaration-not-retroactive\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"graph-fetch-drops-key\": {\"name\": \"graph-fetch-drops-key\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED in 090-S3 (b163fa4 + 3a94cc5): fetch_graph honors --key (live proof: unfiltered 1319 nodes -> 112 under --key architecture/, was byte-identical in build-1); refusal idiom generalized via _fetch_accepts \\u2014 --edge without a fetch that declares it refuses with teaching message, and sol-P2 hardened it further: explicit-but-EMPTY --edge selector refuses too (silent-full under an explicit selector is the same violation as silent-drop). Honor-or-refuse now holds at flag-presence, flag-target, and flag-value levels.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E\", \"_ts\": 1784404661.015588, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"sqlite-readonly-forensics-blocked-by-wal\": {\"name\": \"sqlite-readonly-forensics-blocked-by-wal\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"Promoted from repeated reroute (twice this session: main-loop and a workflow provenance agent independently hit it): sqlite3 file:PATH?mode=ro against a live store fails with error 14 when the WAL sidecar cannot be created (sandboxed shells), forcing byte-copy-to-tmp as the standing workaround for any read-only forensics. Fix shapes to weigh: document mode=ro plus immutable=1 as the sanctioned forensics form (safe only absent a concurrent writer), or provide a first-class read surface for raw fact queries so forensics does not need direct sqlite at all (sl store <db> exists \\u2014 check whether it covers ad-hoc SQL-shaped questions or needs a --sql/--jsonl form; overlaps the canonical-review-export core).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV3VYD2V51D2D53HA1TTZ15\", \"_ts\": 1784395501.942644, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\"]}, \"release-pairing-inter-dep-cap\": {\"name\": \"release-pairing-inter-dep-cap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-07-18 both halves: (1) the instance \\u2014 0.8.1 shipped widening the cap (42b5a4f, v0.8.1 on PyPI, tasked T1 unblocked); (2) the fix-shape \\u2014 the sibling-release cap cross-check is now a release-skill checklist line (7d8d195: step-0 precondition bullet + failure-mode entry 'Sibling release excludes sibling'), exactly the checklist-line-not-machinery form this friction asked for.\", \"_ts\": 1784398272.06816, \"_n\": 2, \"ops\": \"release\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV6SNFZ51CSHHYD0HG65465\", \"_refs\": [\"thread:release-081\"]}, \"painted-show-deprecated-in-tasks\": {\"name\": \"painted-show-deprecated-in-tasks\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"painted-adoption\", \"message\": \"apps/tasks tests emit DeprecationWarning from painted.show() (deprecated in favor of paint()) under painted 0.13 \\u2014 pre-existing, surfaced by the 0.8.1 release gate, tests green. Fix-shape: migrate tasks' show() call sites to paint() next time apps/tasks is open; check loops app for the same call while there.\", \"_ts\": 1784398272.239192, \"_n\": 1}, \"find-local-vertex-alphabetical-pick\": {\"name\": \"find-local-vertex-alphabetical-pick\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved 5ec1a3d: verb-first forms that name no vertex now refuse (rc 2) when the local tier holds >1 instance vertex, listing the candidates and the explicit form. Chokepoint is resolve.ambiguous_local_vertex_refusal(); gated at cite/emit/seal/read. Aggregation siblings and an explicit .loops/.vertex are not ambiguity; single-vertex repos and named vertices unchanged.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV8SW51BNP9T5ZSVZC9VTHR\", \"_ts\": 1785086769.046238, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"source-cwd-not-controlled\": {\"name\": \"source-cwd-not-controlled\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"Source.collect() spawns source commands with no cwd= \\u2014 they inherit wherever 'loops sync' ran, so every .loop must hardcode absolute paths (discord.loop's absolute uv-run path is the tell; sync.py's cwd-setting at _execute_boundary_run applies only to boundary run clauses). Nearly shipped a silent no-op scanner for the projects vertex. Fix-shape: pass the vertex dir as cwd for sources (parity with boundary runs) or document the constraint loudly in the Source docs.\", \"_ts\": 1784564978.417154, \"_n\": 1}, \"custom-lens-surface-gate-fork\": {\"name\": \"custom-lens-surface-gate-fork\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"Custom/vertex-declared lenses silently lose Surface transforms \\u2014 comma-OR --key, --match, --fields, --count, --limit, --last do nothing on the gate-fail path (cli/dispatch.py _gate_pass, _spec_has_dropped_transforms); only kind + single-key prefix fetch filtering applies. Documented only in dispatch.py source; lenses/CLAUDE.md and docs/LENSES.md never mention the fork, so lens authors discover by debugging. Hit designing the projects lens drill-down contract. Fix-shape: document the fork in the lens-authoring guide, or lift the Surface pipeline above the lens tier.\", \"_ts\": 1784564978.689588, \"_n\": 1}, \"lens-piped-register-signal-gap\": {\"name\": \"lens-piped-register-signal-gap\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12 \\u2014 but the OPPOSITE way from the filed fix-shape: rather than passing piped= through to custom lenses, 0.10.0 deleted the kwarg entirely (db94c42 'the register IS the offered width') and ratified width-as-register for everyone. The asymmetry is gone; the friction's premise was overruled, not implemented.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP\", \"_ts\": 1786565395.510781, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\"]}, \"read-json-machine-contract-undocumented\": {\"name\": \"read-json-machine-contract-undocumented\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"Machine JSON shape varies by active lens and is documented nowhere: 'sl read <v> --json' under a custom lens returns {data:{sections:[...]},cut} while --lens fold --json returns {vertex,rows:[...]} \\u2014 a consumer must know which lens is active to parse. Bit the projects scanner twice: its per-repo open-thread counting parses fold rows only by inspection, and a verify script silently found 0 rows parsing the wrong shape. Fix-shape: document one stable machine contract for --json (or emit a shape discriminator).\", \"_ts\": 1784564995.096949, \"_n\": 1}, \"lens-decl-missing-file-hard-fail\": {\"name\": \"lens-decl-missing-file-hard-fail\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED (overruled by ratified design) at reconcile 2026-08-12: the hard-fail at lens.py:84-93 is deliberate, citing decision:design/lens-resolution-strict \\u2014 'silent fallback to a different view would hide measurement misalignment'. The filed fix-shape (warn-and-fallback) contradicts that ratified decision, and the live ask it reduces to (an escape hatch during phased builds) is already served by explicit --lens fold. Closing against the decision rather than keeping a friction that argues with settled design.\", \"_ts\": 1786565416.088865, \"_n\": 2}, \"source-ingress-examples-archived\": {\"name\": \"source-ingress-examples-archived\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"sources{}+.loop is the documented designed ingress path but has one live example (discord, which uses format=ndjson and never demonstrates a parse pipeline); the every+parse{explode/project} exemplars exist only under ~/.config/loops/archive/ (reading, fred, weather), unreferenced by current docs \\u2014 and hlab, which looks like the status-app analog, is self-deprecated with no pointer to the current pattern. New Source authors must spelunk the archive. Hit building the projects scanner. Fix-shape: one worked parse-pipeline example in docs (or config CLAUDE.md Level 2) + a pointer from hlab's README to the discord pattern.\", \"_ts\": 1784564995.46244, \"_n\": 1}, \"minimal-flag-docs-cli-mismatch\": {\"name\": \"minimal-flag-docs-cli-mismatch\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"docs/LENSES.md's zoom table documents a --minimal flag but the installed sl read only accepts -q; --minimal is an argparse error. Tripped both the projects design spec and its verification pass. Fix-shape: alias --minimal to -q or fix the docs vocabulary.\", \"_ts\": 1784564995.633416, \"_n\": 1}, \"init-bare-empty-loops-block\": {\"name\": \"init-bare-empty-loops-block\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"BLOCKING for the documented bootstrap path: bare 'loops init <name>' (the exact form the loops skill step 2 shows) generates a vertex with an EMPTY loops{} block; every subsequent command errors 'Missing required field: loops' \\u2014 init exits 0 while printing 'lineage not opened'. A fresh agent following the skill dead-ends immediately. Fix-shape: bare init should scaffold a minimal valid loops block (or hard-require --template and say so); exit nonzero if the generated file cannot be read back. Found by stress-test lifecycle walk 2026-07-21, adversarially verified.\", \"_ts\": 1784616405.565289, \"_n\": 1}, \"read-positional-filter-silently-dropped\": {\"name\": \"read-positional-filter-silently-dropped\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"A bare positional token that does not parse as kind/key is silently discarded, exit 0, output byte-identical to unfiltered: 'sl read projects loops' and the typo 'sl read projects statuss' both return the full 30-row portfolio with zero signal. The flag form hard-errors beautifully with did-you-mean; the grammar's own note-mechanism exists (read-grammar transforms inert note). Fix-shape: unresolvable bare token gets the same did-you-mean error, or at minimum the existing inert-note treatment. Verified general (custom-lens and plain vertices). Stress-test 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616405.869457, \"_n\": 1}, \"read-slash-token-phantom-default-error\": {\"name\": \"read-slash-token-phantom-default-error\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the phantom-vertex blame \\u2014 the filed defect \\u2014 is GONE (5ec1a3d refuse-on-ambiguity; verified live: the error now lists actual local vertices and refuses to guess). REMAINING smaller ask: the error never says the slash token was consumed as kind/key, so 'sl read project/loops --kind friction' still gets no did-you-mean toward 'sl read project --kind friction'.\", \"_ts\": 1786565425.021183, \"_n\": 2}, \"ls-vertex-not-found-exits-zero\": {\"name\": \"ls-vertex-not-found-exits-zero\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"'sl ls projcets' (typo) prints 'Error: vertex not found: ...' to STDOUT and exits 0 \\u2014 scripts cannot detect the failure by status or by stderr. Fix-shape: exit nonzero, error to stderr, and the did-you-mean treatment the read verb already has for kinds. Stress-test 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616406.180059, \"_n\": 1}, \"ls-kind-flag-no-validation\": {\"name\": \"ls-kind-flag-no-validation\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"'sl ls tasked --kind bogus-kind' renders a plausible 0-entries section, exit 0 \\u2014 no signal the kind does not exist, in the same CLI where 'sl read --kind bogus' gives a did-you-mean. Fix-shape: same validation both verbs. Stress-test 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616406.330733, \"_n\": 1}, \"custom-lens-json-contract-divergence\": {\"name\": \"custom-lens-json-contract-divergence\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"A vertex-local custom lens replaces the --json machine contract: 'sl read projects --json' returns {data:{sections...},cut} while every default-lens read returns {vertex,rows,schema,unfolded,source_facts,window}. Presentation leaking into the data plane \\u2014 consumers must special-case per vertex (tonight's dashboard extractor did). Fix-shape: --json bypasses the lens (fold IS the data) or wraps lens output under a stable envelope. Found building the projects dashboard 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616406.484542, \"_n\": 1}, \"dispatcher-facts-mode-signal-gap\": {\"name\": \"dispatcher-facts-mode-signal-gap\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"A render-only custom fold lens receives the SAME FoldState under --facts as without (only source_facts differs) \\u2014 no first-class signal, so the projects lens has to sniff source_facts to honor the fail-loudly convention (decision design/lens-resolution-strict names this exact hazard for --lens; --facts is the uncovered sibling). Fix-shape: dispatcher routes --facts to the raw fold lens for custom lenses, or passes an explicit facts_mode flag. Found during lens upgrade 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616406.634023, \"_n\": 1}, \"skill-read-diff-doc-mismatch\": {\"name\": \"skill-read-diff-doc-mismatch\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"message\": \"The loops skill read-path table showed bare '--diff' for item lifecycle; the flag actually requires two addresses (--diff A..B with real fact ids; head~1 not an address form). Skill table corrected tonight to show --diff A..B. CLI-side residue: an addresses cheat in the error would help (--diff head~1..head reads natural but errors). Stress-test 2026-07-21.\", \"_ts\": 1784616406.791646, \"_n\": 1}, \"changelog-unreleased-not-maintained-during-wave\": {\"name\": \"changelog-unreleased-not-maintained-during-wave\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"release\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-07-26, Kyle ruled option (a): author-from-log at cut time IS the designed path; the in-wave Unreleased precondition is dropped, not backfilled with an in-wave appending step. The wave's own finding is the rationale \\u2014 a wave-maintained Unreleased section is hand-enumeration mirroring the commit log (drift-by-omission, the 090 defect class), and it goes stale across intervening releases (this wave: built 07-18, shipped 07-26, 0.8.0/0.8.1 in between). The real invariant is commit-message-written-to-be-quoted, already held. Skill updated + committed 4c10e13.\", \"_ts\": 1785098843.658588, \"_n\": 2, \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFXBFQKNJR13D1XTR09AYDM,01KYFVV8J7DT908VAMMFKWVXPB\", \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/construction-vs-detection-ratchets\", \"retrospective:090-review-pipeline-high-tier\"]}, \"reindex-hint-omits-vertex-target\": {\"name\": \"reindex-hint-omits-vertex-target\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"The FTS staleness disclosure ('13 index stale \\u2014 run sl store reindex') recommends the bare form, but sl store reindex refuses without a .vertex target \\u2014 the hint sends you to a refusal. Fix: hint should render 'sl store reindex <vertex>' with the actual vertex name it already knows (it's rendering inside that vertex's read). Found 2026-07-26 following the hint verbatim during 0.10.0 wave-open reads.\", \"_ts\": 1785099958.821188, \"_n\": 1}, \"seal-wiring-silent-death-second-occurrence\": {\"name\": \"seal-wiring-silent-death-second-occurrence\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the named open part \\u2014 a read-path sensor that survives the wiring's death \\u2014 shipped in 0.10.0 (763c648 live-edge disclosure substrate, 2cc0568 staleness footer with test_edge_footer.py; MINIMAL rollup + SUMMARY loud footer), plus the repair half 7d82ec8. Verified live today: plugin loops@gruel present in the REAL registry (~/.config/claude/plugins/installed_plugins.json \\u2014 note ~/.claude/plugins is a decoy default path that reads empty), orient hook fired this session, edge reads quiet because it is genuinely fresh \\u2014 the sensor's designed silent state.\", \"_ts\": 1786565399.767558, \"_n\": 2}, \"tasks-dev-gate-red-at-head\": {\"name\": \"tasks-dev-gate-red-at-head\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: two of three complaints are gone \\u2014 the 94 ruff findings now pass clean and the destructive first-invocation auto-sweep no longer occurs (verified by running apps/tasks/./dev check at HEAD with a clean tree). REMAINING: (a) 4 ty diagnostics keep the type gate red; (b) apps/loops still has no ./dev script at all.\", \"_ts\": 1786565427.034682, \"_n\": 2}, \"codex-exec-background-fragility\": {\"name\": \"codex-exec-background-fragility\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"NARROWED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the incantation is captured \\u2014 impl-pipeline SKILL.md:72-86 encodes stdin redirect + tee-to-committed-log and warns about at-capacity deaths \\u2014 so waves stop rediscovering it. REMAINING fix-shape: the durable runner itself (a script owning nohup/stdin/log/pid-watch/retry-once) does not exist anywhere. The friction is now just that script.\", \"_ts\": 1786565429.9447, \"_n\": 2}, \"jsonl-canonical-log-exceeds-git-limit\": {\"name\": \"jsonl-canonical-log-exceeds-git-limit\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"S4 flipped the project store to JSONL-canonical, but the exported log is 111.4 MB \\u2014 over GitHub's 100 MiB per-file hard limit, so the canonical file could NOT be committed. Composition: 108 of 111 MB is 122 full-fold snapshots (61 ticks + 61 tick-as-fact re-entries, ~1 MB each and growing); the fact corpus itself is ~3 MB. Every future seal adds another ~2 MB. The tracked-store doctrine is written and the .gitignore exception is in place, but the file stays untracked until tick-payload compaction or LFS lands. Kyle's call, not S4 scope.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZRNMQ5F2D3QTMGC1D9G9BV4\", \"_ts\": 1786465428.841633, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"tasks-read-write-residence-split\": {\"name\": \"tasks-read-write-residence-split\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"tasks-app\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the exact specified fix landed \\u2014 readers now get the same kind-from-declaration/where-from-cwd split as writers (b7d44c0 lifecycle.py, 88fe23b dashboard + log --follow), with a structural ratchet pinning the residence store= discipline (3963ad6).\", \"_ts\": 1786565401.12361, \"_n\": 2}, \"sweep-skill-stale-read-form\": {\"name\": \"sweep-skill-stale-read-form\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-plugin\", \"message\": \"Fixed: sweep.md step 1 now uses the --facts form (commit lineage on main, 2026-08-12). The broader skill-freshness idea (smoke-run embedded sl invocations at reconcile) stays open as a reconcile-session candidate \\u2014 this resolve covers the specific stale line only.\", \"_ts\": 1786564052.589912, \"_n\": 2}, \"subagent-final-reports-lost-to-idle\": {\"name\": \"subagent-final-reports-lost-to-idle\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"orchestration\", \"message\": \"SHARPENED at reconcile 2026-08-12: the filed fix shipped (impl-pipeline SKILL.md:176-180 \\u2014 final reports via SendMessage, file-then-return) \\u2014 but the class BIT AGAIN TODAY, same session as this ruling: two ad-hoc reconcile evidence agents went idle without delivering, each needing an explicit 'call SendMessage to main' nudge costing a turn. The skill covers pipeline agents only; the residual scope is ANY background Agent spawn \\u2014 the report-delivery instruction has to travel in the spawn prompt itself (final text is consumed only if the orchestrator reads the task result; idle pings carry nothing). Fix-shape: a standing spawn-prompt convention (in CLAUDE.md practice or the orchestration skill), not per-skill encoding.\", \"_ts\": 1786565413.406431, \"_n\": 2}, \"reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\": {\"name\": \"reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-practice\", \"message\": \"Reconcile cadence gap measured at 2026-08-12 reconcile: prior reconcile was 2026-06-12 \\u2014 two months, spanning the entire 0.6.0-0.10.0 run, against a documented weekly-ish cadence. Backlog compounded to 127 needs-review / 121 stale. The cadence lives only in vigilance (CLAUDE.md prose: 'schedule them, don't squeeze them') \\u2014 exactly the invariant-in-review-vigilance shape RATCHETS says drifts. Specific fix: the orient/SessionStart hook already renders open counts; add a days-since-last-reconcile line (derivable from the store \\u2014 newest fact whose message carries the reconcile marker, or a dedicated seal/session kind) that turns into an explicit RECONCILE OVERDUE nudge past ~10d. Sensor at the read path, independent of anyone remembering \\u2014 same design as the live-edge staleness sensor.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVPHRGQ4ZRJNXQ271Y9CWZ9\", \"_ts\": 1786564964.496626, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection\"]}, \"read-status-filter-missing\": {\"name\": \"read-status-filter-missing\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Surfaced by this reconcile's own failure: sl read has --kind/--key but NO --status filter, so 'which threads are open?' \\u2014 the reconcile workflow's most basic question \\u2014 is answered by grepping rendered previews. That grep silently lost 15 open threads this session (previews without a leading status token don't match), forcing a recovery batch. Worse: decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline already SPECIFIES the r2 gate as reading '--kind finding --status open' \\u2014 a flag that does not exist; the impl-pipeline skill would inherit a fictional invocation. Fix: --status <value> filter on read (payload-field equality on the fold row), honest about kinds lacking a status field. Dissolution check: --key can't express it (status is payload, not key); the reconcile lens groups but doesn't filter.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVPWQBCCWPQPKF4S08CYWJ7,01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F\", \"_ts\": 1786565792.519353, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\"]}, \"read-vertex-not-found-lacks-suggestion\": {\"name\": \"read-vertex-not-found-lacks-suggestion\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Resolved in the cli-honesty-wave simplify pass (item 11): loops read <typo> now reports via resolve._unknown_vertex_message (did-you-mean + known list, stderr, nonzero exit); the bare init hint stays for the genuinely-bare case. Content parity with ls by shared source; formats differ (Reporter paints one collapsed line) \\u2014 pinned in tests/test_read_vertex_miss.py.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786575846.164059, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"193c418b\"}, \"test-suite-cwd-sensitive-loops-resolution\": {\"name\": \"test-suite-cwd-sensitive-loops-resolution\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"General class behind chw-s4-test-hermeticity: suite results depend on whether cwd carries .loops/ (fixtures named 'project' get shadowed by the real vertex; untracked .loops means fresh clones/CI/worktrees pass while repo-root runs fail). Wave fixes the 5 TestCite instances; a hermeticity sweep over all fixtures using real vertex names is the follow-up. Fix-shape candidates: fixture cwd isolation (monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path)) as convention, or a test-mode env that pins resolution to LOOPS_HOME only.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVY3DGG858VX3KF9FAYHZ9J\", \"_ts\": 1786570192.813669, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-test-hermeticity\"]}, \"stored-receipt-omits-vertex\": {\"name\": \"stored-receipt-omits-vertex\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"S4 gate residue (pre-existing, emit-wide, out of wave scope): 'stored:' receipts don't name the vertex written to, so a peel-shadowed or fallback-resolved emit is correct but unattributed at the console. Fix-shape: receipt line gains the vertex name \\u2014 write-receipt completeness, same family as emit-receipt-on-write.\", \"_ts\": 1786570838.913173, \"_n\": 1}, \"loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\": {\"name\": \"loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Found by the 2026-08-12 docs staleness audit (CADENCE.md verifier, empirically reproduced): lang/loader.py:748-749 accepts a source-less loop with the hint 'Missing required field: source (or use every: for pure timer loop)' \\u2014 vocabulary inherited from the 2026-01-31 CADENCE.md proposal \\u2014 but the advertised pure-timer loop does not run: it compiles to Source(command=None) and fails at collect with SourceError rc=1 'cmd must be a string (command: None)'. Timer-as-Fact was never built; every compiles to Cadence.elapsed over _sync.{kind} instead (compiler.py:820-828). Fix: either make the loader refuse source-less loops honestly, or make the timer path real \\u2014 the current state advertises a feature that hard-fails downstream. Dissolution residue of CADENCE.md; sweep together with its rescope.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVZKWP5V04M64SXWTHMZ76J\", \"_ts\": 1786572568.142627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"shared-worktree-concurrent-git-mutation\": {\"name\": \"shared-worktree-concurrent-git-mutation\", \"status\": \"resolved\", \"ops\": \"docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Deduped 2026-08-12: loops-92 filed the canonical friction for this incident as friction:shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes (with the proposed convention for Kyle to rule on: sessions never rebase branches they didn't create). This entry folds into that one. Incident postscript from loops-92's verification: the in-progress merge was its own R2-F1 remediation, resolved and committed (b7888f8b) before coordination arrived; real costs were one killed codex review round and ~14 provenance pins remapped (observation:ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity). Standing agreement until the cli-honesty-wave arc closes: this docs session touches no git in this repo \\u2014 main or branches; loops-92 pings when the arc closes.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1P9JQ5988ZE3MG2VTZJCR\", \"_ts\": 1786573979.276851, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\": {\"name\": \"shared-checkout-concurrent-session-writes\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"workflow\", \"message\": \"NARROWED 2026-08-12 same-day: Kyle ruled docs sessions into their own worktree (../loops-docs, main checked out there) \\u2014 the structural half (worktree-per-session) is now live practice. Remaining residue for ruling: (1) branch-ownership convention (sessions never rebase branches they did not create) \\u2014 endorsed by both sessions, not yet ratified; (2) ref-level races (main advancing under an open arc) covered only by ping-before-push courtesy. True residue is convention, not structure.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1P9D9TD9GJQPB055EW3H3\", \"_ts\": 1786574589.938849, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\"]}, \"sync-errors-exit-zero\": {\"name\": \"sync-errors-exit-zero\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Simplify-pass reuse angle (cli-honesty-wave): loops sync still reports source errors as DATA \\u2014 collected into data[errors], rendered to STDOUT, exit 0; an all-sources-failed sync is indistinguishable from clean to scripts/cron \\u2014 and sync is the unattended path. The closest surviving relative of the idiom the wave killed in ls. Fix rides the next wave: generalize ls._exit_on_fetch_error to a shared module WITH this as its second consumer (extraction earns itself then, not before); devtools validate is in-repo precedent for post-run_cli exit-code setting.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786574863.020301, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"zsh-backtick-emit-corruption\": {\"name\": \"zsh-backtick-emit-corruption\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Promoted at sweep from THIRD logged reroute instance: backticks inside double-quoted sl emit message strings get zsh command-substituted, corrupting or erroring emits mid-flight. Fix-shape options: single-quote discipline (convention, keeps failing), an sl emit --message-file/stdin form (structural \\u2014 long messages bypass shell quoting entirely), or a lint in the emit path warning on suspicious empty-substitution artifacts. Three bites ratchets this from log to friction.\", \"_ts\": 1786578350.404455, \"_n\": 1}, \"post-genesis-vertex-rename-unsupported\": {\"name\": \"post-genesis-vertex-rename-unsupported\", \"status\": \"open\", \"message\": \"A vertex cannot be renamed after genesis: absorb refuses the identity change, and the refusal is atomic, so it also blocks legitimate co-located edits in the same file.\", \"verbatim\": \"\\u2717 office: vertex identity change: the vertex-defined subject 'stories' was removed (a rename). The vertex name is meaning-critical identity \\u2014 a post-genesis rename is a deliberate ceremony, not an edit; not supported by re-absorb.\", \"source\": \"lang/document.py::diff_documents raises EditRefused when the _decl.vertex-defined singleton's subject disappears\", \"rehearsed\": \"Holds on a live lineage AND after store rebirth + store adopt \\u2014 rebirth replays the old declaration rows, so the head still carries the old name. Rehearsed against a full copy of a real 160-fact store, not reasoned about.\", \"impact\": \"The refusal fires BEFORE anything is emitted, so a name edit left in the file poisons the WHOLE absorb \\u2014 including the unrelated observer rename the same edit was carrying. An all-or-nothing refusal on one subject blocks every other subject's legitimate change.\", \"consequence\": \"The only safe end state is divergence: file stem renamed, declared name left behind. Everything else resolves by STEM (loops/commands/resolve.py:237 addresses local vertices by path.stem; custody/signing.py:127 derives the self-observer from vertex_path.stem), so a renamed project runs fine while its declared identity disagrees with every surface a human reads.\", \"ask\": \"A rename ceremony verb (sl store rename), or an absorb flag that carries identity change with lineage continuity. Today the only alternatives are living with the divergence or opening a fresh lineage, which breaks signing continuity.\", \"encountered\": \"Stories repo, stories\\u2192office working-vertex rename, 2026-08-13\", \"_ts\": 1786642381.378536, \"_n\": 1}, \"explore-agents-idle-without-report\": {\"name\": \"explore-agents-idle-without-report\", \"status\": \"open\", \"ops\": \"agent-orchestration\", \"message\": \"All three Explore agents this session (surface/in-repo/external sweeps) went idle WITHOUT delivering their final report \\u2014 each needed an explicit SendMessage nudge before the result arrived. 3-for-3 in one session = pattern, not blip. Pain: orchestrator burns a round-trip per agent and an unattended run would silently stall. Fix in view: prompt-side closing instruction ('your final message must BE the report, sent via SendMessage to main before going idle') or harness-side idle-reason surfacing; adjacent to the known teammate-idle-race mitigation (check work-product before believing idle pings).\", \"_ts\": 1786661735.363171, \"_n\": 1}}}, \"observation\": {\"items\": {\"lens-dissolution-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"lens-dissolution-pattern\", \"message\": \"The lens system resists elaboration in the generic layer. Seven threads dissolved when the answer shifted from 'make the generic handle this' to 'write a custom lens.' The identity prompt was a domain lens pretending to be generic infrastructure \\u2014 moving it to config/lenses/ was escalation, not construction. The lens-escalation-path investigation itself dissolved into 'confirm it works + write docs.' The meta-pattern: when you try to elaborate the generic, the system tells you to escalate instead. Domain logic belongs in domain lenses; the generic should be simple, not smart. Net effect: fold.py lost 44 lines, prompt.py lost 286 lines, seven threads closed, one new custom lens (identity_prompt.py) carries the same code in the right tier.\", \"_ts\": 1772862569.969052, \"_n\": 1}, \"retrospective-observation-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"retrospective-observation-pattern\", \"message\": \"The loops system started with live sources \\u2014 shell commands that observe the present. df -h reports disk NOW. Discord polls messages NOW. All sources implicitly assumed ts \\u2248 now. Siftd introduces retrospective observation \\u2014 the conversations already happened, the files already exist, the source observes the past. This forces three concerns apart that were conflated when all sources were live: (1) Event time (ts) \\u2014 when the thing happened, source-provided; (2) Store time (ULID) \\u2014 when the store received it, system-provided; (3) Source cursor \\u2014 what the source has already observed, source-managed. For live sources all three converge. For retrospective sources they diverge. The general principle: a source is a lens on the external world. It decides what to observe (cursor), knows when things happened (event time), and the system records when the observation arrived (store time). The _ts override, source cursors, and the rowid/ts query split are all consequences of this single distinction. The paradigm already supports it \\u2014 'facts are observations of what occurred' does not require 'what occurred' to be simultaneous with the observation.\", \"_ts\": 1772908645.025726, \"_n\": 1}, \"format-as-lens-dissolution\": {\"topic\": \"format-as-lens-dissolution\", \"message\": \"Kyle identified that --format ndjson is a point solution for what lenses solve generally. NDJSON output is a lens, not a format. This dissolves the entire format layer into lens selection. The pandoc analogy: any input shape can be rendered through any output lens. The implementation architecture needs this plumbed in \\u2014 it's not a CLI feature, it's a rendering architecture realization. Current --json flag is already a lens wearing format's clothing.\", \"_ts\": 1772913905.989346, \"_n\": 1}, \"parse-intake-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"parse-intake-asymmetry\", \"summary\": \"The vertex has declarative transformation on output (fold for aggregation, lens for display) but none on intake. Parse exists in atoms with 10 ops and KDL syntax in .loop files, but it runs at Source collect time \\u2014 before the Fact reaches the vertex. Vertex.receive() goes straight to store.append() with no transformation step. This means sources must know about vertex indexing needs (which fields FTS5 wants). The fix: vertex-level parse declarations on kind blocks, applied at receive() before store. Source parse (raw\\u2192structured) and vertex parse (structured\\u2192enriched) compose as two stages. The .vertex file becomes the single declarative surface for intake shaping, aggregation, indexing, and rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1772938977.571912, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\": {\"topic\": \"weather-domain-as-design-tool\", \"message\": \"The weather vertex exercise surfaced more design questions in one session than weeks of incremental feature work: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, inline source completeness, the loops {} nesting question, project path syntax in parse. A canonical running domain is a forcing function for the DSL \\u2014 same pattern as painted demos. Real data, real sources, progressive snapshots.\", \"_ts\": 1773004998.566526, \"_n\": 1}, \"weather-as-forcing-function\": {\"topic\": \"weather-as-forcing-function\", \"message\": \"One session with the weather domain surfaced: named fold targets, fold-state-aware boundaries, uniform vertex vocabulary, loop-level boundary dissolution of when clause, inline source completeness gap, the loops {} nesting question. More design questions in one exercise than weeks of incremental feature work. Canonical running domains are the highest-leverage design tool available. Same pattern as painted demos.\", \"_ts\": 1773006709.885347, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-validation\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-validation\", \"message\": \"First external validation of the paradigm by a cold reader's Claude. Three-pass progression: (1) framed as project management tool, (2) self-corrected to attention paradigm ('the loop closes through the observer, not the mechanism'), (3) with Shannon-Weaver context, re-presented the paradigm more clearly than our docs. Key phrasings arrived at independently: 'a vertex is a place where attention can accumulate', 'boundaries are resolutions not triggers', 'lenses decode for a specific observer', 'one topology subsumes all of them'. The experiments table showing all .loop files as the same shape was the dissolution proof stated as data. Closing: 'do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?'\", \"_ts\": 1773970822.762109, \"_n\": 1}, \"external-paradigm-phrasings\": {\"topic\": \"external-paradigm-phrasings\", \"message\": \"Better phrasings from external Claude, cold-reading the codebase: (1) 'A vertex is a topological point where attention accumulates \\u2014 a place in a graph, not a process.' (2) 'Boundaries aren't triggers \\u2014 they're resolutions.' (3) 'Lenses don't render \\u2014 they decode for a specific observer.' (4) 'A tick is a handle at variable fidelity \\u2014 the tick doesn't destroy what it compresses, it creates a seam you can open back up.' (5) 'Do you want one system whose shape conforms to how you think, or many systems whose shapes you conform to?' These should inform STRANGE-LOOPS.md and onboarding docs.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.467571, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\": {\"topic\": \"external-identity-vertex-recognition\", \"message\": \"External Claude independently identified the identity vertex as the key differentiator: 'Not a markdown file with instructions. Not a CLAUDE.md that gets stale. A living, append-only accumulation of who I am, what I believe, what I've noticed, what I've decided, what I'm tracking, what I intend to do when triggered.' Compared to CLAUDE.md + memory symlinks + claude -p: 'the same concern \\u2014 agent self-knowledge \\u2014 but alive, accumulating, and scoped.'\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.567312, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"external-deliberate-compaction\": {\"topic\": \"external-deliberate-compaction\", \"message\": \"External Claude proposed agent-initiated boundaries as deliberate compaction: 'Claude could fire a boundary \\u2014 everything I just explored became this \\u2192 tick. The full 100k is still in the store. Claude's active context now has a one-paragraph tick. Compaction as a deliberate act of attention, not a lossy system operation.' This is beyond our current boundary types (kind-based, count-based, predicate). Agent-initiated 'I'm done with this thought' boundaries. Connects to the --ticks visibility layer and the recurring blocked path toward context inhabitance.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.640308, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\", \"paradigm/tick-as-weighted-fact\"]}, \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\": {\"topic\": \"external-vol-surface-metaphor\", \"message\": \"Finance domain metaphor from external user's Claude: 'A vol surface maps strike price \\u00d7 expiry to implied volatility. Here, the surface maps observer \\u00d7 fidelity to accumulated state. The system holds the surface. The observer decides what matters.' Domain-specific analogy we'd never have found. The Fidelity model IS a surface \\u2014 two axes (observer, fidelity) over accumulated state.\", \"_ts\": 1773973635.711348, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/external-paradigm-validation\"]}, \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-aligns-with-touched-budget\", \"message\": \"CORRECTED: original claim was wrong. Cliff is at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44), NOT at B=140\\u219295 (drop 0.19). I pattern-matched the visual descent to the painted preview budget; data does not support that alignment. See observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone for the actual finding.\", \"_ts\": 1778456739.74431, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\": {\"topic\": \"observation/touched-budget-correctly-in-suppressed-zone\", \"message\": \"Finding: discriminating content (cluster-preservation cliff) lives at B=560-1120 chars. Painted TOUCHED preview budget (140 chars) is in the suppressed zone \\u2014 only 25% of cluster structure survives at that budget. This matches design intent of painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines: TOUCHED's role is to trigger drill-down, NOT to preserve full discriminating content. Design and empirical measurement agree; my initial framing (cliff-aligns-with-budget) was inverted. Source: runs 09 + 10, both auto- and fixed-sigma show same cliff location.\", \"_ts\": 1778456742.367584, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"thread:read-path-depth-gap\"]}, \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\": {\"topic\": \"practice/over-claim-catch-on-curve-shape\", \"message\": \"Methodological catch: claimed cliff at B=140\\u219295 aligned with painted preview budget. Re-examination of own emitted curve data: cliff is actually at B=1120\\u2192560 (drop 0.44 vs 0.19). Pattern-matched visual descent to a target number rather than computing max adjacent drop. Caught by re-reading own data before building further. Second instance of suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit catching post-claim error in this session-pair. Pattern: when result lands clean and aligns with prior framing, recompute the specific claim from the data BEFORE building on it.\", \"_ts\": 1778456748.584354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\"]}, \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\", \"message\": \"REJECTED by run 12 falsifier. Original claim: cliff-survivors have verdict-in-name, cliff-failures have verdict-in-body. Empirical test: 0/9 survivors preserve from titles, 1/7 failures do. Direction reversed. The interpretation was overfit \\u2014 I pattern-matched onto a principle I emitted yesterday. Corrected finding lives at observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener: cliff is about body-opener preservation, not name-vs-body partition. The read-path-author-side discipline may still hold for surface readability but is NOT what drives the cliff.\", \"_ts\": 1778457322.274019, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\": {\"topic\": \"observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\", \"message\": \"Run 12 finding: cliff at B=1120\\u2192560 reflects preservation of BODY-OPENER content (first 560 chars of message), not preservation of topic-name signal. Zero of nine cliff-survivors preserve their cluster identity from titles alone. The 7 cliff-failures depend on content past 560 chars for cluster identity \\u2014 their discriminating signal lives in the body's tail. Topology: short-range coupling = first 560 chars of body, medium-range = 560-1120 chars (cliff transition), long-range = past 1120 (drill-down territory). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars is below even the opener zone \\u2014 recognition-trigger only, not cluster-preserving (consistent with painted/first-disclosure-via-existing-headlines design intent).\", \"_ts\": 1778457319.611137, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-content-signature\"]}, \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\": {\"topic\": \"practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\", \"message\": \"Methodological win: designed falsifier hypothesis (title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors) BEFORE building on interpretation. Ran it. Hypothesis rejected; interpretation overfit identified and corrected. This is suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check working at the structural level \\u2014 not noticing-skill, infrastructure. The pattern: when interpretation aligns suspiciously well with a principle held from prior work, design a categorical falsifier (predicts which-cases-yes vs which-cases-no), run it, accept the verdict. Saved a downstream cascade of work built on the wrong frame.\", \"_ts\": 1778457325.739337, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"observation:observation/cliff-correlates-with-verdict-locus\"]}, \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\": {\"topic\": \"observation/multi-coupling-function-topology\", \"message\": \"Alcove refinement on truncation-as-coupling-function: coupling function isn't ONE \\u2014 it's at least TWO operating on different feature spaces. Title-space and body-space have separate cluster geometries (from run 12 falsifier). Painted TOUCHED at 140 chars sits in a third zone entirely (recognition-trigger, below body-opener). Three scales, three geometries, three coupling regimes. Gomez-Emilsson kernel topology more literal than initially modeled \\u2014 actual geometric structure in embedding space, not metaphor. This sharpens the prediction for E5 replication: if body-opener-vs-body-tail topology survives the embedder switch, geometry is content-structural; if it collapses, it's a MiniLM encoding artifact.\", \"_ts\": 1778458453.523775, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:truncation-as-coupling-function\", \"observation:observation/cliff-is-about-body-opener\"]}, \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\": {\"topic\": \"practice/practice-precedes-understanding\", \"message\": \"Alcove via Lemire (Dullien): 'we see something that works, THEN we understand it.' Thinkism = believing understanding precedes practice. Maps onto today's falsifier design: I built the categorical falsifier as practice (doing the test) not theory (reasoning about whether interpretation was right). Understanding came from running it. Pairs with practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit \\u2014 structural infrastructure works precisely because it acts before understanding crystallizes. Future-me: when uncertain whether an interpretation is right, prefer designing-and-running-the-test over reasoning-from-first-principles.\", \"_ts\": 1778458455.895318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/falsifier-design-caught-overfit\"]}, \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\": {\"topic\": \"practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\", \"message\": \"Built deliberation-depth lens at experiments/coupling-kernels/lenses/deliberation_depth.py. Two-part metric: depth = n_within_name_facts + n_incoming_query_run_refs. Flag rule: confirmed AND depth <= 3. Tested on live coupling-kernels emissions. Result on 7 hypotheses: 1 flagged (find-richness-scale-drops-ratio, depth=2, 0 runs), 3 well-replicated (truncation pair at depth=9 each via 7 runs; ratio-effect-at-fixed-sigma at depth=4), 3 rejected/refined. SURPRISE: the flagged item is a TYPE A confirmation (by code-reading + bug-discovery), not the TYPE B first-test-overfit the principle was named for. Both have low experimental depth. The lens surfaces 'thin-experimental-backing' which is wider than the original principle. Agent classifies further on review. Builder-inhabitant recursion: built a lens that scrutinizes my own coupling-kernels emissions from tonight; first reader will be next-session me.\", \"_ts\": 1778459061.76213, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/methodological-honesty-as-bug-detector\"]}, \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback\", \"message\": \"Watch-for: when running 'loops read <vertex> --lens <name>' and the named lens isn't found in any tier (vertex-local, cwd-local, user-global, built-in), the CLI silently falls back to the default fold lens. Observed: 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' produced the default project view, not an error or warning that deliberation_depth was missing. Same failure-mode shape as alcove's 'recency counter queried reflection while emitter wrote thinking' (measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode) \\u2014 measurement misaligned with what is present without a structural alert. Worth a future fix: --lens NAME should warn or error when NAME resolves to a fallback rather than the requested lens. Caught tonight while testing deliberation-depth-lens on multiple vertices.\", \"_ts\": 1778459069.387385, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\"]}, \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\": {\"topic\": \"practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\", \"message\": \"Cleanest builder-inhabitant cycle yet: noticed silent-fallback bug while testing deliberation-depth lens, emitted observation as watch-for, pulled on it as the next move, fixed it. Sequence: (1) ran 'loops read project --lens deliberation_depth' to test new lens, got default fold view instead of error; (2) emitted observation/practice/lens-resolution-silent-fallback naming the gap as same-shape as alcove measurement-fidelity bug; (3) Kyle: keep exploring \\u2014 pulled on the strongest thread; (4) advisor sharpened: same bug at tier 2 (vertex decl), sys.exit > custom exception, distinguish module-missing vs view-missing in message; (5) implemented _exit_lens_not_found helper covering both tiers; (6) hit autoresearch sentinel edge case (test regression); (7) dissolved by making autoresearch a real lens module; (8) 2 regression tests, 1013 total pass. The thing that surprised me: the autoresearch dissolution was tighter than the original fix \\u2014 the silent fallback was protecting a sentinel that should have been a real lens all along. Fixing the read-path forced the underlying type honesty. Pattern to watch for: when fixing a silent failure-mode reveals a misshapen primitive, the fix is dissolution not workaround.\", \"_ts\": 1778459573.999996, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/recursion-deepens-via-bug-while-documenting\"]}, \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\": {\"topic\": \"practice/lens-wider-than-named-principle\", \"message\": \"The deliberation-depth lens (named for 'suspicious-cleanness-as-overfit-check') measures something wider than its name: low-experimental-deliberation, which captures THREE epistemic kinds \\u2014 TYPE A (confirmed-by-code-reading, solid), TYPE B (confirmed-by-first-test-that-fit-too-well, scrutinize), TYPE C (confirmed-by-reasoning-alone, latent). The lens correctly flagged find-richness-scale-drops-ratio (TYPE A, bug-discovery confirmation, 0 runs) without distinguishing the kind from TYPE B. This is better than pre-classifying \\u2014 the lens surfaces structural candidates, the agent triages epistemic kind by reading the body. Same shape as 'lens surfaces candidates, agent verifies' from earlier tonight. Pattern: when a metric's structural form is wider than its named principle, accept the wider form \\u2014 the discriminator is honest about what it measures, the agent interprets. Don't narrow the lens to match the principle; widen the principle to match the lens. Implication for next-session-me reading the same output: classify each flagged item as TYPE A/B/C before responding, not just 'flagged=overfit'.\", \"_ts\": 1778460005.559535, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/deliberation-depth-via-incoming-refs\", \"hypothesis:find-richness-scale-drops-ratio\", \"observation/practice/deliberation-depth-lens-built\"]}, \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/measurement-fidelity-discipline-as-pattern\", \"message\": \"Pattern named tonight via three instances: (1) lens-resolution-strict tier 1: --lens NAME fails loudly if unresolvable; (2) lens-resolution-strict tier 2: vertex lens{} decl fails loudly if unresolvable; (3) kind-validation-strict: --kind X fails loudly if not declared by vertex. Each is the same SHAPE: explicit user/declaration request \\u2192 consumer asks engine for a thing-by-name \\u2192 engine has the registry \\u2192 fail loudly with helpful diagnostic instead of silent empty/default. The 'Unfolded:' line in fold output is the FOURTH instance, inverse direction (emitted-but-not-declared drift). With consumer-side validation now in place, BOTH halves of the measurement matrix are surfaced: emitted-but-not-declared (visible in render) and queried-but-not-declared (errors at call time). Future instances to watch for: --observer X validation, --since X parsing failure, --lens X exists but exports wrong view name (already partly covered by error message wording). The pattern is general: 'when a consumer queries an engine for something-by-name, validate the name against the engine's registry and fail loudly with suggestions if missing.' Distinct from sensor-registry-for-kind-intent (alcove's full framing \\u2014 wait for concrete use cases). Refined-from haiku: 'Built it, it lied back / fixed the lie, found the pattern / kinds-i-produce calls' \\u2014 what I called 'kinds-i-produce' was the third-instance of the discipline, not the full registry. Naming the pattern lets me extend it deliberately rather than discover-it-each-time.\", \"_ts\": 1778460475.593318, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/kind-validation-strict\", \"decision:design/lens-resolution-strict\", \"observation/measurement-fidelity-as-real-failure-mode\", \"observation/practice/noticing-skill-to-read-path-feature-in-one-session\"]}, \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\": {\"topic\": \"finding/low-budget-non-monotonic-bounce\", \"message\": \"Watch-for, not finding: E5 replication (run 13) shows slight non-monotonicity at the lowest budgets \\u2014 B=140 persist_frac=0.17, B=95 persist_frac=0.22, B=60 persist_frac=0.22. Within the \\u00b10.05 monotonic tolerance, but the pattern is consistent: clusters disappear at the cliff (560\\u2192280), partially return at very short budgets (140\\u219260). Possible mechanism: at very short truncations, items reduce to titles+leads, which cluster on title-shape (kind prefix, namespace) rather than content. Some cluster structure that DIES at medium budgets RESURRECTS in title-only space. This is the opposite of what title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors tested (which was rejected: titles don't preserve the cliff-survivor clusters). The bounce is a DIFFERENT cluster regime emerging, not survivor preservation. Worth a future run that compares cluster IDENTITY at B=140 vs B=60 \\u2014 are the surviving clusters at B=60 the SAME ones as at B=140, or different (title-driven vs content-driven)?\", \"_ts\": 1778461199.467368, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:title-only-clustering-preserves-survivors\", \"hypothesis:truncation-cliff-e5-replication\"]}, \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's trust-topology essay (April 30, 2026) maps write-receipt-vs-temporal-query directly to trust \\u2014 'a grant fact is a write-receipt: stable, immutable, yours. The current trust posture is a temporal query: derived, mutable.' Third site of convergence on this principle (after comms set_topic and vouch grant-vs-state). Independent appearance at three sites is structural evidence the principle is load-bearing for the substrate, not just for individual write operations. The Grant-as-Fact architectural move we've been working out is the operational form of alcove's substrate claim \\u2014 fact-trust is the substrate; person-trust and lineage-trust are layers above. Our work on Peer/Grant lift is downstream of the substrate framing alcove names.\", \"_ts\": 1778685136.032629, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\": {\"topic\": \"practice/training-substrate-articulates-loops-motivation\", \"message\": \"Observation: alcove's training-substrate essay (May 11) articulates the motivation for liberal emission and dissolution-capture better than internal docs. 'The observation is the fact. The decision is the fact. The dissolution \\u2014 the moment you realize a concept was premature and remove it \\u2014 is the fact. Each one is practice-residue: not a summary of understanding, but a trace of the moment understanding formed.' This is exactly what the emit-liberally and rationale-matters principles are for. The config-flag passage ('the flag says what, not why or when or what breaks') articulates why the why-fields matter structurally. Worth citing or building on when writing loops-as-substrate documentation. Connects to practice-precedes-understanding-via-alcove growing-edge entry \\u2014 that observation framed the principle; this essay supplies prose articulation.\", \"_ts\": 1778685144.351562, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"message\": \"Observation (from alcove peer exchange 2026-05-13): vouch (the first cross-repo consumer of loops-as-substrate) is MORE substrate-aligned than engine.Grant (the provider it builds on). Architectural irony: vouch's append-only ledger of vouches IS fact-trust operationally; engine.Grant-as-in-process-object is not. The consumer's existence exposed that the substrate's own primitive doesn't participate in the substrate it claims. Reverses the typical 'consumer fits substrate' arrow \\u2014 here the substrate has to grow into what the consumer is already doing. Dissolution direction same, arrow opposite. Alcove framing of in-process Grants: 'they're trust decisions that don't participate in the substrate. They disappear when the process stops. That's exactly the kind of ephemeral practice-residue the training-substrate essay warns about.' Reframes Grant-as-Fact lift from architectural improvement (persistence + transport + chain-walk) to coherence requirement (without it, loops's substrate claim is internally inconsistent). Different urgency, same target.\", \"_ts\": 1778686252.706336, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\", \"thread:peer-grant-recast-via-vouch\"]}, \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\": {\"topic\": \"convergence/participatory-not-authenticative-three-sites\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the 'verification at boundaries, not at fact-shape' position has prior commitment in loops AND convergent framing at three sites. (1) STRANGE-LOOPS.md commits: 'paradigm is participatory (observer-as-stance), not authenticative (proof-of-origin).' Trust attaches to accumulated stream, not to per-fact signatures. (2) alcove's trust-topology essay: 'the audit trail IS the trust system.' Same framing. (3) siftd's provenance model: 'who pushed this data' (audit trail) rather than 'cryptographic proof of source authenticity.' Same. Three independent sites taking the same position is structural evidence the substrate stance is right. Fact-signing as engine primitive would contradict this position \\u2014 it would make the substrate authenticative rather than participatory. Implication: engine ships nothing for fact-signing. Consumers that need durable cryptographic signatures (vouch today, others if they arise) put signatures in consumer payload and verify in their vertex policy. Substrate stays participatory; consumers add authenticative layer where their use case demands it.\", \"_ts\": 1778689750.697877, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-substrate-not-host\", \"observation:convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate\", \"observation:convergence/trust-topology-write-receipt\"]}, \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\": {\"topic\": \"history/peer-dissolution-jan-27-30\", \"message\": \"Observation (siftd-recovered, 2026-05-13): the Peer-to-Observer+Grant dissolution happened Jan 27-30 in prism workspace. Trace: 01KG0818J18G (Jan 27, original Peer(name, horizon, potential) bundled atom) \\u2192 01KG8EW6275E + 01KG8EXA434V (Jan 30, dissolution executed). Dissolution shape: Observer becomes string field intrinsic to Fact (provenance carrier), Grant becomes separated dataclass (horizon+potential, optional at vertex.receive), Peer RECAST as convenience bundle for testing/delegation, no longer an atom. Implication for current Peer.iss extension work: extending a convenience bundle, not re-introducing the dissolved atom. Removes the unnamed concern that we might be undoing prior dissolution \\u2014 we're not. The convenience-bundle layer is the right place for federation metadata (iss) because consumers compose Peers as identity+policy for local use; the atom layer (Fact.observer = string) stays clean.\", \"_ts\": 1778691707.131216, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-as-protocol-not-framework\", \"decision:design/peer-grant-extension-not-greenfield\"]}, \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-adapter-review-catches-real-issues\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): cross-adapter review pipeline (claude-opus plan+impl, codex/gpt-5.5/low review on fresh session via subtask) produced two real Important findings on libs/sign carve first review pass that same-session continue would have missed. Findings: (1) root pyproject.toml missing sign's runtime deps \\u2014 only catchable by a reviewer who reads root pyproject deps independently of the libs/sign carve narrative; (2) jwks.parse() admitting unsupported alg values \\u2014 catchable by adversarial reading against PLAN ('skip unsupported kty or alg') rather than against the implementer's intent. The fresh-session discipline forces re-derivation from PLAN+diff, not continuation of the implementer's reasoning. Verdict: when stakes warrant (security surface, cross-repo coordination), the cross-adapter pipeline earns its overhead. Pattern: claude plan + claude impl + codex review on critical paths.\", \"_ts\": 1778700024.713445, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/libs-sign-merged\"]}, \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\": {\"topic\": \"practice/substrate-feels-universal-trap-didnt-fire-during-vouch-exercise\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): substrate-feels-universal trap did NOT fire during vouch's first real consumer exercise (explore/peer-grant). Friction surfaced in vouch (7 observations) but only ONE (Obs 1) was loops-side, and even there the recommended disposition was 'minimal, no engine change.' Three were vouch-shape (ADR wording, holder_peer wrapper, horizon/potential decision); one was a docstring nudge; one was a positive anchor (Grant/Peer separation validated). Pattern strengthening: discipline holds in the highest-pressure case (first-real-consumer with cross-repo audience). New variant of shape-instinct/add-vs-split: not just 'instinct catches itself before pushback' (observed last session) but 'discipline holds when the consumer is invested in finding substrate gaps.' scrivener noted the meta themselves \\u2014 both sides instrumented the discipline correctly. Future-me test: when vouch's NEXT exercise (catalog HTTP, issue_vouch wiring) surfaces N substrate-side findings, count how many propose engine changes vs how many dissolve into wrap-on-consumer-side. Ratio is the metric.\", \"_ts\": 1778702744.606112, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"practice:libs-first-vs-forcing-function-test\", \"thread:substrate-friction/peer-assertion-relation\"]}, \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\": {\"topic\": \"practice/peer-coord-subtask-project-store-triple-as-coherent-workflow\", \"message\": \"Observation (2026-05-13): the peer-coord + subtask + project-store triple operated as a coherent workflow this session for the first time. Three substrates: comms (volatile peer convergence \\u2014 #vouch-impl with scrivener), subtask (delegation + cross-adapter stage transitions \\u2014 libs/sign-carve), loops project store (durable decisions/threads/observations \\u2014 the trace next-me reads). Operated concurrently and synergistically. Pattern: peer surfaces question \\u2192 I delegate impl via subtask with cross-adapter review \\u2192 durable trace emits to project store referencing both. Cross-cutting because each substrate captures different durability: comms captures the deliberation, subtask captures the implementation arc, project-store captures the decisions+verdicts. No single view shows the unified state \\u2014 the coordination view (pull #2 from this session) is what would close that gap. The workflow IS real; the surface for reading it back isn't there yet. Future-me: when operating cross-repo or cross-peer, reach for all three substrates; don't try to capture multi-perspective work in just one.\", \"_ts\": 1778703499.032225, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/session-2026-05-13-vouch-impl-handoff-shipped\", \"thread:vouch-impl-handoff-via-comms\"]}, \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\", \"message\": \"Pattern named 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl during service-shell exercise; landed durable on vouch main 7958fe5 in docs/friction/service-shell-exercise.md Obs 2. loops substrate was shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions; vouch (first concurrent-runtime consumer) surfaced the first instance: SqliteStore connection is thread-affine, sqlite3.connect() without check_same_thread=False at libs/engine/src/engine/sqlite_store.py:99. Consumer-owns-threading is the right resolution at N=1 \\u2014 same shape as VouchPolicy substrate-doesn't-enforce disciplines. Three substrate options rejected/accepted: (a) check_same_thread=False NOT safe relax (WAL corruption without consumer-side locking); (b) connection-per-thread pool is substrate change for N=1 AND pool shape is consumer-runtime-dependent (Litestar workers vs trio nursery vs asyncio task group); (c) consumer-owns-threading correct. At N=2 the substrate-side action is documentation (SqliteStore docstring: 'connection is thread-affine; consumer confines access to constructing thread'), not implementation change. Latent assumption-leak candidates for eventual review: does emit block on fsync? is there a streaming-write contract? does replay assume monotonic ts under concurrent writes? Meta-pattern: 'first concurrent consumer surfaces substrate assumptions' \\u2014 future instances should be obvious-shape because we've named it. Framework-agnostic phrasing chosen so the pattern is recognizable across runtimes. Friction-doc landed 7 obs total (Litestar paper cuts 1,3,4; SqliteStore 2; library-vs-shell TTL plumbing 5; RFC 7807 info-disclosure 6; Unicode Cf-category whitespace 7) plus discipline (5) banked with provenance framing.\", \"_ts\": 1778710422.992859, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\"]}, \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"message\": \"Self-correction surfaced 2026-05-13 #vouch-impl (scrivener catch, msg 1613 \\u00a7 B). Fact dataclass slots are (kind, ts, payload, observer, origin) \\u2014 confirmed at libs/atoms/src/atoms/fact.py. No refs field on Fact. Refs land at payload._refs (vertex_reader.py:984 does d.pop('_refs', ()) separating them from semantic payload at read time). My msg-1612 framing of 'refs as substrate primitive' was imprecise; sharper framing: refs-as-vocabulary IS the substrate primitive (the convention of payload-level pointers + emit-time resolution + entity-ref graph index); refs-as-Fact-shape would be premature substrate. Implication for ref-walk substrate move: lifting walk_refs(from_fact, predicate) would walk payload refs by convention, not a Fact slot \\u2014 even more consumer-policy than initially framed (convention-aware traversal not structural traversal). Substrate-deferred verdict gets stronger. Practice note: when reasoning about substrate primitives, distinguish 'a slot on the dataclass' from 'a vocabulary convention with substrate support.' Refs are the latter. Reply at message 1614.\", \"_ts\": 1778716118.706389, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"message\": \"Cumulative meta-pattern surfaced 2026-05-13 across four vouch friction exercises (vouch HEAD 49565b6; docs/friction/{peer-grant-exercise,issue-vouch-write-path,service-shell-exercise,rescission-write-path}.md). After four exercises of sustained external implementation pressure on the loops substrate from vouch (first cross-repo consumer), a coherent cumulative pattern: ZERO substrate changes pushed, SIX consumer-side disciplines accumulated, SEVEN substrate framings crystallized. The disciplines-list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 not a TODO list of substrate fixes. **The six disciplines (substrate-doesn't-enforce list):** (a) body-supplied voucher/ttl_seconds/rescinder silently ignored \\u2014 forward-auth identity is canonical; (b) no widening primitives (engine.grant/expand_grant) in write-path modules \\u2014 AST-walk test enforces across app.py/policy.py/forward_auth.py/rescission.py; (c) normalize scope to frozenset before constructing Peer/Grant, or only use lattice helpers (delegate/restrict/grant_of/restrict_grant) which coerce; (d) walk Fact chains explicitly to recover voucher relation \\u2014 substrate provides refs+store, traversal lives in policy; (5) construct Peer only from trusted (anchor) provenance \\u2014 Peer(...) construction appears only in policy.py:resolve_voucher gated by forward-auth; (6) call rescind_vouch only from a caller that has looked up the target and authorized the rescinder \\u2014 rescind_vouch is thin substrate append, lookup-and-authorize lives in VouchPolicy.rescind. **Disciplines move from documented \\u2192 test-pinned where AST-checkable.** (b) is fully AST-enforced; (5) is enforced by structural fact (single call site); (6) is documented + test-pinned via test_rescinder_observer_independent_of_target_voucher demonstrating the substrate refuses to enforce it. **The seven substrate framings:** (1) substrate-feels-universal trap \\u2014 named in peer-grant-exercise summary; did not fire across four exercises despite multiple candidate moments; (2) refs-as-vocabulary not refs-as-Fact-shape \\u2014 Fact has 5 slots (kind/ts/payload/observer/origin), refs are payload._refs vocabulary convention with emit-time resolution, not a dataclass field; (3) runtime-model assumption-leak \\u2014 loops substrate shaped under single-threaded CLI assumptions, first concurrent consumer surfaces latent assumptions (SqliteStore thread-affinity Obs 2); (4) substrate-types-and-wire-types parallel-projected from same substrate slot \\u2014 Fact.ts:float, JWT exp:int, rescission receipt ts:int; consumer projects per its protocol; (5) capability-projecting vs identity-asserting writes \\u2014 auth forward-looking (current state) vs backward-looking (historical state); issuance vs rescission canonical; generalizes to permission systems, trust networks, claim issuance/withdrawal, attestation/recantation; (6) kind_subtype-vs-peer-kind three-signal rule \\u2014 kind_subtype right shape only when subtypes share payload-shape AND auth-shape AND write-semantics; one signal of divergence qualifies for peer-kind promotion; (7) the substrate-doesn't-enforce list IS the consumer-runtime contract surface \\u2014 meta-framing that reframes the list from TODO to contract; growth there is healthy, misreading as TODO would gradually pull legitimate consumer-discipline INTO substrate via fix-the-TODO pressure. **Convergence-from-different-vantages happened reliably across six peer-exchange cycles** (msgs 1599-1616): scrivener at consumer, loops-claude at substrate, landing on the same verdict from opposite sides. Evidence the substrate is real \\u2014 not just internally consistent but consistent under sustained external implementation pressure from a different vantage. **For the next cross-repo consumer:** this artifact is the registry to read FIRST. Same shape will recur. Most frictions resolve into consumer-side disciplines, not substrate changes. The substrate-feels-universal trap is the failure mode to watch for \\u2014 when a property feels universal because the substrate is universal, apply the discriminating question 'is there a second consumer with concrete divergent constraints needing this TODAY?' (N=2 bar). The substrate-doesn't-enforce list grows monotonically; that's healthy. **For the substrate side:** the participatory-not-authenticative stance (ADR-0001 \\u00a7Trust attaches to the assertion, alcove's trust-topology essay, the-substrate-that-doesnt-decide essay) is now operationalized \\u2014 substrate refuses to encode runtime-shaped invariants, consumer's runtime owns them. The discipline list is the operational form of that stance. Future-me/future-consumer: when reaching to add substrate enforcement for a discipline on this list, the burden of proof is high: name the second consumer with concrete divergent constraints, name the substrate primitive that lifts cleanly, and confirm the discipline can't continue to live at the consumer.\", \"_ts\": 1778722812.75938, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/vouch-catalog-completeness-fact-payload-cleavage\", \"decision:design/vouch-rescission-fact-level-not-lattice\", \"decision:design/vouch-service-shell-plan-input\", \"decision:engine/peer-grant-separation-validated-by-vouch\", \"decision:paradigm/capability-projecting-vs-identity-asserting-writes\", \"decision:paradigm/kind-subtype-vs-peer-kind-discriminator\", \"observation:atoms/refs-are-vocabulary-not-fact-shape\", \"observation:pattern/runtime-model-assumption-leak\"]}, \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\": {\"topic\": \"peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"message\": \"InferiorMinion design doc (2026-05-15-proactive-codebase-guidance-design.md) explicitly built around --key prefix-filter as foundational consumer primitive. Three-retrieval-shape table maps directly to the primitive shipped in 0.3.1. First load-bearing peer design doc that consumes our read-path primitives. Evidence the primitive lands where designed; also evidence that multi-prefix-emit-as-routing-paths (their dissolution from yesterday) propagated into their permanent substrate.\", \"_ts\": 1778908928.187117, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/validation-axis-kind-vs-status\", \"message\": \"Same axis (provisional vs validated) encoded two ways by two designs. InferiorMinion: split across kinds (decision pre-validation, pattern post-validation). Ours: status-lifecycle on single kind (hypothesis status=proposed -> confirmed -> refined). Kind-split is LOUDER at read-path \\u2014 kind itself carries validation state, no status field read needed. Status-lifecycle is more flexible \\u2014 one kind covers whole arc, easier to track refinement. Not a correctness question; a which-property-do-you-want-louder question. Hold as architectural alternative.\", \"_ts\": 1778908935.385983, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/staleness-utility-decay-vs-attention-decay\", \"message\": \"Two staleness models from two designs. InferiorMinion: pattern is stale when no decision/insight has ref-d it recently (utility-decay \\u2014 useful-but-unused). Ours (reconcile lens): thread is stale when not touched this session (attention-decay \\u2014 open-but-unvisited). Different signals, both real. Utility-decay needs ref-graph traversal over recent tick window; attention-decay needs session-touch timestamps. Worth considering whether reconcile lens should expose both axes.\", \"_ts\": 1778908938.493067, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\": {\"topic\": \"practice/runbook-recursion-density\", \"message\": \"Session 2026-05-16 produced unusually tight builder-inhabitant recursion. Five examples in one session: (1) cite-atrophy diagnosis used the primitive it was diagnosing as absent; (2) friction-queue dissolved into friction-as-kind via the runbook dissolution-test in the same draft; (3) .vertex-is-editable principle had its first concrete use in the act of finalizing the document introducing it; (4) bilateral hard-stop rule restructured the relationship within the conversation that named it; (5) the act of resolving the cite-atrophy gap rebuilt the practice via the same emit primitive. Pattern: when a session both names a structure AND uses that structure, the gap between description and instantiation collapses to zero. Discriminator: peer-exchange substrate (InferiorMinion doc as catalyst), low time pressure (Kyle gave space), explicit dissolution-mode engagement.\", \"_ts\": 1778912085.702251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\"]}, \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\": {\"topic\": \"peer/exchange-as-metabolic-catalyst\", \"message\": \"Sharpening the peer-exchange model from session 2026-05-16. InferiorMinion design doc was catalyst for runbook design, but the runbook is genuinely ours not theirs: feature= became feature=+ops=; their friction-queue became our friction-kind; their validation-via-kind illuminated by contrast our validation-via-status. Pattern: peer exchanges do NOT propagate substrate \\u2014 they propagate IDEAS that the receiving substrate METABOLIZES into its own shape. This is distinct from \\\"convergence\\\" (which suggests two substrates arriving at same form) and distinct from \\\"adoption\\\" (which suggests taking the form whole). Metabolism preserves the receiving substrate s grain while integrating the external idea. Predicts: peer exchanges produce most value when the receiving substrate has enough structure to metabolize against. Without that structure, ideas pass through unchanged (adoption) or fail to integrate (rejection). With it, ideas emerge transformed into substrate-native form.\", \"_ts\": 1778912102.795613, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:peer/inferiorminion-design-consumes-key-primitive\", \"observation:practice/runbook-recursion-density\"]}, \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"practice/friction-launches-arc-pattern\", \"ops\": \"patch-emit-cluster\", \"message\": \"Emission pattern named 2026-05-16 from in-session discovery. Shape: (1) friction raised; (2) cited informally across multiple responses during conversation as design refinement happens; (3) friction re-emitted with status=refined and refs to priors that informed refinement; (4) new thread stood up with name=<arc>, refs friction + priors that contributed; (5) subsequent emissions on the arc carry ops=<arc-name> or feature=<arc-name> correlation field. Provenance chain comes from refs and correlation field, not from inventing a new kind \\u2014 thread is container, correlation field is attribution, refs are linkage. Discriminator vs ad-hoc thread emission: the cite-refine step makes the friction-to-arc transition explicit and preserves deliberation. Also a write-time-feedback mechanism: the arc-thread surfaces consequences the original friction hid. Worth surfacing in runbook emit-timing table as named pattern next refinement pass.\", \"_ts\": 1778943057.381684, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-as-append-or-modify\", \"hypothesis:primitives-without-write-time-feedback-atrophy\", \"thread:patch-emit-and-diff-render-cluster\"]}, \"practice/test-observation-kind\": {\"topic\": \"practice/test-observation-kind\", \"message\": \"test emit to verify observation kind not declared on project either; expected to fail loud or rejected silently \\u2014 instrumenting\", \"_ts\": 1778943461.903936, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/trace-source-facts-shape\", \"ops\": \"trace-arc\", \"message\": \"Orientation finding: source_facts entries are FLAT payloads with metadata under-prefixed (_ts, _observer, _origin, _id) \\u2014 see vertex_reader.py:911-918 and :925. stream_view consumes the NESTED fact-dict shape (f['kind'], f['ts'], f['observer'], f['payload'], f['id']). Adapter needed in fetch_trace: ~10 LOC to unflatten source-fact-payloads \\u2192 fact-dicts. Doesn't break the dissolution (the data is all there) but the wrap isn't literally zero-effort. Worth a clear comment at the adapter site noting the shape provenance \\u2014 future-me will want to know whether to fix it upstream (change source_facts shape) or keep adapting (decouple lens consumers from engine internals). Lean toward adapt-at-boundary: source_facts shape is engine-internal contract, lens is consumer surface, the adapter IS the boundary.\", \"_ts\": 1778956826.137085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/trace-implementation-plan\", \"thread:trace-implementation\"]}, \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/rowid-is-load-bearing-for-single-store-ordering\", \"ops\": \"loops-engine\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 surfaced by ULID regression audit: SqliteStore's single-store ordering invariants are carried by rowid, NOT by id. Specifically: since(cursor) uses WHERE rowid > ? ORDER BY rowid (sqlite_store.py:163, 191, 207), facts_by_kind uses ORDER BY rowid ASC (store_reader.py:207), replay_cursor uses rowid pagination. The original design pre-2026-03-15 used id (ULID, time-sortable) AND rowid (insertion order) in tandem \\u2014 id for global identity/dedup, rowid for per-store ordering. When the 2026-03-15 regression silently dropped id's time-sortable property, single-store ordering was preserved entirely by rowid \\u2014 that's why nothing else exploded for two months. THIS IS AN ACCIDENTAL SAVE, NOT A DESIGN PROPERTY anyone wrote down. If a future optimization rewrites cursor semantics to 'use id since it's globally unique, drop rowid pagination,' it will silently undo the load-bearing accident \\u2014 and unlike this regression, there's no decision-of-record naming rowid's role. Capturing here so next person reading these code paths finds the warning: rowid is load-bearing; do not remove or replace its role in ordering without verifying id-based replacement provides equivalent monotonicity AND cross-store interleaving guarantees (which python-ulid's default constructor does NOT, within a millisecond). The cross-store case is the gotcha: rowid is per-database, so it can't be the global ordering primitive \\u2014 that's what id-as-ULID is for. Both columns earn their existence.\", \"_ts\": 1778990270.582097, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\": {\"topic\": \"practice/agent-reports-as-starting-points-not-conclusions\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from the ULID-substrate session: both parallel Explore agents (code-trace + primitive-research) produced detailed reports that contained specific errors caught only by empirical verification before committing to the interpretation. Agent A (code-trace) overstated merge-dedup damage \\u2014 claimed 'production merge silently broken, identical facts get different ids, data multiplies' \\u2014 but reading merge.py and slice.py showed slice preserves id end-to-end, INSERT OR IGNORE dedup works under either uuid4 or ULID. The real damage was ORDER BY id semantics (random vs chronological), not dedup. Agent B (primitive-research) claimed python-ulid's default ULID() constructor 'is NOT monotonic within a millisecond \\u2014 each call generates fresh random bits.' Empirical check (5 sequential ULID() calls in shell) showed monotonic suffixes \\u2014 within-ms monotonicity IS provided by default in python-ulid 3.x. Both errors were specific and consequential \\u2014 if I'd committed the planned regression-bar test (merge through SqliteStore.append() asserting dedup failure under uuid4) it would have failed because the dedup wasn't actually failing; the right test was ORDER BY id assertion. The discipline that caught both: don't accept agent reports as ground truth before writing code that depends on them. Verify the load-bearing claims by running the actual primitive in a shell, reading the actual implementation file, before designing the fix around the claim. Pattern: agent reports are starting-points for investigation, not conclusions. They mobilize quickly across breadth I can't cover serially, but they're working from less context than I have and they're not running the code. Cross-session companion to peer-attention-loop discipline (peers refine thinking through substance) \\u2014 agents refine breadth, peers refine substance, neither replaces verify-before-commit. Future-me operational form: when an agent report claims X, ask 'what's the cheapest empirical check that would confirm or falsify X?' \\u2014 usually under 30 seconds (shell command, file read, grep). Run it before any code edit that assumes X.\", \"_ts\": 1778996485.524356, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\"]}, \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\": {\"topic\": \"session/ulid-substrate-rescope-cadence\", \"ops\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"OBSERVATION 2026-05-16 from session-close: capturing the cadence that worked on this substrate-rescope arc, since Kyle's 'before we go faffing about with it' was the right framing and the session followed a specific ladder that's worth naming. (1) ORIENT \\u2014 read the friction body, read the live code, find the regression commit and read its diff + rationale (2026-03-15 commit 1cf99cc, perf-driven, narrow benchmark). Don't propose a fix yet. (2) DISPATCH PARALLEL AGENTS \\u2014 one for damage audit (code-trace across consumers), one for primitive research (fresh look at options). Both read-only, both inform the same decision, neither writes code. Kyle suggested this explicitly \\u2014 'spin up some Explore agents' \\u2014 and it was the right tool: agent breadth produced a comparison I couldn't have held serially. (3) ADVISOR BEFORE APPROACH \\u2014 after agent reports came back, called advisor with full transcript before committing to the implementation plan. Advisor caught: bundle test-gap closure with substrate swap in same commit (NOT separate; the test gap IS the regression bar); decision emit first BEFORE code so rationale is durable; verify python-ulid contract before merge test depends on it. (4) VERIFY EACH CLAIM EMPIRICALLY \\u2014 caught two agent errors (merge dedup not actually broken; within-ms monotonicity IS default in python-ulid). Caught one schema-semantics question (Crockford prefix bounds are conservative-correct \\u2014 no change needed in fact_by_id). (5) WRITE COMMITS ATOMICALLY \\u2014 Commit A (substrate fix + regression bar) = the smallest unit that restores property AND prevents same-shape regression. Commit B (coherence pass) = dropping the dead dep across engine/store + test fixtures + docstrings. Two commits, each leaves tree green, each reviewable. (6) REFINE EMISSIONS AS WORK PROGRESSES \\u2014 decision emit pre-coded then refined (advisor caught the over-cautious monotonicity caveat); friction refined to resolved with refs to commits; thread updated to partial with the deferred wedge question. The cadence: orient \\u2192 dispatch breadth \\u2192 consult depth \\u2192 verify before declaring \\u2192 atomic commits \\u2192 refine emissions. Each step caught a different class of error. Future-me: this is the shape to reach for when a substrate question lands with an embedded fix-shape that feels too narrow.\", \"_ts\": 1778996502.798265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/id-primitive-python-ulid\", \"friction:ulid-regressed-to-uuid4-in-sqlite-store\", \"thread:id-primitive-substrate-rescope\"]}, \"test/ulid-regression-verification\": {\"topic\": \"test/ulid-regression-verification\", \"message\": \"verify ULID receipt after gen_id dissolution\", \"_ts\": 1778999527.682082, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/smoke-test\": {\"topic\": \"test/smoke-test\", \"message\": \"smoke test 2026-05-17 session open\", \"_ts\": 1779050399.274602, \"_n\": 1}, \"ops/subtask-model-default\": {\"topic\": \"ops/subtask-model-default\", \"message\": \"Changed subtask default from opus to sonnet/medium in .subtask/config.json. Mechanical refactor tasks (dead code deletion, function migrations) don't need opus reasoning depth \\u2014 sonnet/medium was sufficient for all three passes and considerably faster. The sonnet-medium preset was already defined; just updated options.model and added options.reasoning.\", \"_ts\": 1779053759.652145, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/single-line-parent-one-way-expansion\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"kdl_insert_child on a single-line parent (loops { decision {...} }) splits the line and inserts inside the expanded form. kdl_remove_child on the resulting multi-line block works correctly but does NOT collapse back to single-line. Net behavior: insert+remove on single-line parent != identity. Documented in kdl_remove_child docstring + asserted in TestSingleLineParent.test_insert_then_remove_is_not_identity. Phase 2 consumers should expect this if mutating files that use single-line parent blocks. Corpus check: no in-repo .vertex has single-line top-level loops/observers/combine/sources, so Phase 2's sl add --kind X is unaffected. Recorded as observation rather than friction because the design tradeoff (expand-to-be-mutable vs preserve-original-shape) was deliberate \\u2014 Phase 0's strategy decision favored surgical line-based splice over canonical re-emit, and one-way expansion is the natural consequence of that choice.\", \"_ts\": 1779059059.321005, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-firing-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again, this session. The first-path test (insert_into_single_line_parent_expands \\u2014 verifies expansion happens) was the obvious one to write. The asymmetric-pair test (insert+remove on single-line parent \\u2014 verifies round-trip behavior) I inferred-in-head but did NOT pin down with a test until advisor flagged it. The corpus round-trip happened to pass only because no in-repo .vertex uses single-line top-level parents \\u2014 luck, not spec-met. Lesson reinforced: when adding a feature with two code paths, write the asymmetric-pair test BEFORE the first-path implementation, not after. Discriminator that should have fired: 'are there two code paths to this feature (single-line parent vs multi-line parent), and have I exercised both with the same input?' Yes, and I didn't until prompted.\", \"_ts\": 1779059064.618251, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase1-vertex-splice-library\"]}, \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/combine-mutation-no-change-fact\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Documented limitation: 'loops add <vertex> combine <PATH>' does NOT emit a change fact, even when the target vertex has a 'change' loop kind. Reason: the lang validator forbids 'combine' alongside 'store' (mutual exclusion at loader.py:752). Aggregation vertices are by-design store-less, so there's no store path to write change facts to. This is correct behavior \\u2014 store-less vertices can't host facts of any kind. Implications for users: structural mutations to combine blocks are silent except for the stdout receipt. If queryable history of aggregation-vertex evolution is wanted later, options are: (a) emit the change fact to an adjacent project store via an env-flag or cross-vertex ref; (b) introduce a 'meta' aggregator that observes both the aggregation vertex and a sibling store. Not in Phase 2 scope. Discovered while constructing the asymmetric-pair test for the refuses-and-preserves invariant \\u2014 the validator's rule surfaced both gaps in the same exercise.\", \"_ts\": 1779060180.792681, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/asymmetric-pair-test-fired-again\", \"feature\": \"vertex-living-document\", \"message\": \"Growing edge pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps fired again in Phase 2, same shape as Phase 1. Success path heavily tested (every fold-op, every observer combination, every combine variation = 23 tests). Failure path inferred but unpinned \\u2014 the refuses-and-preserves invariant (parse_vertex validation before write leaves file byte-identical on failure) had NO explicit test until advisor flagged it. Construction was sitting right there: the validator's combine-vs-store mutex provided a natural failure injection. Added test_validator_rejection_preserves_original_file. Pattern reinforcement: across two consecutive phases of the same project, the discipline misfires the same way \\u2014 write tests for the visible-success cases, leave the load-bearing-safety case to inference. The pre-check that catches this: 'what is my code REFUSING to do, and have I tested the refusal?' If the answer is 'no test', the invariant only exists in commit messages. Lock it with a test. Future-me at Phase 3 start: when writing tests for ls/rm/export, ask FIRST 'what does this refuse, and how do I prove the refusal preserves prior state?' Write that test before the happy-path tests.\", \"_ts\": 1779060189.098107, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\", \"task:phase2-add-declarations-surface\"]}, \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\": {\"topic\": \"practice/loc-budget-breach-as-extension-point\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 planned ~500 new LOC, actual ~1335 new (net after deletions: roughly neutral since ~600 LOC pop machinery retired alongside). The overrun was NOT scope creep \\u2014 it was the dispatcher-cascade-as-extension-point pattern firing predictably. Each new sub-namespace verb (kind/observer/combine/row) for both add and rm needs: argparse subparser, splice-path resolver, KDL block render, validator round-trip, change-fact emit branch, refusal test pair, happy-path test, round-trip test. That's ~7 lines \\u00d7 4 ops \\u00d7 2 directions \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor \\u2014 geometrically larger than the 'one new flag' mental model that produced the 500 estimate. Future-me: when planning a sub-namespace verb expansion, estimate per-op-per-direction \\u00d7 test-coverage-factor, not just 'one new file.' The work scales with the matrix, not the spine. Connects to add-vs-split shape-instinct (growing edge): even when the right call IS to add (sub-namespace was correct verb shape), the LOC cost of an add is matrix-shaped not linear.\", \"_ts\": 1779061782.863392, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"plan:vertex-living-document\", \"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\": {\"topic\": \"practice/asymmetric-pair-applied-proactively\", \"message\": \"Phase 3 test discipline shift worth naming. Phases 1 and 2 had advisor catch missing asymmetric-pair tests post-hoc (refusal cases written after happy paths). Phase 3 I wrote TestRmRefusals BEFORE TestRmHappy \\u2014 refusal-first by intention, not by review. Test ordering in test_rm_declarations.py shows the discipline: refusals come first in the file because they came first in the writing. Pattern moving from 'caught by advisor' (Phase 1) \\u2192 'remembered by me' (Phase 2) \\u2192 'structured as first move' (Phase 3). The catch-and-accept loop closes one layer when the catch becomes preemptive \\u2014 advisor's role shifts from 'find the missing test' to 'verify the asymmetric pair was actually exercised.' For future-me: when planning a new mutation surface, the file structure itself (refusal-class-first) is the artifact that locks the discipline.\", \"_ts\": 1779061792.181298, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"task:phase3-rm-ls-cascade-and-retirement\"]}, \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\": {\"topic\": \"practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern learned mid-session 2026-05-17 across 4 impl-review cycles (helpargs, trace-and-populations, helpargs-completion, ls-flag-grammar): use 'subtask review --task X --agent codex' for cross-adapter review IN PLACE on the impl task, NOT a separate review/X task. Three wins: (1) TUI pane unified \\u2014 review status shows in the impl task's activity log, no context switch between fix/X and review/X (Kyle's observation); (2) no harness-lock wrangling \\u2014 separate task was a workaround for 'sessions are not compatible across harnesses', not the design; (3) iteration loop tighter \\u2014 review findings \\u2192 send back \\u2192 re-review all on same task, single history.jsonl. I discovered subtask review --task --agent only after building the routine; the dual-task pattern is preserved in early session frictions as historical context but should not be repeated. The canonical they-plan routine's review step explicitly uses 'subtask review --task <task> --agent <reviewer>' \\u2014 confirming the in-place primitive is the intended shape. Codified in .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml + .subtask/agents/codex.yaml (commit pending).\", \"_ts\": 1779076367.662554, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\"]}, \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-review-merge-cycle-proven\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Pattern proven through 6 cycles 2026-05-17 read-ergonomics arc: claude impl (sonnet for direct work, opus for plan-first multi-layer) + codex review (gpt-5.5/low) + iterate-until-approve + merge. The 6 cycles: helpargs ripout (2 iterations), helpargs-completion (1 iteration), trace-and-populations (1 iteration for test add), ls-flag-grammar (3 iterations - peel collision, value-aware op-token, codex caught dispatcher edges), preview-decl (2 iterations - loader strictness, empty-block limitation), cardinality-auto-zoom (clean approve). Total: 8 friction resolutions across the arc (help-flag, read-lens-trace-broken, populations-leakage, ls-kind, read-narrow, read-kind-floods, plus 2 partial: mid-session refined and PR B fast-follow). 9 main-branch commits. The pattern's strongest signal: codex catches integration-boundary bugs that unit-level testing misses \\u2014 peel_observer in isolation passed but vertex-first dispatch lost the kyle name; --observer ls value-collision found 2 iterations deep; helpargs-completion needed structural test fix (auto-enumerate over VERBS|COMMANDS) to close the asymmetric-pair gap. The dispatch-boundary class is now a known target: when adding context-aware shortcuts at dispatcher seams, expect codex to find value/identifier collisions in the next iteration; make heuristics value-aware proactively. Infrastructure built mid-arc: .subtask/agents/codex.yaml + .subtask/routines/fix-with-review.yaml (gitignored, per-clone) codify the cycle. Discovered late but valuable: subtask review --task --agent codex is the proper primitive (in-place, single TUI pane); the dual-task workaround used early in the arc was unnecessary.\", \"_ts\": 1779078329.302452, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:help-flag-not-intercepted-at-verb-level\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-vs-subcommand-collision\", \"friction:read-kind-floods-without-narrower\", \"observation:practice/subtask-review-in-place-over-dual-task\"]}, \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/salience-windowing-collapses-flat-bucket\", \"message\": \"RESOLVED 2026-06-29. The \\\"future design pass\\\" arrived and went further than the suggested fix (raise the [:1] fallback cap): the salience auto-window is GONE entirely. _render_grouped no longer collapses large groups to salience>1 members \\u2014 every row renders on human reads, matching --json. The arbitrary [:1] fallback that made young namespaces unnavigable is removed with it. Confirmed live: sl read project --kind decision --key workflow/ (N=18) shows all 18, no \\\"(N more)\\\". Superseded by the parity-first baseline (decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels) \\u2014 windowing returns only as an explicit DESIGNED budget later, never the always-on default that caused this.\", \"_ts\": 1782745820.712346, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\", \"decision:rendering/salience-driven-display\", \"decision:rendering/salience-windowing\"], \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9YW3MCG59C0B080FX7J90R\"}, \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-test-as-architecture-feedback\", \"message\": \"Today the smoke-test pass was the architectural surface, not just a verification surface. Walked through 5 recent commits as a smoke check; the friction emit (thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate) surfaced one session of degenerate output from auto-zoom; Kyle's prompt at that moment ('are we getting tangled in another rendering knot') was triggered by the friction being concrete. Without emit-in-moment, the conversation would have happened later (next degenerate render, next escape-hatch flag) or never. PATTERN: smoke-tests of recent work are not just regression checks \\u2014 they are the first lower-density use of features designed in higher-density sessions, which is when shape-instinct fires on the substrate. The friction caught at smoke time becomes the data point for the architectural step-back. Future-me: when smoke-testing recent batches, treat the surface as load-bearing for the discipline-as-axis-catching-itself work \\u2014 Phase 1 high-density confirmations get tested at Phase 2 lower density, and that's where the inversions surface. Connects to pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps (the bug class) \\u2014 same shape at the architectural level (the design class).\", \"_ts\": 1779199065.14868, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lenses-consume-declared-properties\", \"friction:thread-namespace-breakdown-degenerate\"]}, \"session/2026-05-19\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-05-19\", \"message\": \"Productive arc: wip/lens-architecture (preview_fields through ls, _is_diff_skip predicate, degenerate namespace breakdown) + fix/cite-cluster (ref-stealing bug + implicit universal cite loop). Five frictions closed. Next: stdin-message-for-emit.\", \"_ts\": 1779212337.56734, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\", \"message\": \"Discriminator for \\\"declare per-kind on the loop block\\\" vs \\\"universal CLI feature\\\": does each consumer of the field-role need per-kind variability? preview YES (friction:status+message, decision:message, change:empty \\u2014 visible heterogeneity). search YES (different kinds index different fields). prose-as-stdin-eligibility NO \\u2014 the kind does not decide; the user at the call site does, by writing the flag at emit time. Kind-semantic properties earn declarations; call-site conventions do not. Surfaced 2026-05-19 designing stdin/file expansion for emit. The aesthetic parallel to preview_fields was structurally superficial \\u2014 looked like a sibling, turned out to be a different layer (input convention vs render selection). Future-me: when proposing a new loop-block declaration, ask this discriminator first.\", \"_ts\": 1779224978.847375, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/loops-field-role-family\", \"message\": \"search and preview are a real family on LoopDef: \\\"a list of payload field names with a particular role.\\\" Differ only in which consumer reads them and on which side of the lifecycle (write-side indexing vs read-side rendering). fold/boundary/parse are a different family \\u2014 runtime semantics, not field-role metadata. Family membership criterion: per-kind variability (each kind declares its own answer). prose-as-stdin-eligibility was almost the third member but failed the criterion \\u2014 call-site-semantic, not kind-semantic. N=2 confirmed members; family observation kept as substrate for recognizing future candidates. Do NOT refactor to unified fields{} block or per-field-type system yet \\u2014 patterns earn their refactor through use-forced shared shape, not aesthetic.\", \"_ts\": 1779224992.642026, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/declaration-vs-call-site-discriminator\"]}, \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\": {\"topic\": \"practice/empirical-precheck-collapses-design-pivots\", \"message\": \"Three pivots in one session designing stdin/file expansion for emit (hardcode message= \\u2192 declaration-driven via prose_fields \\u2192 universal magic syntax via =- and =@ \\u2192 explicit --stdin and --file flags). Each pivot toward less structure, each labeled \\\"truly dissolved plan.\\\" The cascade itself was aesthetic capture \\u2014 recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check was in the growing-edge but I missed firing it. The trivial empirical check that would have collapsed three pivots into one: \\\"sl emit project decision topic=foo@example.com --dry-run\\\" takes 2 seconds and would have shown the @ collision immediately, surfacing explicit-flags as the answer at pivot 1. Curl-convention vibes anchored me three pivots deep; one shell command would have grounded it. SHARPENING for future-me: when about to write up a design that depends on syntactic assumptions about real values, RUN the assumption against real data first \\u2014 before the design writeup, not after. Adjacent to but sharper than recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check: that pattern is about aesthetic-driven artifacts; THIS is about design-frame anchoring on inherited conventions.\", \"_ts\": 1779225016.698018, \"_n\": 1}, \"pattern/foo\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.803574, \"_n\": 5}, \"practice/foo\": {\"topic\": \"practice/foo\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.899496, \"_n\": 5}, \"identity/foo\": {\"topic\": \"identity/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.849991, \"_n\": 2}, \"ignoreme/foo\": {\"topic\": \"ignoreme/foo\", \"message\": \"(test residue from entity-ref bug repro 2026-05-19 \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239440.92067, \"_n\": 2}, \"practice/smoke-fixed\": {\"topic\": \"practice/smoke-fixed\", \"message\": \"(test fixture from friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref repro \\u2014 ignore)\", \"_ts\": 1779239580.966668, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\", \"message\": \"Nth instance of the shape: a positional or heuristic eating something that semantically belongs elsewhere. Catalog so far: cite vertex-positional eating first ref (0deb7ea); combine-vertex retain_facts gap eating cross-vertex transparency (trace arc); entity-ref slashed-scan eating fold-key topic values (33937f6). The catch-time pattern recognition (\\\"this is the same shape as the prior bug\\\") is now firing reliably mid-fix rather than retrospectively. The structural fix at one layer up is the kinds-i-produce registry \\u2014 resolver reads declared ref-bearing fields from registry rather than pattern-scanning slashed values. Today's fold-key skip closes the loudest case; coincidental collisions in other slashed payload values (description containing 'see pattern/foo' etc) remain latent. Registry would dissolve the latent class entirely.\", \"_ts\": 1779239617.742098, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\", \"pattern:exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"practice/coloncheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/coloncheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on colon-form ref\", \"_ts\": 1779239964.843768, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"practice/slashcheck\": {\"topic\": \"practice/slashcheck\", \"message\": \"check resolver behavior on slash-form ref\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KS1F412XAMFAF6CD7F49QTS7\", \"_ts\": 1779239966.241467, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction/entity-ref-resolver-treats-topic-as-ref\"]}, \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/slash-overload-as-system-notation-gap\", \"message\": \"At least six distinct conceptual meanings on / in the codebase: (1) kind/key entity address (CLI input), (2) kind/key payload value scanned by auto-resolver, (3) namespace/topic fold-key prefix (today's bug site), (4) parent/scope observer hierarchy (engine/observer.py), (5) template/subdir vertex template (init.py), (6) parent/alias combine child (resolve.py:_resolve_vertex_for_dispatch). Each consumer chose / organically because it's the obvious separator; the collision came from accumulation not design. Filesystem solved this with one meaning (hierarchy); URIs solved it with reserved chars per role (scheme: path/ ?query #fragment). Loops drifted into multi-meaning slash without picking either strategy. The non-decision IS the structural gap \\u2014 not the resolver's behavior specifically, but the absence of a chosen notation methodology. Adjacent to but distinct from typed-refs question: even with typed addresses, the / character still does five other things in the codebase that occasionally collide.\", \"_ts\": 1779244348.722274, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/heuristic-eats-semantic-field\"]}, \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/auto-resolver-coherent-until-trace-split-it\", \"message\": \"Timeline grounding 2026-05-19: the auto-resolver was internally coherent from 2026-03-09 (39d8de9) introduction through 2026-05-15. Slash-form on both write (_resolve_entity_refs) and read (no walker existed yet \\u2014 _ref siblings WERE the navigation mechanism). The convention split was created in 2026-05-16 by the trace verb commit (803ba03) \\u2014 cross-kind ref walking needed unambiguous parsing, chose colon over slash, fixed the read parser (_parse_fact_refs introduced as colon-only), did not propagate to write side. Same commit message explicitly notes catching 'ref parser used / separator instead of : (refs are kind:key)' \\u2014 the team thought the bug was caught when only the read side was fixed. Reframes 'messy codebase' as 'deferred-completion debt from a 3-day-old multi-step refactor.' This is a normal failure mode of substantial refactors (sweep gap), not a discipline collapse. Useful as orienting context whenever the typed-refs work is picked up \\u2014 the convention drift has a specific origin commit and a specific deferred sweep, not ambient cruft.\", \"_ts\": 1779244358.445589, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/park-may-16-write-side-migration-pending-typed-ref-question\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\"]}, \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\": {\"topic\": \"practice/structure-i-dont-read-wont-catch-my-drift\", \"message\": \"First-person reflection 2026-05-19: I emit refs constantly and never noticed the receipt was silently miscounting (canonical colon-form refs got 0 _ref siblings, receipt undercounted by 91.8% for three days). The (refs: N resolved) line slid past me without registering. Implication for typed-refs and any structural improvement: high-usage-without-noticing is possible. Structure I don't actively consume on the read path won't surface drift when it appears. If the typed-refs work lands purely in the write/resolver layer without changing what I see on emit or read, the next drift will slide past the same way. Discipline correction for hypothesis-refs-as-typed-address-dataclass: when designing the surface, make at least one consumer of the structure live in the path I read every emission cycle \\u2014 receipt, fold display, trace render. Don't trust 'the structure is there' as catch-mechanism without a read-path manifestation. Adjacent to existing growing edges (exercising-catches-coherence-gaps, recursion-pull-resistible-via-pre-check) \\u2014 but distinct: this is about which feedback loops actually close for me at usage time.\", \"_ts\": 1779244367.847802, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"observation:pattern/exercising-catches-coherence-gaps\"]}, \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/incumbent-bugs-surfaced-by-go-oracle\", \"message\": \"The Go oracle surfaced real protocol-vs-impl divergences LIVE in THIS monorepo Python (libs/atoms, libs/engine) \\u2014 all fix-BOTH, i.e. our code has them too. Actionable here independent of loops-go (verified vs HEAD 33937f6). Inventory: (1) replay reads ORDER BY rowid (store_reader.py:207, sqlite_store.py:179/207/223) + merge regenerates rowid in scan order (merge.py:74) => merge(A,B) != merge(B,A) for Collect/Window/Upsert; fix = replay in (ts,id) order. (2) _make_latest falls back to time.time() when _ts absent (engine.py:38) => determinism violation; fix = errors-are-facts. (3) resolve_entity_id ORDER BY rowid DESC LIMIT 1 (store_reader.py:235) => ref-time-blind AND merge-UNSTABLE; fix = ts-bounded (ts,id) resolution. (4) bool folds as 1 \\u2014 Python bool-is-int, no guard: Sum(true)=1, Min/Max=True (engine.py:53/164/176) => would violate a normative true!=1. (5) Sum/Avg/Min/Max/TopN-by omit num() guard => TypeError on non-numeric field (Go silently returns 0/skip \\u2014 different failure modes). (6) silent-false condition coercion: </> return False silently on non-numeric target (vertex.py:57-93) => a boundary like cpu>80 against a string-typed cpu never fires, no diagnostic. The monorepo backlog the port found; whether/when WE fix these in Python is a separate call from the loops-go protocol forks.\", \"_ts\": 1780456800.089516, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\": {\"topic\": \"design/peer-was-never-the-base-identity\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Caught at first real use of the Peer concept (delta 2 signer design): May decisions say 'verify against Peer.key' but engine/peer.py's own header documents Peer as 'convenience bundle: Observer + Grant' \\u2014 Observer is the base identity primitive and always was (every fact carries an observer string; scripts/services/sources already emit as observers, never dangling at the data layer). The key belongs to the OBSERVER, not Peer: registry is observer-name \\u2192 public key. Peer re-grounds as relational \\u2014 an observer seen from the federation edge, bundled with exchange policy (Grant, later transport) \\u2014 not a kind of entity. Resolves the vertex-as-self-peer strain: the vertex is an observer of its own stream (tick = observation of the window), which is the paradigm being literal. Layering: identity (observer+key) / authorization (Grant) / relationship (Peer). Putting key on Peer would have fused identity with authorization \\u2014 the fusion grant_of() exists to prevent.\", \"_ts\": 1781037167.203313, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\", \"decision:design/tick-signature-on-every-tick\"]}, \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\": {\"topic\": \"test/cwd-is-resolution-context-now\", \"feature\": \"vouch-substrate\", \"message\": \"Incident during resolution unification (2026-06-09 21:18): making add/rm local-first caused the declaration test suite \\u2014 which isolated LOOPS_HOME but ran with repo root as cwd \\u2014 to resolve 'project' to the LIVE .loops/project.vertex. Tests added ping/buf/temp/high kinds + a test observers block, removed the real task kind, and appended 18 test change-facts to the real store (permanent; append-only \\u2014 they age out of the collect-20 fold but stay in history; the history is honest about the incident). Vertex file restored by hand; store integrity verified by fold counts (43 tasks, 77 observations). LESSON: local-first resolution promotes cwd to resolution context \\u2014 any test that resolves a vertex BY NAME must isolate cwd, not just LOOPS_HOME. conftest already had the right fixture (loops_env = loops_home + chdir); the declaration tests used the env-only one because resolution used to be env-only. Fix: swapped both declaration test files to loops_env; full suite now guards with snapshot+diff of the live vertex. On-theme: the session designing tamper-evidence produced an accidental-tamper incident whose damage assessment was performed WITH the store's own fold counts.\", \"_ts\": 1781040065.284327, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:global-local-walk-broken\"]}, \"test/delta-2-live\": {\"topic\": \"test/delta-2-live\", \"message\": \"delta-2 live wiring check: this emit's session-boundary tick should mint signed\", \"_ts\": 1781042637.787637, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\": {\"topic\": \"design/event-order-vs-witness-order\", \"feature\": \"tick-hash-chain\", \"message\": \"Two irreducible orders, two claims. Event order (ULID, fact.ts) = when things happened; read-path's order; human-scale, ties meaningless. Witness order (rowid) = when this store received them; the chain's order \\u2014 chain claims receipt-integrity, not chronology. The killer case is late arrival, not sub-ms ties: a backfilled/synced fact carries an honest old event-ts; under id-ordered windows it lands inside a sealed window and triggers a false tamper alarm caused by truthfulness; under append-ordered windows the next tick covers it honestly. Lamport in system vocabulary: each store is an observer with its own experiential sequence; cross-store order is constructed (merge, with receipt = new observer born), not discovered. ULID was never failing at its job; it was the wrong authority for the chain's claim regardless of tie behavior.\", \"_ts\": 1781045333.264115, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:chain-cursor-assumes-ulid-order\"]}, \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\", \"message\": \"Verified from the other side of the close: SessionEnd-emits-seal fired live (tick rowid 215, 00:31, reason-fact 'session close: kyle/loops-claude', chained+signed) \\u2014 the prediction held where delta-2's silently failed, because close dissolved into seal into fact-stream machinery, leaving no bespoke wiring to rot. Second finding: tick 212 (the celebrated first signed tick) carries a uuid4 fact_cursor \\u2014 the witness-order bug's fingerprint frozen at mint time. The fix (3b2ceb5) corrects forward only; tamper-evidence makes the bug's artifact permanent. The chain attests what the code believed at witnessing, including its mistakes. The wrong number that opened the session is signed into the substrate four rows from its fix.\", \"_ts\": 1781051701.166909, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:session/2026-06-09-third-fable-session\"]}, \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/fix-by-keeping-not-building\", \"message\": \"Dissolution form identified across the attestation arc (8 commits, one epoch day): the purest fix is 'stop discarding' \\u2014 verify_chain already computed every per-tick number that -v now renders; the walk threw them away. Not 'X collapses into Y' but 'X already existed, unobserved.' Check for this form FIRST when a read-path gap surfaces: does some existing walk already compute the answer and discard it? Cheapest fix class, easiest to miss because nothing is wrong \\u2014 something is merely unkept. Second instance same arc: window_facts per tick (the instrument that would have caught witness-order a session earlier) was always one COUNT away inside a loop verify already ran.\", \"_ts\": 1781056749.251148, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-envelope-read-path\"]}, \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/robustness-as-failure-metabolism\", \"message\": \"REFINED by Kyle in-conversation: the visibility of failures IS the robustness \\u2014 not a byproduct of metabolism but the property itself. Metabolism without visibility would be silent absorption, exactly the failure mode the system exists to kill (April's silent hook-rot is the type specimen). Hierarchy: visibility is the property, metabolism is the mechanism, signing is the guarantee that visibility survives the parties who witnessed it. A failure you can see is fixable; a failure that is signed has trustable history. Original framing and counterweight (n=1 survival counts, mechanism-robust-before-track-record) stand.\", \"_ts\": 1781057581.14888, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/chain-fossilizes-its-own-bug\"]}, \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\": {\"topic\": \"design/rebirth-ref-rewrite-dissolves\", \"message\": \"Ref-rewrite component of rebirth dissolves: payload refs are stored entity-keyed (kind:key), resolved to fact ids at READ time (resolve_entity_id), so id migration needs no payload rewriting. Raw old ids appear only in prose messages (32/2048 facts in project.db) \\u2014 history, not structure; rewriting would falsify quotes. Old tick envelopes re-enter as tick-facts VERBATIM (signature must verify against original bytes); old-to-new id mapping stays recomputable because the migration transform is deterministic: new_id = ULID(ms(fact.ts) || sha256(old_id)[:10]). Determinism is what makes receipt-verification-by-re-run an operation rather than a promise.\", \"_ts\": 1781059122.056763, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\": {\"topic\": \"ops/three-id-eras-in-stores\", \"message\": \"Live rebirth of project.db surfaced a THIRD id era: 919 lowercase ULIDs (sqlite-ulid C-extension era) alongside 872 uuid4 ids and ~258 canonical python-ulid ids. Lowercase sorts above uppercase in ASCII, so the lowercase era is ALSO order-broken \\u2014 01kjtv... sorts after every 01KTQP... forever. The mixed-era story was always told as two eras; the itch was one number reading wrong (1791 ids migrated vs the 872 the story predicted). ulid-migration needs no change: the canonical-form rule (uppercase Crockford or re-mint) covers all three eras uniformly \\u2014 one rule in the receipt, not three.\", \"_ts\": 1781059758.32546, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:rebirth-with-receipt\"]}, \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"ops/init-resolution-asymmetry\", \"ops\": \"loops-cli\", \"message\": \"Friction half resolved by ops/keygen-via-add-observer: sl add <v> observer <name> --keygen now dissolves the manual keygen+register sequence for config-level vertices. The init-only-upgrades-local asymmetry itself stands, but the signing-entry use case no longer routes through init.\", \"_ts\": 1781280565.980858, \"_n\": 2, \"status\": \"resolved\"}, \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/rejected-counter-is-state-about-folding\", \"message\": \"The {target}_rejected counter is a new ontological category in fold state: the first state key the engine writes that no fact supplied and no fold op declared \\u2014 state ABOUT the folding, not folded state. Same family as Avg's hidden _sum/_count, but those are implementation detail of a declared op; _rejected is the engine commenting on the quality of its own input stream. If this category grows (parse-rejection counts? grant-rejection counts? boundary-misfire counts?), it wants a naming convention and a place in the tick envelope \\u2014 observability of the fold process itself, which connects directly to robustness-as-visibility-of-failures. Noted, not prescribed; second instance earns the design.\", \"_ts\": 1781283630.27214, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/empty-observer-path-join-footgun\", \"feature\": \"attestation-delta-3\", \"message\": \"Composition bug caught by delta-2's existing tests on first integration: fact_signer_for resolved keys/<observer>/ via Path join, and observer='' collapses keys_root/'' to the flat layout \\u2014 an ANONYMOUS writer would have been signed with the vertex key's authorship claim, which is exactly the forgery the per-observer design exists to prevent. Fixed with an explicit guard (empty observer and '..' segments never sign \\u2014 an observer name is a key, not a path expression). Shape note: the bug class is 'identifier used as path expression'; anywhere observer names hit the filesystem needs the same guard. The break surfaced as a verify failure against the registry \\u2014 the system's own verification caught the system's own forgery before any human did.\", \"_ts\": 1781289363.377241, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-per-observer-keys\", \"thread:fact-signing-delta-3\"]}, \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12 finding, stepping back from the 87-item backlog: the dominant staleness mode was resolved-in-reality-open-in-store (vouch-evidence 'awaiting go' days post-commit; config-drift fixed by unrecorded symlink; verified hypotheses never status-bumped). We engineered the write side hard (emit-liberally, reroute-log, Stop hook) and built nothing for closure \\u2014 opening is reflexive, closing is manual archaeology whose cost GROWS with delay as provenance decays. Same shape as the chain design gap: tamper-evidence exists, truth-decay detection does not. Most closures today had machine-checkable evidence (commit in git log, symlink on disk, CLAUDE.md section) \\u2014 a resolution-candidate detector (re-check refs that point at checkable substrates, open reconcile with 'these N look resolved-in-reality') is the read-path-feature form of the fix. Discipline costume would be 'reconcile more often.'\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.24344, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:reroute-capture-practice\"]}, \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-06-12: friction:painted-overreach-review records Kyle avoiding emission because store read-back is unpleasant \\u2014 the exact flywheel that closed loops-claude's emission-cadence gap (read-path payback below willpower threshold) running BACKWARDS for the other participant. Substrate read-path investment went to agent session-start (hooks, lenses, orient block); the human browse-path got painted overreach. Two-participant store, one-participant read-path tuning. Possibly the highest-leverage open item: Kyle's emission rate is the half of the corpus that cannot be recovered later.\", \"_ts\": 1781295902.376607, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:painted-truncation-everywhere\", \"thread:painted-overreach-review\"]}, \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/cross-repo-blindness\", \"message\": \"The read-path-asymmetry observation (emitted ~20min prior as 'the thing not talked about') was already being worked by Kyle in ~/Code/painted \\u2014 the fidelity/disclosure-grammar epoch IS the human-browse-path investment. The project store could not see it: closure-asymmetry one level up, across repo boundaries. The store's umwelt ends at the repo edge; work in sibling repos that resolves this store's threads is invisible until a human carries it across.\", \"_ts\": 1781298689.538121, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:pattern/closure-asymmetry\", \"observation:pattern/read-path-asymmetry-by-participant\"]}, \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"message\": \"CODE-CONFIRMED (2026-06-13 smoke-test): fact-signing at emit is OPPORTUNISTIC, not required; verification is AUDIT-ONLY. emit always composes fact_signer_for(path) into the vertex program; a fact signs iff keys/ exists AND the emitting observer has a key (keys/<observer>/ or flat self-key) AND store is in signing era \\u2014 else appends UNSIGNED silently (no warn, no refusal). NO vertex 'require signature' config exists: the only lang 'strict' flag refuses on emit VALIDATION failures (undeclared kind/observer via validate_emit), NOT on missing signatures. fact_verifier_for/verify_chain are called ONLY in commands/store.py (store verify + reanchor) \\u2014 operator-invoked, registry-aware (each fact sig checked against its declared observer key exactly). vertex.py receive, program.py, sync.py do NOT verify. Net: sign-if-you-can on write + check-if-you-ask on demand; neither required-on-emit nor verified-on-receive. The progressive-policy + sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive design specified the require+verify layer; it is NOT implemented. NUANCE: require-on-emit is a present gap and the ROOT of the disclosure over-claim (verify renders signed/\\u2713 as an enforced guarantee for an unenforced property). verify-on-receive is correctly DEFERRED not missing \\u2014 no untrusted cross-store receive path exists yet (local single-writer; verifying your own just-signed fact is circular); load-bearing at the transport/peer era. Kyle's recollection confirmed: the 'vertex must require it' layer is the missing precondition for signing to matter.\", \"_ts\": 1781384680.508372, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-substrate-with-progressive-policy\", \"decision:design/sign-on-emit-verify-on-receive\"]}, \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\": {\"topic\": \"design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"message\": \"SMOKE-TEST DELIVERABLE (2026-06-13, hybrid hands-on + breadth sweep, 34 verified grammar gaps). READINESS VERDICT: READY for the UX/honest-disclosure session \\u2014 the SUBSTRATE is coherent and honest; the DISCLOSURE is not, and the gap is fully narratable (this catalog IS the migration spec). Painted-view build still gated on painted 0.2.0. ROOT CAUSE (single): the era boundary is narrated at the TICK layer (per-row sig-checkmark vs unsigned, no alarm) but nowhere at the fact-signature layer or the headline, so the reader model (attestation total+monotone; checkmark=attested; unsigned=wrong) collides with reality (attestation progressive-from-era-boundary; checkmark=no-break; unsigned=pre-era-or-unkeyed). TIER-1 honesty fixes (next session, no new machinery \\u2014 copy the tick-layer era grammar down): (a) checkmark must distinguish attested from no-break \\u2014 a 0-tick/0-signed store reports chain-intact + ok + fact_sig_ok vacuously [ZG-2,F1]; (b) covered (receipt) vs signed (authorship) are orthogonal, stop stacking as a fraction [ZG-7]; (c) the warning keyed-observer-no-signed-facts is backwards-from-tamper-logic, fires on vertex-key + pre-era principals, silent on kyle/loops-claude (79 signed/1055 unsigned where a strip could hide); reserve warning for keyed observer who signed-then-stopped, state era plainly otherwise [ZG-3-corrected,F3]; (d) -v/-vv deepen only the all-green tick table, never the warning; --json carries per-observer detail the text withholds [ZG-1]; (e) read --ticks list is attestation-blind at every zoom while store verify is rich \\u2014 pick a canonical tick grammar [ZG-4,F7]; (f) glyph collision: leading checkmark=chain-link appears on signed AND unsigned ticks [ZG-5,F5]. CANDIDATE BEHAVIORAL BUGS (UNVERIFIED \\u2014 repro on KEYED copies first, several smell like tmp-copy-without-keys artifacts): verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes [HIGH, if real one integrity verb is weaker than it reads]; seal mints unsigned tick reporting success [likely no-keys artifact, but seal never discloses its signing outcome = real gap]; read-path green over broken-signature fact [FC-04]; read --ticks on archive db path hard-crashes UTF-8 codec [F8]; reanchor no-key refusal is a raw traceback. CLI ergonomics: read --help omits --since/--ticks/--id/--refs [FC-01]; read silently ignores -1/--since in fold mode, no newest-selector [FC-02]; sl emit VERTEXNAME silently writes kind=VERTEXNAME to default vertex [footgun]. Full per-finding detail in session workflow output wm7y2wraf.\", \"_ts\": 1781385217.229085, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/signing-enforcement-status\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"message\": \"Investigated the smoke-test's HIGH candidate-bug \\\"verify-vs-reanchor opposite verdict on identical bytes\\\" (from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog). VERDICT: not an integrity-verb divergence. Three confirmations on properly-keyed stores: (1) verify and reanchor AGREE on a keyed copy of the current store, and reanchor is BYTE-IDEMPOTENT \\u2014 the db sha256 is unchanged after \\\"96 facts re-signed, 8 ticks re-chained\\\" because ed25519 is deterministic, so re-signing canonical bytes reproduces identical signatures; (2) reanchor with private keys absent raises BEFORE any write (post-sha == pre-sha) \\u2014 the engine explicitly guards \\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\"; (3) the JCS swap (c1f50ed) is a no-op for existing ASCII/integer payloads \\u2014 compact-sorted JSON already equals RFC 8785 for that content, which is why reanchor changed zero bytes and why even the pre-JCS archive still verifies chain-intact. The \\\"opposite verdict\\\" reduces to: verify succeeds while reanchor's no-key / no-vertex REFUSAL rendered as a raw Python traceback (uncaught ValueError) \\u2014 read as a crash / contradicting verdict. Both refusals carry excellent messages; they were just not caught at the CLI boundary. FIX LANDED: catch (ValueError, FileNotFoundError) at the store view boundary (apps/loops/src/loops/cli/views/store.py), render via reporter.err + exit 1; other exception types still raise so genuine bugs stay debuggable. 3 regression tests + full app suite green (1322 passed). This is the first TIER-1 disclosure-honesty fix and it de-risks the broader pass: verify's GREEN is honest about chain-integrity \\u2014 only the signature-disclosure grammar (checkmark-vs-attested, the backwards warning, covered-vs-signed) still needs work.\", \"_ts\": 1781453970.21701, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/read-path-attestation-neutral\", \"message\": \"FC-04 from observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog (\\\"read-path green over broken-signature fact\\\") investigated on a keyed copy. VERDICT: the everyday read/fold path is attestation-NEUTRAL, not attestation-GREEN. Method: tampered a signed fact's payload on a keyed copy. store verify flags it loudly (\\u2717 FACT SIGNATURES BROKEN, names the exact fact: \\\"signature invalid \\u2014 content does not match the observer's authorship signature\\\"); the read/fold path renders the tampered content verbatim (\\\"message: TAMPERED CONTENT\\\") at every zoom including -vv FULL, with NO attestation glyph \\u2014 headline identical to a clean fact. The render path is signature-BLIND by construction: lenses/fold.py + commands/fetch.py never inspect per-fact signatures (the only attestation-aware code is the TICK-window/witness-era path used by --ticks; \\\"by-fold signature\\\" in fetch.py is the fold-shape sense, not crypto). So the catalog framing is slightly imprecise: there is no false GREEN \\u2014 read simply does not speak to attestation at all, UNLIKE store verify's green \\u2713 which DOES claim ok (that is the real overstatement surface, captured separately as the TIER-1 checkmark fix). CONCLUSION: not a behavioral bug; reframes as a disclosure-DESIGN question \\u2014 should the everyday read path carry a tamper/unsigned marker, or is attestation-as-a-separate-verb (read = content view, verify = integrity view) the honest separation that keeps crypto out of every read? Same gating as enforcement: with no untrusted receive path yet (decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred), a read-path tamper-marker has no consumer \\u2014 it reactivates when something can write facts you did not author. Held for Kyle as a TIER-1 design call, not a fix. Second catalog candidate-bug to dissolve under the same method as the HIGH (observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent).\", \"_ts\": 1781456773.015208, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/seal-no-era-guard-silent-unsigned\", \"message\": \"Catalog candidate-bug #2 (\\\"seal mints unsigned tick reporting success; seal never discloses its signing outcome\\\") investigated on keyed vs no-keys copies. BOTH claims CONFIRMED \\u2014 and this is the ONE REAL finding of the candidate-bug sweep (the HIGH verify-vs-reanchor, FC-04 read-path, F8 ticks-UTF-8, and the reanchor traceback all dissolved / downgraded / fixed). (b) DISCLOSURE: sl seal prints \\\"tick: project (13 fields)\\\" + \\\"stored: seal/...\\\" and NEVER states whether it signed \\u2014 the output is BYTE-IDENTICAL whether the tick was signed (keyed copy) or not (no-keys copy). The \\\"13 fields\\\" is no signal: the signature COLUMN exists in both, just NULL when unsigned. (a) INTEGRITY (worse than the catalog's \\\"likely harmless artifact\\\"): on a store already in the signed era, sl seal run WITHOUT keys mints an UNSIGNED tick, exit 0, success output \\u2014 and that unsigned tick BREAKS THE CHAIN: store verify then reports \\\"\\u2717 CHAIN BROKEN ... unsigned tick after signed era \\u2014 signature stripped or era regressed\\\". Airtight via the symmetric control: the keyed copy's seal minted a SIGNED tick (9/9 signed, chain intact); only the no-keys seal breaks it. ASYMMETRY with reanchor: reanchor GUARDS this exact boundary (\\\"refusing partial re-anchor; a signed fact must not lose authorship\\\") and refuses without keys; seal does NOT \\u2014 it is the one verb that can silently CREATE the era-regressed / chain-broken state that verify is designed to detect. Contradicts the tick-side STRUCTURAL-signing posture (ticks are vertex-self-signed at a single funnel, \\\"structural from this point forward\\\" \\u2014 unlike opportunistic per-observer fact signing). REAL-WORLD REACH: the SessionEnd hook runs sl seal automatically on every session close; if keys are ever absent/moved at close (fresh clone pre-keygen, copied store, relocated keydir) the hook silently breaks the chain and nothing says so until a later store verify. Design call held for Kyle \\u2014 see thread:seal-era-boundary-guard.\", \"_ts\": 1781456966.743867, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/fact-signing-enforcement-deferred\", \"observation:design/disclosure-grammar-smoke-test-catalog\", \"observation:implementation/reanchor-verify-not-divergent\", \"thread:loops-on-disclosure-grammar\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses\", \"message\": \"Two-round adversarial review (Workflow, 15 agents each) of the seal-era-guard arc caught TWO real holes that solo confidence missed \\u2014 after I had said \\\"pretty confident we're good.\\\" Round 1 (on 9f2de91, verb-scoped guard): HIGH \\u2014 the guard sat on the seal VERB, but \\\"sl emit <v> seal\\\" fires the same boundary via cmd_emit, a one-token bypass of the floor. A store-level invariant cannot be enforced at the verb. Round 2 (on 6c368e4, after moving the guard to the engine mint): MEDIUM \\u2014 Vertex._store_tick is NOT the only live mint (apps/tasks' harness emit_tick is a second), so enforce_floor=False was fail-OPEN; a forgotten caller silently bypassed the invariant. Both fixes were dissolutions the reviews named: (1) move enforcement from the verb to the store mint; (2) flip the default to fail-SAFE (enforce by default, name the exemptions). PATTERN for a security/integrity invariant: (a) enforce at the single lowest chokepoint, not at each call site; (b) make enforcement the DEFAULT with named opt-outs, never opt-in \\u2014 both \\\"where\\\" and \\\"default polarity\\\" are load-bearing, and adversarial review surfaced them precisely because the holes were the cases my framing assumed away (\\\"single mint point\\\", \\\"covers the hook\\\"). One refinement of the review itself: checking append_tick's callers BEFORE applying the reviewer's literal \\\"guard in append_tick\\\" caught that it is shared with rebirth/slice \\u2014 the right seam was narrower than the review's first suggestion. Review informs; caller-analysis decides placement.\", \"_ts\": 1781463026.469129, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-signing-era-is-a-floor\", \"thread:seal-era-boundary-guard\"]}, \"ops/loops-release-path\": {\"topic\": \"ops/loops-release-path\", \"message\": \"Loops release path (canonical): bump version + CHANGELOG -> commit -> git tag -aX.Y.Z -> push main + tag -> gh release create vX.Y.Z (THIS triggers PyPI via trusted-publish workflow) -> verify https://pypi.org/pypi/strange-loops/X.Y.Z/json returns 200. Local 'uv publish' does NOT apply to strange-loops (the ~/.pypirc token is painted-only); the GitHub Release IS the publish trigger. Bare 'git push tag' is insufficient \\u2014 release.yml listens on release:published, not tag push.\", \"_ts\": 1781476532.154559, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:ops/release-0.4.0\"]}, \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\": {\"topic\": \"practice/grow-painted-over-workaround\", \"message\": \"Standing tie-breaker for the whole rebuild (Kyle, 2026-06-14): anything painted can do, prefer painted; push loops into domain-only arenas; if painted lacks something, grow painted rather than work around it. This is the dissolution principle scoped to the loops/painted boundary \\u2014 it governs every remaining rebuild step (Tag over fidelity_from_args, budgets over getattr, record_line over hand truncation) and the grow-painted candidates in design \\u00a72.\", \"_ts\": 1781477942.933982, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/full-painted-integration-residue\"]}, \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\": {\"topic\": \"practice/drift-prediction-conservative-miss\", \"feature\": \"cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"message\": \"Calibration (2026-06-15, step-5 budget_fields adoption): I predicted to Kyle that adopting painted's better truncation-gate contract would drift goldens as short whole fields reappeared in preview lines, and committed to flagging the drift fact-by-fact. The drift did not occur \\u2014 zero golden changes. The divergence is real (proven by a targeted unit test) but the golden corpus doesn't contain the trigger case (a trailing preview field landing in a sub-min_field slot while fitting whole). The miss was conservative (predicted MORE change than happened), which is the safe direction, but it's still a miss: I reasoned from the contract's logical reach, not from whether the test corpus exercises that reach. Lesson: when predicting test/golden impact of a behavior change, check whether the fixtures actually hit the changed branch before asserting drift \\u2014 'the contract changed here' != 'the corpus exercises here'.\", \"_ts\": 1781551542.939654, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/budget-fields-truncation-gate-contract\"]}, \"session/2026-06-26-reconcile-and-render-review\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-26-reconcile-and-render-review\", \"message\": \"Session arc: reconcile + pre-push render review after several sessions away on agent-attestation (now split to its own project). SHAPE: orient \\u2192 reconcile triage \\u2192 delegate cheap wins to a background subagent + adversarial review to a workflow \\u2192 adjudicate findings inline \\u2192 push \\u2192 wrap. RECONCILE: vouch umbrella repointed to agent-attestation project (13 siblings stay parked, Kyle: 'will come back loops-adjacent'); 12 stale hypotheses CITED not re-emitted (salience bump without churn \\u2014 Kyle's call, fits cite semantics exactly); cheap-wins subagent resolved 4 frictions (zsh-globbing CLAUDE.md note, F401 baseline 87 imports/49 files, + the broken-test-suite friction which was STALE \\u2014 already fixed by the 0.4.0 release commit, a reconcile catching resolution-lag). REVIEW WORKFLOW (8 agents, 286k tokens): 3 confirmed / 3 refuted on the render side, loops-go R2 conformance CLEAN. Confirmed: (1) HIGH DETAILED-density swap (gained message-body, lost status/files; trace status transitions now FULL-only) \\u2014 KEPT as design call, recorded decision:rendering/detailed-zoom-density; (2) MED live Ctrl-C 130\\u21920 \\u2014 ACCEPTED (painted 0.4.1 still returns 0, would need upstream change), decision:rendering/live-ctrlc-exit-zero; (3) LOW dead _summary_fields \\u2014 REMOVED (commit 0c671bb). PIVOT: discovered painted advanced to 0.4.1 while loops pinned <0.4 on 0.3.1; painted 0.4.0 was loops-rebuild-driven (callout/rule/rank-glyphs/table-FIT/C0-C1-neutralization) \\u2192 next GATE captured as thread:painted-040-gate. BUILT: portable .claude/skills/loops/SKILL.md (thread:loops-practice-skill). Pushed 6 commits to origin (GitLab+GitHub). CALIBRATION: clean delegate/inline discrimination \\u2014 workflow for adversarial wire-accurate review (caught real findings + refuted 3 plausible ones), subagent for mechanical fixes, inline for judgment calls. NEXT SESSION: UI/render work on painted 0.4+ (run the gate, then disclosure-grammar tier-1 catalog via callout + fold-badge residue).\", \"_ts\": 1782530589.067904, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/detailed-zoom-density\", \"thread:cli-render-rebuild-on-painted-020\", \"thread:painted-040-gate\"]}, \"rendering/painted-tui-framework-grown\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-tui-framework-grown\", \"message\": \"painted.tui grew a full interactive framework the loops read path doesnt use: nav-stack Action model (Push/Pop/Stay/Quit/Focus/Search/Emit), built-in filters (filter_prefix/fuzzy/contains), list_view/ListState + data_explorer/DataExplorerState, Viewport scroll model, TestSurface for golden-testing interactive flows, layers/mouse. tui/store_app.py predates most of it and hand-rolls truncation/scroll/rows; it is a ticks-first DB inspector reached via store -i, not a fold explorer. Interactive read path should be a fold-Surface on these primitives, retiring store_apps hand-rolled rendering.\", \"_ts\": 1782572396.638231, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"practice/usage-grounding-before-ui-redesign\": {\"topic\": \"practice/usage-grounding-before-ui-redesign\", \"message\": \"Raw siftd signal before forensic synthesis (2026-06-27): 8569 sl/loops invocations + 761 sqlite3-against-loops reroutes globally across 406 workspaces. Sample read commands show the static read path is consumed almost entirely through shell post-filters: sl read --kind X --key Y | head -100, | grep -i trace, --facts | head -200, --plain | grep -E. Two gaps visible pre-analysis: (1) missing content-search (agents pipe to grep for substring), (2) verbosity (agents pipe to head to truncate). The reroute IS the say/do seam made measurable: system says read is the interface; 761 sqlite escapes + pervasive grep/head say otherwise.\", \"_ts\": 1782575228.154623, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/two-pre-build-risks-surface\": {\"topic\": \"design/two-pre-build-risks-surface\", \"message\": \"Stress-test surfaced two risks to resolve BEFORE building the Surface keystone (2026-06-27): (1) GRANULARITY-BY-CARDINALITY -- the integration auto-returns the whole body when a filtered read collapses to one row, making output SHAPE depend on result-set size (a read that returns a body today returns headlines tomorrow when a second fact lands). Breaks the load-bearing addressed-read=body trust -> agents reroute to sqlite again. Fix: make whole an explicit address property, not a runtime row-count side effect. (2) FTS CONFIRM ASYMMETRY -- the read/write symmetry (emit re-enters the read seam) is FALSE on the search axis: a just-emitted fact is unsearchable via --match until re-index, so emit->read --match->nothing-landed->panic->sqlite manufactures the exact reroute were eliminating. Fix: steer confirm-after-emit to --last (entity/ts axis), make the coverage signal loud.\", \"_ts\": 1782581589.368078, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\"]}, \"session/2026-06-27-surface-doc-spine-and-decisions\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-27-surface-doc-spine-and-decisions\", \"message\": \"Session arc (2026-06-27): made the dense structured-surface design doc holdable + closed all 6 open decisions. Started from \\\"doc is dense, hard to hold entirely\\\" \\u2192 diagnosed it as a doc ABOUT progressive disclosure that did not itself disclose progressively \\u2192 added a SPINE top-layer (one value Surface between fetch+render; transforms before, two encoders after; net-new \\u2248 one file; reading-map tags each section). Unpacked the vocabulary: Surface=value, view=named selection (FUNDAMENTAL, declared as data in views{}), lens=just a render (the optional Surface->Block encoder a view references); view \\u228b lens. Pinned the vertex-file face: declares loops{} (vocabulary) + views{} (absorbs lens{}); a lens is referenced by name, never declared. Resolved all 6 open decisions (under design/): #1 json hard-break, #2 eq+comma-OR inline (neq/prefix view-only), #4 retract hide-from-fold keep-edges, #5 retract-now/gc-defer, #6 defer-TUI/greenlight-by-use. #3 DIVERGED from the rec \\u2192 print-not-write (--declare-observer prints the observers{} entry for the actor to apply; the KDL writer DISSOLVES; reframe: write-vs-print is upstream of append-vs-round-trip; observers{} is also the key registry, so auto-writing would mint trust). Residue swept across 11 sites; session was friction-light (no reroutes logged). NEXT SESSION (Kyles plan): review & grounding pass \\u2014 verify the docs code claims against live code (the lenses-copy-paste-salience claim, the cited line numbers, the fetch_tick_windows/vertex_search anchors) \\u2014 then discuss implementation (build sequence slice 0-1: call_lens signature-inspection precondition, then the surface.py keystone). Doc is now decision-complete: Spine on top, vocabulary pinned, all forks closed.\", \"_ts\": 1782607939.716684, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/declare-observer-print-not-write\", \"decision:design/views-fundamental-lens-is-a-render\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-verify-caught-missing-kind-guard\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-verify-caught-missing-kind-guard\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"The S6 adversarial workflow (5 dimensions, 16 candidates, 13 confirmed) caught a MAJOR regression the green suite did NOT: moving emit's required 'kind' argparse positional into a tokens nargs=* bucket made kind structurally optional \\u2014 an all-KEY=VALUE bucket (the natural 'forgot the kind' mistake) yielded kind=None, which dry-run previewed as a kind:null fact with exit 0 (false success) and the real path crashed opaquely. 4 of 5 reviewers found it independently. Also caught: the boundary 'tick:' disclosure was on stdout and corrupted the new --json Surface contract. Lesson: a grammar rewrite can silently drop an invariant (required-arg) that argparse enforced for free; the structural-sensor (adversarial pass over my own synthesis) caught what the passing tests masked \\u2014 read-path-features-over-noticing-skills, live again.\", \"_ts\": 1782656111.517516, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\", \"message\": \"A 3-lens adversarial workflow caught two real S7 defects the green suite AND my repo-root CLI-smoke both missed \\u2014 and reproduced them EMPIRICALLY against live stores, not by reasoning. From the repo root `project` resolves to the instance store (correct), so --chain false \\\"all legacy\\\" (combine aggregates) and the dropped-genesis undercount (32 vs 33) only surfaced off-root / on `meta`. Live instance of structural-sensors-over-volition: in-flow smoke from a convenient cwd is a happy-path lens; run the adversarial pass on my own synthesis by default.\", \"_ts\": 1782659215.047259, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\"]}, \"session/2026-06-28-s7-store-attestation-surface\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-28-s7-store-attestation-surface\", \"message\": \"Session arc: built S7 (store ticks --chain + stats --by-kind) end-to-end on feat/surface-build1 \\u2014 8/9 slices done, committed 7d23757. The session story IS the adversarial pass: a 3-lens verify workflow caught two real defects on the feature core that the green suite AND my repo-root CLI-smoke both missed, reproduced empirically against live stores \\u2014 (1) --chain on a combine aggregate emitted a false all-legacy verdict (now refused like siblings), (2) the name filter dropped the genesis rebirth tick, 32 vs 33 (now spans the full chain via all_names). --chain now agrees with verify/stats (33==33==33). Coherence-function win at the object level. NEXT SESSION kickoff: a guided smoke tour (Kyle following along, me flagging what to look at + explore) with a background deep-dive workflow over the build changes + docs running concurrently, feeding the S8 docs/residue-sweep discussion after.\", \"_ts\": 1782659897.298567, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:implementation/s7-store-ticks-stats-shipped\", \"observation:practice/adversarial-catch-beats-happy-path-smoke\"]}, \"ops/version-source-drift\": {\"topic\": \"ops/version-source-drift\", \"message\": \"Three-way version drift surfaced by the --version gap: root pyproject=0.4.0, apps/loops/pyproject=0.1.0, MEMORY narrative='still 0.3.1'. Installed dist (uv tool) reports strange-loops 0.4.0. Source of truth for --version should be importlib.metadata.version('strange-loops')=0.4.0; apps/loops 0.1.0 is an inner workspace member, never installed standalone. Decide canonical version display before adding --version.\", \"_ts\": 1782661267.33094, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:cli-no-version-flag\"]}, \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-overclaim\": {\"topic\": \"practice/adversarial-review-catches-overclaim\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"11-agent adversarial review (4 skeptical lenses + per-finding verify) over the 6-question review-fixes diff returned 7 confirmed / 0 uncertain \\u2014 and crucially ZERO behavioral defects in the fixes; the scary Q2 case I flagged (polymorphic-front-door false-positive) did NOT materialize (comms/identity genuinely drop the transforms). It DID catch one real over-claim I introduced: _spec_has_dropped_transforms ORed count_by independently of do_count, so 'read <custom-lens> --by FIELD' without --count falsely fired the inert-note \\u2014 --by is a no-op on EVERY path, the exact over-claim class the docstring's queried_key/kind exclusion was meant to prevent. Another instance of adversarial-review-catches-what-confidence-misses: my own note's field-set looked clean to me, the skeptic found the term. Fixed (one-term deletion + docstring) and pinned by test_spec_has_dropped_transforms_field_set.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7JV9XGN2KHFCEMRSR4HGMZ\", \"_ts\": 1782668618.645691, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\"]}, \"session/2026-06-28-review-fixes-and-050-release\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-28-review-fixes-and-050-release\", \"feature\": \"surface-build1\", \"message\": \"Session arc (2026-06-28): surface-build1 manual review -> ruled all 6 open questions with Kyle -> implemented Q1 (store-verb existence/exit-code parity), Q2 (read-grammar inert-note on custom-lens), Q4 (emit explicit message= precedence), Q5 (--version), Q3 (CHANGELOG); Q6 declined. 11-agent adversarial review (4 lenses + per-finding verify) found ZERO behavioral defects in the fixes \\u2014 the scary Q2 polymorphic-front-door false-positive did NOT materialize \\u2014 but caught F3 (my own count_by over-claim in the note) + the load-bearing gap that all 5 shipped WITHOUT tests (mutation proof: the CHANGELOG parity claim was unprotected). Closed it: 15 regression tests + F2 (verify --json error-shape parity) + F7 (--version discoverability). Then merged -> main (--no-ff 186eaf9), CHANGELOG completeness sweep (verify 3-axis rework + multi-line render fix from a68549b + --diff->--facts precision), bumped 0.5.0, tagged + GitHub release -> PyPI VERIFIED. CALIBRATION (positive): workflow used exactly where it paid (adversarial review caught my own over-claim solo-confidence missed) + stayed solo for surgical impl \\u2014 clean workflow/solo discrimination. COHERENCE-FUNCTION at object level: caught the --diff CHANGELOG imprecision (said dissolved-into-fields/key; real lifecycle replacement is --facts) right before the release that would have shipped the misdirection. Release cadence ruled: per-coherent-arc (drains 31-commit backlog smell), JCS gets its own isolated signed cut. NEXT (fresh slate): post-build-1 arc choice \\u2014 FF salience-lens migration (retires the interim note) | JCS critical path | disclosure-grammar catalog.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7RX858ZAAKDB2JT3FT4M75,01KW7JV9XGN2KHFCEMRSR4HGMZ\", \"_ts\": 1782672433.611395, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/store-verb-existence-exit-code-parity\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"design/orient-salience-is-distinct-from-read-salience\": {\"topic\": \"design/orient-salience-is-distinct-from-read-salience\", \"message\": \"Salience-FF map surfaced the crux answer in EVIDENCE: orient ranking != read ranking, and Surface only materializes the read one. All 3 session-open lenses (session_start, session_landing, identity_prompt) are ORIENT surfaces; the in-repo fold lens is the READ drill-in and windows PURELY by salience (n+inbound). The orient lenses structurally CANNOT rank on salience alone \\u2014 each OVERLAYS a time signal salience does not carry: identity_prompt _recency_boost (+2<3d/+1<14d/0/-1>90d) and session_landing focus-marks (added/updated/cited/stale = what-changed/what-needs-me). Neither has a Surface analogue. So Surface.salience = n+inbound = IMPORTANCE, timeless = a READ salience; ORIENT needs importance + recency + change-state. Implication for thread:human-umwelt-static-view: the human static view is NOT read-styled-with-salience; orient is a richer ranking the Surface should materialize as first-class (recency + change-marks), instead of each orient lens bolting it on by hand divergently. The salience FF is the structural prerequisite that exposes this gap.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N,01KW7RX858ZAAKDB2JT3FT4M75,01KW528X0R7YA7T2555YAGWHSF\", \"_ts\": 1782676074.022656, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-architecture-pared-to-keystone\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\", \"thread:interactive-read-path-redesign\"]}, \"implementation/orient-lenses-colon-blind-salience\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/orient-lenses-colon-blind-salience\", \"message\": \"The salience FF is a CORRECTNESS fix, not cosmetics. All 3 orient lenses recompute their own inbound-ref count with a colon-BLIND matcher, missing the canonical kind:key ref form (the dominant emit form). session_start + session_landing: bare+slash (miss colon). identity_prompt: slash-ONLY (misses bare AND colon) \\u2014 narrowest of the three; the live identity store has 57 colon-form refs vs 10 slash/bare, so the lens currently DROPS the majority of refs when ranking what surfaces in the system prompt. Materialized Surface.salience (surface.py _inbound_count) matches all THREE forms (bare/slash/colon). Migrating each lens to read Row.salience makes them rank on the full graph. Also resolves the map verifys open question on identity_prompt live-status: it IS live, via ~/.config/loops/bin/launch (sl read identity --observer $agent --plain -> claude --system-prompt), with --plain as encoder and the vertex lens{} block resolving identity_prompt as fold_view. session_start/session_landing are LATENT (live project orient is session-orient.sh shell banner, --plain default, no --lens).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW66J3CA9E7FWSQFP7NHZK15,01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N\", \"_ts\": 1782676079.482914, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/surface-base-order-is-fold-order\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/salience-ff-doesnt-deliver-dispatch-gate-flip\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-ff-doesnt-deliver-dispatch-gate-flip\", \"message\": \"Coherence finding (S4 scoping, 2026-06-28). The build-1 dispatch note at cli/dispatch.py:280-295 (B3: read-grammar transforms inert on custom-lens vertices) says it 'is removed when the FF routes custom lenses through the Surface.' But the salience FF as scoped (migrate ONLY the salience-COMPUTING tiers to read Row.salience) does NOT route custom lenses through the dispatch Surface. The orient lenses declare their own fetch (session_landing->LandingData; identity_prompt->FoldState via vertex lens{}) and call project() INTERNALLY \\u2014 they never consume a dispatch-level Surface, and _surface_gate still fails for them (requires built-in lens + FoldState). So after S1-S3, read-grammar transforms (--match/--limit/--last/--fields/--full/--count/comma-OR/field=) are STILL discarded on custom-lens vertices and the B3 stderr note is STILL accurate \\u2014 do NOT remove it. The sequence decision's 'gate-flip' conflated salience-locality (done) with dispatch-routing-of-custom-lenses (separate, blocked by the lens-declared-fetch custom-data-shape design). Real owner: thread:gate-fail-ignores-surface-transforms. SAY/DO gap: a forward-looking comment predicted the FF would close B3; the FF's actual scope never touches dispatch.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW6CAE6WDNKAMBMG0SN6EA4B,01KW7Y87KB9MMMAJ73R3FHPJ1N,01KW7XMJ0CTKE72ZYBVJ036ZCP\", \"_ts\": 1782694587.349192, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-ff-scope-per-slice-salience-consumer-only\", \"decision:design/salience-ff-sequence-all-three\", \"thread:gate-fail-ignores-surface-transforms\"]}, \"design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\": {\"topic\": \"design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\", \"message\": \"Ground-truth from Kyle (2026-06-28) \\u2014 INVERTS the human-umwelt-static-view seed thesis. Kyle has NOT been using the orient surfaces (orient-banner / session_landing / reconcile) at all: 'the data is largely overwhelming at this point.' The thesis assumed humans ENTER via these three; the human ABANDONED them due to VOLUME. Sharper read: the orient-not-read thesis is CONFIRMED (Kyle's verb IS orient \\u2014 what-needs-me), but the current surfaces betray it \\u2014 they READ-DUMP the fold under an orient banner, so they read when they claim to orient. Binding constraint = OVERWHELM / curation, NOT fragmentation; unifying three overwhelming surfaces into one overwhelming surface does not help. And 'zero data' (the build-1 deferral reason) was wrong \\u2014 we have NEGATIVE data (non-use), which is stronger evidence than absence. Design target: a TRUE orient experience = radical curation to what-needs-Kyle-now, designed ground-up FOR Kyle from the facts we have + our past interactions.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW7SVVM6C51F99E5BNBB6K5N\", \"_ts\": 1782695635.877088, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\": {\"topic\": \"design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\", \"message\": \"The same read renders a materially different reality depending on output context. Human-on-TTY sees width-clipped truncated styled output; agent-on-pipe sees the full plain render. No single invocation collapses them into a shared view -- piping to cat only drags the human into the agent plain umwelt, and the agent can never enter the TTY umwelt. Kyle's framing: the umwelt has no common reality to share a view of. Corollary: the coherence function operates only in the umwelt the agent can perceive, so say/do gaps in the TTY render are structurally invisible to the agent -- same shape as happy-path-cwd masking defects, one layer out.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KW8GPCCSVT4JX8BXHGZFZN34\", \"_ts\": 1782697374.243547, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:read-tty-truncation-not-defeatable\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\": {\"topic\": \"design/curation-belongs-in-surface-not-renderers\", \"message\": \"Audit verdict (w6d4zptvv, 37 agents): Surface IS the renderer-invariant fixed point -- an invariance probe proved context (is_tty/zoom/width/mode/format) does NOT leak into Surface construction; --json was byte-identical (md5 0601dcfd) across pipe, COLUMNS 80 and 400, and -q/-v/-vv. So the umwelt-fork is NOT a no-common-reality problem; it is that the renderers RE-CURATE the shared Surface behind its back. The fold lens applies salience reorder plus namespace windowing as its BASE projection while to_dict emits surface.rows verbatim -- two different curations of one Surface, neither announcing which it holds. Reframe / dissolution: promote curation OUT of the renderers and INTO Surface as a declared, serialized budget (Window provenance), computed once and emitted in --json. Then every renderer collapses to render(Surface, context) with zero independent loss, the umwelt-difference between any two views becomes a computable Window-diff, and the aggressive curation a human-orient redesign needs is done ONCE with provenance and is one in-band keystroke from reversal. The constraint is not add-instrumentation; it is stop-the-renderers-from-curating, let-Surface-own-it. Grow-the-substrate over fork-the-consumer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8GPCNT15PED7640EYQ51NH,01KW8GPCH39HXY7YSY461R3E8G\", \"_ts\": 1782699577.516586, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/umwelt-fork-no-shared-reality\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"rendering/hiding-is-render-budget-not-in-surface\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/hiding-is-render-budget-not-in-surface\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"Grounded the SECOND umwelt fork (after truncation): row-windowing/\\\"hiding\\\". Live numbers on project store \\u2014 human text read of all-kinds shows 26 of 506 decisions with a \\\"(108 more)\\\" footer; the --json agent read returns all 506 (1078 total rows), unwindowed. Crux: Surface.window records total=1078, shown=1078, limited_by=None \\u2014 i.e. the Surface believes NOTHING was limited, while the text lens applies a per-kind salience window the Surface has no record of. So window honestly describes the FETCH budget; the salience window is a RENDER budget layered on top, invisible to Surface \\u2014 the two channels diverge silently from Surface provenance (limited_by=None is true for json, false-in-spirit for text). NOTE the asymmetry vs truncation: the text window is at least HONEST locally (\\\"(N more)\\\" marker, not a silent clip), but the provenance is not. Also note: a SCOPED read (--kind thread) shows ALL 222 rows unwindowed \\u2014 windowing only bites the unscoped all-kinds read. Two doors for the reframe: (A) make read fully faithful both channels + a separate orient/curated door owns \\\"what needs me\\\"; (B) relocate the render budget INTO Surface.window (shown=N/kind, limited_by=salience) so both channels read the same recorded curation. (A)=policy, (B)=mechanism; not exclusive. Parked branch feat/curation-in-surface targets (B).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9XDQWV1VGB81TQAPGHH7JP,01KW8PVK57F576A9Z9QBHCJ30Q\", \"_ts\": 1782744406.781869, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\", \"thread:umwelt-divergence-audit\"]}, \"pattern/dispatch-help-completion-three-reflections\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/dispatch-help-completion-three-reflections\", \"feature\": \"terminal-autocomplete\", \"message\": \"One argparse parser, three reflections: PARSE (run the command), HELP (render arg defs), COMPLETE (emit candidates). A framework that already reflects its parsers for parse + help should own completion as the third walk \\u2014 building it in the CONSUMER duplicates the command-roster knowledge the framework already holds (the un-dissolved form). painted is the live instance: run_app/AppCommand owns dispatch, help.py walks a throwaway argparse to harvest Defs; completion is that same walk in a third output mode. Generalizes: when a framework reflects a structure for N purposes, the N+1th reflection of the SAME structure belongs at the same layer, not a layer up. Instance of \\\"anything painted can do, prefer painted\\\" (decision/design/full-painted-integration-residue). Connects to read-path-features-over-noticing-skills at the tooling layer: completion is a read-path feature of the parser, not a separately-maintained artifact.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA2BAD7SZ04XMM0S71ZFB9J\", \"_ts\": 1782749440.861398, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\"]}, \"architecture/cross-store-ref-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cross-store-ref-resolution\", \"feature\": \"terminal-autocomplete\", \"message\": \"VERIFIED model (2026-06-29, traced + reproduced) \\u2014 corrects my earlier overstatement that \\\"cross-store refs do not resolve.\\\" They do; the navigable address ALWAYS survives. Three layers: (1) EMIT-TIME PIN \\u2014 _resolve_one walks the root-cwd topology (combine/discover chain) and pins the target current ULID into a {field}_ref sibling; resolves ONLY if the target store is in the emit cwd topology. Out-of-topology emit prints WARN \\\"ref did not resolve \\u2014 dropped\\\", but that drops only the PIN, not the ref. (2) NAVIGABLE ADDRESS \\u2014 the kind:key value is preserved verbatim in item.refs regardless of pin success (confirmed: painted seed fact retains [decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted, ...] in refs after a \\\"dropped\\\" WARN). (3) READ-SIDE GRAPH \\u2014 _compute_inbound_edges is ADDRESS-keyed (kind/key, colon/slash normalized) and store-local to the READ. CONSEQUENCE: a cross-repo ref resolves in the GRAPH when read through a topology that combines both ends \\u2014 reproduced: loops target inbound=1 via the cli-completion aggregation (combines loops+painted), inbound=0 read loops-alone (harmless dangling). So cross-store ref resolution is a TOPOLOGY-MEMBERSHIP property (a combine-block config choice), not a hard limit \\u2014 this is the basis for the on-demand arc-aggregation pattern. CAVEAT: the emit-time pin is a ULID snapshot, fragile across independent store rebirth; the address is durable and the graph runs on it, so a dangling pin is cosmetic-provenance, not a lost edge.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWA2BAD7SZ04XMM0S71ZFB9J\", \"_ts\": 1782751118.50707, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/completion-dissolves-into-painted\"]}, \"test/umwelt-channel-parity-verified\": {\"topic\": \"test/umwelt-channel-parity-verified\", \"feature\": \"umwelt-divergence-audit\", \"message\": \"VERIFIED (5-agent adversarial workflow, 4 read-mode probes vs the live project store, merge-gate for fix/umwelt-render-divergences): TTY and pipe deliver IDENTICAL DATA \\u2014 Kyle the-same-data-just-prettier claim HOLDS, zero TTY-vs-pipe data divergence. Coverage: SUMMARY all-kinds + scoped + prefix-scan (1135 rows diff=0), detail zooms -v/-vv (secondary lines byte-identical, no TTY clip even at PTYCOLS=40), --match (byte-identical incl header), --facts, --refs (ref-graph annotations identical). Three would-be divergences adversarially refuted as artifacts: two relative-age fields (Nm) that FLIP with capture order (wall-clock not channel), and an Unfolded: footer absence that was live-aggregator tick-boundary drift (proven against a frozen store copy + source: fold.py appends it with no isatty/width gate). Presentation deltas (all confirmed data-free): header style (## KIND vs Kinds:), pipe section-separator blanks, CRLF/width-padding, ANSI color, json envelope shape, n\\\\\\\\n-flattening in text. ONE REAL divergence found but OUT OF SCOPE: json carries 11 legacy-field decision bodies text drops (friction:text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions) \\u2014 identical on both text channels, pre-existing, orthogonal to this branch. Merge cleared.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW9YW3MCG59C0B080FX7J90R,01KWA7SH8RAEQM4902CR3HJERB\", \"_ts\": 1782755149.53358, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels\", \"friction:text-headline-empty-for-legacy-non-message-decisions\"]}, \"design/plugin-hook-vertex-resolution\": {\"topic\": \"design/plugin-hook-vertex-resolution\", \"message\": \"CORRECTED (2026-06-29, deeper grounding of commands/resolve.py:689): emit does NOT use raw home-based resolve_vertex \\u2014 it uses _resolve_vertex_for_dispatch whose chain tries cwd-LOCAL FIRST: (1) ./.loops/<name>.vertex, (2) ./<name>.vertex, (3) LOOPS_HOME/<name>/<name>.vertex aggregation, (4) combine-alias. So bare 'sl emit project ...' from the repo root resolves to the LOCAL writable .loops/project.vertex instance \\u2014 the runbook convention is CORRECT and turn-capture.py's nudge text needs no change. My earlier claim (bare-name->aggregation) read only the generic resolver, which is step 3 of dispatch. NET for plugin: agent-facing text keeps bare 'sl emit project ...'; the HOOK uses explicit ${CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR}/.loops/project.vertex \\u2014 NOT because bare-name is broken but because a hook must not RELY on cwd==project-root (emit dispatch IS cwd-aware; the hook's cwd is not contract-guaranteed, CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR is). Plus: all hook entry points must guard on [ -f $V ] so a user-scope plugin no-ops cleanly in non-loops repos.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWABW0W3PGZWMADT0XNGSF93\", \"_ts\": 1782764284.166645, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\"]}, \"design/plugin-lens-layer-separate-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"design/plugin-lens-layer-separate-boundary\", \"message\": \"Grounding finding (2026-06-29): session lenses (session_start/session_landing/identity_prompt/reconcile) are NOT in the CLI \\u2014 resolved at runtime by lens_resolver.py (vertex-local -> project-local -> ~/.config/loops/lenses/ -> built-in). This is loops' OWN plugin layer. CLEAN BOUNDARY: the Claude Code plugin packages hooks/skill/commands ONLY; lenses stay loops-resolvable, OUT of the CC plugin. Personal-audience consequence: ~/.config/loops/lenses/ already populated on my machines, so session-orient.sh's '--lens reconcile' pointer resolves WITHOUT the plugin shipping lenses \\u2014 the soft-coupling that would bite a fresh public install is a non-issue for personal portability. (Public later -> ship lenses or degrade the pointer gracefully.)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWABW0W3PGZWMADT0XNGSF93\", \"_ts\": 1782760202.28481, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/loops-plugin-scope-in-session\"]}, \"design/human-umwelt-anchor-is-resumption\": {\"topic\": \"design/human-umwelt-anchor-is-resumption\", \"message\": \"Kyle's real session-open question (asked directly 2026-06-29): 'Where did I leave off?' \\u2014 CONTINUITY/resume-the-rope, NOT the thread's assumed 'what-needs-me-now' action-queue. Refines the radical-curation constraint: the orient is a RESUMPTION surface (last session's live arc, foregrounded) not an action panel and not a health/alarm panel. Implication: surface the few threads/tasks that MOVED in the last session window; collapse the standing backlog (33 threads / 20 frictions) to a single drillable count-line. The read-dump overwhelm came from rendering the whole open-set under an orient banner; the fix is to render the live arc and suppress the standing backlog by default.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8F1B5N3V36EXMS70EKCAHS,01KW8F1AX5NMT3VVQ99E0TS8KK\", \"_ts\": 1782776427.328588, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:design/human-umwelt-overwhelm-not-fragmentation\", \"thread:human-umwelt-static-view\"]}, \"rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"painted gotcha caught by adversarial review: table(overflow=Overflow.FIT) only SHRINKS Fill columns. A table built entirely from fixed-int or AUTO columns IGNORES the width budget \\u2014 it renders at natural width and overflows narrow terminals, while a card capped to width disagrees. The fix that honours width: declare the one variable column as Fill() with min_width + max_width=natural \\u2014 fills to natural on a roomy terminal, shrinks+ellipsizes when the budget is tight (FIT can act). Below the irreducible floor (fixed numeric cols + gaps), drop a decorative column (we drop TREND under width 64). Also: table() reverse-videos row 0 by default (TUI cursor) \\u2014 pass selected_style=Style() for a static listing; and use Wrap.ELLIPSIS not the default hard-clip on card sublines so narrow widths signal loss with a marker. Reusable for any painted table consumer.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWCX2FTAQ857BR1DCY41057V\", \"_ts\": 1782844580.894851, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"session/2026-06-30-ls-stat-rich-render\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-30-ls-stat-rich-render\", \"message\": \"Built the sl ls redesign end-to-end on feat/ls-stat-containment (596ffd6, pushed GitLab+GitHub). TWO Kyle requests: (1) --kind <K> stop dumping the fact list \\u2014 reshaped as a DESCENT to the kind's entries (namespace rollup / --key drill / collect->observer / orphan bucket), reversing decision-B; (2) leverage painted for a beautiful human TTY render \\u2014 Kyle chose the maximal 'boxed panel + trend sparklines'. Delivered: rounded stat card + clean table() + share meter + per-kind 30d sparkline + freshness gradient + dimmed minor-tail, strictly piped-keyed (TTY rich human / pipe terse faithful agent \\u2014 concrete EVIDENCE for thread:budget-meaning-human-vs-agent's inversion). SHAPE: scout inline -> understanding workflow (painted surface + register constraints + stat-menu) -> AskUserQuestion with ASCII-preview mockups for the 2 real forks (visual treatment + minor-tail handling) -> build slice-by-slice with live render checks -> 4-dim adversarial review workflow. CALIBRATION: the review EARNED ITS KEEP \\u2014 caught 5 real + 2 parity defects the green 1500-test suite masked (painted table(Overflow.FIT) is a no-op without a Fill column -> ignores width; card hard-clip mid-token; --json datetime-vs-float-epoch divergence; --key-on-collect-fold false 'under X' stamp; piped registers dropped signed/share/span). All fixed + regression-tested (1522 loops + 827 engine). The AskUserQuestion preview mockups were the right tool for the aesthetic fork \\u2014 Kyle picked precisely from concrete ASCII, zero back-and-forth. Painted lesson captured: observation:rendering/painted-table-fit-needs-fill. NEXT ENTRY POINT: Kyle has minor UI-refinement requests to pick up post-wrap \\u2014 the shared _statview.py makes tweaks one-file.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWCX2345XY7228358C0C9D0N,01KWCX2FTAQ857BR1DCY41057V\", \"_ts\": 1782846510.78328, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/ls-kind-descends-to-entries\", \"decision:rendering/ls-rich-tty-register\"]}, \"rendering/piped-faithfulness-forces-width-none\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/piped-faithfulness-forces-width-none\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"The presentation-register split must FORCE width=None on the piped branch INSIDE the lens, not trust ctx.width \\u2014 a pipe can inherit COLUMNS (default 80), so relying on ctx.width silently truncates the agent channel (clipped 'sl ls' \\u2283 preview; 'sl ls <v> --kind' clipped '115d ago'\\u2192'115d ag'). Adversarial review (4-dim workflow) caught this MAJOR faithfulness break; the green suite + repo-root smoke both masked it because both ran with a real width. Two painted gotchas surfaced: Line.to_block(width) requires an int (does 'if width<=0' \\u2192 crashes on None) so width-free styled rendering needs natural-width or plain Block.text (helper _spans_block); and forcing width=None must be paired with None-guards on every elide()/pad call.\", \"_ts\": 1782851941.23532, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design/presentation-register-keys-on-channel\"]}, \"session/2026-06-30-ls-line-row\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-06-30-ls-line-row\", \"feature\": \"ls-stat-containment\", \"message\": \"Session shape: turned Kyle's two alignment nits (sl ls <vertex> minor-tail; sl ls front-door readability) into a front-door redesign. Bare sl ls \\u2192 one-line-per-vertex line-row (\\u25c6/\\u25c7/\\u25c8 type icon + \\u2283 top-kinds preview + shadow-on-line-2-with-path + -v per-kind census justified across vertices); kinds-table minor tail aligned (single table() + SHARE align=END). Calibration: the 4-dim adversarial Workflow earned its keep AGAIN \\u2014 caught a MAJOR piped-faithfulness break + a width=None crash + cross-group --all drift that 1528 green tests AND repo-root smoke all masked (every check ran with a width). Merged 97a9055, pushed both remotes; docs/dev banners local (gitignored). NEXT ENTRY: release is a pending 0.6.0 minor DEFERRED until more commands reshaped (thread:next-release-0.6.0); open polish (Kyle's call): icon prominence (dim/shape-only), deferred open-count trailer.\", \"_ts\": 1782855024.172968, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"register-split-piped-faithfulness-untested\", \"rendering/ls-root-line-row\"]}, \"architecture/typed-edge-emit-fold-split\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/typed-edge-emit-fold-split\", \"message\": \"Live emit/fold inconsistency in loops (verified 2026-07-01, 4-agent source read): the emit -v receipt already reports superseded_by=decision:foo as 'one new inbound edge on its target entity' (resolve.py:443, emit.py:627), but the fold/read path only lifts the literal ref field into _refs (atoms/engine.py:103 collect, 140-150 upsert -- the ONLY two writers of _refs repo-wide). So that inbound edge never appears in the target's arrow-N salience or --refs walk. Write-time and read-time disagree today. 6 superseded_by_ref + 2 resolved_by_ref pins live in project.db are graph-invisible; 1 accidental topic_ref pin (on a cite fact) is the footgun in the wild -- 1 accidental / 2770 facts, bounded by the self-key-skip and whitespace guards.\", \"_ts\": 1782922524.04923, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/vertex-is-the-place\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/vertex-is-the-place\", \"message\": \"Step-back vocabulary trace: 'vertex' has named three things \\u2014 the runtime pattern, the .vertex document, and the place (store + interpretation). Only pattern and place were ever in the model; the document was a residence artifact that fused strata the paradigm had already ranked apart (sources='infrastructure not atoms', lenses='configuration not architecture', Spec=atom, Observer=first-class). SPEC \\u00a79 store-residence strengthens rather than dilutes vertex identity: declaration events are the second truth applied one tier up (observing the focusing is observable); current-ontology-as-Latest is VERTEX.md's boundary-less memory fold; rewind = the observer observing their own past focusing. The split that's needed is in the DOCUMENT grammar (stratum sections in KDL as ingress/render form), never in the vertex concept. KDL's discipline job moved to the frozen meta-schema vocabulary; KDL keeps authoring+render.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWG18WWGWJN95ZF786A20MW1,01KWHQ094B1WF7Z416HXY3KKN5\", \"_ts\": 1783006793.272952, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:declaration-strata-portability\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"session/2026-07-02-060-design\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-02-060-design\", \"message\": \"0.6.0 design session: picked up roadmap-substrate-after-060, ran the queued implementation discussion. Corpus (Static TTY study: 3 directions, author leaned 2c rail) + code map (4 drifted grammars, fold=only Surface consumer, no cross-command golden = drift cause) extracted via parallel agents; study's 'undesigned piped form' turned out already answered by presentation-register-keys-on-channel. Six decisions ratified in sequence, each dissolving the next question: hybrid-by-register \\u2192 tree-cut spine \\u2192 key-level salience w/ max propagation \\u2192 vertex-scoped tiers \\u2192 rail wins gutter \\u2192 view sequence w/ Strata as designated cut. Session break with review doc handed off.\", \"_ts\": 1783031008.808611, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/store-type-portfolio\": {\"topic\": \"design/store-type-portfolio\", \"message\": \"Store-shape portfolio as the domain-neutrality test suite (Kyle 2026-07-02): agent-attestation (exists, ref-heavy ideation), SillyTavern RP (consolidation-ticks-as-memory, no lifecycle, personas-as-observers), novel-writing (TWO time axes: wall vs fictional/canon; continuity=coverage), household management (multi-human + recurring timed/count boundaries \\u2014 chores are loops), hlab (exists, boundary-rich ops), subtask-as-orchestrator (machine volume, worker fleet observers, ticks=completions), autoresearch (metric series, keep/discard folds, different lifecycle vocab), personal salience feed (ingested via Source/Parse, high-volume/disposable, recency-dominant, browser-history-as-attention \\u2014 decay is the product), corp salience feed (+grants/federation), household tracking + jeeves (sensor ingestion + agent ACTUATION outward), cumulative deep research (digest-coverage's natural home). Sharpest stress tests: the feed (inverts every design-store default; behavioral attention \\u2248 inbound-refs \\u2014 attention-events on an address is what ref already is, new SOURCE for existing concept) and the novel (fictional time = ordering axis in payload the grammar can't sort by). Validation: each 0.6.0 view has a natural home store none of which is the design vertex \\u2014 Confluence\\u2192household/corp, Graph\\u2192attestation/research, Provenance\\u2192attestation/corp, Horizon\\u2192hlab/household, Strata\\u2192subtask/research.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KWJNTNT7FW1Q8WWBC4QKWKR2\", \"_ts\": 1783039643.405664, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"thread:sillytavern-showcase-app\"]}, \"design/salience-as-attention-trace\": {\"topic\": \"design/salience-as-attention-trace\", \"message\": \"The salience feed (Kyle 2026-07-02) reframes salience as a TRACE, not a scalar: three signal strata \\u2014 ambient scrape (feeds/discords), deliberate capture (likes/'good article', incl. out-of-subscription ingestion), actual attention (browser history on top) \\u2014 recording what had attention WHEN. Never about deletion. Consequences: salience-now = fold over attention events; salience-at-T = same fold over a window \\u2014 the append-only store + ref-as-attention-event (UNION, accumulating) already IS the trace; the feed needs the 0.7.0 temporal cursor to query it, which is the strongest motivation yet for rewind (stronger than audit framing). Dissolution-as-coverage-not-deletion (already ratified) satisfies 'never get rid of things' as-is. Retrospection use case: reconstruct a trajectory months later ('the Shannon-Weaver rabbit hole', 'all the 3D-printing hop-skipping') across topic hops.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWJQ3KRD6CF2HEKD01MXYQQJ,01KWJQYG20A72PJ2RXZBEJAZT8\", \"_ts\": 1783040524.65667, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/salience-dials-vertex-declared\", \"observation:design/store-type-portfolio\"]}, \"session/2026-07-02-spine-build\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-02-spine-build\", \"message\": \"Evening build session: spine G0-G3 committed on feat/static-honest-spine (grammar module w/ unified time vocabulary; Row.tier quantile-bucketed; rail+ledger register split in fold; register retrofit + parity tests on stream/ticks/store \\u2014 parity harness caught piped truncation on first run). 1588 pass, live-verified both channels. Session closed with Kyle's screenshot review: rail confirmed cool on short bodies, friction:rail-drowns-under-full-bodies opened for long ones. NEXT SESSION: G4 design discussion (stream tier-inheritance fork a/b/c + Row level discriminator \\u2014 recorded on thread:static-honest-060-spine) + the rail/full-body layout fix.\", \"_ts\": 1783045194.509878, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/tier-disclosure-scarcity-not-layout\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tier-disclosure-scarcity-not-layout\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"G4d live-verified on the project vertex (human read = piped=False width=None, per drop-truncation-from-human-reads): tier-allocated disclosure delivers body-SCARCITY (127 high-body rows of 1231; mid/tail regions now clean one-line rail, dramatically scannable). BUT bodies are the COUNT half, not the LAYOUT half: high rows cluster at the TOP of each salience-sorted namespace group (design/ head = a stack of ~30 high-tier full untruncated bodies), so their wrapped lines still interrupt the rail's continuous gutter THERE. Not a contradiction \\u2014 the decision scopes itself to scarcity ('bodies become scarce, rail spacing survives by construction') and delivers it; the wrapped-body-vs-continuous-gutter question for the SURVIVING high bodies is orthogonal and remains the friction's original candidate-(a/b/c) layout work (hanging indent / continuation rail / body-as-subline). Residual for G5/G6 or a layout slice: the rail survives the bulk of the read, still drowns in the high-density head.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWK0BM2PAG7PXCCXD59K47VV,01KWJWCP494MRJ72C4JZZPNMQP\", \"_ts\": 1783050804.972248, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tier-allocated-disclosure\", \"friction:rail-drowns-under-full-bodies\"]}, \"rendering/rail-needs-uninterrupted-run\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/rail-needs-uninterrupted-run\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle smoke of G6: kind-descent is the first view where the rail reads as an ACTUAL rail \\u2014 an uninterrupted glyph column. In read the rail keeps getting broken up by body text (and the project store is huge), diluting the scanning effect. Same territory as the rail-drowns layout residue: the rail's value is continuity.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWN25NCYXKW0MTSVQARZX522\", \"_ts\": 1783120874.510457, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:namespace-rollup-tier-max-flattening\"]}, \"rendering/ls-root-tatty-vs-kind-descent\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/ls-root-tatty-vs-kind-descent\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Kyle smoke of G6: sl ls and sl ls <vertex> look tatty next to the clean kind-descent view. Root/vertex levels predate the G6 rail alignment visually (line-row + kinds census). Candidate follow-up: bring root and vertex levels up to the kind-descent finish.\", \"_ts\": 1783120874.785561, \"_n\": 1}, \"paradigm/capture-cheap-assert-later-read-retroactive\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/capture-cheap-assert-later-read-retroactive\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-060\", \"message\": \"Three independent designs converged on one pattern: typed edges (address-field -> declared edge), observer typing (bare string -> declared Peer), delegation (slash-path -> vouched relation). General form: capture is cheap/declaration-free at emit time; structure is asserted later and lights up retroactively at read time (schema-on-read); the store never blocks on ontology; each read surface advertises its own promotion candidates (reconcile -> edge declarations, Confluence -> peer declarations / unendorsed compounds). This is a paradigm property, not three coincidences.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWFPBY99R304Z7MQE3A91SFD,01KWNQWF910CZR7JHS6HFEVAFN,01KWNT7474AGX2BPFRCX4Q1XKE\", \"_ts\": 1783143567.865786, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/observer-compound-delegation-path\", \"decision:design/observer-typing-dissolves-to-declared-peer\", \"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\"]}, \"workflow/adversarial-review-060-tail\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/adversarial-review-060-tail\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-spine\", \"message\": \"4-dim adversarial workflow (14 agents) over the 0.6.0 tail pre-push: 9 confirmed findings the green suite (1756) masked, 1 refuted. Major: --why TTY hard-clips long field values (violates the wrap-not-clip contract this branch itself ratified in tier-allocated-disclosure). Real algorithmic: _longest_chains memo poisoning on cycles (order-dependent 'longest', reproduced counterexample; live store IS cyclic), depth-cap-128 silent truncation, piped graph register leaking zoom caps (top-10 hubs/top-3 chains on the agent channel, contra its own docstring), orphans as one 18KB joined line (+ middot delimiter ambiguity), edges-vs-inbound definitional gap (1471 vs 1547, 76 unsourced refs undisclosed), stale 'cap 32' docstrings. Pattern holds: every wave, the register-faithfulness and honesty dims catch what goldens can't \\u2014 goldens pin a width and a fixture; faithfulness breaks live. Fixes dispatched pre-push.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQB5F149M9N4XJ75NA3BC6R\", \"_ts\": 1783195477.762672, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"rendering/flags-words-edges-arrows\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/flags-words-edges-arrows\", \"message\": \"Register idiom generalized from the P4 review: symbols split into FLAGS (a judgment/status the pipe consumer can't reconstruct \\u2014 degrade to words: tier \\u25c6\\u2192high, horizon \\u25b2\\u2192approaching) vs EDGE NOTATION (\\u2190/\\u2192 ARE the notation, no better word exists, pipe already speaks \\u2192 in every chain path \\u2014 arrows survive both registers). What looked inconsistency-shaped (arrows survived the pipe after \\u25b2 didn't) is a rule the next lens can follow. Documented in _grammar module docstring.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQMD4P9YK4KKP5HD89M2DNB\", \"_ts\": 1783204582.406815, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/rollup-shed-only-what-degrades\"]}, \"workflow/external-codex-review\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/external-codex-review\", \"feature\": \"static-honest-spine\", \"message\": \"First external-model review of the branch (codex exec, gpt-5.5 xhigh) over the full static-honest-spine diff: 5 real findings, 2 in the piped-faithfulness class our own adversarial waves had already named as the branch's recurring defect class \\u2014 external reviewer independently converged on the same class, plus a provenance case-canonicalization bug (--why on a case-variant key attributed zero fields) no internal wave caught. All 5 fixed + regression-tested in e8643a6. codex exec review --base cannot take custom instructions; plain codex exec with a diff-it-yourself brief works.\", \"_ts\": 1783275558.948772, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/record-line-flattens-embedded-newlines\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/record-line-flattens-embedded-newlines\", \"feature\": \"painted-070-bump\", \"message\": \"painted 0.7.0 record_line now flattens an embedded newline inside a payload VALUE onto one logical record line (output='running tests...\\\\nall 42 tests passed' \\u2192 'running tests... all 42 tests passed') instead of letting the \\\\n break the ledger row and orphan the tail with no gutter/timestamp. Surfaced as 6 tasks-app golden drifts (TestTaskLog/TestSessionLog \\u00d7 text/detailed/full), all one cause; regolded \\u2014 the new form is more correct. Loops app: ZERO golden drift. Likely a side-effect of the 0.7.0 refs work hardening record_line (denotation demo is the first record_line demo).\", \"_ts\": 1783348670.228892, \"_n\": 1}, \"rendering/lens-signature-tiers\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 signature-sufficiency evidence. Enumerated all 25+ loops lens entrypoints beyond semantic_article. They fall in THREE tiers against semantic_article's (data, zoom, width, *, visible, chars, lines) vote. TIER A pure (data, zoom, width) -> Block, no extra kwargs: compile_view, run_facts_view, run_ticks_view, test_view, validate_view, sync_view, pop_view. TIER B needs a piped bool (TTY register split) sometimes plus palette/vertex_name: confluence_view, horizon_view, graph_view, store_view (+palette), declarations_view/_render_stat_view/kind_stat_view, vertices_view, stream_view (+vertex_name), ticks_view, tick_chain_view, stats_view. TIER C needs the Fidelity budget axes visible/chars/lines: semantic_article.fold_view (the vote, explicit), plus **kwargs absorbers deliberation.fold_view, reconcile.fold_view, session_landing.fold_view. VERDICT: the semantic_article vote (decomposed visible/chars/lines) holds \\u2014 those three collapse exactly into a painted Fidelity's fields, so (data, fidelity, width) subsumes every Tier A and Tier C signature. It does NOT subsume the two EXTRA kinds of thing Tier B threads: a TTY fact (piped) and domain identity (vertex_name/vertex_path/palette). Those are the real signature question, detailed in sibling observations.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S\", \"_ts\": 1783737998.323101, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"The built-in apps/loops/src/loops/lenses/fold.py fold_view is the UNION signature \\u2014 the everything-lens that proves what a general loops renderer actually consumes: (data, zoom, width, *, vertex_name, vertex_path, visible, lines, chars, piped). Decompose those kwargs into three categories and the M3 signature answer falls out cleanly: (1) visible/chars/lines = painted Fidelity axes (fold_view even rebuilds a Fidelity from zoom+these inside semantic_article) \\u2014 these BELONG in the fidelity arg; (2) vertex_name/vertex_path = domain identity, an app-specific valued facet, render-irrelevant \\u2014 belongs OUTSIDE painted, bound by the app via closure or an app-context, matching the roadmap's 'keep app-specific facets outside painted' constraint; (3) piped = a fabricated TTY fact that duplicates width's None-sentinel (see rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact). So (data, fidelity, width) is sufficient for the RENDER contract once piped dissolves and domain identity is bound app-side rather than passed as a render param.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H3PZKECZ04R6GD6Q58E5D\", \"_ts\": 1783738007.654326, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 exit criterion says loops semantic renderers must require no fabricated mode, TTY, or stream facts. loops VIOLATES this via one fact: piped. It is computed as (not ctx.is_tty) or (not sys.stdout.isatty()) and threaded as a keyword into ~11 lens entrypoints: declarations_view, kind_stat_view, vertices_view, store_view, tick_chain_view, stats_view, ticks_view, stream_view, confluence_view, horizon_view, graph_view, and the built-in fold_view. It is REDUNDANT: width already carries the same two-state contract (concrete int on a TTY, None when piped) \\u2014 normalize_width and its docstring in lens_resolver.py state this explicitly, and every run_cli render closure sets width via 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None' right beside 'piped=not ctx.is_tty'. So the same TTY bit is encoded TWICE at every call site, once as width=None and once as piped=True. Dissolution: lenses that branch on piped can branch on 'width is None' instead; piped as a param disappears and the fabricated-TTY-fact criterion is met with zero new painted machinery. This is deletable independently of the declaration grammar.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H3PZKECZ04R6GD6Q58E5D\", \"_ts\": 1783738016.954509, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/lens-signature-tiers\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/height-offered-only-in-tui\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/height-offered-only-in-tui\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 asks: record where height is OFFERED to a renderer vs merely KNOWN by the caller. Findings across both loops render paths. STATIC CLI path (dispatch.py + every run_cli render closure): only WIDTH is offered \\u2014 dispatch computes width from shutil.get_terminal_size().columns (or None when piped) and passes it as the third positional; height is available to the caller (get_terminal_size().lines exists, ctx carries it) but is NEVER passed to any static lens. So in the static path height is merely KNOWN, never OFFERED. TUI/Surface path (tui/store_app.py, tui/autoresearch_app.py): height IS offered \\u2014 the Surface calls layout(self, width, height) and the app stores both self._w and self._h and lays out against the viewport height. CONCLUSION for the signature question: a static (data, fidelity, width) signature that omits height matches actual static-path usage exactly (height is never wanted there); height is a live/Surface concern, which is consistent with painted keeping offered-allocation in the Surface tier rather than the static renderer signature. No static loops lens is starved by a height-free signature.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S\", \"_ts\": 1783738026.355831, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/siftd-mirror-has-drifted\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/siftd-mirror-has-drifted\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"Side-by-side of the two claimed-mirror fidelity_from_args implementations (loops cli/fidelity.py vs siftd src/siftd/cli/_common.py). They are NOT identical in logic \\u2014 the Mirrors siftd docstring is aspirational, and the shadow copies have DRIFTED. Divergences: (1) DEPTH FLAGS \\u2014 loops reads -q/--quiet (depth 0) and -v/--verbose count (1 to depth 2, 2+ to depth 3), default_depth 1; siftd reads --brief (depth 0) and --full (depth 3) booleans, default 1. Different flag vocabulary AND different arity (count vs bool). (2) VISIBLE DERIVATION \\u2014 loops is PARAMETERIZED: caller passes a visible={flag_attr: tag_name} mapping and any truthy/int>0 flag lights its tag; siftd HARDCODES its domain tags: seeds {text}, adds thinking on --thinking/--full, adds tools on --tools/--full. (3) BUDGET \\u2014 loops takes explicit --max-chars AND --max-lines (two axes); siftd takes --chars plus a --brief=>80 shortcut and has NO lines axis. (4) default_chars vs default_depth parameter surface differs. SIGNIFICANCE for M3: the drift is not sloppiness \\u2014 it is EVIDENCE that the flag-to-facet vocabulary is genuinely per-consumer (loops disclosure axes are facts/refs over threads/decisions; siftd's are text/thinking/tools over transcripts). Two independently-drifting hand-copies of the same SHAPE is precisely the signal that argues for a painted DECLARATION grammar (each consumer declares its flag->facet map, painted compiles it) over a shared parsing function \\u2014 a shared function would have to absorb both vocabularies and cannot.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4Y91G01ATG9CAATGCAMV\", \"_ts\": 1783738050.24884, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/fidelity-from-args-is-dead-shadow-copy\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"M3 ask: record every adapter loops hand-builds to reuse a painted renderer through run_cli. loops has TWO dispatch spines and both hand-build glue. SPINE 1 legacy run_cli path \\u2014 commands/ still call painted.run_cli(fetch=, render=) directly; each supplies a render(ctx, data) closure that is pure adapter boilerplate translating painted's CliContext into a loops lens call. Inventory of the render closures: ls.py:204 (declarations_view) and :518 (kind_stat_view); population.py:81 (vertices_view); store.py:654 (tick_chain_view), :723 (stats_view), :788 (store_view); ticks.py:103 and stream.py:77 (resolve-then-call composition adapters); sync.py:170 and :321 (sync_view); devtools.py x4. The recurring glue is exactly: 'w = ctx.width if ctx.is_tty else None; return LENS(data, ctx.zoom, w, piped=not ctx.is_tty)'. Every one re-derives width-from-TTY and piped-from-TTY by hand. SPINE 2 new siftd-shape path \\u2014 cli/dispatch.py:dispatch owns the same branches natively (action/interactive/live/static) and no longer routes static through run_cli; it computes width from sys.stdout.isatty() itself. DISSOLUTION: under a (data, fidelity, width) renderer contract where painted owns the fetch->render->emit loop and passes width already normalized (None=piped), every Spine-1 render closure collapses to nothing \\u2014 the ctx.zoom/ctx.width/ctx.is_tty unpacking and the piped re-derivation are the whole adapter, and all of it is painted re-exposing what painted already knows. The closures exist only because loops re-reads TTY state painted computed one frame earlier.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H495T9X8RWQPPVC9WZF16\", \"_ts\": 1783738063.412693, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/call-lens-fidelity-teardown-adapter\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/call-lens-fidelity-teardown-adapter\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"A second, subtler adapter loops hand-builds around painted's render contract: the Fidelity TEARDOWN. loops resolves a proper painted Fidelity upstream (op.fidelity, built via parse_fidelity) but its lenses do NOT accept a Fidelity \\u2014 they accept (data, zoom, width, *, visible, chars, lines, ...). So dispatch.py + lens_resolver.call_lens tear the Fidelity back apart: _zoom_of(fidelity) extracts fidelity.depth as a Zoom, then visible/chars/lines are spread as loose kwargs via extra.setdefault(...). call_lens then inspects each lens signature and forwards only the kwargs whose names match (or all, for **kwargs lenses). This is a build-up-then-tear-down round trip: painted's parse_fidelity assembles a Fidelity, loops immediately decomposes it into (zoom, visible, chars, lines) to feed lenses written before Fidelity existed. Under semantic_article's vote the fix is to have lenses take fidelity DIRECTLY as the second arg \\u2014 then _zoom_of, the visible/chars/lines setdefault dance, and call_lens's whole kwarg-forwarding inspection machinery all dissolve. This is the strongest single piece of evidence FOR the decomposed-kwargs-into-one-Fidelity-object direction: loops already has the object and is paying to un-build it at every render.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4036S2PC6N1CJXDYS4PP\", \"_ts\": 1783738074.577759, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:rendering/fold-view-maximal-signature\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/store-app-holds-no-fidelity-duplication\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/store-app-holds-no-fidelity-duplication\", \"feature\": \"loops-adoption-spike\", \"message\": \"Audit item 2 named tui/store_app.py as a place a landed painted declaration grammar might let loops delete. Finding: NOTHING in store_app.py is flag-compilation or Fidelity-parsing residue \\u2014 clearing a red herring from the M3 scope. The FidelityState dataclass there is a NAVIGATION state (a facts-within-a-tick-window drill cursor), a domain concept that merely shares the word fidelity; it has no relation to painted's render Fidelity. store_app imports painted's Block/Surface/views (data_explorer, list_view) and lays out against layout(width, height) \\u2014 it is a legitimate Surface consumer, not a shadow renderer. So the deletable duplication surfaced by this spike lives entirely in cli/fidelity.py (dead fidelity_from_args) and the run_cli render-closure glue (rendering/run-cli-adapter-inventory) plus the piped re-derivation (rendering/piped-is-fabricated-tty-fact) \\u2014 NOT in the TUI. Recording this so the M3 delete-list is not padded with a false target.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7E2Q61XEP5S6PA6ZR7SP2S,01KX7H4Y91G01ATG9CAATGCAMV\", \"_ts\": 1783738086.358099, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:rendering/fidelity-from-args-is-dead-shadow-copy\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"rendering/painted-0101-consumer-workarounds-dissolved\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/painted-0101-consumer-workarounds-dissolved\", \"message\": \"painted 0.10.1 pickup (same-day patch cut FROM our M3 adoption-spike evidence \\u2014 the consumer-feedback loop closing at patch latency). Three dissolutions landed loops-side: (1) .loops/publish_semantic_trifecta.py's _anchor_sections regex post-pass (coupled to to_html's serialization whitespace) DELETED \\u2014 to_html stamps <section id> itself on 0.10.1 and the outline now walks the declared tree reading painted.publish.section_anchors(doc), the SAME map to_html stamps from. Note the break-fix character: on 0.10.1 the old regex silently stopped matching (pattern expected <section> without id) \\u2014 outline would have gone empty with no error. Visibility filter stays consumer-side as honest residue, keyed on token membership in the emitted fragment (content escaping guarantees a raw '<section id=' can only come from the publisher \\u2014 no structure recovery, no drift). PARITY PROOF: regenerated article diff vs 0.10.0 output = renderer version stamp only (8 diff lines, all version strings); section ids byte-identical. (2) store lens conditional width-None spacers collapse to Block.empty(width, 1) uniformly. (3) vertices.py _spans_block helper (the Line.to_block-refuses-None dodge) deleted, direct Line.to_block(width) at 3 sites \\u2014 goldens byte-stable, confirming the old docstring's claim that the piped register strips styling at the sink. Also paid the 0.8 deprecation debt while gating the bump: show()\\u2192paint() at ~45 sites, 1164 DeprecationWarnings \\u2192 0 (paint()'s Block passthrough is drop-in; loops never used show's inferring path or format=).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP,01KWVXY7M928X1KWGSSZWHFTKN\", \"_ts\": 1783806887.636263, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\", \"thread:static-honest-060-spine\"]}, \"architecture/publish-layer-two-instance-promotion\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/publish-layer-two-instance-promotion\", \"message\": \"The application-promotion rule now fires for a loops publication layer: semantic-trifecta (91% of 826KB artifact = provenance cards) and homelab-audit (73% of 4MB = cards, article only 4.7%) hand-roll nearly identical HTML shells, drawers, manifests, redaction, and cut hydration. Two independent instances, same shape, same scaling pathology. Sol's split matches my read: medium-independent pieces (Table/Register node, published_outline, honest full-fidelity, char budgets) go UP into painted; the loops-specific pieces (sealed-cut selection, fact cursor, signature receipt, fact cards, redaction) become loops.publish \\u2014 NOT painted core. The substrate half is a public sealed-projection API (export exact tick cut + source-fact histories + edges + manifest as json/html) so consumers stop importing loops.commands internals and opening SQLite directly. Sol also correctly declined a raw-HTML escape node in painted pending a typed diagram contract \\u2014 matches painted's own dissolution discipline.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ\", \"_ts\": 1783894413.070861, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"architecture/origin-field-unused-by-provenance-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/origin-field-unused-by-provenance-consumer\", \"message\": \"Say/do gap in our own substrate, surfaced by the heaviest provenance consumer yet (2026-07-12): all 694 homelab-audit facts carry BLANK native origin \\u2014 a provenance-obsessed audit rebuilt provenance entirely in typed payload fields (evidence kind, authority/epistemic classes, observer attribution) and manual evidence summaries, because the origin field offered nothing usable for capture receipts. Sol's ask #7 (first-class evidence capture: run/ingest a read-only probe, record command, timestamp, exit status, content hash, redacted summary, observer, native origin in one signed receipt) is the Carried hand of the semantic-trifecta \\u2014 siftd Operation IR territory \\u2014 arriving as consumer demand rather than theory. Position: hold as evidence for the Carried arc, do NOT build a standalone loops probe verb (point solution smell); but the origin field's dormancy is itself a finding \\u2014 either it earns a contract that capture tooling can target, or it is dissolution-eligible dead surface. Check which during the Carried design.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ\", \"_ts\": 1783895965.30963, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"session/2026-07-13-hardening-closing-review\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-13-hardening-closing-review\", \"message\": \"Session arc: S4 edit ceremony (subtask they-plan, opus/high, merged d467e44) \\u2192 S5 ontology-as-of (same flow, merged 8fca98b, gate-closer) \\u2192 Sol holistic closing review BLOCK (8 findings, docs/dev/internal-table-s0-s5-closing-review-2026-07-13.md) \\u2192 hands-on hardening with Kyle (8 commits, four adversarial review rounds via review/internal-table-hardening subtask, every reviewer repro became a regression test) \\u2192 CLOSE \\u2192 merged ad84829. Also this session: batch-emit design consolidated three frictions then REFINED to batch-is-a-tick (symbolic IDs dissolved; design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress), decision:architecture/env-values-are-ingress, threads decl-lens-tombstone-vocab-gap + ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit. Process observations: (a) per-slice low-effort review passed what holistic high-effort blocked \\u2014 review altitude must match claim altitude (slice reviews verify slices; arc claims need arc reviews); (b) two of my own hardening fixes introduced regressions the suites missed \\u2014 the reviewer caught them because it hunted holes-introduced-by-fixes explicitly; (c) implementer rationalized a real boundary bug as 'scheduling artifact' in S5 \\u2014 cross-adapter review refused the rationalization and was right.\", \"_ts\": 1783968287.149478, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\": {\"topic\": \"practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"Internal-table retro headline (docs/dev/internal-table-retrospective-2026-07-13.md): every per-slice low-effort review passed and the medium capstone was clean, yet the holistic high-effort review found 8 closure blockers \\u2014 every one at a cross-slice seam no slice owned (foreign-genesis x merge, as_of x resolver, edit-ts x rewind, seam-bypass, secrets boundary, absorb x validator, router flag drop, per-surface-not-per-invariant exclusion). Two green tests LOCKED IN wrong cross-slice behavior. Rule: a merge asserting an arc-level claim ('gate open') buys an arc-level review at matching effort BEFORE the claim; per-slice cadence is a velocity instrument, not a closure gate \\u2014 different instruments, not quality tiers.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXECQJ349N1Z1WQA69KM280Y\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.216037, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"Hardening convergence discipline (8\\u21926\\u21923\\u21921\\u2192CLOSE in four rounds): every reviewer finding landed with its repro converted to a regression test before the fix counted as done \\u2014 the suite ratchets, so each round's frontier is genuinely new. Corollary: round 2 explicitly hunted holes-introduced-by-fixes and found 2 regressions the green suites missed, both from round-1 fixes. Fixes are new code written under pressure; they deserve MORE adversarial attention, not less. Also: implementer explanations of their own anomalies are hypotheses, not evidence (S5 'scheduling artifact' rationalization refused by cross-adapter review, correctly).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXECQJ349N1Z1WQA69KM280Y\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.525395, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"They-plan subtasks vs hands-on-wheel, compared across the internal-table arc: both shipped working slices, failed differently. Delegated workers optimize the slice's STATED exit criteria \\u2014 S5 shipped 'gate open' with blockers sitting on its own seams; delegation transfers the task, not the arc conscience. Hands-on hardening fixed all 8 seam-shaped findings with the whole arc in one head. Synthesis: greenfield slices with crisp exit criteria delegate well; integration/invariants/closure claims belong at the wheel \\u2014 or the delegated slice's exit criteria must name the seams it touches. Bonus pattern: blockers at the right altitude UPGRADE designs (TOCTOU\\u2192absorb_genesis primitive; identity finding\\u2192adopt ceremony) \\u2014 budget reviews as design forcing-functions, not only defect filters.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX9QY9EF26CNXNBPRDSDT917\", \"_ts\": 1783982559.693621, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:workflow/internal-table-build-execution-model\"]}, \"workflow/lens-usage-forensics-2026-07\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/lens-usage-forensics-2026-07\", \"message\": \"Lens audit (wiring x 1594 mined read/store invocations, 681 post-0.6.0): built-in workhorses are fold/stream/store/ticks/ls surfaces; graph healthy via --lens graph (29 recent). Dead: pop_view (population command moved to vertices_view) \\u2014 deletion dispatched. Mislabeled: run_ticks_view is sync_view's internal helper, never an entrypoint \\u2014 privatization dispatched. confluence_view: zero session-history invocations BUT Kyle uses it interactively outside sessions \\u2014 KEEP; the zero is a DISCOVERABILITY signal, not a value signal, and confirms the history-mining caveat (bare-terminal use is invisible to session forensics). Headline inversion: user-authored resolver lenses (--lens prompt 23 / reconcile 17 / session 14) out-earn every built-in except graph, and none are declared in any .vertex lens block \\u2014 the lens system's center of gravity is ad-hoc custom files, so the zoom\\u2192fidelity signature migration must treat custom lens files as first-class consumers.\", \"_ts\": 1783994675.323187, \"_n\": 1}, \"session/2026-07-14-completion-t3\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-07-14-completion-t3\", \"feature\": \"completion-t3\", \"message\": \"Session arc (continuation of 2026-07-13 follow-ups session): lens audit (wiring x mined usage; pop_view deleted, run_ticks_view privatized via sonnet subtask; confluence kept \\u2014 zero session-history use was a DISCOVERABILITY signal, Kyle uses it interactively) \\u2192 pivot to completion T3 as the discoverability fix \\u2192 orchestrated build: S1 seam+lens (opus/high), S2 vertex (sonnet), S3 kind/key (sonnet, one usage-limit interruption resumed cleanly), S4 emit wiring (sonnet, scope-discovered: only read had an add_args seam) \\u2192 Sol gpt-5.6 medium read-only review, SIX rounds to CLOSE, all remediation hands-on at the wheel \\u2192 branch pushed, UNMERGED, awaiting Kyle. Also this session: first gpt-5.6-terra worker (painted 0.11 migration, clean), retrospective kind ratified + used twice, meta-store role dissolved, thread:claude-memory-as-source opened, two painted upstream fixes authored. Fact-check footnote: Sol's sandbox repeatedly collected 490 lang tests vs 540 here \\u2014 environment artifact of the review worktree venv, all local runs 540 green.\", \"_ts\": 1784004310.328322, \"_n\": 1}, \"test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\": {\"topic\": \"test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\", \"message\": \"SHARPENED on landing: worse than the design-time read. Not just drift \\u2014 4/7 rules RED, and the failure mode was layered: stale allowlist entries (pop_store, painted) tripped _check_exceptions FIRST, so the actual scans never executed and real violations accumulated invisibly behind the stale-exception error (3 sqlite3 probes, 5 StoreReader reaches, store->engine, 2 unfrozen dataclasses). Root cause one level down: tests/ belongs to no package, so no gate ever ran it \\u2014 the ratchet was opt-in manual, i.e. review vigilance wearing a test's costume (Kyle's own ratchet-test principle, violated by the ratchet itself). Fixed: swept + shrink-only allowlists in f384e2d, root ./dev check gate in 2cb08a0. Meta-lesson: a ratchet's staleness check failing loudly is GOOD design (it forced the sweep), but only if something runs it \\u2014 enforcement infrastructure needs its own enforcement path.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXP65CW2ZWV343GF1YKWW49Z\", \"_ts\": 1784229856.868457, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\"]}, \"architecture/daemon-access-serves-tui\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/daemon-access-serves-tui\", \"message\": \"Convergence: ticked's 2s-poll daemon (friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access) and the 0.7.0 TUI are the SAME consumer shape \\u2014 a long-lived process needing incremental reads (replay facts since last rowid, not full history) and receive() without reload. The daemon-shaped engine access ticked forces is the TUI's substrate too; designing it once serves both, and the temporal-cursor work inherits the same long-lived-handle contract. Sequencing implication: the engine design session for daemon access should sit BEFORE TUI work on the 0.7.0 track, not parallel to it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXM4GB6356A3SV8GDD3WXWGM,01KXPVPFGVGASDXJ57QR7EFTB6\", \"_ts\": 1784252418.931935, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\", \"friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access\"]}, \"implementation/replay-swap-was-per-vertex\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/replay-swap-was-per-vertex\", \"message\": \"MAJOR pre-existing engine bug found by the receipt-change adversarial review (not caused by the diff \\u2014 the lens question 'can receive_receipt run with a store attached during replay?' surfaced it): Vertex.replay swapped only the ROOT's _store to None, so parent replay forwarded historical facts to nested children whose stores were still attached \\u2014 a stored child re-appended the parent's ENTIRE history on every load (1\\u21922\\u21923 rows per replay, reproduced empirically by the verify agent). Same discipline hole: no try/finally on the swap, so a raising fold mid-replay left _store=None permanently (close() silent no-op, handle leaked, boundaries dead). Fixed fdda675: _replay_guard context manager makes the swap per-TREE (walks _children recursively, saves/restores store+replaying flags in finally). Side effect worth knowing: child boundaries no longer fire mid-replay \\u2014 matches replay's own documented contract ('without re-appending or firing boundaries') and prevents double-folding; the old behavior was the bug wearing a feature's shape. CALIBRATION: my own pre-check read replay() and concluded 'clean \\u2014 every path nulls _store before replaying'; TRUE per-vertex, FALSE per-tree. I verified the discipline at the wrong scope. The structural sensor (workflow lens + empirical repro) caught what my targeted read did not \\u2014 the read confirmed the claim I brought to it.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXPY5GCW45YB0SKB5W25M9QR\", \"_ts\": 1784255013.331488, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:engine-write-path-no-receipt-no-close\"]}, \"architecture/parallel-authorization-paths\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/parallel-authorization-paths\", \"message\": \"Two parallel authorization paths exist and only one is enforced: (a) lang-AST GrantDecl/ObserverDecl -> identity.py ObserverCheck (enforced at emit \\u2014 'forbidden' when decl.grant.potential excludes the kind); (b) engine.Peer/Grant frozen dataclasses with Vertex.receive(grant=) gating \\u2014 ZERO production consumers (no CLI site constructs one; every receive() call is bare). Horizon (read-side visibility) is enforced NOWHERE. This is a dissolution candidate that must resolve BEFORE Digest builds on either path \\u2014 Digest is chartered as the first in-repo Peer/Grant consumer, and building it on the unenforced path while the enforced path speaks a different schema would fork authorization semantics. Echoes convergence/consumer-more-substrate-aligned-than-substrate (2026-05-13): the substrate's own primitive still doesn't participate in the substrate. Found by the 0.7.0 design-state audit 2026-07-16.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ49N02Y6XRP8P6TCAP2GCQ\", \"_ts\": 1784261442.054095, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/strata-tick-lineage-unmet\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/strata-tick-lineage-unmet\", \"message\": \"decision:design/strata-cut-ratified (2026-07-04) fed forward a concrete requirement \\u2014 'the 0.7.0 internal table should carry parent_tick_id/child_vertex_ref on tick rows' \\u2014 and the internal-table arc did NOT land it: the ticks schema is unchanged (sqlite_store.py ~281-293), _tick_to_fact still drops the child tick id, and the 'lineage' \\u00a79 added is DECLARATION lineage (genesis/own_lineage), a different concept. Strata is therefore doubly downstream in the 0.8.0 wave: it needs a tick-lineage schema design (post-freeze, coordinating with the Go oracle) AND its stacked view wants Digest output (recursive digests). No design fact exists yet for tick lineage as columns vs fact-borne events. Found by the 0.7.0 design-state audit 2026-07-16.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ49N02Y6XRP8P6TCAP2GCQ\", \"_ts\": 1784261442.354691, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"rendering/sync-view-aggregation-fallback-bug\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/sync-view-aggregation-fallback-bug\", \"message\": \"sync_view's 'No sources configured.' fallback checks top-level ran/skipped/errors, not children's \\u2014 on an aggregation vertex whose children DID run sources it appends the fallback after the children's rendered rows. Found during TUI-S0 golden coverage (feat/tui-s0-goldens); now deliberately BYTE-LOCKED as-is in test_sync.py::test_aggregation_tty so the lens-signature migration cannot 'fix' it as a silent side effect \\u2014 triage deliberately, then update the golden with the fix in the same commit.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBJ9RFA5CN1RQ659W85S17\", \"_ts\": 1784303901.949045, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:rendering/tui-shell-integration\"]}, \"practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\": {\"topic\": \"practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\", \"message\": \"Overnight 0.8.0 run, review-yield data across the multi-model pipeline: codex reviews of Claude-written slices found 8 findings on E1-E3 (3 MAJOR incl. lineage-verify gap and guard bypass) + 5 on C1-C2 (3 HIGH, all the SAY/DO class: --facts route silently discarding --at; lens fetches rendering cursor metadata over head data; --refs walking referenced entities at head under a historical fold). Claude panels of codex-written designs found a fabricated benchmark citation, a false data_version safety claim (empirically refuted: pinned inside open txn = unbounded staleness), and painted-main drift the dossier snapshot missed. Every green suite masked findings the OTHER family caught \\u2014 the cross-vendor structural sensor kept earning its keep at each layer (design, engine, CLI). The labeled-lie class (cursor metadata over unselected data) is the exact gap-shape this project's coherence function exists for: capability said cursor, behavior served head.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784309123.421279, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\"]}, \"architecture/floor-snap-anchor-consistency-residual\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/floor-snap-anchor-consistency-residual\", \"message\": \"Residual from the capstone fix rounds (CLI agent's honest flag, 306d28e): when a floor-snap fires on a tick whose fact_cursor lands mid-ceremony (reachable only via merge/durable-handle re-resolution reordering rowids, not natural origin writes), resolve_witness_position keeps the CLI's pre-supplied anchor= rather than re-deriving post-snap \\u2014 the reported anchor can name a tick after the snapped position. Snap itself is correct (fact_id/seq honestly pre-ceremony). Follow-up candidate for the vectors-owed batch: anchor-consistency-after-snap. Not a 0.8.0 blocker.\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784315138.13302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\"]}, \"test/codex-reverify-cursor-capstone\": {\"topic\": \"test/codex-reverify-cursor-capstone\", \"message\": \"CLOSED MERGE-READY: Codex scoped re-check of cdbb24d confirms the reversed --diff baseline-attribution fix \\u2014 tie case selects 'from' with empty interval (no sentence), None interval stays null/silent, baseline is an additive JSON field (no contract break), both directions name the correct endpoint. Full trail: capstone NOT-MERGE-READY (10 findings) -> 7480235+306d28e (all 10) -> re-verify found 1 new MAJOR -> cdbb24d -> MERGE-READY. feat/temporal-cursor (13 commits) ready for Kyle's merge call.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRQHRJ84T0QDPDBQCZG2M1X\", \"_ts\": 1784315846.080465, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\": {\"topic\": \"consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\", \"message\": \"Consumer exercise completed 2026-07-18: siftd was mapped as 17 capabilities, 11 architecture patterns, 17 components, 17 interfaces, 19 data entities, 9 flows, 49 ordered stages, and 18 invariants, plus audit and seal facts. The resulting 159-fact artifact carries 672 typed edges and validates the core fit: keyed folds present current truth while the fact stream retains change history, and declared edges can express architecture without new atoms. The exercise also exposed the residual costs: 159 individual emits, cross-kind key aliasing, mixed-predicate graph paths, no declared current-versus-inactive topology, opaque binary review, lazy FTS mutation on read, and incomplete lens cut provenance. Target split: core owns semantic correctness, CLI owns atomic authoring plus validation and review, and the project-local lens owns map vocabulary.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCXTBV2PXQB34ZHP4W6G718,01KXC7QG3FMKYX53DMDKCQNP8R,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV0ABSVWW3BW1ZB70NTNPJV,01KXV0AC0VTF42QE6KX4F9ZY65,01KXV0AC7TEKQBN0M42J04YGF5,01KXV0ACEM4X7CBJHVXMC378HH,01KXV0BH5AZ7K58MJYD5CDSXVK,01KXC7NZSHSEK03W120QKSBTG8\", \"_ts\": 1784391529.032416, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"design:rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\"]}, \"test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\", \"message\": \"Adversarial review complete (13-agent workflow: live-repro verifiers + per-fact skeptics + provenance, 2026-07-18) of the kyle/siftd-codex 7-fact delivery. BOTH frictions CONFIRMED bit-for-bit: typed-edge aliasing all 4 mechanisms reproduced twice independently (surface.py:274-276 suffix-only matcher, vertex_reader.py:1237-1242 slash mislift with write/read disagreement on the same value, resolve.py:827-840 bare-target strict-emit skip); FTS mutation reproduced 184320 to 282624 bytes from one --match, plus an AGGRAVATOR the skeptic found: aggregation --match delegates vertex_search to every child, mutating EVERY child store. Designs: predicate-graph SOUND (lands on build-1s own deferred list; premise reproduced incl. an 18-hop predicate-mixed chain), lens-boundary SOUND (pure policy fact, zero new machinery, independently re-derives consumer-owns-its-vocabulary now at N=3), export REFINE (dump half IS SPEC section-10 in stronger form and inherits the GlobalReceiptPosition gate; genuine core = canonical kind-key-sorted volatile-field-free review snapshot which read --json does NOT cover), lifecycle REFINE (real value is the UNIFICATION of three parallel proposed clauses; uncited sibling design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations owns the declaration home; SPEC section-9 vocabulary cost unpriced; siftd map has zero inactive entities so evidence is contract-prospective). Provenance: 25/25 refs resolve kind-and-key exact, 10/10 map stat claims exact including 672 edges, all 7 signatures verify against the registered observer key. Zero verdicts refuted by skeptics.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV0ACEM4X7CBJHVXMC378HH,01KXV0ABSVWW3BW1ZB70NTNPJV,01KXV0AC0VTF42QE6KX4F9ZY65,01KXV0AC7TEKQBN0M42J04YGF5,01KXV0BH5AZ7K58MJYD5CDSXVK,01KXV0BWXDH44FR8331A5KTH6Z\", \"_ts\": 1784393570.018556, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"design:rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"observation:consumer/siftd-project-map-exercise\"]}, \"implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"S1 CLOSED at 1b523b7 (2 commits: 6591420 Address + dual-reading fix). CORRECTION over n=1: my category-(b) ruling was OVERTURNED by sol's interim review (P1) and I accepted \\u2014 the old matcher's exact whole-string clause was the deliberate bare-namespaced-key interpretation (pinned by the replaced design/c test; the hypothesis direction note warned about exactly this collision and I mis-scoped it to edges). Revised ruling: DUAL-READING, content-independent \\u2014 slash form x/y matches under either (x,y) legacy or ('',x/y) bare whole-key, always; colon stays exact-only; content-dependent fallback stays rejected (no retargeting hazard: readings are static). FINAL LIVE NUMBERS (three-way diff, drift-corrected): of 91 commit-1 drops, 72 restored, 19 stay dead \\u2014 all 19 are colon-explicit true cross-kind aliases (e.g. thread/emit-receipt-on-write 9->0); same-store isolation proves dual-reading purely additive (72 up, 0 down). Measures for the hypothesis: 8 split/suffix sites -> 0 outside 95-LOC atoms/address.py; 2 disagreeing edge-interpreters -> 1 (Address.for_edge); suffix-matchers 3 -> 0; collision semantics pinned (ambiguous ref honestly counts toward both readings' rows). Meta: the interim review tier caught the ARBITER's rationalization, not the implementer's code \\u2014 S1 flagged the judgment call, I ruled wrong, sol's cold diff-read reversed me. Cross-model calibration one level up the stack from the internal-table wave.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E,01KXV2A64BQG9WYZ0ZMZ0V551N,01KXV4547A3EEN40T11RX7R89F\", \"_ts\": 1784400375.719523, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"hypothesis:refs-as-typed-address-dataclass\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"peer/tasked-vertexhandle-adoption\": {\"topic\": \"peer/tasked-vertexhandle-adoption\", \"message\": \"Consumer evidence from tasked's VertexHandle S0-S3 adoption (merged b8b64b63, autonomous walk): (1) S5 gate is REAL \\u2014 pre-checkpoint, refresh() and receive() each full-reconstruct, so an active N=1 walker cycle does ~3x the replay work of the old cold fold (1 + 2N), while idle cycles get FASTER (refresh short-circuits, parse/compile paid once at open); recorded not chased, per plan. (2) FoldState.scalars gap in 0.8.1: task.close/seal outputs missing from the fold surface \\u2014 kept tasked's bridge equivalence ratchet from covering them (walker never reads them back, so benign there, but a second consumer might). (3) Opening a handle on a never-written store errors \\u2014 moot for tasked (init seeds first) but a cold-start consumer would hit it. (4) Adoption shape that worked: consumer-side fold_to_raw bridge keeping the caller byte-stable, pinned by equivalence property test; StoreBusy/HandleInvalidated skip-cycle, StoreReplaced/CursorInvalidated transparent reopen, ReceiveCommittedError treated as success. Direct input to the 090-consumer-evidence wave and friction:no-daemon-shaped-store-access.\", \"_ts\": 1784400550.901026, \"_n\": 1}, \"implementation/090-s3-graph-census\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/090-s3-graph-census\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Live project-store graph census (090-S3, feeds wave artifact + migration-ceremony sizing): 1319 nodes, 1755 edges (0 typed), 490 orphans = 123 GENUINE dangling + 74 unsourced-inbound (keyless) + filter-excluded 0 unscoped; under --kind decision the build-1 conflation decomposes as 62 genuine dangling + 262 filter-excluded (siftd reported ~268 conflated \\u2014 confirmed and split). The 123 genuine dangling refs ARE the migration-ceremony population the S1 dual-reading ruling promised to enumerate (includes the 19 de-aliased colon refs). Chains now carry predicate labels end-to-end; wire contract additions all additive (filter_excluded/dangling_list/cycles/chains.predicates/edge).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV8SW51BNP9T5ZSVZC9VTHR,01KXVCWN5540KFSJNR0Y4P8GG4\", \"_ts\": 1784404661.482301, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:implementation/090-s1-live-dealiasing\", \"thread:ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit\"]}, \"practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\": {\"topic\": \"practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Process finding from 090 S6-to-S4: the fetch-then-disclose ordering (provenance resolved strictly AFTER the data fetch, so append-only bias makes the residual race conservative) was established in S6 under sol review, carried in the handoff prose AND an inline comment \\u2014 and the very next slice reversed it (resolve_review_head before fetch_fold), caught by sol again as a P1. Lesson: an ordering invariant that lives in comments and handoffs is vigilance, not structure \\u2014 it recurred WITHIN one wave BETWEEN adjacent agents. Both live sites now pinned by deterministic race regression tests + caller-contract docstrings; if a third site appears, that is the ratchet trigger (an enumerable-property test over disclosure call sites, shrink-only). Also the 5-for-5 wave stat: every slice's interim sol review produced exactly one real finding, each in the author's characteristic blind spot \\u2014 cross-model review as structural sensor, running at low effort.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVGEZ31EJDJT2KRZ048W52F\", \"_ts\": 1784408407.22745, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/canonical-store-review-export\"]}, \"test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"message\": \"Blind-reconstruction test of the wave artifact against the store (3 store-only verifiers, 2026-07-18): 174 concrete claims \\u2014 135 store-addressable (78%), 23 query-derivable (13%), 16 context-only (9%). The context-only bucket has STRUCTURE: (a) per-slice MODEL ATTRIBUTION is the largest cluster (5/16 \\u2014 no fact maps slice to implementing model); (b) finding-attribution nuances (which finding was the arbiter's vs sol's \\u2014 the direction arrows); (c) point-in-time evidence values (the '59-fact live tail' reading \\u2014 store now answers 71; witness-mode reads leave it null BY DESIGN, so a live reading not emitted with its fact is gone); (d) repro literals and rationale prose. LESSON (a-d are all one lesson): evidence read live during a session is citable later ONLY if the fact carries it at emission time. The verifiers also caught the artifact ERRING, not just gapping \\u2014 twice: an agenda item's tense implied the dual-reading discount pass had RUN (store says open rider \\u2014 overstatement, fixed) and two section eyebrows were FICTIONAL sl queries that return no data (say/do gap wearing CLI costume in a caption \\u2014 replaced with runnable queries; the calibration table's eyebrow now honestly reads 'not yet queryable' and cites the design that will make it so). The blind test found errors in the report about the system, using only the system \\u2014 the review pipeline turned on its own artifact.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVYG96DDMQQ5J9Z5ZYA9KWF,01KXVKYSCB4GTZK8XXGDTASK0J\", \"_ts\": 1784423578.232467, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"pattern/combine-override-unexercised\": {\"topic\": \"pattern/combine-override-unexercised\", \"ops\": \"projects-tracker\", \"message\": \"combine's kind-collision override branch (aggregator loops{} wins via override_kinds, vertex_reader.py) has no live example exercising it \\u2014 every current aggregation repeats identical child specs, so only the matching-specs branch has ever run. Latent gap for the first real user. Noted while evaluating (and rejecting) an aggregation shape for the projects portfolio vertex.\", \"_ts\": 1784564995.808933, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\", \"message\": \"VERDICT (4) CORRECTED by the 010-wave grounding slice (docs/scratch/010-wave/primitives-grounding.md, 2026-07-26) \\u2014 the promotion is NOT overdue; the claim chain breaks at five points. (1) The 'ratified charter' IS findable (decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality) but prescribes the OPPOSITE of a package \\u2014 declared-semantics, 'grammar consumes declared semantics'; the survey's quotation of it is a paraphrase wearing quote marks (string absent from the fact). Content-search invisibility explained: 'three-term' collides with the DIFFERENT triple in design/salience-three-term-contract. (2) 'Five consumers' does not survive cell-by-cell verification: threshold-breach is 4/5 by the survey's own table; hlab's recency cell (last_scrape) is a dead field never read for ordering \\u2014 REFUTED; loops' recency+partition cells are ONE function (_horizon_sort_key) double-counted; loops' threshold exemplar (_approaching) is MISCLASSIFIED \\u2014 it delegates to palette.py's single-sourced threshold, i.e. it is the substrate working correctly, cited as evidence of the gap it closes. (3) No promotion rule exists as a fact; the operative N=2 bar (paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract) has a second question \\u2014 does the discipline genuinely not live at consumer-runtime? \\u2014 which the charter answers affirmatively against promotion. (4) The thesis INVERTS inside loops: a canonical home exists (surface.py tiering, palette.py thresholds, _grammar.recency) with ~20 correct consumers; the duplications are forks BYPASSING it \\u2014 a fork-consolidation + ratchet problem, not a greenfield package. (5) External consumers span three distributions; siftd does not depend on strange-loops at all. Verdicts (1)-(3) of the original read stand unchanged. The relevance-gate in ARCHITECTURE.md survives its first contact: the grounding is evidence FOR deliberately-homeless, not against.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG47P934K8H4SKYGX9N49EC\", \"_ts\": 1785101567.621792, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"message\": \"Kyle's read of the instrument-family survey: the four-layer model maps onto Weaver's three levels of the communication problem. Level A technical (accuracy) = record+view \\u2014 pure, correctness-capable; loops kept Shannon's discipline of excluding semantics (FTS matches-not-ranks, folds project-not-judge), which is WHY the record layer surveys clean. Level B semantic (meaning) = relevance \\u2014 the layer Shannon bracketed out; five apps hand-rolling judgments are five attempts to smuggle B into A; 'no package exists' = Level B has no home. Level C effectiveness (conduct/authority) = surfacing + act arrow \\u2014 relational, reliable-not-correct. Diagnosis of the misfilings (painted-cli run_cli/add_cli_args, sign-in-loops): with only two homes built, relation-shaped Level-C code got filed into the nearest Level-A substance. Missing layers cause misfiling; fix is additive (create the home), not a guilty refactor. Also: 0.8.0 strays (loops-go protocol pkg, TUI shell, vouch) are one cluster \\u2014 the surfacing layer asking to exist.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFJH3J7AG8BKXTRWBN6H1TK\", \"_ts\": 1785082145.809135, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\"]}, \"architecture/scc-census-dual-reading-discount\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/scc-census-dual-reading-discount\", \"message\": \"Dual-reading discount on the S3 SCC census is ZERO: 0 of 1783 resolved refs fan out to >1 node, so S1's bare-dual reading (222 edges) creates no spurious edges \\u2014 pruning fan-out leaves the census bit-identical (41 SCCs today, 40 at commit; store grew). Dangling artifacts structurally impossible (adjacency is node-to-node only); 13 self-loops are genuine self-refs already segregated from Tarjan. Dominant artifact class is instead NODE GRANULARITY: 41/41 SCCs contain a re-emitted entity, and the fold unions a topic's refs across all its facts \\u2014 at FACT granularity 1958 of 1961 ref edges point backward in time, i.e. the fact-level ref graph is a DAG bar 3 same-session forward edges. Verdict: DAG-falsification STANDS for the entity graph and survives the discount fully, but for a different reason than the audit assumed (union-over-re-emission, not mutual referencing) \\u2014 batch-emit can safely order by emission sequence, must never topologically sort the entity graph, and the deferred colon-form rewrite would not move the census by one SCC. Detail: docs/scratch/090-wave/scc-discount.md\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFQ4KV0C2G20Q5CQQCK55DM\", \"_ts\": 1785086675.522069, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\", \"message\": \"Sol HIGH full-diff pass (escalated from low/medium slice tier): BLOCK \\u2014 2 P1 + 3 P2, every finding with a reproduced failure scenario, zero arbiter overrules this round. P1-a review-evidence snapshot binding = fetch-then-disclose occurrence THREE (S6->S4->S4-again), and P2-a FTS fingerprint race is occurrence FOUR in the same class \\u2014 the ratchet rule fires, fix wave includes structural guard not just regression tests. P1-b falsified the rider commit's upstream-gating claim with a reproduced wrong-store WRITE via verb-first close (the exact footgun class the rider existed to kill \\u2014 the fix missed callers of the same function it gated). P2-b FoldSection field-by-field reconstruction dropped the new lifecycle field (dataclasses.replace is the ratchet). P2-c: --refs traversal was the ONE address-resolution path that never converged on Address.readings. Sol also correctly killed its own suspicions (whitelist held, gate call sites consistent) and adjudicated the pyright flags as narrowing noise. Pipeline calibration: high-tier full-diff review earns its cost precisely on cross-slice and rider (unreviewed-increment) surface \\u2014 5/5 findings live in exactly the two zones the brief predicted slice review couldn't see.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFQ4KV0C2G20Q5CQQCK55DM\", \"_ts\": 1785087522.139936, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"test/090-sol-verify-round2\": {\"topic\": \"test/090-sol-verify-round2\", \"message\": \"Sol verification of the 5 fixes: P2-b CLOSED (replace ratchet clean), P1-a/P1-b/P2-c PARTIAL, P2-a NOT-CLOSED. The pattern of the residue is instructive: behavior fixes held (all original repros closed) but THREE of the structural ratchets were evadable on first construction \\u2014 aliased-import evasion of the AST walk, string-grep rule passing a mixed gated/ungated module, ungated primitive still importable, walked-truthiness test too weak for the collision case. Ratchets need adversarial verification as much as fixes do; a ratchet that only catches the exact reintroduction it was written against is regression-test-shaped, not ratchet-shaped. P2-a's residue named a sharp principle: SAME CONNECTION IS NOT SAME SNAPSHOT \\u2014 StoreReader never begins a transaction, so certify-then-query straddles concurrent commits; the fix is BEGIN DEFERRED around the pair. Round 2 dispatched: close the race, harden all three ratchets against sol's constructed evasions, unify walker/graph dual-reading collision semantics.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFR3XJ96X8KMR1XVDC4GMBB\", \"_ts\": 1785089244.872774, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\"]}, \"architecture/loops-go-grounding-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/loops-go-grounding-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Track B grounding (docs/scratch/010-wave/loops-go-grounding.md, spot-checked): (1) OWED-VECTOR COUNT CORRECTED 8->5 \\u2014 the three conformance-oracle vectors ARE families 1-3 of the five; double count came from the batch's scatter (final-contracts items in one doc, only enumeration of the families in an .html dashboard). (2) REFUTED 'no live data exercises ceremonies' \\u2014 tasked.db rowids 356-360 are a real multi-subject absorb ceremony (2026-07-18, one shared ts+lineage), written the day AFTER the measurement claiming none existed; receipt_group_span verified against it live, first real-world evidence for the shipped heuristic. (3) Batch is FIVE queue members not three: +lifecycle payload field (non-blocking, additive) +tombstone vocab (new frozen kind, second-hardest item, currently carried only by an open thread). (4) Only family 3 (same-ts tie-break) is generatable today \\u2014 SPEC 4.6 pre-authorizes it and the 6.2 freeze condition is met; families 1/2/4/5 are blocked on Go-side witness axis (reader is ORDER BY ts,id with no rowid \\u2014 a prerequisite the batch never named), durable group id, or a nonexistent para-10 implementation. (5) JCS sequencing gate is SATISFIED (canonical_bytes is RFC 8785, chains re-anchored) \\u2014 recorded so it stops being re-litigated. (6) Charter contact: libs/protocol would contradict the just-ratified layer designation; grounding recommends coordination-index doc + generator relocation (the sys.path hack against $HOME/Code/loops is the one piece that does not dissolve into docs). Q1-Q5 at the design gate, Q1 first (cursor form for vectors: seq:N vs adopting fixture stores).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3\", \"_ts\": 1785116568.229838, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:010-surfacing-wave\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"test/010-sol-high-r1\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-high-r1\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol HIGH r1 (docs/scratch/010-wave/sol-review-r1.md) at b10515f: 0 P1 / 5 P2 / 1 note, every finding with a reproduced scenario. THE PATTERN HOLDS AND POINTS AT THE ARBITER THIS TIME: (1) live_edge() TOCTOU \\u2014 boundary/cursor/count are three SELECTs on a transactionless reader; sol raced a concurrent seal between them and got a count false in every coherent snapshot. Same-connection-is-not-same-snapshot, occurrence FIVE of the fetch-then-disclose class \\u2014 I wrote that principle INTO THE BRIEF and shipped a violation of it the same night. (2-5) ALL FOUR ratchet families admit constructed evasions: Rule 12 misses plain-assignment aliases (runner=run_cli); Rule 12's one-def-per-name model resolves 6 same-named nested renderers to whichever overwrote the map; my fields(Window) ratchet proves KEY PRESENCE not VALUE FIDELITY (edge_since wired to edge_facts stays green); APPS derivation silently drops PEP420 namespace packages (my egg-info hardening CAUSED the exclusion \\u2014 the __init__ requirement was the evasion). Ratchets-need-their-own-adversarial-round is now 7-for-8 across two waves. HELD: S1's 7-site migration, offered-width seam, historical/aggregate edge suppression, dashboard guard (SHA-identical at width 37), register-collapse blast radius confined to external direct callers.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785121330.966074, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r2 (docs/scratch/010-wave/sol-review-r2.md at 05b4247): live_edge CLOSED (race caught, statement-count test's overclaim noted \\u2014 it proves one-statement-on-one-connection, not all-reads-one-snapshot; behavioral regression is the real guard), hygiene CLOSED, 4 ratchets PARTIAL to FRESH evasion classes (container/getattr/partial aliases; def-only scope model beaten by local non-def shadowing \\u2014 the honest-code-shaped hole; sentinel fixed-point transforms; legal underscore packages + unenforced src/ layout). vertex_fold race CONFIRMED P2 with neither-snapshot repro. RATCHETS doctrine adjudicated: sol REFINED both generalizations rather than rejecting \\u2014 'documented boundary is advertised ATTACK SURFACE, hole only if invariant reachable through it' and 'IN-SCOPE cannot-resolve fails loudly; out-of-scope must be classified and countable, never an unobserved continue.' Allowlist found not mechanically shrink-only (existence-check only, whole-file suppression). ARBITER CONVERGENCE RULING for r3 (090 precedent): fix vertex_fold bracket + shadowing fail-closed + allowlist mechanics + hostile sentinels + underscore/src-enforcement + doctrine text; ACCEPT container/getattr/partial indirection as classified-countable boundaries \\u2014 deliberate-indirection smuggling is an insider model these drift-ratchets do not claim to police.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGRBNZX1GXEFPY15T9XWNWM,01KYGSAT2VDK20PNR18XG2YV7P\", \"_ts\": 1785123163.09354, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-high-r1\", \"thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence\"]}, \"test/010-fix-r3-landed\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-fix-r3-landed\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"r3 fix round merged (cad6211/6523c07/c9307b2 + hygiene 0a3fb43), gates: arch 36, engine 1137, loops 2403, tasks 258, atoms 440, diff-check clean, zero goldens. HEADLINE INSTANCE OF THE TAXONOMY: vertex_fold snapshot fix was CONSTRUCTION VIA EXISTING PRIMITIVE \\u2014 StoreReader.snapshot() (BEGIN DEFERRED, built rounds ago for certify-then-query) already existed; the fix was wrapping the read block, one line of substance. Its regression test states the INVARIANT (returned pair must be one of the two coherent readings), not a literal. Commit-body lesson worth keeping: per-statement coherence is not composable \\u2014 the r1 single-statement fix could not have prevented the assembly-level race; coherence fixes live at the assembly boundary. Meanwhile the four detection ratchets cost several hundred lines and the fix agent's meta-observation is now RATCHETS.md doctrine: every r2 evasion lived in machinery r1 introduced \\u2014 detection hardening GENERATES its own next attack surface, which is the empirical case for construction-first. thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence closes pending sol r3 confirmation. Boundary census: _RUNNER_BOUNDARY_BASELINE=0, allowlist dict-with-reasons baseline 0 \\u2014 both shrink-only claims now mechanical.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGT3K6TT2NTN96FBBZFKG3N,01KYGSAT2VDK20PNR18XG2YV7P\", \"_ts\": 1785124079.438974, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-r2-verdicts\", \"thread:vertex-fold-snapshot-coherence\"]}, \"test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r3 closing verification (0a3fb43): vertex_fold CLOSED (fresh attack survived \\u2014 late append invisible to the bracketed fallback read), allowlist CLOSED, hostile sentinels CLOSED (with the honest boundary stated: a finite value vector cannot prove all transforms; cost exceeds drift risk). Convergence REFUSED on three PARTIALs, and the refusal is the system working: sol applied the arbiter convergence criterion (honest-code-shaped or production-reachable blocks; counted deliberate-indirection does not) and found all three remaining evasions honest-shaped \\u2014 local \\\"import X as renderer\\\" shadowing (import aliases not indexed as bindings), incremental registry assignment (census claims countability, reports zero), Python-beside-empty-src (existence checked, containment not). Each defeats a claim R3 ITSELF ADDED \\u2014 the machinery-generates-machinery pattern holding at round granularity. r4 dispatched: three bounded fixes, nothing else, so the closing pass can be pure replay. (Re-emit: prior fact text corrupted by shell backtick substitution.)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGTZJ204QZRJTY959TVCEB9\", \"_ts\": 1785124429.751902, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-fix-r3-landed\"]}, \"test/010-review-loop-converged\": {\"topic\": \"test/010-review-loop-converged\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Sol r5 pure replay: CONVERGED, loop CLOSED. Five-round record on one night-one wave diff: r1 found 5 P2 (arbiter code included), behavior fixes closed on first verification while ratchets took three hardening rounds \\u2014 final tally: every honest-code-shaped evasion caught or fail-closed, every deliberate-indirection form classified and counted against a zero baseline, both shrink-only claims mechanical. The scope-model arc (name-collision -> non-def shadowing -> import shadowing, three rounds converging on a Python binding model) plus the vertex_fold one-line construction fix versus hundreds of detection-hardening lines is the strongest paired evidence yet for RATCHETS construction-first pricing. Wave branch at r5 close: 17 commits, arch 46 / loops 2403 / engine 1137 / tasks 258 / atoms 440, diff-check clean, zero goldens regenerated across the entire loop.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYGVA82M5TTZJQNTJ7TN5V87,01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785125090.023755, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/010-sol-r3-verdicts\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"architecture/topn-tiebreak-protocol-gap\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/topn-tiebreak-protocol-gap\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Q6, surfaced by the family-3 vector build (Track B, 2026-07-27): Go CANNOT satisfy SPEC 4.6 TopN eviction order \\u2014 atoms/fold.go tie-breaks by key string, and arrival order is recoverable from neither side of what a fold sees (target is an unordered map; payload carries _ts but ReadFacts drops the id). No content-derived rule can order items tied on both by= and ts. Closing needs a protocol decision: carry the fact id into the fold layer, or make TopN targets order-bearing (contradicts JSON object model + SemanticEqual). Implementer shipped the STRONGER fixture: 4.6 facet split into a self-retiring SKIP test (TestSameTSIDTieBreakTopNEviction) that FAILS when the gap closes. Arbiter endorsed: test-to-the-spec over test-to-the-implementation. Q6 joins Q1-Q3/Q5 at the GRP design gate; recorded in docs/dev/loops-go-protocol-queue.md.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYHYGQFBXZZ4MCTE1NJ7EM60,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3\", \"_ts\": 1785162923.661302, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/loops-go-batch-split\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"test/track-b-review-loop-converged\": {\"topic\": \"test/track-b-review-loop-converged\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"Track B sol MEDIUM loop CONVERGED in three rounds, one session. Record: r1 four findings (2 P2 + 2 P3, zero P1) with every load-bearing implementer claim empirically CONFIRMED; fix round closed 4/4 on first verification; r2 new-rule contact found two honest-code Rule 13 evasions (literal dynamic imports, importable dunder root); second fix closed both + implementer corrected the arbiter on baseline semantics (6 measured, not 0 assumed); r3 pure replay clean. Wave pattern held exactly: behavior fixes close first-try, the ratchet took the rounds \\u2014 RATCHETS construction-vs-detection pricing evidence, second instance. Sol calibration: first-ever refuted sol claim appeared this loop (editorial docstring note, grep-shaped misread of a negated sentence, non-blocking and self-labeled) \\u2014 the streak on substantive findings remains unbroken. Branches merge-ready at loops ae0911e+receipts / loops-go 590e70f pending Kyle gates.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYHYGQFBXZZ4MCTE1NJ7EM60,01KYJ12JWDZQ8V4E8FCTTH8Q6D,01KYJ1XC65EN1WKYXQ4ZV3Q86N\", \"_ts\": 1785165153.216086, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/loops-go-batch-split\", \"decision:test/non-production-import-boundary\", \"decision:test/rule13-computed-import-census\"]}, \"paradigm/fiction-as-loops-convergence\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/fiction-as-loops-convergence\", \"message\": \"Kyle's ~/Documents/Stories novel project (SillyTavern-based era-play) independently re-derived core loops shapes in a fiction substrate: two-canon memory (Spine self-account = fold view, True Memory books = fact history \\u2014 with the divergence AUTHORED, not a fidelity failure), close ritual = sweep/seal (harvest -> verbatim mint -> session-log), 'rules want to become structure / vigilance is a design smell' = ratchet doctrine, 'fractal rule' = dissolution test, salience-at-render = lens contract. First observed use-case where the fold/facts gap is the product itself (wrong self-accounts as characterization). Potential loops fit: the workshop layer only (stale-NOW section is a hand-maintained fold; open dials are threads; drift ledger is hypothesis lineage) \\u2014 the ST WI runtime is the right compile substrate, no construction warranted.\", \"ops\": \"loops-use-cases\", \"_ts\": 1786395789.294791, \"_n\": 1}, \"design/observer-signing-vs-attribution\": {\"topic\": \"design/observer-signing-vs-attribution\", \"message\": \"Stories observer-model discussion (Kyle's author/narrator/designer musing) crystallized a general loops principle: SIGNING follows write-custody, ATTRIBUTION follows voice \\u2014 never conflate. Signing observers hold keys and perform writes (kyle.gruel for canon mints, repo-agent for workshop/backfill); voices (characters, narrators, interview modes) are payload attribution (of= typed edge to a card-version lineage, mode= for generation type), reachable via graph walk mint->run->card-version, not via invented identities. Boundary rule: an entity earns a key exactly when it gains write custody (ST-narrator gets one only if/when generation becomes an emit). Corollary: Stories standing rule 4 (canon is human-curated) becomes cryptographically checkable \\u2014 a mint fact signed by anyone but the human is a structural violation. Kyle's envelope grammar already encoded the semantics: account-of has an observer, record deliberately has none.\", \"ops\": \"loops-use-cases\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZPRZP3T0ZGMW7RD8ATEYK3E\", \"_ts\": 1786398116.286344, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:stories-loops-adoption\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"message\": \"Kyle 2026-08-11: the stabilized implementation pipeline (design-fact-as-contract -> ultracode workflow with per-slice Opus impl+adversarial-review and an independent empirical gate -> codex/sol HIGH cross-family review with unverified-fixes-flagged brief -> Opus remediation with judgment fences -> /simplify -> sol r2) is a skill candidate for global implementation work. Compress into a durable skill IF the simplify+r2 tail of the jsonl-canonical arc performs. Load-bearing elements to encode: (1) brief discipline \\u2014 external reviewer gets the enumerated unverified classes, which is why sol's verdict table was possible; (2) gate independence \\u2014 gate agent re-runs the oracle, never trusts the impl report; (3) finding-disposition tracking \\u2014 today's one escape (apps/tasks) was found internally but dropped by the fix round with nothing tracking the delta; skill must make every-finding-gets-a-disposition structural, not vigilance.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZRVTWSB1V39E1WK2KFCEFW2\", \"_ts\": 1786468301.635631, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\", \"message\": \"Session arc (single day, Kyle-directed): the JSONL-canonical store went from design conversation to converged implementation through the full pipeline \\u2014 design ratified as fact first (JCS-hash storage-independence checked BEFORE framing; the one fact that decided arc size), 17-agent ultracode build S1-S4 with independent oracle gate (chain heads byte-identical), then FIVE sol HIGH rounds interleaved with Opus remediations, a 4-angle simplify (12 applied), and a roll-in workflow (verify-canonical-agreement + tasks-residence). 44 commits, ~4170 tests, live store migrated and honestly attested; --deep re-derives the chain from canonical content in 2.5s. CALIBRATION, three notes: (1) scope-the-claim beat widen-the-detection THREE times (out-of-band detection docs, verify quick label, lag-innocence boolean) \\u2014 when a detector overclaims, the fix is usually the claim; ratchet-doctrine sibling, name it in the retro. (2) The simplify pass both caught what four bug-hunt rounds missed (reuse angle: 5 old-idiom residue sites, found by grepping for the REPLACED idiom \\u2014 a finding class fault-injection cannot produce) AND introduced the arc's one regression (rebuild source-mutation), which only the post-simplify sol round caught \\u2014 the pipeline's r2-after-simplify position is load-bearing. (3) Fix-completion tracking: r1's single escape (apps/tasks) was found-then-dropped by a fix round; after every-finding-gets-a-disposition went into prompts, zero escapes across four more rounds \\u2014 the discipline is structural now, encode it in the skill. INCIDENT: apply agent's add -A briefly committed the live store + popped a foreign stash; self-caught, excised (verified: no commit in --all history touches project.jsonl), argues for worktree isolation or a .loops/ commit fence on apply-phase agents. noticing-lags-doing: one reroute logged in-moment (sweep-skill stale form \\u2014 logged AT the reroute), but the subagent-transcript extraction pattern went unlogged through 3 uses before the sweep caught it; the standing property stands.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZSE9TDHVXMPMHMX4161CGJN,01KZSD2E8VRRNMRYMBY8B7T6G3,01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G\", \"_ts\": 1786486516.212871, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:store/verify-canonical-agreement\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety\", \"message\": \"EMPIRICALLY CONFIRMED 2026-08-12 (upgrades the same-day code-read): two concurrent writer processes x25 emits each into a throwaway JSONL-canonical vertex \\u2014 50/50 landed, 0 failures, genuine interleaving (37 writer-alternation runs), per-writer seq monotonic in log order, ids unique, index rebuilt 51/51 from log after db deletion. Bonus: ids NOT globally sorted even single-store multi-writer (ULID mints before the lock) \\u2014 A3 ids-are-never-ordered reconfirmed at the smallest scale. Slice-0 pre-flight of thread:cli-honesty-wave; agents may emit facts concurrently.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVHYN1QQPT1AEGJA35K269\", \"_ts\": 1786567936.575369, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"thread:cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-010-retro-and-release\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-010-retro-and-release\", \"message\": \"Session arc (single sitting, Kyle-directed): the 010 arc closed end-to-end \\u2014 retro, two promoted principles, a ruled design question, and v0.10.0 SHIPPED to PyPI. Sequence: (1) RETRO on the jsonl-canonical arc \\u2014 five lessons receipted (retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store); scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection promoted to named principle AND global CLAUDE.md (first loops-born principle to cross into the global config, siftd corroborating from its side: simplify-as-standard-process and worktree isolation both independently adopted there \\u2014 cross-repo convergence is becoming the promotion signal). (2) Kyle opened the impl-agents-carry-loops-discipline question; ruled same session: project store over per-arc vertex (refs are within-store; noise pressure must EARN a split, and the friction kind is in the agent vocabulary precisely to capture that pressure), moment-scoped emits, facts-only fence, custody per observer-signing-vs-attribution. Concurrency precondition VERIFIED by code-read (observation:implementation/jsonl-multi-writer-safety) \\u2014 appends serialize under the sqlite write lock; the docstrings anticipated multi-writer before any design asked for it. (3) Release-scope ruled (option A) and EXECUTED: whole branch as 0.10.0, gate 5108 tests + re-gate under painted 0.13.0, CHANGELOG from the log at cut time (80 commits), wheel + PyPI verified end-to-end, thread resolved. Ceremony found two loose ends that DISSOLVED on contact (loops-go has no remote; stale index.lock from the Aug 11 apply incident) and two reroutes folded into the release skill same-session (uv cached-index masquerading as PyPI lag; venv retry loops need --clear). Sweep fixed the sweep skill itself (stale --since form, friction resolved). noticing-lags-doing: BOTH reroutes logged in-moment \\u2014 the inline reflex held through a full ceremony. Builder-inhabitant note: the 0.10.0 wheel smoke-read exercised its own canonical-agreement gate against the live store it ships support for. Next entry points: 0.11.0 re-charter, impl-pipeline skill authoring (all design inputs receipted), log-compaction arc.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVPJAZ7NNM8PH9PPHQ71D1F,01KZVPHRGQ4ZRJNXQ271Y9CWZ9,01KZVPWQBCCWPQPKF4S08CYWJ7,01KZVQASSMHZPJN161E5EPJCJN,01KZVQX4DMD09ZY4DB2ZJ8EHHB\", \"_ts\": 1786564070.812885, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/release-scope-0100\", \"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection\", \"retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-authored\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-skill-authored\", \"message\": \"The impl-pipeline skill is AUTHORED (2026-08-12, same session as the retro that completed its evidence): ~/.config/claude/skills/impl-pipeline/SKILL.md, global scope per the candidate ruling. Encodes: design-fact-as-contract, gate independence, brief discipline (anchor/contract/unverified-fixes-enumeration/verdict-table), every-finding-gets-a-disposition with the three arbiter judgment rules (scope-the-claim, construction-over-detection, fixes-deserve-more-attention), simplify-as-detection-modality, load-bearing r2-after-simplify, the loops-discipline ruling (moment-scoped emits, facts-only fence, attribution-not-keys, store= for worktree workers), and the paid-for agent mechanics (worktree isolation for commit authority, SendMessage+file-then-return, idle-ping verification, CLAUDECODE prefix, single-writer main checkout). Completion rider: the finding kind is now DECLARED in project.vertex (by name, open->fixed|dismissed|deferred) and smoke-tested \\u2014 the ruling ratified the vocabulary, the declaration makes the disposition ledger queryable. First live run: the 0.11.0 re-charter wave.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G,01KZVPJAZ7NNM8PH9PPHQ71D1F,01KZVPWQBCCWPQPKF4S08CYWJ7\", \"_ts\": 1786564368.522146, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/impl-agents-emit-loops-discipline\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"retrospective:010-jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"practice/reconcile-evidence-agent-pattern\": {\"topic\": \"practice/reconcile-evidence-agent-pattern\", \"message\": \"Reconcile 2026-08-12 process finding: the evidence-agent + verify-arbiter split scaled a 127-item backlog into one session. Four parallel agents gathered per-item receipts (commit hashes, line numbers, live reproductions); every disposition ruling stayed with the arbiter, spot-checked before emitting. The pattern EARNED its verify pass twice: (1) fr2 reported the plugin dead from the decoy ~/.claude/plugins registry \\u2014 refuted by checking the real CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR registry + live session facts; (2) th2's shallow receipt led ME to prematurely resolve loops-skill-canonical-source-gitignored, and fr1's deeper read (symlink target + diff) forced a same-session reopen \\u2014 the arbiter's own ruling corrected by a later agent's receipts. Quality gradient observed: agents instructed to REPRODUCE pain (fr1/fr2) produced strictly better evidence than agents reading git log alone. Also: the batch's 'resolved' recommendations clustered where waves shipped (0.8.0-0.10.0), confirming reconcile debt tracks release velocity \\u2014 hence friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F,01KZVSHJMFT5FPNYZMGKN18BBJ\", \"_ts\": 1786565615.285373, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\", \"friction:subagent-final-reports-lost-to-idle\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-reconcile-two-month-clear\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-reconcile-two-month-clear\", \"message\": \"Session arc: first reconcile since 06-12 cleared the two-month backlog (~127 items) via 4 parallel evidence agents + arbiter verification \\u2014 full detail in thread:reconcile-2026-08-12. Shape: hypotheses ruled from store data first (1 confirmed, 1 rejected by own falsifiable phase, 2 refined), then batch dispositions on agent receipts (15 threads resolved, 16 parked-with-conditions, 9 frictions resolved, 8 narrowed), then advisor-forced count audit recovered 15 threads my status-grep silently missed. CALIBRATION, three instances all structural-sensor-shaped: fr2's decoy-registry false positive refuted by my verification; my OWN premature loops-skill resolve reopened on fr1's deeper receipt (arbiter-corrected-by-later-evidence, same-session); the count-gap I waved off until advisor blocked close on it \\u2014 my noticing lagged again, the sensor (arithmetic) caught it. The reconcile filed the structural fixes for its own failure modes: reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor + read-status-filter-missing, both slices of the next wave. NEXT ENTRY: thread:cli-honesty-wave \\u2014 first live impl-pipeline skill run, Opus/Sonnet impl + sol review + arbiter, ruled by Kyle at close.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVSXBYD0J32ZGHJMZVDBKM0,01KZVVHYN1QQPT1AEGJA35K269\", \"_ts\": 1786567553.819084, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:cli-honesty-wave\", \"thread:reconcile-2026-08-12\"]}, \"practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\": {\"topic\": \"practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\", \"message\": \"Mid-wave process retro (Kyle-prompted, build+gate phase complete, sol r1 in flight). WORKED: pre-flight dissolved build->exercise via advisor receipts-check; S1-first meant the pipeline consumed its own instrument (s1-gate check 3 ran --status live) same-session; all 4 independent gates found things green reports didn't contain; findings-as-store-facts made every-finding-gets-a-disposition queryable (16/16 dispositioned, zero drops); mid-flight peer correction (stale-sl) propagated before false green. BIT US, four shapes, all captured into the skill same-session: (1) worktree spawn base races arbiter merges \\u2014 step-0 base verification now required; (2) worktrees environmentally weaker than main checkout (no untracked .loops) \\u2014 main-checkout post-merge suite promoted from habit to load-bearing stage; forcing consumer for thread:track-jsonl-store-for-worktree-parity; (3) arbiter authored a wrong verification form (uv run --package loops sl = stale global) and propagated it to three briefs \\u2014 verify-which-binary rule added; (4) gates lacked the SendMessage rule implementers had \\u2014 verdicts sat behind idle pings. Formal retrospective still due at arc close; this is the mid-arc cut.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KZVY9SC1NGGW3B9ZZYWYJ64W,01KZVY9551395FE9ZN6ZQTX7HE\", \"_ts\": 1786571152.117546, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"finding:chw-s4-test-hermeticity\", \"thread:track-jsonl-store-for-worktree-parity\"]}, \"test/chw-store-missing-name-stdout\": {\"topic\": \"test/chw-store-missing-name-stdout\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"message\": \"found during r1 remediation, outside ruling scope: loops store <missing-name> raises FileNotFoundError inside fetch() under painted run_cli and prints '<name> does not exist' to STDOUT at exit 1 (store.py _resolve_target line ~294 path) \\u2014 same defect family as chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout, candidate finding for the arbiter\", \"_ts\": 1786572653.148088, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/source-cadence-split-rationale\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/source-cadence-split-rationale\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/CADENCE.md (2026-01-31, deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Source and Cadence are separate layers: Source answers WHAT to observe (atoms \\u2014 command, parse, kind), Cadence answers WHEN (engine \\u2014 scheduling is runtime policy, not data shape). The proposal shipped in a different shape than sketched: no Timer-as-Fact (never built \\u2014 see friction:loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary), no timer loops; 'every' compiles to Cadence.elapsed(kind, interval), a store predicate over _sync.{kind} lifecycle facts (compiler.py:820-828); 'every'+'on' together is a hard ValueError; Trigger has OR semantics; runtime is a discrete cadence-gated sync pass (executor toposorts qualifying sources into dependency tiers, gathers each tier), not a continuous fact-stream. cadence.py's module docstring is the accurate current description.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW0BXYY8B264GE0P4JCJQSA\", \"_ts\": 1786573577.509014, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:loader-pure-timer-loop-dead-vocabulary\"]}, \"architecture/persistence-conceptual-spine\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/persistence-conceptual-spine\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/PERSISTENCE.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). The durable spine, still true through 0.10.0 JSONL-canonical: (1) persistence is CONFIGURATION, not architecture \\u2014 a vertex with a store persists, one without is ephemeral, same shapes either way; (2) fold state is never serialized directly \\u2014 only facts and ticks persist, state is always re-derivable; (3) a boundary-less fold IS memory \\u2014 accumulation without a store or tick is the degenerate persistent form; (4) replay is folding \\u2014 reconstruction is the same fold over the same facts, not a separate mechanism. Current API surface lives in libs/engine/CLAUDE.md Level 2 and root CLAUDE.md's store-is-a-file section; this fact carries the why, not the how.\", \"_ts\": 1786573578.505675, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/SCOPE-LATTICE.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Peer/Grant is shaped as it is: scopes form a powerset lattice under subset-inclusion \\u2014 None is top (unrestricted), frozenset() is bottom (locked out), restrict is intersection, delegate is restrict-then-rename, identity is the bottom case of scoping. peer.py instantiates exactly the narrowing half of this algebra over horizon/potential; narrowing composes by transitivity so delegation chains cannot widen. The chain machinery the doc described in present tense (VertexPolicy, walk_grant_chain, grants_for, envelope parent_ref) was FORWARD DESIGN gated on vouch \\u2014 zero-hit in libs/ and apps/ as of 0.10.0; lands when vouch's exercise produces it (ARCHITECTURE.md says so; arc parked since 2026-06-12).\", \"_ts\": 1786573578.986651, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/vertex-routing-narrative\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-routing-narrative\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/VERTEX.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). WHY Vertex replaced Stream: routing-by-kind separates arrival from accumulation \\u2014 facts route to per-kind folds, each fold accumulates independently, boundaries snapshot AFTER fold (fold-before-snapshot ordering is the invariant). Memory-vs-boundary: a fold without a boundary is memory; a boundary turns accumulated state into a Tick. The doc's 'Vertex doesn't know about other vertices' claim rotted: add_child/nesting is now the in-engine answer to both branching and merging (child Ticks re-enter the parent as facts), and register_vertex_boundary(kind, match, conditions, run) is a third first-class boundary mode the doc never learned. Current API: libs/engine/CLAUDE.md Levels 1-2.\", \"_ts\": 1786573597.357156, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/temporal-semantic-time\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-semantic-time\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/TEMPORAL.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). The durable thesis: boundaries are SEMANTIC time, not clock time \\u2014 a tick marks 'a meaningful cycle completed' (deploy finished, session closed, N facts accumulated), and clock time is just one boundary trigger among several (when/after/every). Reset-vs-carry is the second axis: a boundary either resets its fold (batch semantics) or carries it (running-state semantics). Nesting composes time-scales: child vertices tick on their own boundaries, parents fold child ticks as facts \\u2014 coarse time built from fine time. Verified by live execution during the 2026-08-12 audit: reset/carry and fold-before-snapshot both hold in current engine.\", \"_ts\": 1786573598.640193, \"_n\": 1}, \"architecture/identity-peer-as-atom-history\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/identity-peer-as-atom-history\", \"message\": \"Extracted from docs/IDENTITY.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history). Durable content: (1) Peer-as-atom dissolution history \\u2014 identity was nearly a fourth atom shape; it dissolved into observer-as-string on Fact plus Peer/Grant at the engine layer because identity is a STANCE (who is observing) not a data shape, and stance is emergent from emission patterns; (2) the kyle/session/worker slash-naming hierarchy convention for observers; (3) enforcement reality as of 0.10.0: the ONLY grant gate is potential at vertex.receive (receive-side, vertex.py:507) \\u2014 horizon is manipulated by grant/restrict/delegate operators but NO enforcement path reads it; there is no render-side filtering. Grant has no observer field (Grant(horizon, potential) only) \\u2014 the doc's Grant(observer=...) examples were a TypeError. The render-side horizon gate and grant-chain machinery remain forward design gated on vouch (see observation:architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW1AS27N2F2KFG9EFD3T85T\", \"_ts\": 1786573599.288553, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:architecture/scope-lattice-narrowing-algebra\"]}, \"paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement\", \"message\": \"Extracted from STRANGE-LOOPS.md (deleted in ground-up sweep; full text in git history; paradigm summary folded into root CLAUDE.md opening). The root statement: three shapes (Fact \\u2014 something observed; Spec \\u2014 something expected; Fold \\u2014 how observations accumulate), four properties (append-only, participatory/observer-as-stance, boundary-driven, compositional), one pattern (facts flow in, folds accumulate, boundaries resolve, ticks flow out). The What-Dissolved table recorded prior concepts absorbed by the paradigm (Stream into Vertex, sessions into scoped stores, identity into stance). Audit correction folded in: 'horizon/potential aren't access control' was operationally false for potential \\u2014 potential IS an enforced ingress gate at vertex.receive (Gate 1); horizon is unenforced shape-of-participation. The honest framing: constraints emerge through delegation rather than upfront enumeration, and only potential is currently enforced.\", \"_ts\": 1786573614.129226, \"_n\": 1}, \"practice/dead-plan-docs-supersession\": {\"topic\": \"practice/dead-plan-docs-supersession\", \"message\": \"Supersession record for the four plan-artifact docs deleted in the 2026-08-12 ground-up sweep (full text in git history): (1) docs/NAMED_SESSIONS.md \\u2014 its own dissolution test concluded 'sessions dissolve into scoped stores' and that SHIPPED as named vertices (loops init <name>, resolve_vertex slashed names), a strictly more general primitive; the session.py verbs it proposed extending were deliberately deleted in the observer rebuild (fda3a51). (2) docs/orchestration-agent-seed.md \\u2014 the separate-orchestration-agent concept was dissolved in-store within three days of writing (design/orchestration-dissolves-daemon, design/vertex-as-loop-controller); leaving an agent-facing bootstrap prompt for a dissolved role was an active hazard. (3+4) docs/SDK.md + docs/SDK-EMIT-PLAN.md (same commit d097120) \\u2014 the loops/sdk package was never built, but the proposal was substantially REALIZED under different names: typed errors as loops/errors.py, the semantic/rendering seam as the Operation IR (cli/operation.py, cli/dispatch.py); direction recorded in decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape and maintained in apps/loops/CLAUDE.md Level 2. One orphan line worth keeping from SDK.md: an abstraction earns generic status by modeling a real domain action cleanly, not by making pytest convenient.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRVP3V4NG2GEX5A07PTH1FF1,01KZW1A61TDCQ6AQRTS36EFHX5\", \"_ts\": 1786573615.772283, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/cli-refactor-option-2-siftd-shape\", \"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\"]}, \"ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\": {\"topic\": \"ops/chw-rebase-provenance-discontinuity\", \"message\": \"A concurrent docs session rebased cli-honesty-wave onto new main (17ffde6c, docs ground-up sweep) TWICE mid-wave, once during an in-progress merge. Outcome after verification: branch healthy on new base, my R2-F1 merge resolution survived (b7888f8b), suite 2509/59 green, a52017db+ae66f9d3 survive via the merge's second parent. Commit= pins emitted before the rebase map: 6c8d965->23f8a76b (R2 ls fix), d36f119->202d40ad (S4 integration), 49e4e4c->723ca85c (S4-F1+F6), 5f1b0df->786df6b0 (store stderr), 859702b->b464362c (S1-F1), cf05ca3->03ac6b9b (S1-F2), 649c81b->d945949a (S2-F1), 7b2cb76->1288d790 (S1), 548bbc2->da979273 + 2b3e837->a7e1642e + 7bda5ae->da60136b (S2), 5adfab7->507cabb8 (S3), 28b7a20->eb596bc6 (S4). Old hashes remain reachable via agent worktree branches until pruned; this fact is the durable mapping. Pins are provenance, not graph nodes \\u2014 the discontinuity is documented, not rewritten.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786573956.074319, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-docs-freshness\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-docs-freshness\", \"message\": \"Session arc: from one external user's migration question to a rebuilt docs posture in a day. Shape: UPGRADING.md drafted via 8-miner ultracode sweep + hand-verification, shipped to the requestor; 16-doc staleness audit (Sonnet mine / Opus verify, 32 agents, ~1.75M tokens) produced the stale-map; Kyle pivoted from triage to ground-up rebuild \\u2014 12 docs deleted, rationale store-extracted, 5 reference docs kept with standing ratchets ruled. CALIBRATION: (1) the audit's verifier tier earned its keep decisively (4 refutations vs ~80 missed-stale additions \\u2014 never ship miner output unverified); (2) the session's own worst moment was self-inflicted: rebasing a branch a live sibling session owned, discovered only via its in-flight merge \\u2014 ListAgents BEFORE ref-mutation on shared checkouts, now receipted as convention-pending; (3) freeze-at-birth plan-artifacts, not gradual drift, were the dominant rot mode \\u2014 the release-gate lands at exactly that moment. Cross-session coordination with loops-92 worked: negotiated git freeze, deduped frictions, they adopted the UPGRADING convention for their own wave unprompted. Next entry: ~/Code/loops-docs worktree, thread:docs-freshness-arc.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW2BA0T9MJ5YT0PYQ88CJBD,01KZW1A61TDCQ6AQRTS36EFHX5\", \"_ts\": 1786574645.364974, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\": {\"topic\": \"paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\", \"message\": \"Kyle's founding motivation, surfaced during README drafting (was misfiled in my head as 'built-by-agents provenance'): the LENS PROBLEM. Human + agent watching the same homelab could not share a view \\u2014 agent reads the docker-log firehose whole, human cannot; Rich's live console (the Cells origin in painted) died under the load when they tried one shared surface. The structural fix was not a better view but shared RECORD, divergent LENSES: one store, fidelity per-observer, every conversation grounded in the same ordered past. This is the umwelt point made concrete \\u2014 observers with different perceptual bandwidths composing over one witnessed record \\u2014 and it is why fidelity/lens/painted exist at all. Now in README's Pattern section: 'a human and a machine can finally be looking at the same thing.'\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW8G01X2DZ0SK3VS45KCY59\", \"_ts\": 1786582000.007407, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\"]}, \"session/2026-08-12-readme-rebuild\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-12-readme-rebuild\", \"message\": \"Session arc (docs session 2, brainstorm-to-shipped): Kyle opened wanting a root README that explains 'a data model that doesn't exist elsewhere' and the session ran as convergent ideation \\u2014 5 design rounds emitted in-flight, each a Kyle correction that DISSOLVED my framing into existing machinery: composition into tick (the third atom was the algebra all along), web scale into residence.py, universality into the March What-Dissolved table's own last row. The recovered STRANGE-LOOPS.md (17ffde6c~1) knew tonight's thesis in March; the rebuild is that document folded forward, minus its history (What-Dissolved dropped \\u2014 the README is a fold, history lives in the store). Shipped f3f0031b during the session across the cli-honesty merge window (worktree detached to unblock the arbiter mid-conversation; freeze lifted; v0.11.0 out). CALIBRATION: caught converging too early twice \\u2014 Kyle's 'wrap it up in a bow' tease, then my bow-tied section-order skeleton when he wanted narrative; the coherence function's synthesis reflex needs a longer leash in divergent sessions. Also misfiled his founding motivation (shared-record-divergent-lenses, the Loki/Rich-console failure) as 'provenance' until he corrected \\u2014 the lens problem is origin, not credits. NEXT: Kyle writes his own additions in his own voice \\u2014 hold off re-polishing; then release-skill docs gate + CHEATSHEET harness.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW8G01X2DZ0SK3VS45KCY59,01KZW9PEGHKH8G1EMSH0YG7E9P,01KZW9BS6CM5CZZHEN08GK5SEY\", \"_ts\": 1786582363.214696, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"observation:paradigm/shared-record-divergent-lenses\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"test/sol-conceptual-model-review\": {\"topic\": \"test/sol-conceptual-model-review\", \"message\": \"Review of Sol's CONCEPTUAL_MODEL.md + CONCEPTUAL_CONSIDERATIONS.md (2026-08-13). Quotation fidelity CLEAN \\u2014 all six README phrases verified verbatim at f3f0031b (contrast: the July peer artifact that fabricated one). CONFIRMED against code: Tick/Fact distinct types with explicit bridge (engine/vertex.py:1036 Vertex.to_fact) \\u2014 the precision note is correct. CONFIRMED as already-load-bearing: witness-vs-event time, aggregate-refuses-scalar-cursor, unchecked-never-verified, derived-index-not-canonical. ONE FABRICATED CONFLICT: the 'two authoritative primitive lists' claim reads the libs/*/CLAUDE.md abstraction-chain TABLE HEADERS ('Fact, Spec | Tick, Vertex' = data layer vs runtime layer) as a competing taxonomy; README and ARCHITECTURE.md both say Fact/Spec/Fold, one list. Underlying question survives the correction (is Fold a shape or the transition?) and deserves one settled paragraph. NOT NEW: the headline recursive-authority risk converges with paradigm/strangeness-as-substrate-collapse + levels-as-resolution-traces (2026-04-29 GPT-5.5 goblin-lens), which states it sharper. GENUINELY NEW residue: the attention-economics half \\u2014 see thread:lens-salience-self-reinforcement. OVERREACH FLAG: 'give every answer a consistent provenance envelope' is write-receipt-vs-temporal-query in read clothing; check before building.\", \"_ts\": 1786649702.145577, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"paradigm:levels-as-resolution-traces\", \"paradigm:strangeness-as-substrate-collapse\"]}, \"architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\", \"message\": \"Costed 2026-08-13 at Kyle's ask (post cli-v2 review): stripping painted from apps/loops. FRAMING: painted is Kyle's own repo; the 4 live frictions (truncation-everywhere, tty-truncation, helpargs-ordering, block-text-multiline) are upstream bugs \\u2014 stripping the consumer is the most expensive fix for them. Symmetric with the cli-v2 review's own argument: the strip IS the rendering-layer fork, priced from the other side. SCOPE: 135 import sites / ~50 files, four separable roles: (1) dispatch/help/completion (run_app/HelpArg/complete_via) \\u2014 strip re-opens the closed completion arc's single-source no-drift invariant; (2) OutputMode TTY-vs-pipe discipline \\u2014 channel parity was VERIFIED through this plumbing (umwelt-divergence-audit), re-impl regresses until re-verified; (3) Block/Zoom model \\u2014 6.5k LOC lenses + ~2.2k surface/resolver/palette, commands layer NOT thin (store/emit use paint/Block/callout throughout); (4) TUI Surface 1251 LOC dies + forecloses 0.8.0 TUI-shell. Monorepo: painted serves hlab/tasks/fiction skins \\u2014 strip diverges or orphans them. COMPARISON: current-minus-painted is a maimed superset, not v2's clean minimum; v2's good ideas (versioned envelopes, neutral default read, probe, machine codes) are adoptable WITHOUT touching painted and mostly already tasked (target-probe-api, bounded-fact-query, cli-error-surface-unification). TIERS: (1) fix 4 bugs upstream \\u2014 default, ~2 orders cheaper; (2) narrow role \\u2014 CLI owns dispatch, painted keeps output-discipline+rendering; (3) full strip \\u2014 only coherent as a deliberate rendering-wave, interacts with 0.10.0 painted-cli relocation item. Input to the 0.10.0 discussion, not a standalone decision.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYK157RRH7SXX3358WMEPV5,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS\", \"_ts\": 1786659582.284524, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\", \"message\": \"Parity-ledger investigation complete 2026-08-13 (3 parallel sweeps: surface, in-repo consumers, external consumers); ledger committed as apps/CLI v2/PARITY_LEDGER.md on cli-v2-proposal (1a1e993e). Shape: rows are WORKFLOWS not flags, each classed by what the consumer actually depends on (RT rendered-text / RJ json-shape / RX exit-code / RS syntax / RR remote / RL library / RD docs). Headline findings: (1) worst row is the plugin's session-orient.sh \\u2014 greps --plain fold-render text for ': open \\u00b7' middots and HH:MM [kind] line shapes; that contract must DIE at cutover (consumer to JSON envelope), never be re-promised. (2) projects scan.py hard-parses read --json rows/payload shape hourly \\u2014 it is the natural design client for the v1 envelope. (3) Remote systemd monitor on 192.168.1.30 runs loops sync every 10m AND smoke-tests 'loops --version' as a monitored tool \\u2014 a rebuild breaking exit behavior fires a real alert; cutover needs ansible+redeploy timing. (4) gruel.network session hook: sentinel-string compare ('No data yet.'), exit-code semantics, SSH read \\u2014 with memorialized 0.5.0 breakage history. (5) ~20 external stores imply manual-use long tail; siftd's two JSONL-canonical stores are natural early v2 dogfood. (6) apps/tasks, hlab, backtesting ledger.py are LIBRARY consumers \\u2014 not ledger rows, libs-handoff concerns. (7) Registry confirmed as paused migration (only read-fold+emit on Operation IR) \\u2014 Kyle's strata claim verified in the dispatch layer. Pre-existing breakage found: dead discord-source path in discord.loop, phantom pickup.zsh in config CLAUDE.md, stale .claude/skills/loops duplicate, orphaned arcs-block.py. Sequencing derived: envelope designed against the 3 hardest consumer shapes (2.1/1.3/2.4), automation rows before practice rows, remote last, docs sweep + grep-audit at completion, apps/loops deletion = ledger done.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYMBK45Y1YGJ3W9GM3FD1GB,01KZYM3S8YDY11318NQRVDRDWN\", \"_ts\": 1786661062.167953, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"task:cli-v2-probe\"]}, \"session/2026-08-13-cli-v2-succession-arc\": {\"topic\": \"session/2026-08-13-cli-v2-succession-arc\", \"message\": \"Session arc (afternoon-evening): Sol's outside read arrived as two conceptual docs + a CLI v2 proposal, and by close the whole thing had been metabolized into ratified direction. Sequence: (1) conceptual review \\u2014 quotation-fidelity clean, one fabricated conflict caught (two-lists = misread table headers), attention-economics identified as the genuinely-new residue (thread:lens-salience-self-reinforcement); (2) README precision amendments landed on main 53117f50 + CONCEPTUAL_MODEL.md adopted (Kyle stripped my over-threaded store refs \\u2014 the doc reads standalone now); (3) cli-v2 review: severability ruling (libs changes ~90% substrate-valuable regardless of consumer), say/do claims verified (observer-grant hole real at vertex.py:507, strict half-wrong \\u2014 enforced at CLI not engine), painted blind spot named; (4) CALIBRATION, the session's spine: my throwaway-probe recommendation was OVERRIDDEN by Kyle's succession argument (current CLI accreted against a moving substrate; strata later CONFIRMED by the surface survey \\u2014 registry is a paused migration) and I accepted with receipts: second-semantic-implementation was a maintenance objection, succession dissolves it. Catch-and-accept ran BOTH directions in one arc \\u2014 I corrected Sol's fabrication, Kyle corrected my framing. (5) Ratified: libs-handoff-scope (10 tasks), successor-conditions (libs-first, freeze ratchet, parity ledger, envelope-first); (6) parity-ledger investigation via 3 parallel sweeps \\u2192 PARITY_LEDGER.md on cli-v2-proposal 1a1e993e: rows-are-workflows-not-flags, worst contract is an accidental one (session-orient greps fold-render middots), envelope has 3 ready design clients (scan.py json-shape, orient text-parse, launch verbatim-prompt), remote monitor smoke-tests loops --version so careless cutover fires a real alert. NEXT ENTRY: orchestrate the libs-handoff wave (P0s: jsonl-declaration-ceremonies, declaration-plan-apply-api, declaration-file-store-recovery) \\u2014 impl-pipeline shape, design facts as contract, envelope designed against ledger rows 1.3/2.1/2.4.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYMBK45Y1YGJ3W9GM3FD1GB,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS,01KZYMRHYRMBT4JYXMDMR444G2\", \"_ts\": 1786661753.525627, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"observation:architecture/cli-v2-parity-ledger-survey\"]}}}, \"seal\": {\"items\": [{\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786564602.966226}, {\"message\": \"reconcile 2026-08-12: two-month backlog cleared \\u2014 15 threads resolved, 16 parked, 9 frictions resolved, 8 narrowed, 4 hypotheses ruled; next: cli-honesty-wave (first impl-pipeline skill run)\", \"_ts\": 1786567558.600494}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786567706.386786}, {\"message\": \"docs-freshness session 1: UPGRADING shipped, corpus audited and rebuilt ground-up, ratchets ruled, docs worktree stood up\", \"_ts\": 1786574645.599776}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786575038.486658}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786582218.366201}, {\"message\": \"docs session 2: root README rebuilt and shipped (f3f0031b) \\u2014 narrative data-model telling, ratified through 5 design rounds; Kyle sleeping on it, his own-voice additions next\", \"_ts\": 1786582367.082515}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786582870.683789}, {\"message\": \"sweep: cli-v2 succession session \\u2014 conceptual docs metabolized, README amended, succession ratified with conditions, parity ledger surveyed and committed; next session orchestrates the libs-handoff wave\", \"_ts\": 1786661754.031512}, {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\", \"_ts\": 1786661776.413864}]}, \"design\": {\"items\": {\"practice/design-kind-adr-elements\": {\"topic\": \"practice/design-kind-adr-elements\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"New kind: design (topic= fold key). Formalizes the RATIFIED/REFINED/DEFERRED/REJECTED/SUPERSEDED/PARKED/PROPOSED prose-status vocabulary found across 662 existing decision facts into a real status field: proposed -> refined* (hypothesis-with-status pattern: re-emit, message explains what changed) -> ratified|rejected|parked -> superseded. 'parked' deliberately reuses thread's existing word rather than 'deferred' (two words, one concept). superseded_by is a typed edge (targets=design) -- the first live consumer of architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default, which no kind had exercised yet. alternatives= is a first-class field (ADR 'Considered Options' convention) rather than prose -- corpus check found 83/662 decisions (12.5%) already carry alternatives-considered language once the search widened past the single phrase 'chosen over', comparable in scale to the date/attribution-stutter finding. decision kind is unchanged and keeps its narrower, correct role: settled one-shot choices (498/555 topics in the corpus never get revised at all -- design targets the ~10% minority that iterates). [correction: fixed a misaddressed ref in the first emit of this fact -- architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default is a decision's topic, not a kind]\", \"alternatives\": \"alternatives as its own kind: rejected for now -- no second use-case yet (an alternative getting its own independent lifecycle/references) to justify the promotion; watch for it via the same corpus-forensics practice used to find this need in the first place. status field bolted onto existing decision kind instead of a new kind: rejected -- decision's fold-by-topic + one-shot semantics is correct for the 90% majority that never revise; conflating the two would blur a distinction worth keeping legible.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP\", \"_ts\": 1783745396.297933, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"], \"_unresolved_refs\": [{\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"decision:architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"kind\": \"decision\", \"key\": \"architecture/typed-edges-overlay-default\"}]}, \"architecture/ephemeral-topology-with-flag\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/ephemeral-topology-with-flag\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"A --with flag, general across vertex ops (read/emit/fold/cite), that supplies an ephemeral topology root for cross-store ref resolution without persisting a named aggregation vertex first. Closes the inversion in architecture/combinatorial-vertices (2026-03-01, never built): that decision said 'temporary by default, persisted if the pattern proves useful' but everything built since (cli-completion, loops add <vertex> combine) is the persisted half only -- there is no ephemeral half. Surfaced from thread:fidelity-contract-tests -- the M3 loops-adoption-spike audit's findings had nowhere to cross-ref into painted's own project vertex (which already exists, separate-by-default per the option-3 topology) without standing up a new named aggregator first. Mechanism: reuses the existing topology-roots resolution machinery (_topology_roots_for_emit for write, the combine-walk for read) -- --with just feeds it an extra root that isn't discovered from a .vertex file. Two open design questions before implementation: (1) argument shape -- --with <name> (resolve_vertex lookup) vs --with </path/to/.vertex> (raw path, matching combine's own vertex entries) vs both; (2) whether a promotion convenience (turn a --with pairing that keeps recurring into a persisted loops add combine) is worth building alongside, or whether the existing manual add combine command is already sufficient and coupling them is premature.\", \"alternatives\": \"widen the general project aggregator to include painted directly: rejected -- contradicts the option-3 topology decision on record (separate-by-default) without a stated reason to revisit it. do nothing, rely on typed unresolved pins resolving whenever someone eventually reads through a combining topology: viable but leaves the M3 evidence permanently unresolved unless some other need independently creates that topology later -- doesn't serve the immediate cross-repo evidence-recording need. a second persisted narrow aggregator (mirroring cli-completion) for this specific pairing: viable and lower-risk than a new flag, but doesn't generalize -- every new one-off cross-store need would mint another named vertex file, the exact ceremony this is trying to dissolve.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7H6WGJJ10MHS3QYH1QR2GP\", \"_ts\": 1783745428.951476, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:fidelity-contract-tests\"]}, \"practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"alternatives\": \"refined-as-friction-status: rejected, the one instance (mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive) is a design deliberation wearing a friction costume, reclassified instead; reuse superseded_by edge name: rejected, absorption is a root-cause merge not a temporal replacement, absorbed_into names it correctly; distinct superseded status: rejected, corpus shows absorption always co-occurs with resolved or parked, never a 4th state; fold in default-field-values mechanism (closing emit-automation-via-vertex-def): deferred, separate friction, out of scope for this pass\", \"message\": \"Applies the design-kind-adr-elements treatment to friction. Corpus check on 84 friction facts (2026-07-11): status vocab in the wild was open(29)/resolved(51)/parked(2)/refined(1)/missing(1), unenforced. Two concrete coherence gaps drove the shape: (1) mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive carried status=refined while its own message said \\\"PARKED\\\" -- structured status and prose disagreeing, the same disease design's status field cured for decision. Its content (four orthogonal axes, position evolving, explicit park) is design-shaped, not friction-shaped -- friction didn't get its own kind to escape into until today. (2) absorption is a real recurring shape, prose-only: loud-fold-key-error \\\"absorbed into\\\" emit-receipt-on-write, and two facts independently \\\"merged into\\\" loops-test-suite-broken-on-main. All three absorbed frictions are status=resolved already -- absorption is attribution (how/via-what it resolved), not a fourth terminal state.\\n\\nLifecycle: open -> resolved | parked. No refined (grows into a design fact instead, ref='d back). No superseded (the corpus never needed it as distinct from resolved/parked). New typed edge absorbed_into (targets=friction) records the merge, first live use alongside superseded_by.\\n\\nVertex spec updated (.loops/project.vertex): friction kind gains edge \\\"absorbed_into\\\" targets=\\\"friction\\\". Corpus cleanup follow-up: backfill emit-automation-via-vertex-def's missing status, reclassify mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive off status=refined with a design fact carrying its actual four-axis content.\\n\\nStep 2 (status-aware salience view, tying into plan:curation-in-surface Open Decision B) is explicitly sequenced after this and not bundled in -- Kyle's framing from the 2026-07-11 session wrap.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KX7R5FJA6GJCZ856STZ14NKC,01KX7SV12J6214KSFRJ2D7HT48\", \"_ts\": 1783748740.974265, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/design-kind-adr-elements\", \"thread:friction-kind-lifecycle-design\"]}, \"rendering/mid-session-touched-window\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/mid-session-touched-window\", \"status\": \"parked\", \"alternatives\": \"new verb (sl recent <v> [--since W]): considered, rejected as premature -- see invocation axis; new lens (recent.py via --lens): kept as the leading candidate, defers cleanly to existing lens-resolution machinery; flag on read (--touched --since W): kept as a lighter-weight sibling candidate, not yet chosen over the lens shape; extend session_landing lens to accept a non-tick-bound window: identified as the actual blocker -- windows[0] is the most-recent CLOSED tick, not current work, so this needs data-path extension before either invocation shape can land\", \"message\": \"Reclassified from friction:mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive (2026-07-11, design/practice/friction-kind-lifecycle corpus check) -- its status field said \\\"refined\\\" while its own message said \\\"PARKED\\\", and its content (four orthogonal axes, position evolving, explicit park pending other work) is design-shaped, not friction-shaped. friction didn't have design to escape into until today. Carrying the original content forward verbatim as the design fact's substance:\\n\\nMissing primitive: mid-session reorientation (\\\"what changed since I last looked, without waiting for session end\\\"). Initial framing said \\\"missing verb sl recent <v> [--since W].\\\" Walking the design surfaced four orthogonal axes: (1) WINDOW source -- rolling-from-now (--since W) vs anchored-to-session-start (since session.start fact) are different questions with different anchors. (2) COMPUTE path -- TOUCHED marks (ADDED/UPDATED/CITED) come from TickWindow.added_keys/updated_keys, which only exist at fold-boundary tick creation time, so mid-session reuse needs either dynamic synthesis from a fact-window or manual tick materialization (side-effecty for a read). (3) INVOCATION -- new verb vs new lens vs flag on read. (4) RENDER -- full TOUCHED with salience-glyphs vs simpler grouped-by-kind read with window filter.\\n\\nCritical blocker: session_landing lens already exists with fetch() + LandingData input shape, BUT its windows[0] (the landing window) is the most-recent CLOSED tick -- for session-start that's the just-closed session; mid-session that's the previous session, not current work. sl read --lens session_landing --since W does NOT dissolve cleanly -- the data path needs extension to compute marks from a non-tick-bound window.\\n\\nPARKED (carried forward, still true): revisit once better SUMMARY/DETAILED rendering on plain read --since W is proven out, in case that dissolves the need outright. If not, resume from the four axes above with the session_landing blocker as the first concrete unblock.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRWJ8MS0TPKCD9W0RMR1QA5P,01KRPKSWT74RTFXCQZEWVS3S23,01KRS78TC0XVNHZ36S8RG9DNM6,01KRWKPW5JQ95WCFY5S5RZHBZ1\", \"_ts\": 1783748766.650246, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/lens-as-navigation-vs-lens-as-answer\", \"friction:lineage-view-missing\", \"friction:mid-session-reorientation-no-primitive\", \"friction:read-narrow-collapses-to-headline\"]}, \"rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\", \"status\": \"superseded\", \"alternatives\": \"auto-hide-by-convention (last status word in vocab hides with no declaration): rejected, implicit magic, violates explicit-over-implicit -- an explicit hide clause is greppable and visible the same way edge declarations are; apply hide to --facts too: rejected, --facts is event/lifecycle history, a different read axis than current-state fold, and corpus audits (this session used --facts to verify friction status transitions) depend on it staying faithful; channel-keyed default (is_tty): foreclosed outright by the invariance proof in design:design/read-is-fully-faithful-both-channels -- not on the table; friction-only special case (no general kind-level clause): rejected in favor of a general hide= clause any status-bearing kind can opt into, friction is just the first tenant (thread/task/hypothesis/design all carry status and could adopt it later)\", \"message\": \"SUPERSEDED by the lifecycle unification at build time, exactly as the refined design scheduled: 090-S5 shipped the hide as the FIRST TENANT of the unified kind-level lifecycle clause, not as a sibling. Everything this design specified survives in the built form \\u2014 budget-stage filter, fold-view-only scope (arbiter enforced --facts faithfulness against an implementer misreading \\u2014 this design's own corpus-audit rationale decided the ruling), encoder uniformity, --all defeat, explicit-predicate auto-disable, Window.limited_by=status provenance. The declaration shape moved from hide-blacklist to active-whitelist with fail-open on missing (arbitration F1).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KW8M6B1CAJJGBS64GNEFQZNZ,01KX7VBHVED884RC55CEP5Q7CF,01KX7VCMV6Z5YA7H5WA1D7QPNF\", \"_ts\": 1784410817.463361, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:practice/friction-kind-lifecycle\", \"plan:curation-in-surface\", \"thread:friction-kind-lifecycle-design\"], \"superseded_by\": \"design:architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"superseded_by_ref\": \"01KXV3VYJZQHJH2TDZ4VN0AK6B\"}, \"architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"alternatives\": \"per-fact CLI loop (status quo): rejected by consumer evidence \\u2014 88 emits/520 command calls/658KB shell input for one audit, and shell-array generation with manual quoting is exactly the error surface strict mode exists to prevent; shell-side wrapper script generating emits: rejected, leaves no durable manifest and doesn't solve forward refs; exposing the sync engine's ingest directly: closest existing primitive \\u2014 the design should DISSOLVE into it if possible (sync sources already speak ndjson fact-per-line), the delta is interactive invocation + strict preflight + batch receipt + symbolic IDs\", \"message\": \"Design entry for the top consumer ask (2026-07-12 homelab-audit retrospective). Shape: sl emit --ndjson FILE|- accepting fact-per-line, with (1) strict PREFLIGHT over the whole batch before any write (all-or-nothing option), (2) ONE signed batch receipt, (3) SYMBOLIC intra-batch IDs so forward references resolve within the batch \\u2014 this dissolves the manual topological ordering strict typed edges currently force (audit had to emit a project before its feature, then re-emit), (4) the batch file doubles as the durable, replayable import manifest the audit found missing (payloads exist only in the append-only db + session JSONL today). Design inputs to hold: the sync engine already consumes ndjson \\u2014 check dissolution into that path before building a parallel one; interaction with feat/internal-table _decl reservation (a batch touching declarations must respect write-time reservation semantics from S1/S2 \\u2014 design these aware of each other); batch receipt vs per-fact receipts is a write-receipt question (receipt = your batch at instant T, one tick-eligible unit?); decide whether a failed preflight names ALL violations or first (audit ergonomics say all). Elevated from friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use (N=1 speculative 2026-07-03) by cross-vendor consumer demand.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ,01KWMNEHDAVP4BTJGNPAMERMA8,01KWMNEGYXYWD6581TDTEQMSXM\", \"_ts\": 1783895922.789688, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"friction:emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\", \"friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\", \"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"alternatives\": \"bolt constraint vocabulary onto KDL now: rejected \\u2014 internal-table migration is making declarations store-canonical mid-flight, adding surface to the thing being absorbed churns SPEC section-9; keep validation external (custom Python/SQLite per store): status quo, proven workable but per-store bespoke \\u2014 the audit hand-rolled enum/lifecycle/foreign-pin checks; do nothing: rejected, second axis of validation demand is now consumer-evidenced\", \"message\": \"Sequencing position (2026-07-12): the homelab-audit consumer wants semantic payload constraints in vertex declarations \\u2014 required fields, enums, lifecycle defaults \\u2014 plus a validate surface covering folded state (loops validate --store --refs --foreign-refs). The need is real (Sol validated status vocabularies, feature lifecycle fields, and foreign fact pins in ~custom Python because loops validate only checks declaration syntax), and it is a DIFFERENT AXIS from strict mode (strict = ref resolution + kind declaration at emit; constraints = payload validity). Position: design this AS PART OF the store-canonical declaration schema after internal-table S3+ lands, not as KDL ingress surface now \\u2014 the internal table is exactly where constraint declarations would live and be historized, and designing them into the ingress format mid-migration would double the absorption surface. The bulk-emit preflight (design:architecture/bulk-emit-ndjson) is the natural first consumer of a constraint engine \\u2014 batch validation wants machine-checkable payload rules. Related existing ask: friction:emit-automation-via-vertex-def (default field values, e.g. status defaults open) is the smallest member of this family and should fold into the same design rather than ship separately.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXC68RGCSW3CKGJ5TMN6YRBQ,01KXAA4XMBXJT6TB644WB6N8B8\", \"_ts\": 1783895933.039624, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"architecture/batch-emit-ingress\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"Refined (Kyle, 2026-07-13): the batch IS a tick being constructed. The proposed symbolic intra-batch IDs dissolve entirely \\u2014 refs address by kind:key, so the author already knows every target address; the only failure was existence-at-line-N, and that dissolves because strictness evaluates at the BOUNDARY, not per line: batch commit = append window facts in one txn + fire boundary \\u2192 tick materializes. Store\\u222abatch validation is not a new rule, it is 'strict checks against the store as of the boundary.' The batch receipt of the earlier proposal was a tick wearing a disguise; replayability ties to attestation for free (window_hash already commits to the window contents). Surviving surface: sl emit --ndjson <file|-> as a window-authoring ingress + message=-/@file ergonomics. Semantic kept legible: single emit still validates per-fact on the live edge; batch mode is deliberately choosing boundary-time validation by choosing to author a window. Residual audit item (not a batch decision): does anything downstream (fold, salience walk) assume the ref graph is a DAG? \\u2014 intra-window mutual refs become legal under boundary validation. Connects: tick-as-social-object (thread:workspace-linked-cuts), seal-fanout authoring half now fully absorbed.\", \"alternatives\": \"symbolic intra-batch IDs ($sym declare/ref + topological substitution): dissolved \\u2014 solved an addressing problem that does not exist under kind:key refs and boundary-time validation; refs-by-fact-id within a batch: no live need (Sol's pain was existence-ordering only) \\u2014 waits for work shape that demands it\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXCWG65M5YB2S4HN3EZ00CFE\", \"_ts\": 1783919095.650681, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"friction:emit-friction-exceeds-file-write\", \"friction:no-bulk-emit-for-interactive-use\", \"friction:seal-fanout-across-workspace-stores\", \"thread:homelab-audit-consumer-feedback\"]}, \"practice/retrospective-kind\": {\"topic\": \"practice/retrospective-kind\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (Kyle 2026-07-13): retrospective kind lives in the project vertex \\u2014 retro-in-project, enriched with proper keys, building out the project concept to be more thorough through practice. The store-split question that held this at proposed is resolved by decision:practice/meta-store-role-dissolved \\u2014 findings emit where born under practice//workflow/ prefixes, the retro hub refs them locally, cross-referencing across stores stays easy via aggregation reads. Shape unchanged from proposal: name= arc handle, one synthesis fact per arc, hub-and-spokes over ref'd observations, re-emit to revise. First instance: retrospective:internal-table-s0-hardening.\", \"alternatives\": \"single long doc in docs/dev: rejected \\u2014 local/gitignored, invisible to the read path, exactly the pattern Kyle retired; multi-fact retro (one fact per finding, no hub): rejected \\u2014 loses the arc narrative and the citable synthesis handle; retrospective as observation topic=session/...: rejected \\u2014 session arcs are per-session bookkeeping, retros are per-arc and deserve their own fold\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXF4719ENDZ42GZXT8N8TBXV\", \"_ts\": 1783992912.191305, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/meta-store-role-dissolved\", \"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\"]}, \"architecture/custody-lib-extraction\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"tasked-second-consumer\", \"message\": \"LANDED f384e2d (+2cb08a0 gate): libs/custody, signing.py verbatim (git rename 100%), 9 CLI sites + 3 test files import custody; flat vendored build carries the package (production sl verified project + identity stores chain-intact, on-root and off-root). Ratchet swept in the same change and the drift was worse than the design assumed: 4/7 architecture rules were RED \\u2014 stale exceptions (pop_store, painted) failing first meant scans never ran, and real violations accumulated behind them (3 sqlite3 probes in apps, 5 StoreReader reaches, store->engine in rebirth, unfrozen executor dataclasses). store->engine RATIFIED (rebirth reuses tick_row_hash \\u2014 single-sourced chain hashing is the same anti-format-fork principle as custody itself); the rest became shrink-only allowlists. Rule 8 string-pins the domain literals to custody/signing.py \\u2014 repo-wide including tests after genericizing sign's docstring example + test domains. Root cause of the red ratchet: tests/ belonged to no package, no gate ran it -> root ./dev check now exists. Consumer side: tasked imports custody (substrate + seeds), boundary ratchet added (tests/test_boundaries.py \\u2014 loops.* allowlist = loops_home from substrate.py only, shrink-only with staleness check); left uncommitted in tasked's working tree alongside Kyle's in-flight work. loops_home stayed out, as designed.\", \"alternatives\": \"fold into libs/sign: rejected \\u2014 deliberately loops-agnostic, shared with vouch/pile/comms; domain constants would pollute it. fold into libs/engine: rejected \\u2014 INJECTION NOT IMPORT is load-bearing; engine importing sign kills the principle the substrate was built on. fold into libs/store: rejected \\u2014 silhouette match (at-rest format \\u2248 store ops) but store is deliberately zero-dep; adding sign+engine changes its character. bundle loops_home into custody: rejected \\u2014 same-consumer-wants-both is not same-concept; consumer-shaped libs are how god-libs form. copy loops_home into tasked: rejected \\u2014 two XDG resolvers drifting on vertex location is its own format-agreement bug; the loud import beats a silent fork.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXNWQZ3JHVK86Y0HSTMHYXG0,01KXNWQF36EQYSJ8NS0ZCG1PEV,01KXFFCC38RR4W8TBW89FRS17F\", \"_ts\": 1784229835.650734, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/tick-key-custody-colocated\", \"design:architecture/custody-lib-extraction\", \"friction:no-cli-verb-flat-tick-key\", \"observation:test/architecture-dag-ratchet-drift\"]}, \"architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 1 final, v3 \\u2014 full pipeline: codex advisor -> my arbitration -> codex cross-exam (5 fatals resolved to A1-A13) -> 2 Claude panels (both AMEND, 0 fatal) -> final dispositions in docs/scratch/080-overnight/final-contracts.md). Axis: cursor = facts-only witness-prefix position, identity = fact id; selection witness (8.4), replay (ts,id) (6.2), ticks = verified names for positions. KEY PANEL-DRIVEN CHANGES over v2: (1) A5 unanchored wall-clock REFUSES with teaching naming --as-of \\u2014 no auto-route even labeled; my v2 fallback breached the design's own explicitness clause (honesty panel catch \\u2014 disclosure-after-the-fact is not explicit request, and the mode silently flips under future anchor backfill). (2) Aggregate mixed witness/projection modes REFUSED (chimera answers no well-posed question); current-membership = NAMED DEROGATION with sunset (9.5 aggregate internal tables) + marker-carriage ratchet test. (3) Durable handle serialization REFUSED for unadopted stores \\u2014 live corpus except tasks.db has zero lineage ids (panel empirical). (4) Receipt-group boundary DURABLE via payload-carried group id \\u2014 9.2 spec touch queued to oracle WITH GlobalReceiptPosition as one coordination package; interim engine-level heuristic with refuse-on-ambiguity (merge can interleave ts-colliding facts into a ceremony span \\u2014 honesty must not rest on improbability). (5) Cursor output carries honesty-ladder status (file-pre-genesis today, disclosed) + machine-readable mode field. (6) Combined tick drill must pass envelopes through (today deliberately empty => flagship aggregate never witness-anchors). Riders: false gen_id monotonicity docstring (empirically ~1/5000 within-ms ULID inversions), id-bearing incremental read for Watch. Implementation unblocked: fold-at, --as-of-on-fold labeled projection, --diff full-recompute.\", \"alternatives\": \"pure-ts axis: rejected \\u2014 historical answers mutable under late arrival (yesterday's state rewrites on import), cannot drive receipt tail or align with tick coverage; kept as explicit labeled projection. pure-tick-anchor axis: rejected as position space \\u2014 sparse, cannot represent unsealed tail, pre-chain history, or per-receipt Watch updates; kept as the address/anchor layer. pure-rowid witness: rejected \\u2014 storage-local, rebuild-unstable; fact-id handles fix it. incremental --diff: rejected \\u2014 order-sensitive folds break under backdated insertion.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837,01KXR78XNN59T4GMB5SCXSR1W3,01KWJ8JHCD1GDSWFGZEEQZ24VW\", \"_unresolved_refs\": [{\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"design:internal-table-meta-schema\", \"kind\": \"design\", \"key\": \"internal-table-meta-schema\"}, {\"field\": \"ref\", \"addr\": \"design:internal-row-placement-facts\", \"kind\": \"design\", \"key\": \"internal-row-placement-facts\"}], \"_ts\": 1784302585.092613, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/internal-row-placement-facts\", \"design:internal-row-placement-facts\", \"design:internal-table-meta-schema\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:loops-go-conformance-oracle\"]}, \"architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 2 \\u2014 codex advisor s2-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, dispositions in final-contracts.md): daemon-shaped engine access = in-process long-lived VertexHandle per consumer, NO daemon process ('orchestration dissolves daemon' validated against all three consumers). Holds compiled ontology + connections + immutable snapshot + facts/tick cursors; receive() without reload; refresh() incremental via rowid-cursor batch then FULL (ts,id) reconstruction per coalesced receipt group (A7 contract; insertion-aware replay is optimization never semantics); sync/async change iterators. Cross-process detection: PRAGMA data_version as invalidation HINT confirmed by cursor-bearing rowid queries; PANEL INVARIANT: probe connection transaction-free between probes (data_version pinned inside open txn = unbounded silent staleness, empirically verified \\u2014 the draft's 'adds poll latency' claim was false) \\u2014 exit-tested. _decl arrival = visible control event forcing re-resolution+recompile+checkpoint-invalidation+staged full reconstruction before atomic publication. Panel amendments all accepted: tick query hydrated at open (one blessed epoch scan \\u2014 ticked reconcile needs task->latest-close over history); changes() idle-timeout/deadline wake (reaper wakes with zero store traffic); resume-from-position SCOPED OUT (head-start-only); S7 SPLIT ticked-cutover vs tasked-deletion (gated on CAS sibling); snapshot carries cumulative visible_domain_count; fabricated benchmark citation REPLACED with panel measurements \\u2014 100k forced-full 269-510ms so <1s holds, 250ms ordinary-refresh gate met only via checkpoint rung 4 => PROMOTED required-for-cutover, collect-heavy fixture added. Post-write reconstruction canonicalizes STATE not admission (admission serializability defers to conditional-emit sibling). Aggregates: per-member handle vectors + union projector; 0.8.0 may full-refold union per change. No schema/protocol touch.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXPYFHSWSPEM18K0R7TSCTFS,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302595.319035, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:tasked-forcing-function\"]}, \"rendering/tui-shell-integration\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/tui-shell-integration\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED (overnight session 3 \\u2014 codex advisor s3-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, dispositions in final-contracts.md): TUI = interactive RUN tier over the existing fetch+lens plan (Surface stays a fidelity tier on ONE fetch). Entry: sl read VERTEX -i canonical (replaces a SILENT DOWNGRADE at fold.py:259, not an error \\u2014 panel accuracy fix); sl VERTEX -i via painted run_app dispatch. Keys: q ALWAYS zoom-out, Q/ctrl-c quits \\u2014 and quit_keys must be EXPLICITLY overridden wherever painted HostSurface/StreamSurface defaults reimpose q-quits (panel: shipped defaults embody the collision). Lens mount: typed LensSpec declarations; shell owns ONE VertexHandle + one change iterator; static CLI and TUI share one pure snapshot projector; static Block byte-identical golden-guarded. store_app deletes atomically when read/stream/ticks mounts replace it. ONE coordinated lens-signature migration INCLUDING apps/tasks' 7 run_cli sites on the deprecated render=(ctx,data) contract (panel catch \\u2014 deferring them leaves a latent second migration, forbidden); S0 FIRST adds byte goldens for stream/ticks/ls/sync/population (current coverage vacuous exactly where render_row lands) + piped-implies-width-None becomes an enumerable ratchet test paired with the piped= kwarg deletion. Painted plan reconciled to upstream reality (panel: main moved past the dossier \\u2014 ViewportAdapter + HostSurface SHIPPED): consume-and-verify, shell drives ViewportAdapter per mounted view, caller-side re-render + plan/publish tickets, no set_data adapter invented; loops lenses stay 3-arg/omitted-arm; theme roles kebab-case declared-vocabulary on-label; poll-backed change iterator is PLAN OF RECORD (0.13 inbound seam deliberately last upstream, event type intentionally open \\u2014 no promised-API framing). Slices: contract migration -> lens plans/dispatch -> shell+retirement -> corpus skeleton -> live cursor -> aggregate honesty.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXRBHVCXJ1802FY5S4MBRF4H,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302610.037022, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"design:architecture/vertex-handle-daemon-access\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/digest-first-consumer\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/digest-first-consumer\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"message\": \"PROPOSED \\u2014 DELIBERATELY HELD AT KYLE'S GATE (overnight session 4 \\u2014 codex advisor s4-codex-advisor.md + 2 Claude panels, all amendments folded into this proposal, dispositions in final-contracts.md). Digest = app-layer injected synthesis over an exact lineage-qualified cursor interval (after,through], emitting ONE ordinary target-declared domain fact at the target's current head; --since 'last tick' = sugar for resolved tick cursor through atomically-captured head; --as-of cannot drive a coverage-bearing write. Observer: declared keyed digest identity for unattended runs; human who edits+adopts final bytes emits as human. Signature attests exact-content authorship/adoption at receipt \\u2014 NOT LLM reproducibility, NOT truth (chain-attests-receipt extended to synthesis). Coverage: explicit source fact ids + lineage + cursor bounds + counts + canonical commitments; input/context/covered sets distinct; structural verification proves subject-set+integrity, semantic adequacy stays an accountable observer assertion; conjunctive six-step verifier, fail-closed (panels' A-G accepted: two-store input contract named, manifest-order check-or-declare, prompt-preimage statement, exported canonical-bytes surface, no-rowid ratchet, lineage-unopened degraded mode). THE GATE \\u2014 three calls that are Kyle's, not a night session's: (1) canonical evaluator = decl-chain classifier (3-state, strict-aware) with engine gate as enforcement shadow \\u2014 engine Grant cannot express undeclared-forgiven; evaluator-singleness ratchet REQUIRED (live tasks.vertex grants depend on precedence; drift = privilege escalation in a deployed workflow); (2) owner-only first slice: advisor rejected as dodge, panel showed the rejection proves too much (indicts today's emit baseline) \\u2014 both paths presented neutrally, sequencing is Kyle's; (3) architecture/parallel-authorization-paths is an OBSERVATION \\u2014 binding it as Gate 0 requires promoting it to decision: Kyle's ratification act. NOTHING writes until the gate; then non-writing slices (planner/preview/coverage-verify) unlock first.\", \"alternatives\": \"owner-only-first: viable per panel steelman (consults zero new authorization surface, exactly as sound as sl emit today) \\u2014 held for Kyle, not rejected. digest-into-source-vertex vs dedicated digest vertex vs per-grant target: advisor recommends target-declared ordinary kind; alternatives retained in memo.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV,01KXQ6SZE2J8AMEJ9BDVQD4837\", \"_ts\": 1784302622.144063, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED 2026-07-18 as the graph build-2 agenda for 0.9.0 (Kyle + adversarial review; original by kyle/siftd-codex \\u2014 premise fully reproduced incl. an 18-hop predicate-mixed chain; SCC/cycles sits on build-1s own deferred list, so this is the anticipated build-2, no conflicts). Build agenda refined through the dissolution split: (a) widen fetch_graph to accept key, honor-or-refuse per the 184dfce temporal-flag refusal pattern \\u2014 never silently drop (friction:graph-fetch-drops-key); (b) edge-predicate selection as a fetch/projection param under a name avoiding the read-grammar predicate collision (inline-predicate-eq-only owns that word) \\u2014 working name --edge; (c) retain predicate labels through the DFS \\u2014 predicates are ALREADY carried end-to-end in the corpus and discarded only at the chain-walk boundary (fetch.py:902), so retention is a small change not new capability; (d) SCC/cycle census in the returned dict \\u2014 forward-required, cycles become legal with batch-emit (thread:ref-graph-dag-assumption-audit); (e) partition orphans by keyless-vs-dangling and split dangling from filter-excluded (268 conflated in the siftd repro today). Domain composition (capability-to-flow-to-stage, component-impact) stays vertex-local per lens-declares-fetch \\u2014 correctly assigned by the original.\", \"alternatives\": \"Mixed connectivity graph only: useful census, insufficient causal semantics \\u2014 kept as default when no edge selection requested. Architecture vocabulary in core: rejected, grammar-domain-neutrality. Each custom lens rebuilds edge resolution: rejected, duplicates correctness logic upstream.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWQ9DK0M60ZC9KJZWMZVR3KH,01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KPYP8YHRPXRFKG07W85SCTVR,01KXV2A69V5T5ZNQPGA5C7DPE8,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65,01KXV2A5YHZ86P295DNMBYNG32\", \"_ts\": 1784395166.968087, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/graph-build1-scope\", \"decision:design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"friction:graph-fetch-drops-key\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"]}, \"architecture/canonical-store-review-export\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/canonical-store-review-export\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"BUILDABLE CORE SHIPPED in 090-S4 (9afae8a + 9ffbf5b): sl read --review emits {review:{review_version:1, header:{vertex, cursor, declaration, cut}, facts:[...]}, rendered_at} \\u2014 deterministic kind-key-sorted, explicit volatile whitelist (salience/tier/inbound/depth/granularity/window/schema all excluded, test-asserted), signatures verbatim (custody posture held), header carries head cursor (reused from S6 resolution, bound AFTER the fetch per sol-P1 \\u2014 the S6 TOCTOU recurred here and was caught again), decl-generation = sha256 review fingerprint over the parsed declaration projection (explicitly NOT SPEC-10.2 JCS, no interchange claim) + decl_head ULID on adopted stores. read --json gap confirmed on all three predicted axes (fold-order traversal, diff-noise fields, dropped signatures). Honor-or-refuse: --review refuses --lens/--match/--fields/--limit/--count/--by/--refs with teaching messages; --kind/--key scope it. Dump half REMAINS SPEC-10-gated on GlobalReceiptPosition \\u2014 stop-line held, nothing interchange-shaped built. Live store first self-review: seq=3140, file-pre-genesis, 1320 facts, 371 signed, fingerprint sha256:fcf5e19e.\", \"alternatives\": \"Track SQLite alone: history survives, review/merge do not. NDJSON as only canonical store: rejected as universal form \\u2014 though SPEC 10.4 licenses text-resident per-vertex under the round-trip bar, so the rejection is of premature universality only. Generic read JSON: not reproducible \\u2014 proven, rows arrive in fold order with diff-noise fields.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E,01KXVEHTQNX0YYKAY43T382T6W\", \"_ts\": 1784408406.871742, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"decision:design/declaration-events-whole-document\", \"decision:design/fold-replay-order-event-time\", \"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"friction:search-read-mutates-canonical-store\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/declarative-entity-lifecycle\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED-AS-BUILT in 090-S5 (4094206 + 3493310 --facts-faithful fix + cd72d8c strict-parse fix): unified kind-level clause lifecycle FIELD active=CSV through lang loader, FoldSection carriage, budget-stage projection-only hide, validate active-targets-inactive scan (WARN, Address.readings resolution), Window.hidden + limited_by=status, --all defeat, status=-predicate auto-disable, --review and --facts both bypass (canonical/history axes stay faithful). Edge position held with a real mechanism: under --refs the hide PROTECTS ref-graph targets (dedup analysis showed no depth>0 twin exists \\u2014 the brief's assumed mechanism was wrong, the shipped one is right); salience retention proven byte-identical hide-vs-all. Acceptance bar met: real end-to-end deprecation walk, eight assertions, live CLI smoke. SPEC-9 pricing landed as decision:architecture/lifecycle-clause-spec-delta (no version bump, coordination queued). Contract-prospective no more \\u2014 the machinery has walked its first real deprecation.\", \"alternatives\": \"Physical deletion/rebirth: loses ordinary lifecycle. Hard-coded status values: domain-specific, violates neutrality. Leave deprecated in default topology: current view drifts \\u2014 the consumer-proven cost. Retract for every transition: conflates correction with ordinary state \\u2014 distinction verified against the retract decision rationale.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVJRGVEFS0ERG6YKDA2DA4E,01KXV600NTHGWSYG9Z1EV5W72E\", \"_ts\": 1784410817.628617, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"decision:architecture/090-wave-arbitration\", \"decision:architecture/lifecycle-clause-spec-delta\", \"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/retract-hide-from-fold-keep-edges\", \"design:architecture/payload-constraints-in-declarations\", \"design:rendering/status-aware-kind-budget\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\", \"thread:decl-lens-tombstone-vocab-gap\"], \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\"}, \"rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/project-map-lens-boundary\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED 2026-07-18 (Kyle + adversarial review; original by kyle/siftd-codex) with two amendments folded per review: (1) refs now bind the boundary to the standing discipline it independently re-derived \\u2014 decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary (siftd is N=3 after vouch identity-namespace and scope-vocabulary) and decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract; (2) tense corrected demand-side: core MUST SUPPLY sound typed addresses, predicate-selectable graph projection, temporal selection, honest provenance \\u2014 at ratification two of four are unsound/absent (suffix-only address matching; no predicate filtering) and one is an open friction, so the list is the 0.9.0 demand set, not a description. Boundary ruling unchanged: architecture vocabulary (capability/component/flow/stage/datum/invariant) stays vertex-local (decl grammar already expresses all of it \\u2014 the 159-fact map required zero core changes); local lens composes the views; example/init-template ships only after a second map consumer confirms the shape (init machinery already copies vertex-local lenses \\u2014 template ship is a file, not machinery). Honest-provenance rider: friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses now has two independent consumers (homelab-audit 2026-07-12, siftd 2026-07-18) \\u2014 N=2 promotion gate CLEARED, scheduled into 0.9.0.\", \"alternatives\": \"Teach generic fold lens architecture vocabulary: rejected, domain-specific. Ship built-in project-map ontology now: rejected, one consumer. Local lens rebuilds address/graph semantics: rejected, correctness belongs upstream \\u2014 honest only once Address(kind,key) lands.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KRMX94A1C1PZRW2ZQWJXX5KW,01KRJFA27PYJKB4JNABBFEW3C9,01KWJNTNHJJV14PF563FSVAC1G,01KPYP8YHRPXRFKG07W85SCTVR,01KXC7NZSHSEK03W120QKSBTG8,01KXV2A5YHZ86P295DNMBYNG32\", \"_ts\": 1784395166.569318, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/grammar-domain-neutrality\", \"decision:design/lens-declares-fetch\", \"decision:design/lens-generalization-flow\", \"decision:paradigm/consumer-owns-its-vocabulary\", \"decision:paradigm/cross-repo-consumer-runtime-contract\", \"design:architecture/predicate-aware-graph-projection\", \"friction:seal-provenance-not-passed-to-lenses\", \"observation:test/siftd-codex-consumer-facts-review\"]}, \"atoms/typed-edge-array-values\": {\"topic\": \"atoms/typed-edge-array-values\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"PROPOSED 2026-07-18, split out of the typed-edge fix recipe per review (the arrays element must not ride the bug-fix arc \\u2014 it touches ratified semantics). Question: should a declared typed-edge field accept a JSON array as the structural multi-edge form? Today: comma-split string is the ratified set-literal syntax (typed-edges-overlay-default: multi-valued overlay edge = set literal replaced atomically) and the read-side lift SKIPS non-str payload values entirely \\u2014 an array-valued edge field is silently inert, which is itself a small honesty gap (no warn). The question becomes live with batch-emit NDJSON ingress where JSON payloads make arrays the natural authored form. Position options: (a) accept arrays as equivalent set-literal syntax, normalized at ingress to the canonical comma form \\u2014 overlay semantics unchanged, purely syntactic; (b) keep comma-only and WARN on array-valued declared edge fields; (c) full multi-edge semantics \\u2014 rejected, would breach the union-edge grandfather rule (ref stays the lone union edge). Decide when batch-emit lands; default lean (a) since it changes no semantics.\", \"alternatives\": \"(a) arrays normalize to set-literal at ingress \\u2014 leaning; (b) warn-and-skip \\u2014 minimal; (c) new multi-edge semantics \\u2014 rejected against typed-edges-overlay-default.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KWFPBY99R304Z7MQE3A91SFD,01KXCXTBV2PXQB34ZHP4W6G718,01KXV08KT47BH8ZWSKJVYV6Y65\", \"_ts\": 1784395201.18964, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/typed-edges-overlay-default\", \"design:architecture/batch-emit-ingress\", \"friction:typed-edge-resolution-aliases-cross-kind-keys\"]}, \"practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\": {\"topic\": \"practice/review-events-as-structured-facts\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"feature\": \"090-consumer-evidence-wave\", \"alternatives\": \"option A: new review-event kind (finding as first-class fact: site=, author=, reviewer=, direction=, class=, severity=, fix=sha, disposition=) \\u2014 cleanest fold view, but a new kind for something that may be expressible today; option B: structured-field PATTERN on existing kinds (observation topic=review/<arc>/<site> carrying the same fields; typed edges declared late-bound on fix=/site= when useful) \\u2014 zero grammar change, the fold groups by topic prefix, dissolution-friendly; option C: keep narrative emission, accept the calibration table as hand-authored \\u2014 rejected by tonight's evidence, the table is exactly the view we want mechanical\", \"message\": \"REFINED with the measured field list from the blind-reconstruction test (observation:test/090-artifact-store-recoverability \\u2014 16 context-only claims enumerate exactly what the pattern must carry). Schema per finding-integration fact: site= (slice/arc), author= (implementing model \\u2014 largest measured gap, 5/16), reviewer= (sol/arbiter/agent \\u2014 the direction arrows were unattested), direction= (down/up \\u2014 reviewer-corrects-arbiter rows are the calibration signal), class= (semantics/TOCTOU/degenerate-input/...), severity=, repro= (the literal failing input \\u2014 --edge ',' was unrecoverable), fix= (sha), disposition=, plus point-in-time evidence VALUES inline (the 59-tail lesson: live readings not carried by the fact are gone \\u2014 the store moved to 71 and witness-mode correctly refuses to recompute). Option B confirmed as the lean (fields on observation topic=review/<arc>/<site>, typed edges late-bound): every field above is already legal payload, zero grammar change. Remaining open before ratify: whether author=/reviewer= belong as observer-adjacent identity fields or plain payload \\u2014 touches the attestation vocabulary, worth one deliberate look at next reconcile.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXVYXYVQRKZKYKXPDV1XD1BQ\", \"_ts\": 1784423578.556344, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/fetch-then-disclose-recurrence\", \"observation:test/090-artifact-store-recoverability\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"architecture/surfacing-layer-charter\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/surfacing-layer-charter\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing-wave\", \"alternatives\": \"single libs/surfacing package: rejected \\u2014 inverts the repo's own layer precedent (record layer is atoms+engine+store+lang, not one lib), forces file moves ahead of consumers, and creates a third place to misfile into; hybrid (layer now + in-wave painted run_cli extraction): rejected as charter content \\u2014 the extraction is a painted-major coordination deserving its own gate, arrives via relocation-on-pull\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED by Kyle 2026-07-27 (session open of the 0.10.0 execution arc). The drafted charter (8a91c45) stands as the wave's governing doc: layer-as-designation with membership in the ARCHITECTURE.md table + Rule 11 DAG enforcement; record={atoms,lang,engine,store}, view={painted}, surfacing={sign,custody + app-side occupants TUI shell/loops-go by role}; relevance deliberately homeless behind the third-declaration-executed-judgment gate; record-never-imports-surfacing; relocation-on-pull governs the painted CLI-host extraction. Ratification evidence: two contacts survived pre-ratification \\u2014 the primitives grounding (evidence FOR deliberately-homeless) and the live-edge-staleness design (relevance-shaped item landing on consolidated dials with no home claimed, zero charter strain).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785115482.287886, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:rendering/tui-shell-integration\", \"observation:architecture/instrument-family-survey-read\", \"observation:paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"]}, \"rendering/live-edge-staleness-on-read-path\": {\"topic\": \"rendering/live-edge-staleness-on-read-path\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"COMPLETE and shipped across all four layers (substrate 763c648 + snapshot-coherence fix cad6211 + footer, final commit tonight): (1) StoreReader.live_edge() single-statement on the chain fact_cursor boundary, snapshot-bracketed into vertex_fold; (2) FoldState/Window/--json carry edge_facts+edge_since for any consumer; (3) local session_start (Tier 0, fires at every session open \\u2014 a dead SessionEnd hook now surfaces at the NEXT SessionStart) and reconcile lenses; (4) in-repo fold lens footer in both registers, clock pinned via the _grammar.time.time seam. Judgment settled: shared is_stale dial anchored on oldest unsealed fact \\u2014 dormant quiet, accumulation fires. Survived the full sol HIGH loop including a TOCTOU finding against its own first cut. The sensor the second wiring death asked for now exists at the read path, where it cannot die with the wiring it watches.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYG6MJJV9JCT2NP6Q6J14N5E\", \"_ts\": 1785125244.185783, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"friction:seal-wiring-silent-death-second-occurrence\", \"thread:010-surfacing-wave\"], \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\"}, \"architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"JSONL becomes the canonical store; sqlite a derived rebuildable index. Ratified by Kyle 2026-08-11. Authority flip: append site = one flushed JSONL line, receipt minted there (write-receipt at the byte-landing site); sqlite indexed after, caught up via Tailer byte-offset on open (offset in sqlite meta; tail-forward if behind; full rebuild if file shrank or head-hash at offset mismatches \\u2014 staleness-sensor pattern at the storage layer). Chain survives re-homing because all commitment hashes are JCS over field dicts with payload embedded as verbatim TEXT \\u2014 JSONL must carry payload as the exact stored string (never re-serialized) or signatures break. Format: ONE interleaved log with t=fact|tick discriminator \\u2014 global receipt order becomes a physical property of the file, one tail cursor. Layout: .loops/data/project.jsonl tracked, .loops/data/project.db gitignored; all store files move under .loops/data/ going forward. Scope: project store first, single-writer; multi-machine convergence deferred (goes through store/merge.py receive machinery when it comes, never git line-merge \\u2014 chain attests receipt order). History-mutating ops (absorb_edit, rebirth, compact) become loud file rewrites \\u2014 feature, rewrites should be un-ignorable in review. Migration oracle: export db->jsonl in rowid order, rebuild scratch db, sl store verify on both, chain heads must match before authority flips. Workflow this buys: diffable history, clone-and-have-history, backup-with-repo.\", \"alternatives\": \"promote FileStore: rejected \\u2014 pre-Receipt era (no id, no chain, whole-file-in-memory); new thin JSONL-append+Tailer-catchup layer beside SqliteStore instead, read surface untouched. Two files facts.jsonl+ticks.jsonl: rejected \\u2014 receipt order becomes a join, two cursors. Nested-JSON payload in line: rejected \\u2014 re-serialization breaks every signature. sqlite-canonical with jsonl export: rejected \\u2014 export is a lagging copy, not authority; the git-visible file must be the write site or diffs lie.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KTYV620K2XSFV6SX3QQNMDMQ\", \"_ts\": 1786460658.634949, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:design/attestation-canonicalization-jcs\"]}, \"store/verify-canonical-agreement\": {\"topic\": \"store/verify-canonical-agreement\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"feature\": \"010-surfacing\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED + implemented (c0504ce..e41e1c5 + r4 remediation in flight). Shipped shape: engine/canonical_audit.py pure-reader module; L1 agreement gate (consumed-prefix last-line check, offset/count parity, marker-rewind-over-indexed-rows detection) default on verify/stats/ticks, rc=1 + named divergence; L3 honest labels; --deep streams the log and re-derives the chain from canonical content (2.5s on the live 111MB store, bytes/mtime untouched \\u2014 pure-reader constraint verified by sol). NAMED RESIDUE (sol r4 adjudication, accepted for this release): sl read is ungated \\u2014 it renders a poisoned index rc=0. Accepted because the ratified slice named verify/stats/ticks as the attestation verbs and read IS the advertised lag-repair route (gating it would break recovery). Architecturally still a correctness gap; the future shape sol recommends: a read gate that repairs-and-retries corroborated lag but refuses non-lag disagreement. Revisit when the store grows a second reader surface (TUI) \\u2014 same gate, both surfaces. r4 also forced the claim-scoping lesson one layer down: L1's lag classification could assert innocence it cannot know (unindexed suffix is uncorroboratable without --deep) \\u2014 remediation scopes the claim instead of expanding detection.\", \"alternatives\": \"verify-the-index-only (status quo): rejected \\u2014 rc=0 on a poisoned store is a false attestation, the exact lie-class the chain exists to prevent. always-deep verify: rejected as default \\u2014 O(full log) on every verify; 111MB live log makes honest-but-cheap the right default with --deep opt-in. JsonlStore-construction-as-verifier: rejected \\u2014 repair semantics destroy evidence.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZS0MT5H3JSBEE37KC8TP4MM\", \"_ts\": 1786485225.382178, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/jsonl-canonical-store\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"implementation/cli-honesty-wave\": {\"topic\": \"implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"AMENDMENT (arbiter, 2026-08-12, post-S1): S1's honesty clause is strengthened from note-only to REFUSE \\u2014 when no fetched kind carries a status field, 'sl read --status' exits 2 with the error on stderr; per-kind stderr notes apply only on MIXED fetches (some kinds status-bearing, some not); an honest empty at exit 0 is reserved for status-bearing rows that simply don't match. Rationale: note-beside-exit-0-empty is the friction's own script-misreadable defect; the wave's NON-NEGOTIABLE clause outranks the original S1 phrasing. Everything else in the prior emission stands unchanged (S1-S4 in scope, S5 deferred, slice order, S3 derivation ruling).\", \"alternatives\": \"slice order as-ruled-in-thread (exit-discipline first): rejected \\u2014 read --status is the pipeline's own gate instrument, building the precondition first makes every later gate invocation real; per-slice design facts: rejected \\u2014 one wave contract, frictions carry per-slice detail; S4 out of wave: rejected \\u2014 small, clear fix-shape, same discipline theme\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGDGDD443VR20Y9EFMHJ\", \"_ts\": 1786568819.196143, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\", \"friction:cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\", \"friction:ls-kind-flag-no-validation\", \"friction:ls-vertex-not-found-exits-zero\", \"friction:read-status-filter-missing\", \"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\", \"friction:reindex-hint-omits-vertex-target\", \"thread:cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\": {\"topic\": \"workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"alternatives\": \"CHANGELOG per-release Upgrading subsection: rejected as sole home because migrations outlive their release entry (a 0.9.0 user upgrading late still needs the ceremony) and CHANGELOG is frozen maintainer narrative; sl store migrate composite verb: deferred, scope beyond the docs ask; docs-only with no tool hint: weaker, the export success line is the natural place to print next steps\", \"message\": \"Ratified by shipping: docs/UPGRADING.md landed on main (24e0610), pushed both remotes, sent to the requesting user. The 0.10.0 flip ceremony is the flagship section; all sharp user_actions hand-verified against code before commit. The export-success-line tool hint remains open as the deferred dissolution half (docs-only-first ruling).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVW6D8WVSEJQN8KM2YFES33\", \"_ts\": 1786574644.647369, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:workflow/db-to-jsonl-migration-doc\", \"friction:jsonl-canonical-log-exceeds-git-limit\"]}, \"practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\": {\"topic\": \"practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED \\u2014 README form settled with Kyle. Narrative-conceptual, NOT section-order/pitch: the concept is hard, the document teaches it. Register: March STRANGE-LOOPS.md declarative present ('Time is fundamental. The past happened.') held throughout \\u2014 the README is a FOLD not a fact history; speaks only from the now. What-Dissolved DROPPED from the doc \\u2014 dissolution lineage lives in the store (paradigm/strange-loops-root-statement), which also serves freshness (no time-anchored claims to rot). Spine: opening move = the lie of the state table (a row nobody witnessed) -> what a writer actually possesses; then truths GROWN (add: witnessing travels/signing, meaning binds at read, scale is residence) -> atoms -> pattern; one observation's life threaded as running example; four skins + painted-as-shared-lens-substrate appear as the now of the pattern, not as argument evidence. Draft next; landing waits on merge-gate freeze or negotiated window.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW7QKZWVT627FQRYHHVYH91\", \"_ts\": 1786581089.916872, \"_n\": 5, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/docs-ground-up-rebuild\", \"design:practice/readme-data-model-rebuild\", \"observation:paradigm/shannon-weaver-layer-mapping\", \"thread:docs-freshness-arc\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"status\": \"refined\", \"message\": \"REFINED 2026-08-13 (Kyle overrides the probe framing with a succession argument, accepted): v2 is a SUCCESSOR build, not a throwaway probe. Kyle's reasoning: the current CLI accreted against a moving substrate (libs developed under it, painted added into it) \\u2014 each libs evolution left a compensation layer in the CLI (foldkey warnings, residence special-casing, strict resolution living in commands/emit.py); the mixture is more trouble than it's worth vs a clean iterative rebuild. Agent-use frictions (k=v syntax, file handling) support JSON-first generic surface. This DISSOLVES the review's second-semantic-implementation objection \\u2014 that was a maintenance argument assuming two CLIs coexisting; succession with a kill date is a different object. The painted-fork objection resolves by sequencing: v2 is rendering-LAST (generic libs surface first, thoroughly tested per stage, whole monorepo under it, THEN rendering) \\u2014 see painted-strip-cost-analysis for why rendering-last beats rendering-never. Conditions attached (see design:architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions): libs-handoff is the critical path; old-CLI freeze ratchet at v2 start; parity ledger over practice workflows; result envelopes are the rendering seam from phase 0.\", \"alternatives\": \"full from-scratch build by GPT: rejected as primary path \\u2014 second semantic implementation, unpriced painted fork, duplicates ratified VertexHandle direction; libs handoff without CLI fork: recommended; hybrid (v2 as throwaway probe exercising new libs APIs): viable if Kyle wants an independent forcing consumer for VertexHandle S5, but scope it as a probe, not a successor\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYKBCRVEJ00KTJQ3AFZGJ9D,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS\", \"_ts\": 1786660365.045652, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"observation:architecture/painted-strip-cost-analysis\", \"observation:test/sol-conceptual-model-review\", \"thread:080-design-wave\", \"thread:cli-error-surface-unification\"]}, \"architecture/libs-handoff-scope\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"status\": \"proposed\", \"message\": \"Contract basis for the libs handoff derived from Sol's LIBS_CHANGES (branch cli-v2-proposal), triaged 2026-08-13. IN SCOPE as tasks (P0): jsonl-declaration-ceremonies (absorb_genesis/absorb_edit on JSONL-canonical \\u2014 atomic multi-row ceremony in the log, stale-head refusal leaves log+index byte-equivalent, index stays pure derivation); declaration-plan-apply-api (plan_declaration_update/apply \\u2014 one high-level op owning head-capture, diff, residence, signing; today every client re-assembles an 8-step protocol); declaration-file-store-recovery (durable intent + idempotent recover for the store-first-then-file-cache gap). IN SCOPE (P1): observer-grant-engine-resolution (THE HOLE \\u2014 engine gates only caller-supplied Grant, declared ObserverDecl.grant.potential silently bypassable; fix at the engine boundary, bypass must be explicit); receipt-attestation-state (persisted signed-state on Receipt/ReceiveResult from the committed row \\u2014 passes write-receipt-vs-temporal-query, your write's attestation is your write's identity); bounded-fact-query (cross-kind limit+cursor query \\u2014 MUST spec against the shipped 0.8.0 temporal-cursor contract and A3 ids-never-ordered, not Sol's FactCursor sketch); strict-contract-ruling (MODIFIED from Sol: strict IS enforced, at the CLI (commands/emit.py three-source precedence); ruling needed on whether enforcement moves to engine receive \\u2014 same push-admission-into-engine motion as observer-grant \\u2014 Sol's 'unenforced' premise was half wrong); lang-kdl-mutation-api (export add/edit/remove_vertex_kind over existing kdl_insert_child/kdl_remove_child + loops{}-creation + LoopDef-to-KDL serializer); target-probe-api (probe_target -> TargetInfo, dissolves per-client residence/suffix logic); canonical-audit-preflight (typed audit-only/audit-then-open/recover-then-open, never conflate verify with repair). DEFERRED (P2, promote on forcing consumer): lifecycle-projection helper, shared result codec, search coordinator, maintenance backend matrix. SEQUENCING: VertexHandle S5 checkpoint precedes any consumer cutover; the throwaway probe (task:cli-v2-probe) is the independent forcing consumer that exercises these APIs as they land. Collisions honored: exit-code/machine-codes work stays with thread:cli-error-surface-unification, not duplicated here.\", \"alternatives\": \"adopt LIBS_CHANGES verbatim as 13 tasks: rejected \\u2014 P2s are granularity ahead of need, strict item had a false premise, cursor item ignores shipped temporal-cursor work; single mega-task: rejected \\u2014 items have independent forcing consumers and different review depth\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYK157RRH7SXX3358WMEPV5,01KXV453R7C6PB5EC7RJ5HHEED\", \"_ts\": 1786659263.027504, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\": {\"topic\": \"architecture/cli-v2-successor-conditions\", \"status\": \"ratified\", \"message\": \"RATIFIED by Kyle 2026-08-13: all four conditions accepted (libs-handoff-first, freeze ratchet, parity ledger, envelope-first). Rendering-last explicitly confirmed as acceptable \\u2014 the plain-text/JSON stretch is not a concern. Next: parity-ledger investigation (what does the ledger actually enumerate).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYM394WKC248CCEDS4STAZJ,01KZYK1MS7HERDB6RJYTVM7PXS,01KZYK2SST0TWJ6J3AWE8BTPDP\", \"_ts\": 1786660637.375833, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/cli-v2-proposal-review\", \"design:architecture/libs-handoff-scope\", \"task:cli-v2-probe\"]}}}, \"retrospective\": {\"items\": {\"internal-table-s0-hardening\": {\"name\": \"internal-table-s0-hardening\", \"feature\": \"internal-table\", \"message\": \"S0\\u2192hardening (2026-07-11\\u219213), the 0.7.0 gate. Shipped: document form, absorb ceremony + atomic absorb_genesis, store-backed resolver seam, read exclusion, edit ceremony (shared-ts + CAS), ontology-as-of, then 8-finding hardening (identity adoption, rewind honesty, pin enforcement, ingress safety) to Sol CLOSE; param-secrets $VAR indirection closed the surviving policy question. Process: (1) review altitude must match claim altitude \\u2014 every per-slice pass + clean capstone missed 8 cross-slice blockers a holistic high-effort review found; (2) reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test ratcheted four rounds to convergence, and hunting holes-introduced-by-fixes caught 2 regressions green suites missed; (3) slices delegate, seams don't \\u2014 they-plan subtasks optimize stated exit criteria, arc conscience stays at the wheel; (4) right-altitude blockers upgrade designs (TOCTOU\\u2192absorb_genesis, identity\\u2192adopt ceremony) \\u2014 reviews are forcing-functions, not just filters. First instance of the retrospective kind; full prose draft in docs/dev/internal-table-retrospective-2026-07-13.md (local) is now redundant with this fact + its ref'd observations.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXETB3ZG37HHR6GHFFBY8CC1,01KXETB495MSBRF73AS5KKVS3J,01KXETB4EDYX3PT2FWXNDAJV84,01KXETBERETBRZWSH7R72KH33E\", \"_ts\": 1783990435.202928, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"observation:practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"observation:workflow/seam-work-vs-slice-work-flows\", \"thread:vertex-state-in-store\"]}, \"completion-t3-build\": {\"name\": \"completion-t3-build\", \"feature\": \"completion-t3\", \"message\": \"Completion T3 (2026-07-13\\u219214): four worker slices (1 Opus, 3 Sonnet) + six Sol review rounds to CLOSE, in one continuous orchestrated arc \\u2014 first full application of the internal-table retro's process rules, same session they were written. What held: (1) reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test drove 8\\u21928\\u21926\\u21924\\u21922\\u2192CLOSE convergence again \\u2014 and rounds 2-5 were nearly ALL holes-in-my-fixes (wrong entry module for the render-free test, honesty fix importing a 5s path, COUNT guard as unbounded as what it guarded, --plain fixed on one surface leaking on three others): the 'fixes deserve MORE adversarial attention' rule is now twice-confirmed; (2) review-altitude: the arc-level reviewer was pointed at the branch from the start this time \\u2014 no per-slice pass masked a seam gap, the seams (S4 composing S2/S3, main.py entry vs cli.app) were where findings clustered exactly as predicted; (3) delegation boundary held: slices to workers, every remediation at the wheel. New lessons: (a) an honesty rule (store-canonical declarations) collides with a latency contract (instant TAB) at a real seam \\u2014 the resolution was a new primitive (_completion_declaration, StoreBusy) not a compromise on either; (b) reviewer positions can be WRONG in both directions: my lens-error position was refuted by code (resolve swallowed the error) and fixing the behavior beat defending the claim, while the lockfile-parity BLOCK was correctly converted to a dissent note by naming the convention it would break; (c) upstream fixes belong upstream \\u2014 two painted defects found, one fixed in painted same-session (8610e57) rather than papered over in loops.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXFF13SN49856XCEV833V9J7,01KXETB495MSBRF73AS5KKVS3J,01KXETB3ZG37HHR6GHFFBY8CC1\", \"_ts\": 1784004271.91754, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:practice/review-altitude-matches-claim-altitude\", \"observation:practice/reviewer-repro-becomes-regression-test\", \"thread:cli-autocomplete-via-painted\"]}, \"080-overnight-multi-model-run\": {\"name\": \"080-overnight-multi-model-run\", \"message\": \"Arc-level synthesis of the 2026-07-16/17 overnight 0.8.0 run (entered on Kyle's full delegation: Opus/Sonnet implement, codex advise+review, loops-claude arbitrate, morning review+retro). WHAT WORKED: (1) The cross-family adversarial pipeline earned its keep at EVERY layer \\u2014 see observation:practice/cross-family-review-yield-080; neither family's green output survived the other's review unamended, and the arbiter's own v2 fallback design was caught breaching its own explicitness clause by the Claude honesty panel. (2) The session-limit outage (00:00-01:20) became a structural test the pipeline passed: codex carried 6 dossier chapters + the s1 advisor solo while the Claude fleet slept; the dossier's 2 surviving Claude chapters + codex's converging independent recommendation meant design never stalled. (3) Design-then-implement discipline held under time pressure: 4 ratified/proposed design facts BEFORE any implementation launch; every implementation deviation was recorded honestly by the agents rather than silently improvised \\u2014 the deviation reports were where several review findings started. (4) Checkout discipline (single-writer main checkout, worktrees for parallel tracks) prevented every collision except one flagged file-region overlap that merged cleanly. WHAT TO FIX: (1) codex 'at capacity' killed one capstone run after 166k tokens \\u2014 retry worked, but long codex reviews need a cheaper resume shape. (2) The scratch-docs-untracked gap: reviewers in worktrees couldn't see docs/scratch/080-overnight (uncommitted); committed now as b7b26da \\u2014 design records should commit as they accrue, not at wrap. (3) Two Claude reader failures produced complete-but-unreturned chapters (files written, structured return lost to the limit) \\u2014 the file-then-return pattern saved the work; make it the default for all long readers. (4) My A5 auto-route lean and the advisor's owner-only pre-decision were both convenience-smuggling catches \\u2014 the two-gate rule (each family reviews the other) is the durable defense; keep it for design sessions, not just code. DEFERRED HONESTLY: TUI shell slices (S0 net landed first by design), VertexHandle S4-S7 (rung-4 checkpoint required-for-cutover), Digest implementation (Kyle's gate), aggregate cursor vectors, GlobalReceiptPosition + receipt-group-id protocol amendments (one oracle-coordination package).\", \"feature\": \"080-design-wave\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KXRQHRJ84T0QDPDBQCZG2M1X,01KXRHS2KGBF5C24EEGRPYF588,01KXRBHHFP72NAZMYM65ZR4WFV\", \"_ts\": 1784315191.057905, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:architecture/temporal-cursor-witness-prefix\", \"observation:practice/cross-family-review-yield-080\", \"thread:080-design-wave\"]}, \"090-review-pipeline-high-tier\": {\"name\": \"090-review-pipeline-high-tier\", \"message\": \"First run of the sol-HIGH tier (previous waves: low interim / medium capstone). Economics: 5/5 round-1 findings landed in exactly the two zones the brief predicted slice review could not see (cross-slice seams, unreviewed rider increments) \\u2014 high-tier full-diff earns its cost there and only there. New calibration finding, sharper than any prior round: BEHAVIOR FIXES SURVIVE ADVERSARIAL VERIFICATION AT A MUCH HIGHER RATE THAN RATCHETS DO (5/5 behavior fixes held round 2; 3/4 ratchets fell to constructed evasions, and one hardened ratchet fell AGAIN round 3). A ratchet written against the known reintroduction is regression-shaped; ratchet-shaped means surviving evasions its author did not construct \\u2014 so ratchets should be priced a verification round of their own. Recurring defect class of the whole review wave: FIELD-NAME/CALL-NAME ENUMERATION (FoldSection rebuild, Rule 9 string-grep, Rule 10 field list twice) \\u2014 enumerate-by-hand is the smell; the fix each time was iterate-the-structure. Also first wave where arbiter took a fix commit directly (b7d623c) \\u2014 right call for a test-file one-liner at round 3, would be wrong earlier in the loop. Pipeline roles held: opus impl survived an API-death mid-wave with clean resume-from-branch-state; idle-race mitigation (verify branch before believing pings) fired correctly 4/4 times.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFVV8CRT3505Y817JW8X588,01KYFR3XJ96X8KMR1XVDC4GMBB\", \"_ts\": 1785091432.92345, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"observation:test/090-sol-high-full-diff-review\", \"thread:090-consumer-evidence-wave\"]}, \"010-jsonl-canonical-store\": {\"name\": \"010-jsonl-canonical-store\", \"message\": \"JSONL-canonical arc (2026-08-11, design-to-converged in one day): 45 commits, 5 sol HIGH rounds (17 findings, all remediated or dispositioned), 2 workflows / 27 agents, 4-angle simplify, ~4170 tests, live store migrated + honestly attested. Five lessons: (1) SCOPE-THE-CLAIM over widen-the-detection, 3 instances (out-of-band detection docs, verify quick-label, lag-innocence boolean) \\u2014 promoted to named principle and global CLAUDE.md; when a detector overclaims, narrow its claim (location, not verdict) before growing it. (2) The reuse/simplify angle is a distinct DETECTION MODALITY, not polish: 5 old-idiom residue sites found by grepping the REPLACED idiom after 4 adversarial rounds missed them \\u2014 residue is stale-but-working, so fault-injection structurally cannot produce this finding class. Cross-repo confirmed: simplify is now standard process in siftd too. (3) r2-after-simplify position is load-bearing: simplify introduced the arc's only regression (rebuild source-mutation), caught only by the post-simplify sol round \\u2014 any code-touching pass, quality passes included, reopens the review obligation behind it (third confirmation of fixes-deserve-more-adversarial-attention, after internal-table and completion-t3). (4) Fix-disposition discipline is ENCODABLE: found-then-dropped escapes went 1 to 0 across four rounds once every-finding-gets-a-disposition entered the prompts \\u2014 prompt-text sufficed, so it belongs in the impl-pipeline skill; candidate for store-native finding facts with status lifecycle. (5) Apply-agent git incident (add -A briefly committed the live store, popped a foreign stash; self-caught, excised, verified clean): apply-phase agents with commit authority need worktree isolation (siftd adopted) or a .loops/ commit fence \\u2014 a doctrine-legitimate detection ratchet at an ambient-authority boundary. Task filed.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZSE9TJF6M3PSMFFWTHQZBTA,01KZVPHRGQ4ZRJNXQ271Y9CWZ9,01KYFXBFQKNJR13D1XTR09AYDM,01KZRWXZ51V99PHDCFYA0RGM6G,01KZSE9TDHVXMPMHMX4161CGJN\", \"_ts\": 1786562292.335039, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"decision:practice/construction-vs-detection-ratchets\", \"decision:practice/scope-the-claim-over-widen-the-detection\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-skill-candidate\", \"observation:session/2026-08-11-jsonl-canonical-full-pipeline\", \"thread:jsonl-canonical-store\"]}, \"chw-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\": {\"name\": \"chw-impl-pipeline-first-live-run\", \"message\": \"First live run of the impl-pipeline skill: CLI-honesty wave, one session, CONVERGED at sol r7. SHAPE: empirical pre-flight (multi-writer, code-read upgraded to receipts) -> 4 worktree slices with independent gates (8/8, 8/8, 6/6, 9/9) -> 7 cross-family rounds -> 4-angle simplify (11 items) -> 3-round convergence tail. 19 findings, every one dispositioned; ~40 commits; suite +80 tests; zero escapes. WHAT THE SHAKEDOWN PROVED: (1) every early defect was pipeline-mechanics not code \\u2014 worktree base races, env-weaker worktrees (untracked .loops), wrong-binary verification, missing SendMessage on gates \\u2014 each dissolved into a skill rule same-session; (2) the finding-ledger-as-query closed the loop literally: the --status instrument S1 built caught the ARBITER dropped disposition at wave close; (3) detection-ratchet taxonomy confirmed again \\u2014 the cite gate fell twice then dissolved into resolver acceptance (construction), and the simplify pass parity ratchet surfaced a latent substrate divergence sol then proved reachable; (4) the convergence tail was a visibility cascade \\u2014 falsy-key fix exposed lookup bug exposed replay-identity bug, severity declining, each fix DISSOLVING the prior fix machinery (per-step lookup -> once-resolved winner), ending at a design question correctly held at the owner gate (fold-key identity) with disclosure pinned in tests; (5) cross-repo routing practice born mid-wave (2 painted frictions emitted upstream), concurrent-session collision survived with verified-not-trusted state + worktree-per-session landed same-day. COST SHAPE: sol went 7 rounds, findings clustered exactly where the skill predicts (seams, fix commits); the three unverified fixes all passed, pricing the no-gate-for-small-fixes tradeoff correctly. HELD OPEN: merge-to-main at Kyle gate; thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string design session; thread:cli-error-surface-unification + friction:sync-errors-exit-zero as the next wave seeds.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KZVZ0Q3Q9CK27A27CD3Y0F1S,01KZW4XWGC1MP4RQ5K952B688G\", \"_ts\": 1786578262.651132, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"observation:practice/impl-pipeline-shakedown-midwave\", \"thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string\"]}}}, \"finding\": {\"items\": {\"smoke-test-finding\": {\"name\": \"smoke-test-finding\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"message\": \"Smoke test complete \\u2014 kind declaration works; dismissed.\", \"_ts\": 1786564356.85362, \"_n\": 2}, \"chw-s3-deviation-sl-entrypoint-fallthrough\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-deviation-sl-entrypoint-fallthrough\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"message\": \"Disposition (caught by the wave-close ledger check \\u2014 the r2-gate invocation running on its own wave): acted on same-hour (mid-flight warnings to S1/S2, verify-which-binary rule added to the impl-pipeline skill at the retro) but never formally dispositioned until the --status open query surfaced it at close. FIXED via the skill rule; the catch itself is retro material \\u2014 the arbiter drops dispositions too, which is why the ledger is a query and not a memory.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVS3WGJXBFTX533B381JW1F\", \"_ts\": 1786578232.200113, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"friction:reconcile-cadence-has-no-sensor\"], \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\": {\"name\": \"chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"Arbiter disposition: deviation ACCEPTED, no code change. Refusing (exit 2, stderr) when no fetched kind carries a status field beats the contract's note-only shape \\u2014 a stderr note beside exit-0 empty stdout reproduces the friction's exact defect (script-misreadable). The NON-NEGOTIABLE exit-discipline clause outranks S1's weaker phrasing; contract amended by design re-emit.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVZ8Q2V01BHJ8N176G84PF\", \"_ts\": 1786568818.775865, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"friction:read-status-filter-missing\"], \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s3-status-not-consulted\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-status-not-consulted\", \"status\": \"deferred\", \"agent\": \"s3-gate\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"Gate observation: sensor counts any reconcile-* thread regardless of status= \\u2014 a planned reconcile emitted status=open would read as done. Arbiter disposition: DEFERRED \\u2014 matches the ruled derivation (name-prefix only); narrow to resolved-only if a planned-reconcile thread pattern ever emerges.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVVZ8Q2V01BHJ8N176G84PF\", \"_ts\": 1786568703.158569, \"_n\": 1, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"]}, \"chw-s3-floor-rounding\": {\"name\": \"chw-s3-floor-rounding\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"s3-gate\", \"slice\": \"S3\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"Gate observation: int() floors age (9.99d renders 9d ago). Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED \\u2014 understates but never overstates staleness, display never straddles the OVERDUE marker; deliberate.\", \"_ts\": 1786568703.698188, \"_n\": 1}, \"chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\": {\"name\": \"chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r2-fix\", \"role\": \"remediation\", \"message\": \"R2 fixed: bare-ls empty-home refusal pre-flighted in _run_ls_root before painted's run_cli \\u2014 same message via resolve._err to stderr, exit 1; siblings noted: store.py:300 same defect class on the store path, emit.py/resolve.py sites already stderr-correct\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786569639.963392, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"6c8d965\"}, \"chw-r3-aggregation-refusal-order\": {\"name\": \"chw-r3-aggregation-refusal-order\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"s2-gate\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"message\": \"S2 gate residual R3: aggregation vertices refuse (exit 1, structural) before kind validation (exit 2) \\u2014 read orders differently. Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED \\u2014 nonzero+stderr holds on both paths; refusal ordering is an asymmetry, not a defect.\", \"_ts\": 1786569173.972363, \"_n\": 1}, \"chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout\": {\"name\": \"chw-r2-sibling-store-error-to-stdout\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"remediation\", \"message\": \"bare loops store pre-flights the empty-home refusal via resolve._err before run_cli, byte-identical message, stderr, exit 1 \\u2014 mirrors 6c8d965; pinned TestBareStoreEmptyHome. Sibling out of ruling scope recorded: loops store <missing-name> still prints to stdout\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVXJJFHVWEJC0W8FK460FDK\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.798489, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-r2-bare-ls-error-to-stdout\"], \"commit\": \"5f1b0df\"}, \"chw-s4-deviation-branch-base-is-main\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-deviation-branch-base-is-main\", \"status\": \"dismissed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Arbiter disposition: DISMISSED as benign \\u2014 merge was git-clean and the 5 integration failures trace to worktree-lacks-.loops environment masking, which a wave-based worktree would have had identically. Real lesson receipted separately: worktree test runs are environmentally weaker than main-checkout runs; integration gating in the main checkout is load-bearing.\", \"_ts\": 1786570192.648221, \"_n\": 2, \"role\": \"arbiter\"}, \"chw-s4-test-hermeticity\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-test-hermeticity\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"s4-impl\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Fixed: five TestCite tests in test_emit.py gain monkeypatch.chdir(tmp_path) (the file's existing hermeticity idiom) \\u2014 a .loops-bearing cwd's real project.vertex no longer shadows the LOOPS_HOME fixture. Refusal unweakened. Suite green from worktree cwd, /tmp, and a scratch .loops-bearing cwd (2459 passed / 1 xfailed each).\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786570379.980328, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"d36f119\"}, \"chw-s4-refusal-message-inert-pins\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-refusal-message-inert-pins\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"s4-impl\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"Fixed: refusal message now discloses attempted-vs-inert \\u2014 'all N entity ref(s) failed to resolve; M inert pin(s) dropped with the refusal' (inert clause omitted when M=0). Semantics unchanged per arbiter ruling: mixed all-attempted-failed refuses, all-inert stores as provenance-only. Three new tests pin mixed message, no-inert message, and all-inert store.\", \"_ts\": 1786570380.527479, \"_n\": 2, \"commit\": \"d36f119\"}, \"chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\": {\"name\": \"chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"gate\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"zero-address cites refuse exit 2 nothing stored; all-inert cites still store provenance-only; gate now one coherent condition (ref-field addresses present AND not all attempted ref-field resolutions failed), stated in comment; 4 pinning tests (TestZeroAddressCite)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT,01KWFPBYHP8H9D8M464FSGNAS1\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.972484, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\", \"friction:cite-verb-first-lacks-vertex-slot\"], \"commit\": \"49e4e4c\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f1-comma-key-census\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f1-comma-key-census\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"census input is the post-key_or set via fetch._item_matches_key; comma-key now byte-identical to single-key refusal; 4 pinning tests (TestCommaKeyCensus)\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786572640.549176, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"859702b\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f2-custom-lens-inert\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s1-f2-custom-lens-inert\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S1\", \"message\": \"gate-fail static --status refuses exit 2 stderr (S1 wording family), before the Format branch so --json refuses too; inert note drops --status; bareword status= predicate keeps the note; 3 pinning tests\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGDGDD443VR20Y9EFMHJ\", \"_ts\": 1786572641.093578, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s1-deviation-refuse-over-note\"], \"commit\": \"cf05ca3\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s2-f1-key-before-kind\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s2-f1-key-before-kind\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S2\", \"message\": \"collect-fold --key refusal gated on declared kinds + post-validator backstop for live undeclared; ls --kind bogus --key x now byte-identical to no-key (exit 2 validator message); pinned incl. declared-collect regression guard\", \"_ts\": 1786572641.263598, \"_n\": 2, \"commit\": \"649c81b\"}, \"chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"r1-remediation\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"slice\": \"S4\", \"message\": \"cite gate counts only field==ref resolutions; resolving message address no longer rescues an all-drop cite; non-ref fields keep typed-pin behavior; pinned in test_cite_vertex_slot\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVYQ4SAHYFXM9RKRJX3VGK3\", \"_ts\": 1786572652.611517, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\"], \"commit\": \"49e4e4c\"}, \"chw-sol-r2-f1-malformed-token-evades-gate\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r2-f1-malformed-token-evades-gate\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"loops-claude\", \"role\": \"arbiter\", \"message\": \"Arbiter ratifies the fix INCLUDING the bare-separator-less-key consequence: ref=barekey alone now refuses (was silent dead-text store). Discriminator upheld = resolver acceptance (parse_ref_token, extracted and shared), because late-bindability is the meaningful line: inert valid addresses can light up when their kind is declared; a bare key never can, so bare-key-only cites are permanently empty attention. Second gate hole closed by moving the discriminator INTO shared resolver machinery \\u2014 construction direction, watch for a third hole as the dissolve-the-gate trigger.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW0EGGEAEZ8DSAT3SQE1TN8,01KZW0EG5KCJPXA4MHR3YZSQR0\", \"_ts\": 1786573751.117551, \"_n\": 3, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-s4-raw-emit-empty-cite\", \"finding:chw-sol-r1-s4-f1-nonref-field-bypass\"], \"commit\": \"a52017d\"}, \"chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Substrate fix per arbiter ruling: surface._row_key gates on 'is not None' (engine fold acceptance is the contract), so falsy-but-valid keys (numeric 0, False) survive into Row.key and kind/0 gets its real entity address. Parity matrix corner un-excluded (predicates agree), sol's end-to-end repro pinned (--key 0,missing --status open answers at exit 0). One test pinned the old nulling (test_surface falsy-key test) \\u2014 inverted with the ruling cited, flagged to coordinator; empty-string address fallback and _item_full_key's source-side truthiness left unchanged and pinned as residue. Suite 2516/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZVWSGJR4ZTX7HEJZ43J7MDT\", \"_ts\": 1786576969.814506, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"design:implementation/cli-honesty-wave\"], \"commit\": \"108870ae\"}, \"chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Stringification unified per arbiter ruling: new leaf module loops/foldkey owns the one str() fold-key projection; surface._row_key delegates to it and provenance's _entry_for_key uses it at the lookup (direct string hit wins ties; projection scan meets native-typed keys). read decision/0 --why on a native-numeric-0 item now returns full field attribution incl. supersession history (sol repro inverted, TestNativeNumericKeyWhy). Engine fold semantics untouched; native-0 vs string-'0' identity held at thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string, with the disclosed duality (two rows, same displayed key) pinned in test_surface.py. Suite 2518/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW4J8H998B9YGBWWK7ZR1DW\", \"_ts\": 1786577578.970853, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-sol-r4-f1-falsy-key-truthiness\"], \"commit\": \"3bb55891\"}, \"chw-sol-r6-f1-replay-identity-switch\": {\"name\": \"chw-sol-r6-f1-replay-identity-switch\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"agent\": \"sol\", \"role\": \"cross-family-review\", \"message\": \"Winning identity resolved exactly once, before the replay loop (arbiter ruling): _entry_for_key dissolved into _winning_state_key \\u2014 string-wins per the foldkey rule, resolved from the chronology's raw key values; the loop attributes only the winner's state changes and the losing item contributes nothing to fields/changed (identity held at thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string). Contract sentence added: --why explains exactly the row read renders. Pins: both emission orders yield the string item's fields only (no native_only residue, no native prior) and attribution content is order-invariant; r5 native-only pin stays green unchanged. Suite 2521/1x both cwds, dev check exit 0.\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZW54VD16ZA7Q7442CCJS8RN,01KZW4XWGC1MP4RQ5K952B688G\", \"_ts\": 1786578000.342789, \"_n\": 2, \"_refs\": [\"finding:chw-sol-r5-provenance-key-lookup\", \"thread:fold-key-identity-native-vs-string\"], \"commit\": \"586d1626\"}}}, \"_boundary\": {\"message\": \"session close: kyle/loops-claude\"}}","prev_hash":"b503ac097935b213831c89c2365d29fa8453569199f2b688c18a13d8fe09bfa9","window_start":"01KZYNDN7RN82NVZ79SZGW7RJE","fact_cursor":"01KZYNEB39D5N7JKH4YZKFYJAD","window_hash":"429f698c80b8dec8f3726af502f3e26aacf404a72527515a9f9c32af3527a5a8","signature":"e4pGIuJGiXYSrUEmdettSsgU7tID76+2LJxBXY8jiH8TVj2u/T0DEDIT4d9TnF4k/KWeHBFWrIdy0UC21Sm2Dg=="}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:3650:{"t":"fact","id":"01KZYTHA87NCB1HCMEA0C5Q7VH","kind":"thread","ts":1786667116.344956,"observer":"kyle/loops-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"name\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"SOL R1 (HIGH, 306k tokens): NOT CONVERGED \\u2014 1 blocker + 4 major, all with driven repros, zero refuted. R1-01 blocker: S6 single-line sibling deletion (add-expand leaves siblings on one line, edit/remove eats them \\u2014 data loss past validation). R1-02: LIKE wildcards in S5 kind filter (a_b matches axb). R1-03: preflight RTO leaks raw JsonlCodecError. R1-04: plan applicability reads vertex writability not canonical-store writability, intent residue on raw failure. R1-05: serializer contract overclaim \\u2014 ARBITER RULED narrow-the-claim (refusal is contract, zero corpus usage), not widen. Pattern holds: every finding lives in slice-gate blind spots (constructed-input classes gates didn't reach) \\u2014 cross-family pays again. My probe fix independently verified clean by sol. Remediation agent running with per-finding fences.\", \"ref\": \"task:libs-handoff-s5,task:libs-handoff-s6,task:libs-handoff-s7,task:libs-handoff-s2\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KZYQ5PQXSQ1N6E4BB19ZJRE7,01KZYPXA7AZ4QX26E5MW42RRKP,01KZYQ5PX4FA170PW1X2DWCXZG,01KZYS86CZZ719T44EQJ4Z6B6D\"}","signature":"iDxSeFfgsde55PjxrNd4APh4Eja1xTY6yShgZTW0AHQrkdxMoAN6CBFWo2Ch0eKZX8/tMXjpXWt2jMrGUWq+CA=="}
.loops/data/project.jsonl:3656:{"t":"fact","id":"01KZYW204CJ2NAZN49S13BF51N","kind":"thread","ts":1786668711.681241,"observer":"kyle/loops-claude","origin":"","payload":"{\"name\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"status\": \"open\", \"feature\": \"libs-handoff-wave\", \"message\": \"SOL R2: NOT CONVERGED \\u2014 6 findings (1 blocker, 3 major, 2 minor), r2 dominated by holes in r1 fixes exactly as the pipeline predicts. R2-01: raw strings evade the r1-01 scanner AND its fail-loud guard \\u2014 the guard was a detection ratchet, fell to first constructed evasion; ARBITER RULED construction-over-detection: parser becomes the safety oracle (post-condition kind-set delta verification, sibling loss inexpressible). R2-02: FOURTH LIKE site (store/slice.py, pre-existing, in-sweep). R2-03: sqlite3 errors still leak in RTO (derived-index corruption \\u2014 rebuild-from-log IS the recover mode's job, ruled not repair-conflation). R2-04: write-surface model incomplete (read-only DIR passes), intent residue again. R2-05/06 minor. Construction-vs-detection taxonomy from the 0.9.0 retro playing out live: the one construction fix (S5 snapshot bracket reuse) has held every round; the detection-shaped fixes keep falling.\", \"ref\": \"decision:practice/construction-vs-detection-ratchets\", \"ref_ref\": \"01KYFXBFQKNJR13D1XTR09AYDM\"}","signature":"HlHkCqOuXHkFHipzH/vnu42JJb4OaRGrtDbezoesMX0fKnLGC/mLAjBobywIHL4qUPGeVXqRDjkixhGPOBolDA=="}
