commit cb385220a68b8f32964dec1ac338a6e8d49368c5
Author:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Aug 13 22:30:05 2026 -0500
Commit:     Kyle Gruel <kylegruel@gmail.com>
CommitDate: Thu Aug 13 22:30:05 2026 -0500

    fix(engine): intent creation is the gate — O_CREAT|O_EXCL closes the apply TOCTOU
    
    thread:intent-gate-toctou (S2 gate finding): the pending-intent gate was
    exists()-check then tempfile+rename, so two racing applies could both
    pass the gate and the loser's rename clobbered the winner's intent
    evidence. _write_intent now creates the intent with
    os.open(O_CREAT|O_EXCL|O_WRONLY) — the create IS the gate, atomic by
    construction; an existing file raises FileExistsError, which apply
    translates to the same typed pending-intent refusal the fast-path
    exists() check produces, with the winner's bytes untouched. fsync
    discipline kept (a crash mid-write leaves a partial intent that
    recovery classifies loudly as IntentCorrupt); a failed write after a
    won create unlinks the partial so 'nothing mutated' stays true. The
    exists() pre-checks stay as fast paths; the sibling
    no-parent-dir-fsync limitation stays as-is (shared with JsonlStore,
    documented).
    
    Regression (red-first, deterministic interleaving — the gate is now
    atomic-by-construction so no real threads needed): _write_intent over
    an existing intent raises with bytes untouched; a two-apply race shape
    (loser's existence check lies clear, winner's intent present) returns
    pending-intent with the winner's intent evidence byte-identical. Both
    residences (jsonl + sqlite).
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C9MfGCNdAoSqKQ34mKevuF

